3337634433	Zur Tant	Rheinbergstraße 49	Germany	Cologne	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.zurtant.de/	1 Star	Classic Cuisine, Farm to table	3.0	€€€	f	t	In this well-maintained half-timbered house set in an idyllic location on the Rhine, chef Thomas Lösche celebrates cuisine that puts top-notch ingredients and craftsmanship centre stage. For example, he emphasises the excellent quality and characteristic flavours of Berkshire pork from the Black Forest, cleverly underscoring those flavours with an accompanying sweet-and-sour note. This is cooking that eschews frills in a bid to remain true to the authenticity with which this house is synonymous. The wine list features a good selection of Austrian labels. And then there is the terrace with a magnificent view of the Rhine – best enjoyed at sunset!	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3335143517	Pottkind	Darmstädter Straße 9	Germany	Cologne	Terrace	https://www.restaurant-pottkind.de/	1 Star	Creative, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Enrico Sablotny and Lukas Winkelmann, the duo who run this little restaurant, are from the Ruhr Valley. In the kitchen, first-rate ingredients are transformed into distinctly original, creative compositions. Skilfully combined flavours and harmoniously balanced contrasts are particularly evident in dishes such as Eifel salmon trout, apricot with long pepper and chamomile velouté, or boiled beechnuts with radicchio compote and cherry balsamic ice cream. Diners never know what to expect from the carte blanche set menu. Excellent service comes courtesy of very attentive, competent and charming waitstaff, who give the place a pleasantly unpretentious feel. The seats at the counter overlooking the open kitchen are especially popular. In summer, soak up the lively atmosphere of Cologne's Südstadt neighbourhood on the terrace.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3337026167	Daigo	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed	https://www.atago-daigo.jp/	1 Star	Shojin	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Being originally located in the grounds of Seishoji Temple is why Daigo began serving shojin ryori. What Nomura inherits as the restaurant’s fourth-generation owner is shojin ryori for gracious service. Note that dried bonito flakes are used in the broth, so the meals are not completely vegetarian. The nutrition and flavour of the vegetables and the sukiya architecture put the mind at ease. Relax and enjoy this moment of tranquillity.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3331353295	Sterneck	Cuxhavener Straße 86	Germany	Cuxhaven	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.badhotel-sternhagen.de/	1 Star	Creative	4.0	€€€€	f	f	A breathtaking view of the North Sea, the Elbe world shipping route and the UNESCO-listed Wadden Sea forms the backdrop for first-class cuisine served in the compact fine dining restaurant of Badhotel Sternhagen. This is the domain of Marc Rennhack, whose modern cooking builds on classical culinary foundations. He uses high-quality ingredients and has a knack for creating delicious dishes with just a few simple components. His sauces are particularly noteworthy. With consummate skill, he injects dishes with creative flair and conjures up interesting flavour combinations. His set menu comes in three to seven courses (there is also a vegetarian version). At five elegantly laid tables, diners are served cordially and attentively. The walk-in wine cellar – 3m below sea level – holds a large selection of fine wines.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3336027315	[KOOK] 36	Oberer Stadtplatz 18	Germany	Deggendorf	Air conditioning	https://kook36.de/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine, Asian	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Relocating from Moos to Deggendorf, chef-patron Daniel Klein has brought his [KOOK]36 to the fourth floor of the ERL real estate group's building. The stylish upscale setting is complemented by lovely views through the floor-to-ceiling windows – in good weather, the roof terrace is the perfect spot for an aperitif. The service is friendly and professional. The kitchen team conjures up modern, creative and visually appealing dishes that draw heavily on Asian influences^ these are served as a set menu comprising four to seven courses with vegetarian options. Wine pairings are also available. Handy for motorists: the lift takes you directly up to the restaurant from the public car park below.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
