3330300604	Tudor Hall	3A Vasileos Georgiou A	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.tudorhall.gr	1 Star	Contemporary	5.0	€€€€	t	t	If the idea of having lunch or dinner on the elegant rooftop of a hotel, with piano music in the background and the eternal Acropolis as a backdrop sounds appealing, then Tudor Hall is definitely the place, especially for a romantic candlelit supper – but make sure you book a table in advance. Here, on the 7th floor of the King George Hotel, next to the central Syntagma Square, chef Asterios Koustoudis (who is also executive chef of the adjacent Hotel Grande Bretagne, home to the GB Roof Garden restaurant) showcases his contemporary take on Greek cuisine that is built around a concise à la carte and one tasting menu. The end result is a superb mix of slick service, sommelier recommendations and meticulous cuisine featuring delicious dishes that are surprisingly technical and pleasing on the eye. Make sure you try the superb cod.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3335199081	The Zillers	54 Mitropoleos	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	http://www.thezillersroofgarden.gr	1 Star	Contemporary, Greek	4.0	€€€	f	f	This restaurant occupies the former family home of the German architect Ernst Zillers, who came to Athens to design some of its public buildings, fell in love with the city and remained here for the rest of his life. The building, which is situated next to the Greek Orthodox cathedral and has now been converted into a hotel (Zillers Boutique Hotel), boasts a rooftop terrace and multi-purpose Roof Garden with fine view of the cathedral and the Acropolis. During the day it serves light meals and snacks, but in the evening chef Vasilis Roussos and his team spring into action here! He offers two tasting menus: Synecdoche and Synthesis, both with creative dishes of traditional Greek influence and touches of international flavour. One standout dish was the Prawn Valley, a refreshing combination of raw prawns with a delicate tomato sauce, bergamot and kumquat that will definitely leave a lasting memory. The wine list also features a variety of Greek options to pair with your meal.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3338733002	Pelagos	40 Apollonos Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.pelagosathens.com	1 Star	Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	If you’re keen to escape the hustle and bustle of Athens, why not consider a visit to the Four Seasons Astir Palace Hotel, a luxury resort located on an archipelago to the south of the Greek capital? At Pelagos, a restaurant that delights guests with its spacious sea-view terrace, enjoy Mediterranean cuisine with an Italian touch and classic French influence. In the kitchen, where talented chef Luca Piscazzi is at the helm, the cooking showcases a successful fusion of solid technique which extracts maximum benefit from local ingredients. The end result is highlighted on three tasting menus: Discovery, designed in the winter, when the chef explores the islands in search of ingredients and inspiration to bring life to the menu^ Adventure, the most extensive, combining creations from the other two options^ and the enticing The Best Of, that brings together superb dishes created by the chef during his career. We recommend booking a table on the veranda to enjoy the magical views.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3337632722	Makris Athens	10 Astiggos - 119 Ermou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://makrisathens.com/en/	1 Star	Creative	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Located at the foot of the Parthenon, this restaurant comes as something of a surprise for various reasons. Firstly, for the stunning view from its terrace^ secondly, for its setting, in a historic building that was once the country’s first inn, with a decor that ensures a unique experience enabling guests to view its historic vestiges through the glass floor in the dining room^ and, lastly, its cuisine, the main attraction, which comes courtesy of chef Patron Petros Dimas and which showcases the country’s gastronomic heritage through dishes that are creative and impeccable technique. The majority of the ingredients used are sourced from the restaurant’s own farm or from local producers and provide the basis for three tasting menus: Genesis, Utopia and the vegetarian Physis Vegan (the latter requiring pre-ordering). Guests can also explore the impressive wine list, home to a selection of 300 labels, including Greek and international options, plus interesting cocktail pairings.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
