3339744225	L'AUBERGE DE PLAISANCE SAKURAI	2217 Taie	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.hiramatsuhotels.com/plaisance-sakurai/	1 Star	French	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	This auberge overlooks the magnificent Yamato Plains. What the chef says is characteristic of the Nara approach, which is to pursue local production for local consumption—to which end he uses local vegetables, Yamato beef and duck, and deer and boar from Gojo. Prix fixe offerings, intertwined with the history and culinary culture of the old capital, flow as if weaving a tale. The chef also serves Miwa somen, a very Sakurai-style dish. The service will put you at ease.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3337585987	La Terrasse irisée	1-34-7 Ayameike Kita	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list	https://laterrasse.jp/irisee/	1 Star	French	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	There is a particularly beautiful sunset view from the elegant dining room overlooking Ayameike pond. Susumu Sasaki puts to work his many years of training in Switzerland and France, creating harmony between what he learnt there and the Japanese ingredients. He introduces the local vegetables prior to the meal out of respect for the producers. The name means ‘iridescent’, invoking a rainbowand his desire to span Nara and Europe in his approach.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3337157333	LA TRACE	2-1-5 Omiyacho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://latrace.jp/	1 Star	French	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	‘La Trace’ means ‘footprints’ and Chef Ryo Sato traces the roots of the foodstuffs he uses, building strong relationships with the farmers of Nara. In gratitude to those who grow the vegetables and raise the chicken and pork he serves, he incorporates their stories into his cuisine so they can get an idea of the landscapes he saw there, the personalities of his producers, and what they felt as they nurtured his ingredient. This leaves the footprints of French cuisine in the food culture of the ancient capital.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3335556774	akordu	70-1-3-1 Suimoncho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://akordu.com/	2 Stars	Innovative	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	‘Akordu’ is Basque for ‘memories’. Chef Hiroshi Kawashima reflects the history of Nara, the story behind each ingredient, and the memories of the diner in his food. A small box sits on the table^ inside are several cards, each inscribed with a menu whose poetic style stirs the imagination. Kawashima’s gastronomy is deeply rooted in the land and character of Nara, while modern Spanish cuisine inspires his freewheeling imagination and technique.	salajakub	\N	\N
