3337333601	Herberg Onder de Linden	Burg. van Barneveldweg 3	Netherlands	Aduard	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.herbergonderdelinden.com/	1 Star	Asian Influences	3.0	€€€	f	t	Steven Klein Nijenhuis's commitment to sustainability is apparent as soon as you enter his restaurant. He no longer serves dairy, beef or pork^ instead, he lays the focus squarely on vegetables and fruit. His creativity and penchant for working with Asian ingredients make for dishes that are full of surprises and frequently have an unusual umami twist. Techniques such as pickling and the subtle use of seasonings such as sambal give local ingredients an extra dimension. He incorporates locally foraged lion's mane mushroom, for instance, into an intensely flavoursome dish with onion dashi, fermented black garlic and apple, crispy potato and dried leek powder. The chef is a real beer lover, so it is well worth perusing the beer menu to find the perfect beverage accompaniment. This stylish listed building (1735), with its grand chandelier, exudes the atmosphere of an inviting inn. The cosy lounge is the perfect place for a digestif or coffee by the fire. Should you wish to extend your stay, there are lovely guestrooms available.	paganialex	\N	\N
3335724491	Aan de Poel	Handweg 1	Netherlands	Amstelveen	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking	https://aandepoel.nl/	2 Stars	Creative, Modern French	4.0	€€€€	t	f	The view of De Poel Lake is simply breathtaking. The large windows and elegant interior design allow you to fully immerse yourself in the charm of this location. Stefan van Sprang's culinary creations are a perfect match for this gorgeous setting. The chef likes to add the finishing touches to his dishes tableside and present the day's lunchtime set menu – which makes for a more personal dining experience. (In the evening, there are à la carte options and a set menu.) This skilled craftsman deftly combines diverse influences and uses his creativity to put his own spin on classic recipes. To add aromatic nuances, he avails himself of the herb garden right behind the restaurant. For example, he showcases the intense flavours of Dutch lamb saddle and neck with a playful combination of tender and crispy textures, adding zest with a chimichurri and depth with a lamb jus. To provide further complexity, he incorporates a Mediterranean ratatouille and salty oyster leaf. The captivating blend of familiar flavours and original garnishes elevates the produce to new heights. This is a treat for both the palate and the eye, complemented by an exclusive wine list that the sommeliers will be happy to help you explore.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3330739200	Symbiose	4 quai des Chartrons	France	Bordeaux	Terrace	https://symbiose-bordeaux.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Run by four young partners, Symbiose makes it all look easy: the bold and efficiently prepared dishes, the friendly, relaxed service, the mostly young, if not trendy, clientele. Then there is the little bistro - style dining area – and unbeatable value for money at lunchtime. Highly recommended.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3336670533	Bistro de la Mer	Utrechtsestraat 57	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.bistrodelamer.com	1 Star	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	In this cosy bistro it is easy to imagine that you're in Paris instead of Utrechtsestraat, in the heart of Amsterdam. The large oyster bar, the walls adorned with the menus of legendary French brasseries, the vintage crockery on the tables: this place is a celebration of a bygone era. Traditional fish recipes are given a fresh but down-to-earth twist with a sure hand. Richard van Oostenbrugge and Thomas Groot are once again making their mark here with no-nonsense dishes that you can feast on every day of the week – including at lunchtime!For example, a generous portion of perfectly cooked mussels are served, dotted with vadouvan mayonnaise and calamansi jelly, which add freshness and nuance without spoiling the seafood's distinctive flavour. As a nod to the traditional recipe, a creamy vadouvan soup and green celery provide the finishing touch to this delicious reinterpretation. A beautiful piece of turbot roasted on the bone is topped with morels incorporating a mousse created from the fish's barbel, fine slices of lardo di colonnata and a rich beurre blanc. This is next-level fish cuisine. Old school. Original. And it can all be ordered à la carte!	basileryan	\N	\N
3334044161	Flore	Nieuwe Doelenstraat 2	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://restaurantflore.com/	2 Stars	Contemporary, Creative French	4.0	€€€€	f	t	(Temporarily closed. Flore has opened a pop-up at Basecamp Amsterdam, Tom Schreursweg 40, 1067 MC Amsterdam) Flore is entirely focused on providing a mindful fine dining experience. Housed in De L'Europe hotel, this upscale restaurant is lent a unique feel by its modern interior design, which features natural materials. Bas van Kranen's original approach to nature, which characterises his cuisine, emphasises vegetables, local produce and sustainability. Biodynamic growers have become regular suppliers and dairy products have been banished from the kitchen. His search for solutions feeds his creativity, and has resulted in a very pure style of cooking. Game appears on the menu in the autumn and winter, but in spring and summer, the chef turns his attention to the North Sea. The plant-based set menu is a constant, all year round. The small dishes are full of surprises right up to the last bite – a prime example is his signature dish featuring seasonal fruits and vegetables, each prepared differently. The intricate dance of flavours and textures is complemented by a fig peel oil, its gentle sweetness binding everything together. A light, airy hazelnut and Dutch wasabi emulsion adds a moderate kick. Bas van Kranen explores the depths of his ingredients, creating dishes that evoke emotion. He clearly takes pride in working with Dutch produce and now has the confidence to cook just the way he wants to.	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3331048088	Ciel Bleu	Ferdinand Bolstraat 333	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking	https://www.cielbleu.nl/	2 Stars	Creative	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Ciel Bleu immediately lives up to its name. Here, you dine on the top floor of the luxurious Okura Hotel with a spectacular view of the blue sky and the Amsterdam skyline as a backdrop. The modern elegance of the restaurant and the superlative presentation of the dishes are equally pleasing to the eye.Arjan Speelman's cuisine is technically accomplished, creative and laced with international influences and seasonings. This chef effortlessly combines a classic beurre blanc with exotic spices and ingredients from around the globe. Every detail is precise, every bite a surprise. A nice touch: with each course, a herb in its original form is brought to the table – this herb will be featured in the next dish.Dining at Ciel Bleu is intriguing. You will be served by one of the best front-of-house teams in the country, starring sommelier Noël Vanwittenbergh and maître d' Francesco Simonelli. The sky really is the limit here!	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3330574987	Daalder	Postjesweg 1	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Terrace	https://daalderamsterdam.nl/	1 Star	Creative	3.0	€€€€	f	t	With its neon lights, bold graphics, street art and night-club atmosphere, Daalder's new home in Het Sieraad will leave a lasting impression. In this hip spot, Dennis Huwaë says he can really do his thing. He has long been known for his dishes that are creative without being pretentious, and you can see him in action on his 'cooking podium' as he continues to work in this vein. The chef's strong personality is evident in every detail. Chef Huwaë draws on his Indonesian roots and other Asian influences to add pep to his inventive creations, and he is certainly not averse to contrasting flavours. This chef's talent lies in the harmony he achieves with combinations such as chicken satay, anchovies and vadouvan. Sometimes he keeps things a little more traditional, serving up langoustine cooked to perfection with a butter sauce with champagne, orange and Grand Marnier. Subtle, intense, explosive – this is what Dennis Huwaë is all about.Meticulous but generous, he is always looking for variety and the element of surprise. Every plate is designed to be fun. At Daalder, you are guaranteed a blissful dining experience.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3334458905	Restaurant 212	Amstel 212	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://212.amsterdam/	2 Stars	Creative	5.0	€€€€	f	t	As soon as you step into this quintessential canal house in the centre of Amsterdam, Richard van Oostenbrugge and Thomas Groot draw you into their world. There is something theatrical about the sight of the chefs working meticulously in their open kitchen. There is an enchanting intimacy and luxurious comfort about Restaurant 212. Nothing is left to chance here, and that goes for the attentive service, too. Fun fact: On the ceiling, you can still see marks from the champagne being uncorked when this place was awarded its first MICHELIN star. With their inventiveness and classical know-how (those sauces!), both chefs put their own stamp on their creations. An ingredient will undergo the most surprising of transformations, and it all seems to happen with such ease – therein lies the chefs' originality. The venison cooked in hay, for instance, is elevated by a perfectly reduced, intensely flavoursome sauce with a glistening sheen. A padrón pepper in tempura and an ingenious association of plum and Meaux mustard provide fine spiciness and extra dimensions. The simplicity of this cuisine is what makes it so ingenious! Nothing is overdone, and nothing is lacking. The real stars of this show are the extraordinary produce and the talent of two friends.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3337301995	Spectrum	Herengracht 542	Netherlands	Amsterdam	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking	https://www.restaurantspectrum.com/	2 Stars	Creative	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Sidney Schutte produces an astonishing range of flavours. At De Librije, he developed his own inventive culinary style, and at Amber (in Hong Kong) he mastered the sophisticated techniques particular to Asian cuisine. His food looks as spectacular as it tastes – exciting and colourful with a unique interplay of textures. First-class Dutch produce and international seasonings come together here in complex dishes. The technically gifted chef does not shy away from contrasts, and he is certainly an innovator rather than an imitator! This goes for his vegetarian set menu as well as his fish and meat creations. The vibrant red wine and magnolia reduction, for instance, creates a burst of fruity and tangy flavours to complement a perfectly cooked lobster medallion and scallops^ the cream of black truffle then provides earthy nuances, and crispy duck tongue adds pleasing contrasts. Every bite creates a new impression that increases the appetite. This typical canal house enchants visitors with its understated class and beautiful elegance. The extremely attentive service comes courtesy of the highly accomplished front-of-house team. A real fine dining experience!	k�nigsara	\N	\N
