3332437581	Het Koetshuis	Panoramaweg 23a	Netherlands	Bennekom	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.hetkoetshuis.nl/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This traditional thatched property deep in the Veluwe forest was turned into a culinary hotspot by the Löhr family. It was first awarded a MICHELIN Star in 1998 and, today, this great achievement is continued by Jurre Klein Bleumink.The cuisine here is impressively composed: rich without being heavy and full of well-balanced flavours. All the classics are honoured here at Het Koetshuis, but there’s also room for updates^ there will always be, for example, powerful game dishes – but you’ll find modern twists here and there to add some excitement. An excellent selection of wines chosen by the restaurant’s sommelier, Danny, completes the picture.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3337185114	Pieters Restaurant	Hoofdstraat 73	Netherlands	Bergambacht	Terrace	https://www.pietersrestaurant.nl/	1 Star	Modern French	4.0	€€€	f	t	You’ll feel very much at home when you dine at Pieter and Paula’s pleasant restaurant. Here, the welcoming interior provides a perfect backdrop for a delightful gastronomic experience created by chef Pieter who calls upon all his experience and an abundance of enthusiasm. Far from being show cuisine, his cooking demonstrates a classical finesse in keeping with traditional techniques, coupled with attractive, playful and highly original touches.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
3335408584	Kaatje bij de Sluis	Brouwerstraat 20	Netherlands	Blokzijl	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.kaatje.nl/	1 Star	Organic, Creative French	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Blokzijl is a picture-perfect little slice of the Netherlands. Opt for a table by the window to enjoy the delightful view of the lock and the quintessential brick houses. The wall decorated with cartoons is also sure to draw the eye. When it comes to the food, the dishes on the menu are testament to the creativity of the talented chef. With an eye for detail, he bends organic and local produce to his will. Fine classic flavours are shaken up in occasionally daring combinations. Lobster with blue cheese? Sardines and beetroot? It is the meticulous dosing that creates exciting nuances of flavour. The cheese and wine selections are equally tempting. It is no accident that, bar one year, Kaatje bij de Sluis has retained at least one Michelin star consistently since 1978. Quality reigns supreme here.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
