3336831292	Sihlhalde	Sihlhaldenstrasse 70	Switzerland	Gattikon	Car park,Terrace	https://www.smoly.ch/	1 Star	Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	The location is somewhat rural, with the drive there taking you down a small road that leads past green pastures and grazing cows... But the journey to this idyllic little hamlet is well worth it, for Gregor Smolinsky has a special talent: his ability to strip things down to the bare essentials. The focus is squarely on the produce. His style of cooking is classic, clear-cut and free of unnecessary frills^ nothing distracts from the superior quality of the ingredients. Only a few components are ever used, and they are always brimming with intense flavours. You should definitely try his brasato ravioli or his soufflé – they almost have cult status! It's no wonder that the cosy restaurant in this charming historical farmhouse (which was actually once his parents' farm) is often fully booked.	donatidiego	\N	\N
3338503413	Tsé Fung	Route de Lausanne 301	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lareserve-geneve.com	1 Star	Chinese	5.0	€€€	t	f	Born in Shenzhen, Frank Xu represents the third generation of a cooking dynasty, and the Cantonese and Chinese culinary arts have found a peerless ambassador in this veteran chef. His authentic, flavourful creations are meticulously prepared using top-notch ingredients: the langoustine dim sum, the sea bass fillet with ginger, the Peking duck (two courses) and the Sichuan aubergine cannot fail to impress. Don't hesitate to ask for advice when it comes to choosing your dishes – the front-of-house team will be happy to talk you through them. As for the setting, the pleasant interior has a classy, exotic feel and is done out in a red, black and gold colour scheme^ the elegant bay windows command a view of the pool and lake.	semenovirene	\N	\N
3336217008	Bayview by Michel Roth	Quai Wilson 47	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantbayview.com	1 Star	Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	In addition to a jaw-dropping view over the lake, hence the restaurant’s name, we were enchanted by the high-flying repertory of Danny Khezzar served at the Hotel President Wilson’s fine dining establishment. Under the expert guidance of award-winning executive chef Michel Roth (Meilleur Ouvrier de France and Bocuse d’Or), Khezzar crafts a masterfully creative version of pedigree French classics. The dishes, whose plating is modern and sophisticated, are served in an airy, elegant setting, the centrepiece of which is an incredible suspended table made out of Saint-Louis Amadeus crystal. The experienced and attentive front-of-house team blends in seamlessly with this outstanding dining experience.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3339840582	L'Atelier Robuchon	Quai Wilson 37	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.oetkercollection.com/hotels/the-woodward/restaurants/latelier-robuchon/	2 Stars	French Contemporary	4.0	€€€€	t	f	On the shores of Lake Geneva, luxury hotel The Woodward boasts a fine dining restaurant that is the epitome of elegance. In a space done out in warm dark wood and vivid reds, diners take their seats at high tables or at the counter affording interesting views into the open kitchen. Opt for the tasting menu (there is also a vegetarian set menu) or choose from the à la carte dishes. Service courtesy of a charming and highly attentive team!	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3332085824	Il Lago	Quai des Bergues 33	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.fourseasons.com/geneva	1 Star	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	The iconic Four Seasons hotel, Geneva’s oldest luxury hotel (1834), dripping with pilasters and frescoes, is the setting of Il Lago, or Lake Geneva’s classy remake of the dolce vita. The kitchen team offers high-flying Italian cuisine, with the odd Mediterranean accent, rich in aromas, subtlety and delicacy. The quintessence of fine dining.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3339322933	La Micheline	Avenue de la Gare des Eaux-Vives 3	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamicheline.ch/	1 Star	Mediterranean Cuisine, French Contemporary	5.0	€€€	f	t	This restaurant opposite the new station sports a magnificent bistronomy concept over two floors. The Mediterranean cuisine has been stripped of superfluous frills so shine the spotlight on the ingredient and flavour. The service is as smooth as a bearnaise sauce and the vibe is smart and upmarket. La Micheline refers to the first train from Annemasse to Eaux-Vives – equipped with Michelin tyres.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3336372136	Arakel	Rue Henri Blanvalet 17	Switzerland	Geneva	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.arakel.ch	1 Star	Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Tucked away in one of Geneva’s liveliest districts, the sleek open kitchen of this dainty restaurant captures your attention right from the start, drawing you into the heart of the action. A blend of modernity and tradition, the score adds an innovative spin to a lineup of classics, illustrated by risotto of mussels, celery, saffron mousse, passion fruit gel or a carpaccio of giant red shrimps, subtly marinated in yuzu, lemon zest and fresh herbs and paired with stuffed carrot rolls and a slightly sweet carrot sauce. The small pavement terrace offers a chance to get a real feel for this delightful quarter. The young, enthusiastic and appropriately irreverent front-of-house team adds to the venue’s lively vibe.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3336159282	F.P. Journe - Le Restaurant	Rue du Rhône 49	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning	https://www.fpjourne-le-restaurant.ch/	1 Star	Modern French	3.0	€€€	f	f	The great Geneva watchmaker François-Paul Journe and the former chef of Le Chat-Botté, Dominique Gauthier, have set their sights on this legendary institution (listed as a heritage site in the canton of Geneva), a chic upmarket bistro, with its black and white tiled floor, old wooden panelling and ceiling, red velvet banquettes and chairs.Studded with fine produce, the plates turn like fine timepieces, like this saddle of lamb from Chandossel with fennel and artichoke, accompanied by a purée worthy of Robuchon's own. Expect colourful dishes too, such as lobster from Brittany with Green Zebra tomatoes or langoustines roasted with kadaif. In this lively atmosphere, you can also count on perfectly oiled service and excellent advice from the sommelier.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3332496382	Le Chat-Botté	Quai du Mont-Blanc 13	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.beau-rivage.ch/	1 Star	Modern French, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	This restaurant is housed in the Beau Rivage Hotel, one of the finest palace hotels on Lake Geneva. Get ready to tuck into cuisine designed for the modern palate that showcases local producers (beef, poultry, fruits and vegetables). The whole experience is enhanced by the admirable work of the sommelier, who will guide you through an impressive 1 400-bin wine list.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3335697169	L'Aparté	Rue de Lausanne 43	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelroyalgeneva.com/	1 Star	Modern French, Farm to table	3.0	€€€	t	t	Perfectly suited to the swish, intimate vibe of Hôtel Royal in which it is located, take a seat at one of the restaurant’s four tables and let yourself be guided. The chef serves each elegant, immaculately crafted dish himself, explaining the ins and outs of their preparation. You will sample a lineup of outstanding produce – Swiss veal and beef, fish straight from Brittany, Bresse poultry, harnessed to ambitious cuisine packed with character. We recommend booking well in advance, particularly in the evenings, both in light of the seating capacity and its popularity, which is not about to wane. Bogie’s Bar is ideal to kick off or finish your meal in style. Valet parking available.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3335613546	Tosca	Rue de la Mairie 8	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.tosca-geneva.ch/	1 Star	Tuscan	4.0	€€€€	f	t	Tosca, an emblematic address of the Eaux-Vives district, famous for its fountain, takes la cucina very seriously! The interior by a contemporary Italian artist pays a distinctive tribute to the art and culture of the Italian Renaissance in a Florentine-inspired romantic setting. The food is the inspired work of Ivan Baretti, born and bred in Florence, who trained at Arpège in Paris and was a former chef at Il Lago, no less! With a magnificent supporting cast of top-class ingredients, his delicate, refined dishes unveil a strong Tuscan bias and hit the spot every time. Amiable, professional service and knock-out selection of Tuscan wines.	popafarah	\N	\N
3332798623	Pichlmaiers zum Herkner	Dornbacher Straße 123	Austria	Vienna	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.zumherkner.at	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Well worth a trip to the outskirts of the city. The inn formerly run by famous Viennese chef Heinz Herkner has been given a successful makeover that combines modernity and tradition – this applies to the warm and charming setting as well as the food. The Austrian and classic French dishes are peppered with modern touches. The pretty terrace extends over two floors.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3332757777	1910 Gourmet by Hausers	Dorfstrasse 53	Switzerland	Grindelwald	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.belvedere-grindelwald.ch/de/restaurant/gourmet-1910/	1 Star	Contemporary	3.0	€€€€	t	t	The fine dining restaurant of the Hotel Belvedere welcomes diners in a compact space with just six tables. In the kitchen, Hungarian chef Dávid Imre Rózsa runs the show. His technically modern and pleasingly pared-back style conveys emotions through its flavours, and comes into its own in dishes such as dry-aged pike perch with Oscietra caviar from Frutigen – this also exemplifies the firm focus on using local produce. There is a choice of two set menus, one of which is vegetarian, as well as a good wine selection with the option of ordering by the glass. The kitchen team provide back up to the friendly waitstaff.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3337232484	Sommet by Martin Göschel	Alpinastrasse 23	Switzerland	Gstaad	Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.thealpinagstaad.ch/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	As if the exclusive Alpina Gstaad were not an impressive enough hotel, it also comes up trumps with this appealing restaurant. It is something special in several respects: first, there is its distinctive decor, which sees rustic charm elegantly blended with modern sophistication^ second, the fantastic panoramic terrace and, last but not least, the elaborate seasonal tasting menu created by Martin Göschel. The Mannheim-born chef, who previously earned MICHELIN stars at Hotel Paradies in Ftan and Alte Post in Nagold, successfully combines classic cuisine with modern influences, using only Swiss ingredients. The set menu also comes in a vegetarian version.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3331573703	Radius by Stefan Beer	Höheweg 41	Switzerland	Interlaken	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.victoria-jungfrau.ch/	1 Star	Regional Cuisine, Swiss	3.0	€€€€	f	f	In his kitchen in the restaurant of the time-honoured Victoria Jungfrau Grand Hotel, Stefan Beer only uses ingredients sourced within a 50km radius (the clue is in the name!). He proposes a conventional set menu and a vegan set menu, as well as a menu for two people sharing, which includes classics finished at your table and large cuts of meat. Diners are talked through the pleasingly uncomplicated dishes – sometimes by the chef. Produce that they harvest themselves is used, as well as local shrimps or caviar from the region. The high standards are also reflected in the tasteful and upscale interior.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3335216229	Fahr	Grossacherweg 1	Switzerland	Künten-Sulz	Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://fahr-sulz.ch/	1 Star	Regional Cuisine, Contemporary	5.0	€€€€	t	t	The trip out here into the countryside is definitely worth it! Clad in Swiss hardwood, the building housing this restaurant stands directly adjacent to a recreational area and close to the Reuss River. Chef Manuel Steigmeier serves up modern cuisine with sustainability at its heart and that is bold, sophisticated and stripped down to the essentials. His ingredients are of the highest quality, and he makes a point of sourcing from Switzerland or the region. A prime example is the wonderfully succulent and perfectly cooked char, with a delicately balanced and rich beurre blanc with lime, potato brunoise and caviar from Frutigen, accompanied by spicy sweet-and-sour pickled celery with a crisp texture. Part of this culinary experience is an extensive wine list featuring around 600 labels, along with a knowledgeable and communicative service team. The decor is sleek and stylish, with striking designer lamps created by the owner's son. The terrace is glorious. A small selection of dishes from the evening menu is available at lunchtime.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3336522119	RICO'S	Seestrasse 160	Switzerland	Küsnacht	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.ricozandonella.ch/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Rico Zandonella's restaurant stands out from the crowd! It is charming, cosy, colourful and packed with art – a tastefully eclectic mix of styles and highly individual decorative details. In addition, the service is pleasingly laid-back and professional. Served in the form of a set menu comprising three to eight courses, the food has an international flavour^ to accompany it, choose from the nicely curated wine list, which has a particularly good selection from Switzerland and France. There is a set lunch menu Wed-Fri. For anyone looking for a venue for private events: you can book Rico's Privé.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3333418129	LA CHAVALLERA in der Krone - Säumerei am Inn	Via Cumünela 2	Switzerland	La Punt-Chamues-ch	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://krone-lapunt.ch/de/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine, Alpine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	The time-honoured Krone, long renowned as a destination for foodies, is now run with dedication by the well-travelled James Baron (most recently head chef at the Michelin-starred Amber in Hong Kong) and his charming wife Natacha. Entirely done out in Swiss stone pine, the compact dining space brims with atmosphere, further fuelled by the lively energy of the attentive staff. The cuisine is pared down to the essentials and made with top-notch produce, some of it regional. Comprising four, six or eight courses, the set menu features dishes such as pear ravioli, brown butter and sage, or veal, grapes and black salsify. An interesting touch: the cutlery is made by a local blacksmith. Modern Alpine-style guestrooms for overnight stays.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3335628591	Pic Beau-Rivage Palace	Place du Port 17	Switzerland	Lausanne	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.brp.ch/	2 Stars	Creative	5.0	€€€€	t	f	After nearly a year's renovation, French chef Anne-Sophie Pic's luxurious restaurant now welcomes diners with its elegant, bright and modern leather livery overlooking the lake. This exquisite new atmosphere is a perfect match for the light, expressive and almost airy creations of chef Jordan Theurillat. Once past the entrance to the restaurant, there is a table-bar where excellent non-alcoholic cocktails and small plates to combine are prepared, using produce from the garden in particular. Dishes such as the famous ‘Lake Geneva féra impregnated with fig leaf from the garden and spruce, fresh almond cream with amazake’ or ‘venison chop marinated and smoked with juniper berry and imperator root, end-of-summer tomato confit with mace’ clearly express this refined and daring vision of cuisine, with a strong regional inspiration. In four set menus customers will find the same concern for demanding invention that has always linked the history of the Pic family to that of French gastronomy. Quality service.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3335744338	Le Berceau des Sens	Route de Berne 301	Switzerland	Lausanne	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.berceau-des-sens.ch/	1 Star	Modern French, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Lausanne's EHL Hospitality Business School can be proud of this top-notch restaurant. A crack team of chefs (several Meilleurs Ouvriers de France are on the teaching faculty) work with the students to orchestrate a series of dishes that abound with coherent flavours, bringing their classroom learnings to the table! The dishes, which are perfectly poised between classic and modern, demonstrate a mastery of technical skill. From start to finish, each bite is bliss, and the setting also enhances the experience: the bright interior has a superb view of the surrounding mountains. Hats off!	martinooliver	\N	\N
3337596488	Maison Wenger	Rue de la Gare 2	Switzerland	Le Noirmont	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.maisonwenger.ch/	2 Stars	Modern French, French	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Temporarily closed for renovation.Take a drive through the picturesque landscape to this elegant restaurant in a small town in the canton of Jura. Jérémy Desbraux's classical cuisine is impressive – its depth of flavour packs a punch to the palate. There is a coherence to the dishes, with nothing feeling over-egged or contrived. Very pleasant and competent service^ the wine recommendations are excellent. There are also guestrooms for an overnight stay.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3330010380	Skin's - the restaurant	Dammweg 15b	Switzerland	Lenzburg	Air conditioning,Car park	https://skins-restaurant.ch/	2 Stars	Modern Cuisine, Creative	4.0	€€€€	f	t	This restaurant is to be found on the upper floor of a former factory in a rather unlikely location not far from the railway station. The interior is chic and sophisticated^ the open kitchen turns out modern dishes inspired by cuisines from around the world, but also by produce from Switzerland. The patisserie is a highlight! Professional and charming service. Tip: the clever alcohol-free drink pairings.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3333038200	Portuondo	Barrio Portuondo	Spain	Mundaka	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	http://www.restauranteportuondo.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Seafood	3.0	€€€	f	f	A delightful property that stands out for its panoramic views, thanks to its setting overlooking the estuary. The cuisine here showcases top-quality products ranging from fish from the Bermeo auction and primes cuts of meat, all of which are cooked to perfection on the grill.	shirocky	\N	\N
3330336545	Neue Blumenau	Romanshornerstrasse 2	Switzerland	Lömmenschwil	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.neueblumenau.ch/	1 Star	Contemporary, Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	What a lovely place! This attractive building may be a bit out of the way, but it's worth the journey, especially in summer if you can secure a spot on the wonderful garden terrace! It is also pleasant to dine inside, in the elegant restaurant. Whichever space you plump for, you will be treated to courteous service – Bernadette Lisibach, the extremely friendly owner, also makes frequent appearances at the tables. She really puts her heart and soul into running this place, using select ingredients in her fuss-free, tasty and expressive cooking, which leans towards the classical. Diners choose between two set menus. There is a good wine list and a nice selection of cheeses to round off the whole experience.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3333157434	Osteria dell'Enoteca	contrada Maggiore 24	Switzerland	Losone	Car park,Terrace	https://www.osteriaenoteca.ch/	1 Star	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Situated in a quiet residential district, this charming, elegant and modern restaurant is run by a friendly and professional young couple who serve delicious and imaginative contemporary-style cuisine. The dining room is dominated by a large fireplace, while in summer meals are also served alfresco in the flower-filled garden. Works of art grace the premises both indoors and out. Interesting selection of wines from Ticino.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3338433724	Lucide	Europaplatz 1	Switzerland	Lucerne	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.lucide-luzern.ch/	1 Star	Contemporary, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	t	This place ticks all the boxes! It has a central location right by Lake Lucerne, on the first floor of the Culture and Congress Centre, commanding fantastic views of the lake and the city. It boasts a stylish and chic interior. Furthermore, there is a well-staffed, friendly and highly proficient service team. And then there's the food – modern flavoursome dishes made with high-quality ingredients and prepared in an open kitchen. In the evenings, diners have a choice of two four- to six-course set menus, one of which is vegetarian. For lunch, a budget-friendly set menu is available, along with a small selection of items from the evening menu to be ordered à la carte.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3331749097	Maihöfli by UniQuisine	Maihofstrasse 70	Switzerland	Lucerne	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.maihoefli-luzern.ch/	1 Star	Creative, Innovative	5.0	€€€	t	t	Since its reopening, this lovely restaurant just outside the city centre has acquired a new head chef in Robert Steuri. In the evenings, he and his dedicated team showcase precise craftsmanship and top-notch ingredients in two intriguing and innovative three-, five- or seven-course set menus, one of which is vegan. The dishes are full of finesse and carefully composed, elaborate but not cluttered – a great example is the green asparagus, mushrooms, snow peas and beans. Options are more limited at lunchtime. The attractive setting sees the charming features of this old building, such as high ceilings with decorative mouldings and wood panelling, seamlessly integrated into its sleek and elegant modern design. Professional and well-coordinated service.	costasergio	\N	\N
3339995515	Colonnade	Haldenstrasse 10	Switzerland	Lucerne	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/luzern/palace/dine/colonnade	2 Stars	Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	Dating back to 1906, the Mandarin Oriental, situated on the lakeshore, is certainly a stylish setting in which to dine. This restaurant exudes the charm of yesteryear with contemporary elegance. With wonderful Art Nouveau light fittings hanging from the high ceiling, striking marble columns and an almost floor-to-ceiling glazed wine cabinet, the interior is a sight to behold. Chef Gilad Peled and his enthusiastic team showcase their modern take on French cuisine – take, for example, the sweetbreads with peas, asparagus, morels and wild garlic. There are two tasting menus, which can comprise three, five or eight courses (with an optional additional cheese course), one of which is vegetarian. There is an excellent selection of wines from around the globe, and head sommelier Moritz Dresing provides the most astute recommendations. A nice touch: The tasting menu includes a brief visit to the kitchen.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3334614554	THE VIEW	Via Guidino 29	Switzerland	Lugano	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.theviewlugano.com/	1 Star	Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	t	At this restaurant, Diego Della Schiava creates beautifully presented cuisine that is truly a feast for the eyes! This chef’s philosophy focuses on seasonal ingredients, which he transforms into Mediterranean and Swiss dishes with an equal emphasis on meat and fish, including highlights such as the delicious scallop tartare with sesame oil, nasturtiums and porcini mushroom puff. In fine weather, we recommend booking a table on the spacious terrace to enjoy its stunning views of Lugano and the lake.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3336295672	META	Riva Paradiso 2	Switzerland	Lugano	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://metaworld.ch	1 Star	Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian	5.0	€€€€	t	t	Guests feel as though they’re sitting in the lounge of a beautiful private house in this restaurant in Palazzo Mantegazza, which boasts spectacular views of the lake. Here, the kitchen team creates an imaginative and seasonal gourmet menu that showcases local specialities alongside more international dishes.	paganialex	\N	\N
3336289480	Chesa Stüva Colani	Via Principela 20 A	Switzerland	Madulain	Car park,Terrace	https://www.paolocasanova.ch/engadin/restaurantcolani-by-paolocasanova.html	1 Star	Innovative, Italian	3.0	€€€	f	t	The interior boasts an exquisite blend of warm and cosy local wood furnishings and elegant minimalist design. Modern Italian cuisine with a strong connection to the region and the seasons is on a menu showcasing excellent ingredients and the head chef's interesting personal touch. Stylish and charming chalet-style guestrooms are on hand for overnight stays. There is also a bistro.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3330014501	Schlüssel - Nidbergstube	Oberdorfstrasse 5	Switzerland	Mels	Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.schluesselmels.ch/	1 Star	Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	A real institution in the canton of St Gallen. Since 1974, the Kalberer family name has been synonymous with exquisite fine dining. Son Roger has now taken over the reins and continues to run the kitchen in the same vein. Dishes brimming with robust flavours are complemented by a fabulous wine list including a decent selection of Swiss wines and an abundance of French labels. Friendly and well-drilled service team. The cosy, refined interior also hits the right notes, with the small Nidbergstube doing full justice to the historical setting of this elegant patrician house dating back to 1811. This restaurant is named after the Nidberg hill in the village, where wine has been grown since the 15C.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3339037224	Gasthaus Löwen	Holzhäusernstrasse 2	Switzerland	Menzingen	Terrace	https://loewen-menzingen.ch/	1 Star	Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	Dating back to the 16C, Löwen is a lovely traditional inn that has been run by Tanja and Franco Körperich since 2019. She takes care of the service in the charming and elegant wood-panelled dining space on the first floor, and Franco is at the helm in the kitchen. Diners sit at elegantly laid tables to savour a surprise menu comprising four to eight courses, with vegetarian options available if pre-ordered. Top-quality ingredients go into classic dishes that draw on modern and international influences. A shining example is the gently barbecued and mildly spiced king prawn, accompanied by lightly sautéed buck's horn plantain and fine baby peas, all complemented by a tom kha gai beurre blanc with a wonderful aroma and texture. The chef-patron makes a point of offering guidance and presenting his dishes himself. In summer, you can dine al fresco in the pretty Steingarten on the opposite side of the street.	ozmax	\N	\N
3333955564	Stéphane Décotterd	Route de Glion 111	Switzerland	Montreux	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://maisondecotterd.com/restaurant-stephane-decotterd/	1 Star	French Contemporary	5.0	€€€€	t	t	In a premium location on the heights of Montreux, the restaurant of the Glion Institute of Higher Education commands a fantastic view of Lake Geneva and the mountains. The interior is elegant and modern and the service warm and professional. The legible, unpretentious cuisine of Stéphane Décotterd shines the spotlight on Swiss produce (fish from the lake, regional cheese). The chef regales us with wholesome dishes such as free-range poultry from Gruyère cooked in hay, but his star dish is Dry Aged duck reared in Walzenhausen, roasted whole in wine vinegar (order in advance). Business lunch menu available in addition to the à la carte offering.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3332974286	Schlüssel	Hauptstrasse 41	Switzerland	Oberwil	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.schluessel-oberwil.ch/home	1 Star	Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	A meal here is a real pleasure, thanks to Felix Suter and Sandra Marugg Suter, who are truly passionate about what they do – he in the kitchen, she front of house. There are no menus: your extremely cordial hostess will acquaint you with the set menu and explain the dishes. Always on hand, she has a delightfully natural way with guests. Chef-patron Felix Suter (who might be familiar from Säge in Flüh) shows the same passion in his cooking, delivering down-to-earth dishes that prize one thing above all else: flavour! His cooking draws on classical foundations and spurns fleeting modern trends. At lunchtime, a three-course lunch set menu is served. Lovely garden terrace.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3336771902	Restaurant de l'Hôtel de Ville	Place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville 3	Switzerland	Ollon		https://www.hotel-restaurant-ollon.ch/	1 Star	French Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	f	In the centre of the village, near the bell tower, this country house champions tradition in all its glory. Beneath the vaulted ceiling of the dining room, you will be served seasonal French cuisine with a choice of menus and courses. Grégory Halgand conjures up creative dishes such as asparagus, grapefruit and pistachio or Brittany lobster, red beetroot, blackberries and fish bisque. The dessert lineup is the work of Audrey Feutren-Halgand, who also respects the seasons, with delicacies such as a medley of apricots (stewed, jellied and grilled), flanked by a frothy coconut mousse. Artwork (paintings and sculptures) graces the interior, and there is a pleasant outdoor patio for a final alfresco flourish. The ‘café’ offers a brasserie-style menu and a more casual vibe.	semenovirene	\N	\N
3336140351	Gasthaus Zum Gupf	Gupf 21	Switzerland	Rehetobel	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.gupf.ch/	1 Star	Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Perched 1 083m above sea level and reached by a steep, narrow path, this place is a little slice of heaven! The pretty inn with a wood-panelled interior exudes regional charm and boasts a view of the mountains or the lake, plus a wonderful terrace. Walter Klose cooks up aromatic classic cuisine that follows the seasons and combines finesse with a certain unpretentiousness. When it comes to the service, you are in good hands thanks to the excellent team led by the lady of the house, who serves diners with a warm and easy manner. The wine list is sensational – a tour of the wine cellar with over 30 000 bottles is a real experience! You can also spend the night in the pleasant guesthouse.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3334956924	Château Attisholz - Le feu	Attisholzstrasse 3	Switzerland	Riedholz	Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.attisholz.ch/	1 Star	French, Contemporary	4.0	€€€€	f	f	This is a rather grand establishment located just outside Riedholz. A truly splendid historical property houses the exquisitely elegant and tastefully designed fine dining restaurant Le feu, with the garden and courtyard outside being a draw in themselves. Chef-patron Jörg Slaschek proposes a sophisticated modern-classical set menu, but there is also an à la carte selection. It goes without saying that the Bavarian-born chef uses only select produce. A well-curated selection of European wines makes for the perfect accompaniment to your meal. Overnight accommodation is also available: There are really appealing guestrooms that fit perfectly into the overall picture of sophistication.	langalice	\N	\N
3338522824	Regina Montium	Staffelhöhenweg 35	Switzerland	Rigi Kaltbad	Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.kraeuterhotel.ch/	1 Star	Creative, Swiss	3.0	€€€€	f	f	A great place to experience nature untamed – in a sensational location at an altitude of 1 550m! Under the direction of Benedikt Voss, the cuisine is well devised and very technically sophisticated^ refined yet brimming with ideas, it steers well clear of gimmicks and ostentation. Only high-quality, mostly organic produce from Switzerland is used, as well as over 400 different herbs from their own garden. Opt for the alcohol-free drink pairings, which include house-made lemonades. Why not book one of the simple but well-kept guestrooms at the Kräuter Hotel Edelweiss, in which the restaurant is located? To get here from Vitznau, take the Rigi-Bahn railway, which stops just outside the building (station: Staffelhöhe).	beckerradu	\N	\N
3338205564	La Table du Valrose	Place de la Gare 2	Switzerland	Rougemont	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.valrose.ch/	2 Stars	Modern French, Farm to table	3.0	€€€€	f	t	At an altitude of some 1 000m, in the triangle formed by the cantons of Fribourg, Bern and Waad, this restaurant takes you to new heights of culinary enjoyment and refinement. Surrounded by a magnificent mountain landscape, the chic decor is an artful blend of Alpine wood, contemporary furnishings and designer lamps. Chef Benoît Carcenat creates modern and seasonal French cuisine that embraces both tradition and innovation. The menu features produce from the Pays d'Enhaut, Saanenland and Intyamon regions – a host of ingredients that have benefitted from the mountain air! List of 700 different wines for you to choose from. Modern guestrooms, exceptional service and a delicious breakfast round off this delightful experience.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3330701943	Cà d'Oro	Via Mezdi 27	Switzerland	Saint Moritz	Car park,Valet parking	https://www.kempinski.com/stmoritz	1 Star	Alpine, Swiss	4.0	€€€€	t	f	The restaurant in the impressive Grand Hotel des Bains Kempinski St. Moritz exudes classic elegance. From the comfort of your table, beneath the high ceiling with striking chandeliers and moulding, enjoy obliging service in the time-honoured tradition of fine-dining culture. Leopold Ott decamps to Locanda Barbarossa in Ascona in the summer season, and in winter proposes classic-modern cuisine with Mediterranean and international influences – the Cà d'Oro caviar selection is also a mainstay here. Fantastic wine selection.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3330127827	Ecco St. Moritz	Via Maistra 3	Switzerland	Saint Moritz	Car park	https://giardinohotels.ch/	2 Stars	Creative, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Ascona in summer, St Moritz in winter? This is how top chef Rolf Fliegauf and his team do it, changing locations according to the seasons. In the warm season they cook at Ecco on Lake Maggiore and as the snow settles on the ground they migrate to the Engadine valley, to the fine dining restaurant of the Giardino Mountain hotel. You can sense the energy and expertise of this Swabian-born chef – this is cuisine you can rely on! He wins over diners with the light and playful touch he brings to his modern dishes. Throughout the four to seven courses of the set menu, the focus is on the top-notch ingredients. Your highly committed and charming host, Jenifer Fliegauf, is the driving force behind the extremely friendly front-of-house team, ensuring her guests receive attentive and unflappable service.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3338879552	Da Vittorio - St. Moritz	Via Johannes Badrutt 11	Switzerland	Saint Moritz	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://carlton-stmoritz.ch/en/restaurants/da-vittorio-st-moritz	2 Stars	Italian	3.0	€€€€	f	f	If you happen to be in St Moritz in the winter season, then take advantage of the opportunity to dine at the stylish yet cosy restaurant of the Carlton Hotel, in its serene location overlooking the lake. During the winter months, a fantastic kitchen team serves up precise and light Italian cuisine that steers clear of fuss and frills. The focus lies squarely on the produce that goes into the dishes. Some of the brilliantly prepared specialties from the parent restaurant in Brusaporto, Lombardy, make an appearance, including, of course, the signature pasta dish, paccheri alla Vittorio, but also many fish dishes, such as crudo d'Amare, raw fish and shellfish. Plus, an excellent front-of-house team: confident, charming and classy!	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3339169670	Krone	Via Tinus 9	Switzerland	Saint Moritz	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.kronesanktmoritz.com/	1 Star	Italian, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	This long-established restaurant is located in a quiet street a stone's throw from the town centre. With its dark blue fabrics, warm wood finishings and antler chandeliers, the interior is at once upscale and warm and welcoming. The exceedingly friendly service team led by Fabio Rovisi also deserves a mention – charming, efficient and highly organised, they cater to their diners' every need. In the semi-open kitchen, the chefs prepare modern dishes with a strong Italian influence, while also incorporating classic elements. Risotto with horseradish, snails, cashew and raspberry, or scampi with porcini, almonds, wild strawberries and parsley are just two examples of their delicate and elegant creations. There is a five- or seven-course set menu, as well as an à la carte selection.	benesemily	\N	\N
3330835233	Einstein Gourmet	Berneggstrasse 2	Switzerland	Sankt Gallen	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.einstein.ch/de/	2 Stars	Creative, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	t	On the fifth floor of the renowned Hotel Einstein, chefs Sebastian Zier and Richard Schmidtkonz present an international set menu, showcasing exceptional precision and culinary artistry. Over four to six courses, diners are treated to meticulously crafted compositions of impeccably sourced, top-notch ingredients. A prime example is the exquisite French duck breast – bursting with flavour and finesse, cooked to a perfect rosy hue, it offers a delightful contrast of tenderness and texture, complemented by harmonious roast aromas. If you would like a vegetarian alternative, it's best to mention it when you book. In the stylish dining space, the exceptional front-of-house team will attend to you with charm and a laid-back demeanour. When it comes to wine, you are in good hands with sommelier Loris Lenzo, who engages with diners in a relaxed yet professional manner. With 3 000 labels stored in an impressive vaulted wine cellar made of white Bordeaux limestone, he presents the big names as well as the odd hidden gem from Switzerland.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3339471439	Domaine de Châteauvieux	Chemin de Châteauvieux 16	Switzerland	Satigny	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.chateauvieux.ch/	1 Star	Modern French, French	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Courtesy of chef-patron Philippe Chevrier, this institution that is full of soul and character has had a youthful makeover. All the more reason to come to this culinary landmark in the vicinity of Geneva in an ideal location surrounded by vineyards and off the beaten tourist track. Assisted by a seasoned team, Philippe Chevrier crafts refined French cuisine, ranging from modern to classical, based on outstanding produce and instantly identifiable flavours. Attentive service and a wine list that turns out to feature plenty of treats. Enjoy your meal on the idyllic terrace overlooking the hills. Finally, to digest this culinary experience in style, take advantage of the charming, tastefully decorated guestrooms.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3330539477	Gilles Varone	Rue du Stade 5b	Switzerland	Savièse	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://gillesvarone.ch/	1 Star	Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Located in the heart of this quaint village overlooking Sion, this restaurant may appear unassuming from the outside. You would never suspect such culinary delights to be served at the simple wooden tables, showcasing a cuisine that is entirely dedicated to Switzerland and bursting with rich flavours! Following stints with Anton Mosimann, Gordon Ramsay and Claude Bosi in London, owner and head chef Gilles Varone has returned to his homeland to serve up a pleasantly pared-down cuisine, complete with a focus on sustainability. The restaurant itself, with its unpretentious and simple decor, is a perfect match. The front-of-house team win diners over with their charm and expertise. The wine list is exclusively Swiss – alternatively, you could opt for the house-made kombucha.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3331434564	Villa Sommerlust	Rheinhaldenstrasse 8	Switzerland	Schaffhausen	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://sommerlust.ch/	1 Star	Innovative, Creative	4.0	€€€	f	f	Led by two young Spanish chefs, Dan Rodriguez-Zaugg and Alejandro Perez Polo, the kitchen team creates highly innovative, exciting and technically complex dishes, such as Swiss Alpine pike-perch ceviche with white soya mayonnaise and jalapeños. The menu showcases a blend of Spanish avant-garde, South American and Asian culinary influences. There is a four- to eight-course set menu with a vegetarian alternative. Options are simpler and more limited at lunchtime, but the evening menu can also be made available upon prior request. Friendly and adept service. The restaurant is housed in a charming villa, just a street away from the Rhine. If you can't get a table on the fabulous garden terrace, the Orangerie is a delightful alternative – with its light and airy atmosphere, it makes you feel almost like you're dining al fresco. Stylish cigar lounge on the first floor.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
