3332267940	Baie	30 rue de la Ferté	France	Saint-Valery-sur-Somme		https://www.restaurantbaie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This tiny restaurant, which has only two tables for guests, proposes a short menu and sources its produce from suppliers who lie within a strict 100km radius. The natural ingredients are prepared without gimmicks, as in the monkfish roasted on the bone. Add to that the friendly welcome and you have one of the best places to eat in town. Given all that, you should really book!	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3333374799	Nozawa Bar	212 N. Cañon Dr.	USA	Beverly Hills	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking	https://www.nozawabar.com	1 Star	Japanese, Sushi	4.0	$$$$	f	f	Nozawa Bar is secreted away in the back of the Beverly Hills location of Sugarfish, yet this jewel box is entirely independent of the local chain it's housed within.Omakase is the sole dining option here, served as multiple courses of nigiri along with some sashimi and handrolls. Each sequence centers on exceptional seafood, most of it sourced from local waters. Chef Osamu Fujita may be a traditionalist, but the menu includes many novelties. Start with the perfectly crunchy jellyfish dressed with ponzu. This might be followed by an impressive presentation of deliciously tender slivered octopus. Sushi highlights include the delicate halibut fin, ruby-red snapper cut before your eyes and a handroll of mountain yam, ume and shiso leaf.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3333954983	Frasca Food and Wine	1738 Pearl St.	USA	Boulder	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.frascafoodandwine.com/	1 Star	Italian, Regional Cuisine	4.0	$$$$	t	f	This sleek restaurant is set in the heart of downtown Boulder on a charming street lined with shops and restaurants. All are treated as special guests here, where the cooking is Italian, but in a hyper-specific way: it's the food of the northeast Italian region of Friuli Venezia Giulia. You'll find pasta and seafood on the prix fixe and tasting menus, but Slavic and Alpine elements also appear. Focused and distinct, the menu might showcase a lesser known part of Italy, but the ingredients are clearly Coloradan. The plates are beguiling with a minimal, straightforward approach, as in cjalson, half-moon fresh spinach pasta pockets filled with an English pea and potato purée. Save room for dessert, like the beautifully arranged goat cheese semifreddo.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3339471991	Al Braciere	Via Livurcio 50	Switzerland	Ronco sopra Ascona	Car park,Great view,Terrace	http://www.albraciere.ch	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Situated just above Ascona, about 1km from the town centre, this friendly hotel boasts panoramic views of Lake Maggiore, the surrounding mountains and the island of Brissago. Enjoy modern, carefully prepared cuisine in the comfortable dining room or on the idyllic outdoor terrace in summer.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3339411529	The Four Horsemen	295 Grand St.	USA	Brooklyn	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.fourhorsemenbk.com/	1 Star	American, Californian	5.0	$$$$	t	f	Reservations are required or be ready to queue at this eternally cool Williamsburg wine bar part-owned by LCD Soundsystem frontman, James Murphy. Four Horseman's wine list is eclectic and laser-focused on varietals, and Chef Nick Curtola's succinct and seasonally changing menu rarely misses.Start with the veal sweetbread skewers with soy-cured egg yolk. Or the crisp chickpea crepe, woven with pieces of squash blossoms that lures you in with a layer of glistening lardon. Fried skate wing comes to you deep golden and impossibly crisp, and the Berkshire pork is tender with a hint of cider glaze. Let the sociable staff talk you into closing over a silky crème caramel topped with deeply toasted crispy bits of soba.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3332038878	Le Domaine de Saint-Géry	Le Domaine de Saint-Géry	France	Lascabanes	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.saint-gery.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	Self - proclaimed ‘farmer - chef’, Patrick Duler does not mess around with the origin of his ingredients. Much of what is on your plate – ham from black pigs, truffles, foie gras – comes straight from his own fields! His simple, meticulous dishes reveal the soul of a truly passionate chef.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3333783814	Francie	134 Broadway	USA	Brooklyn	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.franciebrooklyn.com/	1 Star	Contemporary, Italian	5.0	$$$$	f	f	Francie is headed by John Winterman and native New Yorker, Chef Chris Cipollone. Set within a striking, limestone-clad building in South Williamsburg, this haven features sleek ash wood and mosaic tile flooring, exposed red brick walls, and widely spaced tables.The open kitchen is a true-to-life stage for this team, who can be seen prepping, cooking, and putting the finishing touches on a series of Mediterranean-style plates. Pasta is a must, as in the conchiglie with a luscious clam sauce. Shelled clams, bits of bacon, and sesame breadcrumbs complete the delightful preparation. Lamb is a springtime treat when dressed with green garlic persillade and young onion soubise. Caramelized apple atop buttery cake with crème fraîche and green apple brunoise is a fine finale to the array of impressive cuisine offered here.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3339623402	Clover Hill	20 Columbia Pl.	USA	Brooklyn	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.cloverhillbk.com/	1 Star	Contemporary, Latin American	3.0	$$$$	t	f	Squirreled away on a quiet street in Brooklyn Heights, this intimate restaurant is a charming box of elegance and comfort. Under the leadership of Chef Sam Rogers, this tiny but mighty kitchen now enters a new chapter. He and his team are a focused bunch, working in perfect sync to deliver an abundance of courses that draw inspiration from Latin America. Little tarts stacked with poblano peppers and guanciale give way to a single boiled potato coated in a Huancaína-inspired sauce flecked with caviar. Find spice and smoke deployed across a range of local fish and American wagyu, with one highlight being a grilled, dry-aged sirloin paired with a stunning cabbage puree. Service matches the setting, quiet and calm in all the right ways.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3331523578	Restaurant Yuu	55 Nassau Ave.	USA	Brooklyn	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.yuunewyork.com/restaurantyuu/?fbclid=IwAR3V1uhGIP6q5V_4R9aiSpCHhy7UkIedQQVwU0EzQCrrjGCwWCubFS0jUDw	1 Star	French Contemporary, Japanese	5.0	$$$$	t	f	At the start of service, the lights dim and servers pull back curtains to reveal the full kitchen team dressed in stark whites and standing at attention. This is just the beginning of a carefully choreographed performance by Chef Yuu Shimano, whose classic French training and Japanese heritage translates to beauty and boldness on the plate. The lengthy menu celebrates top-grade shellfish and proteins that waver between light and indulgent. Think smoked surf clam with celeriac or abalone risotto with nori powder. The signature duck and foie pastry is a treasure from another era, while a pre-dessert “mojito” is a sweet flash of modern-day brilliance. The warehouse-chic space is impressive in scale and carefully tended to by a quiet but attentive team.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3335037647	Shota Omakase	50 S. 3rd St.	USA	Brooklyn	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.shotaomakase.com/	1 Star	Japanese, Sushi	4.0	$$$$	t	f	Far from the subway stop on a quiet street in Williamsburg, find this welcoming omakase counter hidden away near Domino Park. Chef Cheng Lin sets the tone as a friendly, relaxed guide for the night’s proceedings. And whereas some chefs practically take vows of silence with regards to sourcing and technique, he is quick to share where in Japan the fish is from, why he uses Inochi-no Ichi rice, and what it took to find his special aged soys and vinegars. His intentionality delivers in the form of excellent, seasonal product and a fine-tuned parade of nigiri, for which the rice is refreshed repeatedly. Prepared dishes like binchotan-seared sawara with citrus sauce, shiso, and nori or even a restorative cup of dashi with mushrooms also show distinction.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
