3338433797	Brandstätter	Münchner Bundesstraße 69	Austria	Salzburg	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.hotel-brandstaetter.com/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, International	3.0	€€€	f	f	A real Salzburg institution! The atmosphere in the various dining areas is perfect for a cosy dinner, but in the summer, you might prefer to sit out on the gorgeous terrace. Traditional Austrian fare dominates the menu, but you will also find dishes that take their cue from the seasons or from global culinary trends. The service comes courtesy of an attentive and well-drilled front-of-house team. Good to know: You can buy house-made jams to take home.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3336627051	Gasthof Auerhahn	Bahnhofstraße 15	Austria	Salzburg	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://auerhahn-salzburg.at/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Run with great dedication, this friendly, family-owned restaurant is located at a slight remove from the city centre, close to the train station, but it's well worth making the detour for the excellent food. The cuisine is regional, seasonal and pleasingly down-to-earth. Their appealing range of dishes includes venison ragout with bread dumplings and chanterelles, as well as delicious desserts such as Topfenknödel (curd dumplings). Order à la carte or opt for the set menu, which comprises three to five courses – a vegetarian version is also available. Dine in the inviting interior or out on the charming terrace to the rear of the building. The adjoining hotel has well-appointed guestrooms.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3334859532	Paradoxon	Zugallistraße 7	Austria	Salzburg	Brunch	https://www.restaurant-paradoxon.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€€	t	t	The atmosphere here is pleasantly down-to-earth, and the waitstaff laid-back and friendly. The cuisine is modern and seasonal. Along with à la carte options such as char ceviche or local ribeye steak, there is a set menu comprising four or six courses. Tip: Brunch is also served on Sat and Sun (10am-2pm). N.B. cash payments only. The restaurant also has an online shop selling home-made goods (sauces, pesto, jam etc), as well as beer and wine.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3335939933	Brunnauer	Fürstenallee 5	Austria	Salzburg	Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-brunnauer.at/de/startseite/	Nessun premio	French, Country cooking	3.0	€€€€	f	f	In the lovely historical setting of Villa Ceconi, Sybille and Richard Brunnauer's restaurant is the place to experience fantastic Austrian-style hospitality and cuisine. The dishes draw on French and international influences but give pride of place to the region and the seasons – vegan options included. Tip: reasonably priced lunch set menu. Attractive and stylishly modern interior and a fabulous view of the fortress from the terrace!	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3337970581	Animo by Aigner	Nonntaler Hauptstraße 55	Austria	Salzburg	Terrace	https://www.animobyaigner.at/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Having worked together at Hangar 7, Elisabeth (Lizzy) and Jakob Aigner have now opened their own place here, introducing a charming new concept to the area. While he presides front-of-house, providing friendly and attentive service and astute wine recommendations, she prepares Mediterranean fare in the kitchen. Made from the finest ingredients, her dishes are flavoursome and unfussy – the offerings are written up on a blackboard. The terrace is delightful in summer.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3336295187	Die Gersberg Alm	Gersberg 37	Austria	Salzburg	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	http://www.gersbergalm.at	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Austrian	3.0	€€	t	t	This restaurant overlooking Salzburg boasts a wonderful location and stunning views. The atmosphere in the pretty wood-panelled dining area is cosy. The cuisine is rooted in the region but also draws on international influences, with a house speciality of Zitronen-Rahm-Herz vom Milchkalb (milk-fed calf's heart in a creamy lemon sauce) featured alongside dishes such as venison yellow curry served with spiced rice. There are set menus, one of which is vegetarian, an à la carte menu and an additional afternoon snack menu – there really is something for everyone. This lovely spot, which is also a favourite among locals, is housed in the hotel of the same name.	calincolin	\N	\N
3334250733	Zum Buberl Gut	Gneiser Straße 31	Austria	Salzburg	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.buberlgut.at/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	f	More than just a pretty face, this gorgeous 17C country estate, located on the outskirts of the city, is also a delightful setting for a delicious meal. The cosy interior marries classic elegance with charming regional touches, creating a welcoming atmosphere. In the summer, the lovely garden beckons. The cuisine is a flavoursome blend of Austrian and Mediterranean influences. The wine list, too, is definitely worth a look. Tip: Come at lunchtime for the small, moderately priced menu available.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3333991403	Hospiz Alm	St. Christoph 18	Austria	Sankt Anton am Arlberg	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.arlberghospiz-alm.at/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Just so you know: This place is a haven for wine connoisseurs! The Gothic wine cellar is a real treasure trove, boasting a unique collection of large bottles that is world-famous, not least for its Bordeaux selection. Magnums, primats: you name it, they have it. Be sure to take a look at the impressive Wine Dome with its private dining table for exclusive tastings. In the restaurant itself, a typical ski hut feel prevails at lunchtime, but in the evening, it's all about fine dining in a lovely cosy setting brimming with Alpine charm.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3338843660	Verwallstube	Kandaharweg 9	Austria	Sankt Anton am Arlberg	Great view,Terrace	http://www.verwallstube.at/de/	Nessun premio	International, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	At an elevation of 2 085m, the gondola ride up here (free with your reservation) is even worthwhile for non-skiers. In addition to the breathtaking view, you can expect ambitious cuisine made from high-quality ingredients that doesn't limit itself to a specific style – rather it showcases traditional, regional, Mediterranean and even Asian influences. Appetising options include yellowfin tuna sashimi, Wiener schnitzel and risotto alla carbonara. The exceedingly friendly and charming waitstaff will be happy to recommend the right wine from the extensive list.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3336157276	Endlich	Dorfstraße 61	Austria	Sankt Anton am Arlberg		https://endlich-arlberg.at	Nessun premio	Scandinavian, Contemporary	3.0	€€€	t	t	Coming here is like being invited to dine with good friends in their home – such is the feeling conveyed by your very friendly hosts, Henrik Helmuth Olsen and Henriette Hansen, who are the couple at the helm here. In their modern, tastefully decorated restaurant, the Danish-born owners create an incredibly charming, intimate atmosphere and make a point of doting on their guests. There is no menu or wine list. Instead, Henrik prepares a surprise menu made up of three courses, while Henriette is on hand to recommend the wines to best accompany your meal.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3330656259	Keplingerwirt	Sankt Johann am Wimberg 14	Austria	Sankt Johann am Wimberg	Car park,Terrace	https://www.keplingerwirt.at/	Nessun premio	Contemporary, Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant, which has been run as a family business since 1938, is the beating heart of this modern hotel with welcoming guestrooms. Diners can expect a refined atmosphere and exceedingly friendly service, as well as delicious food prepared by a kitchen brigade headed up by chef Andrea Lunson, sister of owner Heinz Keplinger. On the menu: traditional dishes such as Kalbsrahmbeuscherl (creamed chopped calf's lights) with bread dumpling, but also more modern fare, eg fillet of Piberbach salmon trout in a ratatouille broth with Erbsentascherl (pea pasties) and a coconut-chilli foam.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3330271122	Broadmoar	Oisnitz 36	Austria	Sankt Joseph	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://Www.broadmoar.com	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€€€	f	t	This country house, accessible via a narrow driveway, is in a truly idyllic location with stables and paddocks, surrounded by woods and meadows. The food is seasonal and regional, served à la carte or in the form of a set menu. By the way, the dishes are presented on handmade ceramics. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, a moderately priced, slightly shorter set menu is available. The waitstaff are friendly and well-organised, and the wine recommendations are always spot on. Given the beautiful setting, tables on the terrace are coveted – especially in summer.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3333080037	La Torre	Grabenstraße 39	Austria	Sankt Veit an der Glan		http://www.latorre.at/	Nessun premio	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	The keep of the medieval St Veit fortress is a truly remarkable setting. Nestled within the historic walls and surrounded by greenery, the small terrace is a particular highlight. This restaurant is run by husband-and-wife team Rosemarie and Ammar Trabelsi, who create a welcoming atmosphere with a personal touch. The Sicilian presides front-of-house and has charm in his blood. His dapper, old-school style is anything but stuffy. She is in charge of the kitchen and cooks up ambitious Italian and Mediterranean cuisine using select ingredients. Her dishes are pared down to just a few components, allowing their natural flavours to shine through. Turbot with samphire and datterini tomatoes or house-made paccheri with wild prawns, tomatoes and rocket are prime examples. Fish and seafood take centre stage and vary depending on what the market has to offer. The tasting menu is definitely worthwhile, but you can also order à la carte. Italian wine list.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3335195826	Greisslerei beim Taubenkobel	Hauptstraße 31	Austria	Schützen am Gebirge	Credit cards not accepted,Terrace	https://www.taubenkobel.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Classic French	5.0	€€	t	t	Barbara Eselböck and Alain Weissgerber offer a delightful alternative to Taubenkobel restaurant with this charming eatery located in the adjacent building. The atmosphere is friendly, relaxed and completely unpretentious, and the food is simply delicious. Select ingredients go into flavoursome dishes such as Alsace-style snails, Wiener schnitzel and gnocchi with fresh truffles. The interior is wonderfully cosy and has a vintage feel to it, with charming decorative touches and shelves displaying house-made and Pannonian food items, as well as regional wines. By the entrance, there is a counter displaying desserts. A small terrace shaded by an old tree is just outside.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3334535461	Hirschen	Hof 14	Austria	Schwarzenberg	Car park,Terrace	https://www.hotel-hirschen-bregenzerwald.at/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	The concept of sustainability shines through in Jonathan Burger's cuisine. Ingredients are sourced in the region, the fruit and vegetables are predominantly organic or grown by neighbouring farmers, and a nose-to-tail approach is applied to all produce. The latter philosophy is evident, for example, in a dish of grilled chicken hearts, pumpkin, Schupfnudeln (finger-shaped potato dumplings). They also conjure up vegetarian fare, especially in winter when in-house fermentation methods play a major role – for example, their Vetterhof radish with gochugaru and miso broth. The setting is also beautiful: Housed in the Hirschen hotel, a hub of art and tradition that dates back to 1755, the restaurant's tastefully decorated dining rooms draw on a sense of history. At lunchtime, only salads, light bites and cakes are served.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3333943945	AD VINUM	Schmiedhofstraße 2	Austria	Sölden	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ad-vinum.at/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	f	This restaurant done out in a chic modern-Alpine style is part of the small Chalet Resort Sölden, which boasts five cosy and tastefully decorated log cabins. From 3pm, classic fare in the vein of braised veal cheeks or beef tartare is served^ from 7pm, the interesting set menu comprising four, six or seven courses features dishes such as salmon trout, baby leek, verjus, hazelnut, or shoulder shank, sweet potato, savoy cabbage, pepper. The produce used is almost exclusively regional, as the exceptionally friendly, well-trained and attentive service team will explain when talking you through the menu. Be sure to ask for their recommendations when it comes to the wine list of around 150 labels, including many from Austria.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3337039438	Black Sheep	Dorfstraße 114	Austria	Sölden	Car park	https://www.bergland-soelden.at/de/kulinarik/black-sheep	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€€€€	t	t	The fine dining restaurant of Bergland hotel boasts a chic interior with a stylish dark colour scheme. The cuisine is entirely dedicated to the Alpine region. Ingredients are sourced within a 200km radius, with Austria and South Tyrol being the main suppliers. Much of the produce comes from the immediate vicinity, including herbs from the restaurant's own garden. They even raise their own sheep. The cooking style is very contemporary and incorporates subtle Japanese influences. For example, the six-course set menu includes dishes such as Alpine prawn katsuobushi with tomato and yuzu bisque, or Tyrolean catfish and broad beans.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3334047692	FUXBAU	Dorfstraße 22	Austria	Stuben am Arlberg	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-fuxbau.at/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This building's traditional shingle façade demonstrates its affinity with the region, as does its smart interior drawing on modern straight lines and natural materials such as wood and stone. Markus Grittle conjures up cuisine that also takes its cue from the region. In the evening, the interesting set menu is formed of three to five courses (dishes include THE ELEGANT FISH – sturgeon, carrot, purslane)^ at lunchtime, a three-course version is served. Slightly more traditional fare is available à la carte. The terrace affords a view of the ski slopes. Overnight accommodation is to be had at the Fuxbau Lodges and, just around the corner, the Das Johann hotel, through which you can also book the Arlberg Lodges.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3339187162	OKTO	26 rue du Vieux-Palais	France	Rouen	Terrace	http://www.okto-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Just a stone's throw from the Place du Vieux Marché, this navy blue storefront certainly catches the eye. A couple of industry professionals, Laure Touyre on the restaurant floor and Brice Legrand in the kitchen, serve up modern, accomplished cuisine. The menu focuses on just a few items, allowing the chef to cook market-fresh cuisine with top-quality ingredients, such as line-caught meagre and green asparagus – delicious and aromatic. A contemporary bistro with a clear sense of identity^ friendly, smiling service.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3334247310	Altes Gericht	Taverneweg 1	Austria	Sulz	Car park,Terrace	https://www.romantikhotels.com/de/hotels/romantik-restaurant-altes-gericht/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The building itself is really quite something. Dating back to the 13C, this former courthouse – also known as the Schmiedhaus – has retained its original charm both on the outside and in its five dining areas, which feature plenty of old wood and historical details. A cosy atmosphere prevails throughout. Diners are served cuisine in a classical vein that draws on high-quality ingredients. Think variations of scallop – carpaccio au gratin and crispy scallop on a bed of mango and avocado salad. In summer, the garden planted with chestnut trees makes for a romantic setting.	benesemily	\N	\N
3339844097	Goldader - Alpine Kulinarik	Gewerbepark Litzelsdorf 281	Austria	Tamsweg	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.goldader.at/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Austrian	3.0	€€€	f	f	Housed in a modern building in a rural setting, this is an interesting location. The interior is stylish and minimalist with a soothing colour scheme – don't miss your chance to take in the lovely view from the terrace. The dishes served here are a modern take on Austrian cuisine showcasing the finest local ingredients including game and fresh trout. There is a tasting menu with a flexible number of courses. Friendly and attentive service.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3334519577	Bergfried - Chefs Table	Lanersbach 483	Austria	Tux	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://www.bergfried.at/kulinarik/chefs-table-tastingmenue.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	You're right in the thick of it here! From the high tables in this stylish little space, you have a constant view of the bustling activity in the kitchen – there's a lot to see! The way the individual dishes are presented is also rather unique: with background music and a proper explanation - the service is somewhat in family hands. All in all, an entertaining evening and a culinary adventure are guaranteed! Chef Sebastian Stock proposes a seven-course set menu (supplemented by two surprise courses). His dishes are modern, clearly structured and made from predominantly locally sourced ingredients. When it comes to wine, you can rely on Franz Stock's recommendations. The best place for an aperitif is the cosy bar of Hotel Bergfried, which houses the restaurant.	donatidiego	\N	\N
