3332426423	't Overhamme	Brusselsesteenweg 163	Belgium	Aalst	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.toverhamme.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Patrick and Anne’s villa has been a magnet for foodies since 1991. Bold wall coverings and a designer edge add a quizzical spin to their impressive establishment, whose terrace overlooks a magnificent, landscaped garden. Chef Bogaert rolls out a classical lineup, such as quail with foie gras or hare à la royale but is not averse to playing a more modern tune, adding tangy fresh notes to his nattily crafted side dishes.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3336428131	Cul'eau	Gentsesteenweg 177	Belgium	Aalst	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.culeau.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€€	t	t	Kick off the evening in style with an aperitif and nibbles, before sampling Master Karim’s excellent nosh. The extensive menu of this modern brasserie reads like a classical cookery book with vol-au-vent and sole meunière, together with aged meat and the plating is exquisite. Spot-on cooking, entirely from scratch and jazzed up with occasional inspired note. Connoisseurs will drool over the wine list!	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3336230391	't Vijfde Seizoen	Stationsstraat 9	Belgium	Aalter	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.tvijfdeseizoen.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Broes Tavernier hails his suppliers as “heroes”, which speaks volumes for his commitment to locally sourced produce. From asparagus and fish from the North Sea to partridges, he unfailingly selects the best. His creative, high-flying approach to cooking aims to let the ingredients shout their name. We recommend the insightful wine-food pairing suggestions. After a fine meal in this friendly establishment (great patio), pop into Eetalage and take a few goodies home.	carlinikita	\N	\N
3331142817	Calla's	Stationsstraat 250	Belgium	Aalter	Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-callas.be	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Calla’s immerses you in an enchanting Art deco ambience. In the heart of Aalter, this former solicitor’s home (1930) flanked by a delightful garden, is the epitome of cosy. The dishes to share bear witness to Niels Landtsheer’s creative streak, illustrated by sucrine salad leaf stuffed with subtly spiced North Sea crab and briny seaweed. Niels’ classical background comes to the forefront in recipes such as his rich vol-au-vent. Gutsy, big-boned flavours are the hallmark of this talented craftsman.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3339016204	Cinq	route de Lennik 361	Belgium	Anderlecht	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.resto-cinq.be/nl/	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€€	t	t	The young and not so young come here to be spoiled rotten in this contemporary villa near the ring road of Brussels. Chef Verzele rustles up a varied menu in tune with the zeitgeist, adding a new spin to his classical background. Examples include perfectly poached fillets of sole, paired with fried prawns, a velvety saffron-flavoured risotto and a knockout fish sauce. Cinq is the sort of place that invites you to dig into meals steeped in gutsy, big-boned flavours whilst enjoying the casual buzzy vibe. Should you have cause for celebration, we can recommend the lobster menu.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3338785996	Moma	Chaussée de Namur 72	Belgium	Annevoie-Rouillon	Great view,Terrace	https://www.restaurantmoma.be	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	The view of the River Meuse and its lush green banks immediately catches the eye as you enter Moma. Olivier Bruckner reveals his flair for enhancing each dish with subtle details, like a sweet-sour tomato and rich creamy burrata which provide the perfect foil to lacquered calf sweetbread. The menu features classical and gastronomic recipes, all of which are enticingly displayed thanks to inspired plating and at gloriously eater-friendly prices.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3330319541	Black Smoke	Boomgaardstraat 1	Belgium	Antwerpen		https://www.blacksmoke.be/	Nessun premio	Barbecue	4.0	€€€	t	f	Black Smoke packs a distinctly American punch. The dimly lit, unpolished, rough and rugged interior is steeped in the smoky aroma of BBQ. The pitmasters have perfected the art of grilled meat in true Texan fashion. Traditional techniques, Latino influences and local produce for meals rich in big-boned, heart-warming flavours. Examples include lamb tacos jazzed up with a spicy za’atar, jalapeno pepper and fresh lemon. Or how about a cut of premium beef from the De Laet & Van Haver butcher’s shop? The drinks menu is practically as long as the food menu, while the ‘Bonanza Experience’ is billed as the ultimate sharing experience! So, let’s crank up the heat!	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3337924632	Qin	De Keyserlei 66	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurantqin.be/	Nessun premio	Cantonese, Chinese Contemporary	4.0	€€	t	f	Emperor Qin provided the inspiration for the team at the helm of the restaurant of Hotel Keiser, hence the dark wood furnishings, soft red fabrics and oriental details like Chinese lanterns and paintings. The Cantonese culinary lineup is the quintessence of authentic, albeit subtly updated to suit today’s palates. The varied range of home-made dim sum dishes are characteristic of this ethos. Stuffed with chopped wagyu beef and a black pepper Chinese sauce, or with ginger and taro - piping hot delicacies that embody the generous character of this aromatic cuisine.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3330374767	Cuichine	Draakplaats 3	Belgium	Antwerpen	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.cuichine.be/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	€€	f	f	House-made Peking duck with crispy skin, fresh veggies and pancakes ready to be stuffed, all of which flanked by a gutsy sweet and sour hoisin sauce. This signature dish embodies the philosophy of Cuichine: a modern version of old-school Chinese nosh, starring all our favourite Cantonese recipes. The interior of this eye-catching establishment is ideally suited to the trendy vibe and the restaurant also boasts a pleasant terrace.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3337661945	Bar(t)-à-vin	Lange Slachterijstraat 3	Belgium	Antwerpen		https://www.bartavin.be/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Authentic, polished and vintage – such is the vibe of this delightful bistro, quirkily established in a former butchery, as the colourful wall tiles and meat hooks bear witness. The concise menu is a guarantee of quality. Pedigree Gallic standards like steak tartare or less common dishes like a stew of girolle mushrooms, sea lavender and poached egg are crafted with text-book precision, blessedly free of fripperies and packed in punchy flavour. Ask Bart, a walking wine encyclopaedia, for his insightful tips to help you choose just the right tipple to pair with your meal. At the weekends, Bart Gils and Sally Lauwers run the joint, in line with its founding DNA.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3338870715	Minerva	Karel Oomsstraat 36	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurantminerva.be/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Minerva was a legendary Belgian luxury automobile firm, whose repair workshops were located here. The site is now that of a well-oiled restaurant, whose outer industrial casing hides a warm, even stylish interior. The menu abounds in pedigree gourmet classics, prepared with textbook skill and flair, even the meat is still carved at the table. The turbot is cooked on the bone and served with a light frothy mustardy sauce, unless you wouldn’t prefer Barbary duck, carved in front of you, and garnished with a sauce that is made from blood and bone marrow that is extracted by way of a press – heroically wondrous! At Minerva, quality is much more than a word – it is a way of life!	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3337779256	Yue Jing Xuan	68F	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.hyatt.com/en-US/hotel/china/park-hyatt-guangzhou/guaph/dining	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Diners get to take in lovely city views, as well as the action in the open kitchen – the chefs, flames, aromas and dynamic energy of the team. The chef has nearly 20 years' experience and his sand ginger chicken is famed for its thick, tender flesh: he uses only 225-day-old free-range birds from Zhanjiang. Try also the crispy roast pork belly or honey-glazed sleeper goby. Besides the main menu, ask the servers about seasonal dishes.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3336268943	Bistrot L'îlot	Kribbestraat 15	Belgium	Antwerpen	Terrace	https://bistrotlilot.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, French Contemporary	4.0	€€	f	f	A Parisian vibe mixed with industrial and minimalist details sets the welcoming scene. “What you see is what you get” is their motto! The chef intertwines international inspirations and punchy flavours as he orchestrates a mouth-watering score. He gives flawlessly steamed halibut a playful edge by flanking it with a range of mushroom textures and an expressive buttermilk crème. Rather than fussy frills, you can expect dishes in the zeitgeist and a splendid selection of (mainly French) wines.	ferraroedoardo	\N	\N
3330120471	September.	Minderbroedersrui 7	Belgium	Antwerpen	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://septemberlokaal.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Vegetarian	3.0	€€€	f	t	As you step over the threshold of September, you will immediately find yourself immersed in its zenitude. A stripped-back, minimalist vibe depicts the spacious interior, which is dotted with plants and has soft music playing in the background. It’s as if nature has merged with inner city Antwerp. Every detail of this establishment has been puzzled over and preened from its respect for the produce and attention to the seasons down to the ‘farm to fork’ concept. Veggies are the stars of the show, sometimes served with meat or fish. Ann Van der Auwera’s inventive, expressive cuisine is bold and distinctive and occasionally sprinkled with the odd Italian or Japanese accent. Intense umami flavours are frequently paired with fresh Mediterranean ingredients. It is summertime at September all year round!	giulianijames	\N	\N
3333727117	GLASS	Vlaamsekaai 40	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning	https://wijnbistro-glass.be/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, Classic French	4.0	€€€	t	f	Wine bistro GLASS is elegant and cosy – make a beeline for the terrace on Vlaamse Kaai if you really want to soak up the hip atmosphere of the Zuid neighbourhood. Sally, who presides front-of-house, consistently proves that she is a hostess at heart, while chef Alain showcases his versatility. His cuisine is intricate and draws inspiration from both Eastern and Western culinary traditions. Think house-made pasta stuffed with potato and truffle, paired with ginger and five-spice chicken, Chinese cabbage, a creamy truffle sauce and foie gras. He balances rich flavours with a sure touch, creating ingredient-led cuisine that is truly captivating.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3335957498	Nage	Reyndersstraat 17	Belgium	Antwerpen		https://www.restaurantnage.be/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, Creative	3.0	€€€	t	f	The character of this medieval mansion has been intelligently enhanced by the cosy, trendy revamp. Niki shares his know-how in terms of choice of excellent natural wines to pair with the modern French recipes crafted by Koen. The chef sprinkles his cooking with the occasional unexpected note in a bid to further highlight the ingredients’ authentic flavours. Examples include saddle of lamb cooked in butter with suave, flavoursome side dishes based on wild garlic. A word of warning: à la carte only at lunchtime and set menu only in the evening.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3338558298	Cella	Kattendijkdok-Oostkaai 21b	Belgium	Antwerpen	Great view,Terrace	https://cella.be/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, International	5.0	€€€	f	f	One half of the restaurant commands a view of the kitchen team crafting all sorts delicacies, while the other overlooks the Antwerp docks and skyline. There is never a dull moment at Cella, starting with the industrial cachet of this stylishly repurposed warehouse by the team that used to run Het Pomphuis. The menu features a tempting lineup of pedigree Belgian fare with matured meat grilled over charcoal embers, fresh fries and a last-minute sauce, together with a smattering of ubiquitous international dishes of the likes of ceviche and sushi. Flawless technique and aromatic sauces are the hallmark of the gifted chef.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3334933067	Bistrot de Pottenbrug	Minderbroedersrui 38	Belgium	Antwerpen	Terrace	https://www.bistrotdepottenbrug.be/	Nessun premio	French, Belgian	4.0	€€€€	t	f	This former café’s wooden bar counter, floral wallpaper, wainscoting and old wood-burning stove set the quintessentially Parisian bistro scene of this characterful town house, providing the perfect foil to a soul-warming culinary score that stars outstanding ingredients. Vincent Greeve enjoys crafting gutsy, big-boned recipes, exemplified by a melt-in-the-mouth house terrine of foie gras with onion preserve or a Rossini steak with a punchy port wine sauce, all of which define the chef’s consummate culinary technique. The Pottenbrug sings a splendid ode to fine produce.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3334584760	Pazzo	Oude Leeuwenrui 12	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://pazzo.be/	Nessun premio	Fusion, Italian Contemporary	4.0	€€€	t	f	Ingrid Neven’s jovial, casual eatery with a separate patio is well-known among foodies for its international score and superb wine list (wine bar above the restaurant). Ingrid avows a weakness for Italian recipes and truffles, without forgetting Asian and Middle Eastern notes. The extensive menu features dishes such as risotto al dente with black truffle, Korean-style gnocchi and seabass in mandarin and cardamon. A seasoned chef, Ingrid lures us back with her playful, unconventional approach to cooking.	donatidiego	\N	\N
3339441283	Ferrier 30	Leopold de Waelplaats 30	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.ferrier-30.be/nl/home	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	t	The stylish Ferrier 30 will immerse you in the buzzy, hipster vibe of the Zuid. The terrace opposite the Fine Arts Museum attracts diners like bees to honey in fine weather. The venue is ideally suited to the text-book perfect classical Italian recipes. Truffle-flavoured home-made pasta, slowly braised ossobuco… An explosion of Italian aromas and flavours!	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3335666954	Upton	Napelsstraat 42	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://upton.be/	Nessun premio	Italian, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Upton is a hip eatery in a buzzy neighbourhood. Experienced chef, Gianfranco Van de Maele, invites you to sample his globe-trotting approach to food. Start with a cold glass of draught lager, before digging into his succulent fresh pasta, the recipes of which come from his “nonna”. Bisque-flavoured homemade spaghetti and super fresh seafood and shellfish – magnifico! A fascinating modern culinary melting pot that blends Italian authenticity with Asian influences gleaned from his travels.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3330551437	RAS	Ernest Van Dijckkaai 37	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ras.today/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	The view of the Scheldt River and the docks makes this restaurant's terrace one of the finest in Antwerp! Thanks to all the windows, the water feels omnipresent, even if you are seated inside. Charcoal sketches by Rinus Van de Velde lend an arty feel to the sleek interior. The extensive menu is dominated by traditional favourites. The fried sole is an obvious classic, but for something truly special, try the crispy veal sweetbreads in a brown stock and port sauce. The generous portions certainly go down well. And for those in a hurry, a quick lunch is always available, too.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3337693663	InVINcible	Haarstraat 7	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning	https://www.invincible.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative French	3.0	€€€	t	t	Take a seat at the counter and soak up the warm atmosphere of inVINcible. You can admire chef Burssens and his team crafting traditional Gallic bistro fare. Examples include seabream in a sea salt crust for two, veal kidneys with green peas, Holstein entrecote steak, rare and flanked with a bone marrow, mustard seed and anchovy butter… Big boned, heroic flavours overflowing in character are the hallmark here. The wine list is equally first-rate, particularly thanks to a splendid choice of wines by the glass. You can even ask to taste your tipple before choosing – further proof that inVINcible is determined to bend over backwards to pamper its guests.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3334392529	U Eat & Sleep Antwerp	Nassaustraat 42	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.u-eatsleep.be/nl	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, French	4.0	€€€	t	f	U Eat & Sleep is one of the hotspots of the buzzy Eilandje district thanks to a phenomenal view over the MAS and marina and a glammed-up interior oozing in vibrant sensuality. After kicking off your meal with knockout cocktails and tapas, we recommend the extensive menu which features playful, light dishes as well as big-boned brasserie classics. Whether you opt for a sole meunière or a vegetarian dish of aubergine, sesame and miso, you can rely on the establishment’s funky ethos: affordable luxury!	salajakub	\N	\N
3330072024	Dôme Sur Mer	Arendstraat 1	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.domesurmer.be/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	t	t	You are well and truly in the Art nouveau district of Zurenborg, even if this fish bistro would be quite at home in a seaside resort. The produce is outstandingly fresh, embodied by seafood platters overflowing in briny odours, delicately flavoured langoustines, cooked to perfection on a teppanyaki or sautéed fillets of seabass garnished with a gutsy olive oil sauce… In their open-plan kitchen, the chefs demonstrate that such delicacies have no need of prissy details, courtesy of spot-on cooking and ultra fresh side dishes.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3335591024	Het Nieuwe Palinghuis	Sint-Jansvliet 14	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning	https://www.hetnieuwepalinghuis.be/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	f	t	There is an authentic feel to the dining area of this charming seafood restaurant. Adorned with various nostalgic photos of maritime scenes, it harks back to its opening year: 1983! Over the years, Het Nieuwe Palinghuis has earned a reputation for its classic fish dishes. The menu features langoustine with an intense nantua sauce, sole Véronique in a full-bodied white wine sauce, as well as a distinctively herby eel in green sauce. The dishes here have always been big on flavour, steering clear of any unnecessary frills. A firm favourite!	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3332179428	Bar Raket	Bresstraat 10	Belgium	Antwerpen	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.barraket-antwerp.be/	Nessun premio	Sharing, International	5.0	€€	f	f	Convivial and buzzing Bar Raket provides a chic industrial-style setting in which to share a variety of delectable dishes. Flavours from all over the globe are represented here in cuisine that is all about enjoying the simple things: from Catalan bread to the umami of tonkatsu with North Sea crab to super-fresh clams with fried diced guanciale and a delectable hot sauce. The bread is simply divine! With a selection of smaller dishes and three main courses, the menu shows that good food can also be a delightfully laid-back affair.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3331793406	Cobra	Leopoldplaats 3	Belgium	Antwerpen	Terrace	https://www.cobra-antwerp.com/	Nessun premio	Sharing, International	5.0	€€	t	t	With its casual yet chic vibe, this lively establishment draws inspiration from the CoBrA art movement. A number of colourful pop art paintings command attention the moment you walk in. Behind the bar, the mixologist is at the ready. All manner of delicious dishes for sharing are served here from noon onwards. For example, you could start off with a lobster roll or pâté en croûte, then have Oedslach beef entrecôte as a main course and round off your meal with tarte Tatin. It's all possible here. No messing around, just simple, delicious flavours that will keep you coming back for more.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3335277584	Bar Bulot at Botanic	Lange Gasthuisstraat 41	Belgium	Antwerpen	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://barbulot.be/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	This hip, cosmopolitan brasserie, Antwerp’s outpost of Bruge’s Bar Bulot, has found refuge in the lavish Botanic Sanctuary Hotel. Timeless classics such as asparagus à la flamande, vol-au-vent of Bresse chicken, sweetbread and shrimp are revamped to tempt and tickle today’s tastebuds. Top-notch ingredients and contemporary flavours, by way of exotic spices, add character to each dish. Heaven for discerning foodies!	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
