3336618632	Tafeltje Rond	Peperstraat 14	Belgium	Beveren	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace	https://www.tafeltjerond.be/	Nessun premio	Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Tafeltje Rond enjoys something of a reputation as a romantic venue. Parisian chic defines this brasserie which sports parquet floors, elegantly laid tables, a black and white colour scheme and tableware that is as classy as the wine list and chef Slangen’s polished Gallic score. Old school classics like seabass in a salt crust, tournedos Rossini and hop shoots in a divine hollandaise sauce are rich in the distinctive flavours of yesteryear and the ethereal profiteroles filled with rich vanilla ice cream and smothered in intense dark chocolate are to die for! Don’t hesitate to give the chef your feedback directly as he loves popping out of the kitchen to add a final touch to dishes and say hi to his guests. Set menu at lunchtime only^ à la carte in the evening.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3333979137	VAS	Gentseweg 536	Belgium	Beveren	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.restaurantvas.be/	Nessun premio	Creative French, Farm to table	5.0	€€€	f	f	Jolien and Robby have moved shop, but retained their win-win formula. Near the Gentseweg highway, VAS occupies an attractive street corner edifice whose interior sports a range of elegant materials and a tasteful colour scheme. The bubbly front-of-house team sets the scene as you peruse the interesting Franco-Belgian repertory dotted with trendy, spot-on twists. Fillet of duck cooked rare might be flanked by a champagne sauce and a creamy gravy jazzed up with hints of sea buckthorn for added vibrancy together with a velvety purée and a range of textured kohlrabi. VAS is the quintessence of warm and welcoming, enhanced by a festival of familiar family favourites underscored by feelgood flavours.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3338765530	Delphine Ronsyn	Chaussée d'Enghien 61a	Belgium	Bierghes	Car park,Terrace	https://www.restaurantdr.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking	3.0	€€	t	f	Delphine Ronsyn opened this cheerful spacious restaurant, whose floor-to-ceiling windows command fantastic views of the surrounding fields and meadows, less than a kilometre from the family farm. Naturally enough, Delphine is a champion of local produce and her region. Her bistronomic menu is deceptively simple and straightforward, as the delicate chervil sauce that flanks gilt-head bream consummately illustrates.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3332778851	Delys	rue d'Yernawe 3	Belgium	Bodegnée	Air conditioning,Car park	https://delys-restaurant.be/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Delys is a haven of design depicted by a chic black colour scheme. Intimacy and mystery set the stage, while floor-to-ceiling windows seem to invite the countryside indoors. Be it for a quick lunch or a more leisurely dinner, chef Doucet’s modern approach always hits the spot. He avows a weakness for crisp, legible, contrasting flavours. For example, he may add an exuberant edge to lightly poached Atlantic cod courtesy of lemon zest and a subtly smoky mushroom stock. Doucet leaves his heroic, distinctive stamp on each dish thanks to sensitive nuances.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3339053486	Jacqueline	Van Colenstraat 8	Belgium	Boechout	Terrace	https://www.restaurantjacqueline.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€€	f	t	This former butchery is named after the grandmother of Evelien Swiers, who is in charge of the kitchen you can see behind the original counter. Good humoured Raf supervises the dining room, which sports a gentrified workshop vibe. Evelien’s delicious, no-frills cuisine revolves around a menu of four or five dishes. Guinea fowl from Maison Garat is cooked in a frying pan and underscored by a knockout jus enriched in miso, while chicory adds a fresh note with a mandarin sabayon. At Jacqueline, the food is rustic, gutsy and wholesome.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3336245618	Tabernakel	Dorp 41	Belgium	Bonheiden	Air conditioning	https://www.tabernakel.be/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, International	5.0	€€€	f	t	Brothers Steven and Bart refuse to be hampered by a single style. As a result, you may sample an appetiser of fresh, mildly spicy baba ghanoush or a playful new twist on the traditional tomato-mozzarella bruschetta, followed by a rack of lamb in a rosemary jus. Versatile and talented, they create appetising set menus and a splendid à la carte lineup. Kim enthusiastically supervises the front-of-house, bending over backwards to ensure that you savour every morsel of your meal to the full. An elegant, neoteric industrial vibe with just the right dose of authenticity.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3330452128	Silo's	Leuvensesteenweg 350	Belgium	Boortmeerbeek	Car park,Terrace	https://silos.be/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Silo’s is breathing life into the annex of the former malt house of Boortmeerbeek. The slick, well-oiled operations of this trendy luxury brasserie work like clockwork, seamlessly catering to large numbers of diners. The food is equally spot on, featuring updated versions of brasserie classics such as bouillabaisse and Clamart pigeon steeped in knockout flavours. Generous, voluntarily unfussy recipes that hit the nail on the head every time. The extensive menu and wine list, (including wines by the glass), ensures that there is something to tickle everyone’s fancy!	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3335512939	Atelier Maple	Karel De Preterlei 210	Belgium	Borgerhout	Terrace	https://ateliermaple.be/	Nessun premio	Creative, Farm to table	4.0	€€€€	f	t	Authentic details, such as a stunning glazed dome, and a plush, yet cosy ambience depict this stylish Art nouveau edifice. Chef Tynes crafts cosmopolitan fare, adding his own spin to pedigree French dishes, thanks in particular to Asian and Indonesian influences. Splendid terrace.	landirobert	\N	\N
3331304488	Nyde	Tongersesteenweg 30	Belgium	Borgloon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.nyde.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	The decision to call their restaurant Nyde, which means “to enjoy” in Danish, was far from ingenuous. Chef Céline, flanked by Martijn, your host, bend over backwards to make sure their guests enjoy their meal. The restaurant, whose vibe is serene and boasts a gorgeous patio to the rear, offers a set menu and a selection of cocktails and mocktails and insightful food-wine pairings. Céline underscores each ingredient’s purity as she seeks to sensitively enhance their flavours. She may garnish a lemon-flavoured mackerel tartare with a delicate concoction of diced cucumber and briny oysters, all of which is further offset by a lemon and cucumber dressing. Feelgood food that is guaranteed to lift your spirits.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3331707568	Basile	Rue du Moulin 52	Belgium	Bovesse	Car park	https://www.basile-cuisinegourmande.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table	5.0	€€€	f	t	Basile De Wulf’s endearing restaurant is part of La Petite Campagne farm, which boasts both a butcher’s and a dairy. Established in a modern-day wooden chalet, the chef will introduce you to local produce (some from the farm) rich in gutsy, rustic flavours. After stints in a number of top establishments, Basile seeks to showcase fresh ingredients with an international twang. The chef’s surprise menu is tailored to today’s tastebuds and his passion for wine adds the final flourish to a fine meal.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3335229107	Toit	Chaussée de Tubize 481	Belgium	Braine-l'Alleud	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.toit-restaurant.be/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Sardinian	4.0	€€€	f	t	The Boulemberg firm has opened this unusual restaurant on the roof of its manufacturing showroom. Floor to ceiling windows (their stock in trade!) and a terrace command splendid views of the lush green countryside, while a Mediterranean-inspired interior provides the perfect foil to extravagant, full-bodied Sardinian recipes underscored by French technique. Hence the contrast between steamed seabass and cooked sweetbread, paired with a lemon confit beurre blanc. The menu (renewed every six weeks) is rich in big-boned Mediterranean flavours and aromas.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3333228360	Max & Moi	Grand Place Baudouin Premier 4	Belgium	Braine-l'Alleud	Terrace	https://www.maxetmoi.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, French	4.0	€€€	f	f	Max & Pina have set up shop on Place Baudouin 1er in a tastefully refurbished town house dripping in understated glamour and sporting a suitably tasteful colour scheme. The couple works with a talented youthful chef, Julien Hauspie, who prefers to work with local produce while rolling out his experience gleaned in worldclass establishments at home and abroad. The chef’s know-how can be tasted in the beurre blanc that flanks seabass or in his way with carrots, which he might pair with a béarnaise sauce and tarragon and lemon oil, also demonstrating his creative side and fun-loving personality. Vibrant, exciting cuisine that comes in a four- or five-course menu.	costasergio	\N	\N
3334439164	Maurice	Bredabaan 662	Belgium	Brasschaat	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://restaurantmaurice.be	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, Modern French	4.0	€€€	t	f	The friendly eatery of delightful Kaatje De Blick and chef Karl Ave is in fact named after their cat! They aim for a home-from-home vibe and welcome guests like old friends: “Maurice is like coming home” in their own words. The sommelier can be relied on to ply you with insightful tips, whilst the veteran chef masterfully deploys his classical training to craft knockout dishes and sauces, albeit with the occasional more modern twist. For example, he often slips in Asian notes, illustrated by a ballotine of langoustine underscored by a sublime yuzu and dashi sauce.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3339701693	Sardis	Kapelsesteenweg 406	Belgium	Brasschaat	Terrace	https://ristorantesardis.be/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	f	Tiziano Cappai welcomes diners warmly into this stylish red-brick terraced house, which boasts a cosy interior, sensual artwork on the walls and a blissfully peaceful patio at the rear. Chef Eveline Cappai deftly updates a pure-bred lineup of Italian classics. For example, she might pair bigoli pasta with a subtle stock, to which she adds white wine, parsley, savoury vongole and a hint of umami thanks to kombu. The tiramisu manages to underscore authentic flavours with an amusing new spin thanks to a play on textures. Attention to detail is the watchword here.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3334292913	L.E.S.S. Eatery	't Zand 21	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://lesseatery.be/	Nessun premio	Asian Influences	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Love Eat Share Smile is the baseline of this hip urban eatery, which is equally suited to a hunger-obliterating snack at the bar as to a full-course feast with all the trimmings with all the family. You can expect an international culinary repertory with a definite Asian slant. From steak tartare with a Korean kick and ceviche scattered with distinctive fresh, spicy, tangy Peruvian notes to Hong-Kong-style young turbot, the extensive menu is a treasure trove of premium produce and creativity. A trendy, suitably casual vibe depicts one of Bruges’ most popular foodie hotspots!	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3332033016	Locàle by Kok au Vin	Ezelstraat 21	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.locale.be/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Farm to table	3.0	€€€	t	f	Locally sourced ingredients and a deep respect for nature's rhythms are the cornerstones of this cosy establishment. Influences from around the globe and the occasional use of the Mibrasa charcoal oven take things up a notch. The menu features dishes for sharing, such as zingy ceviche made with earthy beetroot or Zeeland mussels cooked in Bruges wheat beer. Nothing overly complicated, just playful, on-trend delicious food.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3330406720	Goesepitte 43	Goezeputstraat 43	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.goesepitte43.be	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Modern French	4.0	€€€	f	f	Step into the picturesque Goezeputstraat 43 and be transported to a jungle paradise, complete with a living moss wall and monkeys! Chef Jan Supply likes to come to the table in person to serve his dishes. These are characterised by a deft use of the Mibrasa charcoal oven, rich sauces and intriguing vegetable creations. This is bistronomy with that little bit extra, as evidenced by the hand-whipped lobster béarnaise that elevates smoky filet pur to new heights. Be sure to try the crêpe normande, a house classic.	benesemily	\N	\N
3330784361	Refter	Molenmeers 2	Belgium	Brugge	Terrace	https://www.bistrorefter.com/	Nessun premio	Flemish, Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Top notch ingredients, complex-free combinations and gutsy flavours. Don’t expect fancy frills in this casual bistro, adorned with a colourful eye-catching mosaic. The food is always first rate and flawlessly executed – skin-on cod and yummy dame blanche (vanilla ice cream and hot chocolate sauce) dessert.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3334244260	L'aperovino	Academiestraat 2F	Belgium	Brugge		https://www.aperovino.be/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	€€€	f	f	“Wine, dine and unwind” is the motto of this stylish upmarket bistro. Upstairs is the wine bar where sommelière Julie unveils a knockout selection of prestigious tipples and a fine choice of cocktails. Downstairs, you will sample dishes poised between tradition and exotic innovation, ranging from a winter venison stew to Sebastes fish served with a refreshing tom kha kai. “Where wining meets dining” is their other baseline…	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3337819754	ATELIER D THE BISTRO	Hoogstraat 12	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning	https://www.atelierdthebistro.be/	Nessun premio	French, Belgian	5.0	€€€	t	f	Diego De Baets is clearly at home in this sophisticated bistro, in which art and authenticity go hand in hand with a truly romantic vibe. The chef loves popping into the dining room to add a finishing touch to his dishes. You can expect a Franco-Belgian lineup starring outstanding ingredients, truly memorable sauces and big-boned flavours. Examples include crispy sweetbread coated in a flavoursome gravy further enhanced by sakura vinegar, or a match made in heaven of finely sliced wagyu and scallops paired with a knockout consommé made with the cooking gravy. The à la carte menu, which will have fine food connoisseurs slavering in anticipation, is a treasure trove of Belgian and French staples with a twist. Sheer bliss from start to finish.	costasergio	\N	\N
3332023589	L'Hibiscus	175 rue de Bourgogne	France	Orléans	Wheelchair access	https://www.hibiscus-orleans.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	In a bustling pedestrian street, the façade is discreet. Venture inside for fresh ingredients, original recipes and modern cuisine, courtesy of Céline Lefebvre, a chef with a proven track record. No à la carte, but a short set menu changing regularly abreast of the seasons and availability. Reasonable prices.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3333734764	Bruut	Meestraat 9	Belgium	Brugge	Counter dining	https://www.bistrobruut.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	The initial impression of romanticism conjured up by the historic edifice in which Bruut is located, quickly gives way to a pared-down, almost brutal interior that is emblematic of its colourful, rock ‘n roll chef, Bruno Timperman. He crafts a single surprise menu that elegantly showcases his unconventional streak and technical ingenuity. He may pair the breast and thighs of slow-cooked partridge in a winter recipe with cèpes, a gutsy jus of the carcass, thyme, marinated pine buds and capers marinated in garlic. “When food meets wine” is the baseline…	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3332737203	Assiette Blanche	Philipstockstraat 23	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning	https://www.assietteblanche.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€	f	t	The locals flock to this bistro, which appeals equally to socialites and a more casual crowd. The jovial mistress of the house and the subtle cooking of chef Timmerman further add to the establishment’s friendly vibe. Gutsy Gallic flavours are combined with vivacious Asian highlights, without forgetting local produce, in particular North Sea fish. Classical fare with a twist in the heart of picturesque Bruges.	krausmartina	\N	\N
