3334584148	Le Mystique	Niklaas Desparsstraat 11	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.lemystique.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	3.0	€€€	f	f	If you’re looking for a romantic getaway venue in the picture postcard perfect city of Bruges, book a table in the restaurant of the Relais & Chateaux Heritage Hotel, whose opulent interior oozes authentic historic details. It is truly the epitome of stylish elegance! The chef avows a preference for French and Mediterranean ingredients, which he delicately crafts into spot-on dishes. Examples include a marinated fillet of mullet paired with sweet-sour fennel, labneh and radish pickles. Each dish is a master class of subtlety and originality. A date night kinda place with which you will immediately fall head over heels.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3334601913	Mémoire	Dijver 7	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.hoteltuilerieen.com/nl/p/gastronomie/restaurant-memoire	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€€€	t	f	The luxury De Tuilerieën Hotel will leave you with unforgettable souvenirs, including that of a meal in its restaurant, Mémoire. Both its minimalist dining rooms are the pinnacle of unobtrusive opulence and style. Chef Wouter van Tichelen however disrupts this serene portrait courtesy of vibrant powerful cooking. Classically trained, the chef rolls out his know-how in sauces, adding elegant contemporary touches. He may give halibut marinated in salt a mineral edge courtesy of a creamy sorrel and seaweed sauce, while a caviar quenelle adds a final touch to this consummate dish, as does the Albariño wine with which it is paired. Van Tichelen deploys a local, sustainable ethos at the service of fine dining.	paganialex	\N	\N
3334438998	Rock-Fort	Langestraat 15	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning	http://www.rock-fort.be	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	f	f	North Sea fish and natural wines are the bedrock of this bright, elegant bistro. Chef Laurent and Eline, in charge of the front of house, who first came to our notice at Amuzee in Zeebrugge, are going from strength to strength as they settle in here. The menu overflows in the generous produce of the North Sea with a distinctive subtle, sometimes spicy edge. The fascinating culinary score is depicted by almost translucent grilled langoustines, which are paired with a dashi umami edge or raw scallops served with green apples and jalapeno. Rock-Fort is alive and kicking – in every sense!	pirijiri	\N	\N
3338695073	Tanuki	Oude Gentweg 1	Belgium	Brugge	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.tanuki.be	Nessun premio	Teppanyaki, Asian Influences	4.0	€€€	t	t	Since 1989 Ivan Verhelle has been treating his diners to a genuine taste of Japan. The table service and interior are larger than life and the open - plan kitchen provides a bird’s eye view of the preparation of fine ingredients, such as fresh wasabi. The chef is a fan of teppanyaki cuisine and can even organise (bookings) a tea ceremony.	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3332146449	Brasserie Grand Cru	Noorweegsekaai 5	Belgium	Brugge	Car park,Terrace	https://www.brasseriegrandcru.be/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, French	5.0	€€€	f	f	Red and white chequered tablecloths and a rustic interior set the delightfully vintage scene in this brasserie. The huge open kitchen is equipped with both spit-roasting and barbecue facilities. Lovers of hunger-obliterating wholesome fare will be in seventh heaven as each dish hits the spot from the Flemish stoofpotje made with Belgian beer, the vol-au-vent or sole meunière to calf’s liver in madeira sauce – an authentic lineup of no-nonsense familiar brasserie cuisine. The extensive menu has something for everyone and is a genuine ode to the cooking of yesteryear. A great vintage indeed!	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
