3331893940	Lily's	Avenue Emile de Mot 1	Belgium	Brussels	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.lilys.be/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€€	t	t	Lily’s, which recreates the vibe of a Saint Tropez or Los Angeles club in Brussels with elegant, premium materials, a pretty green pergola in summer and dancing at the weekends, has become a hotspot of the Belgian capital. Indulge in a glass of wine or a signature cocktail as you cast your eye over the awesome menu. Familiar Belgian favourites, such as immaculately cooked veal chop with fresh béarnaise sauce, are prepared with the same flair and talent as a ceviche of seabass or truffle taglioni. Attracts A-listers like bees to honey for an unforgettable evening!	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3336557820	Aster	Rue Antoine Dansaert 202	Belgium	Brussels	Counter dining	https://aster.brussels	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€	t	t	Veg, locally caught fish and fire are the raison d’être of this urban eatery at the end of Rue Dansaert. The menu sports a cornucopia of creative combinations and amusing textures that frequently astound. Examples include monkfish underscored by a fascinating butter and sake sauce, while fish liver, steamed in spinach leaf, further highlights the savoury notes and finely chopped lovage adds a powerful final flourish. Aster is well and truly in the zeitgeist thanks to wholehearted, big-boned flavours and perfectly judged nuances.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3331904322	San Sablon	rue Joseph Stevens 12	Belgium	Brussels		https://sansablon.be/	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€	t	t	San Sablon features a welcoming natural decor in the smart Sablon district, albeit with a trendy, suave twist. Rather than plates, forks and knives, you will eat out of bowls with spoons – all the better to do justice to original recipes that keep pace with the seasons. The main ingredient is enhanced by gutsy vegetable side dishes that illuminate each meal.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3330135462	Ciao	Place Poelaert 6	Belgium	Brussels	Terrace	https://www.ciao-brussels.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	t	The 17C stately house on Poelaert Square belongs to TheMerode, a private club. Have no fear, though, everyone is welcome at Ciao. Our favourite in this edifice, oozing in character and elegance, was the dining room with a pretty bar. Authentic Italian flavours are treated to a sensitive modern makeover, illustrated by homemade tortellini with beef marinated in Chianti and a parmesan sauce subtly underscored by Campari. The chef avows a weakness for Tuscan recipes and delicately crafts succulent comfort food. Making your choice from the menu can be something of a challenge!	weberdragos	\N	\N
3333126163	Samouraï	rue du Fossé aux Loups 28	Belgium	Brussels	Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.samourai-bruxelles.be/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	€€€	f	f	Samouraï is both minimalist and sleekly contemporary and yet this restaurant, tucked away in a nondescript shopping mall near Rue Neuve, has been a culinary landmark of Brussels since 1974. Razor-sharp precision and rich flavours embody the authentic Japanese cuisine, depicted by a varied menu of sushi and sashimi, together with table preparations like sukiyaki. The chef steams the shiitake with shrimp-flavoured pasta and then flanks it with a ginger and soy stock and with fried ciboule onion and shiso leaves, creating a harmony that is both subtle and distinctive. Popular lunchtime bento boxes^ set menus in the evening as well as à la carte.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3337629745	Umā	Rue de la Reinette 8	Belgium	Brussels	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://uma-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, International	5.0	€€	t	f	Umā stands on a quiet side street near the bustling Porte de Namur. Its white-washed brick outer facade and modern artwork inside are both inviting and attractive. Admire Aurélie Kluyskens at work in the open-plan kitchen, rustling up her own spin on Nikkei cuisine, which she rolls out in a spot-on blend of gutsy Japanese and powerful Peruvian flavours. She adds her signature with subtle spicy notes, imparting a spicy/sweet edge to scallops, courtesy of an espuma of smoked pork. Both the varied à la carte menu and the enticing set menu provide an insight into Ms Kluyskens’ distinctive culinary flair and talent.	ferrettivladislav	\N	\N
3334930364	Henri	rue de Flandre 113	Belgium	Brussels	Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://restohenri.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€€	f	f	This laid-back bistro perfectly embodies the hip, urban vibe of Brussels’ Rue de Flandres and we warrant you will fall in love with its casual ambience, cobbled terrace and splendid choice of wines and Brussels’ beers. The dishes are free of frills, all the better to allow the ingredients to take front stage. Mussels in a pastis-flavoured sauce, beef tartare with a Thai slant or text-book perfect sole meunière: the chef enthusiastically navigates between influences with a fondness for fresh Mediterranean fare. Fine dining with a Brussels’ signature!	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3332308981	Osteria Romana	Avenue Legrand 11	Belgium	Brussels	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.osteriaromana.be	Nessun premio	Roman	4.0	€€€	t	f	Don’t even try to resist the appeal of this Osteria Romana - you will be bowled over by the romantic allure of the mansion, the cocktail bar and the immaculate tailored service. Roman specialties and tableside preparations set the scene. Delicacies include Roman-Jewish deep-fried artichoke, carbonara pasta, pasta with tuna tartare, pepperoncino, combava and ginger in a lineup whose subtlety, generosity and flavour are to die for! What more proof do you need that Italians do it better!	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3333881588	L'Écailler du Palais Royal	rue Bodenbroek 18	Belgium	Brussels	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.lecaillerdupalaisroyal.be	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	f	f	L'Écailler is a Brussels institution. The turquoise tiles behind the long bar, the wonderful woodwork, the gorgeous carpets and the nostalgic charm of this building make for an irresistibly inviting setting. A champion of classic cuisine, the chef excels in preparing fish and seafood dishes, but during the hunting season, his game specialities are also not to be missed. Briny oysters, the aromatic bouillabaisse, his inimitable sole meunière… Fans of traditional fare will feel right at home.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3331445822	La Marée	rue de Flandre 99	Belgium	Brussels	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.lamaree-sa.com/en/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	f	f	Everything is traditional, big-boned and wholesome from the homemade shrimp fritters and cod cooked in butter with a fresh tartar sauce and piping hot fries to the velvety custard tart, with which the chef celebrates her Portuguese roots: such are the delicacies conjured up by Teresa Alves for her diners. An authentic Brussels’ bistro steeped in vintage nostalgia to the delight of a mixed crowd of regulars. A classic seafood restaurant in which time seems to have stood still.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3330673231	Le Vismet	place Sainte-Catherine 23	Belgium	Brussels	Terrace	https://levismet.be/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	t	f	The Vismet (Brussels’ fish market) is a stone’s throw from this traditional restaurant, as quickly becomes apparent. The ambience is relaxed, the service typical of Brussels and the food scrumptious. Fish and shellfish take pride of place in dishes with an emphasis on fresh, generous portions.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3338297168	La Belle Maraîchère	place Sainte-Catherine 11a	Belgium	Brussels	Air conditioning	https://www.labellemaraichere.com/en/	Nessun premio	Seafood, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Depuis 1973, les gourmets apprécient ce restaurant traditionnel où la famille Devreker choie ses hôtes. On y redécouvre le temps où Sainte Catherine était le quartier le plus prisé de Bruxelles pour les restaurants. Croquettes de crevettes, homard, gibier, sauces intenses et bien d’autres plats y sont préparés dans les règles de l’art. Pas de chichis, mais une cuisine chaleureuse et savoureuse.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3331572450	Gus	rue des Cultes 36	Belgium	Brussels		https://www.gus-brussels.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Belgian	4.0	€€	t	f	Pierre Baeyens and Jonathan Delhière acquaint you with the “brassonomy” concept (beer meets gastronomy) in their cosy brasserie. They skilfully incorporate the many flavours of artisan beer and hops into a Franco-Belgian line-up, in the glass and also in the subtle food. A foamy beer mousseline nestles up to a soft-poached egg and mushrooms or steak is smoked in hops: the chefs add an individual touch to creative recipes. A bubbling Brussels brasserie-cum-brewery!	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
