3337086700	Les Tilleuls	place Communale 2	Belgium	Céroux		https://tilleuls.be/	Nessun premio	Home Cooking	4.0	€€	f	t	The former village hall of Céroux-Mousty has been turned into a welcoming bistro. Marc Volkaerts has thrown all his experience and enthusiasm into his own individual version of classical cuisine, such as tartare steak or duck shepherd’s pie, adding a personal and distinctive spin to consummately bistronomic dishes. Masterful!	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3339004365	Le Délice du Jour	Rue du Chemin de Fer 57	Belgium	Chapelle-lez-Herlaimont	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.ledelicedujour.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Fabrizzio Chirico, who needs no introduction in Wallonia, is back on the gastro scene. He has set up shop in this elegant villa adorned with tasteful decor in warm tones. The chef's passion for working with top-quality, local ingredients is evident in every dish, and the sauces are particularly impressive. Classically trained, he is nonetheless keen to embrace new techniques and likes to play with zingy and smoky flavours, as well as juxtaposing textures. Think raw scallop taken to the next level with a lacto-fermented sauce or black tea enriched with the scallop's coral. One thing is for sure: you won't leave hungry!	sannamateo	\N	\N
3336691362	Chez Duche	avenue de Waterloo 5	Belgium	Charleroi		https://chezduche.be/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	You can expect unadorned dishes that throb with flavour in what is the epitome of a neighbourhood eatery: rib of horse meat with house-made fries, lavishly served cassoulet, piled high with duck confit and Toulouse sausage or a waterzooi of seasonal veggies. A patriotic pageant of French and Belgian classics prepared and served with textbook precision and generosity. Chez Duche has been feeding us well since 1993!	marchettimarko	\N	\N
