3330827172	Racines	chaussée d'Ixelles 353	Belgium	Ixelles	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.racinesbruxelles.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€	t	t	Leave the noisy Chaussée d'Ixelles and walk past the grocery counter into this delightfully vintage restaurant, which is awash in Mediterranean details and boasts an delightful terrace. Welcome to this authentic Italian establishment, where the chef will take you on a culinary journey from the north to the south of the Boot. Try the house-made tagliolini with parmesan and earthy cavolo nero, or the intensely flavoursome San Marzano tomato flan, drizzled with olive oil. The chef's creative and meticulous take on traditional recipes shines through. Featuring an impressive range of Italian labels, the wine list is well worth exploring.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3331733739	Ricciocapriccio	rue Américaine 90	Belgium	Ixelles	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://ricciocapriccio.be/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€€	f	t	This bistro is a popular spot for Belgian Italians, as evidenced by the amount of Italian that is spoken here. The chef, a fan of fine produce (sea urchins and squid are his specialties), deftly whisks up enticing dishes featuring carefully considered and, occasionally, unusual combinations. For instance, he prepares risotto with a sea bream tartare and parmesan foam, or puts a new spin on the classic tiramisu, but he always respects the essence of the dishes he prepares. The ample à la carte menu promises a Mediterranean feast!	rossidino	\N	\N
3339205222	Fico	rue Américaine 118	Belgium	Ixelles		https://www.ficosteria.be/	Nessun premio	Italian, Sicilian	4.0	€€	f	f	At Fico, Nadia Bruno pays tribute to Sicily and her mamma, Grazziella. The cosy ambience and vibrant, vintage-inspired decor make for the perfect setting in which to savour her sun-drenched cooking. The chalkboard displays a tempting array of authentic dishes. Think al dente fettuccine elevated with sea urchin, an intensely flavoursome semifreddo made with grappa, honey and saffron. Here, bold flavours meet Italian finesse, with no room for pretension. Don't forget to make a reservation!	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3336591438	Nonbe Daigaku	avenue Adolphe Buyl 31	Belgium	Ixelles		https://nonbedaigaku.be/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Sushi	4.0	€€€	t	t	If you like eating Japanese, you shouldn’t miss this modest venue. The very experienced chef has mastered the subtlety and nuances that are typical of the cuisine of his home country. You can see him at work behind the sushi bar, driven and precise, creating a delicious variety of flavours and textures.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3338232553	Maru	chaussée de Waterloo 510	Belgium	Ixelles			Nessun premio	Korean, Asian	4.0	€€	t	t	This urban Korean eatery on the doorstep of the Châtelain district never fails to deliver. The locals flock here at lunchtime to polish off a main course or take their time over a more leisurely meal with a glass of wine. Pajeon is one of its star dishes: a crisp pancake filled with meat or fish flanked by a sweet vinaigrette and a spicy chili sauce. This dish symbolises the delicate balance between sweet, sour and spicy notes achieved by the chef, further underscored by a playful melody of varied textures. The epitome of authentic Korean nosh!	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3336177732	Quartz	Rue de la Réforme 22	Belgium	Ixelles	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.quartzrestaurant.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Local foodies still remember the street corner premises that housed La Canne en Ville for many years. Chef David-Alexandre Bruno has retained the soul of this former butcher’s shop with its wall tiles and floor mosaics. Bruno honed his skills and love of classical cuisine in upmarket establishments, as the personal spin he effortlessly adds to familiar recipes demonstrates. His take on Bellevue lobster is a splendid example: he pairs the tail with a skinned tomato stuffed with meat from the claws, samphire, a herby cream and vanilla-flavoured tomato stock. Sauces are one of the pieces de résistance of this chef, whose bold personality seeks to shine the spotlight on preferably local produce – simplicity and harmonious flavours are the goal.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3336430954	Odette en Ville	rue du Châtelain 25	Belgium	Ixelles	Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.odetteenville.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€€	f	f	Odette is a well-known eatery of the trendy Châtelain neighbourhood. The stylish 1920’s townhouse aims to combine British style, Parisian sensuality and New York glamour. The highly varied menu is equally fascinating: both classical and international, with an accent on the ingredient. Crunchy nems in a spicy sauce, al dente taglioni in lemon with pink shrimps, scallops and foie gras in a duck stock: a festival for fine food lovers. And why not treat yourself to one of the swish designer-inspired guestrooms to finish your evening in the lap of luxury?	habiliragip	\N	\N
3334979127	Savage	Rue de la Paix 22	Belgium	Ixelles	Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.savage.restaurant	Nessun premio	Organic, Vegetarian	3.0	€€	f	t	The trendy natural interior of Savage is perfectly at home in the fashionable Saint-Boniface neighbourhood. The plant-based cuisine is depicted by fascinating combinations of herbs and vegetables, whose varied impressions and textures never fail to surprise. You can choose meat (from the refrigerated meat counter) or fish to accompany your meal, also selected according to sustainable development criteria.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3339970292	Maison du Luxembourg	rue du Luxembourg 37	Belgium	Ixelles	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.maisonduluxembourg.be/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	A stone's throw from the EU Parliament, this contemporary establishment champions the bounty of Luxembourg's terroir. The restaurant draws an international crowd, who come to savour an array of culinary treats, frequently sourced from the province of Wallonia, including seasonal specialties such as asparagus and wild game. To suit the palate of the modern urban diner, traditional recipes are reworked with a light touch and a sprinkle of international flair, without sacrificing their core flavours. Smoked eel, for example, forms a winning combination with foie gras, a poached egg and subtly spicy rocket coulis.	shirocky	\N	\N
3337120539	Toucan sur Mer	avenue Louis Lepoutre 17	Belgium	Ixelles	Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking	https://toucan.brussels/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	f	f	How about an impressive skate dish with capers, oysters opened behind the seafood counter or a sumptuous seafood platter? This lively bistro serves up wonderfully fresh delicacies from the sea. Despite its lack of pretensions Toucan sur Mer definitely holds its own against the grander restaurants on the coast.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3332988322	Villared	Leenstraat 51	Belgium	Izegem	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.villared.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Pink flamingos adorn the wallpaper, green marble abounds and gold and ochre depict the colour scheme. Elegant and fashionable, Villared provides the perfect foil to chef Debal’s eclectic score. Melanzane alla parmigiana, sole meunière, Asian-inspired salmon… The enticing menu by a seasoned craftsman has something for everyone.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3330125608	Nast	Hondekensmolenstraat 60	Belgium	Izegem	Car park	https://www.restaurantnast.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French, French Contemporary	3.0	€€€	f	t	Dean Masschelein has added his inimitable stamp to a former chicory factory, retaining the original rough brick walls, but cleverly dotted with modern fixtures and fittings. The chef is a genuine West Flemish lad, as his exuberant personality and passion for regional produce quickly reveal. The food is succulent, straightforward and international and he might mix presa iberico with a sweet-sour baba ghanoush and Mediterranean fregola, all of which comes together thanks to an emulsion of bacon. Creative seasonal cooking, rendered even more flavoursome when paired with gueuze beers or organic wines.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3333200487	Côté Préféré	Dorpsstraat 47	Belgium	Jabbeke	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://coteprefere.be/	Nessun premio	Creative French	5.0	€€€	t	t	A delicious slab of turbot cooked on the bone with a beurre noisette, al dente asparagus and a creamy morel sauce. Such are some of Tim Versyck’s emblematic recipes. The ingredient rules in his mainly classical repertory, albeit with the occasional international spin. The chef sources his produce locally, particularly fish from the North Sea and veggies, meat and poultry from the polders of West Flanders. The bright contemporary interior aims to pay tribute to the earthy, wholesome terroir of Flanders.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3339788897	La Plage d'Amée	rue des Peupliers 2	Belgium	Jambes	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.laplagedamee.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	The terrace of this modern villa on the banks of the Meuse is one of the finest in the region. The knockout view through floor-to-ceiling windows gives the impression of almost floating on water. This watering hole is a favourite with regulars who appreciate its creative cuisine and superlative value for money. Examples include soufflé stuffed with a cream of gruyere and fresh tomato coulis. Well-crafted cuisine, subtle delicate sauces and the occasional surprising texture or flavour!	venturialessia	\N	\N
3338600304	Wine in the City	place Reine Astrid 34	Belgium	Jette	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://wineinthecity.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, International	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Make your way past the shelves of bottles and into the dining room-cum-wine cellar of Eddy and Arnaud Münster. Father and son work side by side in their small open-plan kitchen, while mum Isabelle curates the knockout wine list with the chefs. The food features a range of tapas to share depicted by an international, creative and fun-loving edge. Examples include slow-baked cod in sea lavender and a sesame sauce that definitely packs a punch, or homemade lamb tortellini in a scrumptious sakura-flavoured stock. What’s not to like?	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3331029295	Vonk	Kachtemsplein 13	Belgium	Kachtem	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.vonk-gastrobar.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table	3.0	€€€	f	t	Stijn and chef Bart are the fifth generation of the Hoonaert family, whose DNA is rooted in culinary excellence! The conservatory of the former café, planted with trees, is now a cosy gastrobar. A charcoal Mibrasa oven adds a distinctive flavour to market-fresh recipes, made with meticulously chosen ingredients (simple lunchtime menu, more varied in the evening).	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3333093096	Rascasse	Kalmthoutsesteenweg 121	Belgium	Kapellen	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantrascasse.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Seafood	3.0	€€€	f	t	Erwin Denijs is a genuine ambassador of his region, the North Sea and Oosterschelde River. This “North Sea Chef” crafts the best seasonal produce into dishes that combine a tangy freshness with a playful element. For example, beurre blanc flanks a skate wing cooked in butter and paired with mussels and a medley of leeks. Caroline, your cheerful hostess, will ply you with wine, as well as beer tips, all of which in a pared-back setting that provides the perfect foil for striking works of art, starring fish!	kralrosa	\N	\N
3337139719	Seir	Geelsebaan 40	Belgium	Kasterlee	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.seir.be/	Nessun premio	Creative French, Modern French	4.0	€€€€	t	t	The sunny conservatory of this swish restaurant immediately catches the eye. The leather-seated lounge is ideal to sip a drink while admiring chef Thomas at work. An accomplished artist, he composes his visual masterpieces right on the counter. Intelligent combinations, precise and meticulous cooking. This youthful chef gives a free rein to his creative flair and is clearly determined to go places! A genuine treat for the senses.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3331260221	Potiron	Geelsebaan 73	Belgium	Kasterlee	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.potiron.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Friendly Dirk and Sophie aren’t shy of demonstrating their phenomenal know-how. They smoke their own salmon, the ice cream is homemade, and they are justly proud of their 3-acre vegetable garden (visits by appointment). Vegetables and aromatic herbs add a playful twist and authentic purity to updated recipes. Distinctive French cuisine that eschews jargon and fancy frills.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3330191116	KAN10	Geelsebaan 85a	Belgium	Kasterlee	Car park,Terrace	https://www.kan10.be/	Nessun premio	World Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	“Original”, “captivating”, “adventurous” and “regional” sum up the ethos of this cosy urban eatery. As a result, you can expect to sample a mind-blowing range of flavours and savours. Asian flair depicts the semi-cooked salmon, underscored by excellent homemade sambal and flanked by a traditional beurre noisette… A culinary banquet! Ask the lady of the house to show you the popular menu of shared dishes and get ready to embark on an exciting voyage of international flavours in a casual vibe.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3336122019	Maison Belge	Haachtsebaan 150	Belgium	Keerbergen	Car park,Terrace	https://www.maisonbelge.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€€	t	t	A subtle sprinkling of vintage details lends this modern brasserie a pleasant homely feel^ the terrace is delightful. The chef specialises in traditional, Belgian in particular, classics, to which she adds her own light, fresh hallmark signature.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3330725873	In de Zon	Dikkebusstraat 80	Belgium	Kemmel	Car park,Terrace	https://www.indezon.be/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In de Zon is a haven for foodies and cycling enthusiasts (it is located in the heart of the Heuvelland region). The decor is filled with nostalgic finds from flea markets, which add a touch of charm. On a clear day, you can see all the way to France from the gorgeous terrace. This is a restaurant that is full of character and that showcases Flemish cuisine at its best. Crispy shrimp croquettes, herby paling in 't groen (eel in a green sauce) with fresh fries, succulent pork cheeks cooked in Saint Bernard beer: this heartwarming food leaves a lasting impression.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3333930493	De Kruidenmolen	Dorpsstraat 1	Belgium	Klemskerke	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.kruidenmolen.be/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	f	Ostend-style shrimp fritters, rabbit stew in stout beer, a German jam doughnut filled with rosemary flavoured crème patissière: such are a few of the culinary gems that explain the success of this tastefully restored former miller’s house in the heart of the unspoiled polder countryside. Ask for a table on the terrace sheltered by panes of glass and admire the landscape. A fan of humble, often overlooked ingredients, the chef has no lack of creativity and his enticing menu appeals to all foodies. The establishment’s continuing popularity is borne out by the lively, bustling vibe that inevitably sets the scene at mealtimes.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3336653802	La Rigue	Elizabetlaan 160	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://la-rigue.be/	Nessun premio	Belgian, Classic French	5.0	€€€€	f	t	The stunning La Réserve hotel boasts a brasserie that is quite the equal to its elegant host. The Zegemeer landscape, visible from the handsome terrace, provides the perfect foil to this urbane restaurant. Local foodies adore the place for its extensive range of national and Gallic favourites, jazzed up with a delicate new spin. For example, the rich vol-au-vent is paired with an exquisite millefeuille and a subtly contrasting acidic sabayon while the bouillabaisse of North Sea fish explodes with big-boned gutsiness… A tailored culinary experience overflowing in generosity and a capacity of some 120 diners. Be it for a snack or a special occasion, La Rigue is just the ticket.	ozmax	\N	\N
3337481242	Esmeralda	Jozef Nellenslaan 161	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurantesmeralda.be/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Stefan Verhasselt has been at the helm of this elegant edifice, next-door to Knokke casino, since 1975. His vast experience can be felt and tasted in every detail and particularly in the choice produce, which is mainly from the sea. He has a flair for transforming Zeebrugge shrimp into crispy fritters and his sole meunière garnished with fresh tartare sauce and piping hot fresh fries is second to none. Rather than complex or fussy preparations, you will be treated to a banquet of classical know-how, illustrated by the house specialty, seabass in a salt crust.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3339462093	Escabèche	Dumortierlaan 94	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning	https://www.escabeche.be/	Nessun premio	Creative French	5.0	€€€	t	f	The trendy welcoming interior of Escabèche is a hit with the inhabitants of Knokke. They pop in to chat with the friendly hostess, Lisbeth, and to sample the delicacies rustled up by chef Verhasselt, a virtuoso in the art of enhancing first-class ingredients. Blessedly free of fancy frills, you can expect a wholesome lineup of pedigree Gallic nosh, flanked by subtle side dishes and occasionally jazzed up with Mediterranean or Oriental twists. The extensive appetising menu ranges from a hamachi-based festival of Asian flavours to a juicy fillet of turbot in a Dijon mustard sauce or the gamey earthiness of pheasant à la brabançonne during game season. The vast menu is heaven for foodies!	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3335561039	Dah Makan	Dumortierlaan 64	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning	https://www.dahmakan.be/	Nessun premio	Fusion	3.0	€€€	t	t	Cod marinated in miso and grilled on a robata, served with crunchy veg and lashings of frothy beurre blanc spiked with yuzu… Dishes to share such as these explain the success of this snug eatery. The culinary score, depicted by Asian flavours and western influences, demonstrates a clear preference for superior produce such as wagyu beef or crab from the North Sea, which are often finished on a robata grill or teppanyaki griddle. The menu is almost impossibly varied!	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3339529701	Il Trionfo	P. Parmentierlaan 203	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://iltrionfo.be/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	t	Il Trionfo is both an elegant restaurant and a family story. The father and daughter-in-law preside front-of-house, and their enthusiasm is infectious. He also has some fantastic wine recommendations up his sleeve. Upon entering the restaurant, you will catch a glimpse of the mother and son at work in the kitchen. You can opt for the more creative set menu or order à la carte from a selection of traditional robust Mediterranean classics like vitello tonnato and spaghetti vongole. Don't miss the osso buco – the meat is unbelievably tender, and that typically rich tomato sauce is simply divine. The quintessence of Italian generosity!	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3333712436	Carcasse	Oosthoekplein 1	Belgium	Knokke	Air conditioning	https://www.carcasse.be/carcasse	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Grills	4.0	€€€€	t	f	An artisan butcher, Hendrik Dierendonck chose to open the first offshoot of his meat-lover’s establishment in Knokke’s Oosthoekplein. On entering, your eye is first drawn to the refrigerated counter and massive glazed aging cabinet, before it is distracted by the chefs in the open-plan kitchen as they craft outstanding produce that is Dierendonck’s signature. Delicacies such as Oedslach ribeye and tongue of Belgian red cattle are enhanced by subtle side dishes that add a wealth of nuances and refreshing notes. Grilled melt-in-the-mouth Menapii pork cutlet is coated in a creamy emulsion of tarragon and other fresh herbs and served on fregula seasoned with the same herbs and a mousse of thyme and coarsely ground hazelnuts. Diners are invited, even encouraged to share dishes, giving you more chance to taste the full scope of the appetising menu.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
