3336662159	Brasserie Daefnis	Rekkemstraat 2	Belgium	Lauwe	Terrace	https://www.brasseriedaefnis.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€	t	t	It isn’t easy to nab a table in this luxury brasserie, which is always a sign of top-notch quality. Daefnis specialises in first-rate produce: North Sea sole, fillet of venison and premium Holstein beef are just a few of the delicacies that are showcased on the up-to-date brasserie menu. Familiar flavours are nonetheless respected, albeit with judicious nuances.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3331832700	Talloor d'Or	Ledebergplein 20	Belgium	Ledeberg	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.talloordor.be	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	You will immediately feel at home in the tasteful interior of the Talloor d’Or. Seated at the counter, you can admire the chef at work, rustling up contemporary dishes in keeping with the establishment’s vibe. Subtle vegetable dishes, fine sauces and a few citrus notes enhance and underscore the main ingredient. Seasoned Matthias and Nikki give free rein to their creative bent.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3330466614	Atelier Noun	Dorpstraat 252	Belgium	Leefdaal	Car park,Terrace	https://www.ateliernoun.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Bert and Sandra’s workshop sports a cosy, lounge vibe, underscored by Scandinavian accents and a splendid leafy al fresco area. The couple’s passion can be felt throughout the restaurant and Bert adores rustling up fascinating modern recipes, scattered with Asian nuances and incisive, acidic notes. Paradise for foodies!	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3335901107	Auberge du Château de Leignon par Isabelle Arpin	Rue du Sacré-Coeur 1	Belgium	Leignon	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.leignon.com/restaurant	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	t	Today, the neo-Gothic Château de Leignon is home to a variety of businesses, including a brewery and, of course, this charming restaurant run by Isabelle Arpin, whose market-fresh cuisine showcases ingredients from local producers. Look forward to playful dishes that draw inspiration from all over the world – for example, she pairs brill with barley infused with coffee, artichoke, a creamy fish sauce and a sabayon with aged rum. Be sure to sample the creations of the local brewery, whose beers frequently find their way into the desserts.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3339771400	Osteria Cellini	Sint-Pieterstraat 46	Belgium	Leut	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.osteriacellini.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	f	t	Dining at this cosy osteria is an immersive experience. As soon as you enter this converted school, you are greeted by the sound of Italian songs playing in the background^ you will notice the Mediterranean colour scheme, the terracotta and the decorative plants. And then there's the friendly welcome extended by the charismatic owner and maître d. The Italian specialities served here are mainly based on recipes from the Marche region and Sicily. Think al dente tagliolini, a slightly sweet tomato sauce with white wine, chopped lobster and flat-leaf parsley. And if you order the zabaglione, they bring the whole pot to your table. Mediterranean generosity at its best!	tohnjohn	\N	\N
