3333376052	Fou du Goût	Kasteeldreef 63	Belgium	Lovendegem	Terrace	https://www.foudugout.be/nl	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Fou du Goût manages to be both chic and cosy, with the beautiful glass conservatory being the best spot in the house. Thomas Cocquyt has a penchant for giving familiar flavours an exotic twist – chicken cooked in a spicy masala sauce, or pan-fried plaice with smoked eel and a beurre blanc infused with a yuzu gel for a burst of citrus brightness. This chef is a master of balancing bold flavours with a touch of intrigue. A perennial favourite in the Meetjesland region!	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3333045881	Compagnique	Vellare 93	Belgium	Lovendegem	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.compagnique.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€€€	t	t	Ideal for a romantic date night, this charming farmstead is the quintessence of poised and intimate and only offers tables for two (but there is a private room that caters to groups). Working hand in hand, Angélique manages the front-of-house while Tim runs the kitchen, in a bid to provide a personalised experience. Luxury ingredients enjoy the leading role on the menu and the chef might sign a high-flying combination of oysters and seaweed, caviar and a distinctive beurre blanc made out of curds. He has a soft spot for fresh, tangy notes, illustrated by the subtle sauce vierge that contrasts so wonderfully with the mild yet sweet flesh of turbot. A mouthwatering prospect…	palombasauro	\N	\N
3336502544	Atelier de Bossimé	rue Bossimé 2B	Belgium	Loyers	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.atelier-de-bossime.be/	Nessun premio	Organic, Modern French	5.0	€€€	f	f	Ludovic Vanackere’s converted this old farm in line with his sustainable vision. If the produce doesn’t come from his own impressive kitchen garden, which can be admired from the floor-to-ceiling windows, it is sourced locally. The surprise menu showcases the best of Namur and the region. Veggies take the limelight, prompting extra creativity in the winter season, illustrated by the chef’s work with different cabbage textures enhanced by a sauce packed in fermented veg, peanuts and sate-flavoured spices. Regional cooking founded on throbbing recipes and powerful sauces.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3337241916	Bleuet	Bovenstraat 4	Belgium	Maarke-Kerkem	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://allthingsbleuet.be/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	Time seems to have stopped still at Bleuet, which is confirmed by the view over the rolling hillsides of the Flemish Ardennes from the exquisite terrace and the cosy interior of this cosy cottage. Pieter-Jan is in the kitchen, while Yoran makes sure the dining room never gets too crowded to ensure optimum quality. Yoran can be relied upon to open a bottle of wine for you to taste, which is something of a rarity these days. The chef plays with familiar flavours and international accents, as his seabass fillets in a miso and champagne sauce with a risotto of wheat and crunchy veg demonstrates. Food that throbs with flavour and a felicitous feast of unexpected associations.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3336617718	Kwizien	Brugse Steenweg 200	Belgium	Maldegem	Car park,Terrace	https://www.kwizienmaldegem.be/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	The ingredient plays the star role in this welcoming farmstead. Thomas Coppejans scours the region for produce such as Malines chicken and asparagus, which are often on the menu. He also crafts a ceviche of seabass that will doubtless find favour with younger foodies. Ellen and her team will ply you with insightful tips to help you make your choice between the à la carte, dishes to share and the set menus. Sit back and soak up the infectiously bubbly vibe.	szabosofia	\N	\N
