3339185488	Bottega Bernacca	Rua Amauri 244	Brazil	São Paulo	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$	t	f	A small restaurant with a bistro-style ambience where the cuisine and decor are as meticulous as each other, the latter featuring a plethora of wood, impressive wine display cabinets and unusual details such as chairs hanging from the ceiling, a detail that is also found in its sister restaurants. The cooking here is authentic and delicious, and includes pasta cooked al dente in traditional Italian style and served straight from the pan to the table as if you were eating at home. Musts on the menu include the legendary Cipriani carpaccio, prepared with wafer-thin strips of filet mignon, served with a special house sauce and crunchy toast^ and the pesto lasagne that is suitable for sharing. For dessert, the classic tiramisù, made with mascarpone, is balanced by the flavour of bitter chocolate.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3337761065	Maza	Rua Manuel Guedes	Brazil	São Paulo	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking	https://mazarestaurante.com.br	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	$$$	f	f	As well as a highly enjoyable dining experience, Maza boasts a relaxing and welcoming setting, where the combination of wood and soft tones is clearly evident as soon as you walk through the door – a decor embellished by the beautiful cherry tree. The cuisine here is based around classic Japanese fare with a modern and personalised touch, including some Korean dishes. The different types of menus on offer include a seven-course option called Shinrai (served exclusively at table), the Omakase (only available at the bar counter), an à la carte. Exquisite dishes include karasumi, ussuzukuri, Wagyu tataki, “shake butter”, as well as sushi, sashimi, temaki. An impressive choice of sakes and cocktails completes the picture.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
