3337396342	Chosop	Shop 01	China Mainland	Fuzhou	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Sichuan	5.0	¥¥	f	t	This stylish venue in a shopping mall sports low fabric-clad partitions that provide privacy and enhance the overall vibe. The kitchen is helmed by a Sichuanese chef^ the extensive menu covers most bases of authentic Sichuan fare. Try pork belly braised in wine and soy with salted duck egg and rice for a satisfying meal. The Sichuan classic jidouhua – minced chicken and egg white poached in chicken stock to mimic tofu texture – is also impeccably crafted.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3337048618	Beiyuan Cuisine	202 Xiaobei Road	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.beiyuancuisine.com/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	¥¥	f	f	The national historical site in the heart of the city faithfully replicates details of a Lingnan-style Chinese garden. Inside, diners are wowed by 14 gilded redwood vases with elaborate carvings on all sides. Opened in 1928, it is famed not only for its palatial decor but also for such Cantonese home-style dishes as Huadiao drunken chicken and its exquisitely made dim sum – try char siu puff pastry, and steamed chicken with fish maw.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3330162907	BingSheng Pin Wei (Dongxiao Road)	33 Dongxiao Road	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	http://www.bingsheng.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	¥¥	f	t	The group first made its name with sashimi and, at this branch, diners may choose from sea perch, grass carp, amberjack and a myriad of live prawns. It also prides itself highly on the unmissable 'four beauties' – crispy char siu (pork belly crusted with breadcrumbs and sugar), soy-marinated pork trotters, pork tripe and goose intestines. Large parties may also try their jumbo-sized pineapple buns, to be ordered by the half dozen.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3339827182	Chao Ji Claypot Rice (Liwan)	723 Longjin East Road	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	¥	f	f	Time is of the essence when it comes to cooking claypot rice. In this popular two-storey joint, both the rice and soups are made to order, so expect to wait for at least 15-20 minutes, longer at peak hours. The rice is perfectly cooked, soft but toothsome with a crispy golden crust. Choose from an array of toppings: pork liver, chicken, pork patty, preserved pork and sausage, raw or fried eggs…	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3338313549	Deli Boutique・Uncle De Abalone	909 Xingye Avenue	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted	http://www.deshubaoyu.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	It’s a bit out of the way, but the ample parking, privacy in individual rooms and tasty abalone dishes make this trip worthwhile. The menu features abalone from South Africa, Middle East, Australia, Japan and Lienchiang in varying sizes—from 22 to 1.5 heads. The chefs cook the gastropod perfectly, rendering them flavourful and tender, but with a lovely chew. Other Cantonese dishes, especially those served in a claypot, also stand out. Reservations are recommended.	leonoscar	\N	\N
