3333486497	Mr & Mrs Bund	6F	China Mainland	Shanghai	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.mmbund.com/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	On the city's dining scene for over 10 years, Chef Pairet's brasserie never ages. Lovely service, great music, a terrific wine list and bags of French joie de vivre make dining here a real experience. In the modern space – inside a former bank dating from 1922 – diners feast on chilled seafood platters, and charbroiled steaks and seafood. Original creations such as lemon & lemon tart with a sorbet-filled whole lemon also stand out.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3330350675	Nuits	68 Tongren Road	China Mainland	Shanghai	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list		Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The bistro may not have a big shopfront, but its bright orange sign and full-height windows more than compensate in terms of impact. Named after Côte de Nuits in Burgundy, it serves a nice selection from that wine region. Head to the cellar to talk to the sommelier. The menu is mostly classic French and the signature beef tartare is laced with lightly cooked geoduck and oyster liquor, reflecting the bounty of sea and land.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3335570773	Hokkien Huay Kuan	5F	China Mainland	Shanghai		https://yueyegroup.com	Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The interior is inspired by Fujian-style ink paintings, with water features dividing the room into zones. On the menu, premium produce from the province is deftly prepared by Fujian natives for the most authentic experience possible. Try the signature Shuizhu seafood trio – live prawns, razor clams and giant red squid are blanched in a mild mala broth over a bed of pickled broccoli stems, cucumber and bean sprouts for crunch and tartness.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3330570521	Min He Nan Huan Xi	2F	China Mainland	Shanghai	Car park	https://www.lvdaohotel.com	Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The F&B group has been active in Fujian Province for over 30 years and its Shanghai outpost sports a classy décor. The menu features a line-up of lavish recipes, but even simple dishes like radish rice can be a highlight – long-grain rice is cooked with dried seafood, pork meat and bones for impressive sweetness and depth. Another iconic dish is layered chitterlings that delivers a gutsy mix of texture and flavour. The tea menu is worth exploring.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3338799384	Tea Culture (East Beijing Road)	L201A	China Mainland	Shanghai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Huaiyang	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	You can tell from the name that this restaurant is serious about the national beverage – professional tea masters brew the perfect cup, using top quality loose leaves and natural spring water. As for the food, the Guangdong chef displays his skills in a predominantly Huaiyang-inspired menu with some Jiangzhe and Cantonese dishes. The classic Buddha Jumps over the Wall is reworked with head of silver carp from Qiandao Lake (two portion sizes available).	langalice	\N	\N
3333114147	Wan Yan (Changning)	Inside Jin Jiang Cypress Hotel	China Mainland	Shanghai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Hui Cuisine	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Brace yourself for nostalgia aplenty: velvet tufted chairs, walls covered in vintage blue bricks, art pieces from around the world…Most ingredients are shipped from Anhui, including mouldy tofu – a speciality you can’t miss. Wine-scented fermented mandarin fish is another classic slightly adapted to suit the local palate. The Anhui-style braised pork trotter in soybean paste is cooked in a 30-year-old marinade for exceptional depth and layered flavours. On top of the à la carte menu, you can also have one tailored in advanced.	tudoroh	\N	\N
