3338037891	Waldinger	Županijska ulica 8	Croatia	Osijek	Air conditioning,Car park	https://waldinger.hr/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	The name of this restaurant situated in the Art Nouveau-style hotel of the same name pays tribute to the painter Adolf Waldinger, who was born in Osijek in 1843. In bright, modern dining rooms adorned with contemporary paintings, enjoy a selection of traditional dishes, with something for all tastes on the menu. If you like strong flavours, try the Slavonian black pork cheeks, while guests with a sweet tooth will be tempted by delicious desserts from the Gold pastry shop on the other side of the street, including Krempite tart (a puff pastry speciality with custard cream). The wine list includes labels from local, small-scale wineries. Comfortable, well-appointed guestrooms complete the picture.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3332139743	Spinnaker	Obala Maršala Tita 15	Croatia	Porec	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.restaurantspinnaker.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative	4.0	€€€	f	t	It was at Heinz Beck’s La Pergola that chef Goran Hrastovčak learned how to make an ingredient the centrepiece of a dish. In his two tasting menus, “Istrian Fables” and “Modern Tales” (as the names suggest, the first is more traditional and the second more innovative), the cuisine showcases the region and its iconic ingredients, such as scampi, squid, sea bass and Istrian beef. The ravioli filled with lobster and served with Jerusalem artichoke and a scampi bisque is highly recommended. The view of Poreč harbour plus a wine list that features excellent Istrian labels as well as an extensive selection of Croatian wines and renowned bottles from elsewhere in Europe add to the appeal. Among the local wines, we suggest the Primo Fakin, an Istrian Teran-based red with spicy aromas and a pleasant roundness.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3336990558	Ribarska Koliba	Verudela 3	Croatia	Pula	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.ribarskakoliba.com/en/restaurant/?/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood	4.0	€€	t	f	This century-old restaurant in the modern resort of Ribarska Koliba (the name translates as Fisherman’s Hut) stands near the Marina Veruda, which can be admired through its large picture windows or from its attractive summer terrace. Delicious Mediterranean cuisine takes pride of place on the menu, ranging from pasta-based starters to fish and seafood dishes made from the freshest ingredients (the bouillabaisse is superb), although a few meat specialities also feature. Vintage car enthusiasts can also admire the Triumph Spitfire convertible that is “parked” inside the restaurant.	winternoemi	\N	\N
