3336911223	Ô Gayot	2 avenue de la Ferté-Macé	France	Bagnoles-de-l'Orne	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ogayot.net/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This chic bistro in a pretty stone house certainly has its finger on the pulse. On the menu find good bistro recipes that change on a weekly basis. These include, soft - boiled egg with cream of mushroom soup and Calvados baba. A taste sensation!	havelisabella	\N	\N
3332142526	1217	Château de Bagnols	France	Bagnols	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.chateaudebagnols.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	This superb medieval château seems bent on upholding the opulent traditions of banquets of yore… Take a seat by the imposing, delicately carved Gothic fireplace and dig into a feast of infinite refinement. The strawberry-rhubarb dessert is to die for: crunchy strawberry topping, savory-flavoured pannacotta and fresh strawberry purée with a rhubarb sorbet. Wickedly tempting!	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3331197892	Epona	928 route de Chomérac	France	Baix	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	http://restaurant-epona.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Epona, Gallic goddess of travellers and abundance, watches over this welcoming establishment, conveniently located between Valence and Montélimar in the Ardèche. In the evenings and at weekends, peruse the set menu (without options) and the short, appetising seasonal à la carte menu. Rustic and warm, as he himself defines it, the chef's cuisine is rooted in the local terroir. With real jus and pretty presentations, his dishes show a deft touch: cold courgette velouté and gravlax salmon^ confit pork belly and seasonal vegetables. At lunchtime, a daily menu only is served.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3334653255	Maison de Laveline	5 rue du 8-Mai	France	Ban-de-Laveline	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.maison-de-laveline.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This rustic Vosges inn, depicted by a spruce yellow facade, is run by a youthful couple. The accent is clearly on wholesome French country fare and theme dinners based on a seasonal ingredient are organised throughout the year. Heart-warming dishes, such as melt-in-the-mouth veal chop and asparagus risotto. Meals are served in the recently refurbished dining room or on the patio in fine weather.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3335136738	L'Espérance	21 rue du Docteur-Louis-Marçon	France	Bandol	Air conditioning	https://www.lesperance-bandol.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	If you're lucky enough to be in Bandol, leave the harbour area and make a beeline for the refreshing establishment of Maria and Gilles Pradines, a treasure trove of culinary talent and delight. Born in the Basque country, the chef has retained his love of the south of France, from stuffed piquillo peppers to black cherries and pata negra. Each ingredient is fastidiously sourced and prepared with great care: wild sea bass marinated in fennel seeds, grilled special oyster no. 2, apricots from Provence, olive oil and lemons… The presentation of the dishes is beautiful, and the service is charming!	montanarijack	\N	\N
3330520388	Le Shardana	16 rue de la République	France	Bandol	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Bang in the middle of the seaside resort, this spruce, modern edifice is reminiscent of Sardinia, both in terms of the décor and the succulent seasonal food. The menu, which changes monthly, is liberally strewn with local and Sardinian ingredients. Examples include gently steamed local croaker in a tomato and cognac sauce with crunchy vegetables and black garlic or panettone French toast with roast apples, salted butterscotch and a scoop of stracciatella ice cream. The chef’s radiant wife cheerfully and professionally manages the front of house. Concise wine list of mainly Italian and local vintages.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3331937684	Les Oliviers	Hôtel Île Rousse	France	Bandol	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-les-oliviers-bandol.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	In Renécros Bay, this posh, stylish, fashionable restaurant commands a breathtaking view of the Mediterranean. Open for dinner (only!), Martin and Fleur craft colourful, flavoursome Mediterranean and Provençal cuisine, presented in several tasting menus, starring ingredients such as green asparagus from Mallemort, line-caught fish direct from local boats, strawberries from Hyères… As you might expect, the vision of the sun gently setting over the glittering horizon is truly spectacular!	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3331847146	Le Fanal	18 avenue Pierre-Fabre	France	Banyuls-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.pascal-borrell.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	The lights of Le Fanal (“The Lantern”) will guide you to this idyllic spot overlooking Banyuls marina. Catalan-born Pascal Borrell has decided to drop anchor here after stints in several top Paris restaurants and running the Chapon Fin at Perpignan. The main attraction here is fish: hake, monkfish, sole, turbot, cod and anchovy pickles delicately marinated in Banyuls vinegar.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3332201483	Bistro Saint-Jean	132 boulevard de la Rochelle	France	Bar-le-Duc	Air conditioning	https://bistrostjean.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This ex-grocer’s shop is now a contemporary bistro, rich in flavour and colour, that hits the spot every time. The owner, son of a pastry chef, rustles up market-fresh cuisine in tune with the seasons, like this slow-cooked pork belly with baby onions and braising juices. Respect for the ingredients is the motto. Efficient, unobtrusive staff.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3333354011	Ineffable	3 rue Grande	France	Barbentane	Air conditioning	https://restaurant-ineffable.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In a small Provençal village with bags of character, Ineffable promises diners a feast for the senses. The restaurant is run by a couple with a passion for what they do: Nicolas Thomas and Marie Salomez (previously of La Promenade, La Flibuste, Château de Courban). This space with a decor of exposed stone walls and contemporary furnishings, and animated by a soundscape of soothing birdsong has just five tables. The chef riffs on poetic culinary leitmotifs, marrying olives and olive wood, plants and seafood (even meat on the larger set menu). A music lover, he has a sense for timing and harmony, as demonstrated by his composition of vegetables topped with a smoked cream.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3332728360	La Bastide	Avenue des Thermes	France	Barbotan-les-Thermes	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.bastide-gasconne.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	In the small spa village of Cazaubon, this swanky 5-star Relais & Chateaux hotel, owned by the Guérard family, has been refurbished in a tasteful chic country house vein. The chef crafts a score founded on the classical, dietary recipes invented by the late Michel Guérard: the food is light, healthy, modern and overwhelmingly mouthwatering and each dish is generously laden in first-class, locally sourced seasonal produce, all of which is consummately crafted. Spot-on service and a swish, tasteful setting.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3333087647	Chilo	1410 rue Principale	France	Barcus	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.maison-chilo.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Arnaud Chilo and his sister Marina embody the fourth generation at the helm of this family inn established back in 1937. They brought a breeze of change, illustrated by new furniture and a reappointed dining room, which has happily retained its comforting rustic character, without forgetting the splendid view over the lush valley and the mountains from the terrace. The delicately updated cuisine is liberally sprinkled in fine Basque produce and keeps pace with the seasons: smoked trout^ baked pollock in a crust^ 7-hour slow-roasted shoulder of lamb…	vargalucia	\N	\N
3337090676	Le Carré des Saveurs	1770 chemin du Mas-du-Terme	France	Barjac	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.le-carre-des-saveurs.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	In the charming, peaceful setting of this former silkworm farm, surrounded by vineyards and olive groves, dine in the resolutely contemporary interior or on the pleasant terrace in a pretty courtyard. The cuisine draws inspiration from the terroir and tradition to showcase local ingredients: aubergine caviar with extra virgin olive oil^ delicious daube provençale (beef stew)^ pistachio financier and vanilla mousseline. As an added bonus, you can taste the wines and olive oil produced right here on the estate. Spacious contemporary guestrooms and a sense of serenity.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3331837629	Marnage - Hôtel La Marine	11 rue de Paris	France	Barneville-Carteret	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelmarine.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	With its panoramic view of the sea and the port, this local institution on the Cotentin peninsula faces the Channel Islands of Jersey and Guernsey. In a pleasant contemporary interior, you will sample modern, elegant cuisine that shines the limelight on Normandy produce, with a weakness for local seafood, illustrated by pollock, fennel (confit and roasted) and a lemon-flavoured butter emulsion.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3332172048	La Table du 5	Hôtel 5 Terres	France	Barr	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.5terres-hotel.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This contemporary restaurant located within the 5 Terres Hotel looks out over the magnificent Renaissance town hall (1640). In a light-filled space done out in premium materials, you can enjoy contemporary cuisine that brings the best out of carefully sourced local ingredients. The wine list is particularly impressive, featuring hundreds of organic and biodynamic labels.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3338868041	Maison Zugno	Les Monts de Vaux	France	Barretaine	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.maison-zugno.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Dating back to the late 18C, this former coaching inn has been turned into a charming hotel (nine guestrooms, a swimming pool and spa) and a restaurant with three small dining areas (wooden floors, walnut tables, exposed brick walls, floral wallpaper or a green wall). Chef Quentin Defert makes modern, entirely gluten-free cuisine from seasonal, often local produce (but that's not all). Starters include a pear brunoise paired with blue cheese from the nearby dairy in La Marre, creamed corn combined with hazelnuts, and melt-in-the-mouth Iberian pork belly served with romanesco and elevated by a flavoursome Thai emulsion.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3337226934	Loiseau des Vignes	31 rue Maufoux	France	Beaune	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.bernard-loiseau.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	A Bernard Loiseau stamped score and a chic bistro vibe (stone, wood and velvet-upholstered banquettes) paint this culinary portrait. The menu includes classics such as eggs in a red wine sauce, pâté en croûte, Charolais ox cheek and Saône catfish, without forgetting beautifully fresh Burgundy veal tartare with smoked eel. The splendid wine list also unveils a wide range of wines by the glass.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3338693032	Restaurant du Pont	147 rue du Grignon	France	Basse-Goulaine	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-du-pont.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Next to the small Canal de Goulaine, this white building, once a bar and inn, has a refined contemporary interior and pleasant terrace-garden for fine weather. Having plied his trade abroad, chef Mathieu Corbineau now navigates between rather traditional recipes and more contemporary influences: crispy chicken with tandoori spices, carrot, cumin and kumquat sabayon^ herb-crusted catch of the day, cereal risotto, citrus butter^ gariguette strawberry, yuzu cream, frosted marshmallow gariguette, Montélimar nougat ice cream. An affordable set menu at lunchtime, and a wine list that gives Muscadet top billing.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3336456496	Villa Mon Rêve	2 levée de la Divatte	France	Basse-Goulaine	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.villa-mon-reve.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	On the banks of the Loire, this restaurant is set in a pretty townhouse dating back to the late 19C. It has been proudly serving its guests delicious food in an elegant, cosy decor for 75 years – so you could say it's an institution. The current chef uses the finest local produce in traditional regional cuisine: frogs' legs with parsley butter or a herb sauce^ local fish (pike, pike-perch and sea bass) with beurre blanc^ golden-brown calf sweetbreads with a morel cream. A smiling welcome awaits you, as does a large shady terrace surrounded by a bucolic garden planted with colourful flowerbeds. Mon Rêve really is a dream!	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3337419916	Auberge du Prunelli	Pont de Pisciatello	France	Bastelicaccia	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://auberge-du-prunelli.fr/	Nessun premio	Country cooking	5.0	€€	f	t	A cosy, inviting atmosphere reigns in this restaurant that first welcomed guests in 1860 in its former life as a coaching inn. It's been a family affair since 1997, when father André Orlandazzi bought the place – today his sons have taken over the reins. Charcuterie, cheeses and honey from the valley, vegetables from the garden, simple dishes simmered for hours on the stove, tarts made with fruit from the orchard, over 200 Corsican wines... Timeless! In fine weather, you might like to take advantage of the large terrace surrounded by greenery overlooking the Prunelli.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3332519701	La Table du Lion	71 rue Saint-Jean	France	Bayeux	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.liondor-bayeux.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	At Le Lion d'Or, the chef works his magic with produce sourced in Normandy that he embellishes with Asian flavours. An unexpected culinary marriage inspired by his travels in Asia, particularly Japan and Thailand. Add to this, flawless culinary technique and seasoning and you will be roaring with pleasure!	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3338158913	Le 1720 - Château de Sully	Route de Port-en-Bessin	France	Bayeux	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.chateau-de-sully.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Grandiose is the term that springs to mind when describing this 18C château, set in landscaped grounds planted with Lebanese cedars and sequoias. Take a seat in one of the plush dining rooms or in the bright conservatory to savour the chef’s predominantly Normandy-focused cuisine: vegetables, cheeses, foie gras and, of course, line-caught fish.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3337421531	La Table - Sébastien Gravé	21 quai Amiral-Dubourdieu	France	Bayonne	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://latable-sebastiengrave.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Cuisine from South West France	3.0	€€	t	f	After the success of Pottoka in Paris, the chef, a key figure on the Bayonne bistronomy scene, is back on his home turf. All smiles behind the stove, he prepares dishes inspired by the best produce South-West France has to offer, including natural hake from Saint-Jean-de-Luz, marinated and charred mackerel and Ibaïma pork shoulder. You can eat at the zinc-topped counter, at the large table d'hôtes with friends or in the kitchen (there is a table for two, for a more immersive experience). An inviting restaurant with a convivial atmosphere!	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3339362526	Nuance	23 rue des Cordeliers	France	Bayonne	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://restaurantnuance.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Having worked at Choko Ona in Espelette, Brice Goeuriot and Margaux Le Baillif have a taste for nuance, as reflected in their refined interior decorated with natural materials by Basque artisans. The result is on point – an upscale and comfortable setting with a warm and friendly vibe. A lot of work has gone into sourcing produce from small-scale organic farmers and producers from the Landes and Basque regions, and the chef's blind menu is stacked with complex dishes, in which ingredients are often prepared in several guises (eg lamb leg, chop and shoulder confit). Aromatic plants and herbs are skilfully used in a variety of ways: oxalis flower and sea fennel sorbet, wild garlic sabayon, nasturtium extraction. Infinitely delicate cuisine.	calincolin	\N	\N
3330221690	Relief	11 rue Sainte-Catherine	France	Bayonne	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.reliefrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Slap-bang in the middle of the Saint Esprit neighbourhood, Thibault Deverre is at the helm of this bistro that cultivates a nostalgic vibe with rustic furnishings and rush straw-upholstered seats. The chef prepares fresh, spontaneous, multi-dimensional dishes with finesse and originality, eg crabmeat, asparagus ice-cream and grapefruit tempura^ red tuna, creamy polenta, smoked aubergine caviar, crisp red cabbage salad^ white chocolate cream, gariguette strawberry and sorbet. A resounding success, especially with Bayonne's young foodies!	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3338875480	Auberge du Cheval Blanc	68 rue Bourgneuf	France	Bayonne	Air conditioning	http://www.cheval-blanc-bayonne.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This 18C coaching inn has been run by the same family since 1959. Chef Jean-Claude Tellechea adds a new spin to the traditional regional line-up: crispy hake, black pudding, Ibaïama ham, Bayonne chocolate. The interior is patriotically decked in red and white Basque Country colours. The range of menus is such that there is something for every budget.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
3338439106	La Grange	26 quai Galuperie	France	Bayonne	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lagrange-bayonne.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	In this city centre restaurant, old stones blend seamlessly with contemporary decoration. On the menu: market - fresh ingredients and a handful of bistro specialities with Basque overtones. In summer, make the most of the terrace beneath the arcades, on the banks of the Nive.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3335735174	Le P'tit Bateau	54 rue du Pont	France	Beaugency	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-lepetitbateau.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of the medieval city, Le P'tit Bateau sets out to tantalise our taste buds with fresh produce, including fish sourced directly from Brittany's fish markets, as well as game from Sologne in season. The dishes are generous, precise, carefully presented and tasty. It is worth noting there is a pleasant patio for a meal al fresco. An eatery committed to doing a good job.	salajakub	\N	\N
3338331955	La Table de la Réserve	5 boulevard du Maréchal-Leclerc	France	Beaulieu-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.reservebeaulieu.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Supervised by chef Julien Roucheteau, this restaurant is a welcome gourmet addition to the dining options at this superb establishment. The contemporary Mediterranean-inspired menu takes inspiration from the local terroir – note the textures of pissaladière with house-marinated anchovy and a sweet onion espuma, or the tartlet showcasing figs from the Var, with its melting brambleberry centre. You might also like to sample their bouillabaisse (Fri and Sat), traditional octopus dishes from the South of France, or rockfish soup. Diners take their seats in a bistro-style setting that is suitably cordial and laid back.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3335971771	So'Mets	5 rue du Lieutenant-Colonelli	France	Beaulieu-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.somets-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	After honing her skills in top restaurants (including La Vague d’Or), chef Anne-Sophie Sabini has struck out on her own in this modern, colourful gastropub, flanked by a lovely terrace. She has devised a concise menu that changes monthly, in which she adds a feminine, modern touch to Gallic standards: cream of green peas with a 64° poached egg, coppa, crunchy croutons and organic olive oil from Provence^ roast squid and black pudding, purée of carrots, citrus-flavoured dressing^ sorbet of Beaulieu mandarin, anis-flavoured biscuit, praline and drizzled citrus fruit and bergamot … Slick service, charming welcome. Heaven for foodies!	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3337030568	L'Étape Louis 13	2 route de la Barre-en-Ouche	France	Beaumesnil	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://etapelouis13.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This 17C presbytery located near the Château de Beaumesnil has a superb Louis XIII - style and exudes a timeless atmosphere. Under the direction of its young owners, it is the ideal place to discover some of Normandy's culinary traditions such as hot oysters with Camembert and light Calvados soufflé. Freshness and flavours are on the agenda.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3337094124	Domitia - Maison de Cuisinier	440 rue des Micocouliers	France	Beaumettes	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://domitia-maisondecuisinier.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	t	Slices of Mediterranean dentex served raw, caraway, cauliflower and elderberry vinegar^ Camargue bull, oyster tartare from the Étang de Thau and salicornia-pistachio pesto: there's no doubt that chef Jérôme Faure has a masterful understanding of gourmet cuisine. His subtly innovative take on fine dining is based on a rigorous selection of local ingredients. The same goes for the wines.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3336051648	Auberge de l'Abbaye	2 rue de la Libération	France	Beaumont-en-Auge		http://www.auberge-abbaye-beaumont.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Local produce, meticulous plating, generous helpings and a taste for fresh herbs, all in tune with the seasons: the scene is set. And let’s not forget the rustic interior of this inn in the heart of a Normandy village that is the epitome of French rural charm.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3336841876	Caves Madeleine	8 rue du Faubourg-Madeleine	France	Beaune	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://cavesmadeleine.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	A stone's throw from the town centre, this wine bar-restaurant is a little gem. Chef Martial has hooked up with the best local producers, including some top wine growers, to create wholesome, punchy cuisine that is rife with flavour, eg warm potatoes, haddock, and tarragon sabayon. Relaxed, no-fuss service – the focus is firmly on the contents of your glass and your plate. In fine weather, make the most of the pleasant terrace in the shade of a fig tree.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3333459731	Garum	10 rue de l'Hôtel-Dieu	France	Beaune	Terrace	https://www.garum-beaune.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The chef has turned his Jardin des Remparts into a “living table”. This fashionable, classy bistro uses premium ingredients in a menu ranging from pre-dinner snacks to share with friends (Gillardeau oysters, charcuterie and French fries) to a selection of mouth-watering, well-crafted seasonal dishes. The bistro’s namesake (garum) is a fermented sauce, popular with the Romans, that Christophe Bocquillon uses to season beef tartare, in particular.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3337303324	L'Alentour	10 rue d'Alsace	France	Beaune	Wheelchair access	http://www.lalentour.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This quintessentially cosmopolitan, downtown eatery of Beaune is the joint brainchild of Tatenda Mhende, in charge of the dining room, who hails from Zimbabwe, chef Natasha Watson, who is from Calgary (Canada) and Marc Marchetti, also a chef, who is a Beaujolais lad. This alchemy of buddies has sparked a particularly appetising culinary offering that is depicted by a concise menu of hearty dishes packed with punchy flavours, to be shared (or not!): barbecued oxheart tomatoes, smoked tomato water and mozzarella^ crunchy fritters of mushrooms with marrow, chardonnay-flavoured vinegar gel^ pork belly, patty pan squash and courgettes.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3339675745	L'Écusson	2 rue du Lieutenant-Dupuis	France	Beaune	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ecusson.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Proudly flying the fine dining flag, the chef, who trained in prestigious establishments (La Côte Saint-Jacques, Lameloise and La Pyramide), crafts a fresh, colourful score that is often jazzed up with citrus fruits. The result is often inspired, illustrated by langoustine and tourteau crab, leeks, buckwheat, watercress and smoked yoghurt or scallops, Belgian endive, salsify and clementines… Meals are served in a bright, contemporary interior.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3331048480	L'Expression	11 rue Maufoux	France	Beaune	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.lexpressionbeaune.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This city-centre establishment serves top-drawer ingredients, many of which are to share (whole fish from the market, rib of Galice beef, butterflied, plump fattened Bresse Miéral chicken), in two trendily appointed dining rooms (open kitchen, glazed wine cellar and high tables). The food is cooked in a wood-fired oven. Extroverted, friendly atmosphere. Beautifully curated wine list.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3339473181	Le Bénaton	25 rue du Faubourg-Bretonnière	France	Beaune	Terrace	https://www.lebenaton.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	In the heart of Burgundy, Beaune is known the world over for its annual charity wine auction held in the iconic Hospices edifice, famous for its glazed tile roof. A steadfast champion of fine French food and wine, Japanese chef Keishi Sugimura, couldn’t have found a town that suits him better. Trained in Japan, the chef excels in the art of the porkpie, which earned him the title of vice world champion in 2013. Flavoursome seasonal dishes sprinkled with creative touches.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3339846856	Soul Kitchen	1 rue Rousseau-Deslandes	France	Beaune	Air conditioning	http://www.soulkitchen-beaune.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table	3.0	€	f	f	“Let me sleep all night in your soul kitchen” hauntingly sang Jim Morrison on the Doors’ first album and you can always ask Mathieu Guennal, the owner-chef who works alone in this dinky (12 seats only) downtown eatery in Beaune, if he’s willing to put you up! Mathieu works with local producers (chalked up on the blackboard) and cheerfully dishes up soul-warming, heartfelt nosh, as good as it is unfussy (such as slow-cooked pork belly, a ginger reduction and gratin of helianthus) in two gloriously priced €30 menus (one of which changes weekly). Take a seat and soak up the friendly, casual vibe of this small eatery with wooden floors and a raftered ceiling in the company of a generous chef.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3330669926	La Table de Beaurecueil	66 allée des Mûriers	France	Beaurecueil	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.latabledebeaurecueil.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This restaurant is housed in a former sheep barn and features a resolutely contemporary design (only a few of the original rustic features remain). It offers “cuisine du terroir” based on high quality produce. Wine by the glass.	basileryan	\N	\N
3331382687	Autrement	128 rue de Paris	France	Beauvais	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.autrement-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	At a slight remove from the town centre, this quiet little restaurant lays out its own fresh vision. The chef perfectly masters cooking times and seasonings, and works with quality ingredients. His original and colourful cuisine is meticulous and tasty^ for instance, his half-cooked veal carpaccio, beetroot, carrots and citrus fruit is a showstopper. Not forgetting his signature dessert: the Paris-Brest. What are you waiting for?	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3330977779	Le Senso	25 rue d'Agincourt	France	Beauvais	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://Sensobeauvais.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	On the market square, this spruce, well-kept restaurant provides the perfect foil for simple, unfussy cuisine in which local produce takes pride of place. Chef Allan Castellote cannot be faulted for his artistic presentations, while his brother Tristan masterfully attends to the wine-food pairing suggestions. The house speciality, kouign amann, is to die for!	santoronicola	\N	\N
3335703996	Au Roman du Vercors	1 ancienne route de Presles	France	Beauvoir-en-Royans	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-roman-du-vercors.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	The chef and his wife now welcome guests on the slopes of the Vercors in the listed medieval site of a former Carmelite convent (flanked by a museum, garden and conservatory orchard with fruit varieties native to South Grésivaudan, which can be visited after your meal). The menu showcases market-fresh seasonal and regional produce, racks reminiscent of walnut drying sheds adorn the interior, outdoors is a pleasant, shaded patio.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3332637792	Restaurant Côté Marais	Le Grand Pont	France	Beauvoir-sur-Mer	Car park,Terrace	http://www.restaurant-cotemarais.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	A starter of ceviche of white mullet (a fish rarely found on restaurant menus) with rhubarb for a hint of tartness, followed by a savoury/sweet main course of pollack fished by small boats, French peas al dente and a smattering of sweet cherry condiment. The young chef applies his own personal culinary style to local ingredients, while his partner works the restaurant floor in this outlying establishment surrounded by marshland (and with a lovely terrace).	casiniivan	\N	\N
3337110735	Le Contemporain	4 rue Jean-Jaurès	France	Beauvois-en-Cambrésis	Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lecontemporain.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	This family home dating back to the 19C was converted into a restaurant in 2008. At the helm, an experienced couple: she works in the kitchen, showcasing the home - grown produce by creating tasty dishes^ he is in charge of front of house, as well as upkeep of the vegetable garden. Modern, light - filled conservatory.	beloveva	\N	\N
3331289622	Auberge Le Bouc Bleu	2 rue du 5-Décembre	France	Beblenheim	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.aubergeleboucbleu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Chef Romain Hertrich and sommelier Romain Lambert, after stints in top establishments in France and abroad, are at the helm of this pretty half-timbered inn. Pan-fried girolles with pak choy, pumpkin seeds and pine nuts, or seared beef chuck steak with onion and beetroot pickles... All produce are from organic or small producers. Thoughtful food-wine pairings.	berninialex	\N	\N
3330682432	La Colombe	3890 route du Mont-Ventoux	France	Bedoin	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.la-colombe.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	At the foot of Mont Ventoux surrounded by vineyards, this gourmet dove coos a delicious melody. Chef Christophe Schuffenecker (formerly of the star-rated Château de Mazan) serves modern, spot-on dishes, blessedly free of superfluous extras, such as Sarrians pigeon with geranium-perfumed mashed carrots. When the weather is fine, make a beeline for the terrace shaded by awnings overlooking the vineyards. The stylish interior sports bare beams and a large Provençal fireplace, as well as a permanent art exhibition.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3330694306	Le Lien	32 faubourg de Montbéliard	France	Belfort	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurant-lelien.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	The bond here (‘lien’ in French) is that which ties this young couple (he’s in the kitchen, she in the front of house) to the winegrowers and producers whose work is showcased in the plates and glasses of this friendly bistro. Modern food with a creative twist founded on first-class seasonal ingredients that are allowed to shout their name. Two lunchtime menus and a more elaborate offering in the evening. Highly recommended.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3336529412	Château du Bost	27 rue de Beauséjour	France	Bellerive-sur-Allier	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://chateau-du-bost.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	A few minutes from Vichy, in peaceful grounds, this château with towers and a water-filled moat (15C-19C) offers a contemporary and cosy decor, complemented by a beautiful terrace and some comfortable guestrooms. The restaurant has a refined setting and serves tasty seasonal cuisine.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3337531198	La Fine Fourchette	2500 avenue du Bugey	France	Belley	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.restaurantlafinefourchette.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	A jaw-dropping view over the Canal du Rhône and an elegant interior set the scene in this renowned regional temple of good food. Generous portions of Ain produce take the limelight in the chef’s well-crafted score, depicted by fascinating flavour combinations and impeccable plating. Special mention for the strawberry-themed dessert that will knock the tastebuds off fans of fine French fare!	testagabriel	\N	\N
3338053764	L'Imparfait	8 rue des Fontaines	France	Bergerac	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.imparfait.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In this medieval edifice in historic Bergerac, the chef has been crafting seasonal cuisine of regional inspiration that packs a punch for over 15 years. In summer on the terrace or in winter by a huge fireplace, you will sample elegant, deftly curated dishes, such as panacotta of white asparagus, crab meat and aïoli or a chou craquelin (half chou – half macaroon) with Timut-flavoured stewed strawberries and basil ganache: the antithesis of imperfect in fact!	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3331701958	L'As de Trèfle	420 rue Léopold-Hettier	France	Bernières-sur-Mer	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantasdetrefle.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€€	t	f	Slightly set back from the D-Day landing beaches on the Côte de Nacre, here we are in the very pleasant restaurant of Anthony Vallette, an energetic chef from Normandy, born in Condé-sur-Vire. Over the course of the seasons, he draws on the flavours of the local terroir – fish from the Channel, andouille de Vire, De Bayeux pork – and composes meticulous dishes with just the right amount of daring! His modern cuisine takes its cue from the market and follows his heart… and his personal favourites are reflected in the menu!	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3337987287	Épicéa	11 rue Claude-Pouillet	France	Besançon	Air conditioning	https://restaurant-epicea.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In a narrow street near the Doubs, this couple, who earned their stripes in prestigious establishments, work in tandem in the open kitchen, occasionally venturing out to serve diners. Their single set menu, based on carefully selected seasonal produce and enhanced by wild-picked ingredients, is akin to a natural history lesson: carrot / marjoram / plantain / burnet / bay leaf^ black pork / pumpkin / poultry jus / spring onion oil^ beetroot / raspberry / coriander / iced nougat.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3333142495	Le Manège	2 faubourg Rivotte	France	Besançon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurantlemanege.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	At the foot of the citadel, this former military riding arena specialises in delicate, flavoursome fare rich in regional twists (such as a mushroom crust cooked in vin jaune or their amazing sliced black pudding). The self-taught chef is a stickler for perfection – as the first and last bite will confirm.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3336291796	Le Parc	Place de la 1ère-Armée-Française	France	Besançon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://leparcbesancon.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of the Parc Micaud, on the banks of the River Doubs, this glass, concrete and steel pavilion is the Modernist work of Besançon architect Michel Demenge. The chic, contemporary interior, with its open-plan kitchen, also offers a view of the river. Dishes are in a contemporary vein, the menu under the supervision of the chef of nearby Château de Germigney.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3332888070	Le Sauvage	6 rue du Chapitre	France	Besançon	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lesauvage-besancon.fr/le-restaurant/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	At the foot of the Vauban Citadel, this smart hotel occupies the former convent of the Poor Clares. The restaurant provides a cosy setting, with old parquet floors and tablecloths, and – a major asset – its terrace overlooking the park! Chef Hugo Mathieu (trained in Lyon's top restaurants) is no novice, judging by his polished dishes: glazed pea velouté, cod loin fillet cooked at 50C, crispy pistachio tartlet.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3334512022	Loiseau du Temps	27 rue des Boucheries	France	Besançon	Wheelchair access	https://www.bernard-loiseau.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Set in a former 18C grain store, this handsome dining room, with vaulted ceiling and contemporary details, is home to the Besançon outpost of the Bernard Loiseau Group. The menu focuses on produce and recipes from Bourgogne-Franche-Comté: hotpot of snails with cancoillotte and Morteau sausage, chicken fricassée Gaston Gérard style, Côte d’Or pork chop with Jura tomme gratin… Enticing dessert trolley and a decent selection of wines, particularly by the glass.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3331648792	L'Adress...	1 rue des Iris	France	Bessines	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-ladress.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	A glazed parallelepiped extended by decking and framed by greenery: such is the modern, stylish setting! David Seguin’s inventive menu is devised around high-calibre produce. The cooking is flawless, the plating exquisite and the flavours ideally balanced, such as crab and avocado ravioles with buckwheat and a tangy shellfish stock. Splendid cheese platter.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3331046627	Maison Renard	15 place de la République	France	Béthune	Wheelchair access	https://www.maisonrenard-bethune.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Chef Sébastien Renard (Top Chef semi-finalist in 2022) has taken over the former premises of his mentor, the great chef Marc Meurin. This red-brick mansion oozes style, and its bar and elegant glass roof lend it undeniable flair. The chef, who hails from the region and made his solo debut here, turns out a carte blanche menu inspired by conversations with the growers who supply his kitchen with their produce. Dishes such as green asparagus, sheep's milk fromage frais and tarragon cream, or poached eggs in a red wine sauce with mushroom cream and walnut emulsion showcase all the savoir-faire of this chef with an impressive CV to his name.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3335015269	Le Pavé d'Auge	Le Bourg	France	Beuvron-en-Auge	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.pavedauge.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Situated between Caen and Lisieux in the heart of the Pays d’Auge, Beuvron-en-Auge is picture postcard perfect with its 17-18C half-timbered houses, its manors and its gardens decked in flowers come summertime. The restaurant, which occupies the village’s former covered market, is fully in keeping with this olde worlde character. Chef Adrien Haye champions local producers in a bid to work with the best seasonal produce. The enticing culinary lineup allows diners to choose from oysters from Saint-Vaast, lobster from Carteret or John Dory, as well as foie gras, veal sweetbread, tripe and andouille sausage. The quintessence of Normandy!	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3330785483	La Maison de Petit Pierre	22 avenue Pierre-Verdier	France	Béziers	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamaisondepetitpierre.fr/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Enthusiastic chef Pierre Augé is at the helm of this restaurant with a personalised decor that is located close to the bullring. He greets each and every customer with an infectious smile because he is there to spread joy with his tasty creative cuisine based on local ingredients! Rather than bask in the media hype, he is clearly driven by a desire to continuously explore new culinary avenues. It's a joy to behold – and tuck into – dishes such as his whisky-marinated pavé de bœuf steak and cauliflower mousseline with vanilla^ hake with piperade and green jus^ or stracciatella with asparagus and bacon tuile. A buzzy, friendly vibe, enhanced by the personality of the chef, and the warm, cheerful service of his wife, adds the final flourish: recommended!	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3335019679	Freya	1 rue du Lycée	France	Biarritz	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://freya-biarritz.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative, Vegetarian	5.0	€€	t	f	Freya, the goddess of nature in Norse mythology, presides over the very vegetable-forward feast served at this compact restaurant in the Saint-Charles neighbourhood. At the helm is a couple with a wealth of professional experience and many trips around the globe under their belt. Chef Guillaume Chatillon doesn't shy away from using meat or fish (particularly the top-notch fish from Saint-Jean-de-Luz fish market), but focuses on vegetables, which are elevated in the same way as any other premium ingredient, with a host of indulgent preparations and occasionally daring combinations, such as his beautifully balanced cauliflower with seaweed. N.B. Guests at the same table are invited to share the same plate. Wine recommendations come, with a smile, from Margot – most are organic or natural, and all are available by the glass.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3339201828	Cheri Bibi	50 rue d'Espagne	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://cheribibibiarritz.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Cheri Bibi is named after the hero of Gaston Leroux's novel Chéri-Bibi et Cécily. The chef at this trendy bistro is Brittany-born Adrien Witte, formerly a financier, who has turned his passion into a career. Seen in action in his kitchen from the restaurant floor, he goes to great lengths to make his guests feel good. The chef's dishes, which are designed for sharing (but don't have to be!), are based on the best local ingredients. Expect uninhibited and flavoursome creations, with nods to his international career: mimosa eggs^ grilled sweetcorn, oyster mushroom pickles, peanuts from Aquitaine, shiso and crispy chilli oil^ line-caught mahi-mahi, pil-pil sauce and roast aubergine. His efficient partner welcomes guests with a smile. You can choose your own bottle in the wine shop.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3330493795	L'Entre Deux	5 avenue du Maréchal-Foch	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.lentredeuxbiarritz.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Young chef Rémy Escale is at the helm of this trendy bistro, which is inviting and tastefully decorated. Food - wise, the objective has been set to stick close to the ingredients and bring out their natural flavour. He weaves flavours together with panache, demonstrating faultless technical know - how: an enjoyable experience.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3338291585	Le Café de Paris	5 place Bellevue	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-cafedeparis-biarritz.com/views/fr/restaurant.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	The legendary Café de Paris boasts a prime location in the heart of town, just above the Grande Plage. Diners choose dishes from an intelligently updated brasserie repertoire, inspired by the local terroir and peppered with nods to the Iberian peninsula. Think supreme of free-range poultry browned in a sauté pan, piperade spiced up with chorizo and confit grenaille potatoes. Pleasant terrace.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3331492075	Le Sin	1 avenue de la Plage	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.le-sin.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Within the Cité de l'Océan, Le Sin’s eye-catching wave-shaped architecture commands drop-dead views of the sea and Château d'Ilbarritz. The ingenious chef-craftsman selects first-rate ingredients which he incorporates into an elaborate bistro menu that changes regularly. An example: farm-reared pigeon, gutsy garlic-flavoured jus and mashed potato.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3337414248	Léonie	7 avenue de Larochefoucault	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-biarritz-leonie.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The name is a tribute to the founder of this modest eatery, which opened in the late 1940s. It has since morphed into a pleasant contemporary bistro in the capable hands of an enthusiastic young couple who are no strangers to the business. Originally from the Deux-Sèvres, the chef fell in love with the Basque Country and its produce^ he has made game his speciality in season. On this occasion, though, we were treated to an onion, tomato and pepper compote tart, followed by a hake steak with basil pesto and extra virgin oil, and a nectarine coulis with crème diplomate and meringue.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3332497736	Lore Ttipia - Auberge Ostape	Domaine de Chahatoenia	France	Bidarray	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ostape.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	A sprawling country estate on the heights of Bidarray and Itxassou is home to this inn that occupies a 17C farmstead. A panoramic terrace commands a jaw-dropping view of the grandiose rolling countryside. Chef John Argaud, who trained with the best of the Basque Country (La Table des Frères Ibarboure, Ithurria) as well as at Le Meurice with Alain Ducasse in Paris, shines the spotlight on outstanding local produce. Some ingredients are cooked over embers or finished on a hot stone for an added distinctive edge. The food is crisp, legible and delicate, like the stuffed courgette flowers with grilled cuttlefish. From Monday to Wednesday, the restaurant only offers a bistronomic menu, which is simpler but just as appetising as that available later in the week.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3333549787	Ezkia	6 avenue de la Grande-Plage	France	Bidart	Terrace	http://www.ezkia-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Whether beneath the lime trees (ezkia in Basque) on the terrace, or inside the small, inviting and intimate restaurant room with exposed stonework, floorboards, saffron-coloured velvet seats and banquettes, it is the same traditional Basque house. Standing in the heart of the delightful village of Bidart, it exudes a quiet, refined atmosphere. The couple who run the place, defectors from Michel Guérard's restaurant, serve nice seasonal precisely cooked dishes, full of good local Basque produce e.g. farm-reared pig, line-caught tuna, black cherry, mature farm cheeses.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3336438029	Domaine de Rochevilaine	à la Pointe de Pen-Lan	France	Billiers	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list	https://www.domainerochevilaine.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Right on the coast, this estate features a collection of traditional stone-built cottages and manors, some of which centuries old, in manicured grounds. It is just the ticket if you fancy super-fresh seafood^ chef Maxime Nouail is also a fisherman. Tastefully appointed lounges, bar and dining rooms, a knockout wine list, plush guestrooms and a spa for a luxurious seaside stay!	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3332662254	Le Strasbourg	24 rue du Colonel-Teyssier	France	Bitche	Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.le-strasbourg.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Originally a farm mechanic from the former East Germany, Lutz Janisch was trained by chef Jean Albrecht (at the restaurant Au Vieux Couvent in Rhinau). His appetising cuisine is contemporary and generous, and has a variety of inspirations (Italian: home-made strozzapreti to accompany fried squid stuffed with prawns and courgettes^ Japanese: quail leg tempura and a roast quail fillet kebab^ and French: crêpes Suzette and Grand Marnier ice cream). He often uses local ingredients (trout from Eguelshardt, vegetables from Sturzelbronn etc). There are also guestrooms.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3339203693	L'Esberit	34 boulevard du Commandant-René-Mouchotte	France	Bizanos	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-lesberit.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This handsome 19C listed stone house, located by a road and just a few minutes from downtown Pau, deploys all its charms to the rear of the property thanks to the peaceful garden patio, shaded by a hundred-year-old oak tree. Inside, the stylish dining room sports herringbone parquet flooring and high ceilings. Chef Nicolas Lormeau has been thriving in this plush setting for some years now. His inventive recipes are a treasure trove of plays on texture and harmonious or surprising flavours (such as the multiple textures of marinated scallops with passion fruit and sweetcorn or the semolina milk with truffles from Lot, kiwi and yuzu-flavoured white chocolate ice cream). Béarn produce takes the limelight in creative, skilfully plated dishes, served professionally and seamlessly. Book (well) in advance!	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3336900184	Amour Blanc	Hôtel Fleur de Loire	France	Blois	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://fleurdeloire.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Christophe Hay's second restaurant is named after a species of carp. It is located on the first floor of a modern extension slightly set back from the original building. This inviting wood-panelled and light-filled interior, with its large bay windows looking out over the Loire, immediately works its magic. The chef of Fleur de Loire gives free rein to his passion for Loire ingredients (local cheeses, géline de Touraine heirloom poultry, fried small fish and mullet from the River Loire, lamb and caviar from the Sologne), but also Wagyu beef from his own farm. In short, fine ingredients treated with care to create dishes that tend towards the classical.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3332933598	Bro's	36 rue de la Foulerie	France	Blois	Terrace	http://www.brosrestaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This eatery in the historic town just a stone’s throw from the banks of the Loire, which has quickly been taken by storm by the locals, is the brainchild of two enthusiastic cooks and inseparable pals. The scene upstairs sports a stylish rustic interior with contemporary touches, providing the perfect foil to a bistronomic score that shines the spotlight on locally sourced, seasonal ingredients, naturally washed down with Loire wines. Tapas inspired by the produce of south-west France and Spain are also available (evenings only and without reservations) in the ground-floor room.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3334742298	Brut maison de cuisine	14 quai Villebois-Mareuil	France	Blois	Air conditioning	https://www.brutmaisondecuisine.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This tasty bistro with a contemporary feel has an open kitchen, shelves filled with jars of fermented vegetables and books… and just a handful of tables, so it's best to book. The chef, who has a solid track record, devises a short menu that changes regularly. The three pillars of his cooking are seasonality, local ingredients (such as Racan poultry) and modern, often bold cuisine, for example his dessert that combines a naturally sweet Jerusalem artichoke cream and a coffee ice cream with a pronounced flavour. Short list of natural and organic wines.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3331442787	Le Val d'Auge	805 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Bondues	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://www.valdauge.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	It may have an exterior that is typical of northern France, with its white bricks and eaves, small window panes and black surrounds, but this restaurant actually has a smart contemporary interior. Chef Christophe Hagnerelle is a true craftsman, who creates unfussy seasonal cuisine. The menu features excellent fish and shellfish from the North Sea, including turbot, sea bass or John Dory, depending on the catch of the day, but also scallops, as well as grouse and hare à la royale in season, veal sweetbreads and pigeon – from Flanders, of course.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3333169792	Finestra by Italo Bassi	51 quai Jérôme-Comparetti	France	Bonifacio	Air conditioning	https://finestra-d-amore.fr/	Nessun premio	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Among the traditional shopfronts, this elegant façade stands out from the crowd on Bonifacio harbour. On the first floor, this superb designer space mimicking the shape of the inverted hull of a ship, with a subtle maritime-inspired decor, features a large window (finestra in Italian) overlooking the port. Chef Italo Bassi, who presides also over the kitchens of his restaurant in Sardinia, has devised a menu that allies the cuisines of Italy and Corsica. The mainly local ingredients are handpicked in these masterfully prepared dishes – the double ravioli with two fillings, burrata, guinea fowl casserole and its reduction, light cream of parmesan and fresh thyme is a particularly appetising signature dish!	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3330675493	Le Voilier	81 quai Comparetti	France	Bonifacio	Terrace	https://www.levoilier-bonifacio.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Drop anchor in the marina and climb on board this elegant yacht to sample fresh Mediterranean cuisine (fish soup and carpaccio, ceviche, courgette blossoms) in which the local catch (whole or in portions) takes pride of place. Meat lovers are, however, not forgotten and the menu also offers dishes such as a thick juicy veal cutlet or stuffed saddle of lamb.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3339343969	L'A Cheda	Route de Cavallo-Morto	France	Bonifacio	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://acheda-hotel.com/restaurant-gastronomique-bonifacio/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Take a seat on the terrace overlooking the pool in a setting, steeped in romanticism. The chef has a preference for local ingredients and rigorously selects his suppliers. You will enjoy wild fish, organic Corsican meat and vegetables fresh from the permaculture garden. Attentive service and a wine list rich in pleasant surprises.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3330453925	L'An Faim	7 montée Rastello	France	Bonifacio	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This small restaurant is located at the end of the marina, by the stairs that go up to the citadel. Boasting a terrace, it is a favourite with regulars, attracted by the menu bursting with colourful, flavoursome market-fresh cuisine, including Corsican veal and prawns, pastilla of suckling lamb from Bonifacio, and blanquette-style dentex and vegetables. At lunchtime there is a simpler set menu.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3332878357	Auberge de la Poutre	25 Grande-Rue	France	Bonlieu	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.aubergedelapoutre.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	In the hub of a pretty village in the Jura lakes area, this family-run inn dating from 1740 plays on its rustic charm. Chef François Moureaux works with fine ingredients to create delicate and tasty contemporary cuisine, but doesn't neglect to revisit local specialities. As for the decor, the establishment is named after one notable feature: its 17m-long ceiling beam that comes from a 3m3 fir log!	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3334740985	Auberge de la Haute-Joux	2 rue du Jura	France	Bonnevaux	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.aubergedelahautejoux.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	A former philosopher (and the epitome of courtesy and discernment when it comes to her wine recommendations) plus a globetrotting chef who grew up eating at Michelin-starred restaurants have taken over this family-run inn: just the ticket in the middle of this rural village. This pair promises diners a delightful dining experience that combines rustic surroundings and cuisine that nonchalantly switches between regional and more contemporary dishes, and is littered with nods to the chef's many travels: here you see vin jaune and saffron from Franche-Comté, peanut vinaigrette, seaweed emulsion alongside Thai-style mussels from Bouchot.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3335587094	Amicis	19 rue Mably	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.restaurant-amicis.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€€	t	t	In the chic part of Bordeaux, between the Allées de Tourny and the Place des Grands-Hommes, chef Alexandre Baumard (previously at Logis de la Cadène in Saint-Émilion and L'Observatoire du Gabriel) has set up this elegant two-storey restaurant. Served in the form of a tasting menu (at dinnertime only), the refined and clear cuisine showcases quality ingredients – not least fish and seafood – that are precisely and creatively prepared, eg delicately cooked prawn placed on a flavoursome reduction of the heads and dressed with a shell bisque vinaigrette. Damien Amilien's desserts, as delicious as they are technical, continue in this subtle vein – with the likes of his cooked and raw cherries with fresh herbs. The food goes into a more accessible bistronomy mode at lunchtime. Attentive service and a terrific wine list.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3330422456	Cent33	133 rue du Jardin-Public	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://cent33.com/	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€€	f	t	A chic, cosy bistro atmosphere reigns in the restaurant of Grenoble-born chef Fabien Beaufour. He has worked in some of the finest Michelin-starred restaurants in France (eg Anne-Sophie Pic in Valence and Patrick Henriroux in Vienne), as well as in New York and London. So it's hardly surprising that his cooking is unconventional, globe-trotting and eco-responsible. Intense, contrasting flavours and spot-on cooking and seasonings. Signature dishes include delicious miso-glazed black cod slow-cooked on the robatayaki, warm octopus salad, Piedmont hazelnuts with salted butter caramel.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3334119925	Inima	48 rue du Palais-Gallien	France	Bordeaux	Wheelchair access	http://www.inimarestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€€	t	f	In her small restaurant that sports an uncluttered interior (formerly the Cromagnon), young Moldavian-born chef Oxana Cretu gives free rein to her culinary imagination in a surprise menu. This perfectionist rolls out colourful dishes packed with aromas: crayfish, bouchot mussels and roses or imperial prawns, sweetcorn and lavender. Her dessert of meringue with strawberries from the Lot, Namelaka cream, lemon marmalade and jasmine sorbet is an unqualified hit.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3330534941	Mets Mots	98 rue Fondaudège	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning	https://www.metsmots.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	t	What is this restaurant's recipe for success? A venue steeped in history (a former printworks), a trio of chefs who worked for Pierre Gagnaire and elegantly crafted market cuisine. Day after day, the regulars flock here, which is always a good sign. Full-bodied flavours and a friendly vibe set the scene at lunchtime for a slap-up meal^ in the evening, wine bar and a range of dishes to share.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3339715755	TLALI	6 rue du Cancera	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning	https://www.tlali.fr/	Nessun premio	Fusion, Mexican	4.0	€€	t	f	This Franco-Mexican establishment run by a native of Guadalajara, chef Kristian de Anda who was at the helm of the kitchen of the Parisian Biondi, is a delightful surprise. Only open in the evenings, his establishment masterfully proves that there is more to Mexican cuisine than tacos and enchiladas! In fact, the score is more fusion as pedigree Gallic recipes are dotted with intelligent Mexican notes – you won’t find a single tastebud-burning pepper in sight! We do however recommend ordering his array of tacos, in tribute to different regions of Mexico, as the ideal appetiser to kick off your meal in style.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3337166328	Lume	3 rue des Faussets	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.ristorantelume.fr/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€	t	t	A 14-seater restaurant with an intimate atmosphere that is due in part to the candlelight (lume in Italian). Venetian chef Riccardo Suppa regales guests with an appetising single set menu that gives pride of place to seafood and organic vegetables. Everything is made in-house, from the pasta to the bread prepared using heirloom wheat flour. Alice, the chef's partner, is an accomplished hostess who knows her way around a wine list featuring carefully selected Italian labels. On the menu: cicchetti (Venetian canapés), scallop crudo, paccheri with chanterelles, vanilla panna cotta etc.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3336218563	Ishikawa	22 rue du Hâ	France	Bordeaux	Terrace	https://restaurant-ishikawa.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€	f	t	In a busy pedestrian street in the city centre, chef Yugo Ishikawa has set up shop in this elongated, minimalist-style restaurant. He throws himself body and soul into his painstakingly crafted dishes from the traditional Japanese cuisine he so loves. On the daily specials board: tonkatsu shoulder of pork in breadcrumbs, tuna tataki with ponzu oroshi, tsukemono pickled vegetables. Simpler delicious options at lunchtime. You almost feel like you are in an izakaya in Tokyo. A hit.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3335200761	Kedem	16 rue Jean-Burguet	France	Bordeaux		https://www.kedem.fr/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Previously cohorts at Miles (now closed), Gil Elad and Ronan Cadoret strike again! In this small bistro complete with a counter, they serve up a veritable feast of small plates celebrating the flavours and spices of the Middle East. Their dishes make good use of the locally sourced produce at hand (Landes free-range chicken marinated in sumac with a spicy chicken jus^ shish barak stuffed with porcini and seasonal chanterelles). Other highlights include a wide variety of delicious house-baked breads (eg Yemeni kubaneh) and some excellent desserts, including a Lebanese turnover filled with a date and dried fruit mixture, accompanied by a tasty pistachio ice cream. The short wine list has a penchant for natural wines, in particular Mediterranean labels.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3335042059	Arcada	13 rue de la Rousselle	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.arcada-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Tucked away between Place Camille-Jullian and Saint-Michel, a contemporary vibe sets the scene in the vaulted dining room whose bistronomic menu is ingredient-centred: in fact, some 90% of the fruit and veg comes from small, local producers. At lunchtime, you might sample a deliciously priced tataki of marinated watermelon in soy and citrus fruit or confit of loin of hake baked in olive oil. The culinary score becomes more high-flying in the evenings as do the ingredients. The menu changes regularly. Outstanding warm welcome and service.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3338685697	Bo-tannique	2 rue Tustal	France	Bordeaux	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.bo-tannique.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	These attractive premises (with a contemporary interior and exposed Bordeaux stonework) are located on a charming cobbled pedestrian square. The fresh cuisine is full of contrasts and draws on influences from far and wide: grilled sardines with burnt miso and Lebanese-style tomato tabbouleh. The fine wine list features mostly organic and natural wines. Friendly service... A recipe for success!	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3337143360	C'Yusha	12 rue Ausone	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.cyusha.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Modern cuisine that makes full use of herbs and spices, created by a chef who works single - handedly in full view of the diners. Minimalist and intimately scaled (numbers are deliberately limited) in a resolutely contemporary setting.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3338090101	Epicentre	15 rue des Piliers-de-Tutelle	France	Bordeaux		https://epicentrebordeaux.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This eatery is located in a side street off the busy Rue Sainte Catherine. From his tiny kitchen at the rear of the dining room, which enables him to chat with customers, chef Benjamin Wavrant whips up a bargain-priced bistronomic lunchtime menu with a patriotic line-up of dishes, like potato soup followed by a slab of pollock seared in butter, flavoured in citrus fruit and underscored by a gutsy meaty gravy. More upmarket in the evening, premium ingredients such as foie gras, scallops and pigeon are crafted into a more gastro-leaning menu.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3334610392	Influences	36 rue Saint-Sernin	France	Bordeaux	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurant-influences.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	A wind of revival is blowing through this venerable institution, which has changed hands but not name and is still located in a quiet street near Place Gambetta. The handsome sandstone façade now ushers guests into the lair of a youthful couple, cheerful Kéveena, in the front of house and Ismaël who gives free rein to his solid background in the kitchen. Modern, tasty dishes which mainly star ingredients from southwest France, jazzed up with the odd creative twist, like a grilled duck magret, punchy gravy and Japanese-style lacquered aubergine sprinkled in puffed rice. Seamless, smiling service.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3337888818	Joki	33 rue des Bahutiers	France	Bordeaux		https://www.jokirestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In the heart of historic Bordeaux, this cosy, casual eatery dishes up deftly crafted bistronomic cuisine composed with carefully sourced produce: poached oysters, mousse of ham and samphire pickles^ pigeon marinated in oriental spices and a combo of turnips and harissa jus. Enticing cocktail-food pairings concocted by Jodie.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3333881687	La Fine Bouche	30 rue du Hâ	France	Bordeaux	Terrace	http://www.lafinebouche33.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	The chef's interest in regional traditions and his creative spirit are reflected in his use of the capuchin, an ancient utensil with a cast iron cone attached to a long rod, in which pieces of bacon are melted and used to flambée his scallops, lending them a slight grilled and smoked taste. With its hardwood floors, mouldings and exposed stonework, the tastefully refurbished dining room makes for an intimate dinner setting.	carlinikita	\N	\N
