3339396061	Auberge Larochette	110 route des Enceints	France	Bourgvilain	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.aubergelarochette.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This pleasant village inn serves hearty traditional cuisine, such as a fine Charolais entrecôte with gratin dauphinois, or crispy calf sweetbreads. In winter the fire crackles in the hearth^ in summer the shady terrace is the place to be. Attentive front-of-house staff.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3330471891	La Maison des Blés - Le Bouche à Oreille	19 rue du Périgord	France	Boutervilliers	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lamaisondesbles.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	A contemporary place with a modern interior, with two ears of wheat emblazoned on the walls in homage to the surrounding countryside, and two eateries where you can indulge yourself: Brasserie Louis (knuckle joint of lamb, seasonal vegetables etc) and the gourmet restaurant, Bouche à Oreille. Professionalism and dishes that showcase top-notch ingredients every time.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3331992569	La Côte Bleue	Avenue Louis-Tudesq	France	Bouzigues	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.la-cote-bleue.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€	f	t	The Étang de Thau, a major shellfish farming site and lake in Languedoc, famous for its mussels and the legendary oysters of Bouzigues, is also well-known for its biodiversity on land, in the sea and in the airs. So, taking a seat on the terrace overlooking the lagoon is an opportunity not to be missed. Expect to tuck into delicious, ultra-fresh seafood, including oysters, mini squid in garlic and parsley or mussels broiled in garlic butter.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3331318118	La Route d'Argent	1 route de Gabriac	France	Bozouls	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.laroutedargent.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	On the ground floor of the hotel, this restaurant, which sports a bright, modern interior, has been taken over by a dynamic duo comprised of the former second and his wife. Tuck into heartwarming, bountiful fare made with regional produce: Aubrac beef and trout, persillade of lamb sweetbreads or squab breast. Traditional aligot (mashed potatoes and cheese) is served with the main course.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3335179044	Charbonnel	57 rue Gambetta	France	Brantôme	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelrestaurantcharbonnel.com/	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€	f	f	This emblematic inn stands in the heart of the picturesque village of Brantôme. Enticing seasonal cuisine made from painstakingly sourced produce and scattered with Asian notes is served in a cosily comfortable dining room, which leads onto an enchanting terrace overlooking the River Dronne.	monticristian	\N	\N
3337831031	Auberge de Bel Air	1 Moulin de Bel-Air	France	Brélès	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaubergedebelair.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This granite-built farmhouse on the banks of the Aber Ildut cuts a picturesque figure with its large garden and lake. On the menu: the fish and seafood cuisine for which Brittany is so famed, eg fillet of pollack with lobster cream. A rustic setting in which to really unwind.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3332757940	Auberge du Château	67 montée du Château	France	Bressieux	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.aubergedebressieux.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Christèle and Xavier Vanheule are passionate about food and wine, and put their all into making this Auberge a wonderful establishment. The produce they source from surrounding farms is bursting with freshness. While contemplating the peaks of the Monts du Lyonnais, you can enjoy dishes with robust flavours, including filet of Dombes duckling, split pea purée, grilled pork belly etc.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3339339136	Hinoki	6 rue des 11-Martyrs	France	Brest	Counter dining	https://hinoki-sushi.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Sushi	4.0	€€€€	f	f	A real Japanese restaurant in Brest! Hinoki is run by a Breton chef who is deeply passionate about Japanese cuisine. Locally caught fish are selected with minute attention to detail. A word to the wise: opt for a place at the counter (ten covers) for an experience that goes beyond mere dining, as the chef creates his sushi and maki in full view of diners seated here. You will definitely feel a sense of privilege!	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3330603267	Le M	22 rue du Commandant-Drogou	France	Brest	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-lem.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Plenty of originality in the design of the dishes and the marriages of flavours in this typically Breton granite house done out with a contemporary decor. Tuck into modern cuisine that sources its ingredients (fish, poultry, vegetables etc) from local producers. In summer, dine alfresco on the pleasant terrace.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3333610077	L'Attilio - Château de Noirieux	Château de Noirieux	France	Briollay	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://chateaudenoirieux.com/fr/restaurant	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	This handsome little 17C château and charming 15C manor house are set in grounds on the banks of the River Loir. The restaurant has an elegant interior refurbished in a contemporary style, in a palette of light tones, and a pleasant terrace overlooking the valley. Italian chef Attilio Marrazzo chooses quality ingredients – including produce grown in his own vegetable garden – for his modern cuisine. His dishes (free-range poultry, fricassee of chanterelles with parsley, Caesar-style salad) show a good command of culinary techniques, and can be washed down with a wine from a list that focuses on regional tipples.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3339493307	Moon	27 avenue Pasteur	France	Brive-la-Gaillarde	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantmoon.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€	f	f	In this country house that is typical of the area, chef Nicolas Laval, himself a local man (from Corrèze), has opted for a pared-back contemporary interior decor in a palette of light wood, blue and white, in a nod to the maritime world he so loves. Examples of his dishes include shredded beef cheek, parsnip mousseline, red wine reduction, tarragon^ line-caught hake, cauliflower, orange gremolata, grapefruit, citrus vinaigrette. It's pretty creative cuisine, always skilfully executed and the chef's attention to every little detail hits the spot with diners!	farinalucas	\N	\N
3339674333	Chez Francis	61 avenue de Paris	France	Brive-la-Gaillarde	Air conditioning	https://www.chezfrancis.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Chez Francis has the perfect family - run bistro atmosphere with its old - fashioned poster adverts, all manner of bric - a - brac and messages left by clients. You come here as a friend and are made to feel at ease as you sample the quality ingredients woven into lovely recipes: crab remoulade, Jerusalem artichoke and green apple, wok sautéed squid served with Languedoc wines!	brunojulian	\N	\N
3338496552	La Table d'Éole	9 place Jolyot-de-Crébillon	France	Brochon	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://la-table-deole.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Sylvain Gauthier (formerly of La Maison des Cariatides in Dijon) and Valentine have set up shop in a beautiful traditional stone house in the heart of this Burgundy wine-growing village. Instead of a set menu, there is a short à la carte menu of dishes the names of which alone are mouthwatering. The chef's expertise shines through in every course with consistently winning flavour combinations (scallops, cauliflower mousseline, green apple and hazelnut sauce vierge, hint of ginger). The sweet finale hits a perfectly seasonal note with a dessert starring pear. The dining area comprises two distinct spaces: the first is contemporary, with grey tones and a glass-walled kitchen^ the second, warmer and more traditional, is laid out beneath a stone vaulted ceiling.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3335300499	Récolte	2 rue Gaudrine	France	Bruz	Wheelchair access	http://restaurant-recolte.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Take a seasoned, well-travelled chef (Le Chabichou, Le Saturne), source fresh seasonal ingredients for your bistronomy-style dishes – and there you have it. On this occasion, lunch consisted of creamy lentil soup and poultry giblets^ perfectly cooked red mullet, mushroom cream and flavourful root vegetables^ pavlova (crunchy on the outside, soft and pillowy on the inside) and a Timut pepper cream with a pronounced citrus flavour. To be relished in the cosy dining area done out in an understated vein (wood-effect tiled floor, white walls) with an open kitchen.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3331977317	L'Intimiste - Auberge de Buellas	10 route de Buesle	France	Buellas	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.auberge-buellas.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of Buellas village, take a seat in the snug, plush dining room to sample polished, thoughtfully curated dishes presented in a single set menu that shines the spotlight on a seasonal ingredient: lobster, Bresse poultry, celery, etc. The Auberge Bressane de Buellas is more traditional in style.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3337141349	Pérégrinations	1 rue Victor-Hugo	France	Buzançais	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-peregrinations.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	At an age when some might be hanging up their aprons, chef Franck Gatefin continues as the driving force behind his establishment in Buzançais, not far from the Brenne Regional Nature Park. He is extremely particular when it comes to choosing his ingredients: he sources live freshwater fish, which he slaughters himself using the ikejime method, and relies on his regular gardener for organic vegetables^ this botany enthusiast also grows over 150 aromatic herbs on his patio. Fish and vegetables obviously take pride of place in his beautifully presented dishes, which are testament to his commitment: oyster tartare and grapefruit sorbet^ scallops, celeriac purée and a jus made with the scallop mantle and garden herbs. Cordial, attentive welcome and service in a contemporary interior.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3333179670	Le Balbec - Grand Hôtel de Cabourg	Grand Hôtel de Cabourg	France	Cabourg	Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.grand-hotel-cabourg.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	The Grand Hôtel de Cabourg, once frequented by Marcel Proust, is one of the best-preserved seaside hotels from the Belle Époque and a gem of Art Deco architecture. Le Balbec – one of the hotel's restaurants – is located in the gallery, which overlooks the seafront, and where serving precise, refined dishes with an abundance of beautiful flavours is a matter of pride. For food lovers in search of lost time!	huberflorin	\N	\N
3336055817	Symbiose	7 avenue Jean-Mermoz	France	Cabourg	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.symbiose-cabourg.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	The name of this restaurant may refer to the close bond between the chef and the sommelière (who are partners in life), or the association of food and wine – the couple’s respective passions, or to the two set menus served in two separate dining spaces. The first is a “tasting bar”, which rolls out dishes to share that tap into influences from far and wide (ceviche of croaker, ceviche juice and guacamole)^ the second is dedicated to fine dining with two tasting menus (and a third more concise score at lunchtime). The chef, who finds his inspiration in Normandy’s first-class fare and culinary heritage, draws on his years of experience in top flight restaurants to create modern cuisine with just the right touch of creativity. We recommend his new spin on the tarte Tatin with a calvados soufflé.	pingliu	\N	\N
3333579211	Le Baligan	8 avenue Alfred-Piat	France	Cabourg	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://lebaligan.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	t	t	Fishing rods, lithographs, and frescoes set the maritime scene in this bistro. Flawlessly fresh fish from the local fish auction and knockout seafood platters (oysters and scallops) take the limelight on the table. The fish of the day, in our case sole and turbot, is sold by the kilogramme – to the delight of our appetites and wallets!	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3334557039	AGA	7 rue Porte-de-la-Mer	France	Cadillac	Air conditioning	https://restaurant-aga.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Alexandre Goniak and Gerie Jenner met in Australia but opened their first venture in a small country town on the banks of the Garonne just two minutes from a medieval gateway. The contemporary bistro menu illustrates the chef’s spot-on craftsmanship and flair for devising intelligent recipes based on seasonal availability, illustrated by loin of pork with Paimpol cranberry beans, bacon cream, fluffy mashed potato and roast cauliflower. Casual, smiling welcome and a genuine desire to share and inform, in particular regarding the wines.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3333427186	Augia	18 rue Porte-au-Berger	France	Caen	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.augia.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of Le Vaugueux, an area of Caen beloved of tourists, a stone's throw from the castle, this restaurant takes the Latin name of the Pays d'Auge, birthplace of chef Grégoire James. The interior elegantly blends old-world charm – exposed beams, half-timbering and Caen stone – with refined contemporary furnishings. The modern cuisine takes the form of a concise menu, featuring local producers and organic ingredients (pea tartlet, goat's cheese, fresh herbs^ Bayeux pork, sautéed potatoes, grilled courgettes, reduced jus). In fine weather, the patio terrace to the rear of the restaurant makes for a peaceful setting.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3330509260	Le Dauphin	29 rue Gémare	France	Caen		https://www.le-dauphin-normandie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	This place is just the ticket for fans of Normandy's specialities: oysters from the bay of Isigny - sur - Mer, Swiss Normandy pigeon, and Vire andouille sausage. The onus is on ingredients from the region but the chef also knows how to compose more original recipes. Elegant and bright decor.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3330011015	Magma	24 rue Saint-Manvieu	France	Caen		http://magma-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This town house, outside the centre of Caen, is almost on the doorstep of the Abbaye-aux-Hommes. Olivier Barbarin, an experienced chef who is no stranger to fine dining, concocts food that resembles his character – uninhibited and appetising, including a nod to his native Auvergne – the purple walls evoke volcanic rock like pozzolan. Bargain priced lunch deal, and the dinner tasting menu changes depending on the market and the chef’s mood.	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3336161973	Séquence	6 rue du 11-Novembre	France	Caen	Wheelchair access	https://www.sequence-restaurant-gastronomique.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Chef Antoine Triquet may have an unusual career path (which led him from insurance to cooking), but the culinary fundamentals are present and correct! Ingredients are carefully selected to put the spotlight on local producers, nature and the seasons, and the cooking is always on point... This is modern, clear and uncluttered cuisine with a sincere, even generous approach! At dinnertime, the set menu is divided into three sequences, each featuring a given ingredient prepared in three different ways, which allows them to use the ingredient in its entirety. For example, veal: veal croquette, vitello sardinia, or standing rump served medium rare, accompanied by an onion purée and a delicious gravy. To be enjoyed in a contemporary decor with an open kitchen.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3334176090	Restaurant du Musée	2 rue de la Rochette	France	Fréland	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantmusee.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	In this former mill on the Ure, next to the museum of the Welche country, Alain Schmitt’s cooking finds varied inspiration, close to home in “terroir” dishes (fleischschnaka of local trout) and further afield (line-caught grouper in a yosenabe style dashi broth).	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3338449812	Stéphane Carbone	14 rue de Courtonne	France	Caen	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.stephanecarbone.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Just a stone's throw from the marina, in the bustling hub of Caen life, chef Stéphane Carbone explores France's terroirs, from Normandy and the Lyonnais to Bresse (where he grew up and learned to cook) to his parents' and grandparents' native Calabria. Using the freshest ingredients, he serves modern cuisine with a dash of creativity, proceeding according to the mood on any given day. Signature dishes are available à la carte, including the heart sweetbread cooked in a sauté pan or the Caribbean chocolate shell with a hot chocolate velouté… To be enjoyed in the contemporary dining area, from which you can watch the activity in the kitchen from behind a large picture window. A lobster set menu and cookery class every Saturday morning.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3331300882	Le Bouchon du Vaugueux	12 rue Graindorge	France	Caen		https://www.bouchonduvaugueux.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Behind a simple exterior is this bistro with the soul of a true bouchon lyonnais (counter, cheek - to - jowl dining). That said, the chef does not limit himself to tradition and adorns his dishes with more modern ideas. Nice selection of wines from producers.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
