3331663166	Comte Roger	14 rue Saint-Louis	France	Carcassonne	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.comteroger.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant within the medieval city walls has a sleek contemporary design and tables set up on a lovely airy patio – Comte Roger knows how to welcome guests! Cassoulet (the house speciality) is of course given pride of place, along with seasonal and regional ingredients (asparagus and local lamb, Lauragais lentils, Belpech poultry etc), which are prepared with a keen sense of precision.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3336278790	Monique	1 ter impasse du Charron	France	Calvisson	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.monique-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Julien Caligo, previously co-executive chef at Duende (Nîmes), has returned to his natural environment – namely his native Vaunage, a plain surrounded by hills, between Nîmes and Montpellier. The premises, originally a farm building, now accommodate this beautiful interior with white walls, exposed stonework and refined light wood furniture – perfect for a restaurant that is a homage to the chef's grandmother, who taught him the fundamentals of cooking. The carte blanche menu is a masterclass in technical skill, a shining example of which is the daring fusion of calf intestine and red mullet, while the Baron des Cévennes pork is showcased by a spicy black pudding sauce. The culinary innovation at work here is propelled by the finest local ingredients, fresh from the land (or sea).	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3332591204	Ama	6 allée Anne-de-Neubourg	France	Cambo-les-Bains	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://restaurant-ama.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	An amiable name for a restaurant where love is in the air! The restaurant is run by two chefs: Manon Grasset from Marseille and Adrien Layssac from Albi, a couple who met while working at La Bastide de Moustiers, an Alain Ducasse restaurant. Ten years ago, they moved to the Basque Country, whose terroir inspires their seasonal market cuisine, which they cook together. Dishes made with local produce are bursting with colour: cabbage medley, egg yolk confit in olive oil, pecan nuts^ local lamb, asparagus, watercress, bagna cauda^ salad of citrus fruit supremes, heather honey, granola. The bistro-style decor has exposed white beams and a blue wall for a pop of colour.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3336372162	Le Bellevue	29 rue des Terrasses	France	Cambo-les-Bains	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-bellevue64.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The interior is light, and the menu is short. Two reasons to linger in this tastefully decorated restaurant. Traditional cuisine is revisited with enthusiasm and a keen sense of the pleasure of food. Try off - the - bone pig's trotter terrine or, for dessert, the hot soufflé with pear brandy.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3336603235	Terrae	7 avenue de la Mairie	France	Cambo-les-Bains		https://restaurant-terrae.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Grégory Ménard and Lucile Voisin (Choko-Ona and Grand Hôtel de Saint-Jean-de Luz) have converted this former fishmongers into a cosily dinky restaurant steeped in stylish appeal. The tasteful interior sports warm terracotta walls, linen-coloured banquette seating, pale wood tables and fine tableware: hand-crafted Basque silverware, cutlery and ceramics. The menu is inspired by the availability of fresh local produce and the chef’s boundless creativity. Pyrenean trout, marbled in squid ink and beetroot pickles^ Kintoa pork and Iberic pancetta, medley of artichokes: flavour, colour, hard work and a dash of creativity.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3339551924	Le Bout du Quai	Route de la Corniche	France	Cancale	Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.leboutduquai.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Aptly located at the end of the quayside (hence the name), the fashionable slate grey glazed front of this restaurant overlooks the Atlantic and Mont St Michel. Chef Romain Roland, after a stint at a star restaurant in Corsica, crafts ambitious, creative cuisine, dotted with subtle Mediterranean notes.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3337411173	L'Ormeau	4 quai Thomas	France	Cancale	Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-cancale.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	f	t	Who could turn down a platter of Cancale oysters, scallops and abalone (the restaurant’s namesake)? Even better when served with a splendid view of the fleet of fishing boats that guarantees their freshness! A stylish interior fronted by a pleasant terrace sets the scene for premium seafood dishes, such as razor clams stuffed with parsley, garlic and butter, home-made fish soup or local scallops roasted on the shell, white butter and vegetable risotto. Round off your meal on a sweet note with a pancaked stuffed with warm apples for example.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3336703862	Le Bistrot de Cancale	à Port-Mer	France	Cancale	Great view,Terrace	http://www.maisons-de-bricourt.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	t	t	Run by Hugo Roellinger, this restaurant is located opposite the beach at Port-Mer with its small boats bobbing at anchor and Mont-Saint-Michel visible in the distance. The menu features dishes such as oysters, shellfish, langoustines, sole with a caramelised jus, turbot cooked on the bone, lobster cooked over hot coals – excellent fish, distinguished by its remarkable freshness and often seasoned with Olivier Roellinger's famous spice mixes. There is a beautiful terrace with a sea view and, inside, knick-knacks related to Brittany and fishing create a chic and modernised seaside bistro vibe that is enhanced by a 1930s fresco depicting a scene from life in the port of Saint-Malo.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3335676112	Côté Mer	4 rue Ernest-Lamort	France	Cancale	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-cotemer.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Inhale the salty sea air of the little port of Cancale, which makes for a picturesque sight with its fishermen's houses. In this restaurant overlooking the bay, you can sample cuisine that showcases first and foremost local coastal produce, but not to the exclusion of other ingredients: scallops, oysters, saltmarsh lamb, lobster, abalones… And all at eater-friendly prices.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3335842330	La Table de la Caillère	36 route des Montils	France	Candé-sur-Beuvron	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.auberge-de-la-caillere.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Idyllically located for anyone touring the châteaux of the Loire, this inn, firmly in the zeitgeist, is run by an enterprising couple who work together in a bucolic setting of forests and meadows. The original 18C farmhouse has been replaced by a modern building, which reflects the chef's culinary ethos that favours local produce (girolle mushrooms, regional veggies, honey, Racan pigeon, Touraine pork, etc.), but also his homeland, Brittany, illustrated by a wafer-thin tart of spider crab covered in a warm mayonnaise flavoured with sea urchin roe. Each legible dish is a masterclass of exquisite plating and crisp forthright flavours.	costasergio	\N	\N
3330805630	Le Bistrot de la Caillère	36 route des Montils	France	Candé-sur-Beuvron	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.auberge-de-la-caillere.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€	f	f	Ideally located for anyone visiting the châteaux of the Loire, this inn is firmly rooted in its era. It is run by an enterprising couple, who work and live in harmony with the bucolic landscape of forests and meadows. The original 18C farmhouse has been replaced by a modern building – modern like chef Éric Rialland's cuisine. His well-thought-out bistronomy dishes follow the seasons and oscillate between creativity and tradition. Pleasant terrace for fine weather.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3338292482	Riviera	Carlton Cannes	France	Cannes	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.carltoncannes.com/eat-drink/riviera-restaurant	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	t	The legendary luxury hotel, which celebrated its 110th anniversary in 2023, now has its own marble-clad restaurant with a superb terrace overlooking the Croisette. In an opulent-feeling dining room where white meets black, the tables set with Gien porcelain are in line with time-honoured tradition of French table arts. The chef's table opposite the open kitchen also draws the eye. Everything else meets the standard set by your surroundings: Mediterranean cuisine made from top-quality local and seasonal ingredients, the calibre of service, with meat and fish cut at your table. You'll enjoy an excellent rack of Alpilles lamb with vegetables and jus, and a remarkable St Honoré cake with vanilla caramel and walnut pieces.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3338732107	La Palme d'Or	73 boulevard de la Croisette	France	Cannes	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.lapalmedor-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	The restaurant of the emblematic Hôtel Martinez, luxurious realm of the stars during the Cannes Film Festival, is a vibrant tribute to cinema, one of chef Jean Imbert's passions. With wood panelling that wouldn't be out of place on a yacht in the golden age of Hollywood, the decor is overflowing with authentic film props and posters. The menu is written like a screenplay, illustrated with storyboards. The sea and Provence are the two stars of the show here – they provide ingredients that feature in dishes that never fail to pique the interest: wild gamberoni from the Gulf of Genoa, mango and kumquat sauce vierge^ barbecued and glazed John Dory, rocket pesto, shellfish cooked in a sealed casserole pot and local vegetables^ vanilla palmier made to order. Lights, camera, action!	vargalucia	\N	\N
3336548522	L'Affable	5 rue La Fontaine	France	Cannes	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-laffable.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	In the centre of Cannes, this contemporary bistro is always busy and, indeed, it has much to recommend it. First and foremost its menu: courgette flower fritters, cod aioli, rack of lamb roasted with thyme… and the classic Grand Marnier soufflé, the house speciality.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3330720197	La Table du Chef	5 rue Jean-Daumas	France	Cannes	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.latableduchefcannes.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Only open in the evenings, this small bistro just two minutes from Rue d’Antibes never disappoints. In an open kitchen, a youthful chef works with local, seasonal produce, crafting subtle, tasty dishes, such as his knockout velvety carrot soup with star anise and lightly seared shrimp. Market availability dictates the contents of the “Surprise” menu which is great value for money… Booking recommended.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
