3337246105	Le Grand Chaume	Route de Queneau	France	Chaumont-sur-Loire	Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://leboisdeschambres.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Architects Patrick Bouchain and Loïc Julienne designed this unique venue with a traditional thatched roof and an exposed timber frame that calls to mind a star-studded night sky. The pared-back, minimalist interior seems to be open to the elements, courtesy of floor-to-ceiling windows, some of which command a view of the small terrace and its water feature. The entire project is truly jaw dropping! The seasonal menu stars produce from the Val de Loire region.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3331109007	Maison Grandclaude	37 rue d'Épinal	France	Chaumousey	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.maison-grandclaude.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Set in a handsome bourgeois house, fashionably done up in a contemporary vibe with untreated materials such as oak, this inviting venue, a ten-minute drive from Epinal, is the brainchild of Nicolas Grandclaude and his wife. The modern, soul-warming culinary slant, backed up by exquisite plating, is illustrated in the likes of butterflied and seared wild prawns with coconut milk, ginger and lemongrass, or pan-fried whiting filets with courgettes, almonds and basil. Delightful.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3330178502	La Côte des Monts Damnés	Place de l'Orme	France	Chavignol	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-restaurant-chavignol.fr/fr/famille-bourgeois-sancerre-france/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Developed entirely around the wines of this family-owned estate, the bistronomic menu is flanked by some of the house signature dishes: tagliatelle with Chavignol goat's cheese, hot soufflé… Damnably delicious! Comfortable rooms for longer stays.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3337239201	Le Castellane - Château Le Prieuré	Route du Comte-de-Castellane	France	Chênehutte-Trèves-Cunault	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.prieure.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Le Castellane, part of the Château du Prieuré, serves modern fare that keeps tabs on the seasons and is predominantly local. You can choose between the Empire-inspired dining room or the terrace overlooking the Loire. Each of the guestrooms is individually appointed and fully in keeping with the historic character of the valley of kings.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3330297599	Le Coq d'Or	7 place du Champ-de-Foire	France	Chénérailles	Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-coqdor-23.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	‘The Golden Cockerel’ is aptly named: the interior is full of the birds – brought back by customers from their travels! As for the food, expect an array of fine, well - crafted dishes that offer a creative take on local specialities.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3337475396	Auberge du Bon Laboureur	6 rue du Docteur-Bretonneau	France	Chenonceaux	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.bonlaboureur.com/fr/hotel-chenonceaux	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Housed in a converted coaching inn built in 1786, this 100-year-old family-run restaurant sticks to the well-trodden path of cooking with a focus on seasonal ingredients. Chef Antoine Jeudi, now assisted by Julien Perrodin, certainly knows his stuff, and his flavoursome dishes go down a treat with your choice from an appealing wine selection. Thanks to the small kitchen garden, there is also a vegetable-forward set menu that includes, most notably, tomato stuffed with Touraine vegetables, fresh herb coulis and chickpea cream. Along with a charming setting, it all makes for a pleasant meal.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3332694204	Le Patio	5 rue Christine	France	Cherbourg-en-Cotentin	Terrace	https://www.restaurant-lepatio-cherbourg.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	f	At this town-centre restaurant, discover the cuisine of Gildas Gautier, a chef who is passionate about premium ingredients. Stuffed cabbage with beef shank, porcini, yuzu and oyster mushroom broth^ wild sea bass, spinach and cauliflower^ crêpe Suzette ravioli with salted butter caramel: tempting traditional recipes prepared in time-honoured tradition, with regularly changing options on the blackboard. In fine weather, dine on the small patio.	popafarah	\N	\N
3331641537	Le Vallon de Chérisy	12 route de Paris	France	Cherisy	Car park,Terrace	https://www.le-vallon-de-cherisy.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The name is a passing nod to an ode composed by Victor Hugo in this very inn back in 1821. The food has remained voluntarily rustic and hearty and faithfully keeps pace with the seasons, in particular the veggies and aromatic herbs. Save room for the wickedly decadent house dessert: a hot vanilla and butterscotch soufflé – to die for!	landirobert	\N	\N
3334051337	La Table - Maison Lobies	2 rue Porte-d'en-Haut	France	Chevannes		http://www.latable-lobies.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In the middle of the village, with the church on one side and fields on the other, this beautiful 18C manor house with a courtyard to the front has a refined, classical decor. The premises are both home and place of work for an enthusiastic, smiling couple with experience in some of the world's top restaurants. Sun Young, a pastry chef who hails from South Korea, and chef Jérémie work together to devise an appealing, delicious and rather traditional menu: super-soft poultry with crispy skin and an excellent, generous fricassee of chanterelle mushrooms, and a buttery potato purée^ beef chuck confit in its jelly sprinkled with hazelnut and boosted by a real mustard and shallot sauce! As for the desserts (floating island, Tahitian vanilla crème anglaise or raspberry cheesecake), it's as simple as this: they're all mouth-wateringly good.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3337681608	L'Auberge - Les Sources de Cheverny	23 route de Fougère	France	Cheverny	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.sources-cheverny.com/restaurant-cheverny/auberge-restaurant-cheverny/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Set in sprawling wooded grounds, the chic bistro of the hotel Les Sources de Cheverny serves fine and meticulous seasonal dishes that constitute something of a whistle-stop tour of the Loire Valley, as well as a tribute to local producers: vegetables from a market gardener in Mont-Près-Chambord, Sologne strawberries, Roi Rose pork loin from Touraine roasted in the fireplace… which takes pride of place in the dining area: here, cooking over a wood fire is a speciality!	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3335571749	Le Clos de Chevreuse	33 rue de Rambouillet	France	Chevreuse	Terrace	https://www.leclosdechevreuse.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	There's no doubt about it: chef Laurent Gasnier, whose CV speaks volumes (stints at Le Bristol, George V and with the Troisgros), knows how to choose good, mature ingredients, both vegetables and fish. He transforms them into generous dishes, impeccably cooked and seasoned, such as the courgette ball, organic Brousse cheese and basil pistou, or indeed the sea bass, coconut, young broad beans and a butter sauce. In summer, you'll want to sit out on the charming flower-decked terrace in the quiet courtyard. The restaurant is located in the pretty village of Chevreuse – all the more reason to make the trip.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3330584968	Couvert de Vignes	4 place Pommery	France	Chigny-les-Roses	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.benjamingillescuisine.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	The village of Chigny-les-Roses in the heart of the Montagne de Reims is the site of this restaurant in a former classroom, which is, indeed, entirely hemmed in by vineyards. Chef Benjamin Gilles can be seen in the kitchen through a window in the dining room. Now his own boss, he signs modern dishes overflowing in fresh flavours and enhanced by a zest of creativity. Vegetables and fruit feature prominently in his culinary score through a variety of preparations (raw, cooked, pickled).	monticristian	\N	\N
3338144990	Le Lancelot	12 rue des Déportés	France	Chilleurs-aux-Bois	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantlelancelot.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In the centre of the village, this welcoming flower-decked place with a garden and terrace is a real oasis of calm. Cosy setting and cuisine that navigates between tradition and modernity (notably the melt-in-the-mouth pithivier pie, rum crème brûlée, pistachio ice cream), not forgetting Sologne game in season.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3338035862	Les Années 30	73 rue Haute Saint-Maurice	France	Chinon	Terrace	http://www.lesannees-30.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant may be named after the 1930s but that's where the connection to that period ends. The decor is chic and trendy, with walls in hues of terracotta and verdigris and retro dining chairs. Diners will love the appetising cuisine based on fresh ingredients. Tables on the terrace in fine weather.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3334057445	L'Océanic	13 rue Rabelais	France	Chinon	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://loceanic-chinon.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	f	f	The ocean breeze blows as far inland as Chinon! As its name suggests, this restaurant gives seafood pride of place. The chef prepares very fresh fish, adding a dash of originality, with a pinch of spice here and a hint of sweet and sour there. Good value for money.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
3332453527	La Grange	64 rue de Saint-Antoine	France	Cholet	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lagrangecholet.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Wood sets the scene, including in the imposing feeding trough - this isolated old farmstead is proud of its rural vibe. A few modern details do however contrast with the initial portrait, starting with stylised photos, a glazed wine cellar and the smoked black glass service area. In the same vein, Christian Gingreau rolls out a modern score founded on tradition. The menu is concise and enticing: beef tartare, 30-day aged on the bone rib of beef, whole sole meunière, wild seabass and a new take on paella.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3339111108	La P’tite Patte	17 avenue de Nantes	France	Cholet	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.maisonpattenoire.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Located in the same handsome bourgeois edifice as its parent establishment, La Patte Noire, its vintage-inspired sibling, La P’tite Patte bistro, occupies the ground-floor^ both are run by Adrien Roux and Marie Doinel. Top-drawer produce sets the scene in the unfussy, enticing score. Examples range from melt-in-the-mouth veal and poultry liver pâté served with a shallot chutney, or parillada of pork, medium rare inside and nice and crispy outside served with crunchy fries cooked in beef tallow. Wholesome and hunger obliterating – what’s not to like?	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3335184668	Le Patte Noire	17 avenue de Nantes	France	Cholet	Car park,Garden or park	http://www.maisonpattenoire.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Presiding over its grounds, this charming 19C château houses a lovely restaurant on the first floor. Done out with carpeting, beige walls, colourful wallpaper, mouldings, mirrors on the ceiling and a large fireplace, the space is modern and inviting. Chef Adrien Roux expertly selects top-quality seasonal ingredients for his set menus: trout roe, hand-dived scallops, lobster from Brittany and rabbit from the Vendée… And how could we forget the famous pata negra bellota, which not only gives the restaurant its name, but also lends an indulgent touch to a number of dishes. Generosity, colour and bold flavours characterise every dish prepared by this chef who means business.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3330734800	Ermitage de Corton	D974	France	Chorey-lès-Beaune	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.ermitagecorton.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	In this house set in vineyards opposite Corton “mountain”, the chef aims to shine the spotlight on local producers. His modern meticulous cuisine draws upon his classical training and features a traditional Gallic line-up, including snails and œufs en meurette (poached eggs in red wine) crafted with text-book precision. Stylish interior, inviting patio and spacious guestrooms to prolong your stay.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3332264259	Chez Mattin	63 rue Evariste-Baignol	France	Ciboure	Air conditioning	https://www.chezmattin.fr/	Nessun premio	Basque	5.0	€€	t	t	This building, characteristic of the local area, is delightfully rustic, with its wooden tables and exposed beams, and has a real family atmosphere. Basque specialities and market-based daily specials make for lively cuisine that never fails to surprise: txangurro (specialities based on spider crab meat), ttoro (fish soup), txipirones (baby squid). Fish takes pride of place and it is exceptionally good!	popovchloe	\N	\N
3332987819	La Table de Haute-Serre	Château de Haute-Serre	France	Cieurac	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hauteserre.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the wine storehouse of a château in the heart of the vineyards, this restaurant exudes the very particular charm of truly authentic places. Charcuterie rack, butcher's block, ham slicer and cases of wine herald a wonderful moment of gourmet delights, rounded off by wines from the estate. Rotisserie evening every Friday. Just delicious.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3332147498	Les Terrasses de Clairefontaine	1 rue de Rambouillet	France	Clairefontaine-en-Yvelines	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lesterrassesdeclairefontaine.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	In the heart of the Chevreuse Valley and Rambouillet forest, this restaurant on the edge of Clairefontaine pond serves heart - warming, up - to - date food, with a weakness for truffles and game (in season). Fine view of the pond (all year long).	szabosofia	\N	\N
3338897988	L'En-but	107 avenue de la République	France	Clermont-Ferrand	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lenbut.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	The set menus, which are modern and shine the spotlight on local ingredients from the Massif Central, of this restaurant inside the Marcel Michelin rugby stadium, are named after the game's terminology (forward pass, grand slam and backhand spin). Designed in the spirit of a contemporary brasserie, the dining area commands a breathtaking view over the stadium and, from the terrace, over the Puys mountains.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3331929360	Le Bistrot d'à Côté	16 rue des Minimes	France	Clermont-Ferrand	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-bistrotdacote.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Chef Valentin Chambonnière arrived in this pretty, contemporary bistro in a pedestrianised street just off Place de Jaude and near the church (Église St-Pierre-les-Minimes) in spring 2023. He serves up generous, contemporary cuisine based on savvily prepared seasonal ingredients. The creative and masterful menu is replete with tangy flavours: the Jerusalem artichoke – in gnocchi and crisps – topped with pan-fried guanciale pieces strikes a hearty note^ a dish of slow-cooked leg of lamb and shoulder of lamb candied with spices offers appealing culinary contrasts^ the citrus fruit and white chocolate duo on buckwheat biscuit lends a refreshing touch. Choose from a fine selection of cocktails and spirits. A warm welcome and efficient service.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3331568622	Mouffu	4 rue Ribeyre-Jaffeux	France	Clermont-Ferrand	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	After Le Saint Eutrope, here's a second convivial restaurant where diners come to feast on down-to-earth fare such as pâté en croûte, vol-au-vent or pork filet mignon with a mustard sauce – served with a good selection of natural wines. The chef-patron, the son of a baker, changed course to become a chef. His succinct menu with clear headings is a veritable ode to family and humble cuisine. The simple bistro decor is a touch vintage, with antiques and mismatched furniture. Friendly and festive atmosphere.	stepanekgrace	\N	\N
