3339664523	La Maison Haute	Place de l'Église	France	Crolles	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://la-maison-haute.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Veteran chef Thomas Chegaray (in Basque, the “maison haute” (upper house) is called an “etchegaray”), rustles up modern dishes based on seasonal produce presented in a concise menu. The food is fresh and colourful, with a focus on taste and texture: thick, juicy, tender, farm - reared pork chops, cooked on the bone. Terrace in fine weather and service with a smile.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3332133568	Auberge de la Vallée	14 rue Armand-Guillaumin	France	Crozant	Air conditioning	https://www.laubergedelavallee.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Locally reared meat (lamb, veal, beef), regional cheeses (mainly goat’s) and veggies from his large market garden… The chef is a fan of the region as you will taste. The delicious food is served in a pleasantly rustic interior. The epitome of a French country inn!	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3337405013	Le M des Avenières	Les Avenières	France	Cruseilles	Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.chateau-des-avenieres.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	On the banks of the Salève, this early 20C stately home set in over 150 acres of grounds, houses a welcoming hotel-restaurant. The period interior (wainscoting, stone fireplace, coffered ceiling, mirrors, chandeliers and old banquettes) provides the perfect foil to sample a modern lineup tinged with tradition, illustrated by veal cutlet served in a casserole dish and paired with garlicy gratin dauphinois. Other examples include conchiglie stuffed with goat’s cheese, walnuts and a hint of honey. A portion of the produce is sourced locally: cheese, honey, veggies, as are the wines, most of which are organic. Splendid sweeping view over the Alps that extends from Mont Blanc as far as Lake Annecy!	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3335607148	MatCha	Montée du Château-Vieux	France	Cucuron	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Everything is fresh and made from scratch: the veg comes from small, local growers and the meat and poultry is free range. An enticing menu tailored to modern appetites. Smiling service.	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3332572316	Cuq en Terrasses	8 chemin du Château	France	Cuq-Toulza	Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.cuqenterrasses.com/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	High up in the village, this charming 18C house is a haven of calm, boasting an unusual terraced garden that showcases the produce of the kitchen garden. It's a new departure for this restaurant run by two young professionals who have worked in MICHELIN-starred establishments in Toulouse, and who serve up cuisine that is essentially plant-based and finely executed: artichoke au gratin with aromatic herbs, chorizo emulsion^ river trout from Condax fish farm, almond stuffing. Take in the breathtaking view of the Lauragais plain and the Pyrenees from the veranda and terrace. There are charming guestrooms, should you wish to extend the experience in this tranquil setting.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3339963066	La Table du Château	1 Grande-Rue	France	Dampierre-en-Yvelines	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.latableduchateau.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, French	5.0	€€€	t	t	The lord of the manor, who now owns this beautiful 17C inn, has entrusted the kitchens to chef Élisabeth Passédat. She may have worked abroad for many years, but she hasn't forgotten her French classics – pan-fried foie gras, pâté en croûte with Houdan poultry, veal sweetbreads, tournedos Rossini-style Charolais beef. She puts a modern spin on these dishes, blending them with seasonal ingredients and drawing inspiration from France's terroirs. In this way, she comes up with creations such as monkfish and spaetzle, Normandy cider velouté, or ravioli with mushrooms, Morbier cheese and a vin jaune emulsion.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
