3332585455	Auberge de Vigny	Lieu-dit Vigny	France	Digoin	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.aubergedevigny.fr/www/site.php	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Up - to - the - minute cuisine served in a former classroom that is a treat for the eyes. The lady of the house is also an accomplished pastry chef. Lovely south - facing garden - terrace.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3338838736	Azerole	86 rue Berbisey	France	Dijon	Terrace	http://www.azerole-dijon.fr	Nessun premio	Fusion	4.0	€€	t	f	Originally from Northern China, Xin Gan, who happens to be married to the chef of Parapluie, runs this delightful French-Asian fusion place with a simple neo-bistro decor (stone walls, dark wood tables and chairs). Single-handed in the kitchen, the chef skilfully combines spices, tofu and kimchi with high-quality seasonal French ingredients, to compose dishes such as rack of pork, chimichurri, courgette cream and green curry, accompanied by a dash of creamy hummus and multi-coloured carrot ribbons tossed in an orange vinaigrette – delicious!	winternoemi	\N	\N
3334664867	L'Arôme	2 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau	France	Dijon	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurant-aromedijon.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This gourmet bolthole offers a taste of happiness. Chef Kadoguchi delivers well-executed and beautifully presented dishes, alternating between Japanese specialties (gyozas) and French recipes (pollack, Provençal sauce) or mixing the two, as he does in his excellent picanha with Asian sauce. Harmonious textures and flavours, spot-on cooking techniques, a fine selection of wines and a perfect welcome – what's not to like?	cervigaia	\N	\N
3330631755	L'Essentiel	12 rue Audra	France	Dijon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-lessentiel-dijon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	At this restaurant just outside the city's touristy centre, a young owner-chef concocts a seasonal menu, underscored by distinctive, harmonious flavours and exquisitely presented. Those pressed for time will opt for the appetising lunch set menu. Best enjoyed on the patio, which is in great demand in fine weather.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3331369300	Cassis	74 rue Joseph-Dufour	France	Mâcon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.cassisrestaurant-macon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This is a chef who has worked in some prestigious establishments and who serves meticulous, tasty, no-frills cuisine made from quality ingredients (meat from the Haute-Loire area, vegetables from a local market gardener). Be sure to try the memorable pâté en croûte or the Bresse chicken in a cream sauce. The lunch menu is great value^ in the evening a mystery menu is served.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3334584081	L'Un des Sens	3 rue Jeannin	France	Dijon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lundessens-dijon.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Near the antique dealers’ district, this restaurant serves scrumptious food, presented beautifully and rich in distinctive flavours, illustrated by a rack of Ségala veal, ravioles of green peas and pecorino cheese and spring onions. The vegetables and fruit come from the chef’s garden. Several-course surprise menu in the evening and simpler fare at lunchtime. Courtyard patio for alfresco dining.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3331441572	La Maison des Cariatides	28 rue Chaudronnerie	France	Dijon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.maisondescariatides.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Located in the antique dealers' quarter, this listed 17C edifice which boats 12 caryatids on the façade, is now in the hands of Vincent and Marie-Cécile Gomis, whose star-studded careers can be tasted in the beautifully presented food. A modern score with intelligent cosmopolitan accents, like gravlax of Crisenon trout, grilled avocado with jerk spices^ fricassée of snails and mussels marinière in vadouvan spices. A festival of northern flavours and cooking techniques illustrated by line-caught pollock and squid, courgette flowers and a paella-flavoured stock. Pleasant terrace to the rear.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3338143611	La Table des Climats	12 parvis de l'Unesco	France	Dijon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.latabledesclimats.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	Within the Cité Internationale de la Gastronomie et du Vin, this restaurant is just a few metres from the Chapelle des Climats et des Terroirs. The contemporary decor also highlights the building's historical features, such as the exposed stonework and beamed ceiling – a gorgeous setting that serves as a backdrop for cuisine that fetes produce from the region, with the odd surf 'n' turf dish featuring among the options: œuf meurette (egg in a red wine sauce) with a twist^ langoustines, ham terrine with parsley and ginger-steamed artichoke^ matured Charolais beef, red wine reduction and a carrot medley. Food and wine pairings are a serious matter here, with an impressive selection of wines by the glass (around 50). Reasonable prices.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3336542683	Saison	17 rue Lamonnoye	France	Dijon	Terrace	http://www.saison-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In Dijon's Antiquaires neighbourhood, this French-Italian restaurant welcomes diners in a pleasant space decorated in a palette of light colours. Milanese chef Riccardo Maiello, who trained in MICHELIN-starred establishments, is at the helm: he delights diners with modern cuisine that alternates French recipes with nods to local produce, such as a starter of slow-cooked egg, broad beans from nearby Arc-sur-Tille, shiitake, emulsion with garlic and farmhouse Cancoillotte cheese, and 100% Italian dishes, eg al dente paccheri alla carbonara, home-made pasta straight from Italy made with Pecorino and guanciale.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3334034454	Sublime	24 rue Bannelier	France	Dijon	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.sublimerestaurant.net	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	A stone’s throw from the covered market, the modern cuisine of Sicilian chef Giovanni Spataro encompasses carefully executed French dishes such as turbot, asparagus, aioli and lemongrass emulsion, and emblematic Italian specialities including his take on vitello tonnato. He sources excellent ingredients – Charolais beef, carnaroli rice, Sicilian prawns etc, which he prepares and presents with impeccable taste.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3335956600	Monique, boire et manger	33 rue Amiral-Roussin	France	Dijon	Terrace	https://www.moniqueboireetmanger.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	f	What would Monique, the grandmother of chef Clara Reydet, have made of this charming bistro where seasonal vegetables are the star attraction? Only positive things, for sure! Clara cooks without inhibitions, draws on various influences and wins everyone over with her lamb kefta, creamy raw red cabbage or garam masala roasted carrots, toum (Middle Eastern garlic sauce) and reduced carrot jus. This fusion cuisine with vegetarian leanings is to be enjoyed in the simple, spruce space with lots of wood. Small terrace on the pedestrianised street.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3333011962	Cave	29 rue Jeannin	France	Dijon		https://cave.restaurant	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Chef Angelo Ferrigno has opened this bistro across the street from his restaurant, CIBO. The compact space bedecked in light wood has a table d'hôte and two counters, one of which overlooks the kitchen^ along one wall, wine racks are stocked with a selection of organic and natural wines from small-scale producers. Here, the chef applies the same philosophy and works with the same local suppliers. This lunchtime, the single set menu (a terrific deal!) included tomatoes from Le Pré Velot organic market gardens, trout from Crisenon fish farm and a tart made with fruit grown by Nadine Valliot. The evening à la carte menu features plates that can, but don't have to, be shared: house-made cordon bleu^ courgette flower tempura^ beef tataki with ginger and spring onion vinaigrette.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3332723869	Colibri	14 rue de la Mittrie	France	Dinan	Terrace	https://colibri-dinan.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	In the heart of medieval Dinan, this modern bistro sports wood furnishings, oak parquet flooring, a fireplace and a view of the kitchen from the small dining room. Vibrant, often surf ‘n turf recipes set the culinary scene: scallops, pig’s ears and lemon confit^ sweetbread in an anchovy and Iranian dried lime butter^ bream in cardamon and yellow turnips…	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3337421736	Didier Méril	1 place du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Dinard	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-didier-meril.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	In a cosy, contemporary interior, enjoying lunch with a magnificent view over the bay of Le Prieuré promises to be a memorable experience. As they drink in the open sea, gourmets will appreciate the creative cuisine of chef-owner Didier Méril. His top-notch seasonal produce comes mainly from the market and local fisheries (Jerusalem artichokes showcased in a variety of textures and shellfish marinière^ mackerel, spaghetti squash and a fish head jus finished with butter^ pear tartlet with almond crisp, Tonka bean vanilla cream and pear sorbet). Good value for money at lunchtime.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3331840025	Highway4 (Hang Tre Street)	5 Hang Tre Street	Vietnam	Hanoi	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Vietnamese	4.0	₫	f	f	This Vietnamese tửu quán (tavern) has always been popular with the locals and tourists alike. Most diners take their time, enjoying the food and drink in good company. The inn serves Northern Vietnamese fare and we recommend the subtly flavoured appetisers, such as salads or spring rolls. The catfish spring roll is the tasty signature dish. The heart-warming main courses come in earthen pots. The deliciously tender oxtail stew with herbs is to die for!	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3337093409	Ombelle	7 boulevard du Président Wilson	France	Dinard	Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-ombelle.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Having worked for a number of top establishments, chef Alexandre Frin and his partner Ludivine La Rosa, who manages the restaurant floor, have set up shop in this attractive early-20C building, with red brick walls and picture windows with small panes and white frames. The chef composes a modern, open-minded and 100% seasonal menu that keeps things simple: just good ingredients (preferably with short supply chains) and herbs and aromatic flowers from their grandfather's vegetable garden. Seared melt-in-the-mouth hake^ the subtle perfume of sage and pineapple in the panna cotta: a delicious interlude.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3339165081	La Vallée	6 avenue George-V	France	Dinard	Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hoteldelavallee.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	With its large bay windows, the interior is pleasant, but it is outdone by the irresistible south-facing terrace just beyond the picturesque Bec de la Vallée dock. It's the perfect place to sample fine seafood (charred leeks, cockles from the bay with fresh herbs), as well as classics from Brittany's terroir, eg tranche de lard paysan du pays malouin (salted smoked bacon), far breton (traditional flan-style dessert).	popovchloe	\N	\N
3338484377	Ô Dissay	111 place Pierre-d'Amboise	France	Dissay	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://chateaudedissay.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	The Château de Dissay, a 15C stately home with an elegant and refined interior, serves modern, visually exciting cuisine, created by two young chefs, Henri Dupont and Stanislas Simonet. A trained pastry chef, Simonet has not lost his touch, as his work with blackberries in season amply illustrates. In autumn, the duo harness their talents to revealing the big-boned flavours of game. Pleasant terrace in the castle courtyard.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3334217562	La Table du Grand Large	2 avenue de l'Océan	France	Dolus-d'Oléron	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.le-grand-large.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Just a stone's throw from Rémigeasse beach, amidst dunes and unspoilt countryside, Le Grand Large Hotel overlooks the ocean below. The restaurant faces both the indoor swimming pool and the sea, which is perfect for sunset portraits in the evenings. The menu by David Boyer (Meilleur Ouvrier de France) exalts the region’s first-rate produce. The crab with roasted rice and glazed lovage, or the two-course Racan pigeon with a raspberry reduction, bear witness to the chef’s meticulous handiwork.	haascamilla	\N	\N
