3330348573	Le Petit Saint Thomas	25 rue de Lattre de Tassigny	France	La Garnache	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lepetitsaintthomas.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This endearing family-run restaurant is popular with a crowd of locals. The chef, at the helm for over twenty years, painstakingly rustles up French staples, albeit with a tasty new twist and the odd hint of exoticism (curry, sobrassada, nori, mafé, coconut).	guerravictor	\N	\N
3336540449	Le Petit Nor’Cat	16 rue du Docteur-Callegari	France	La Haye	Wheelchair access	http://www.lepetitnorcat.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Théo Hervy, from Cherbourg in Normandy, and Fanny Mandrau, an authentic Catalan from the Pyrénées-Orientales, have merged their regions – Nor(mandy) + Cat(alonia) – in the name of their shared passion for good food. The lunch set menu, which is simple but very well executed using quality ingredients from the region and surrounding area, is unbeatable value: cauliflower, herring^ whiting, mashed potatoes, vegetables and sorrel cream^ raspberry tartlet and strudel. It's not until the more ambitious dinner that the couple combine ingredients from Normandy and Catalonia. In this compact restaurant, the wine list is devoted exclusively to the Côte Vermeille – sun-drenched wines, perhaps all the better to keep at bay the mild, wet climate of the English Channel.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3334316785	Le Panoramique	1 village de l'Église	France	La Pernelle	Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.le-panoramique.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant, run by the same family since 1966, stands next to the village church on a hill overlooking the sea and the island of Tatihou. Initially a bar, then a crêperie, it is now an upmarket eatery that seeks to showcase produce from Normandy.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3339844408	Au Grès du Marché	19 rue du Château	France	La Petite-Pierre	Terrace	https://www.augresdumarche.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A warm welcome awaits you at this cosy restaurant in the old part of the village! The chef rustles up traditional cuisine made with seasonal ingredients and remarkably fresh meats, such as locally hunted venison, cooked in a stew at a low temperature and accompanied by ceps and spaetzle. He does also cook more contemporary dishes, such as duck tataki served with sauerkraut salad.	ferrettivladislav	\N	\N
3330273201	L'Astrolabe	35 rue Gambetta	France	La Rochelle	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lastrolabe.com	Nessun premio	Fusion	3.0	€€€	t	t	An astrolabe is a disc-shaped astronomical instrument that was used to calculate longitudes and latitudes, and this restaurant transports you from one country to another (from Finland to Guatemala) and from one cuisine to another. Each dish is depicted by a fusion of world culinary traditions, as is exemplified by the mohinga of line-caught whiting. A journey to be savoured in a bright, pleasant interior with a buzzy chic bistro vibe.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3330042318	Impressions	7 rue Saint-Michel	France	La Rochelle	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.restaurant-impressions.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	After 18 years at Le Saison near Rennes, David Etcheverry has moved to this restaurant in the centre of La Rochelle. It is a small place with a sleek modern loft design, where they serve refined, unfailingly delicious dishes. A real treat for the taste buds.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3334847385	La Yole de Chris	Plage de la Concurrence	France	La Rochelle	Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://christophercoutanceau.com/fr/la-yole-de-chris.html	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	t	f	This dazzling place by Christopher Coutanceau offers two incomparable pleasures: for the eyes and for the taste buds. A long counter in the shape of a skiff (light, long and narrow boat), houses the open kitchen, where the cooks can be seen in action. Seafood (oysters and shellfish) and fish of the day enjoy pride of place on the menu here... to be enjoyed on the terrace that overlooks the sea, in fine weather. Booking recommended.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3335182723	Le Jas	10 bis rue de l'Église	France	La Roque-d'Anthéron	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.lejas-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	La Roque-d'Anthéron's church is home to one of the world's best-known piano festivals. Hailing from the village, chef Émeric Corbon, who worked for Michel Kayser and Édouard Loubet, came up with the idea of opening this restaurant just a few metres from the church, in a converted dry-stone sheepfold (a jas in the Provençal dialect). Beneath the centuries-old vaulted ceilings or on the terrace, you can enjoy carefully prepared dishes with a clear Provençal influence: delicious aubergine papeton and tomato concassé with fresh herbs, basil coulis^ tasty squab roasted whole, with the legs, gizzards and heart in a samosa, and a creamy pea sauce.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
