3339355881	L'Ogustin	2 place de l'Ormeau	France	La Vacquerie-et-Saint-Martin-de-Castries	Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantdularzac.com/l-ogustin	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Not far from the Cirque de Navacelles, in a small village on the southern edge of the limestone plateau that is the Causse du Larzac, Pricillia Lebon's restaurant is housed in a converted inn. Beneath the stone vaults, the inviting, cosy decor reflects the endearing personality of a chef who has come to this beautiful, isolated setting to cook. The surprise set menu celebrates the Larzac area, with ingredients sourced mainly via short supply chains (not least from local market gardens), as well as from mushroom and plant picking. Plants reign supreme in the intuitive, light and aromatic dishes. The dessert is a tribute to the chef's Malgasy origins, with a sweet potato cream spiked with vanilla. Vegetarian options are also available. A unique and authentic place.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3338724937	Les Semailles	10 rue du Petit-Magmod	France	La Wantzenau	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-semailles.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This spruce Alsace house stands in a quiet side street. On the menu: top-notch ingredients, perfectly cooked, intelligently seasoned and paired and a catering tradition that upholds the practice of tableside service (a rack of veal is carved and langoustine is seared on hot stones right in front of the diner). We were particularly taken with the langoustines, asparagus and caviar – a masterpiece of scrumptious delicacy. When the weather is fine, make a beeline for the terrace shaded by a hundred-year-old wisteria.	popescumaya	\N	\N
