3335614653	Le San Felice	3001 route des Hauts-du-Camp	France	Le Castellet	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelducastellet.net	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	San Felice is not only a Dumas novel: at the Hôtel du Castellet, it is also a swish, imaginative bistro! The menu is deliberately concise, with a seasonal line-up and a mouth-watering focus on matured meats and fish cooked over hot embers. The terrace by the swimming pool commands a drop-dead view of the golf course and greenery. Treat yourself to the lunchtime ‘Gourmand’ menu (Mon to Sat).	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3334420042	La Corniche - Sainte-Barbe	Pointe Sainte-Barbe	France	Le Conquet	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelsaintebarbe.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Sainte Barbe Hotel offers a choice of Instagrammable views looking out to sea or of the harbour. La Corniche sports and elegant contemporary vibe. Finely crafted cuisine, recipes of bistronomic inspiration with a distinct preference for local fish and seafood. The rooftop bar is heaven for a drink before or after dinner.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3335203519	La fleur de Sel	2 rue Albert-1er	France	Le Creusot	Wheelchair access	http://www.lafleurdesel-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The initiative by this pair, chef Willy Lardry and maître d' Edwin Smietanski, to open their restaurant here is most welcome. Both hail from Le Creusot but met while working for Yohann Chapuis in Tournus. The interior is inspired in part by nature (with, in particular, wallpaper depicting a forest in the mist). The chef, working alone in the kitchen, shows undeniable maturity. Delicacy and finesse are the order of the day, for example, the lovely courgette flower with cod stuffing and the olive oil sabayon accompanying the cod tournedos, or the mackerel and its marinated cucumber ravioli.	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3335133585	L'Océan	Port-Lin	France	Le Croisic	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelrestaurant-locean.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	f	f	Founded in 1981 by Louis and Yolande André, who are now assisted by their daughter Dominique and son-in-law Gérard Samson, L’Océan is a treat for the eye and the palate thanks to the huge conservatory and a menu that stars supremely fresh first-class seafood and fish. The establishment’s timeless signature dishes never fail to deliver: seafood platters, scallops in season, sole meunière or whole seabass in a salt crust (to be shared). We also recommend the big-boned lobster bisque, rich in whole pieces of perfectly cooked lobster and deliciously crunchy croutons. Finish with a wickedly tempting rum and raisin baba – the epitome of comforting nostalgia as you watch the sun set over the waves.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3330814322	Le Lénigo	11 quai du Lénigo	France	Le Croisic	Terrace	https://www.lelenigo.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant located opposite the fish market is run by a very pleasant family. Seaside atmosphere (varnished wood, portholes) and fresh, carefully prepared seafood dishes.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3339876632	Auberge de la Marine	1 rue Florentin-Lefils	France	Le Crotoy	Wheelchair access	https://www.aubergedelamarine.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	In a small regional-style building near the docks, this young couple beautifully showcases local ingredients. Example dishes include pressed sea bass with sand carrots, chervil sorbet^ fillet of hake, beurre blanc with sea aster, mashed sandy potatoes^ baba with a citrus syrup, cream with lemon balm… Tasty and expertly executed cuisine!	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3337904233	Les Quatre Saisons	3 route du Frenz	France	Le Frenz	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.hotel4saisons.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This cosy chalet is set in a landscape of forests and mountains. Christelle proposes her own personal brand of cuisine (savoury éclair filled with porcini mousse, chanterelles in vinegar and cured ham, duck pot au feu with autumn vegetables cooked in broth), while Frédéric carefully selects the wines.	leonechristian	\N	\N
3338106089	Confins des Sens	341 Le Villavit	France	Le Grand-Bornand	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-grand-bornand.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	The house speciality is a delicious muscat-flavoured foie gras soup with a confit of red onions and ‘cromesquis’. The chefs pay tribute to the region whilst respecting the seasons, illustrated by a velvety soup of green peas and an ice cream of fresh cow’s cheese flavoured with wild garlic. Other highlights include pork cheeks braised in a local red wine or free-range chicken wings stuffed with morels and flanked by “pressed” potatoes (finely sliced and stacked before being roasted). The terrace is glorious in the sunshine.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3331700522	Le Lucé	Château du Grand-Lucé	France	Le Grand-Lucé	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://leluce.com/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	An 18C palace provides the enchanting location for this restaurant set in a Classical decor of mirrors and chandeliers. When it comes to the food, a savvy approach has been adopted of serving fine dining cuisine based on ingredients sourced from the region and grown in the kitchen garden: white asparagus with wild garlic, a full-bodied vegetable jus, roast asparagus and wild garlic pesto^ trout and chard, hazelnut butter sabayon, crispy and wilted chard. And what better way to round off your meal than a post-prandial stroll through the magnificent formal gardens?	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
