3337487477	L'Auberge de la Pomme	44 route de l'Eure	France	Les Damps	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.laubergedelapomme.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	t	The name may evoke Normandy and its apples, and it may have a half-timbered façade that is typical of the region, but that's where the cliché ends! Inside you will encounter a very contemporary decor, with a bright dining area with large picture windows affording views out over the garden. The dishes, which showcase local producers, include carpaccio of scallops from Normandy, poached monkfish with a coulis of watercress from Cailly-sur-Eure, and farm-raised veal chop casserole.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3339196993	La R'mize	160 rue du Vieux-Village	France	Les Gets	Wheelchair access	http://www.larmize.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Located in the historic village, near the church, this eatery serves traditional toothsome nosh. A veteran chef regales diners with well-crafted dishes like cream of pumpkin soup served with shavings of Abondance cheese and whipped cream lightly flavoured with passion fruit or a carpaccio of scallops with a jus of lobster shells. His gourmet repertoire also includes timeless Savoyard specialities ranging from gratinée gourmande to fondue Savoyard made with champagne!	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3338287533	Le K'ozzie	20 route de Francin	France	Les Marches	Terrace	https://www.lekozzie.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	This inviting and cosy restaurant is run by Maude and Sébastien, who met in Australia, land of the Aussies or Ozzies (the reference behind the name). The concept is to let yourself be guided by the chef's inspiration^ only a (non-exhaustive) list of the ingredients currently in his kitchen will be presented to you. Enigmatic and tasty.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3335526202	La Marmite du Pêcheur	Boulevard des Tilleuls	France	Les Mées	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://lamarmitedupecheur.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	t	f	This restaurant, a former mill, stands at the foot of the village’s iconic pointed rock formation. It serves fish and seafood specialities (bouillabaisse to order). The interior sports a modern vibe, offset by an old mill wheel that adds a characterful note to the décor.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3339487478	Le Pré Fillet	Route du Pré Fillet aux Molunes	France	Les Molunes	Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.hotel-leprefillet.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This former farmstead, turned into a restaurant three generations ago, stands in a landscape of meadows and woodland at an altitude of 1200 metres. Simplicity and generosity are the bywords of this establishment which shines the spotlight on the region’s knockout produce. The chef crafts wholesome, hearty fare: calf sweetbread flambéed in Jura marc and asparagus in flaky pastry or melt-in-the-mouth knuckle of lamb braised in assorted veggies. To be sampled and enjoyed in a dining area overlooking the unspoiled countryside. Diners are pampered by attentive staff.	berninialex	\N	\N
3331128269	Hostellerie du Château des Monthairons	26 route de Verdun	France	Les Monthairons	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.chateaudesmonthairons.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	A thick slab of pan-fried duck foie gras with Granny Smith apple chutney^ fillet of beef, new potatoes^ game in season: this family-run château restaurant serves heart-warming food that adds the occasional contemporary spin to a patriotic line-up of French recipes. The historic château, set in the Meuse Valley and originally a Benedictine monastery, is magnificent with mouldings, old parquet floors, and plush drapes.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3339345173	Les 3 Lieux - La Table	10 Port-des-Noues	France	Les Ponts-de-Cé	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.les3lieux.com/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€	t	f	In this restaurant on the banks of the River Loire, diners enjoy chef Sylvain Justice’s creative, high-spirited cuisine with lashings of generosity to boot: soup of bouchot mussels in kari-gosse spices, green peas, confit of lemon and crunchy croutons^ carpaccio of squid, peppers and lemon^ roast monkfish, lobster bisque risotto with parmesan and basil^ roast John Dory, spring veggies and hollandaise sauce^ nectarines in verbena and almonds or Mirabelle plums and mead in shortbread. Pop next-door to the Bistrot for a more casual dining experience.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3339222931	Le Quai des Saveurs	8 place de Strasbourg	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne	Air conditioning	https://www.lequaidessaveurs.net	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	f	f	You can expect a warm welcome with the bonus of a sea view from Estelle and Maxime Dourdin. The chef, formerly of establishments of the calibre of the Four Seasons George V in Paris, signs a single set menu that changes frequently depending on market availability. Unusual, well-crafted dishes in the zeitgeist, such as mussels in white wine, jalapeno sauce, fermented milk and herb-flavoured tapioca.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3339475055	L'Estran	8 quai Emmanuel-Garnier	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne	Terrace	https://lestran-restaurant-les-sables-dolonne.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Ceviche of seabass, coconut milk, ginger and sweet potato guacamole^ lightly seared wild prawns in Espelette pepper, artichokes glazed in tarragon with a langoustine emulsion… In this dinky quayside restaurant, whose terrace overlooks the port, chef Xavier Audren pursues a bistronomic quest that takes its cue from the seasons and the fish market just down the street. A concise menu, flawless craftsmanship together with lashings of flavour and colour.	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3337779174	La Suite S'il Vous Plaît	20 boulevard Franklin-Roosevelt	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lasuitesvp.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Located behind the casino and the beaches, this establishment is a breath of fresh air on the local restaurant scene. In a trendy bistro decor, to a soundtrack of jazz and R&B, chef Mélanie Sire serves up dishes that echo market availability of ingredients. Skilfully playing on textures and flavours, she prepares simple but delicious plates, including creations such as the beautifully presented trilogy of oysters, or the perfectly cooked pluma ibérica pork. We will be coming back for more... s'il vous plaît!	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3337509272	La Cotriade	18 quai Emmanuel-Garnier	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne	Terrace	https://restaurant-la-cotriade.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	t	t	On the quayside facing the fishing port, the seafood counter piled high with fish and shellfish sits proudly in front of the restaurant. This seafaring theme is naturally pursued indoors, where the chef is busy in his open-plan kitchen. The menu features seafood platters, fresh fish chalked up on the daily specials board, a few family favourites and a scattering of signature dishes like seabream cooked in a banana leaf, lime and coconut milk, whole sea bass roasted in fennel and flambéed with aniseed, or their famous cotriade – Brittany's answer to bouillabaisse. A few meat dishes are also available.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3330948036	Bistro'Quai	17 quai René-Guiné	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne		https://www.bistroquai-ls.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	On the busy docks of the port, this cosy, colourful eatery in tune with the era serves a seafood menu that varies depending on the catch of the day. You may also be tempted by chef François Gauthier’s specialties, such as squid and cuttlefish flanked by an Espelette pepper sauce or pig’s trotters and ears in a mustard seed sauce. Discerning foodies should save room for the île flottante (egg whites floating on vanilla custard) and pink pralines (candied almonds) à la Alain Chapel – to die for!	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3339575629	La Cuisine de Bertrand	22 quai de Franqueville	France	Les Sables-d'Olonne	Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Opposite the fishing harbour, it is well worth keeping an eye open for this low-profile restaurant. The chef unashamedly crafts textbook French recipes with the objective of showcasing first-rate ingredients in dishes that hit the spot every time. Diligent service.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3334339168	Colette	La Plagnette	France	Les Salles	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantcolette.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	In the heart of the Forez region, this group of large stone and timber buildings nestles between a fir forest and a lake. The property is conducive to kicking back on the terrace in summer or, in winter, to embracing the hygge lifestyle by the imposing fireplace in the cosy restaurant room. The cooking of chef Thomas Laurier (Maison Pic and Dame de Pic, Chabichou) proves to be comforting and indulgent: an excellent pâté en croûte (a speciality served in different variations throughout the year) and, for dessert, fresh poached peach accompanied by lemon balm from the garden and buckwheat – a little culinary gem. The chef's partner takes care of the restaurant floor, where there is rarely a free table to be had.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3330694394	Le Constance - Abbaye de Villeneuve	Lieu-dit Villeneuve	France	Les Sorinières	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.abbayedevilleneuve.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	The brasserie of this hotel that has been tastefully refurbished from top to bottom, is set up in a space that is flooded with light through a beautiful glass roof and bay windows overlooking the swimming pool and grounds. The chef presents a menu that combines traditional dishes (e.g. pâté en croûte, egg mayonnaise, fish with beurre blanc sauce, Loire fish quenelle with crayfish bisque) with more modern recipes. We also like the attractive wine list with (very) reasonable prices, especially for the wines from the region.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3337974935	Arraditz	2 rue Cachau	France	Lescar	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.arraditz.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This 19C house near Pau is the haunt of a couple, chef Olivier Nicolau from Lescar, and his partner Karine, in charge of the service, both of whom learnt the ropes in star establishments. The subtle, niftily crafted repertory showcases regional produce: Projan squab, Lucq-de-Béarn mushrooms, Bahus-Soubiran lemon, Poey-de-Lescar pepper… Intelligent surf and turf combinations and generous helpings add the final touch to this epicurean portrait.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
