3335384811	A Pignata	Route de Pianu	France	Levie	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.apignata.com/	Nessun premio	Corsican, Country cooking	3.0	€€€	f	t	This farm-inn, the quintessence of rural charm, specialises in hearty, wholesome dishes that pay tribute to regional traditions through a set menu and top-notch produce. The Corsican cured meats are made from pigs raised on the family farm and the roasted caramelised lamb is exquisite, while the iconic stuffed seabream pays a highly fitting tribute to Corsica’s culinary heritage. Take a seat in the shade of the arbour and admire the knockout view over the mountains and the estate’s vegetable garden.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3335601642	Coup de Main	112 rue Saint-André	France	Lille	Interesting wine list	https://www.coupdemain-lille.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	f	t	Victor Berthe (previously at Rozó) and Clément Delécluse (France's Young Sommelier of 2021) have set up shop in the heart of the Saint-André neighbourhood in Vieux Lille. With good humour, the two partners welcome diners to their compact little restaurant and wine shop with an open kitchen and vintage furnishings. The short menu sets the tone: starters for sharing, a choice between fish, meat and a vegetarian main, and just two desserts. For dinner, there's also a tasting menu that brilliantly combines seasonal dishes with playful and varied cuisine based on ingredients from small-scale producers, with whom the duo maintain close ties. Natural wine list.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3336922394	Ginko	70 rue de l'Hôpital-Militaire	France	Lille	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.ginkorestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Near the Grand’Place, this unobtrusive eatery with a glazed facade is the brainchild of two pals, both of whom boast virtuoso CVs: Valentina Giacobbe was born in Italy and grew up in Asia, graduated in political science before she turned to cooking, training at Gaya with Pierre Gagnaire before working at Rozo and then at SOlange^ and Julien Ingaud-Jaubert, who trained as a pastry chef and who has also worked in top establishments (Pierre Gagnaire, Meurin, La Laiterie). Their trendy venue is the picture of a sleek contemporary bistro complete with a red-brick wall, a tribute to Lille. Valentina’s creative, delicate recipes are both distinctive and exquisitely balanced. Her seasonal menu features dishes dominated by vegetables (like green peas paired with nettles or the wild garlic-flavoured hollandaise sauce that accompanies the cod), all of which might feature Italian or Asian accents. A fully vegetarian menu is also available.	landirobert	\N	\N
3334660954	La Laiterie	138 avenue de l'Hippodrome	France	Lille	Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lalaiterie.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Grandson of dairy farmers and son of restaurant owners, chef Édouard Chouteau, who trained with the likes of Pierre Gagnaire, Alain Passard and Christophe Pelé, has settled in this historic cottage, a former dairy farm (yes, really!), next-door to Citadelle Park and a stone’s throw from the banks of the Deûle. The tastefully appointed dining rooms open onto a huge garden and a patio. The perfect foil for the chef’s creative score, which delves freely into produce from Northern France with a fondness for surf and turf recipes.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3338107951	Le 49R	49 rue Royale	France	Lille	Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.49r-lille.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Behind the somewhat terse name (referring to its address at 49 rue Royale), there lies a charming private mansion whose original decor is enhanced by well-placed modern touches. The delightful terrace overlooking the courtyard to the rear of the building is a particular highlight. The dishes are creative and rigorously executed: sea bass ceviche, hazelnuts and seaweed^ duck breast, chanterelle mushrooms, red curry sauce. Excellent wine list and selection of spirits.	beloveva	\N	\N
3336352141	Le Braque	45 rue de la Monnaie	France	Lille	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.le-braque.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Sous-chef to Florent Ladeyn and a TV cooking show contestant, Damien Laforce and dog, Marcel (a pointer or ‘braque’), have opened this eatery, depicted by brick and light wood. He crafts tasty regional fare, scattered with bold touches. Concise organic wine list, smiling service and 20 or so wall counter seats for customers without a booking.	beloveva	\N	\N
3332022417	Pulpe	7 rue Saint-André	France	Lille	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-pulpe.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Clémence Taillandier and Philippe Platel's bistro has a contemporary look with a very attractive old-fashioned feel (velvet banquettes, designer school chairs, brass wall light fixtures, mosaic tiling etc). In a relaxed atmosphere, the chef, who has worked at Troisgros, L'Astrance and Rozó, crafts precise cuisine that does the job and gets right down to the essentials: octopus carpaccio and Kalamata virgin olive oil (a real taste of Crete)^ confit of line-caught pollack, green asparagus, hay-smoked beurre blanc^ strawberry tart with lemon and verbena ice cream. The flavours, the skilful cooking, the seasoning: this place ticks all the boxes! You'll be coming back for more – and the same goes for the savvily curated wine list.	dinusauru	\N	\N
