3332462671	La Table de Pôl	18 boulevard Georges-Clemenceau	France	Lorgues	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://latabledepol.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	What luck to have a terrace next to the listed Fontaine de la Noix, with the bonus of a bird’s eye view of the show on market days. Inside, the decor blends exposed rafters, parquet floors, bare stonework and a palette of warm terracotta shades. The young chef, assisted by his Scottish partner for the front of house, whips up mouthwatering dishes: cream of green peas, breaded goat’s cheese with a mint and green pea condiment^ grilled haunch of veal, cork-shaped potatoes, baby broad beans and watercress juice^ confit kumquat, gingerbread and frothy vanilla mascarpone… Seasonal menus and ingredients.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3332386707	Le 26-28	26-28 rue Poissonnière	France	Lorient	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.le2628.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Contemporary design, open kitchens, a chef – Arthur Friess (with a fine Michelin-starred career) – and, managing the restaurant floor, Charlotte Le Gall: these are the ingredients that make this place a success. Lovely contemporary cuisine made from impeccable ingredients – such as pigeon, spelt au gratin and roots. Menu renewed every month.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3330877210	Le Yachtman	14 rue Poissonnière	France	Lorient	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.leyachtmanlorient.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	t	t	Unsurprisingly, seafood – in particular fish from the local auction – takes pride of place in this pretty restaurant located close to the marina. Simplicity and accuracy reign on the plate, while the dining area has a minimalist and intimate decor.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3332472542	Le Bout des Canards	104 rue du Général-Leclerc	France	Lorquin	Wheelchair access	https://www.leboutdescanards.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This inn, with its plum and lavender-toned façade, will have a new chapter in its story thanks to its new owners. This couple has worked in some fine establishments (he was sous-chef at Villa René Lalique^ she was assistant to the maître d'). In a decor of pale-coloured wood, pick from a short seasonal menu^ many dishes are based on local ingredients (eg marinated trout, rocket, horseradish, cucumber and smoked oil, or crispy waffles, caramelised mirabelles and fromage blanc ice cream). The lunch deal is unbeatable value and the welcome is particularly warm!	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3336541689	Ricordeau	13 rue de la Libération	France	Loué	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-ricordeau.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Sit out on the pleasant terrace set up in the garden, on the banks of the River Vègre, and treat yourself to a fine dining interlude courtesy of the chef's cooking, which is always in touch with the seasons. The contemporary dishes, which are deliberate and meticulous, make use of the finest local ingredients, including supreme of Loué chicken stuffed with onions and morel mushrooms, first-harvest vegetables and a creamy poultry jus. La Table du Coq, the hotel's second restaurant, serves simpler fare.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3338953770	Kaito	Four Seasons Megève	France	Megève	Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.fourseasons.com/megeve/dining/restaurants/kaito/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Fusion	3.0	€€€€	t	f	At the Four Seasons Hotel, flawlessly fresh sashimi, tataki and sushi rub shoulders with delicately crafted alpine specialties. Fusion cuisine to be enjoyed on the terrace commanding a splendid view of the slopes or in the softly lit interior.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3333927639	La Luciole	3 place de la République	France	Luc-sur-Orbieu	Terrace	https://www.restaurantlaluciole.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	The chef fulfilled a childhood dream when he bought this cafe on the small village square. A passionate self-taught chef, he works hand in hand with his daughter, concocting simple, tasty dishes that do justice to fine local produce: rabbit and maki of haddock^ plancha-grilled veal steak, chimichurri sauce^ rum baba and pina colada sorbet. Served on the terrace, in the shade of a centennial tree.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3338523818	Le Bonheur dans Le Pré	2011 route de Bellevue	France	Lucinges	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lebonheurdanslepre.ellohaweb.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€	f	f	In this 19C farmhouse deep in the countryside, authenticity is the name of the game. The chef creates a single menu (vegetarian version available) using top-notch local ingredients. The food is perfectly paired with wines from the splendid cellar (over 300 references) that abuts the dining room. The restaurant’s name is a playful reference to a well-loved French movie (1995) starring a plethora of Gallic movie stars.	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3337868070	Le Bistrot de Madeleine	67 place de l'Église	France	Lucinges	Terrace	http://www.laubergedelucinges.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This village inn is a real boon for lovers of the finer (and healthier) things in life. It would not be out of place to talk about programmatic cuisine in this bistro with a slightly rustic feel: whole carcass approach, local market gardening, fish sourced directly from the fish markets, a menu that changes every week… The end result? Tasty, generous and delicious cuisine.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3334235731	Au Fil des Saisons	55 route de la Roche-sur-Yon	France	Luçon	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.aufildessaisons-vendee.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This engaging roadside inn provides an opportunity to sample stripped-back, seasonal fare that relies on fresh ingredients of traditional and regional inspiration (duck foie gras with juniper berries, breast of roast guinea fowl in herbs, etc.). A small cottage garden supplies the kitchen with some veggies and herbs. Take a seat in the conservatory or in the garden, depending on the season.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3331699213	Maison Soubeiran	129 cours Gabriel-Péri	France	Lunel	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.maison-soubeiran.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	We fell in love with this family-run establishment whose chef whips up spontaneous regional fare made with fresh, seasonal ingredients from local organic market gardeners. Scents and flavours from the garrigue, Camargue and Mediterranean, jazzed up with spicy notes and flanked by homemade sourdough bread made with heritage wheat. Authentic warm welcome and an exquisite patio shaded by a natural trellis.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3337077508	La Table de Jérôme	26 rue de la République	France	Luzy	Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelrestaurantdumorvan58.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	In the walls of the Hôtel du Morvan, chef Jérôme Raymond plays a modern, culinary score based on regional produce. A single set menu, with more upmarket ingredients at the weekend (Charolais beef is a firm favourite). Whopping 400-bin wine list of mainly Burgundy origins. Comfortable rooms should you wish to stay longer.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3336213805	Café Terroir	14 rue d'Amboise	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.cafeterroir.fr/	Nessun premio	Country cooking	5.0	€€	f	f	Established near the Célestins Theatre, under the auspices of Jean-François Têtedoie (son of legendary Christian!), this house upholds the art of good food. The menu reads like a culinary bible of Lyon’s specialties: signature dishes like homemade terrine and gâteau lyonnais rub shoulders with rotisserie joints, to be shared and carved in front of you (Bresse poultry, rib of beef, lobster), without forgetting a lineup of bistro classics such as calf’s sweetbread vol-au-vent or Monts du Lyonnais snails with girolle mushrooms and cress. The wine cellar boasts over 1,500 references at temptingly reasonable prices.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3335422595	Armada	16 rue du Bœuf	France	Lyon	Air conditioning	https://armada-lyon.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€	t	t	This bolthole in historic Lyon ticks all the boxes: a trendy chummy vibe and a ubiquitous decor of exposed beams and stonework. The food demonstrates a clever, creative slant with uninhibited dishes to share depicted by mussels, curry and dried lime, an exuberant new take on blanquette of veal or stuffed cabbage. Beware: it may well become your new HQ.	caldarolacagilio	\N	\N
3336970856	Omma	38 rue de la Poste	France	Roussillon	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	http://www.ommaluberon.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Taking in the Luberon and the famous ochre cliffs of Roussillon, the view from this restaurant is nothing short of spectacular! As for the food, the short, seasonal menu proposes bistronomy-style dishes with Provençal influences: crispy aubergine, baba ganoush with coriander and fromage blanc with lime^ grilled Ventoux pork, peppers stuffed with Coco de Paimpol beans, piperade and apricot condiment^ Musquée de Provence pumpkin confit with vanilla, sponge cake with pistachios. A moment of culinary bliss far from the crowds of tourists.	salluis	\N	\N
3335905041	Taggat	110 rue Vendôme	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.taggat.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€	f	t	In this contemporary-style bistro with an industrial vibe, the chef showcases his culinary skills. These tend towards the creative, and he is not afraid to lace his dishes with bold flavours: burrata and cucumber, mojo verde, bread crisps, garlic confit and black olive powder… or John Dory, caponata, olive oil puff pastry and a red pepper jus. Set menu at lunchtime and à la carte in the evening in a similar vein, but with more upmarket ingredients.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3337596373	Cercle Rouge	36 rue de l'Arbre-Sec	France	Lyon		https://cercle-rouge.fr/	Nessun premio	Fusion	5.0	€€	t	t	This young bistro nestles behind a small, glass - paned façade on a bustling street close to Opéra. On the menu, fusion cuisine with influences ranging across Asian, South American and British, and a fine technical command. Really friendly atmosphere.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3331149331	Osteria Matto	23 rue de Sèze	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://osteria-matto.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€	t	t	Chef Thomas Asti has Italian blood running through his veins. So, it made sense when he and his partner opened this bistro-styled trattoria. The duo draws on Italy’s glorious culinary heritage to the delight of their loyal regulars, who flock here to sample vitello tonnato, bagna cauda, veal with house-made potato gnocchi – and Sicilian lemon tart, just the way nonna used to make it. To be washed down with premium Italian wines. What’s not to like?	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3334601041	Alebrije	2 rue Belfort	France	Lyon		https://restaurant-alebrije.fr/	Nessun premio	Mexican	5.0	€€€	f	t	After training at the Paul Bocuse Institute and a number of noteworthy spells in top establishments, such as Troisgros, youthful Carla Kirsch, who hails from Veracruz in Mexico, has settled in the Croix-Rousse district. The signature here is clearly Mexican from the décor, which features old rafters with splashes of colour, to the food, which Carla joyfully crafts using top-notch seasonal ingredients (sweet corn in the starter and chili peppers in the dessert). The menu changes monthly and the beverages include a few Mexican wines as well as tequilas and mezcals.	monticristian	\N	\N
3333135557	Aromatic	15 rue du Chariot-d'Or	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://aromaticrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	In La Croix-Rousse, Frédéric Taghavi conjure up inventive, modern recipes which add a new twist to culinary traditions, as well as featuring a scattering of international influences: Limousin sweetbread, leeks and morels in a kalamansi reduction^ quickly seared squid in coconut milk and yellow curry shrimp sauce^ slow-cooked beef cheeks in red wine with farm-reared bacon risotto…	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
