3337591056	Le Piquebaure	166 avenue Dame-Sirmonde	France	Roussillon	Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Provençal	3.0	€€	f	t	At the foot of Roussillon village, this picturesque dry-stone house proposes Provençal-inspired food in an enticing menu in which fresh produce is a major component. The restaurant’s pride and joy is its second terrace overlooking the wonderful Luberon countryside.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3337513877	Cinq Mains	12 rue Monseigneur-Lavarenne	France	Lyon	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.cinqmains.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In this very touristy area alongside the Saône, this house with exposed stone walls is now the HQ of Grégory Cuilleron, with his brother and a friend at his side. The cuisine has a distinctly gastro - bistro and modern tendency, and is accompanied by a selection of well - chosen minor wines – the three partners are oenophiles.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3331239818	Circle	11 rue Chavanne	France	Lyon	Air conditioning	https://circlelyon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	The name of this restaurant pays homage to American rapper Mac Miller, as well as to the circle of friends and co-workers running the show here! Chef Bastian Ruga has perfected his concept. Playing out to a soundtrack of American rap music, his youthful, no-holds-barred cuisine charts a course between bold creativity, North African and Asian influences, and a healthy dose of affection for traditional cuisine – this is Lyon, after all! The original food-and-drink pairings are an integral part of the experience, encompassing beer, herbal teas and a natural wine list. A shining example would be the wonderfully pearlescent cod with black garlic hollandaise sauce, served with a comforting ginger brandade. The style of service is professional and trendy.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3339397204	Danton	8 rue Danton	France	Lyon	Air conditioning	https://danton-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In this friendly neo-bistro, the menu gets straight down to business - it is concise, to the point and stars dishes that are as hearty and unpretentious as they are delicious, while the wine list showcases regional (but not only) producers. The chef’s consummate technical know-how shines through in his perfect mastery of cooking times and techniques, while the desserts are fully equal to those of any high-flying pastry chef. A warm welcome and slick, smiling service. If they are full, try L'Escapade Danton next-door.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3338730451	Epona	InterContinental Lyon - Hotel Dieu	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lyon.intercontinental.com/le-restaurant-epona/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	A hospital for eight centuries, the former Hôtel-Dieu has preserved all the building's historical character. The Epona restaurant serves regional specialities with a modern twist, which you can enjoy in a lovely setting that calls to mind a high-end brasserie. And in fine weather, the team welcomes you in a superb courtyard garden.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3339455868	L'Alexandrin	83 rue Moncey	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.lalexandrin.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	L'Alexandrin combines originality with generosity, serving dishes made using fine, locally sourced produce. Each menu (vegetarian, revisited Lyon classics or pure creation) proposes a different take on the art of fine dining in an exclusive atmosphere. One novelty is the table d'hôte with four guests seated in the kitchen at the heart of the action!	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3331734188	L'Artichaut	Hôtel de l'Abbaye	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://hotelabbayelyon.com/restaurant-artichaut/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Tucked away in a former presbytery transformed into an attractive hotel, this laid-back and stylish restaurant serves tasty contemporary dishes (snails, pumpkin cream, garlic purée and parsley^ arctic char, girolles with amaretto, potatoes and coffee powder) in tune with the seasons.	ozmax	\N	\N
3331575859	L'Établi	22 rue des Remparts d'Ainay	France	Lyon	Air conditioning	https://www.letabli-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	This restaurant run by an alumnus of Christian Têtedoie is a real favourite. The lunch menu is good value for money, the dishes are in keeping with the times and seasonal (hake, asparagus, fennel, smoked raspberry): from start to finish it's a treat. Not to spoil anything, the service is also attentive.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3333918536	L'Institut Restaurant	Le Royal	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.linstitut-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	On Place Bellecour, this training restaurant feels nothing like a school! In a contemporary decor designed by Pierre - Yves Rochon, with open kitchens giving onto the restaurant, the students deliver a high standard of service. The dishes are extremely well made and deserve a high mark.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3333927195	La Table 101	101 rue Moncey	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.latable101.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In the Part-Dieu neighbourhood, near Paul Bocuse Market, Olivier and Maryline Delbergues’ establishment rolls out market-fresh recipes with the odd creative twist: tataki of sea trout, sweet-sour red meat radishes, mashed squash, green apple and pecan nuts… Intelligent wine list.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3333784205	Le Grand Réfectoire	3 cour Saint-Henri	France	Lyon	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://legrandrefectoire.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In the heart of the grandiose Hôtel Dieu, beneath the hundred-year-old vaults of the nuns’ former refectory, the menu of this huge brasserie is signed by Marcel Ravin (2*-chef of Monaco’s Blue Bay). The modern food is sprinkled with exotic West Indian influences. The swish rooftop bar (L’Officine) draws city slickers like bees to honey, as does the exquisite patio in the inner courtyard.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3330072040	Le Suprême	106 cours Gambetta	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lesupremelyon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The brainchild of a Franco-Korean couple of chefs who met in New York, the ubiquitous chicken is the star of this vintage bistro oozing with charm. The chef, former right-arm man of Daniel Boulud, consummately signs a gourmet gateau of sautéed chicken livers and a chicken in “half-mourning” that has already become a signature dish. This virtuoso technician has also invented a wafer-thin tart of Nashi pear, scallops and Brussels sprouts. Local game in season. Knockout wine list.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
