3336735384	Augustine - La Table du Château	Allée des Marronniers	France	Maffliers	Car park,Garden or park	http://www.augustinelatableduchateau-maffliers.fr	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	In a handsome 19C abode near Montmorency Forest, this restaurant aims to uphold French art de vivre: period tableware and furniture, gleaming silverware and copper and high ceilings – all of which in a plush muted interior dominated by wood. The food is suitably classical and generous, whilst traversing the annals of French cookery: pâté en croûte, rabbit cooked in mustard and rice pudding. A few rooms for overnight stays.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3335999442	Côté Quillier	26 avenue de Maremne	France	Magescq	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.relaisposte.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	The sibling of the next-door Relais de la Poste is devoted body and soul to wholesome seasonal cooking. Landes asparagus roasted with parmesan and ham^ fillet of hake with celery tagliatelle^ roast pineapple, frothy coconut mousse and exotic fruit ice cream. The terrace is a hit in fine weather and, even better, why not linger and enjoy a game of skittles on the lawn afterwards? Friendly vibe.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3336184553	Le Bœuf en Écailles	24 avenue du Marais-Poitevin	France	Magné	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.leboeufenecailles.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Authenticity is a word so often used as to be almost meaningless, but it is nonetheless the right term for the gutsy, flavoursome food of this establishment. The meat and fish recipes are steeped in generous mouth-watering flavours, such as 16-hour roast pork with mashed potato in olive oil. The lovely patio on the banks of the Sèvre Niortaise is also authentic.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3339402323	La Plancha	5 avenue de Saint-Germain	France	Maisons-Laffitte	Air conditioning	https://laplanchadekiko.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This place may be discreet, but its original menu makes it well worth coming for a meal here. The dishes are simple, effective and occasionally creative^ the flavours are striking, eg Iberico pork belly with peas, bacon and horseradish. Special mentions have to go to the punchy bulli dog sauce and the profiteroles, which are made in time-honoured tradition.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3331973544	Au Coin du Bois	Rue Sous-le-Rang	France	Mancenans-Lizerne	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-aucoindubois.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	A quiet chalet surrounded by fir trees, whose country setting can be enjoyed from the lovely terrace. The chef deftly crafts great French classics whilst respecting the seasons: local frog’s legs^ fried trout from Franche Comté^ snails in flaky pastry and a Savagnin sauce^ game.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3332524777	Le Repère	Port de la Rague	France	Mandelieu-La Napoule	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.restaurantlerepere.fr	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	This well-established hideaway enjoys a knock-out location, boasting a terrace right on the beach and a panoramic view over the Bay of Cannes and the Lérins Islands. It is a delight to meet up with Nicolas Decherchi, a gifted chef who trained with the best (from Bruno Oger to Alain Ducasse), once again. He has been given carte blanche to devise a Mediterranean-focused menu with a special mention for dishes to share. Flawlessly fresh fish take front stage, although juicy cuts of meat also vie for pride of place. Open all day long, you can expect a pleasure-loving, casual vibe.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3330606988	Pamparigouste - Le Couvent des Minimes	Chemin des Jeux-de-Maï	France	Mane	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.couventdesminimes-hotelspa.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	In addition to his fine dining restaurant, chef Louis Gachet lovingly oversees this upscale bistro. The space is soothing and relaxing, plus there is a dining room-cum-terrace, whose picture windows are opened fully in fine weather. The menu is a skilful blend of traditional favourites and contemporary dishes with a smattering of Provençal touches.	basileryan	\N	\N
3332648627	La Table de Marie-Ange	4910 route du Col-de-la-Croix-Fry	France	Manigod	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.hotelchaletcroixfry.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	The terrace overlooking the Aravis range is so mesmerising, it is difficult to tear oneself away. Marie-Ange aims to serve fine regional dishes oozing with authentic flavour: pan-seared cèpes, fillets of wild perch from Lake Geneva, fillet of beef simmered in mushrooms and grandma’s potato gratin, without forgetting the wickedly lavish dessert trolley. The interior sports old wood and farming tools – charming welcome.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3335537793	Le Bistrot du Chef	180 avenue Régis-Ryckebusch	France	Manosque	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantpierregrein.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Pierre Grein (one MICHELIN star in his eponymous restaurant) has set up his bistro in the wine cellar and delicatessen part of the restaurant: the roomy and pleasant space is set apart and has a contemporary decor enhanced by shelves lined with fine wines and delicatessen wares (jars of conserves, salt, tea etc). The menu features a choice of dishes as well as a set menu without options. The chef's enthusiasm is palpable in his seasonal bistronomy creations, which are really well done and sit alongside the good old bistro classics: truffle croque monsieur, Carnaroli risotto inspired by the Creole dish rougail, steak tartare, or fillet of Charolais beef with chips and Béarnaise sauce. Thank you, Chef!	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3333617949	Au Marquis de Terme	3 route de Rauzan	France	Margaux	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://au-marquis-de-terme.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Surrounded by the Médoc vineyards, this contemporary restaurant is nestled in an outbuilding of the Château Marquis de Terme (a Grand Cru classified in 1855). It boasts a terrace that opens out onto the estate's pretty garden courtyard. Under the stewardship of Grégory Coutanceau, who devised the menu, chef Thibaud Guena welcomes his guests with fresh, modern cuisine that is very much of its time and shuns unnecessary frills. The appealing wine list features almost 600 labels, including a selection of Bordeaux reds and prestige wines available by the glass.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3336454959	Blanc	90 avenue Sindeldorf	France	Marigny-Saint-Marcel	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.blanc-hotel-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This family inn features two enticing options: an elegant, contemporary restaurant, with a well-designed menu based on fine ingredients, or the chalet-inspired wooden interior of the brasserie, where Savoie cheese specialities take pride of place (alongside frogs' legs and pike). Comfortable guestrooms, for those who wish to stay longer the region.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3331742718	Le Point d'Origine	5 place de l'Abreuvoir	France	Marly-le-Roi	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	http://www.lepointdorigine.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Situated opposite the Abreuvoir – the ‘Watering Place’, framed by its famous sculpted horses, this old bourgeois abode is now home to a delicatessen, a wine shop and a restaurant, enthusiastically run by a dynamic team. The restaurant occupies a lovely conservatory with herringbone parquet flooring and an unrivalled view of the Abreuvoir. The chef crafts modern, well-polished dishes: organic œuf parfait, green lentils from Le Puy, smoked herring, parsley sauce and pickled shallots^ confit of turbot in Mat-Khen pepper, braised fennel and citrus notes. A stroll in the park after your meal is just the ticket!	fioreerik	\N	\N
3339362761	Boat aux Saveurs	36-38 avenue Jean-Jaurès	France	Marmande	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantboatauxsaveurs.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This contemporary villa set away from the bustle of the town centre is run by a mother and daughter team. Foodies adore the lovingly prepared dishes fully in tune with the times. The chef makes a point of honour of sourcing ingredients from local producers and most of the veggies come from their own vegetable garden.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3337640404	La Table d'Emilie	8 place Carnot	France	Marseillan	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	The house where the poet Achille Maffre de Baugé was born is home to this very popular restaurant: the delicious and meticulous cuisine is anchored in French tradition (the pâté en croûte is excellent!). Made using fresh produce, this is particularly artfully plated food. To be enjoyed in a dining space with a vaulted ceiling or out on the pleasant patio.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3336551128	Kin	10 rue Francis-Davso	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.kin-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	African	5.0	€€€	f	f	Chef Hugues Mbenda from Kinshasa (Democratic Republic of the Congo) delivers his Congolese cuisine in the form of a single set menu comprising several courses. This menu changes every fortnight and includes creations such as manioc crisps with sweet chilli and burnt onion cream^ crispy Angus beef onglet, dibi sauce, white asparagus and puffed thiéré (Senegalese couscous). The ingredients are fresh, the presentation is meticulous and the flavours are sure to transport you. At lunchtime, Libala, the chef's first cross-cultural street food restaurant, has a simpler menu.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3330228920	Lacaille	42 rue des Trois-Mages	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	http://www.lacaille-marseille.fr	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	f	This neighbourhood bistro offers no-fuss market cuisine that keeps pace with the seasons. Service with a smile.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3337459528	Les Jardins du Cloître	20 boulevard Madeleine-Rémusat	France	Marseille	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lesjardinsducloitredemars.fr	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	Set in a former monastery, this training centre run by the Auteuil Apprentices charity, has a restaurant that is open to the public. Supervised by a professional chef, the brigade of young trainee cooks enthusiastically prepares fine meals in a bistronomic spirit that keeps pace with the seasons, all of which sourced with regional, preferably organic produce. A laudable ethical approach which aims to forge the next generation of restaurateurs.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3332767742	La Cantinetta	24 cours Julien	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurantlacantinetta.fr/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€	f	t	Since childhood, Pierre-Antoine Denis has been passionate about Italian food and regularly pops over the border to scour the country for premium produce. Chalked up on a slate, the menu spans antipasti, fresh house-made pasta and the chef’s signature dish: scaloppine di vitello. Tightly-packed tables, a buzzy vibe and a patio to the rear set the scene.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3333935433	Tabi - Ippei Uemura	165 corniche du Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access	https://www.restauranttabi.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese Contemporary	4.0	€€€	f	f	Tabi, which means journey in Japanese, says it all! Born in Kyoto, the chef has adopted the city of Marseilles as his own. He incorporates locally caught fish into traditional Japanese recipes, prepared in front of customers. Food-saké pairings for aficionados. One of a kind!	vitolajose	\N	\N
3337327839	La Femme du Boucher	10 rue de Village	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	http://www.lafemmeduboucher.fr	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	5.0	€€	f	f	Established in a former butcher’s, energetic Laëtitia Visse, who trained at the Paris Ferrandi School before stints in star restaurants and renowned bistros (Guy Savoy, Alain Dutournier, Cyril Lignac, Olivier Nasti at Kaysersberg) has, unsurprisingly given the name, decided to focus on meat: homemade pâté, fried black pudding, sausages, pig’s trotters, etc… Equally in tune with the zeitgeist, her wine list is strongly focused towards natural and biodynamic wines. Casual service and vibe. In the finest traditions of a Gallic bistro!	venturaroman	\N	\N
3330260772	Cédrat	81 rue Breteuil	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.cedratxmamakyuna.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	A couple, two chefs, two different culinary formulas: at lunchtime, chef Maëlyss Vultaggio chalks up her menu on the blackboard, assisted in the kitchen by Éric Maillet, a young chef who earned his stripes working for the likes of Gérald Passedat. In the evening, the roles are reversed: he takes the lead, creating more of a fine dining menu with his partner supporting him. Dishes such as farmhouse chicken on the barbecue, celeriac confit, sorrel, ginger/lemongrass sauce and XO reduction exemplify this modern Mediterranean-style cuisine. Using organic vegetables, locally caught fish and well-reared meats, the food certainly packs a punch. Contemporary setting.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3331434869	Ekume	139 rue Sainte	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.ekume-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	After clocking up some remarkable experiences, Panamanian chef Edgar Bosquez has dropped anchor in Marseille, not far from the abbey of St Victor. In a spruce, pared-back interior, he showcases fish, seafood and Provençal flavours in a lineup of deftly crafted, suave-tasting menus, including one devoted to bouillabaisse.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3336537155	Belle de Mars	56 rue de Forbin	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	https://belledemars.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Behind wrought-iron railings, this handsome establishment ushers diners into a tastefully understated interior (white walls, parquet floors, wooden chairs and tables) and an open-plan kitchen helmed by Michel Marini and Kim-Mai Bui. This veteran duet (formerly of William Ledeuil, Christophe Moret, Gérald Passedat…) crafts a flavoursome, legible, delicate score with a Mediterranean spin and invariably dotted with herbs they pick themselves. Everything is steeped in crisp, expressive flavours, examples of which include lightly seared squid with a salmorejo sauce or wild seabass in fig leaves. The desserts are low on sugar yet highly addictive!	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3337310520	La Mercerie	9 cours Saint-Louis	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamerceriemarseille.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	An avalanche of quality local ingredients, undeniable know-how and gourmet delicacies... You can count on the young team to take care of your appetite in the best possible way. As for wine, the menu is lovingly put together with an emphasis on natural wines, with a promising turnover: all the ingredients are in place for you to have a great time.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3338983187	Les Bords de Mer	52 corniche du Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.lesdomainesdefontenille.com/fr/lesbordsdemer.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Subtle cuisine and a stunning sea view: what more could we ask for? Chef Camille Gandolfo, who hails from Marseille, adds a fresh (occasionally Asian) spin to her original Mediterranean recipes in a bid to showcase seasonal produce. The savvy wine list gives top billing to the organic production of the Domaine de Fontenille wine estate (AOP Luberon), which owns this elegant establishment. An impressive restaurant that takes its food seriously.	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3333095079	Les Trois Forts	36 boulevard Charles-Livon	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.sofitel-marseille-vieuxport.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	From the seventh floor, the panoramic view over the port is simply sublime! The contemporary dishes with a delicious Southern flavour make for a wonderful gourmet interlude.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3339734148	Nestou	43 rue de Suez	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.nestou.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Just a few strokes from Catalans beach, this restaurant pays homage to Ernest (Nestou), the young son of Jean-Philippe and Jeanne Garbin, who are the joint chefs of this endearing family establishment. He supervises the hot dishes, while she is in charge of the starters and desserts and together, they devise unusual recipes that surf between Mediterranean influences and more globetrotting inspirations. A great place for a meal with the mates!	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3335027590	Prémices	11 rue Beauvau	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.premicesmarseille.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Two friends who met while working at nearby restaurant La Mercerie have opened their own trendy bistro a few doors down, opposite the opera house. A magnificent counter adorned with zellige tiles greets guests^ upstairs, the dining area is sizable. At lunchtime, tuck into a set menu, which comes at a very affordable price considering the quality of the dishes. The menu – renewed twice a month – smacks of good, modern cuisine, and features unusual combinations and trendy names such as celeriac ice cream. The home-made bucatini with spinach condiment and fried sage is a real treat, as is the delicious butternut and nutmeg tart with a subtle quince paste and physalis condiment.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3330722087	Sépia	2 rue Vauvenargues	France	Marseille	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-sepia.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This guinguette perched on the Colline Puget promises an incredible view of the city and the sea as well as a colourful dining experience. In the kitchen, the chef's go-to ingredient is seafood, but he also likes to combine fish with a meat sauce (or vice versa), in dishes such as yellowtail with Albufera-style sauce. Next door is Julis – their offshoot wine and tapas bar, which is very popular with locals from the Saint-Victor and Endoume neighbourhoods for after-work drinks.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3332395960	Un Petit Cabanon Bouillon	63 avenue Robert-Schuman	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.petitcabanonbouillon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In this minimalist neo-bistro just a stone's throw from Joliette metro station, the emphasis is on local produce, with a touch of creativity for good measure. The menu taps into the zeitgeist and highlights what's in season: confit pork belly^ pasta, squid ink, dill and sea almonds.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3338751757	Ourea	72 rue de la Paix-Marcel-Paul	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	http://www.ourea-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Provençal	4.0	€€€	t	t	Matthieu Roche moved from Paris (where he worked at Semilla) to open this tiny bistro with his partner Camille. The space, located between the port and the courthouse, reflects the colours and flavours of Provence. The chef is attentive to the seasons, buying locally (Mediterranean fish directly from the port, vegetables from Mallemort's market gardens, citrus fruits from the Domaine du Jasson).	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3339032308	Chez Fonfon	140 rue du Vallon-des-Auffes	France	Marseille	Air conditioning,Great view	https://www.chez-fonfon.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	f	f	This family restaurant (1952) is pleasing in terms both of its contemporary interior and its seafood, freshly fished in the wooden pointu boats that can be seen bobbing about in the little port.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3331750241	Michel - Brasserie des Catalans	6 rue des Catalans	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurant-michel-13.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Soak up the atmosphere of Marseille in this popular restaurant on the Plage des Catalans. Here they take their bouillabaisse very seriously... and it tastes phenomenal! As you would expect, the menu proposes an exceptionally fresh catch of the day: you will see the fish in the tanks as you come in.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3333007886	Peron	56 corniche John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy	France	Marseille	Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-peron.com	Nessun premio	Seafood, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	On the coast road, this building clinging to the rocks offers a breathtaking view of the bay of Marseille and its islands and the château d’If. A brisk sea breeze has shaken up the menu which features dishes such as local and wild fish of the day, stuffed vegetables, duck breast and beef fillet, without forgetting the ubiquitous bouillabaisse, all of which served on the splendid terrace. A genuine institution since 1855!	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3337587558	Lauracée	96 rue de Grignan	France	Marseille	Air conditioning	https://www.lelauracee.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	There is no doubt that the chef of this joint tucked away behind the old port only serves fresh produce, because, as he himself says “I don’t know how to cook anything else!” Take a seat in the fashionable interior and treat yourself to good food sprinkled with Mediterranean twists. A few examples: stuffed courgette flowers, ewe’s milk cheese, aubergines^ Marseille-style melt-in-the-mouth lamb’s tongues^ warm chocolate mousse, cocoa-flavoured crème brûlée, chou pastry stuffed in hazelnuts. Slick service and warm welcome.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3335095914	Gusto Caffe	4 quai Paul-Doumer	France	Martigues	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurantmartigues.com/restaurant-le-gusto/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€	f	f	In front of the Canal Baussengue marina, a picturesque trattoria where waiters and clients call to each other in a cheerful and distinctly Italian atmosphere! Homemade fare (spaghetti, gnocchi etc), Parma prosciutto cut with the slicer, and the great Italian classics. The terrace is taken by storm in fine weather, as is the lunchtime chalkboard menu, excellent value for money.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3336694627	La Table du Lavoir - Les Sources de Caudalie	Chemin de Smith-Haut-Lafitte	France	Martillac	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://sources-caudalie.com/les-sources-caudalie-restaurants/la-table-du-lavoir/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	When you take a seat in this unabashedly rustic, yet plush establishment, you are reminded of the region’s rich heritage – the winegrowers’ wives used to wash their clothes in the old stone sink that stands in the centre of this reconstructed 18C hall. The menu is accordingly traditional and wholesome: grilled free-range breast of chicken, crunchy potatoes, trompette mushrooms and bearnaise sauce. The epitome of a spruce, country inn of yesteryear, with the bonus of cheerful waiting staff. Even better, it is possible to taste the wines of the property, which is none other than Château Smith Haut Lafitte (also available by the glass)!	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3332865181	Maison Castet	44 avenue de la Gare	France	Martres-Tolosane	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://maisoncastet.com/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	f	t	This contemporary eatery at a remove from the town centre used to be the station café. The chef here employs premium ingredients and his considerable technical skill to conjure up his creative cuisine, transporting diners to Brazil, for example, with a wild pollack moqueca, herb salad and farofa. His impressive desserts, such as beef heart tomato in puffed sugar and sage cream, deserve a special mention. Terrific wine list.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3334204384	Dyades au Domaine des Étangs	Domaine des Étangs	France	Massignac	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://domainedesetangs.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Picture a sprawling estate (almost 2,500 acres) of woodland, forest, meadows, fields, farms and ponds and now add a 13C castle equipped with every modern comfort one would expect from a top-of-the-range luxury establishment. The former stables have been converted into a dining area that adroitly blends antique and trendy details. At its helm, chef Matthieu Pasgrimaud (Saint Tropez’ La Vague d’Or and Manhattan’s Daniel Boulud) can be relied upon to make the most of the first-class produce grown on the estate, scattered with aromatic herbs and garden veggies. Kitchen garden dishes (Camus artichoke flowers and plum amandon oil) vie for pride of place with dishes to share, more classical recipes and the chef’s signatures (like sturgeon loaf and Neuvic caviar) in a culinary repertory that is as eclectic as it is high-flying. Chloé Tardivel, the chef’s partner, elegantly and seamlessly manages the welcome and service.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3335046217	Roze	4 rue Augustin-Fresnel	France	Mathieu	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.roze-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This old building in the centre of the village has been treated to a tasteful contemporary makeover. It now showcases the talents of Clémence Goupil and Alex Néel, who are fountains of knowledge about their profession and its history^ their establishment’s name refers to the inventor of the modern restaurant concept, Mathurin Roze de Chantoiseau. Our two lovebirds sing an ode to fresh seasonal produce with touching sincerity teamed with bold flourishes: artichoke, tartelette fine, confit of egg, barigoule emulsion and spices^ turbot, confit of fennel, potato tagliatelle, fish bone jus with saffron, rouille and pepper condiments.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3336434939	Le Stofflet - Château Colbert	Place du Château	France	Maulévrier	Car park,Garden or park	https://www.chateaucolbert.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This magnificent 17C tuffeau and granite château is already worth a visit for its rich chequered history and its 800m² cottage garden, voted the most beautiful cottage garden of France in 2016 and 2021. Guests are welcomed beneath a 13m-high dome, before progressing into one of two dining rooms, both of which sport high ceilings and crystal chandeliers. This glamorous interior is fully equal to the fine dining experience of contemporary cuisine: wafer-thin tartlet of aubergine caviar, prawns and radishes^ guinea fowl, herb butter, mashed potato and autumn veggies^ roast figs in port wine, almond cake, honey and vanilla ice cream.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3334166740	Aux Ateliers	115 avenue de la Vallée-des-Baux	France	Maussane-les-Alpilles	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This warm buzzy bistro with a vintage vibe is always packed to the rafters. The chef, a Normandy lad who fell in love with the Alpilles, titillates our tastebuds with generous, down-to-earth cooking: Provençal-style stuffed veggies^ terrine de campagne^ rabbit leg confit in olive oil^ shoulder of Maussane lamb baked all night long^ two-lemon pie with orange blossom. A regular clientele and a pétanque ground outside.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
3337886985	Chez Mathilde	97 route de Lugrin	France	Maxilly-sur-Léman	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-chez-mathilde.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Mathilde is the daughter of the famous fisherman of Lake Geneva, Eric Jacquier. She is now established in this cheerful eatery in the heart of the village with a concrete counter, off-kilter lighting and light wood bistro furnishings. Her slate menu resembles her spontaneous, playful and intuitive personality!	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3330667264	Le Saint-Nicolas - Au Coin du Feu	252 route de Rochebrune	France	Megève	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.coindufeu.com/fr/restaurant.html	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€€€	f	t	Snail ravioli from Magland, guinea fowl from the Ain, cheese trolley (100% Savoyard), baba in hay: young chef Marvin Lance, previously Julien Gatillon's sous-chef at Le 1920, is bringing a breath of fresh air to this pleasant chalet in Megève in the form of his technical skills and ambition. A restaurant whose star is in the ascendant in this ski resort!	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3334598243	Vous	36 rue Saint-François	France	Megève	Wheelchair access	http://www.juliengatillon.fr/vous	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	t	A gorgeous building typical of the sort you find in Megève, a refined decor with an abundance of wood, an elegant counter seating 14 diners: a warm welcome awaits you at Vous! Under the guidance of Julien Gatillon (previously at Le 1920), young chef Jean Pastre delights diners with modern cuisine prepared before their eyes. The finest local (and international) produce is used: vendace, watercress and caviar^ langoustine, potato and Savoy saffron^ farmhouse veal fillet, celery confit and lovage emulsion. Elegant, delicate dishes boasting clarity and bold flavours.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3330793651	Le Refuge	2615 route du Leutaz	France	Megève	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.refuge-megeve.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	After a hike to Le Leutaz, enjoy smiling service at this charming wood-panelled restaurant extended by a veranda as well as a terrace in fine weather. Tuck into generous and indulgent dishes taken from a menu that includes some of the absolute classics (egg with green lentils, morels and shavings of foie gras), without forgetting the perennial Savoie specialties.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3338756926	La Bodega	18 quai Hippolyte-Rossignol	France	Melun	Wheelchair access	https://bodega-melun.fr/	Nessun premio	Spanish	4.0	€€	t	f	Diners come here for the atmosphere and tastes of Spain, especially Asturias, where the family who own the place hail from. On the menu, you'll find top-notch ingredients, succulent Iberian recipes – Iberian pork pluma, paella bodega (chicken, chorizo, cuttlefish, mussels and prawns), salt cod with aïoli, delicious turrón for dessert – as well as some daily specials. You won't be disappointed!	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3332123008	Le Palace de Menthon	665 route des Bains	France	Menthon-Saint-Bernard	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view	https://www.palacedementhon.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	A vibrant colour scheme and an unrivalled view of the lake depict this smart, trendy restaurant which serves finely crafted bistronomic fare: foie gras and duck breast^ fillet of roast John Dory with seaweed butter^ Brittany shortcrust with exotic marmalade.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3335789591	Casa Fuego	80 bis boulevard de Garavan	France	Menton	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.casafuego.fr/	Nessun premio	Barbecue, Argentinian	5.0	€€	f	t	Just opposite Mauro Colgreco's flagship restaurant, this is the Italian-Argentine chef's hacienda-style Argentinian grill, which has a large covered terrace overlooking the sea, the town and the harbour. Here, they have mastered the style of cooking over a wood fire that is so typical of Argentina. Expect tasty dishes infused with a pleasing smokiness: aguachile San Remo white shrimps^ grilled octopus^ dulce de leche flan. A masterclass in gourmet conviviality.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3336009805	JR Bistronomie	11 rue Trenca	France	Menton	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.jr-bistronomie-restaurant-menton.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	3.0	€€	t	f	Just a stone's throw from the sea and the Jean Cocteau Museum, in a charming setting that calls to mind a family home (with one corner set up like a kids' playroom), this place serves good seasonal bistronomy food. Under the guidance of an experienced chef (also a member of the Disciples d'Escoffier), the classics are given a tasteful and intelligent modern spin. On this particular occasion, caramelised tomato tarte tatin^ confit saddle of lamb^ deconstructed lemon pavlova. Lovely fresh ingredients, a sure hand: JR works his magic!	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3333298568	La Coursive des Alpes	Galerie des Cîmes	France	Méribel	Air conditioning	https://www.meribel-restaurants.com/index.php/la-coursive-des-alpes.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Welcome to the ski resort’s former cinema, with a lounge bar on the ground-floor for snacks and a drink, and the restaurant proper up on the mezzanine. The chef cooks modern, tasty, well-crafted cuisine, such as toasted ham with truffles and Beaufort cheese^ sweetbread and buckwheat, harissa of carrots^ to finish, rum baba with orange preserve and vanilla cream. Charming welcome.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3334997707	Le 80	88 rue des Jeux-Olympiques	France	Méribel		https://www.chaudanne.com/fr/restaurant-bar-meribel-le-80	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Adorned in colourful hot-air balloons, Le 80 presents a patriotic culinary line-up of French traditions in well-crafted dishes: Richelieu pâté en croûte (porkpie), free-range pork chop smoked in hay or rose-scented praline meringues in a vanilla custard cream. More festive in the evenings. Follow in the footsteps of Jules Verne!	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3330600746	Le Cèpe	1827 Résidence Les Merisiers	France	Méribel	Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	It all starts with fine produce from the local land, mountain porcini or fish from the neighbouring lakes, which the chef comes out and proudly present to diners. He then turns it into delightful, fresh dishes, all the tastier for the unbeatable prices. A place that is quite simply comfortable in its own skin.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3331433700	Blisss	98 avenue de Magudas	France	Mérignac	Air conditioning	https://www.blisss.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€€	f	f	In the suburbs just outside Bordeaux, this modern restaurant proves to be a wonderful surprise. It has an intimate and immaculate decor featuring made-to-measure furniture and crockery that matches the ethos expressed in the food. Let Anthony Aycaguer transport you with his interactive menus, presented as a series of riddles based on seasonal produce (diners have to guess the ingredients). An unusual experience! Booking is essential.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3334917443	La Terrasse des Cigales	21 rue des Cigales	France	Mérindol	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	http://www.laterrassedescigales.fr	Nessun premio	Provençal	5.0	€€	t	t	Between the Durance River and the Sud Luberon, this modern restaurant lives up to its name with a lovely shaded terrasse enveloped by the sound of the cicadas (cigales)… plus, you get attentive, smiling service! Mathieu and Sébastien serve an appetising traditional Provence-inspired menu, as well as a daily special that is great value for money. The delicious dishes are carefully crafted with no messing around. The aim is to keep things simple, flavoursome and generous, while using selected regional ingredients: vegetables and olive oil from the village, lamb from the Alpilles, fish from the Bay of Cannes, beef from the Alpes-de-Haute-Provence. In winter, wood-fire cooking. A pleasant restaurant.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3336871638	Auberge Baechel-Brunn	3 route de Soultz	France	Merkwiller-Pechelbronn	Air conditioning	https://www.baechel-brunn.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	With Thomas in the kitchen and Esther in the dining room, the Limmacher’s restaurant is a family business! The chef favours premium ingredients, local whenever possible and concocts primarily traditional recipes with a welcome hint of creative modernity. For example, he proposes a new take of the familiar flammkuchen or adds a puff pastry Wellington-inspired spin to local venison, flanked by a gloriously velvety game sauce. The menu changes frequently, to the delight of the (numerous) regulars.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3334054586	Le Chiquito	3 rue de l'Oise	France	Méry-sur-Oise	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.lechiquito.fr/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	In a handsome 17C edifice, this restaurant continues to fly the flag of gourmet hospitality and upholds a distinctly bourgeois brand of elegance. Chef Anne-Sophie Godry has remained true to the establishment’s traditional Gallic ethos and its signature dishes, among which calf’s sweetbread with a frothy butter, sole meunière and Paris-Brest praliné à l'ancienne with a chicory custard. The front-of-house team is cheerful, competent and slick. Terrific wine list, with more than 400 references.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3334142785	Yozora	1 parvis des Droits-de-l'Homme	France	Metz	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-yozora.com	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€€	t	f	In the heart of the Centre Pompidou-Metz is one of the few fine dining restaurants to be located in a French museum. The sleek, bright space is housed in a glass and metal setting with glimpses of the canopy of this stunning building^ wood and cardboard furniture designed by Shigeru Ban adds to the serenity of the place. Roxane and Charles Coulombeau homed in on the smallest of details in a quest for excellence when it comes to the table design. A big fan of Japan, where he used to work, the chef cleverly combines seasonal ingredients from Lorraine with his passion for the Land of the Rising Sun. Quail from the Vosges, Lorraine-raised Wagyu beef and truffles from the Meuse blend seamlessly with chawanmushi, shiso and kaffir lime in this chef's inspired dishes.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3333141988	83 Restaurant	83 rue Mazelle	France	Metz	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.83restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Italian, Provençal	5.0	€€	t	t	A ten - minute walk from the Centre Pompidou - Metz, this pleasant restaurant showcases Italian food, through carefully selected ingredients (charcuterie, burrata, pasta, wild fish, purebred meats). And to accompany it all, a fine selection of Italin wines!	shirocky	\N	\N
3337263492	Derrière	17 rue de la Chèvre	France	Metz	Terrace	https://www.restaurant-derriere.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	A great surprise! The chef carefully prepares his appealing dishes without ever giving in to the latest fads, and maintaining a deep respect for the ingredients, as in these calf’s sweetbreads, roasted in butter and served with morel mushrooms. The small dining room to the rear (which gives the restaurant its name) is nicely decorated^ the service is relaxed. A delight from start to finish.	de santistobias	\N	\N
3338215900	La Réserve	5 avenue Ney	France	Metz	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lareserve-metz.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	In the 16C former garrison food storeroom, nowadays the Citadelle hotel, Aurélien Person’s cooking demonstrates a gourmet streak paired with a generous nature: stone-bass tartare with fennel, mange-tout and preserved lemon ^ seared scallops with chorizo and riso venere, fillet of beef with local bacon and carrots… A storeroom with plenty of surprises in store!	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3337132044	Le Jardin de Bellevue	58 rue Claude-Bernard	France	Metz	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.lejardindebellevue.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	The comfortable and elegant setting of this century-old building has been rejuvenated by the recent arrival of Élise and Paul Fabuel. He is the young chef who appeared on French TV's Objectif Top Chef, as well as completing stints at À Table in Metz and À l'Échevin in Colmar. Here, he serves up an attractive seasonal menu, eg a medley of pumpkin, roast chestnuts, Iberian ham and porcini, or turbot a la plancha, radishes, courgettes with mint and sauce vierge.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3338456771	Auberge du Rohan	20 route de Vannes	France	Meucon	Car park	http://www.aubergedurohan.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This traditional old Brittany farmhouse is located by the entrance to the Gulf of Morbihan Nature Park. Here, a self-taught chef welcomes his loyal patrons with traditional, carefully executed, hearty food: tuna gravlax, cairn and caper seasoning, nasturtium oil and caper croutons^ chicken supreme stuffed with spring vegetables, smoked at the last minute, and a punchy rosemary gravy. Lunchtime bistro menu on weekdays.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3334568939	Au Fil du Clos	1 rue de Mazeray	France	Meursault	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://aufilduclos.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	An old farmhouse in Meursault's vineyards, complete with a garden, terrace and pergola, is the charming setting for the restaurant of chef Jean-Christophe Moutet (previously at Pommard). Tartare of sea bream, royale with fresh herbs^ squab, rhubarb, in a sesame crust^ a handful of Burgundy classics: the chef's savoir-faire is as appetising as ever.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3332085296	Le Petit Mézériat	250 Grande-Rue	France	Mézériat	Wheelchair access	https://le-petit-mezeriat-restaurant.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	In a small village near Vonnas, the owner chef serves a bargain priced lunchtime menu and a surprise menu (in several stages) which varies according to the season and market availability, with a distinct fondness for locally sourced ingredients. All of which is served by cheerful Amandine, the chef’s spouse, in their spruce, tastefully appointed venue.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3334552175	La Maison de Mézos	Place de l'Église	France	Mézos	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-mezos.com/restaurant/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In a village set deep within the Landes forest, this restaurant boasts a façade with the red shutters that are so emblematic of the region. A fragrant pergola covered in jasmine leads to a charming covered terrace with mismatched furniture. Inside, the atmosphere is that of a rustic-style country house. The chef, who has gained a wealth of experience from his travels, rustles up cuisine that very much captures the zeitgeist, infused with creative details such as a lemon and caper ice cream to accompany the veal confit with tonnato sauce, or a mussel and red curry mayonnaise on the trout and peas.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3338298872	Le Bruadan	2 rue du Plessis	France	Millançay	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Jean-Charles Boulmier and Christelle Cauli (formerly of L'Épicurien) are clearly passionate about nature. Named in homage to the forest bordering the village where they have set up shop, their appealing modern restaurant has a decor with plenty of wooden features and a palette of green, as if better to evoke the region of Sologne. The chef, who has an impressive track record (L'Espérance with Marc Meneau, Le Grand Coeur in Méribel, La Villa in Calvi), follows the seasons closely with his mouth-watering dishes: fish mousse, mussels and pig's trotter^ pork filet mignon, polenta and corn. A warm welcome and smiling service.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3336185069	Relais Chantovent	17 Grand-Rue	France	Minerve	Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.relaischantovent-minerve.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	A charming country inn in Cathar, where diners and pilgrims alike arrive on foot, eager to do justice to meat dishes that simmer for hours, illustrated by 24-hour low-temperature roast pork, or 20-hour leg of lamb roasted at 70°C. All the ingredients come solely from the surrounding local markets. The terrace with its view over the Briant valley is sumptuous.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3334006724	Le Montaigu - Domaine de la Bretesche	Rue du Château	France	Missillac	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.bretesche.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	The outhouses of Bretesche castle, an imposing medieval behemoth, are home to a plush dining room which overlooks the grounds and lake. Delightful bar in the former stables. The chef signs a score that caters to modern palates: Brittany scallops, parsnips, coffee^ locally grown carrots, Brière honey and cardamon orange.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3331430318	Òliba	Château de Riell	France	Molitg-les-Bains	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.chateauderiell.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Set deep in the Catalan Pyrenees, this refined restaurant in a romantic hotel serves flavoursome cuisine inspired by the surrounding countryside and locally picked produce: the local version of chimichurri sauce with mountain herbs exudes aromas of wild dill and burnet flowers. To be enjoyed on the terrace or in front of the picture windows, as you contemplate the snow-capped summit of Mount Canigou in the distance.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3331840654	Song Qi	7 avenue Princesse-Grace	France	Monaco	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.song-qi.mc/	Nessun premio	Asian, Chinese	5.0	€€€	t	f	Opposite Grimaldi Forum, this swanky, gourmet Chinese restaurant has opted for premium materials and a serene atmosphere. The appetising menu offers a vast array of Chinese cuisine from Peking soup with smoked chicken to crispy dragon prawns with Chinese mustard or the classic dim sum. Bookings advisable!	leonechristian	\N	\N
3331798387	Em Sherif	Hôtel de Paris	France	Monaco	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.montecarlosbm.com/fr/restaurant-monaco/em-sherif-monte-carlo	Nessun premio	Lebanese	4.0	€€€€	t	t	A welcome opportunity to celebrate the pleasures of Lebanese cuisine, the Mediterranean and, of course, the philosophy of sharing. In the kitchen, chef Yasmina Hayek (who has worked at the Institut Paul Bocuse and the restaurants of Mathieu Pacaud, Jean-François Piège and Rasmus Kofoed at Geranium in Copenhagen) skilfully juggles the traditional and the modern, in dishes such as her excellent lentil salad (addas) or her delicious aubergine fatteh with yoghurt. Aromas, colours, flavours – a culinary voyage of the senses out on the panoramic terrace or in a chic bistro-style dining area on the ground floor of the Hôtel de Paris.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3336338958	Elsa	Monte-Carlo Beach	France	Monaco	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.montecarlosbm.com/fr/restaurant-monaco/elsa	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	Established in the Monte Carlo Beach, a magnificent 1930s luxury hotel, revamped by designer India Mahdavi in a subtle Riviera vein, the culinary lineup is the work of executive chef Marcel Ravin (two stars at the Blue Bay Marcel Ravin). Talented, Italian-born chef Domenico D’Antonio sets the seafood score to music, calling upon first-class produce from the Mediterranean along the way: spider crab, white asparagus, yuzu, kiwi and fennel^ John Dory, sorrel sabayon, ravioli stuffed with leeks and shellfish. Everything serves a purpose in this repertory which aims to highlight each ingredient courtesy of intelligent, high-impact seasonings. The quintessence of fine dining on a terrace facing the sea.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3336293684	La Table d'Élise	2 rue du Portier	France	Monaco	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.latabledelise.mc	Nessun premio	Provençal	3.0	€€€	f	f	This swish, fashionable brasserie, located a stone's throw from Monaco’s Japanese Garden and the Grimaldi Forum, welcomes diners in a modern, spacious interior with pop music playing in the background. The Provençal cuisine, prepared with fine seasonal ingredients, is spot on, unfussy, generous and tasty. It is always a pleasure to watch the action in the open-plan kitchen. Excellent lunch deal.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3332685179	MayaBay	24 avenue Princesse-Grace	France	Monaco	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.mayabayrestaurant.com/monaco	Nessun premio	Thai, Japanese	3.0	€€€€	t	t	This establishment combines a Japanese and a Thai restaurant with a single Asian ambience, depicted by contemporary glitz and soft music. High-quality ingredients, well-judged spices and a shared price and quality^ all you have to do is choose between perfumed or minimalist cuisine.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3332121519	Éléonore	5 rue Saint-Pierre	France	Monpazier	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hoteledward1er.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This elegant restaurant is housed in a pretty little château, which has the art of hospitality down to a T. The globetrotting chef welcomes you with a menu presented in two sections: one “classical” which features a traditional lineup, while the other is more “unusual” with creative twists.	berninialex	\N	\N
3333075598	Côté Mas	Route de Villeveyrac	France	Montagnac	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cote-mas.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This inviting restaurant in the heart of a winery is appealingly appointed with contemporary objets d'art and exotic wood furnishings and overlooks the Cévennes. The perfect foil to sample contemporary bistronomic cuisine: duck magret, spicy jus, roast melon in elderflower^ panacotta flavoured with lavender honey, apricots and a dairy mousse. Most of the produce is local and seasonal, like the lovely fruity olive oil which is produced on the estate. A fine list of wines from the estate and nearby vineyards, and an impressive selection of wines by the glass.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3334142024	La Réserve du Presbytère	22 Grand-Rue	France	Montagne	Car park,Terrace	https://www.lareservedupresbytere.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Opposite the Romanesque church of a wine-growing village is this eatery serving bistronomy dishes. Diners savour traditional flavours in a decor comprising bistro tables and industrial chairs set up against a backdrop of exposed stone walls. The delicious desserts deserve a special mention: amandine tartlet with figs, raspberry confit and sorbet. Pleasant terrace to the rear.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3333593417	Königshafen	Alte Dorfstraße 1	Germany	List	Car park,Terrace	https://www.koenigshafen.de/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking	3.0	€€	f	f	The journey up to the north of the island is well worth it! Here, family tradition dates back to 1881, with the fifth generation currently looking after this spruce house with a white-brick façade, serving good regional and seasonal cuisine. Nice garden terrace behind the house. Tip: They are always well booked, so you should book early!	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3335093328	L'Atelier	2 rue Neuve	France	Montaigu	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-la-robe.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Xavier Giraudet, chef at La Robe, has opened a second establishment in a bistro vein. Diners know they are in safe hands here as they tuck into traditional, flavourful and generous cuisine: succulent and aromatic pâté en croûte, melt-in-the-mouth black pudding with mashed potatoes, and a dessert inspired by the Paris-Brest, which is as indulgent as they come. You get up from your table with a smile on your face and your finances intact, thanks to the affordable set menus at lunch and dinner. A bright and modern setting^ friendly service from the cheerful waitstaff.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3334404310	Le Clos Perché	Le Bourg	France	Montarcher	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://leclosperche.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€	f	f	Once upon a time, there was an inn on the high plateaux of the Monts du Forez, set at an altitude of 1 150m. It is here, on the edge of this tiny village, that Julien Magne has set up shop. In the kitchen, this chef creates colourful, inventive cuisine with a playful approach that brings a smile to your face!	giulianijames	\N	\N
3339077182	La Gloire	74 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Montargis	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.lagloire-montargis.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	A venerable Montargis institution, located alongside the N7. For several generations, culinary tradition has been revisited with flair and generosity^ do not miss out on the rather imposing dessert trolley.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3333532773	Nous	7 rue Bessières	France	Montauban	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-nous.fr/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€	t	f	In this modern bistro overflowing in feel-good vibes, Raphaël and Elise Campas treat the foodies of Montauban to a culinary festival, all made in-house, from the bread to the ice cream. Taking their cue from the seasons, the experienced couple conscientiously selects regional ingredients (vegetables from independent market gardeners and farmstead cheeses), which the chef crafts into colourful, appetising dishes. Élise professionally and seamlessly manages the front of house, while Raphaël pops out from time to time to lend a hand and wax lyrical about his cooking. This excellent establishment, only open for lunch, offers a concise menu that changes monthly, giving you the perfect excuse to return again and again.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3337655476	Du Bruit en Cuisine	12 allée Mortarieu	France	Montauban	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://dubruitencuisine.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A chef who trained in several Ducasse establishments is at work in this genuine gourmet bolthole. Mathieu Lévèque creates up-to-the-minute, deceptively spontaneous cuisine in the shape of small, tapas-inspired dishes. This veteran chef has a knack with jus, sauces and spot-on cooking, illustrated by his confit of ox cheeks garnished with mushroom and celeriac gnocchis. The venue sometimes hosts musical evenings, adding a festive dimension to the venue. As it goes from strength to strength, we are likely to hear more from this boisterous kitchen.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3331727573	Les 5 Bouchons	24 place Nationale	France	Montauban	Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€	f	f	A pleasant restaurant for lunch beneath the arcades of Place Nationale, Montauban's architectural pride and joy. The name refers to the five members of the family of experienced chef David Soulier, who works with his wife Joan front of house. Every fortnight, a new seasonal menu showcases well-sourced local ingredients in straightforward, colourful and tasty dishes, for example roasted hazelnuts grown in Tarn-et-Garonne that accompany the beetroot hummus, or the sticks of celeriac and mustard seed pickles served with the pork loin cooked for five hours. Whether seated on the terrace or in the long room with its vaulted ceiling overlooking the kitchen, you'll have an enjoyable meal without breaking the bank.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3335548147	Le Carré d'Ange	2169 quartier Narbonne	France	Montauroux	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-carredange.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	This updated, airy Provençal inn outside town provides the perfect foil for generous, throbbingly good Mediterranean food. Examples include a mouthwatering breast of guinea fowl and truffles with girolles and a millefeuille of potatoes. Served on a pretty patio in fine weather.	naldinadia	\N	\N
3332702150	Le Saint-Martin	1 rue du Général-Leclerc	France	Montbéliard		https://www.le-saint-martin.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Olivier Prevot - Carme's flavoursome cuisine is all about the ingredients. He uses each one in a straightforward way but the apparent simplicity is misleading, as the recipes, cooking and seasoning bring out all of the flavour within. Nothing pretentious, nothing complicated, nothing but pleasure!	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3336279895	Apicius	29 rue Martin-Bernard	France	Montbrison	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://apicius-restaurant-montbrison.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This dinky city-centre eatery is run by a young couple with an enviable track record. In a recently refurbished chic trendy interior, you will sample market-fresh cuisine at unbeatable prices at lunchtime and a more elaborate menu on Friday evenings. The chef makes the most of local ingredients as well as wildflowers and plants. The epitome of generous!	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3339129903	Jérôme Brochot	7 place Beaubernard	France	Montceau-les-Mines	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.jeromebrochot.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Jérôme Brochot concocts a set menu made with market-fresh produce that changes on a weekly basis and comprises several courses. He works with excellent produce: green asparagus, lobster, turbot etc. They offer a cookery class on Sunday mornings.	paganialex	\N	\N
