3330938083	Le 4	5 rue Bonbonnière	France	Mulhouse	Terrace	https://restaurantle4.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	The young couple at the head of this dinky establishment in the heart of Mulhouse rustles up a concise menu of enticingly entitled dishes. The food is colourful, inventive and scattered with Mediterranean notes: “our version” of vitello tonnato^ gilt-head seabream, spaghetti alle vongole and an emulsion of cockles^ tagliata of beef, baby potatoes, rocket salad, Kalamata olives and shavings of parmesan. Enticing wine list.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3334912321	Auberge aux 4 Saisons	40 Grand'rue	France	Munster		https://www.auberge4saisonsmunster.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Beyond the threshold of this large regional-style 1920s building with oriel and stained-glass windows is a lovely, inviting restaurant. Venison pâté en croûte^ roasted pike-perch fillet, Brussels sprouts and chestnuts^ clementine jelly, melt-in-the-mouth sponge and chestnut ice cream: the young chef delights diners with his seasonal ingredients from start to finish. A short wine list with a focus on organic and biodynamic wines^ possibility of gin and tonic pairings (with local gins of course!).	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3331311679	Le Jarrousset	RN 122	France	Murat	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-le-jarrousset.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In a lush green setting, this recently restored inn is a champion of local produce, illustrated by the chef’s painstakingly selected network of nearby farms and producers. Meals are served in a pared-down, modern interior, whose furniture and tableware is the work of local artisans. Let yourself be guided by the expert tips of the knowledgeable sommelière.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3335428326	L'Auberge du Château	Le Bourg	France	Muret-le-Château	Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.laubergeduchateau.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	This restaurant opposite the town hall in an Aveyron village is well known to food lovers, who come here to enjoy contemporary cuisine which places the onus on herbs and vegetables. The dishes are colourful and flavoursome. Lovely flower - filled terrace.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3337011678	ROS[O]	22 rue Maurice-Berne	France	Mûrs-Erigné	Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	The name is a play on words referring to the reeds (roseaux) on the banks of the Louet, overlooked by this restaurant's delightful terrace. Quail eggs, Comté cheese and courgettes make for a fresh, well-seasoned dish^ tender Duroc pork chop cooked rare, served with Noirmoutier new potatoes and vegetables – chef Tony Pasquier (formerly of Casa Corneille in the centre of Angers) knows the ingredients and the seasons inside out. He has a knack for coming up with mouth-watering dishes for you to enjoy in this bright, modern space.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3331167862	La Toq'	1 rue Monseigneur-Trouillet	France	Nancy	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.latoq.fr/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	The professional, highly experienced, virtuoso chef crafts high-flying dishes using top-notch ingredients: smoked to order slab of salmon with cauliflower and French caviar^ Alsace poultry, Agria potatoes, roasted leeks and a velvety Albufera sauce… These flavoursome delicacies are served in a plush, fancy interior enhanced by century-old stone walls. Fine wine list.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3339025153	Cadet	3 rue du Sergent-Blandan	France	Nancy		https://restaurant-cadet.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Between the Villa Majorelle and the Musée de l'École de Nancy, this restaurant is housed in a hundred-year-old former hairdressing salon. In a Scandinavian-style interior, brightened up by crates of vegetables, a few trendy cookery books and a vintage Faema coffee machine behind the counter, chef Theo Mareschal (previously encountered at La Maison dans le Parc in Nancy and Kontrast in Oslo) sticks to the brief and cooks up appealing contemporary cuisine that's simple and accessible, a case in point being the veal, mushrooms and baby potatoes or the surprising dessert of vanilla ice cream with squid ink, as black as a painting by Pierre Soulages!	marinescumario	\N	\N
3338642673	Le 27 Gambetta	27 rue Gambetta	France	Nancy	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.le27gambetta.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€	t	t	Cod simmered in olive oil, butternut purée and bacon powder, or young pigeon with creamy sweet potatoes and foamy mashed potatoes: the chef crafts delicate bistro fare to which he adds his own personal signature, two minutes from Place Stanislas.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3330220994	Le Capu	31 rue Gambetta	France	Nancy	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lecapu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In an ideal location 300m from Place Stanislas, this restaurant boasts an elegant decor in a bold, contemporary vein, enhanced by baroque notes (rich hues and crushed velvet). The cuisine is suitably generous – for example, filet mignon of veal, with aubergine caviar, grilled courgettes and a tarragon sauce.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3331753040	Patern	60 rue Stanislas	France	Nancy		https://patern-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This superlatively located eatery is only a 5-minute walk from Stanislas Square! In a smart, modern interior, Martin Debuiche, former deputy of Jean-Pierre Vigato of the Apicius in Paris, crafts surprise menus based on flawlessly sourced premium ingredients: fish from Brittany, Vosges pigeon, dairy produce from Meurthe-et-Moselle, saffron from Lorraine, etc. Examples include frothy potatoes, Oscietra caviar from Aquitaine and a bay leaf emulsion, or blowtorch-seared Brittany mackerel garnished with fish bone powder and sautéed girolles.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3335319841	Racine	9 rue Stanislas	France	Nancy	Terrace	http://www.racine-nancy.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Located just a stone's throw from Place Stanislas, the restaurant of the young chef Martin Debuiche (formerly Pierre Vigato's second-in-command, at Apicius) and his partner, butcher and restaurateur Alexandre Polmard, offers market cuisine through a short and appetising menu. The ingredients are good quality, the recipes are well put together. Tasty.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3330507550	Transparence - La Table de Patrick Fréchin	28 rue Stanislas	France	Nancy	Terrace	https://www.restaurant-transparence.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	A short walk from Place Stanislas in a busy pedestrian street, transparency is more than just a name and you can actually see chef Patrick Fréchin working his magic in the theatrically visible kitchen. His enticing dishes showcase premium seasonal ingredients, such as loin of skrei cod, roasted in bay leaf oil with mead-flavoured yoghurt.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3334679700	Song, Saveurs & Sens	5 rue Santeuil	France	Nantes	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-song.fr/	Nessun premio	Asian Contemporary	4.0	€€	f	f	Self-taught chef Nhung Phung was born in Vietnam, but grew up in Laos, Cambodia and Thailand. The aromas and perfumes of her childhood have forged her culinary identity: sensitive, intelligent, balanced cuisine, poised between Southeast Asia and France, delicately spicy and crafted with premium produce. The interior sports a striking blend of turquoise, black and wrought iron – a fine setting for a sensibly priced meal.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3338307644	Vacarme	5 rue des Bons-Français	France	Nantes	Terrace	https://vacarme-nantes.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€	t	t	Chef Sarah Mainguy, who won French TV's Top Chef, has set up shop with her partner in this Nantes bistro with a cool, laid-back atmosphere and where everyone seems to be in a good mood. Renewed on a weekly basis, the bistronomy menu alone is enough to bring a smile to the face of any foodie: leek ravioli, anchovy cream^ home-made sausage, rutabaga purée, citrus jus^ cabbage stuffed with octopus and pork. Good list of natural, organic and biodynamic wines.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3330583550	Freia	22 boulevard de Berlin	France	Nantes	Great view,Wheelchair access	http://www.freia-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€	t	f	This greenhouse with timber arches devoted to the goddess Freia is perched on top of a contemporary building. It is the perfect place to grow a garden of aromatic herbs and berries and to admire the panoramic view of Nantes. After the success of Vacarme, Sarah Mainguy crafts poetic and creative cuisine, mainly plant based and scattered with Scandinavian and Asian touches. Each dish is a treasure trove of brainwaves and delicious sauces – cases in point being the white asparagus with a vegetable seaweed XO sauce, or periwinkles with crisp green peas, topped with a glazed gwell snow.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3331727279	Omija	54 rue Fouré	France	Nantes	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.omija.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	t	f	At the helm of his own restaurant since 2019 and with a splendid starred experience under his belt, Romain Bonnet crafts a creative surprise menu of Asian inspiration: the ‘omija’ is a Korean berry known to feature the five ‘flavours’ in perfect harmony. Romain is unswerving in his dedication to taste: radish and seaweed gnocchi brilliantly play on acidic notes as shrimp adds a well-judged spicy edge. Flawlessly cooked, gutsy stocks and irresistible big-boned sauces. The produce, mostly organic, is painstakingly sourced (common shrimp from la Cotinière, Oléron Island, line-caught pollack, Vendée squab). An infectiously cosy eatery with unstarched, yet seamless service.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3337328290	Sépia	1 quai Turenne	France	Nantes	Terrace	https://www.sepia-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	f	t	Lucie Berthier Gembara, riding high from her appearance on France's Top Chef TV competition, often has a full house at her trendy designer bistro on the ground floor of this fine 18C building. After stints working with Gérald Passedat and Alexandre Mazzia, she has retained a clear sense of creativity and an appetite for the Eastern influences of the Mediterranean basin. Her dishes, such as aubergines with charred baba ganoush, eggnog and feta crumble, are full of pleasant surprises. They are distinctly playful, going against the grain when it comes to the codes of gastronomy but no less tasty for it. The lighter lunchtime menu is expanded in the evening.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3331213406	Les Chants d'Avril	2 rue Laennec	France	Nantes	Terrace		Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€	t	f	The enthusiasm of chef Christophe François is infectious. Every day brings his own appealing and confident bistronomy-style take on market-fresh cuisine. Fine ingredients from the region are showcased in surprise set menus (without options), served in a pleasant bistro setting. As for the wine, try some of the surprising picks in their selection, to be tasted blind. A sociable experience!	beckerradu	\N	\N
3333680199	Bairoz	40 bis rue Fouré	France	Nantes		https://bairoz-nantes.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Just a stone's throw from the River Loire, this charming, modern restaurant sports a striking decor: pendant lights, wood panelling and exposed stonework. At the helm are chef Estelle Méheust and pastry chef Jérôme Berdelou, both of whom are active in the kitchen as well as the dining room: one starts the service while the starters and main courses are being served, the other taking over when it comes to the desserts. This charming, discreet couple won us over with their market-fresh fare at lunchtime, and their more high-level cuisine at dinner. The jus are particularly tasty, eg the mushroom emulsion on the raviolo filled with brousse soft cheese, or the creamy bisque on the hake, saffron purple top turnips and fondant potatoes.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3335117471	L'Abélia	125 boulevard des Poilus	France	Nantes	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.restaurantlabelia.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Chef Vincent Berthomeau and his spouse Pascale have set up shop in an edifice dating from 1900 that is slightly outside the city centre of Nantes. Their handsome mansion is further enhanced by a conservatory, a terrace and a garden. The regulars return for the chef’s generous seasonal score and his menus vary depending on what he finds on his frequent forays to Talensac market. Enticing dishes such as a cassolette of langoustines and pleurote mushrooms in a flavoursome seafood stock or an exquisite chocolate, butterscotch and caramelised peanut tartlet, further jazzed up by a carrot sorbet and carrot coulis.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3337968863	Lamaccotte	7 rue Saint-Denis	France	Nantes		https://www.lamaccotte-restaurant-nantes.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Generosity, flavour and good ingredients are the elements underpinning Maxime Fillaut's cuisine, which reaps the rewards of his time at La Mare aux Oiseaux and Le Clarence in Paris. The restaurant occupies a modern, light and airy ground-floor space in a stone building in the historical city centre. The menu changes daily, reflecting the produce available at the market, and the dishes are beautifully presented. This is simple and delicious food: fondant home-made gnocchi, vegetable tops and roasted almond pistou^ vegetable carbonara, parmesan emulsion, paprika-glazed celery and helianthis^ meadowsweet parfait glacé, blossom honey and lemon marmalade, buckwheat sablé and caramelised dried fruit. Fast, well-paced service.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3331240790	Le Bouchon	7 rue Bossuet	France	Nantes	Terrace	https://www.le-bouchon-nantes.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Appetising, up - to - the - minute food, reinvented daily, a prettily appointed interior (terracotta tile floors, old beams and mirrors) and the wonderful terrace, which is a haven of greenery in the town centre. It isn’t difficult to understand why this establishment is so popular with Nantes’ inhabitants!	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3336767761	Maison Bagarre	6 rue Jean-Jacques Rousseau	France	Nantes		http://www.maison-bagarre.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This restaurant in the Graslin neighbourhood is often booked up, so it's best to reserve. The chef makes the most of the extensive network of producers (especially market gardeners) operating in Nantes to create an appealing bistronomy menu. The rather original contemporary setting (over two levels) is very attractive, especially the dining area on the large mezzanine overlooking the open kitchen.	haascamilla	\N	\N
