3330841591	Auberge de la Roussille	30 impasse de la Roussille	France	Niort	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.laroussille.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	One can't help but fall under the spell of this fine lock - keeper's house, which stands in the bucolic setting on the banks of the Sèvre. An enchanting environment, but that doesn't eclipse the main focus, which is the chef's meticulous and well - calibrated cooking. Ingredients are top notch and enhanced without frills. A real pleasure.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3332426957	Le Cercle	374 rue Nationale	France	Nœux-les-Mines	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-lamaisonrouge.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Deftly crafted dishes, high-quality ingredients and cheerful service: it is a delight to eat at Le Cercle. Some of our favourites include snails in garlic and an emulsion of potatoes^ turbot with sand carrots and langoustine bisque. Elegant contemporary artwork graces the interior that is both chic and cosy.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3335385139	La Maison des Toqués	26 rue de la Prée-aux-Ducs	France	Noirmoutier-en-l'Île		https://www.lamaisondestoques.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€€	f	f	Aurore and Sébastien Duchenne share the same passion for top-quality regional produce, often organic, which they transform into delicious recipes that capture the zeitgeist and are inspired by market availability. As you enter, you are greeted by a colourful, modern interior whose blue and white walls are adorned with artwork, providing the perfect foil to elegantly plated ingredients such as lobster, local oysters, John Dory or royal Charmilles pigeon. Booking highly advisable.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3337635294	L'Étier	Route de l'Épine	France	Noirmoutier-en-l'Île	Car park	https://www.restaurant-letier.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	t	f	Between the road and the étier (a seawater channel) onto which the conservatory backs, this characteristic island house showcases splendid local seafood: grilled lobster, wild turbot cooked on the bone, sole meunière, marsh eels in garden herbs, without forgetting the desserts, soufflé au Grand Marnier or Paris-Brest pastry – to die for! The food of a genuine craftsman – fresh and oozing with flavour.	krausmartina	\N	\N
