3330695725	Gric	8 rue des Halles	France	Orléans	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantgric.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Marie Gricourt's career has already taken her to the heights of Christophe Hay's La Table d'à Côté, where she was head chef. She has since opened her own restaurant, a convivial place in keeping with her personality. In this restaurant not far from the banks of the River Loire, the chef and her mainly female team (who provide service with a smile) put a new twist on bistro-style cuisine, simply and precisely: a surf and turf starter with scallops cradled in a sweet potato, bacon and prune purée^ conchiglioni stuffed with beef chuck and porcini^ and for dessert a delicious floating island with citrus fruit, honey and pollen.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3333771258	La Dariole	25 rue Étienne-Dolet	France	Orléans	Terrace	http://www.ladariole.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	In the heart of the old town and not far from the cathedral, this 15C half-timbered house showcases an easy alliance of old stonework and cosy touches. The chef, who even trained here when he was learning his trade, hits the mark with delicious cuisine that is in tune with the times. The seasonal menu changes regularly and features appealingly tasty dishes such as pork chop with potatoes and a caper jus.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3339949516	La Maison	32 rue de l'Horloge	France	Orthez	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamaisondelhorloge.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	In a pedestrianised street in the centre of Orthez, this vast bistro is housed in what was once a fishmonger's shop. The interior decor features disparate decorative objects picked up here and there (the same goes for the plates and cups) – so it's undeniably cosy. In a packed and buzzy dining room, tuck into red cabbage, served raw and cooked, shavings of cured ham and sesame vinaigrette^ a must-try braised beef chuck, fondant carrots and a tasty jus^ and the classic riz au lait, salted caramel and nougatine. The single set lunch menu changes on a weekly basis. At weekends and in the evenings, there is no set menu but a short à la carte menu with starters to share and dishes that, although still in the bistro vein, are prepared with slightly higher grade ingredients (line-caught hake, PGI duck etc).	palombogiada	\N	\N
3335991945	À l'Aigle d'Or	14 rue de Gerstheim	France	Osthouse	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelalaferme.com/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	At one corner of this imposing village house, the wrought-iron eagle seems to herald your arrival. Inside, tuck into classic dishes (home-made goose foie gras terrine with port jelly, Paul Haeberlin's mousseline of frogs’ legs, sole meunière prepared tableside…) in a traditional and inviting setting. Less formal atmosphere in the winstub.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
