3333606778	Signature Montmartre	12 rue des Trois-Frères	France	Paris		https://signature-montmartre.fr/	Nessun premio	Fusion	5.0	€€	t	t	Located in touristy Montmartre, this Lilliputian restaurant sports a minimalist interior and a buzzy vibe. At the helm of the restaurant, that is fully deserving of its success, is a Franco-Korean couple (bookings highly recommended). He warmly welcomes diners, proffering insightful wine tips along the way, while she deploys her pastry talents in the kitchen. The Franco-Asian repertory quietly feeds you well, courtesy of intelligent recipes scattered in subtle aromas, illustrated by a tataki of bonito with cucumber pickles, a watercress crepe and a vitello tonnato sauce jazzed up with mint – flavoursome and surprising! Consider us smitten!	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3337192497	Etsi	23 rue Eugène-Carrière	France	Paris	Terrace	https://www.etsi-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	€€	f	t	Mikaela Liaroutsos, a young chef of Greek origin, has returned to the cuisine of her childhood, after learning the ropes in prestigious establishments. At étsi, she rolls out strikingly fresh mezze with bold touches such as roast cauliflower, anchovies and Serifos capers or scallops in a pistachio butter of mizithra and tarragon – to die for and the antithesis of clichéd! The feta, olives, capers, charcuterie, cheese and olive oil are all imported straight from Greece. Don’t even try to resist the warm, friendly vibe!	orlandofernando	\N	\N
3332655713	L'Ouzeri	41 rue du Ruisseau	France	Paris		http://www.etsi-paris.fr/l-ouzeri	Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	€€	t	f	Saganaki cheese, gyro merida, myzithropita (cheesecake), spanakopita – the menu gives it away: this is French-Greek chef Mikaela Liaroutsos's Greek taverna, and it's just a stone's throw from the original restaurant Etsi that made her name. The food is served as a series of mezes, to savour as you dream of Greek holidays, past or future. The traditional songs playing in the background might tempt you to pull out a sirtaki step after a glass of ouzo.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3336496745	Les Délices d'Aphrodite	4 rue de Candolle	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.mavrommatis.com/les-delices-daphrodite/	Nessun premio	Greek	3.0	€€	t	t	In this charming tavern-style restaurant, you could be forgiven for thinking you are in Greece! Freshly made, sun-drenched dishes such as marinated peppers, spit-roasted leg of lamb on a skewer, etc., all prepared with top-notch ingredients.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3335744882	Osmossi - Maison Mavrommatis	70 avenue Paul-Doumer	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.mavrommatis.com/	Nessun premio	Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	One of the restaurants of Andreas Mavrommatis, maestro of Mediterranean food in Paris. In a contemporary bistro-style interior, decorated with photos from Nikos Aliagas' collection, diners enjoy meze, pan-fried octopus with fava from Santorini or soudjoukakia (beef meatballs with tomato and cumin). It's fresh and tasty. Delicatessen and wine shop.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3335269901	Clover Grill	6 rue Bailleul	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://jeanfrançoispiege.com/clover-grill	Nessun premio	Grills	4.0	€€€	t	t	Mouthwatering dry - aged meats – Baltic black beef, Bavarian beef, Blonde d'Aquitaine, Black Angus – take pride of place in the window, drawing in diners keen to try them for themselves. From the starters to the desserts, everything is cooked over coals or roasted on a spit, giving the dining experience its own particular flavour. A great success.	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3338511156	Sharma Ji	16 rue Frémicourt	France	Paris	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://sharmaji.fr	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	€€	f	t	At the helm of several establishments, Manoj Sharma has boldly set about freeing Indian food from its hackneyed clichés (like the predictable tandoori or korma chicken). In a spruce, modern, colourful venue, his authentic bistronomic cooking delves into an Indian score that has shaken off its traditional visual and technical fetters. Examples include masala fried chicken, with coconut and curry leaves^ long sweet peppers stuffed with masala cheese and yoghurt sauce^ caramelised ginger cake. Simmered and crafted with lashings of spices and aromatic herbs, Manoj’s delicious dishes nonetheless find favour with delicate western palates. The lunch menu is a bargain. The à la carte menu changes regularly.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3337338515	Tavline	25 rue du Roi-de-Sicile	France	Paris	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.tavline.fr/	Nessun premio	Israeli	4.0	€€	t	t	Between Saint-Paul and Hôtel de Ville, a slice of Tel Aviv, a taste of Morocco, a hint of Lebanon – such is the formula of Tavline. Spices supplied by Shuk Ha'Carmel, the largest market in Tel Aviv, adorn the fine cuisine served here, including ksitsot daguim – grilled fish balls with herbs and spices on a bed of lentils with yoghurt and candied lemon, or the memorable memoulam (onions stuffed with lamb), a recipe passed down to the chef from his mother.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3330680983	Adami	19 bis rue Pierre-Fontaine	France	Paris	Counter dining	http://www.adamiparis.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	f	t	This small Italian pasta restaurant breaks away from traditional trattoria fare, embracing a more contemporary approach – an inspired idea reflected in the sleek, modern decor and the long counter from which diners watch the kitchen team at work. Dishes to share and a warm, convivial atmosphere are all part of the experience here. The Italian chef, who has an impressive track record, delivers fresh cuisine that abounds in bold flavours. A case in point is his vitello tonnato-style veal, artichoke and black garlic, or his incredibly indulgent ricotta gnocchi in a creamy courgette sauce. The lunch menu is appealing, as are the mouthwatering à la carte options.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3333892349	Ciasa Mia	19 rue Laplace	France	Paris	Interesting wine list	https://www.ciasamia.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	t	f	Originally from northern Italy (the Dolomites, to be precise), Francesca and Samuel Mocci like to highlight their culinary heritage, which proves to be as delicious as it is surprising. The dishes exude authenticity, as does the space, designed in a cosy little chalet spirit. An appealing place.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3335245705	Cucina Mutualité	20 rue Saint-Victor	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.cucina-mutualite.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	f	t	The colourful modern bistro decor and extremely cordial staff make for an appealing atmosphere. As for the food, the wonderful seasonal Italian menu is a pageant of authentic, flavourful and truly generous dishes: you won't be disappointed by the melt-in-the-mouth braised ox cheek paccheri... al dente, obviously! You may even be allowed a second helping.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3331557826	Emporio Armani Caffè	149 boulevard Saint-Germain	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.armani.com/fr-fr/experience/armani-restaurant	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€	f	f	Just across from the famous Les Deux Magots, this smart contemporary-style brasserie on the ground floor of the Michelin-starred Armani/Ristorante is run at a brisk pace by the same Italian team. From verdure alla griglia drizzled with Apulian olive oil, linguine alle vongole veraci – cooked al dente and served with a delicious helping of bottarga – to classic tiramisu with a light and full-flavoured mascarpone cream, as well as spaghetti al pomodoro, ravioli del plin, risotto, tortellini: all the classics of Italian cuisine are present and correct, executed in time-honoured tradition.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3337702501	La Flamiche	20 place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville	France	Roye	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.laflamiche.fr/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	A classical interior lies behind the large windows of La Flamiche. Here, cuisine with robust traditional foundations is enhanced by a touch of modernity: one example would be the duck foie gras and smoked trout in a Granny Smith jelly, cucumber pickles and apple chutney – a beautifully crafted starter. Then there are the medallions of monkfish with lime, carrot and rocket, perfectly cooked in butter, the good old-fashioned way.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3331636781	Auberge Nicolas Flamel	51 rue de Montmorency	France	Paris		https://auberge.nicolas-flamel.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	The oldest house in Paris (1407) is named after a learned bourgeois who dabbled in alchemy, one Nicolas Flamel. In a pared-back tasteful interior set off by old stones and timber rafters, the high-flying kitchen brigade of Alan Geaam is hard at work crafting premium ingredients into appetising dishes in the zeitgeist: Plouguerneau crab, Baeri caviar^ Racan pigeon, chard, buckwheat^ confit of citrus fruits in a lime jelly.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3332716186	Il Ristorante - Niko Romito	Hôtel Bulgari	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.bulgarihotels.com/fr_FR/paris/dining/il-ristorante-niko-romito	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€€	f	t	Niko Romito, a chef from Abruzzo with three Michelin stars to his name, updates the classics of Italian cooking in a menu that really homes in on the produce and dares to go light (easy on the fat, limited sauces, steamed ingredients, rice starch for the breadcrumb coating etc). The saffron risotto with parmesan is subtle and does not weigh on the stomach, as is the magnificent veal cutlet alla Milanese, to be savoured in this elegantly sleek dining area that opens onto the interior garden.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3332869747	L'Assaggio	Castille Paris	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://collezione.starhotels.com/fr/nos-hotels/castille/restaurant-et-bar/restaurant-lassaggio.html	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€	f	f	Assaggio is all about taste! Chef Ugo Alciati (of Guido Ristorante, in Piedmont) devised the menu for this elegant restaurant in the Hôtel Castille. As expected, Northern Italy takes pride of place in the dishes – house-made agnolotti, risotto minute... The pastas are quite something: the spaghettone with lobster, lemon zest, confit tomatoes and trout roe is absolutely delicious. Tables are laid out in the delightful interior patio adorned with a fountain and frescoes.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3335478726	Loulou	107 rue Rivoli	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.loulou-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	f	The Arts Décoratifs Museum promises an enchanted interlude opposite the Louvre gardens. In the kitchen, Benoît Dargère reinvents Mediterranean classics by means of meticulously selected produce. On the terrace or in the elegant dining room, the service is as exquisite as the food (risotto of the day^ piccata of milk-fed veal al limone and sage^ grilled octopus and aioli). Cosy, refined and delicious.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3338193192	Mori Venice Bar	27 rue Vivienne	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.mori-venicebar.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€€	t	f	Take a seat here, in front of the former stock exchange, to savour the great specialities of Venice and northeast Italy in an interior by Philippe Starck that evokes the refinement of Venice. Painstakingly chosen ingredients: the veggies come straight from a “respectful cottage garden” and the fish from sustainable sources, like the turbot cooked in butter and prosecco with spinach leaf and cream of celery. Let’s not forget the cicchetti (small snacks) or the delicious ice cream topped with hazelnuts from Piedmont.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3332941232	Osteria Ferrara	7 rue du Dahomey	France	Paris	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.osteriaferrara.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€	f	f	Foodies can come here safe in the knowledge that they have found sanctuary in this elegant interior where the culinary magic happens. Sicilian chef Fabrizio Ferrara builds a menu of tasty and well-crafted ingredient-led Italian recipes, such as carpaccio of lean meat, puntarelle and Sicilian citron, or ravioli stuffed with Castelmagno cheese and potatoes. This bistro has soul, and an appealing wine list to boot.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3338062539	Passerini	65 rue Traversière	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.passerini.paris/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	t	f	In his convivial restaurant, Giovanni Passerini treats us to tasty, carefully prepared Italian dishes, such as his trippa alla romana, which could hardly be bettered. Here, it's all about the produce and authenticity: sharing plates are a house speciality, as is Black-Headed Manech suckling lamb or whole pigeon in two courses. This place is very popular, so be sure to book!	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3334185455	Penati al Baretto	94 boulevard de la Tour-Maubourg	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.penatialbaretto.eu	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€€	f	f	It is no secret that Italians have great taste. Milanese chef Alberico Penati has set up shop in this chic bistro with honey-coloured wood panelling, and bay windows overlooking the garden of the Invalides – a highly prized location indeed! Tradition is the chef's passion. With no concessions to passing fashions, his menu features a selection of Italian classics made out of carefully selected ingredients. Home-made pasta remains the forte of this place, eg ravioli del plin piemontesi with a very good roast beef jus. The 100% Italian wine list highlights Piedmontese wines, particularly Barolo and Barbaresco.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3334189258	Piero TT	44 rue du Bac	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantpiero.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Welcome to Pierre Gagnaire's Italian restaurant, where the great chef proposes his personal and creative take on cucina italiana, beautifully made with rigorously selected produce. The dishes are punctuated with subtle contrasts created, for example, by bitter salad leaves, spices and condiments. You can look forward to a chic and opulent but nonetheless relaxed atmosphere, a warm welcome and expert recommendations on the best Italian wines from the sommelier. Booking strongly advised.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3338314003	Racines	8 passage des Panoramas	France	Paris		https://racinesparis.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	t	f	Simone Tondo, a chef of Sardinian origin, runs this charming bistro-cum-wine cellar, having made the excellent decision to turn it into a traditionally styled osteria. The chef's cooking is firmly rooted in Italian produce and he gives free rein to his creativity with a carte blanche menu and daily specials. These present a choice of down-to-earth Italian dishes that are rife with distinct flavours and carefully prepared from well-chosen ingredients: vitello tonnato, polpette al sugo, ricotta ravioli, spinach and squid.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3335630328	Sormani	4 rue du Général-Lanrezac	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking	http://www.sormanirestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	f	This Italian restaurant has an opulent feel, with its Murano glass chandeliers, mouldings and mirrors, and is popular with Paris's celebrities. The cooking pays tribute to Italian specialities, with spaghetti alle vongole and Calabrian chilli, for example, or iconic desserts such as the gigantesco – Italian-style vanilla ice cream frozen to order on site, served with meringue, nougatine and liquid caramel.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3332673549	Tosca	18 rue du Cirque	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.robertonaldicollection.com/fr/splendide-royal-paris/restaurant-romantique-paris	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Italy seems to have converged on this small-capacity, smartly furnished restaurant. The food is an ode to Italian gastronomy, showcasing its meat, olive oil, cheese… Classical at lunchtime, more elaborate, and often inspired, at dinner. The Splendide Royal Hotel (formerly Pierre Cardin’s home) offers swish, elegant suites.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3330479865	Via del Campo	22 rue du Champ-de-Mars	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.via-del-campo.paris/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€€	f	f	Authentic Italian cuisine is not as easy to come by in France as one might expect. Thankfully there is this contemporary trattoria, which also boasts a few tables on the verdant pavement terrace in fine weather. Chef Enrico Masia whisks diners off on a culinary voyage that takes in every region of Italy^ the traditional fare of Sardinia, his birthplace, inspires the lion's share of dishes. Regulars eagerly consult the daily menu, which is devised in line with the food markets and the chef's inspiration on the day. You can expect dishes such as crunchy puntarella finished with an anchovy sauce, Venetian-style calf liver, and clam paccheri with fresh artichokes and shredded bottarga. Tatiana, the chef's partner, runs the show front of house, providing discreet and efficient service that includes astute recommendations when it comes to their selection of Italian wines.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3337168962	L'Inconnu	4 rue Pierre-Leroux	France	Paris		https://restaurant-linconnu.fr/	Nessun premio	Italian, Creative	4.0	€€€	f	f	The chef, who for a long time was second-in-command at Passage 53, concocts Italian-inspired cuisine with influences from France, as well as his native Japan. He only works with the finest ingredients, using them to produce original and creative dishes, such as Breton langoustine tails topped with a cider and confit lemon emulsion.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3331325086	Cavalieri	71 avenue Paul-Doumer	France	Paris	Valet parking	http://www.cavalieri.paris.fr	Nessun premio	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Between Place du Trocadéro and la Muette, this smart, contemporary venue offers another spin on timeless Italian classics: aubergine parmigiana, fritto misto, a smoked version of vitello tonnato, linguine alle vongole... The interior sports Sicilian walnut furnishings, two-tone Italian marble and hand-painted tableware reminiscent of the Amalfi coast.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3332868564	L'Altro Frenchie	9 rue du Nil	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.altro-frenchie.com	Nessun premio	Italian, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Grégory Marchand strikes again with his eclectic take on dining! In this modern Italian-style bistro, diners will also detect the British and American influences of which the chef is so fond. On the menu: a crudo misto with a series of ingenious vegetable condiments, classic dishes like pappardelle with rabbit or a must-try cotoletta alla milanese (veal chop for two). As for the chocolate cake, it is a homage to the recipe devised by Jamie Oliver at London's River Café. The wines are supplied by Frenchie, the wine shop just next door.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3333476088	Restaurant des Grands Boulevards	17 boulevard Poissonnière	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.grandsboulevardshotel.com/	Nessun premio	Italian, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	A hip, trendy vibe and a warm welcome set the scene beneath the hotel's central winter garden structure. The concise Italian-themed menu, devised by chef Giovanni Passerini, is both simple and succulent, illustrated by grilled cuttlefish, risotto of spelt and grilled aubergine^ Giovanni’s ravioli of spinach, ricotta and sage butter^ monkfish in spices, wax beans and chard, emulsion of Savagnin (variety of grape). The beverage list features an intriguing lineup of wines and cocktails. Just the ticket for a party night out on the town!	de santistobias	\N	\N
3330846017	Bon Kushikatsu	24 rue Jean-Pierre-Timbaud	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.kushikatsubon.fr/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€€	t	f	This restaurant is an express trip to Osaka to discover the city's culinary speciality of kushikatsu (meat, vegetables or seafood skewers coated with breadcrumbs and deep - fried). Dish after dish reveals fine flavours, such as: beef sancho, peppered foie gras, and shiitake mushrooms. The courteous service transports you to Japan.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3336490847	Hakuba	Cheval Blanc Paris	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.chevalblanc.com/fr/maison/paris/restaurants-et-bars/hakuba/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	€€€€	t	f	What might one expect from a Japanese restaurant featuring an all-star line-up of chef Takuya Watanabe (previously at Jin) and Arnaud Donckele and his pastry chef partner Maxime Frédéric? Nothing but the best, of course! Takuya Watanabe belongs to the inner circle of the capital's grand masters, channelling all his passion and expertise into his sushi, shaping each and every piece to perfection in view of diners. For his part, Arnaud Donckele brings to the table his talent for sauces, jus and broths, in creations such as shellfish dashi, sweet garlic purée and green shiso coulis, or the clear and potent accompaniment to the ramen. A rarity in Japanese restaurants, dessert is a must here, masterfully orchestrated by Plénitude's pastry chef. The decor and service, just like the meal, elevate the silence and purity of the materials used.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3333031016	Kodawari Ramen - Yokochō	29 rue Mazarine	France	Paris		https://www.kodawari-ramen.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€	t	f	The bustling vibe and cramped dimensions of this eatery instantly conjure up pictures of historic Tokyo. The ramen, made on site and served in delicious broths of Loiret poultry, attract gourmets from every horizon. The house speciality is kurugoma ramen made with a secret black sesame seed sauce and pata negra pork. Avoid peak times, as the place is very popular. Fully deserving of its success.	beloveva	\N	\N
3336366228	Nodaïwa	272 rue Saint-Honoré	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.nodaiwa.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	€€	f	t	This little restaurant, an off - shoot of a Tokyo - based eatery, boasts an unusual speciality: eel! The unagi is meticulously crafted and seasoned with soy sauce, or sanshô, an Asian pepper. The vast majority of diners who come here are Japanese, which gives an idea of the quality of the cuisine.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3334554140	Ogata	16 rue Debelleyme	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.ogata.com/paris/restaurant	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	€€€€	t	f	Ogata, a temple dedicated to Japanese art de vivre, is located in a private mansion in the Marais and masterminded by Shinichiro Ogata, world-famous designer and connoisseur. The (mainly) traditional Japanese food sports an omakase spirit, through a tasting menu comprised of immaculate seasonal produce (first-class sashimi). The best seats are at the counter. Pop into the shop or art gallery on your way out…	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3338579622	Okuda	7 rue de la Trémoille	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.okuda.fr/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€€€	t	f	A sober and elegant decor, 23 seats, hostesses in traditional kimonos and golden silence. It is in this setting that since 2013 diners have been tasting the ‘kaiseki’ creations of the famous Japanese chef Toru Okuda, crowned with Michelin stars back in Tokyo. Harmonious flavours, subtle sauces, delicate textures – this is great art.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3334573216	Marie Akaneya	12 rue Godot-de-Mauroy	France	Paris	Notable sake list,Wheelchair access	http://www.marieakaneya.com	Nessun premio	Japanese, Barbecue	4.0	€€€€	t	t	This is Paris's first sumibiyaki-style restaurant. Particularly popular in Kyoto, this cuisine is prepared with top-drawer ingredients, not least the Wagyu that is shipped here from Ito Ranch, a beef farm on the outskirts of the town of Matsusaka – and according to the Japanese themselves, this is the ultimate breed of Kobe beef. Everything is cooked over the famous binchotan charcoal, which is made mainly from Ubame oak wood – every table in the restaurant has its own barbecue taking pride of place. Some of the menus feature Fukuroi's renowned Crown Melon, which can sometimes fetch a price of several thousand euro.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3339354407	Akira Back Paris	Prince de Galles	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.akirabackparis.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Fusion	5.0	€€€€	f	f	In the Prince de Galles hotel, this is the first European restaurant of American-Korean chef Akira Back. After a career as a professional snowboarder (he grew up in Aspen, home to the legendary ski resort), he turned his hand to cooking. He was recruited by Nobuyuki Matsuhisa and later became the executive chef at the renowned chef's restaurant. Diners are given the opportunity to taste this new take on Japanese cuisine, a real melting pot of cultures and flavours, including Back's speciality: AB Tuna Pizza. Meanwhile, feast your eyes on the sumptuous decor of this large modern restaurant with Art Deco light fixtures emitting subdued lighting, while the kitchen team busy themselves at the marble counter.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3331107298	Sushi Shunei	3 rue Audran	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.sushishunei.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Sushi	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Located on Montmartre’s hill, this joint sports an elegant, minimalist interior that celebrates the aesthetic codes of Japanese restaurants: light wooden furnishings, a long counter and an amazing origami-inspired ceiling by an interior design firm. Chizuko Kimura and the Sushi master Takeshi Morooka pursue the legacy of Shunei Kimura, who made this eatery such a success. The omakase menu comes in two versions, which must be chosen when you book. Both embark the diner on a genuine sensorial experience courtesy of razor-sharp nigiris, a truly exceptional selection of fish, expert handiwork and a range of subtle seasonings, without forgetting Japan’s unique vision of hospitality that is both unobtrusive and highly attentive.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3335023050	Jium	26 rue Tiphaine	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Korean	5.0	€€	f	f	Behind a rather nondescript façade lies an authentic Korean canteen which boasts a lovely vintage vibe and is popular with a clientele from the land of the Morning Calm. It is the brainchild of photographer and guesthouse owner, Kim Hong-Seung, and his wife Sun-Hee, a former fashion designer. As well as bibimbap classics, the menu is packed with authentic delicacies (soft shell crabs, oyster fritters) and unusual recipes (seafood pancakes, kimchi stew, pork shoulder and tofu, etc). You can season these culinary delights with homemade soy sauce (or not) before finishing with a dessert, also homemade, illustrated by vanilla-flavoured rice pudding with red beans and caramelised pecan nuts.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3339824922	Mojju	4 rue de l'Exposition	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.mojju-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Korean, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Chef Thibault Sombardier opened this Korean eatery, the decor of which nods to the traditional hanoks (houses) of the Land of the Morning Calm. The menu is extremely well devised and meticulously executed by a Korean team: beef broth with tofu, shiitake and garlic crisps^ miso-glazed monkfish^ toasted buckwheat cream and soya caramel. Barbecued over charcoal, the matured meats and marinated fish are served alongside the traditional banchan (small side dishes of fermented or marinated vegetables) and accompanied by well-seasoned sauces and crunchy salad leaves for diners to prepare their own ssam (wrap). There is a small and original wine list, complemented by a few Korean rice spirits.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3330895217	Liza	14 rue de la Banque	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.restaurant-liza.com/	Nessun premio	Lebanese	5.0	€€	f	t	Originally from Beirut, Liza Asseily gives pride of place to the food of her homeland. In a bright interior strewn with Middle Eastern touches, you can expect mezze to share, grilled meats or fattet batinjan (aubergine, minced lamb and yoghurt). Numerous vegetarian dishes and a fine selection of Lebanese wines.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3336801269	Qasti Green	41 rue des Jeûneurs	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	http://www.qasti.fr	Nessun premio	Lebanese, Vegetarian	3.0	€€	t	f	Chef Alan Geaam has added another string to his bow with this vegetarian Lebanese restaurant. Behind the stoves is Zeinab Hachem, his niece, who was trained by his mother in the subtleties of traditional Lebanese cuisine. Some of the dishes have already secured iconic status, such as the vegetarian shawarma with celery and mushrooms, or the daoud basha – lentil balls with almonds and spices, served in a tomato sauce. The affordable menu also features their own take on authentic Lebanese flavours: vegetable freekeh^ vegetarian soujouk (sausages) and signature creations such as mama ganoush (cauliflower caviar). Reflecting the cuisine, the minimalist decor is adorned with natural, plant-based materials. Booking essential.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3336250507	Aux Lyonnais	32 rue Saint-Marc	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.auxlyonnais.com/	Nessun premio	Lyonnaise	3.0	€€	t	t	This bistro established in 1890 has a delightfully retro decor and serves delicious cuisine that explores Lyon's gastronomy in all its riches. The terrines, pike-perch quenelles with crayfish, and the chicken liver terrine vie with the specials chalked up on the slate, and the desserts are enough to awaken anyone's sweet tooth.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3333249139	Adraba	40 rue Véron	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.adraba-paris.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	The team at the helm of this trendy restaurant with an upbeat atmosphere is a group of friends headed up by Israeli chef Elior Benaroche, once sous-chef at Balagan and an associate of Assaf Granit since his early days in the heart of Jerusalem's Old City. Tapping into the Levant and the chef's family history, this cuisine is a festival of spices and condiments: hilbeh (fenugreek paste), ezme (Turkish salad of charcoal-roasted vegetables), tahini, zaatar, harif (marinated chillis), tulum (Turkish cheese) – rounded off by a fine cocktail menu. A culinary voyage.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3332749623	Brach	1-7 rue Jean Richepin	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Brunch,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://brachparis.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	In the luxurious setting of this former postal sorting office, redesigned and decorated by Philippe Starck, diners peruse a menu of Mediterranean-inspired dishes^ these are executed with finesse and precision by chef Adam Benthala, who has an impressive CV to his name. The healthy and balanced fare embraces indulgence when it comes to sharing a round of kémia – small plates rife with aromas, spices and textures.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3338384403	Kapara	9 rue d'Alger	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://kaparaparis.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	In their new venue, Kapara, whose interior is almost identical to that of the former Balagan, Assaf Granit and his partner Tomer Lanzman have called upon chef Zohar Sasson. In a setting depicted by groovy background music and hoots of laughter from the ebullient kitchen brigade, Ms Sasson cheerfully conjures up dishes loosely inspired by Sephardic culinary traditions. The menu rolls out a colourful culinary anthology, boosted by spices, seasonings and chickpeas. Some of the emblematic dishes of the former Balagan remain on the menu, such as “deconstructed” kebab. Festive, friendly and (very) buzzy vibe.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3337654399	Marso & Co	16 rue Vulpian	France	Paris		https://www.tomygousset.com/marso-and-co/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Tomy Gousset (Tomy & Co, near Les Invalides) runs this restaurant that sets out to take diners on a culinary journey: the food tours the entire Mediterranean basin from Greece to Portugal via Italy and Lebanon (but also Latin America). Examples of the Colombian born chef’s handiwork include an aguachile of seabream and shrimp, pink grapefruit, cucumber and coriander. The octopus-themed artwork on the walls is by street artist Kraken. Soul-warming recipes, spot-on flavours, fantastically fresh ingredients – a felicitous feast awaits you!	bianconathan	\N	\N
3339428580	Alluma	151 rue Saint-Maur	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://alluma-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Israeli	4.0	€€€	t	t	Former Balagan chef Liran Tal has tastefully revamped this establishment with immaculate white walls. He crafts delicious Mediterranean cuisine with Israeli influences, served in the form of tasting menus that are very good value for money: delicious msabbaha hummus, yellowtail crudo with figs and spices, lamb sirloin and an apricot-miso condiment. Choice of organic and biodynamic wines, most notably from Italy, Spain and Armenia.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3338505048	24 - Le Restaurant	24 rue Jean-Mermoz	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.24lerestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In a quiet street just a stone's throw from the Champs-Elysées, this establishment offers well-crafted, pedigree Gallic cuisine with an occasional personal spin, such as breast of Dombes duckling, chutney of yellow peaches, pine nuts and duckling jus underscored by mulled wine. Cheerful and professional welcome in a stylish setting.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3337939117	Agapé	51 rue Jouffroy-d'Abbans	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking	https://www.agape-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	In this cosy, welcoming room adorned in soft shades, the menu rolls out a lineup of premium ingredients that depend on the whim of chef Yoshi Nagato (Maison Rostang, Le Cinq, Épicure) and his partner, Asuka Ishiba, in charge of desserts. Brittany lobster salad, wax beans, Piedmont hazelnuts and a dressing of lobster roe^ Challans duckling lacquered in honey and Sichuan pepper^ roast sweetbread and sautéed girolles… Stylish, high-precision plating and generous helpings. Fine range of organic and natural wines.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3331740034	Alleudium	24 rue Rodier	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.alleudium.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Keiichi Shinohara, a Japanese chef with solid credentials (including a stint at Le Violon d'Ingres during the Christian Constant era), is at the helm of this restaurant with refined contemporary decor. Customer satisfaction is the goal here, in particular when it comes to the food, which is modern and inspired, with the odd nod to Japan.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3335737449	Amâlia	32 rue de la Fontaine-au-Roi	France	Paris		http://www.amaliarestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	t	Unlike many of the other restaurants in the east of Paris, this one has gone for classic elegance: a refined decor, tablecloths, stylish service. Perhaps this is the mark of the good taste of Italian couple Cecilia Spurio (pastry) and Eugenio Anfuso (cooking), who are familiar with Michelin-starred restaurants. Prepared with small pieces of citrus fruit and cashew nuts, the smoked Galician veal tartare is served in a sea urchin shell, topped with a quenelle of sea urchin ice cream. For his red mullet à la bourguignonne, the chef arranges the fish on shredded beef and cabbage leaves, the whole of which is then doused with a superb sauce. This is a modern iteration of the French repertoire, punctuated by a few Italian touches or other influences from further afield, executed with precision and a clear penchant for acidic notes.	benesemily	\N	\N
3336660723	Ambos	38 rue de Vaugirard	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.ambos-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Overlooking the grandiose seat of the Senate (upper house of the French parliament) and the Luxembourg gardens, this friendly bistro in tune with its era sports untreated materials (exposed stone, brickwork and rafters), an open kitchen and a small counter. ‘Ambos’ (‘both’ in Spanish) refers to Pierre Chomet and his Venezuelan wife, Cristina. Their culinary adventures have taken them from Bangkok to London and Paris, and a Top Chef TV season for Pierre. Together they concoct a light-hearted, personal and vibrant tapestry of flavours which aims to please as it draws on a variety of influences – European (Castilian beef and Paimpol beans) and Thai (pad thai-style langoustine tartar,) as well as South American (stuffed arepa cornbread).	colombostefano	\N	\N
3336604741	Anicia, table nature	97 rue du Cherche-Midi	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.anicia-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Hailing from the Haute-Loire area, François Gagnaire carefully selects small-scale farmers from the vicinity, kitting himself out with excellent raw material for his cooking. Puy lentils, Limousine des Monts-du-Velay beef, Mézenc fin gras beef, Artisous farmhouse cheese, Vellavia beer… His dishes are both delicious and beautifully presented, making a meal here a real treat^ the lunch menu is a real bargain in this neighbourhood. Afternoon tea is served, plus a more fine dining menu in the evening.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3336957752	ASPIC	24 rue Louise-Émilie-de-la-Tour-d'Auvergne	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.aspic-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	After ditching the world of finance to enrol in the Ferrandi Culinary School, the chef went on to hone his skills in a variety of establishments (including the French Ministry of Foreign Affairs and L'Épi Dupin). He then went it alone and opened this restaurant. With its vintage vibe and open kitchen, the chef devises a surprise set menu that is unabashedly creative and showcases carefully selected ingredients: free-range meat and poultry, line-caught fish from small boat fishing, citrus fruits, herbs and spices, all sourced as locally as possible.	dragomirpippo	\N	\N
3338853298	Aux Prés	27 rue du Dragon	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://restaurantauxpres.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	An openly vintage bistro (red banquette seating, smoked - glass mirrors, floral wallpaper) in St Germain and international cuisine by Cyril Lignac, whose creativity never strays entirely from its French country roots.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3337377049	Bistro S	7 rue Saint-Nicolas	France	Paris		https://www.bistros.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	S like secret, savoury, sapid or Spinoza, not the philosopher but the owner who lovingly watches over this discreet Parisian establishment, and who is also a numismatist specialising in antique Greek coins and a genuine wine connoisseur. The talented Japanese chef Shimpei Oié crafts a fresh, healthy, balanced set menu backed up by his flawless culinary technique. Don’t miss the gilthead seabream: expertly fire-roasted and accompanied by white grapes and a kiwi juice. S like Super!	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3339096781	Bistrot Instinct	19 rue de Picardie	France	Paris	Terrace	https://instinct-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This pocket handkerchief contemporary bistro is in the hands of chef Maximilian Wollek and his enthusiastic youthful team. A market-fresh culinary score and updated classics with bistronomic overtones. Everything is homemade, even the cordials used in the unusual cocktails.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3337396103	Bistrotters	9 rue Decrès	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.bistrotters.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	A lovely place in the southern reaches of the 14th arrondissement near Métro Plaisance. The Spanish chef carefully selects his ingredients, with a preference for small-scale producers in the Paris region, and instils them with various influences (Asian, Mediterranean etc). Laid-back service.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3334057368	Bombance	40 rue des Blancs-Manteaux	France	Paris		https://www.bombanceparis.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Pressé de bœuf (beef terrine), kale mayonnaise^ roast mallard, glazed mini beetroots, confit legs^ peanut chocolate, chocolate quenelle, ice cream and peanut praline: chef Guillaume Campion, like the pro he his, having worked in some of the best restaurants in the world, is embracing his role. With a sure hand, he delights diners with his lively bistro-inspired cuisine. In addition to the tables along the banquette, there are also larger tables, ideal for feasting with friends.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3339108041	Bonhomme	58 rue du Faubourg-Poissonnière	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://bonhomme-resto.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The trio who founded this lively bistro in the Faubourg Poissonnière are certainly not short on bonhomie! In this trendy, distressed decor (hand-scraped walls, marble-topped pedestal tables, glass-paned cellar), the chef has savvily set about creating tasty bistronomy fare without falling for faddish effects: breaded pork croquettes, red onion and chilli chutney^ seared mackerel, braised pencil leek, sorrel^ dark chocolate mousse, caramel, chocolate crumble... Great atmosphere guaranteed.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3337569430	Braise	19 rue d'Anjou	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.braise.paris	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	The former second of Substance, Sylvain Courivaud, is determined to kindle our appetites in this contemporary venue entirely devoted to wood-fired cooking. Whatever the method from Japanese barbecue or Big Green Egg to a smoker, Sylvain combines consummate technique with a love of high-quality produce. The vibe of this trendy eatery is warm and welcoming.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3337218877	Brion	17 rue Lamartine	France	Paris		http://www.brion-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	With a star-studded CV (including Pierre Gagnaire and Jérôme Banctel) to his name, chef Geoffrey Lengagne has opened this restaurant with a refined decor (waxed concrete floor, light wood furniture, open kitchen). An avid seasonal cook, he uses the freshest ingredients to deliver predominantly vegetable-forward and fish- and seafood-based cuisine. The roasted Jerusalem artichokes, Jerusalem artichoke purée and Tomme cheese sabayon, with XO sauce for spice and chopped mint providing a twist, epitomise his modern touch. The lunch set menu is good value for money^ pricier and more elaborate fare in the evening.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3331699165	Café Compagnon	22-26 rue Léopold-Bellan	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://cafecompagnon.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	After Richer and 52 Faubourg, Charles Compagnon, restaurant owner, sommelier and coffee roaster, strikes again! This cafe offers an extensive menu ranging from nibbles to share to home-made ices. The original, deftly crafted recipes feature a modern bistro slant, depicted by market-fresh starters and succulent loin of pork. Heart-warming, authentic comfort food.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3331104857	Chantoiseau	63 rue Lepic	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.chantoiseau-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	In 1765, Mathurin Roze de Chantoiseau opened the first modern restaurant (individual tables and dishes to choose from on a menu) in the Louvre area. In homage to him, brothers Nicolas and Julien Durand work in tandem to create lovely modern cuisine, which is also inspired by the French classics and occasionally makes use of noble products, as in the delicious puff pastry pigeon pie.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3331278988	CoDa	15 rue de la Tour-des-Dames	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Set back from the boisterous Rue Blanche, this pocket-handkerchief bolthole is the epitome of an authentic Parisian café. The tables are so tightly packed, it may feel like you are dining with rather than next to your neighbours. Irrepressibly cheerful, Pauline and Vincent Da Costa (former second chef of Bruno Doucet’s Régalade) pamper their guests with nosh that hits the spot every time: field to fork market-fresh seasonal ingredients. Fine food without the fuss. The lunchtime menu is a steal.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3335249919	Colvert	30 rue des Grands-Augustins	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://colvert.paris	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Revealed by the French Top Chef TV show, Arnaud Baptiste and his flamboyant moustache and numerous tattoos, is something of a media darling. He has set up shop in a vintage street corner bistro (banquettes, bistro chairs, tightly packed tables, bare stone walls, cement tiled floor and a counter which now serves standing customers) in the somewhat touristy, but nonetheless picturesque 6th district of Paris. Arnaud happily crafts market-fresh, bistronomic fare. The seasonal menu is suitably concise and hits the spot every time: confit of cod, hollandaise sauce, courgettes and absinthe gel or figs, served roasted, raw and in pickles with a fig sorbet and ice cream.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3335537304	Comme Chez Maman	5 rue des Moines	France	Paris		https://comme-chez-maman.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This contemporary bistro near a green square in the heart of the Batignolles neighbourhood is a real home from home. The Belgian chef, Wim Van Gorp, makes lovely contemporary dishes that he peppers with creative touches, and some of which pay delicious tribute to his Flemish roots.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3335967071	Coretta	151 bis rue Cardinet	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantcoretta.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In the Clichy-Batignolles district, opposite Martin Luther King Park (King's wife was called Coretta), Mexican-born chef Beatriz Gonzalez, with stints in star-rated eateries of the likes of Senderens and La Grande Cascade, consummately curates a season-driven menu rich in big-boned generous flavours. Youthful, buzzy front-of-house team and a bright airy designer interior overlooking the trees in the park from the second floor.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3336944814	Dame Augustine	32 avenue des Gobelins	France	Paris		http://www.dameaugustine.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This is the other restaurant of chef Lilian Douchet, who hails from Bordeaux: you can expect a laid-back atmosphere and a veranda-style space with the feel of a small brasserie. He serves several set menus, including a good-value lunch deal. Diners savour dishes such as a selection of heirloom tomatoes, fresh herb pesto, parmesan buttercrumb biscuits and mizuna sorbet, or a fillet of whiting simmered with coco de Paimpol beans and a lemon thyme emulsion. A welcome address in this residential area.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3334000407	Dandelion	46 rue des Vignoles	France	Paris		http://www.restaurantdandelion.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Antoine Villard, previously chef at Double Dragon and sous-chef at Septime, and Morgane Souris, formerly sommelier at Parcelles, have polished up this little gem of a contemporary bistro in eastern Paris, with its waxed-concrete floors and façade giving onto a tree-lined square. The chef showcases the experience he already has under his belt as he turns out precise and creative cuisine that draws on a variety of influences. He brilliantly combines unexpected flavours: bluefin tuna with redcurrant and marigold^ raw prawns with kimchi and ginger – made with carefully selected quality ingredients. Attentive, relaxed and smiling service.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3335602310	Dante	14 rue de Paradis	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	https://www.danterestaurant.info	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	After a period of purgatory, this hip establishment in Rue de Paradis is back in favour thanks to an enthusiastic young chef who fell in love with haute cuisine after an internship with Alain Passard. Rébecca Beaufour consummately crafts fiendishly flavoursome bistronomic dishes, such as lobster and king prawn ravioles or crisp sweetbread served with squash and apple caramel. The house also offers a range of dishes to share, like pigeon or whole seabream cooked in salt.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3339682288	Des Terres	82 rue Alexandre-Dumas	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A buzzy casual vibe depicts this neighbourhood bistro in the 20th arrondissement of Paris. In the company of natural wines displayed on a bookshelf, you will joyfully do justice to the chef’s competently crafted fare: cauliflower in a herring, hazelnut and green oil sauce^ roast beetroot, Colonnata pork and creamy goat’s cheese. Seasonal nosh and a bargain-priced lunch menu.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3339799251	Deux Bistrot de chefs	58 rue de la Fontaine-au-Roi	France	Paris	Brunch	http://www.deux-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Tiphaine Mollard, from Savoie and Romain Casas, from Béarn, have teamed up, pooling their contagious good humour and respective homelands in this warm, inviting establishment: open kitchen, shelves laden with bottles, knick-knacks, photos and plants. Tomatoes, cream of burrata and vinegar jelly^ grilled sardines, green bean salad, pistou and peaches: the food is joyful, tasty, legible and heartily wholesome. Prices that make sense.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3339736654	Ducasse sur Seine	Port Debilly	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking	https://www.ducasse-seine.com/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Well, no one can say that Alain Ducasse lacks for boldness or ideas, as the Ducasse sur Seine once again proves. An electric boat, moored on the quayside of Port Debilly in the swanky 16th arrondissement, offers a gastronomic cruise that is both ecological and silent. At the same time as you discover Parisian monuments, you will taste up - to - the - minute cuisine, masterfully crafted by a kitchen team worthy of the best restaurants. Well done, mon capitaine!	benesemily	\N	\N
3337587837	Eclipses	27-29 rue de Beaune	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://eclipses.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	This restaurant, by a chef who has carved out a career in Michelin-starred kitchens (Ledoyen, Apicius, Le Grand Véfour), serves contemporary cuisine that is heedful of ingredients and the seasons. Enjoy your meal in the tastefully decorated neo-Classical setting. Lovely vaulted cellar.	raduionela	\N	\N
3339067718	Elmer	30 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.elmer-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Close to République, this terribly chic bistro is officiated by a chef with an impressive career (including L'Oustau de Baumanière, Pierre Gagnaire, travels in Asia and Latin America). He composes a flavoursome menu that packs a punch, with fine meats cooked on embers or on the rotisserie.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3333040256	ERH	11 rue Tiquetonne	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Notable sake list	http://www.restaurant-erh.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	t	The initials E, R and H stand for water, rice and men in French (eau, riz, hommes): a mysterious and poetic name for this unusual place that shares its premises with a sake shop and a whisky bar. The Japanese chef delivers lovely French cuisine that is full of flavour and has a distinctly Japanese feel to it^ he also takes some rather original detours in his creations. You might like to opt for food and sake pairings. The remarkable contemporary space has a large glass roof and a long counter that stretches out in front of the open kitchen, where, as in Japan, the chef officiates.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3330041316	Erso	18 rue Saint-Ambroise	France	Paris	Counter dining	http://www.erso-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Having met at Le Pantruche, these two form a crack team. In the welcoming blue and wood-panelled restaurant room, Marine Bert is in charge of service^ Yann Placet's domain is the open kitchen, and seeing his handiwork from the handful of counter seats whets the appetite. The chef's main aim is to please, and he won't fail to win you over with his modern bistronomy, eg mushroom millefeuille with a coffee emulsion. Tempting lunch deal^ booking definitely recommended for dinner.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3337127971	Fana	14 rue Ferdinand-Flocon	France	Paris		http://www.fanabistro.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	It is clear to see that chef Gabriel Gras Fernandez and pastry chef Jorice Sardain are passionate about food. In their compact restaurant on a pedestrian street in Montmartre (where more and more interesting restaurants are popping up), they work in tandem to create their clever take on seasonal cuisine in the from of carefully crafted dishes: oyster mushrooms, coffee sabayon, parsley, brioche^ corn-fed chicken, butternut squash, endive, orange^ and a stunning chocolate dessert with an array of textures.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3335604678	Gemellus	37 avenue Duquesne	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://gemellus-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	This spruce, modern eatery done up in oatmeal shades features a square dining room with painted mouldings, a coffered ceiling, an imposing chandelier and upholstered velvet seats. Chef Maxime Le Meur, who trained with some of the greats, leaves nothing to chance as he crafts cuisine inspired as much by seasonal ingredients as by his Breton (check out the surf ‘n turf dish of Breton squab with lobster) and Grenoble roots (Chartreuse liqueur is never far from the culinary score). A festival of forthright, meticulous flavours overflowing in creative ideas. Affordable lunchtime menu.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3332036906	Godaille	9 rue Antoine-Vollon	France	Paris	Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.restaurantgodaille.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Godaille in French slang means feasting and making merry among good friends. So let's get to it and tuck into this invigorating, flavoursome cuisine! This eatery run by a group of pals gives pride of place to spices and fresh herbs, in dishes such as fried chicken with super-soft meat in a crispy golden crumb, alongside a ginger-lemon sauce^ bouchot mussels are served with a coconut-green curry sauce and Thai herbs. The pleasant, slightly retro interior is complemented by a lovely bunch of fresh flowers on each table. A fine selection of natural and organic wines (including some orange wines).	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3331550261	GrandCœur	41 rue du Temple	France	Paris	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.grandcoeur.paris	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Take a seat in the warm, welcoming interior (with exposed beams and stonework, marble table tops and velvet upholstery), or on the pleasant terrace in the picturesque, cobbled courtyard of the Marais Dance Centre. The brainchild of Mauro Colagreco, the pedigree Gallic recipes come with an international, often Italian twist… Examples include stuffed confit of lamb in a provençal sauce, Taggiasche olives and a gutsy gravy – high-flying culinary art!	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3332206676	Guefen	9 rue du Vertbois	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.guefen.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	At Ohad Amzallag's restaurant a stone's throw from Place de la République, diners sample his cooking in convivial fashion, all seated at a large marble table d'hôte. The Israeli chef serves Middle Eastern-influenced cuisine that gives pride of place to seafood ingredients and fermented vegetables, such as oyster cream with mint granita, chilli and koshu^ lobster and agnolotti with ricotta, spinach and sage cream^ and a delicious cheesecake with caramelised garum.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3334216943	Habile.	16 rue de Lancry	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://habile.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Our chefs and their partners are never short of bright ideas for new ways to dine. After the trend for caves à manger and restaurants with delis, this place unites bistro and knitwear. Upstairs, fashion designer Camille Andrieux showcases her sartorial creations, while chef Éric Fontanini cooks up generous, no-frills meals: The pâté en croûte with pork and foie gras, and the line-caught bluefin tuna, simply seared and served on a delicious compote of onions and peppers, are good examples. As an added bonus, the kitchen is open 11am-11pm (excluding the lunch set menu). The colourful decor is delightfully dapper, and you can even eat at the counter and see the chef at work.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3335328617	Halo Paris	12 rue Saint-Sauveur	France	Paris		http://www.halo-paris.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This restaurant is tucked away at the back of a fashion and design concept store showcasing young designers. Behind the wooden door, light flows through the glass roof into a space with an open kitchen and a bare concrete floor. A veritable cultural hub, the basement includes a small exhibition room, a cocktail bar and a table d'hôte. In the kitchen, chef Victor Blanchet (who was a contestant on French TV's Top Chef in 2023 and has also worked at L'Arpège and Neso) is inspired by the Mediterranean and the Basque Country – serving dishes that are colourful, light and well composed, such as sea bass tataki flambéed with pastis, beetroot mousseline and preserved lemon. Online bookings only.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3330573213	Hestia	8 rue de la Huchette	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.hestia-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Hestia, goddess of the hearth, presides over this restaurant that absolutely oozes cachet, with its white beams, stone walls and mirrors. Normandy-born chef Loïc Dantec (previously at 114 Faubourg) devises a seasonal menu only, with dishes that hit the mark, such as Cantal pork entrecôte cooked over an open fire with sweet spices. All the meat is grilled to perfection on the barbecue, ready to be carved tableside. The chef cooks without showboating, making flavour the priority. His partner Filipe Fernandes competently and assiduously manages the restaurant floor.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3336788645	Ilô	6 rue Castex	France	Paris		https://ilo-restaurant.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	A marriage between a French gourmet bistro and a Japanese tavern is hidden behind a noren (a vertical fabric divider hung across the doorways of shops in Japan). Ilô is also the lair of a particularly inspired duet, both of whom worked at the star-rated Sola. On one side, Yuki Onuma supervises the service, suggesting perceptive, spot-on wine/saké-food pairings, while on the other, chef Seiya Kumabe conjures up a culinary patchwork of Gallic bistronomy with a smattering of Japanese allusions.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3335526151	Istr	41 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth	France	Paris		https://www.istr.paris/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This cocktail and oyster bar, inspired by New York but also influenced by Brittany, draws a youthful crowd to its packed terrace, plays loud music, and has a trendy atmosphere and decor (technical ducts on the ceiling, high tables, counter-bar). The menu features seafood and contemporary touches – all made from fresh produce.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3330705570	Jeanne-Aimée	3 rue Bourdaloue	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantjeanneaimee.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Bingo for this semi-industrial, semi-cosy bistro alongside Notre Dame de Lorette Church, where two mates tick all the boxes to regale us. On one side, Dan Humphris (who also runs a nearby bakery-grocery store where he sells organic produce from his father’s farm in the Yvelines) and on the other, youthful Sylvain Parisot, with stints in star-studded establishments (l’Astrance and La Marine with Alexandre Couillon) under his belt. Conclusion? First class ingredients (Gascony pork chops, Landes poultry), daring ideas (oysters and camembert ice cream), generosity, sensible prices and spot-on, friendly service.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3330580814	L'Initial	9 rue de Bièvre	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://restaurant-linitial.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This Japanese chef with a brilliant track record proposes French cuisine that demonstrates remarkable precision and is made with fine produce (sea bass, scallops, langoustine, morel mushrooms) and represents good value for money. The roast rack of Lozère lamb, celeriac purée, lemon condiment and reduced lamb jus was a stand-out dish. Highly attentive service and a refined and light-filled setting.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3338744123	Jupi	25 rue des Dames	France	Paris		http://www.jupi-paris.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	At the helm of this modern bistro (polished concrete floor, trendy light fittings, wooden tables), with electronic music playing in the background, young chef Alice Roger shows she has experience (three years in London) and good taste (she worked with Michelin-starred chef Ryuji Teshima at Pages). Her cuisine is full of pep (thanks to elements such as the Noilly Prat sabayon, the gribiche sauce with violet mustard and the horseradish sauce) and decidedly exciting. The lunch menu is a steal. In the evening, plates for sharing are the name of the game.	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3335998962	Ken Yamamoto	144 rue de la Pompe	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.kenyamamoto.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	In a quiet residential street, the establishment of Kenichi (Ken) Yamamoto lies behind a midnight-blue façade. The decor of his intimate restaurant combines contemporary design with Art Deco elements. The eye is immediately drawn to the carefully selected tableware, which includes top-quality meat knives and Japanese crockery. Yamamoto's contemporary cuisine subtly incorporates Japanese ingredients: miso saikyo accompanies the foie gras, yuzu goes into the white wine sauce served with the pollack, and Padrón peppers in tempura sit alongside the beef tenderloin. There is a single set menu in the evening^ with options at lunchtime.	grafpaola	\N	\N
3335869263	Kitchen by Madame Rêve	48 rue du Louvre	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://madamereve.com/restaurants/kitchen/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Restored from head to toe, the iconic Haussmannian Louvre Post Office building is also home to a luxury hotel and a classy neo-brasserie, nestled under an impressive ceiling. The menu is divided into culinary themes in a tongue-in-cheek poke at your usual restaurant codes: healthy trendy, veg out, flashback, etc. The onus is definitely on unstuffy pleasure!	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3335600625	Kitchen Ter(re)	26 boulevard Saint-Germain	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://zekitchengalerie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In his third establishment devoted to pasta, William Ledeuil crafts a kaleidoscope of pared-back tastes and flavours, starring high-flying creations from spelt, durum wheat, einkorn or tender Roussillon wheat by artisan Roland Feuillas. Chef Julien Jéquier (with stints at Le V and L’Écrin) orchestrates a balanced score in which Asian notes and fresh herbs play major supporting roles. From the exquisitely laid tables to the plating, balance is the key word, as is illustrated by his dish of coquillettes (small pasta shells) made out of fresh milled khorasan wheat flour with chicken wings, Taggiasche olives, spinach and Thai broth! Vibrant, lively and the epitome of charming!	dinusauru	\N	\N
3335151797	Korus	73 rue Amelot	France	Paris	Counter dining	https://restaurantkorus.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	This fashionable dinky bistro tucked away between Bastille and République is run by an enthusiastic duo who works closely with a talented chef. Creativity, premium ingredients and unexpected associations result in forthright flavours that hit the spot every time.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3335193784	L'Accolade	208 rue de la Croix-Nivert	France	Paris		https://www.laccoladeparis.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	In a downright convivial atmosphere, the chef – a former sports teacher who has chosen to branch out – prepares tasty cuisine that he changes up every day. He makes ample use of produce from South-West France (pork belly, pointed cabbage and green lentils), but also borrows a smattering of Asian ingredients (carpaccio of Tokyo turnip, crab meat, coriander and black garlic). An appealing place.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3339531273	L'Agrume	15 rue des Fossés-Saint-Marcel	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://restaurant-lagrume.fr/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	In the open kitchen of this bistro, the chef delicately crafts refreshingly wholesome dishes, such as poultry in vin jaune paired with asparagus or a piece of roast turbot with mashed potatoes and poultry jus. Flawlessly fresh produce is the name of the game (the fish comes from Brittany and the fruit and vegetables from the very best suppliers). Tasting menu in the evening.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3337621346	L'Apibo	31 rue Tiquetonne	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.restaurant-lapibo.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In his small bistro in the Montorgueil neighbourhood (hushed atmosphere, oak floorboards, exposed stone), Antony Boucher, a chef with a strong track record, creates beautifully original and delicate cuisine that fêtes ingredients. He is renowned for his two classics: filet of sea bass, black rice and paprika sauce and the eight-hour confit pork with sweet potato mousseline. The laid-back (and very professional) service evokes the rough and ready spirit that used to characterise Les Halles.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3338129719	L'Envolée - La Demeure Montaigne	18 rue Clément-Marot	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.lademeuremontaigne.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	This exclusive venue established in a Haussmannian luxury hotel is a short walk from the Champs-Elysées and Avenue Montaigne. Set in an inner courtyard beneath a glass roof, it is reminiscent of a winter garden conservatory with its cane chairs. Sheltered from prying eyes, you will sample modern seasonal cuisine.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3333748126	L'Esquisse	151 bis rue Marcadet	France	Paris		http://www.esquisse-paris18.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Two enthusiast young food lovers have joined forces to create this inviting vintage bistro with solid wooden flooring and benches. A good time is had here, as you tuck into original dishes that make no bones about drawing on influences from far afield. For lunch there is the menu du jour (with no options) and a mini à la carte menu^ at dinner, a more extensive choice.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3338179300	L'Évadé	23 rue Clauzel	France	Paris		http://www.levade.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A pleasant interior done out in the style of a chic brasserie (red and black chairs, black lacquer tables, exposed beams and stonework). Diners flock here for the serious bistronomy cuisine infused with French tradition… just like at L'Escudella, the other restaurant born of the partnership between chef Rémi Poulain and Anthony Rivière. Dishes include pâté en croûte (a cult favourite)^ pollack, fennel, peas and kumquat^ strawberry-basil vacherin, pistachio and lime crisp. Well-paced service.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3338058899	L'Hommage	36 avenue de Choisy	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lhommageparis.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	In a neighbourhood swarming with Chinese eateries, this establishment stands out from the crowd by courtesy of a bistronomic purebred Gallic lineup and minimalist Scandinavian-style loft interior. The high-flying culinary score boasts quality ingredients and bang-on cooking and seasoning: ravioles of Ossau-Iraty cheese, smoked pimiento sauce, dusting of chorizo, poached rhubarb and roquette oil, or loin of croaker with asparagus, miso and capers in a gutsy red wine sauce…	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3338105635	L’Oyat	11 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth	France	Paris		https://restaurantloyat.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Even in Paris, near the Place de la République, a Ch'ti chef from Dunkirk like Jérémy Sergeant continues to hark back to the beaches of his native region: marram grass – oyat – is a small plant capable of holding in place the sand of the dunes. In the kitchen, he brings to bear all his experience: the produce is fresh, the style modern and light, the jus tasty and the whole thing smacks of sincerity. In the evening, the menu is subtly embellished with premium ingredients. Cosy, contemporary atmosphere.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3338699021	La Causerie	31 rue Vital	France	Paris		https://lacauserie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Two young associates from Le Royal Monceau preside over the destiny of this famous institution in the neighbourhood of La Muette. The chef revisits tradition here, injecting plenty of freshness, through a menu as straightforward as it is tasty^ as for the decoration, it has a pleasant retro side: large mirror, ceramic fresco, Sarreguemines pottery etc. Attentive service.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3333116694	La Contre Allée	83 avenue Denfert-Rochereau	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.contreallee.net/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	In an unassuming side road running parallel to Avenue Denfert-Rochereau, you can expect simple, deftly crafted market-fresh fare. Smart, pared-back interior with a casual vibe. Spot on every time.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3336021246	La Fourchette du Printemps	30 rue du Printemps	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://lafourchetteduprintemps.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	In this elegant little neighbourhood bistro, the young chef has come through some top establishments. He hones the taste of quality ingredients (the menu evolves according to the market), and takes pleasure in revisiting the classics. A good place.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3337642812	La Grande Ourse	9 rue Georges-Saché	France	Paris		https://www.restaurantlagrandeourse.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This bistro named after the Ursa Major constellation has a down-to-earth decor done out in a palette of grey, plum and orange. The mouth-watering menu, concocted by a professional and focused chef, gives pride of place to fish, but doesn't exclude other fare^ the cooking is technically sound, the flavours distinct, and the ingredients of high quality.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3335912609	La Table Cachée par Michel Roth	BHV	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.bhv.fr/magasins/vivez-bhv/un-petit-creux/la-table-cachee-par-michel-roth	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	On the 5th floor of the BHV department store, this “hidden table” lies behind a mysterious green curtain - at the rear of the lingerie department! The cosy setting (all the “props” are sold in the store) is the lair of Michel Roth who crafts an enticing seasonal score (tartlet of haddock, magret of Gers duck with bigarade sauce, millefeuille pastry with Corsican clementines) and a reasonably priced first-class market-fresh menu at lunchtime. The panoramic terrace commands a fantastic view of the townhall of Paris.	salluis	\N	\N
3332033146	La Table de Colette	17 rue Laplace	France	Paris	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.latabledecolette.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	With green electricity, energy-efficient appliances, seed saving and the carbon footprint of the dishes shown on the menu – everything has been thought out with eco-responsibility in mind. Vegetables and pulses, prepared in all manner of ways, take pride of place, eg the medley of lentils – stewed, emulsified and fried. And there is the odd nod to the chef's native Brittany, in the form of the cauliflower surf and turf, Guéméné andouille sausage and abalone.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3335657166	La Table du Caviste Bio	55 rue de Prony	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.latable.bio/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A few well - polished, leather footfalls from Parc Monceau and you are in this stylish restaurant combining a modern dining room and food that is in tune with current tastes, fresh and subtle, concocted by Japanese culinary artist, Junko Kawasaki. The matching wines are naturally organic.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3335781304	LAVA - Cuisine & Vin	9 rue de la Montagne-Sainte-Geneviève	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	http://www.lava-paris.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	How do you combine a chef's passion for volcanoes and fire with a sommelier's passion for his craft? This restaurant unites the talents of two hospitality professionals who cut their teeth in renowned establishments. As for the food: the chef serves up his particularly tempting brand of cuisine based on flames and hot coals. French produce is meticulously combined with ingredients that are full of character – often spices – brought back by the chef from his many travels. A case in point: poultry from the Perche area grilled over binchotan, early courgettes and calçots (green onions), poultry jus with juniper. A lively, colourful feast, enhanced by a wide-ranging wine list.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3339950438	LAZU	47 rue Marguerite-de-Rochechouart	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lazu.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The chef was second in command to Bruno Doucet for three years at La Régalade St-Honoré – so he knows the ropes! Here, he serves up well-crafted bistronomy fare with inspired associations of high-quality seasonal ingredients. The menu changes weekly, but specialities such as caramelised veal sweetbreads and pâté with a potato crust have been permanent fixtures since the restaurant opened. Inviting atmosphere.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3339641645	Le 39V	39 avenue George-V	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.le39v.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	International customers flock to the sixth floor of 39 Avenue George V... and for good reason! Overlooking the rooftops of Paris, you will enjoy consummately crafted, polished French food. After a major makeover, every detail, from the wooden parquet floor to the made-to-measure seating and the haute couture crockery, has been preened and pondered over. The epitome of understated luxury!	novakmonica	\N	\N
3330862953	Le 6	6 rue Paul-Bert	France	Paris	Counter dining		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Le 6 (formerly Le 6 Paul Bert) received a facelift ahead of its reopening with chef Pauline Séné (Top Chef) at the helm. With its bistro-style furniture, zinc-topped bar for guests to eat at, and tightly packed old-school café tables and chairs, the restaurant is in full swing – in fact, it is often fully booked. The appealing menu achieves a balance of delicacy and indulgence, showcasing the ingredient without ever overdoing it, for instance smoked tarama, trout roe, focaccia and wakame^ monkfish, celeriac, beurre blanc, blackberry nori and katsuobushi.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3331782200	Montée	9 rue Léopold-Robert	France	Paris		https://restaurant-montee.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This is what you get when a talented Japanese chef decides to share his love of French cuisine: graphic presentation of the food and solid technical skill. The stripped-back designer decor adds to the experience.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3338764126	Le Bistrot Flaubert	10 rue Gustave-Flaubert	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.bistrotflaubert.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Abutting its parent establishment, Maison Rostang, this Parisian eatery has been an iconic feature of its neighbourhood for several decades, rolling out well-crafted, big-boned dishes. This authentic bistro, which is as popular with politicians as with businesspeople, sports rows of wooden shelves lined with bottles of wine and a few vintage Michelin guides! Formerly of Contraste, chef Erwan Ledru signs a modern score in tune with the seasons, adding a new twist to satisfying Gallic staples, such as a spicy jus that adds a kick to corn-fed duck from Landes, cooked whole.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3331395574	Le Bon Saint-Pourçain	10 bis rue Servandoni	France	Paris	Terrace	https://www.bonsaintpourcain.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	Tucked away behind St Sulpice church in the heart of the high - brow Saint Germain des Prés district, this former 'bougnat' restaurant reopened in the spring of 2015. Bistro traditions with a modern twist depict the delicious food – doubtless due to the high quality fresh produce. Booking advisable!	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3338393408	Le Chateaubriand	129 avenue Parmentier	France	Paris	Interesting wine list	http://www.lechateaubriand.net	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Basque chef Iñaki Aizpitarte attracts an international clientele of food lovers with his unadulterated French bistro in this institution that wholeheartedly embraces the bistronomy movement, of which he was one of the initiators. The place has retained its original interior decor, the likes of which you would have come across in the 1930s, which it juxtaposes with a neo-retro mix of zinc, slate, high ceilings and narrow tables. Their winning formula is a single set menu with original marriages of flavours. Ingredients and wines are carefully selected from independent producers. Reservations are essential.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3338598819	Le Christine	1 rue Christine	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://lechristine.becsparisiens.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	In a quiet little street, you will spot the inviting façade of this restaurant, where the conviviality and generosity are first apparent on the (short and appetising) menu, then in the nicely crafted dishes, which always include a vegetarian option. Thank you, Christine, and see you soon.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3339325962	Le Comptoir Boutary	32 rue Catherine-de-la-Rochefoucauld	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	http://www.comptoir-boutary.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	The third restaurant of the famous caviar-producing family is all about simplicity and conviviality, with its chic bistro atmosphere and open kitchen. Chef Nicolas Arnould makes a convincing case with his contemporary cuisine and, as you would expect, the house's flagship ingredient features in some of his well-crafted dishes: smoked potato with bergamot, Bordier seaweed butter, Isigny PDO crème fraîche and caviar^ caviar and cocoa tart – the scoop of sturgeon roe lends a pleasant salty note to the chocolate flavours. The set lunch menu is a real bargain.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3337622368	Le Cornichon	34 rue Gassendi	France	Paris		https://lecornichon.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Armed with a CV that pulls no punches (Atelier Guy Martin, Lucas Carton, Grand Véfour), Sébastien Dagoneau has been working wonders since taking over Le Cornichon in January 2020. True to his word, he cooks up a fresh and tasty take on ingredient-led cuisine. This is as neo-bistro as it gets, with game in season and a fantastic list of organic and natural wines. Enjoy dishes such as beef chuck lasagne with sauce diable and a crunchy choux bun filled with a Bourbon vanilla cream.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3333127534	Le Cotte Rôti	1 rue de Cotte	France	Paris		https://lecotteroti.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	A restaurant made very much in the image of the friendly, exuberant chef , who brings a touch of finesse to bistro tradition: depending on the market and the mood of the day, he composes delicious, indulgent dishes that hit the mark! Memories of the slow-cooked egg with leek, Morteau sausage and hollandaise sauce. And there's nothing like a few Rhône Valley wines to accompany the food.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3337802280	Le Gentil	26 rue Surcouf	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This restaurant on the rue Surcouf, a street strewn with eateries, is the work of a Japanese pair, chef Fumitoshi Kumagai in the kitchen and his wife front of house. They propose contemporary French cuisine with the occasional Asian influence, such as pig's trotters stuffed with pak choi and beef faux-filet with a Japanese sauce.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3331771062	Le Grand Bain	14 rue Dénoyez	France	Paris		https://www.legrandbainparis.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	In the bustling heart of Belleville, we love this hip bistro and its authentic industrial workshop vibe, complete with a central island counter, glazed partitions, untreated materials (brick and concrete) and numbered tables. Tuck into tasty small dishes – chalked up on the blackboard. The funky playlist reflects the tastes of the hipster night owls and discerning foodies who flock here.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3334473534	Le Matré	42 rue Véron	France	Paris		http://www.lematre.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Just off rue Lepic, this small bistro with a contemporary feel is tucked away in the heart of the Abbesses quarter. The interior keeps things simple: exposed stone walls, floor-to-ceiling window, modern furniture and an open kitchen. At the helm is Lucas Tresse (formerly at Yves Camdeborde's Avant Comptoir), who takes inspiration from the food markets to deliver his straightforward take on contemporary cuisine. The intentionally short menu changes regularly to align with available produce and the chef's imagination: porcini, gnocchi, red wine sauce^ breaded pork loin, sautéed mushrooms, celery purée. A reasonably priced option in Paris, which prioritises spontaneity and super-fresh ingredients.	montanarijack	\N	\N
3331439103	Le Mermoz	16 rue Jean-Mermoz	France	Paris	Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.lemermozparis.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	It is easy to see why this convivial neo-bistro located close to the Champs Elysées is always busy! Diners are won over by bistronomy-style cuisine that strikes a balance between tradition and modernity: impeccable produce, punchy, indulgent dishes and distinctive flavours. The reasonably priced wine list features an interesting selection of organic and natural wines.	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3339066747	Le Saint-Sébastien	42 rue Saint-Sébastien	France	Paris	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.lesaintsebastien.paris/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	It's an enticing offer in this neighbourhood bar turned into a hub of bistronomie cooking: a short menu that respects the seasons, very vegetable oriented, a judicious choice of seasonings, masterful use of herbs and spices to add character to the dishes… not to mention good natural wines. Spot on.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3330838437	Le Servan	32 rue Saint-Maur	France	Paris	Counter dining	https://leservan.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	On the watch of Katia and Tatiana Levha, two Filipino sisters, this place has blossomed into one of the most popular bistros in Paris (booking essential). The interior puts its best foot forward, showing off its period frescoes. Tatiana put her English studies on hold in order to indulge her twin passions of eating and cooking! Trained in the establishments of Alain Passard and Pascal Barbot, she creates lively and cheerful cuisine, French but with a good measure of Asian influences. Indeed, just the right amount of chilli is used to spice up a number of recipes. Particular care goes into the sauces and jus, such as the soy and chilli butter on the pork and langoustine ravioli, and the saffron bisque and rouille served with sea bass, fennel and kale.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3332253939	Les Ombres	27 quai Jacques-Chirac	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lesombres-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	On the roof terrace of the Musée Quai Branly – Jacques Chirac, this entirely glass-sided restaurant boasting interior and exterior architecture designed by Jean Nouvel overlooks the nearby Eiffel Tower. The menu, supervised by Alain Ducasse, is skilfully executed by talented chef Alexandre Sempere, a trusted collaborator. The modern seasonal cuisine is made with fine ingredients and smacks of the Mediterranean influences beloved of its mentor.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3330363839	Magma	9 rue Jean-Pierre-Timbaud	France	Paris		http://www.restaurantmagma.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Like magma, Japanese chef Ryuya Ono fusions French haute cuisine with his own constantly renewed inspiration and gourmet instincts in a tasting menu that shows the greatest respect for the seasons. Spot-on associations are the chef’s hallmark, illustrated by trout garnished with chanterelle mushrooms. The desserts, like the squash-flavoured creamy mont-blanc delight, are equally inventive. Crisp, elegant interior and slick service.	de santistobias	\N	\N
3336878842	Maison	3 rue Saint-Hubert	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.maison-sota.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Sota Atsumi, whose CV boasts lofty establishments such as Le Clown, Toyo, Michel Troisgros in Roanne, etc., transports diners with his Gallic cuisine imbued with modernity, served as a set menu composed of the best market-fresh ingredients. The fashionable dining area calls to mind a post-industrial loft with its gabled ceiling, huge central table d'hôte and open-plan kitchen (with a wood-fired oven), extended by a bar. Dishes include Mediterranean red tuna, grilled white asparagus and garlic sabayon or grilled scorpion fish and turnips… Pleasantly casual vibe.	semenovirene	\N	\N
3330475983	Maison Brut	18 rue d'Abbeville	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	http://www.maisonbrutparis.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	This elegant contemporary restaurant perfectly reflects the spirit of Breton chef Bastien Djait. After a MICHELIN-star-studded run in Paris, he now expresses himself through lovely inspired dishes: green lentils with sweet onion^ cod with cod's head and sea vegetables^ poultry, corn and camelina. Respect for the raw ingredient is a golden rule, and the chef only works with French produce - except for the coffee. Attentive service.	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3333202546	Mamagoto	5 rue des Petits-Hôtels	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://mamagoto.paris/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Mamagoto is Japanese for tea party. Seasoned chef Koji Tsuchiya serves an appealing selection of dishes you can share (or not!), combining Japanese and Basque influences – for example, sea urchin with parsley sayon or grilled squid with pesto. The wine list includes some unusual natural wines. A simpler set menu at lunchtime.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3337818986	Mensae	23 rue Melingue	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.mensae-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Cuisine of the moment, full of freshness and with spot-on flavours. Among the classics, on the menu all year round, the frogs' legs, garlic and parsley or the mousse au chocolat praliné are good enough to spark a riot. The decor has the good taste to make itself discreet. The small sidewalk terrace is welcome in summer.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3333613959	Mieux	21 rue Saint-Lazare	France	Paris		https://www.mieux-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Three long-standing partners have opened this friendly address, the archetype of unapologetic bistronomie that satisfies the taste buds without breaking the bank. The food pays tribute to the market and quality produce, with dishes always in tune with the season. Friendly, unpretentious vibe and great value for money at lunchtime.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3334592118	Milagro	85 avenue Bosquet	France	Paris		https://www.milagroparis.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	An American chef who was born in New Mexico, Justin Kent honed his skills with the likes of Alain Passard and David Toutain. His dinky neo-vintage bistro couldn’t be more bang on: white marble and oak counter, parquet floor, light wooden tables, vintage green velvet wooden armchairs. International and Parisian bistronomic influences happily rub shoulders in the kitchen: fritters of chorizo and sweet potatoes, Greek yoghurt^ lamb chops, emulsion of sweetcorn, risotto of spelt^ creamy delight of celeriac with white chocolate, ice cream and meringues.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3339473779	Mokko	3 rue Francœur	France	Paris		https://mokko-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	A latecomer to catering (he started off in the music business), Arthur Hantz has adopted a no-holds barred, complex-free approach and his trendy, buzzy bistro at the foot of Montmartre gets right down to brass tacks. The formula is fiendishly effective: market-fresh ingredients, creative recipes and bags of enthusiasm with the guarantee of a slap-up meal every time! Examples include: lightly seared black pudding, salad and prunes to start^ line-caught hake, carrots confit in spices, a beurre blanc and olives and a mousse of 80% cacao nibs and fleur de sel – simple, straightforward and spot on!	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3336263896	Monsieur Bleu	20 avenue de New-York	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://monsieurbleu-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	For a location in Paris, it would be hard to do better than this address... Nestled in the Palais de Tokyo, it is superb with its Art Deco interior in a palette of grey, green and gold, and its terrace looking out over the Seine and the Eiffel Tower. Not to be outdone by the setting, the food is sophisticated and tasty. A very high - profile place!	langalice	\N	\N
3335499779	Montcalm	21 rue Montcalm	France	Paris		https://www.restaurant-montcalm.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This is a pleasant neighbourhood bistro, where the tattooed chef sporting a hipster look uses selected market - fresh ingredients. It's well put together, with bold flavours finely teased out. The menu evolves depending on the consignment from Rungis Market.	raduionela	\N	\N
3335157595	Néva Cuisine	2 rue de Berne	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.nevacuisineparis.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The Neva is not only a river in Russia, but also the name of this restaurant, headed by Mexican chef Beatriz González, after completing stints in top establishments including Lucas Carton and La Grande Cascade. In a friendly, modern Parisian bistro setting, she conjures up modern, multi-facetted cuisine, illustrated by blow torch-seared foie gras, smoked eel and dashi stock, or skate meunière with spring vegetables and a gutsy aïoli. Everything tastes of something here.	basileryan	\N	\N
3331080045	Nonos par Paul Pairet	Le Crillon	France	Paris	Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/fr/hotel-de-crillon/dining/nonos-comestibles-paul-pairet	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	In addition to L'Écrin, Hotel Crillon on the Place de la Concorde has this smart brasserie with an Art Deco interior in its portfolio. The chef entrusted with devising its menu is Paul Pairet, well known to the French at this point in time. He pays homage to the grills of his childhood (in the form of a fine selection of matured meats) and brasserie classics (oysters, tartare, Caesar salad, sole meunière etc). And, it must be said, the bill is affordable for such a place. Their sole objective is to create good food out of good ingredients.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3338724227	Nosso	22 promenade Claude-Lévi-Strauss	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.nosso-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	Brazilian-born chef Alessandra Montagne is delighted to be in her new restaurant, which has an inviting contemporary interior featuring a preponderance of concrete and wood as well as floor-to-ceiling windows. Her recipe for success (and pleasure) comprises meticulous plating, seasonal, locally sourced ingredients, a whirlwind of flavours and a patchwork of influences (from Brazil to Asia). Zero waste and 100% natural. Tasting menus in the evening.	raduionela	\N	\N
3334966529	Odette	25 rue du Pont-Neuf	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.maison-albar-hotels-le-pont-neuf.com/fr/page/restaurant-odette-paris.2488.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Two steps from Les Halles, in the luxurious Albar Hotel, the Rostang family demonstrates that they haven’t lost their touch in this urban inn. Odette regales us with dishes to be shared: sea bass in a pastry crust, one of the house’s signature dishes, veal chops, roast guinea fowl. Each dish showcases the chef’s hallmark talent.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3334830517	Oktobre	25 rue des Grands-Augustins	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://oktobre.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	In one of the most bookish streets of the scholarly St André des Arts neighbourhood, Oktobre is warm and welcoming, like an Indian summer. The chef's pantry is stocked with only the finest, painstakingly sourced produce (he buys some animals whole). He takes a fresh, delicate, natural approach to cooking, deftly seasoning his dishes with varied spices and Asian accents. “Dentelles de Cucugnan” cuttlefish pasta with a shellfish bisque^ Dombes quail, buckwheat risotto with mushrooms, fig and gochujang pickles^ figs topped with a shiso-scented diplomat cream…	beckerradu	\N	\N
3337577773	Origines Restaurant	6 rue de Ponthieu	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.origines-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	In this contemporary restaurant, Aveyron-born chef Julien Boscus finetunes bold, crisp cuisine thanks to a solid classical background. His genuine à la carte lineup (something of a rarity these days…) showcases intelligently crafted, flavoursome dishes made with first-class seasonal produce. Examples include a delicious crispy tartlet filled with morel mushrooms creamed in sous-voile wine, or sautéed calf sweetbreads with green asparagus from Vaucluse steamed in citron, while his amazing hare à la royale, reworked in a more modern vein, deserves a special mention. The wine list stars an impressive selection from France's vineyards, served by a slick, professional team. Friendly and endearing!	grafpaola	\N	\N
3339140771	Otto	5 rue Mouffetard	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.otto-paris.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	A welcome addition to the rue Mouffetard: this bistro with a minimalist decor comprising concrete floor and ceiling is modelled on the Japanese izakaya. Under the leadership of chef Eric Trochon, Otto proposes a cuisine for sharing based on a short menu that revolves around the produce, simply accompanied by a condiment or a sauce for that extra kick. Hence chimichurri, sauce vierge or diable, ponzu sauce or lemon condiment are served alongside meat and fish, often cooked over binchotan coals. Please note that they don't take bookings.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3337472171	Passionné	17 rue Bergère	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantpassionne.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Set back from Grands Boulevards, this restaurant plays the minimalist card: a bar with midnight blue mosaics, dark walls and floor and refined lighting. A very Japanese brand of elegance, designed for this location officiated by chef Satoshi Horiuchi, originally from Hokkaido island, a few kilometres from Sapporo, a prefecture with a high concentration of small-scale producers, especially market gardeners. Horiuchi is as passionate as ever about creating a modern French cuisine characterised by his quest to find quality ingredients and cook them perfectly.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3339525587	Petit Boutary	16 rue Jacquemont	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	https://www.petitboutary.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Petit Boutary is certainly living up to the standard set for it by Boutary, its Left Bank counterpart. In this refined bistro, with its chequered floor, zinc-topped bar, leather-clad banquette seating and hanging light bulbs, modern, creative cuisine is served in the form of a single menu with several courses.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3336735078	Petit Gris	67 rue Rennequin	France	Paris	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Jean-Baptiste Ascione, a former Top Chef contestant, dreamed of opening his own restaurant. Now he has done so in this cosy space (oak floorboards, sanded wooden tables, bistro chairs etc), which celebrates the joys of breaking bread together, by drawing on fine terroir produce and the traditional culinary repertoire.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3331072839	Pilgrim	8 rue Nicolas-Charlet	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.pilgrimparis.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Hideki Nishi (owner of Neige d'Été in Paris) has entrusted Yurika Kitano with the cuisine of this restaurant near Montparnasse. In a central and slightly raised kitchen, the chef crafts her elegant, delicate dishes, like tiny masterpieces influenced by France and Japan. This paradise for our tastebuds looks all set to become a place of pilgrimage for foodies.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3334764612	Pleine Terre	15 rue de Bassano	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurant-pleineterre.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Behind a discreet façade, down the few steps leading to the basement, you will find a chef who is passionate about citrus fruits, spices and pepper: he has developed a cuisine that closely follows the seasons and showcases the work of handpicked small-scale producers. An inventive array of dishes, served by a friendly and enthusiastic front-of-house team: a great find.	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3333196275	Plume	24 rue Pierre-Leroux	France	Paris		https://www.restaurantplume.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Born in Tunis, the chef brings a touch of diversity and plenty of talent to this small street near Le Bon Marché. Diners squeeze into this tiny bistro to tuck in to seamless cuisine that is perfectly in tune with the seasons, such as a silky cream of celeriac soup with an intense and slightly spicy taste! Reasonably priced lunch menu and ambitious tasting menu in the evening.	costasergio	\N	\N
3336443909	Pouliche	11 rue d'Enghien	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.poulicheparis.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	In this friendly neo-bistro, Amandine Chaignot fetes market produce, spontaneity and creativity, without ever betraying the flavours of her carefully selected ingredients. Indeed, that is the approach that has informed her single set menu: only the main course is chosen by the guest – meat, fish or vegetarian – with the rest of the meal left to the chef's discretion. On Wednesdays, the set menu is entirely vegetarian. On Sundays, you can enjoy traditional family-style chicken dishes. Good value for money at lunchtime. Pouliche will steal your heart.	carlinikita	\N	\N
3338704811	Restaurant F	10 rue Saint-Didier	France	Paris		https://www.restaurantf.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This compact little restaurant with a chic, contemporary decor exudes a friendly vibe. The Spanish-born chef (who previously headed up the kitchens at Hôtel Raphaël and worked for Hélène Darroze) devises a concise menu of refined modern cuisine, carefully prepared, with meticulously plated dishes: potato fondant with truffle^ sea bass, celery and liquorice^ crunchy meringue with figs.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3333537396	Restaurant Le Dalí	Le Meurice	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.dorchestercollection.com/fr/paris/le-meurice	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	f	The second restaurant of Le Meurice, located at the centre of the action at the luxury hotel, is a place to meet and to enjoy appealing seasonal cuisine peppered with understated Mediterranean touches, as well as the great classics associated with luxury hotel dining. The beautiful decor – pilasters and mirrors – pays tribute to Dalí, who was a regular patron.	marinescumario	\N	\N
3338677705	Rooster	137 rue Cardinet	France	Paris		http://rooster-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	After training in prestigious houses (from Passedat to Darroze), Frédéric Duca has set up shop in the more working-class part of the 17th arrondissement. In a former street corner cafe, the Marseille-born chef signs dishes which pay numerous tributes to his Mediterranean and Provençal roots. The lunchtime menu is at delicious eater-friendly prices. More ambitious in the evenings.	benesemily	\N	\N
3331299699	Sancerre Rive Gauche	22 avenue Rapp	France	Paris		https://www.sancerrerivegauche.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	In this upmarket neighbourhood, Sancerre denotes a hill, a wine and even a great little Parisian restaurant – a location once run by the great Sancerre winegrower, Alphonse Mellot. In a modern bistro atmosphere, Anne-Cécile Faye, no stranger to the art of hospitality, extends an exuberant welcome. As for chef Éric Lecerf, he cooks up humble dishes from French popular tradition and the effect is as remarkable as it is cheering: different pâtés, offal and other filling foods, plus stuffed cabbage – the house specialty. Everything is presented on the counter^ whole pies and cakes are cut to order by the waiter.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3336021368	Shirvan Café Métisse	5 place de l'Alma	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.shirvancafemetisse.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	This restaurant near Pont de l'Alma is the brainchild of Akrame Benallal. Starched white linen has given way to designer cutlery and, first and foremost, a menu inspired by the Silk Road from Morocco to India via Azerbaijan. A delicious melting pot seasoned with a wealth of spices, as in the vegetarian tikki or the confit lamb chops with home-made harissa... Efficient service and you can eat at almost any time of the day.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3338415771	Soces	32 rue de la Villette	France	Paris		http://www.soces.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	A gem of a Parisian brasserie, where Marius de Ponfilly, formerly chef at Clamato, has teamed up with Kevin Deulio. Previously at Bar Vendôme in The Ritz, the latter has taken to the restaurant floor like a duck to water. The pair have found a formula that is as irreverent as it is on point: choice cuts of meat and plates to be shared between friends (aka soces in Parisian slang), not forgetting their trademark fish and seafood… We recommend the Pyrenean trout and its indulgent basil sauce, or the delicious wedge clams from Le Guilvinec in a spicy parsley sauce.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3331956176	Sourire Le Restaurant	15 rue de la Santé	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.sourire-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Blue velours banquette seating, old-school bistro tables, trusted farmers (Galician pink veal, Clavisy Farm lamb): the tried-and-tested formula hits the spot, a case in point being the Bay of Morlaix scallops, medley of cabbage, candied lemon. The lunchtime set menu provides two options for every course. A second restaurant in the 5th arrondissement serves tapas in the evening and brunch at the weekend.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3335528587	Table Penja	2 rue Sédillot	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://tablepenja.paris	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	After a successful stint at Le Garde-Temps in Pigalle, Cameroon-born chef Pierre Siewe now runs this restaurant with a modern bistro decor, where the warm interior is subtly reminiscent of Africa. As for the food, this former mentee of Yves Camdeborde seasons his local bistronomy with African spices (djansang, pebe, turmeric and the famous Penja pepper) and ingredients (hibiscus, yam, cocoa etc). This approach lends his dishes a unique personality: the perfectly braised chuck of beef is spiced up with a coffee, caper, red onion and hibiscus mustard condiment^ the classic Mont Blanc dessert is accompanied by a green peppercorn ice cream that brings a fruity, invigorating freshness to the dessert.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3330630228	Tadam	14 rue du Jura	France	Paris		https://www.tadam-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This delightful little eatery proposes a brief, seasonal and mouth-watering menu, underscored by a commitment to sustainable development. The food hits the spot every time thanks to tip-top ingredients stripped of unnecessary frills, illustrated by the scrumptious hot mushroom pie. A casual vibe and brunch on Sundays. A welcome addition to the Gobelins culinary scene.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3332933528	Terra	21 rue des Gravilliers	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.terraparis.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	A corridor leads to this restaurant, established beneath a glass roof in the courtyard of an old Parisian building, whose vibe is part winter garden, part neo-industrial. Youthful Louis Gallet works wholeheartedly and effectively to transform carefully selected ingredients: egg parfait, lemon confit-flavoured houmous^ barbecued Simmental steak, Choron sauce^ chocolate and blackcurrant-flavoured sponge cake. The main dishes are to share (bellota pork, chimichurri sauce^ Basque veal cutlet with Choron sauce). Well-curated, sensibly priced wine list.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3338474645	Towa	75 rue Crozatier	France	Paris		https://www.towarestaurantparis.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Japanese chef Shin Okusa is at the helm of the Towa, close to the bustling Aligre market. A champion of old-school French culinary traditions and a true disciple of Escoffier, he not only whisks up the great classics (French lamb stew, breast of duck in flaky pastry), but also sauces, hot terrines and pies, with superlative skill and flair.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3330108867	Le Chardenoux	1 rue Jules-Vallès	France	Paris		https://restaurantlechardenoux.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	In this Parisian bistro founded by the Chardenoux family and a listed historic monument, the eye wanders from the beautiful painted ceiling to the Art nouveau details, before it is drawn back to the business at hand, the enticing menu in front of us. Fish and seafood are the name of the game here, including Lignac’s iconic signature dishes: lobster roll, salt-crusted sea bass, tuna tartar, avocado, ponzu, wasabi, without forgetting the decadent millefeuille or the rum baba! We fell in love with the crunchy savoury pancake of curry-flavoured crab and avocado: a masterpiece of balanced flavours.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3339744761	Halle aux Grains	Bourse de Commerce	France	Paris	Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.halleauxgrains.bras.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€€€	t	t	Not only is the old corn exchange home to part of the Pinault Collection, it also houses a highly creative restaurant. In homage to the history of the building, Michel and Sébastien Bras take seeds, cereals and legumes as their starting point and cook up healthy and contemporary cuisine. Be sure to sample a tasty dessert, such as their take on the Paris-Brest: choux pastry meets pumpkin seed cream in a crunchy praline affair. Unbeatable view of the rooftops of Paris.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3339378866	Bloom Garden	Bloom House	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://bloomhouse-hotel.com/restaurant/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€€	f	t	This restaurant channels the spirit of the Mediterranean, from the hardwood floors covered with Berber rugs to the wicker hanging baskets set against a backdrop of zellige-tiled walls. In fine weather, tables are set out by the pool on the lovely interior patio. Chef Olivier Streiff, who arrived on the scene in 2015 as a contestant on Top Chef, has created a bold, colourful menu that is also inspired by southern climes. Veal tournedos, pan-fried polenta and liquorice^ molten chocolate cake with candied pepper^ lemon tartlet with chicory chutney – the chef has lost none of his verve, nor his taste for shaking up culinary conventions.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3332819150	Perception	53 rue Blanche	France	Paris		https://www.restaurant-perception.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	4.0	€€€	f	t	A friendly and contemporary bistro, with exposed stone and dark green walls, mirrors and velvet banquettes. A Korean chef, who is passionate about French gastronomy, creates modern cuisine with occasional nods to his home country, and it proves to be a winning formula: for example, his starter of burrata, duck breast, basil/arugula pesto and sesame. In the evening, he pulls out all the stops, with premium ingredients and more sophisticated dishes (and a tasting menu).	voicucatu	\N	\N
3333450521	a.lea	39 rue Lamarck	France	Paris		https://www.alearestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	a.lea is a play on words, referring to change (‘aléas’) and the name of the talented chef, Léa Lestage, who dabbled in sociology at uni before rolling up her sleeves in the kitchens of the Polisson and the Bristol’s Épicure. Examples of her appetising bistronomic cuisine include creamy soft-boiled egg, cream of green peas, apricots, feta and verbena^ duckling, sweet potatoes, blood orange, mild curry seasoning and gravy… Léa’s spot-on recipes feature a market-fresh slant with a bargain-priced lunchtime (including Saturdays) menu. More elaborate and more expensive in the evenings. Also a chef, William Atlan warmly manages the front-of-house experience.	popafarah	\N	\N
3339405047	Le Maquis	53 rue des Cloÿs	France	Paris		https://lemaquisrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	t	Paul Boudier and Albert Touton, ex-Le Chateaubriand, deliver succulent, no-nonsense bistro nosh, like thick country soup, sausage and mash and indulgent crumble in a nostalgic setting (zinc bar counter and leatherette banquette seating) amidst a lively, buzzy vibe. Unbeatable value for money at lunchtime^ more ambitious set menu with several courses in the evening. Hits all the right buttons!	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3332609796	Pétrelle	34 rue Pétrelle	France	Paris		https://www.petrelle.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€€	t	f	Chef Lucie Boursier-Mougenot and sommelier Luca Danti, formerly at Caves Legrand, have revamped this restaurant once frequented by celebrities. In a romantic and intimate boudoir setting that is decorated with flea-market pieces, the chef serves lovely, delicate and healthy market-fresh cuisine with strong Mediterranean influences. Good wine cellar with over 150 references, for all budgets.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3332914597	Pianovins	46 rue Trousseau	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	http://www.pianovins.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	Both formerly of the Guy Savoy, Michel Roncière and Éric Mancio have joined forces: the first in the kitchen, the second in the wine cellar. The menu is well designed and prepared according to market availability. Meals are served in a small dining room (20 seats at tightly packed tables) with an open kitchen and counter dining.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3337366098	La Traboule	27 rue de Penthièvre	France	Paris		https://restaurantlatraboule.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Italian	5.0	€€€	f	t	Just a few hundred metres from the Élysée Palace, this establishment sports a fashionable bistro interior and a buzzy vibe. The food errs towards well-crafted bistronomic courtesy of simple recipes that focus on big-boned, legible flavours.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3339788587	Le Sirocco	8 bis rue des Gobelins	France	Paris		https://restaurantlesirocco.fr/	Nessun premio	Moroccan	3.0	€€	f	t	The warm air of the Sirocco has reached Les Gobelins, bringing its fragrances of tajines, couscous and hariras into the old stables of the Château de la Reine Blanche, where this Moroccan restaurant with typical decor is located. The owner himself imports the argan oil that flavours his traditional dishes. Of course the couscous itself is home-made, and very fine, just as it should be.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3333198444	Brasserie Lutetia	45 boulevard Raspail	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotellutetia.com/fr/gastronomie-paris/brasserie/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	t	f	Tartare of wild sea bass, sole meunière, Burgundy snails with parsley butter: the famous Brasserie Lutetia proudly serves the classics that have made its reputation, as well as some more contemporary creations. Purists and regulars alike can't get enough of the easy-going refined Art Deco atmosphere. Conservatory, mezzanine or patio: take your pick!	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3339616395	Dessirier	9 place du Maréchal-Juin	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantdessirier.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Contemporary, arty and chic: Dessirier is the Rostang family's flagship restaurant. It attaches a great deal of importance to the fish selection: bouillabaisse and sole meunière are among the signature dishes.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3331918987	Le Duc	243 boulevard Raspail	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://restaurantleduc.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€€	f	t	Despite being in the heart of the Left Bank, you would be forgiven for thinking you were in the cabin of a yacht packed with seafaring acolytes… The chef works with first-rate fish and seafood and is a consummate craftsman: tartare of langoustine with black lemon, sole meunière, lobster sautéed with orange, grilled John Dory… All aboard!	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3335579832	Marius et Janette	4 avenue George-V	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking	https://mariusetjanette-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€€	f	t	This elegant yacht-style décor, replete with fishing rods, nets and copper portholes, caters to discerning food lovers. The chef highlights fish and seafood, with a menu that is renewed daily, according to the catch. Carpaccio of salmon and basil, grilled seabass to share or linguine with lobster (a house speciality): a festival of flavours!	caputostefan	\N	\N
3330545173	Prunier par Yannick Alléno	16 avenue Victor-Hugo	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Brunch,Valet parking	http://www.prunier.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Adorned with the work of some of the greatest mosaicists, engravers and sculptors of the Art deco period, the lavish interior of Prunier is well worth a trip in its own right. The menu, signed Yannick Alléno, gives pride of place to seafood and Prunier’s legendary caviar, of course.We recommend house signature dishes, such as the Christian Dior Egg (poached and sprinkled with caviar) or fish to be shared.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3336585405	VIVE, Maison Mer	62 avenue des Ternes	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.vive-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	t	f	Alsace-born restaurateur Adrien Rech opened this institution dedicated to seafood in 1925. After Ducasse, it is now the turn of David and Stéphanie Le Quellec, whose Breton name alone smacks of the ocean, to celebrate fish and shellfish cuisine. The decor is sumptuous, with its huge bar, dining area on the first floor and long banquette seating. David Le Quellec serves food that is good for sharing and made with excellent, ultra-fresh ingredients from fish markets spanning France, from the Atlantic to the Mediterranean. The ceviche of sea bream with coconut milk, lime and coriander is already a house classic – not to mention the dishes prepared from fish matured on site in the maturing cellar.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3334627123	Lao Lane Xang 2	102 avenue d'Ivry	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	South East Asian	4.0	€	f	t	The Parisian chapter of the history of the Siackhasones, originally from Laos, began in the 1990s with the creation of the Lao Lane Xang 1. In 2007, Do and Ken – worthy heirs of the family know - how – opened this second restaurant. The dishes are Laotian, Thai and Vietnamese specialities. Simplicity and flavour are on the menu!	brunojulian	\N	\N
3339330653	Thaï Spices	5-7 rue de l'Ave-Maria	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.thaispices.fr	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	€€	f	f	Between Quai des Célestins and the village of Saint-Paul, this restaurant is run by Willy Lieu, who was once Jacques Chirac's personal chef! Now his own boss, he serves up a short menu of authentic Thai cuisine, including generous and flavoursome classics such as pad thai and tom yam. Prices remain reasonable^ good service. It is a popular haunt for local residents on account of its friendly, unpretentious atmosphere.	pingliu	\N	\N
3339809628	19.20 by Norbert Tarayre	Prince de Galles	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.19-20paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Built in 1928, the Prince de Galles is a legendary jewel of the Parisian Art Deco movement. It has chosen to democratise luxury hotel cuisine by entrusting its kitchens to Norbert Tarayre, the firebrand chef discovered on French TV show Top Chef in 2012. In a cosy setting that pays tribute to artistic life in Paris, the chef serves up traditional cuisine that channels the tasty regional cooking of yesteryear: grated carrot salad, leeks in vinaigrette, celeriac in remoulade dressing, pork shoulder and pommes Anna, salmon tournedos – not to mention the dessert trolley. It's all lovingly prepared and delivered. Incredibly reasonable price of the menu.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3332196087	À l’Épi d’Or	25 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau	France	Paris		https://jeanfrançoispiege.com/a-lepi-dor	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This quintessential Parisian bistro of the former Baltard market is the latest acquisition of Elodie and Jean-François Piège. The authentic vintage interior (old tiles and mirrors and stained walls) provides the setting for traditional fare that changes daily during the week. Also available: pork pie, croque madame, foie gras, steak tartare and chips.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3338757882	À La Biche au Bois	45 avenue Ledru-Rollin	France	Paris		https://alabicheaubois.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In an atmospheric interior reminiscent of historic Parisian bistros and two minutes from Lyon railway station, regulars and travellers rub shoulders as they dig into traditional no-nonsense nosh. Country terrines, Burgundy snails and Royan ravioles star alongside duck breast in honey, fillet of beef served with cèpes and foie gras or coq au vin (the house specialty), without forgetting game in season (venison and even Scottish grouse!). The crème caramel to finish is wickedly addictive…	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3337376309	Allard	41 rue Saint-André-des-Arts	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.restaurant-allard.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	In the heart of bustling Saint Germain des Près, this authentic Parisian bistro, dripping in charm and now part of the Ducasse empire, has changed very little since it opened in 1932. The culinary score wavers between bistro fare and heroic brasserie staples: snails in parsley, butter and garlic, pâté en croûte, sole meunière, profiteroles. Attractive lunchtime menu.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3337739836	Amarante	4 rue Biscornet	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.amarante.paris/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	This bistro wedged between Bastille and Lyon railway station serves a bighearted, no-nonsense score rich in nostalgic flavours. The ingredients, such as ‘triple zero’ jumbo shrimps from Nantes, Kintoa pork or monkfish caught by small fishing boats, are allowed to shout their name. The interior is equally simple and authentic: tiled floor, red imitation leather benches and wooden tables. Bags of substance and atmosphere!	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3336609797	Atelier Maître Albert	1 rue Maître-Albert	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.ateliermaitrealbert.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	An attractive medieval fireplace and roasting spits take pride of place in this handsome interior designed by J.-M. Wilmotte. Guy Savoy signs the menu which boasts a knockout cast of first-class ingredients. T-bone steak, free-range poultry, spit-roasted suckling lamb chops and leg – all that remains is to choose your side dish, for example, gratin dauphinois or purée, both crafted with text-book precision.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3339010793	Bistrot Augustin	79 rue Daguerre	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.augustin-bistrot.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Taken over by Guy Martin in 2020, this bistro still lives by the same values: a cosy setting, a small terrace on rue Daguerre, and lovely market-fresh cooking that is all about the ingredients. Rabbit terrine and red onion compote^ sautéed farm-reared quasi of veal, seasonal vegetables with country bacon. Table d'hôte to the rear and an appetising menu-carte.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3332265278	Bistrot des Fables	139 rue Saint-Dominique	France	Paris	Air conditioning	http://www.bistrotdesfables.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	A fabulous bistro repertoire of tried-and-true classics: think herring fillets, potatoes in oil^ œufs mimosa (devilled eggs)^ scallops roasted in butter^ veal blanquette^ profiteroles, vanilla ice cream and chocolate gianduja. The menu is devised by David Bottreau in the spirit of Christian Constant, his long-time associate and mentor. Generous, flavoursome cuisine in a typical Parisian bistro atmosphere, where diners tuck in cheek to jowl at small tables laid out next to each other.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3339415671	Café des Ministères	83 rue de l'Université	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.cafedesministeres.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The name of this bistro that is reminiscent of a neighbourhood café is on the lips of every fan of wonderfully rich sauces and authentic French cuisine (especially South-Western fare). The vol-au-vent with sweetbreads, poultry and truffle jus, as well as the stuffed Pontoise cabbage (French champion in 2022) have put this place on the map: book in advance!	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3331775398	Capsule	2 rue Cassini	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	http://www.capsule.restaurant	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	On the ground floor of a handsome Haussmann building, this bistro exudes Parisian charm: at the entrance, a few places at the convivial bar and a handful of tables^ to the rear, a retro-chic space (snazzy green imitation leather banquettes, white walls, vintage hanging lamps) and an open kitchen reminiscent of – you guessed it – a capsule. The chef's comforting home cooking may be simple, but it is precisely executed using fresh ingredients. The roast chicken jus is quite something! The floating island with salted butter caramel and roasted almonds confirm that the proof is in the pudding.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3337245819	Caves Pétrissans	30 bis avenue Niel	France	Paris	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.cavespetrissans.fr/fr,1,13689.html	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This splendid family business has seen successive generations of the Allemoz dynasty at the helm since 1895. Treat yourself to a chicken liver pâté with onion jam, grilled hanger steak or calf’s head with a ravigote sauce. Bistro classics also depict the dessert lineup, with regressive dishes like rum baba or île flottante. An enticing wine list adds the final cherry to this appetising programme.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3338708840	Chez Michel	10 rue de Belzunce	France	Paris	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.restaurantchezmichel.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Since 2015, Japanese chef Masahiro Kawai has been in charge of the kitchens at this restaurant steeped in history. He draws on his experience in Japan, Spain and France (working with Yves Camdeborde and Christian Etchebest) to create traditional yet cheerful bistro cuisine, in which seafood ingredients play a key role. The classics are present and correct – roast foie gras, game in season – the flavours are delicious and the cooking is precise, particularly in the case of the grilled mackerel, ratatouille and pistou.	basileryan	\N	\N
3337553805	Chez Monsieur	11 rue du Chevalier-de-Saint-George	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.chezmonsieur.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	The Parisian bistro in all its splendour (zinc countertop, velvet-upholstered wall seats, patterned tiles), with the immutable – and delicious! – cuisine that goes with it: Burgundy snails with white butter sauce, veal blanquette served in a casserole dish, not to mention a wide selection of wines from all over France.	ozmax	\N	\N
3335130696	Kigawa	186 rue du Château	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.kigawa.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Kigawa is named after Michihiro Kigawa, the chef at this refreshingly simple restaurant. Buoyed by his experience in a French restaurant in Osaka, he now finds himself in Paris, delighting guests with classic French dishes such as pâté en croûte and roast pigeon.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3337212815	L'Ami Jean	27 rue Malar	France	Paris		https://lamijean.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Passionate about fine seasonal produce, Stéphane Jégo serves cuisine that is bursting with generosity and flavours. Dishes with quite some character! Be sure to book.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3336838702	L'Ardoise	28 rue du Mont-Thabor	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://lardoise-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant, whose walls are covered in slate, wears its name well! It pays a pleasing tribute to bistro heritage by means of its style and also its food – chicken pâté en croûte, foie gras and ceps^ fillet of beef with black pepper and pommes Anna^ lemon meringue tartlet^ crème brûlée – a feast of generous, fresh and tasty dishes!	martinooliver	\N	\N
3337853798	L'Os à Moelle	3 rue Vasco-de-Gama	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Thierry Faucher is still in charge of L'Os à Moelle, where, in the early 2000s, he secured his position as one of the forerunners of France's bistronomy movement. Aubergine dip, soft-boiled egg and country ham^ leg of lamb and vegetable fricassee^ bone marrow^ soup of the day… It's simple, delicious and indulgent fare.	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3333717306	La Poule au Pot	9 rue Vauvilliers	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://jeanfrançoispiege.com/la-poule-au-pot	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	The great classics of the French culinary repertoire are given an overhaul here by Jean-François Piège. Service on a silver tray, old-fashioned bistro decor, zinc counter: it has all the trappings. It's Audiard's Paris down to a T... right down to the food: onion gratinée, quenelle of arctic char, beef chuck hash, Colbert fried whiting with tartar sauce.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3333908583	La Régalade Saint-Honoré	106 rue Saint-Honoré	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://laregalade.paris/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Bruno Doucet regales foodies in the Halles neighbourhood with dishes that sing an ode to fresh market and country produce. After titillating your tastebuds with the chef's delicious terrine, dig into pan-fried snails, mushrooms and chorizo, followed by braised chuck steak with a bourguignon garnish or the “famous” rice pudding with a dairy caramel. Fine wine list.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3330684836	Lazare	Parvis de la gare Saint-Lazare	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://lazare-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	In the heart of the famous Gare St - Lazare is this elegant railway brasserie, version 2013. It is the brainchild of Éric Frechon, who respects the canons of the genre: French - style devilled eggs, pike quenelles or mackerel in a white wine sauce. Fine French tradition is right on track! Pleasant and very lively.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3338167238	Le 703	9 rue Fourcroy	France	Paris		http://www.le703.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Navigating between France and Japan, chef Naomi Ogaki trained in Alsace and Provence, under the tutelage of Antoine Westermann and Christian Étienne respectively. In his lovely bistro complete with a long counter, he serves high-quality traditional French cuisine that draws on influences of Alsace in autumn and winter, and of the South of France in spring and summer. House classics include pâté en croûte, game, spaetzle, home-made boudin, fish aioli – not to mention some first-rate classic desserts.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3336656067	Le Baratin	3 rue Jouye-Rouve	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Argentine chef Raquel Carena pretty much invented bistronomy, as many young chefs acknowledge. This stripped-down, retro bistro serves food that is delicate or hearty, but always personal. The blackboard menu makes pleasant reading, the prices are restrained and the wines appealing. Reservations strongly recommended.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3337559573	Le Bistrot du Maquis	69 rue Caulaincourt	France	Paris		https://www.bistrotdumaquis.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	André Le Letty, formerly of the Anacréon, has set up shop in the renowned Rue de Caulaincourt and specialises in bistro classics. Try pressed ox cheek in crystallised lemon, veal kidneys in mustard, roast hake, and not forgetting the house specialty, pressed duck served in two stages.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3335410577	Le Cadoret	1 rue Pradier	France	Paris			Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This local bistro in upper Belleville is the epitome of vintage Parisian with an old zinc-topped counter, moleskin banquettes and a mosaic tiled floor. A sister and brother team, Léa Fleuriot (in the kitchen) and Louis-Marie serve food to an arty crowd of (aspiring) actors and gourmet hipsters. Léa crafts bistro classics with intriguing modern twists, such as finely sliced potatoes, puntarella, radicchio and noisette butter^ free-range roast chicken, turnips, carrots, mushrooms and a spring onion sauce^ choux filled with chantilly cream and a drizzling of chocolate sauce. Vegetarian versions on request. Concise 100% organic wine list. Buzzy, casual atmosphere with rap music playing softly in the background.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3338988108	Le Comptoir du Relais	5 carrefour de l'Odéon	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.hotel-paris-relais-saint-germain.com/restaurant-le-comptoir	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Yves Camdeborde has entrusted the keys of his famous diminutive bistro to chef Bruno Doucet, whom he had already put in charge of La Régalade. Suffice to say, on his watch the place's bistronomy philosophy is scrupulously adhered to. In the tiny restaurant with tightly packed tables or on the heated terrace looking onto the Carrefour de l'Odéon, you can enjoy a menu (served right through from noon to 11pm, which is rare) that embraces local and market cuisine, and absolutely respects quality produce. They do not take reservations.	benesemily	\N	\N
3335587235	Le Florimond	19 avenue de La Motte-Picquet	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.leflorimond.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Florimond – named after Monet's gardener at Giverny – has a convivial bistro atmosphere. The chef makes sure to use plenty of vegetables in his traditional local cooking, featuring many ingredients from his native Corrèze. And like his father before him, who was a pork butcher, he makes all his sausages, black pudding and conserves himself!	ferraroedoardo	\N	\N
3337845720	Le Pergolèse	40 rue Pergolèse	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.lepergolese.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	While the interior is adorned in contemporary art, the food continues to celebrate classicism, in the style of a plush bourgeois home in which each guest is pampered as if they were a VIP. Unsurprisingly, the menu features a patriotic lineup of French classics: lobster, pressed leeks, quince dressing or whole roast pigeon garnished with beetroot chutney and basted in offal gravy.	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3338024104	Le Petit Lucas	9 place de la Madeleine	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://www.lucascarton.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	The bistro counterpart of Lucas Carton is accommodated on the first floor of the fine dining restaurant, in a space with a more low-key vibe (but with a view of the Église de la Madeleine). Chef Hugo Bourny's cuisine follows in the footsteps of fine French tradition (sole meunière, pâté en croute, chocolate mousse etc), thanks in particular to the quality of the ingredients used. The business menu, albeit without options, is a notable bargain in this upscale neighbourhood.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3331507493	Le Quincy	28 avenue Ledru-Rollin	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	A cosy ambience prevails in this utterly timeless establishment, which was dominated by its larger-than-life boss, “Bobosse”, for so many years. Even though he doesn’t pop in quite so often anymore, his personality continues to underscore the DNA of this haunt of foodies. For fifty odd years, fine food lovers have been digging into wholehearted, rustic dishes from Berry or Ardèche. The chef scrimps neither on quality nor quantity when it comes to the house terrine of cabbage and garlic, poultry in cream or the rum-flavoured ice cream! An establishment whose existence is almost anachronistic in today’s restaurant universe.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3331155661	Le Villaret	13 rue Ternaux	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.levillaret-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Not far from Oberkampf, this bistro serves wholesome, traditional and seasonal cuisine crafted by enthusiastic chef Olivier Gaslain. Oxtail in foie gras, pickles and a salad of garden herbs^ calf’s head, tongue and brains in a ravigote sauce and, to finish, a rum-flavoured baba with ginger and clementines flanked by a mascarpone mousse that will leave you speechless! A superb wine list with more than 1 000 labels, some of which are displayed in a splendid glazed wine cabinet.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3333404750	Les Botanistes	11 bis rue Chomel	France	Paris		https://www.lesbotanistes.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Not far from Le Bon Marché, this pleasant bistro is in the hands of a chef who does not cut corners when it comes to ingredients or taste! Take a seat on the characteristic bistro benches and dig into mouth-watering beef and shallots or a decadent rum baba smothered in whipped cream. The well-stocked wine cellar offers ample choice to pair with your meal. Friendly, tasty and casual – a winning formula!	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3338922706	Les Parisiens	1 rue du Pré-aux-Clercs	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://pavillon-faubourg-saint-germain.com/restaurant-les-parisiens	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Inside a new luxury hotel located in Faubourg-Saint-Germain, this restaurant adopts all the codes of the luxury brasserie genre. Wood panelling, large mirrors, mosaic floors, velvet banquettes, gilding, black marble tables: it is elegant, slightly retro and very cosy – a winning formula. Curated by Thibault Sombardier, the menu represents a refreshed and updated take on tradition. A fine and eclectic wine list, complete with some great bottles.	benesemily	\N	\N
3339356580	Maison Cluny	3 rue de Cluny	France	Paris		https://www.maison-cluny.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Much to our delight, the gourmet duet, formerly of the Cornichon in the Daguerre district, has teamed up again in this stylish bistro opposite the Cluny Museum garden in the heart of the Latin Quarter. The slate menu reads like an old-school cookbook: chicken liver pâté, veal kidneys, game in season, rice pudding… Warm interior and casual, upbeat vibe.	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3337224558	Nolinski	16 avenue de l'Opéra	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://nolinskiparis.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	On Avenue de l'Opéra, near the Comédie Française, a chic brasserie whose vintage interior mixes Art Deco and the 1970s, with mirrors, gilding, yellow marble and corduroy upholstering. The culinary lineup by Philip Chronopoulos is big-boned and Gallic down to its core (pot au feu, poultry and sweetbread vol au vent, veal cutlet with morels).	beckerradu	\N	\N
3331708335	Nous 4	3 rue Beccaria	France	Paris	Wheelchair access	https://www.nous4restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Pork in a melt - in - the - mouth crust with lentils and mustard sauce^ poached egg with cabbage and bacon cream… you've probably got the picture. Here you can tuck into a no - nonsense, delicious meal that offers great value for money, considering how much you'll enjoy it. The open kitchen means you can also talk to the chef. A really lovely place, the like of which we'd be happy to see more of in Paris.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3331424496	Parcelles	13 rue Chapon	France	Paris	Interesting wine list	https://www.parcelles-paris.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	The quintessence of retro Paris! In a side street between Arts et Métiers and the Centre Pompidou, this 1936 bistro would not have been out of place on the set of Woody Allen's Midnight in Paris: authentic bistro furniture, bare or beige walls, vintage tiled flooring, gilded ceiling, and a copper and wooden counter. The food is all that you'd expect: pressed pork shank, line-caught sea bass with spelt risotto and smoked eel sauce, and, of course, the dark chocolate and caramelised pecan tart. Ten out of ten for this restaurant that fully deserves its success. (Book if you can.)	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3336390004	Phébé	190 rue de Courcelles	France	Paris		https://restaurantphebe.fr/fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Located next to Place du Maréchal-Juin, this charming little 1900s restaurant has a glass front, green wood panelling and listed ceramic tiles. Chef Pauline Nicolas, who trained at Maison Rostang, conjures up enticingly named dishes that live up to their promise once served. For lunch, a delicious starter of Morteau sausage, mushrooms and a vin jaune sauce, followed by trout with braised baby gem lettuce, and for dessert, it doesn't get more indulgent than the poached pear tartlet. Here, the high-quality ingredients are treated with the respect they deserve.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3335398048	Quedubon	22 rue du Plateau	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://restaurantquedubon.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This is the kind of bistro-cum-wine bar that ensures that Paris will always be Paris! Picture the scene: the owner, sporting a jaunty cap and bristly beard, greets you with a broad grin and seats you at your table, before going on to recommend a good wine produced by one of his mates. In the kitchen, British chef Ollie Clark (Bruno Doucet's former second-in-command) rolls out a big-boned, no-fuss menu (there is often offal to be had), crafted from quality ingredients that the owner has carefully selected: pâté en croûte of guinea fowl, foie gras and pork^ vol-au-vent of poultry, chanterelle mushrooms and cream of vin jaune…	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3331303846	Brasserie du Louvre - Bocuse	Place André-Malraux	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.maisons-bocuse.com/nos-brasseries/brasserie-louvre-paris-1-terrasse/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Lyonnaise	4.0	€€€	f	t	Take a seat in the sleek, spacious dining hall framed by bay windows and marvel at the quintessential view over Paris: Comédie-Française, Conseil d’Etat, Louvre… The enticing menu cleverly navigates between iconic Lyons classics (hot pistachio sausage in a soft bread roll, pike quenelle and nantua sauce) and timeless brasserie staples (foie gras salad, sole meunière, etc. ). Splendid terrace beneath the arcades of this emblematic Haussmannian edifice.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3331645466	Benjamin Schmitt Restaurant	41 rue Catherine-de-La-Rochefoucauld	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.schmittrestaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	In the heart of Pigalle, this eatery pays tribute to the land and those who work it. The youthful chef cultivates culinary eclecticism, seamlessly segueing from one style of cuisine to another and from traditional to modern. The enticing names of the dishes live up to their promise: duck, foie gras and pork pâté en croûte^ veal breast confit with olives, aubergine and anchovies^ strawberry and rhubarb pavlova... Sensibly priced lunch menu, tasting and à la carte menus in the evening.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3332573125	Les 110 de Taillevent	195 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré	France	Paris	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.les-110-taillevent-paris.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Under the aegis of the prestigious Taillevent name, this ultra - chic brasserie puts the onus on food and wine pairings. The concept is a success, with its remarkable choice of 110 wines by the glass, and nicely done traditional food (pâté en croûte, bavette steak with a peppercorn sauce etc). Elegant and inviting decor.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3338762295	Mắm From Hanoï	39 rue de Cléry	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://mamfromhanoi.com	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	4.0	€	t	t	In a corner of the Sentier neighbourhood, this authentic Vietnamese restaurant is a hit, and rightly so (book several days in advance). The Hanoi-born couple at the helm prepare bona fide Northern Vietnamese cuisine – the word mắm refers to a fish-based condiment that is very popular there. The vegetables and meats are of French origin and rigorously selected. Focusing on the essentials, the menu includes the not-to-be-missed pork nems, served with their famous mắm sauce, plus an excellent phở: typical of the North, the soup is slightly salty and all the more easily digestible for it – the quintessence of this aromatic food, which effortlessly fuses simplicity of execution with complexity of flavour.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3338098971	Charbon Kunitoraya	5 rue Villedo	France	Paris	Air conditioning	https://kunitoraya.com/	Nessun premio	Yakitori, Japanese	3.0	€€€€	f	t	Outside, the attractive timber façade has a Japanese feel. Inside, you'll find an old zinc counter, Paris Métro-style tiling, mirrors, wood panelling and mouldings, and two large bar tables built of solid wood. In this chic setting with a vintage feel, chef Nomoto – a pioneer of udon restaurants in France – serves up a range of top-notch yakitori, particularly chicken. Cordial, well-paced service.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3336042614	L'Interprète	8 rue des Orphelines	France	Pau	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.linterprete-pau.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€	f	t	In a chic bohemian setting in the heart of the city centre, you are invited to sample creative bistronomy that takes its cue from the seasons, in the form of well-constructed carte blanche set menus. Chef Quentin Maysou takes pleasure in cooking: pan-fried scallops, banana miso and quinoa with spinach^ veal fillet, salsify au jus, roasted clementine, cashew nuts and smoked pepper… Plus a convivial atmosphere.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3335829694	Les Pipelettes	3 rue Valéry-Meunier	France	Pau		https://lespipelettes-pau.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Here, the delicious dishes are prepared according to the produce available at the market stalls and the harvests of some 30 farmers based near Pau. The chef does her job well, and her dishes are both sophisticated and delicious: beef ravioli with squash and yarrow, line-caught hake from Saint-Jean-de-Luz, or the goat's milk cream with vanilla and Landes raspberry. Set menus (without options) at lunch and dinner, but the value for money at this pleasant little bistro is excellent.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3338049876	Omnivore	1 place Gramont	France	Pau	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.omnivorepau.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Two minutes from Pau Château, on the picturesque Place Gramont, imagine a nostalgic bistro with a zinc-topped counter, wood panelling and upholstered seating. Pau's foodies flock here, sharing good vibes as they tuck into fish fresh from the fish auction or 24hr shoulder of pork. The slate menu features traditional nosh served generously and sometimes enhanced by touches of citrus fruit or well-balanced smoky notes. The jovial front-of-house staff are an added bonus.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3332093837	Resto Dit Vin	8 rue de Foix	France	Pau	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	In a pedestrian street in the centre of Pau, this inviting and indulgent place is one to keep under your hat, as both the dining area and terrace are invariably packed to the rafters! In his semi-open kitchen, chef Alexis Bourdrel gives pride of place to local ingredients that he knows inside out and sources from farmers with whom he has built up a rapport: the vegetables come from the market-gardener parents of his wife, who works in the dining room^ the ale is from Béarn, and the bottles on the menu are for sale at wine merchant prices, to enjoy at home. The short menu changes regularly (seared scallops and Jerusalem artichoke glazed in a meat jus, Pyrenean trout gravlax and, for dessert, Pyrenean flax and pear poached in Jurançon).	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3336440261	Haut-Linage	Place du Maréchal-Davout	France	Penmarc'h	Wheelchair access	http://hautlinage-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Not far from Eckmühl Lighthouse, this restaurant boasts a contemporary interior in shades of white, grey and gold. It is a charming place run by a couple of Breton locals: chef Corentin Ogor and the ebullient Klervi Tanniou, who manages the restaurant floor, armed with a broad smile. When it comes to the modern cuisine, each dish focuses on a fresh ingredient, cooked to perfection and served with a tip-top sauce or jus, eg mackerel confit, carrot, snow peas^ haddock, einkorn, coconut milk sauce and red curry^ pork filet mignon, pink onions, full-bodied gravy. The lunch deal is a steal.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3333534255	Sterenn	432 rue de la Joie	France	Penmarc'h	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-sterenn.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood, Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This pleasant restaurant perched on the Pointe de Penmarch serves cuisine that is rooted in the local area and made using top-notch ingredients. The chef puts a lot of effort into meticulously plating his dishes, particularly when it comes to the fish. For dessert, it's all about tradition and savoir-faire, eg the buttery kouign amann, served warm, is nicely caramelised, and soft and crispy at the same time. Lovely views over the bay and Eckmühl Lighthouse.	paganialex	\N	\N
3335618326	Chez Séraphin	au village	France	Peri	Car park,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	A characteristic Corsican house in a charming mountainside village sets the splendid scene to sample wholesome country fare, prepared simply from painstakingly selected ingredients, among which Corsica’s famous cured meats and fruit, vegetables and herbs from the garden. Take a seat on the spacious terrace and drink in the jaw-dropping view of the mountains and ancient oak forest. Just a word of warning: bank cards are not accepted, so take cash!	venturialessia	\N	\N
