3337817442	Fossé Saint Ange	2 rue du Chantier	France	Richelieu	Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	A new duo has taken over this well-known institution in the pretty village built by Cardinal Richelieu in the 17C. The period varnished wood façade opens onto a bistro-style interior with a warm and friendly atmosphere, where good cheer and good food are the order of the day. The chef keeps things simple: a menu that changes every month, featuring traditional dishes that are firmly rooted in the seasons and spiced up with the odd exotic touch, such as an Asian-inspired guinea fowl raviolo. The desserts, too, hold their own.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3330540515	O'Rabasse	5 place de la Pompe	France	Richerenches	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.orabasse.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	In the heart of the “truffle capital”, O’Rabasse sings an ode to good food that respects traditions. Everything is made from scratch by the chef, with the help of local suppliers and in line with the seasons. A truly pleasant meal, further enhanced by smiling, professional service.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3335674092	L'Atelier Mélanie	20 place de l'Église	France	Riec-sur-Belon	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lateliermelanie.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant pays tribute to Mélanie Rouat (1878-1954), a friend of Curnonsky and a two-starred chef in her day. Her great great grandson, chef Jean-Baptiste Caillarec, and his pastry chef partner Laura Martinon, both of whom have previous experience in prestigious establishments, have opened this bright, contemporary restaurant. Soft-boiled egg marbled with port, creamy mushrooms^ roast mullet, carrots and sesame^ deconstructed apple, caramelised apples, apple and tarragon brunoise, cider emulsion. The duo work meticulously with quality ingredients to create delicious dishes.	berninialex	\N	\N
3330167599	Maison Kieny	7 rue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Riedisheim	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://restaurant-kieny.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This inviting coaching inn (from 1850) not far from Mulhouse occupies an imposing traditional Alsatian building in the centre of the village. In an elegant dining room, the chef serves seasonal cuisine with a contemporary bent, such as slow-cooked egg with peas and a creamy sauce made with their pods, or lamb cooked two ways, accompanied by chick peas in a French curry. Simpler bistro fare on weekday lunches.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3330914465	AOR La Table, le Goût et Nous	2 rue de la Piscine	France	Riquewihr	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.table-aor.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€€	f	f	Something of a UFO in the gastronomic universe of Alsace, globetrotting cook, Serge Burckel, is also part poet, part rock star – check out the old LPs and CDs recycled as place mats! He works with his family in a bohemian, laid-back ambience, with a choice of surprise menus.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3334004645	La Grappe d'Or	1 rue des Écuries-Seigneuriales	France	Riquewihr	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurant-grappedor.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian	4.0	€€	t	f	This flower - decked house built in 1554 could not be more inviting and the characteristic regional interior has lost none of its yesteryear appeal. Classic regional delicacies on the menu: choucroute, baeckeofe, knuckle of ham, stuffed trout, etc.	longoethan	\N	\N
3334976834	La Table d'Aimé	4 rue Francisco-Ferrer	France	Rivesaltes	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.latabledaime.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Established within a winery and appointed in a style that blends Provençal and industrial elements (wrought iron, barrels of wine, bare brick walls), the restaurant offers inspired market-fresh food, organic whenever possible, washed down with wines from the estate. In summertime, the leafy patio is irresistible.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3334899246	Le Central	20 cours de la République	France	Roanne	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access	https://www.troisgros.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Michel and Marie-Pierre Troisgros are behind the family's other gourmet establishment set in a former 1920s hotel. The vibe is smart yet casual and the warm, vintage decor is inspired by the brasseries of yesteryear. You will sample a concise menu that changes daily, flanked by à la carte suggestions in a traditional register, although often reworked with creative twists, illustrated by a profiterole with mustard-flavoured ice cream. The place is always busy, bearing witness to its well-deserved success.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3332843997	ZEN Japanese Restaurant	Bachemer Straße 233	Germany	Cologne		https://www.restaurant-zen.de/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	€€	t	f	Located in a residential area, this restaurant is a firm favourite with fans of Japanese cuisine. In a pared-back Far Eastern-style setting, diners can look forward to a pleasantly lively atmosphere, as well as friendly and professional service with an authentic Japanese touch. It is clear that a well-coordinated team is at work here. Your options include gyoza, tempura, grilled and pan-fried dishes, udon, sushi and sashimi, plus a large omakase set menu. Wine, sake and Japanese whisky to go with it.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3336257601	Maison Bouquet	17 place du Marché	France	Roanne	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.maisonbouquet.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Guillaume Assié is living proof that when a chef is happy in their kitchen, the food follows suit. His modern, pared-back score highlights his flawless technique and knowhow, gleaned in the kitchens of great chefs (Oustau de Baumanière, Lameloise, Auberge du Vieux puits). Devoid of frivolous frills, Guillaume’s cuisine is an ode to simplicity. The asparagus, which is green and al dente, is paired with caviar for added saltiness^ the fresh gleaming monkfish is enveloped in a velvety grenobloise sauce, while an exquisite concoction of chocolate, peanuts and tobacco adds the final touch to the consummate culinary craftsmanship. Swish seamless service. Established in a mansion dating from 1900, the softly lit interior is cosy and inviting.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3335904315	Café Bras	Jardin du Foirail	France	Rodez	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.cafebras.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The Café Bras, established in the heart of the Soulages Museum, pays tribute to Averyron produce. Two possibilities: order a snack or picnic basket from the counter or take a seat in the restaurant… The kitchen team crafts crisp, aromatic, light dishes, rich in generosity, colour and scents, like a tartare of tuna marinated in calamansi and Greek-style cucurbits or breast of roast duckling, acidic jus, new potatoes, cone cabbage and tiger courgettes with a sauce vierge. The attention lavished on flavour is second to none, as are the welcome and interior décor. Fully worthy of its ongoing success.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3330717416	Opéra	1 rue d'Athènes	France	Rodez	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://opera-rodez.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	After stints in three-star restaurants in Italy and with the Bras family, at the Musée Soulages and at their flagship establishment in Laguiole, Italian chef Vasco Baldisserotto has gone solo in this smart restaurant outside the town centre. He signs a pedigree Gallic score, albeit tinged with Italian influences, particularly from his native Venetian region. Accustomed to top-drawer produce, he painstakingly sources and selects only the best local ingredients. The menus celebrate the seasons and his suppliers, on whom he frequently shines the spotlight. Examples include braised Aveyron beef shank in a carbonara sauce^ raviolis stuffed with chocolate and hazelnuts and orange sorbet. If you now add the friendly welcome and seamless service, you will realise why everyone is singing the praises of this opera…	guerravictor	\N	\N
3333231976	Le Préau	1 cours Saint-Étienne	France	Rognes	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In his home village, Antonin Wishart cooks up joyful cuisine using ultra-fresh ingredients from the market and the family's kitchen garden. The mouth-watering set menu changes daily^ this son of winegrowers has also curated an attractive wine list. In short: a trendy bistro with relaxed, efficient service, and an urban vibe in the countryside! A charm offensive.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3337025461	L'Eau d'Oust	6 rue du Lac	France	Rohan	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.leaudoust.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	An old farmstead on the way out of the village near a pond paints the inviting picture. In a contemporary, welcoming décor, the owners focus on genuinely wholesome food with the occasional whimsical touch of creativity. The ingredients are fresh and first - rate, and the service is with a smile. A pleasant meal every time.	naldinadia	\N	\N
3336458924	L'Instant	10 rue de Delay	France	Romans-sur-Isère	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-instant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Outside the centre, in a residential area near the train station, this lovely 1930s town house welcomes you in an attractive contemporary decor^ you are served delicious market cuisine, made with lovely fresh ingredients. Dishes that you wolf down... in an Instant!	dragomirpippo	\N	\N
3331372447	Le Bois Blanc	11 rue de la Sirène	France	Romorantin-Lanthenay	Wheelchair access	https://le-bois-blanc-romorantin-restaurant.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Chambord asparagus and Sologne strawberries, freshwater fish like pike, catfish and carp, game in season: chef Maxime Valleye, with stints at Georges Blanc and in his parents’ establishment, sings an ode to his region. Even the restaurant’s name, which is evocative of a birch tree, is in tune with Sologne’s forests. Maxime carefully crafts seasonal dishes steeped in classical overtones: pork, confit of egg yolk, spinach and goat’s cheese crumble. The classy, stylish interior of this contemporary bistro sports varnished wooden tables and vintage incandescent light bulbs. Most of the tipples on the wine list are from the Val-de-Loire.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3339297591	Auberge à l'Agneau	11 rue Principale	France	Roppenheim	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.auberge-agneau.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This family-run institution dating from 1902 is located in a handsome 17C half-timbered building. It is a great place to indulge in hearty food: in the kitchen, dishes simmer under the watchful eye of the chef, who loves his region. Stand-out dishes include local and meat specialties. Expect unpretentious, generous and authentic fare, served in an inviting setting… plus a warm welcome!	pirijiri	\N	\N
3333924887	La Ville Blanche	29 route de Tréguier	France	Rospez	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://la-ville-blanche.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	This restaurant in a spruce building typical of Brittany is run by a young couple who have built up a loyal clientele with their modern cuisine and meticulous service. The chef keeps an eye on the seasons, thanks to a trusted network of small-scale producers. He skilfully enhances the top-notch ingredients they supply, often teasing out smoky notes and adding just the right dose of bitterness and acidity: poached langoustines, cabbage with lime^ apple, crepe stuffed with apple vanilla compote, fromage blanc sorbet and combawa diplomate.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3338073767	Auberge Quintessence	Route du Col-de-la-Couillole	France	Roubion	Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://auberge-quintessence.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	At the Col de la Couillole, a pass in the Mercantour National Park, this former refuge run by Pauline and Christophe Billau is a top destination for foodies. These two serve up a warm welcome and a single set menu that draws inspiration from the mountains and changes with the seasons. Diners can indulge in creamy local mountain nettle cappuccino, superb roasted white asparagus, whether tangy with candied citrus fruit or in a sabayon sauce, or lightly smoked Mediterranean tuna served confit-style and subtly counterbalanced by the herbal notes of oxalis. Dishes such as veal from the Plateau de Longon accompanied by confit shallots and a courgette flower filled with pine nuts and a herb cream are brimming with skilfully mastered flavours, while the cheeses are carefully matured. There's nothing superfluous or artificial about this place! A few prettily decorated guestrooms are up for grabs for overnight stays.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3330534251	L'epicurius	31 rue Damiette	France	Rouen	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lepicurius.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	On a picturesque pedestrian street in a district packed with antique dealers bang in the heart of historic Rouen, this trendy bistro serves delicate, tasty cuisine. Examples include the catch of the day, savory-flavoured veggies and a hollandaise sauce perfumed with trout roe^ tartlet of raw cocoa, frothy praline and caramelised peanut ice cream… The chef’s deft hand can be tasted in the painstakingly selected ingredients and expertly curated recipes that allow the ingredients to shout their name in a feast of felicitous flavours. Meals are served in a contemporary interior and in a recently opened room upstairs. Gracious, cheerful service. Reservations recommended.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3333354205	Bistro de Montcaud	Hameau de Combes	France	Sabran	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.chateaudemontcaud.com/restaurant/bistro-de-montcaud	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Château de Montcaud's chic new bistro serves traditional Southern French cuisine, with priority given by chef Mathieu Hervé to local, often organic ingredients: poultry and foie gras pâté en croûte, vegetable pickles^ tomato gazpacho, watermelon granita and shiso leaf^ rockfish three ways, bouillabaisse-style fish soup. The shaded terrace looking out onto the grounds is pleasant^ plus a warm welcome and cordial service await.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3337728276	La Conciergerie	4405 rue de la Lys	France	Sailly-sur-la-Lys	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantlaconciergerie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The former concierge lodge in the grounds of the Château de Bac-Saint-Maur is now home to this modern restaurant. Bathed in light thanks to its large bay windows, the space features a few design details that reflect the season. Langoustine and beetroot for starters^ veal, mussels and samphire for the main course^ tomato, vanilla zephyr and oregano ice cream for dessert: the chef aims to surprise with cuisine that is creative (in moderation), and made with good ingredients, mainly local and seasonal.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3336698027	Le Mange-Grenouille	10 rue Paul-Boncour	France	Saint-Aignan	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lemangegrenouille.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This former coaching inn located in a lane just a stone's throw from the banks of the Cher has a pleasant patio in the courtyard, delightfully rustic dining areas with bare stonework and terracotta tiled floors... but above all ambitious cuisine whose roots are firmly embedded in tradition. At lunchtime, a simpler, great-value set menu is served. Don't miss the house speciality: frog's legs sautéed in parsley!	winternoemi	\N	\N
3331653777	Le Petit Prince	28 rue des Marronniers	France	Saint-Alban-les-Eaux	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lepetitprince.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Unlike its namesake, this charming restaurant did not fall from an asteroid^ in fact, it was founded in the early 19C by the great-great-aunts of the current owner. Seasoned chef Quentin Billaud crafts enticing recipes into exquisitely plated dishes. The concise set menu is only available on lunchtime weekdays, while the gourmet evening menu is depicted by a more sophisticated and ambitious note. In addition to the dining room, there is now a lounge area, Le 1534 (date of its original construction), which serves bistronomic fare. The lovely wine cellar is open to visitors and hosts tasting workshops and there is also a delicatessen store (L’Épicerie Anna). This Petit Prince is a delightful surprise all round!	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3338424716	L'Escoubille	56 rue des Barillettes	France	Saint-Alban-Leysse	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.escoubille.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The name of this contemporary restaurant with a terrace and rooftop area pays tribute to a traditional stew, a speciality of Gignac in the Hérault département, which the chef fondly remembers being made in the family home. He prepares good seasonal cuisine at prices that won't break the bank: seared red mullet, fennel, capers and olives^ saddle of rabbit, garlic cream and mushroom tart^ strawberry cheesecake.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3334919163	Auberge du Paradis	70 route des Crus-du-Beaujolais (Le Plâtre-Durand)	France	Saint-Amour-Bellevue	Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://aubergeduparadis.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Two restaurants in one! Chez Lucienne showcases a concise array of creative often spicy dishes to share: free-range chicken kebab marinated in ras-el-hanout^ lamb gyoza in herbs and curry, leeks and soy mayonnaise^ deep-fried scallops and tikka masala girolles pickles. On the other hand, Joséphine à Table features a wine bar with traditional starters and a dish of the day (marbled ham, pork pie, chicken kebabs, rice pudding). Both establishments boast a pleasant patio and a friendly, buzzy vibe – all of which washed down with tipples from Mâcon and Beaujolais and a range of wines by the glass from a magnum. Fans of Sunday brunch should make a beeline for chez Lucienne.	caldarolacagilio	\N	\N
3339250169	La Table de Mentone	401 chemin de Mentone	France	Saint-Antonin-du-Var	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.chateaumentone.com	Nessun premio	Provençal, Contemporary	5.0	€€	t	t	Chef Sébastien Sanjou pops in from down the road (the Relais des Moines at Arcs-sur-Argens) to supervise the cooking of this luxuriously appointed restaurant in the cellar of one of the finest winegrowing estates of the Var. As guests savour the superlative setting (a panoramic landscape of vineyards and olive groves outdoors and a designer-inspired interior), they dig into fine seasonal provençal cuisine which makes the most of the estate’s wide range of produce (chicken coop, orchard, cottage garden, olive groves), illustrated by a tartare of cucumber and fennel with fresh herbs^ Mediterranean skipjack, crunchy salad of quinoa and courgette spaghetti. The food is naturally washed down with one of the estate’s fine organic vintages. A few guestrooms and holiday cottages are available to prolong your stay in style.	beloveva	\N	\N
3331569780	Les Singuliers	6 rue Montaigne	France	Saint-Astier	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://restaurantlessinguliers.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of Périgord Blanc, this traditional stone-built house, which sports a tasteful interior, bends over backwards to shine the spotlight on local artisans (the cutlery is exquisite) and local produce: aromatic herbs from the garden, Chantérac vegetables, Neuvic sturgeon, etc. From his gleaming open kitchen, Louis Festa, a young chef with a great track record, has devised a single surprise set menu (that can be tailored to suit your appetite) starring ambitious, spontaneous dishes that respect the seasons: Le Puy green lentils prepared three ways, Ribérac Limousin beef on the Japanese barbecue.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3337982307	Prosper	3 rue des Lavières	France	Saint-Aubin	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://chateau-st-aubin.com/fr/restaurant	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	When a winemaker from the Côte de Beaune meets a starred chef, you get Prosper! This lovely contemporary bistro in the Château St Aubin is the result of a collaboration between the Prosper Maufoux wine estate and the restaurateur Édouard Mignot (restaurant Ed.Em in Chassagne-Montrachet). The chef proposes a menu inspired by the Burgundy terroir. Pleasant terrace with a view of the vineyards.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3337504224	Le Clos des Oliviers	53 rue de l'Aven	France	Saint-Gély-du-Fesc	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.clos-des-oliviers.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Taste, simplicity, skilful use of quality ingredients: here, you can enjoy good food without unnecessary complications – and what a real pleasure! The wine list is put together with the neighbouring cellarman. In summer, make the most of the terrace in the shade of the reed screening.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3331801695	Le Pérou	341 rue Jules-Ferry	France	Saint-Béron		http://www.restaurant-leperou.fr	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	€€	f	f	Pulpo anticuchero, lomo saltado, tiradito, arroz cremoso, and, of course, the indispensable ceviches: all the classics of Peruvian cooking are on the menu here in the Alps, thanks to a chef and her team, who all hail from Peru. Much of the produce is imported direct from the Andes, via Spain. Anyone who has been lucky enough to taste authentic South American food will be delighted by the incredible range of flavours and tastes of this cuisine rich in seasoning and unexpected ingredients on offer.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3339911294	La Calèche	2 place du Commandant-Marey	France	Saint-Bonnet-le-Château	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantlacaleche.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This 17C mansion with a colourfully decorated interior is home to a generous restaurant that is liable to shake up flavours (snails and frog's legs, horseradish cream^ rack of veal from Haut Forez) with just the right measure of sophistication and daring. La Calèche promises to take you on a culinary escapade!	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3333390596	L'Air du Temps	6 rue Sainte-Barbe	France	Saint-Brieuc	Terrace	https://www.airdutemps.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€	t	t	This attractive old building with a grey granite façade is located in the town centre. Inside, contemporary features are woven into the original decor to great effect, and there is also a patio terrace for quiet dining. A successful transition to its new premises! As for the food, the chef continues to cook traditional dishes, mostly served in casserole dishes, such as the slow-cooked pork loin. Excellent cuisine at reasonable prices	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3336694239	La Croix Blanche	61 rue de Genève	France	Saint-Brieuc	Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lacroixblanche.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Two brothers: one in the kitchen, the other serving in the dining room... It is a family affair in this pleasant restaurant overlooking a pretty garden. The cuisine is gourmet and refined, for instance the excellent Dubarry pannacotta with crumbled crab and a shellfish emulsion. You get plenty of enjoyment for the price.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3334383754	La Table d'Edgar	15 rue Jouallan	France	Saint-Brieuc		http://www.saint-brieuc-hotel.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Chef Sébastien David, who has an impressive career to his name, conjures up appealing cuisine using top-notch ingredients: quality poultry from the Ferme de la Paumerais, brightly coloured farmhouse butter, fresh fish from Guilvinec, and plump, fleshy oysters from Paimpol. The balanced flavours in both the savoury dishes and the desserts come down to meticulous craftsmanship and expert cooking: chicken supreme with lardo di Colonnata, the leg roasted in a lovage broth^ pear with white chocolate and pistachio fondant. A bright and harmoniously decorated interior with tables laid out around a lovely glass-roofed seating area.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3332884637	Ô Saveurs	10 rue Jules-Ferry	France	Saint-Brieuc	Wheelchair access	https://www.osaveurs-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Chances are it won't be the charm of the location near the train station that draws you here, but the restaurant has more than enough of its own merits. Where shall we begin? Scallops from St Brieuc Bay in a Quessoy saffron sauce and seaweed-flavoured conchiglioni or duckling breast roasted in honey and sage with a pear poached in blueberries and shiitakes, and a delicious encounter between cherries and pear with a white chocolate topping to finish…	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3338894912	Auberge du Sombral - Les Bonnes Choses	Place du Sombral	France	Saint-Cirq-Lapopie	Terrace	https://aubergelesombral.wordpress.com/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	In this house at the foot of the Château des Lapopie, you can be sure that good things – Les Bonnes Choses – are to come! Enjoy the pleasant cuisine du terroir, in which local ingredients are the star (lamb, foie gras, cheese... ). There are a handful of pretty guestrooms, if you wish to stay on in this village overlooking the Lot.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3338672877	Sienne	46 boulevard de la République	France	Saint-Cloud	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantsienne.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Baptiste Renouard is at the helm of this contemporary bistro, which is open all day long and serves brunch on Sundays. This talented chef is all about culinary indulgence, in the form of dishes peppered with references to the French classics such as œuf meurette (egg in red wine sauce), whiting Colbert, pot-au-feu or pike quenelle. It's concise and flawless! Opt for the upstairs dining area, which has tables close to the large bay windows, or the terrace in fine weather.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3334076296	L'Atelier d'Olivier Arlot	55 quai des Maisons-Blanches	France	Saint-Cyr-sur-Loire	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://latelier-olivierarlot.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Set up by Olivier Arlot on the banks of the Loire, L'Atelier is modern both in terms of the decor and the menu. They serve up tasty and savvy creations, such as oxtail terrine and foie gras – a happy combination that melts in the mouth! This is bistronomy at its best, with intriguing and punchy dishes, plus a menu that is renewed very regularly.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3339652415	es/pacìo	201 nouveau port des Lecques	France	Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Local vegetables and seasonal fruit, freshly caught wild fish, a bubbly team (including the former sous-chef from La Chassagnette), a short, judiciously curated list of local natural wines – it is a formula that whets the appetite. The dishes are bursting with flavour and that's what counts: dentex crudo, multicoloured radishes, citrus vinaigrette, rouillé condiment^ line-caught meagre, sweet potato, clementine, fennel^ lemon cream, black sesame, meringue. From the low-key bistro interior, the large patio windows look out onto the terrace and beyond onto the marina.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3334041071	La Baratte	Le Bourg	France	Saint-Denis-le-Vêtu	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-labaratte.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking	4.0	€	t	t	Tasty wholesome food crafted from top-notch local produce at eater-friendly prices: such is the pledge of the Lefèvre couple who runs this welcoming inn built out of local stone – formerly the village bar and grocery shop. A bright, trendy interior with a pleasant alfresco space for sunny days and a rotisserie in the hall that fills the dining room with the enticing aromas of dishes of the day such as chicken colombo.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3337026578	Logan Laug	7 rue du 11-Novembre-1918	France	Saint-Dié-des-Vosges	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.loganlaug.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	A smart contemporary interior, with white brick walls, green patterned wallpaper, parquet flooring and glazed wine cellars facing the service counter, is the stage masterminded by chef and entrepreneur Logan Laug, who leaves no detail to chance! With his brigade, he crafts modern, fusion cuisine that bears the stamp of his far-flung travels. Examples might include suckling pork chop Tex-Mex style with corn^ or red mullet two ways, textures of artichoke and chermoula.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3331496355	Chartron	1 avenue Gambetta	France	Saint-Donat-sur-l'Herbasse	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-chartron.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Situated between the Drôme and Ardèche areas in southeastern France, this local family-run establishment dates back to 1946, when Paulette Chartron and her brother René bought the inn in this village famous for its Jean-Sébastien Bach Festival (held every summer). The key to their success? The cuisine, made from quality ingredients, reveals a definite savoir-faire: duck foie gras, sea bream, pike-perch fillet, Provençal lamb… plus there are dishes starring truffles in season. They have a handful of cosy guestrooms.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3334869800	ITO	Antwerpener Straße 15	Germany	Cologne	Notable sake list,Terrace	https://ito-restaurant.de/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	In this trendy Japanese restaurant in the Belgian Quarter, Kengo Nishimi uses top-notch ingredients to create clearly structured dishes in which traditional Japanese cuisine is laced with modern European influences. In the evening, Japanese classics such as tempura, sashimi and sushi can be ordered à la carte, plus there is an extensive omakase menu. At lunchtime, a moderately priced set menu is available. In the front part of the restaurant, you can watch the chef at work at the sushi counter.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3336731370	L'Huitrier Pie	11 rue de la Porte-Bouqueyre	France	Saint-Emilion	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lhuitrier-pie.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	In this famous wine-growing village, the enthusiasm and talent of the young owners, Camille and Soufiane, take us on a journey over the course of the meal. Appealing dishes featuring carefully selected ingredients (heirloom tomatoes from the South-West, raspberries, garden verbena and burrata^ just-seared John Dory, Coco de Paimpol beans). In fine weather, you can sit out in the pretty little courtyard.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3332173733	Le Tertre	5 rue du Tertre-de-la-Tente	France	Saint-Emilion	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurantletertre.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€	f	f	In a small cobbled street in the village, this restaurant has been given a new lease of life by an accomplished professional couple, who took over in 2020. Building on classical foundations, the creative dishes are inspired and harmonious. They showcase produce from the region: Landes duck, Basque country trout, fish from the ports of Aquitaine. In an extension to the dining room, the wine cellar hewn out of the monolithic stone has a table for four that is in great demand in the evening.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3339701014	L'Envers du Décor	9 rue du Clocher	France	Saint-Emilion	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.envers-dudecor.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of this iconic wine village, a few steps from the bell tower, the picturesque red façade of this bistro catches the eye. Inside lies an elegant vintage décor with a zinc counter and leather bench seating. The menu runs the gamut of classic French staples from calf’s liver to rum baba. Fine selection of reasonably priced wines.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3339262189	Restaurant Arcé	630 Mixeleneko Bidea	France	Saint-Étienne-de-Baïgorry	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.hotel-arce.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	A delicious place to eat in a verdant spot at the foot of the Ispéguy Pass. The authentic Basque house has an attractive narrow dining area, the bright white of which echoes the immaculate garb of the Basque pelota players pictured on the walls. The market-fresh cuisine is seasonal and gives pride of place to local produce. Be sure to try the trout with blue cheese – straight from the restaurant's tank, the fish couldn't be fresher. In summer, tables are set up on the terrace, which is lined with plane trees. After your meal, stroll along the ivy-clad metal footbridge spanning the River Nive.	salajakub	\N	\N
3333865496	À la Table des Lys	58 rue Saint-Simon	France	Saint-Etienne	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.latabledeslys.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Recently taken over by its owner/chef, this small restaurant has been turned into a beautiful, contemporary eatery serving tasty and light modern cuisine.	calincolin	\N	\N
3335804711	Auberge du Poids Public	Route de Toulouse	France	Saint-Félix-Lauragais	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.auberge-du-poids-public.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Following in her parents' footsteps, Céline Taffarello continues to showcase the best of the terroir, with produce such as magret of black mountain duck with sarawak pepper and delicious, perfectly seasoned roasted peach with verbena. The cassoulet, which has won several awards, is particularly popular. The panoramic terrace, with its pretty view of the Lauragais plain is delightful. Comfortable guestrooms.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3338004501	La Gaffe	Promenade des Quais	France	Saint-Florent	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lagaffe.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Chef Yann Le Scavarec, who hails from Morbihan, is at the helm of this restaurant, which boasts an ideal location on the Saint-Florent harbour front. His well-crafted contemporary cooking showcases local produce, eg lamb and veal from Oletta, fish sourced directly from a local fisherman and barbecued crayfish. The grouper, courgette flower with spider crab and Vadouvan spices made an impression! The modern interior is in keeping with the menu.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3335311959	MaThy'S	Place Furnellu	France	Saint-Florent	Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Picture a red façade preceded by a delightful patio shaded by a mulberry tree. On a street corner of Saint Florent, this eatery aims for a friendly village restaurant vibe and serves Mediterranean and Corsican cuisine (carpaccio of langoustines, olive oil and dried caviar, tartare of red tuna or grilled squid with chorizo), without forgetting a few more exotic Asian notes (yuzu-flavoured gyoza or crunchy king prawns, nori and wasabi). Simpler lunchtime menu and a highly tempting wine list add the final touch to this inviting portrait.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3336027693	L'Auberge du Pêcheur	Route de Bastia	France	Saint-Florent	Terrace	https://www.aubergedupecheur.net/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	t	t	Damien Muller, a fisherman and fishmonger (owner of Poissonnerie Saint-Christophe), runs an open-air restaurant in the courtyard garden of his childhood home. The concept is simple: at lunchtime, a single set menu based on the catch of the day^ in the evening, a seafood menu with more elaborate dishes, lobster or sushi. The fish is killed according to the ikejime method, said to bring out its full flavour. The ingredients – needless to say ultra-fresh – and the deft technique underpinning his work promise dining pleasure and conviviality. Save room for the chocolate mousse!	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3336175418	Le Moulin à Vent	10 route de Port-Racine	France	Saint-Germain-des-Vaux	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.le-moulin-a-vent.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Seafood	5.0	€€	f	f	By the coastal road leading to the headlands, this old country inn is a lovely refuge from the elements. A short menu showcases inventive cuisine made from local produce (such as pigeon, lamb, fish, abalone) by a chef with a clear interest in Japanese culinary tradition. The interior has a pared-back decor and a view of the sea and the cove, Anse Saint-Martin.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3338160580	Le Wauthier by Cagna	31 rue Wauthier	France	Saint-Germain-en-Laye		https://www.restaurant-wauthier-by-cagna.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This lovely restaurant located in Saint - Germain - en - Laye also boasts a chic bistro interior and attentive service. Dishes are prepared using quality market ingredients and will please a modern palate. Try dishes like: Piedmont risotto with lobster and beurre blanc, braised sweetbread escalopes, celeric mousseline and Albufera sauce.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3331975570	La Table de Marc Turpin – Hostellerie Saint-Germain	635 Grande-Rue	France	Saint-Germain-lès-Arlay	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hostelleriesaintgermain.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Opposite the church, this engaging 17C coaching inn has been entirely refurbished in a low-key, contemporary vein. The chef sources fine local produce, often organic, to craft appetising dishes, occasionally peppered with creative touches, such as pink trout and nori seaweed. All of which is washed down with fine Jura wines. The cosy rooms are pleasant, and quieter overlooking the terrace.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3330444144	La Table d'Armante	L'Armancette	France	Saint-Gervais-les-Bains	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.armancette.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Inside a luxuriously understated hotel, this chic contemporary mountain restaurant (think wood, stone, velvet and an open kitchen) is run by chef Fabien Laprée. Trained in top establishments and a Meilleur Ouvrier de France finalist in 2018, he crafts modern fare that keeps pace with the seasons, showcasing a lineup of fine alpine and also Mediterranean ingredients. The summer terrace commands a view of the Dômes de Miage mountains.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3332942670	Le Sérac	22 rue de la Comtesse	France	Saint-Gervais-les-Bains	Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.3serac.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	The discreet entrance opens into a large, bright and elegant room. The chef's cuisine is inspired by the seasons. The sharing menu allows you to indulge in fine cuts of meat or fish. In short, a fresh and colourful selection of carefully prepared dishes, such as calf's head and pan-fried foie gras or a tartlet filled with raw and cooked seasonal vegetables, and, for dessert, a delicious warm soufflé flavoured with passion fruit. Enjoy your meal in a pleasingly modern interior that offers views of the mountains. Attentive service. A lovely place.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3338805015	Rond de Carotte	50 rue de la Vignette	France	Saint-Gervais-les-Bains	Terrace	http://www.ronddecarotte.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In the heart of the resort, this eatery shines the spotlight on seasonal, sometimes local ingredients, such as Magland snails. The chef conjures up well-crafted dishes, like free-range poached egg flanked by sweet chestnuts and creamy squash, or melt-in-the-mouth chuck beef stew that is eaten with a spoon. The chalet-inspired dining room, divided in two by a small open-plan kitchen, is the quintessence of alpine charm, in particular due to the shelves loaded in bottles (the establishment is also a wine merchant). Daily brunch from 9am-2pm.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3331378626	La Ferme de Cupelin	198 route du Château	France	Saint-Gervais-les-Bains	Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lafermedecupelin.com/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Recently taken over by Florian and Lauriane Langellier, a young couple with a jaw-dropping CV (Megève’s Four Seasons under Gatillon, Megève’s Flocons de Sel with Emmanuel Renaut, L'Armancette and finally Père Bise with Jean Sulpice where he worked as a pastry chef and she was in the front-of-house), this hotel complex in the upper reaches of the resort has changed hands smoothly as the former owner-chef, Romain Desgranges, continues to helm the kitchen. The set menu showcases local produce from the lakes (arctic char), rivers (crayfish) and forests (game in season), without forgetting forays to Italy (Piedmont hazelnut gnocchi and Colonnata bacon). A fine dining experience featuring tasty modern cuisine with a knockout view of Mont Blanc as a bonus. What’s not to like?	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3338497042	Source	43 avenue du Mont-d'Arbois	France	Saint-Gervais-les-Bains	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://source-restaurant-saint-gervais.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Fillet of beef with tiger’s tears sauce, pak-choi cabbage^ calf’s sweetbread seared in savory (the chef’s signature recipe) are some of the dishes of this bistro that focuses on hearty, simple fare. Two veterans from Annecy, keen to pay tribute to local ingredients, are behind this culinary treasure trove in the heart of the resort.	pingliu	\N	\N
3334169814	L'Ortensia	Domaine de la Pièce	France	Saint-Gervais-sur-Mare	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lortensia.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Ortensia means hydrangea in Occitan and this is how it is spelt in the local lingo! Run by a sister-brother team, Lise and Mathieu, this restaurant is in a picturesque village miles from anywhere. The veteran chef is equally at home with gnocchi in gorgonzola and lobster as with duck from Landes, croaker from Corsica or apricots from Provence. Only the veggies and aromatic herbs are local, like mimosa-style celtuce (stem lettuce) from Pezènes-les-Mines and poutargue (fish roe). Super fresh produce and spot-on pairings depict the culinary scene, served in a bright, airy dining room-cum-conservatory which leads onto a panoramic terrace. Five comfortable very spacious guestrooms overlooking the blissfully peaceful countryside.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3332076817	L'Inattendu	18 avenue de la Plage	France	Saint-Gilles-Croix-de-Vie	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-l-inattendu.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Tucked away amid the villas and holiday homes, L'Inattendu is as unexpected as its name suggests. The pleasant surprises keep on coming: from the amuse-bouches to the dessert, diners enjoy cuisine that is based on fresh local produce (including the odd herb plucked from the owner's kitchen garden), and skilfully prepared (eg hibiscus, saffron and lemon gels, ice creams and mousses). Sturgeon, endives and kombucha^ a succulent 48hr-cooked pork belly, sweet potato and hibiscus^ chocolate, caramel and saffron. You can also expect a warm welcome and palpable enthusiasm from the front-of-house team. A culinary hotspot that is a hit with locals and tourists alike.	berninialex	\N	\N
3330068143	L'Auberge d'Antan	Avenue de la Résistance	France	Saint-Girons	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://chateaubeauregard.net/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	In what used to be the barn belonging to the château, this restaurant boasts an impressively high ceiling. Hams suspended from the ceiling, stonework and beams make for a lovely country atmosphere. No - nonsense cooking at its best, with traditional dishes such as grilled meats and suckling pig prepared right in front of you at the huge fireplace.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3336017518	La Table du Royal	Royal Riviera	France	Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.royal-riviera.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	f	Geoffroy Szamburski skilfully crafts a modern score, in tune with the seasons and the environment that showcases produce from the Riviera and the Nice hinterland (Gamberoni of San Remo oxalis, Menton lemons). On the dessert side, head pastry chef Lucas Simoncini is equally on the ball with a Piedmont hazelnut soufflé and ice cream. Picture yourself sitting on the terrace with the sea as far as the eye can see…	rossidino	\N	\N
3330077842	Le Saint Jean	2496 route des Bauges	France	Saint-Jean-d'Arvey	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://lesaintjeanrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	You will be as impressed by the scenery as by your food. By a winding road through the Bauges mountains, this ancient village inn commands a view of Chambéry below. Romain honed his culinary craft in top establishments, and Anaïs, a wine lover, suggests pairings that stimulate and awaken our tastebuds. The food is a bona fide catalogue of local produce (fish from the lake, locally reared lamb), whose flavour and character the chef enhances in modern, seasonal dishes. Surprise menus invite the diner to “let go”…	calincolin	\N	\N
3338455761	L'Auberge Saint Jean	8 rue du Pont	France	Saint-Jean-de-Blaignac	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.aubergesaintjean.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	A couple of industry professionals is at the helm of this contemporary-style restaurant nestling on the banks of the River Dordogne, which is visible just outside the picture windows. The menu includes a number of dishes in which chef Thomas L'Hérisson accurately combines ingredients in a modern and somewhat creative style. The salmon confit with dill yoghurt, green aniseed baby turnips and vinegar-preserved mushrooms, or the veal sweetbreads marinated in miso, floured and fried, soy sauce beetroot and artichokes are the perfect reflection of the chef's personality. The fine wine list – with some 550 labels – has something for everyone. Manuela, the obliging hostess, lavishes diners with attentive service.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
