3333491430	Ilura	Pointe Sainte-Barbe	France	Saint-Jean-de-Luz	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-lareserve.com/restauration/restaurant-ilura/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	Located in La Réserve Hotel on the heights of St-Jean-de-Luz, whose superb terrace overlooks the ocean, this exclusive restaurant delivers an enjoyable fine dining experience courtesy of chef Bastien Soumoulou’s creative, modern repertory. His cooking blends turf and surf produce, like foie gras, seaweed and crunchy samphire^ veal, walnuts, cockles and mimosa vinegar^ pollock, andouille sausage and beetroot^ or even beef, gnocchi, spinach and herrings. One dessert showcases hazelnuts in a complex, wickedly irresistible creation that combines coffee and vanilla notes. Swish, seamless, skilful service.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3339215272	Instincts	20 rue Joseph-Garat	France	Saint-Jean-de-Luz		https://restaurant-instincts.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This place run by a dynamic couple turns out to be a pleasant surprise. They are setting about putting a new spin on good old bistro cuisine, in a contemporary setting – exposed brickwork, wood and an open kitchen. Roast scallops, watercress and Ossau Iraty cheese^ skate wing, parsley root and Grenobloise sauce: a real treat... and a top tip!	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3337408912	Zoko Moko	6 rue Mazarin	France	Saint-Jean-de-Luz	Terrace	https://www.zoko-moko.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the historic fishermen’s district, this “zoko moko” (which means ‘peaceful spot’ in Basque) is quite the local landmark and often fully booked. Charles Olascuaga crafts contemporary straightforward food that is served in a charming interior dripping in authentic cachet (old stone walls and a large fireplace) or on a small terrace. The menu keeps pace with the seasons and aims to showcase regional ingredients, illustrated by the catch of the day from the local fish auction, green risotto and a shellfish emulsion^ haunch of tender veal and a medley of carrots in orange juice, ending with an irresistible millefeuille of caramelised apples and apple sorbet. Slick, low-key service.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3330599447	L'Essentiel	3 rue Vincent-Barjonnet	France	Saint-Jean-de-Luz	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lessentiel-saint-jean-de-luz.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	t	Off the beaten tourist track, chef Morgan Ortéga goes straight to the essentials: industrial loft interior, open kitchen, huge bay window, glazed wine cellar and leather bench seats. His talent and skill metamorphose market-fresh produce, enabling each ingredient to shout its name, to the delight of diners.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3336988012	Le Cairn	41 route de Thônes	France	Saint-Jean-de-Sixt	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lecairn-stjean.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	On the road to the mountain resorts of the Aravis range, between La Clusaz and Le Grand Bornand, this small mountain chalet needs to be marked with a pile of stones, like a cairn! In the small, inviting space done out in mountain style, there is no doubt about it: chef Adrien and maître d' Charline (all smiles) know how to delight their faithful guests. Adrien creates astonishing dishes that are full of flavour and beautifully fresh: the cold lettuce soup with cream of country bacon is a tasty sensation^ tender medallions of farm-reared lamb served rare...	coppolaartem	\N	\N
