3337616629	Lauryvan	200 allée du Bois-au-Bœuf	France	Saint-Junien	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lauryvan.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In this verdant setting in a small wood close to the Vienne River, tuck into meticulous cuisine attuned to the seasons. The inspector was a fan of the organic confit egg, creamy parsnip purée, Cantal cheese shavings and ham crisps, as well as the lovely terrace with a view of the lake. Two spaces: restaurant and bistro.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3336586360	Les Allées	17 allée Gaston-Phoebus	France	Saint-Justin	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://restaurantlesallees.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Antoine and Coralie met in Jean Cousseau's two-Michelin-starred restaurant (Relais de la Poste in Magescq) after gaining solid experience in France and Spain. This former café-restaurant has been given a facelift that subtly blends vintage and modern features (waxed concrete floors paired with exposed beams). As for the food, this pair of pros focuses on flavour, often drawing on the Iberian pantry to put a spin on traditional dishes: calf's head croquette^ leeks in vinaigrette^ sautéed sweetbreads^ grilled octopus etc. Two terraces: one out front and one in the courtyard, away from the street.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3332536873	Les Pieds Dans l'Eau	28 chemin de la Folle-Entreprise	France	Saint-Langis-lès-Mortagne	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://restaurant-lespiedsdansleau.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Built at the far end of the village and surrounded by fields, this old mill is also close to a lake: it is hard to imagine a more bucolic sight! A hard-working chef serves up modern bistro cuisine comprising generous mains (eg beef confit with turnips and lentils) and mouth-watering desserts (coffee panna cotta, ladyfinger sponges and mascarpone). Soak up the warm, laid-back atmosphere as you gaze out over the meadows from the pleasant terrace.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3332092254	La Grange	13 route d'Autun	France	Saint-Lary-Soulan	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-saint-lary.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This former barn is now an inviting country chic restaurant appointed in an alpine vein. The menu stars tasty well-crafted food, made with premium regional ingredients such as marinated salmon trout from Lake Oô^ confit of egg, shredded confit of duck and creamy sweetcorn… What’s not to like?	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3330978738	Auberge de la Source	2 chemin des Falaises	France	Saint-Léonard	Car park,Terrace	http://www.aubergedelasource.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A little country inn hidden away in a remote location is sometimes all it takes to pique our interest. Our curiosity was quickly rewarded by Gabin Bouguet, formerly chef at Le Donjon in Étretat, who, here in his own restaurant, wanted to keep things simple without compromising on indulgence. Hummus, haddock, crunchy vegetables^ pork belly, carrot mousseline, herb crumble^ lemon tart: a treat from start to finish. After your meal, take a stroll to the cliffs a few hundred metres away – there you'll enjoy a beautiful view of Fécamp, as painted by Claude Monet.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3334603560	Yam	4 rue d'Altkirch	France	Saint-Louis	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-yam.com	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	€€	t	f	You can rely on chef Chatchai Klanklong (chef/patron of L'Orchidée, 1 star at Altkirch) and his brother Kriankai to concoct flavoursome Thai cuisine, such as Tom Yam (prawn and coconut milk soup), or 30-day aged Iberico pork chop with cauliflower and spiced tamarind jus... Premium ingredients, distinctive, well-balanced flavours, precise culinary technique and careful presentation.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3338970649	Comète	35 rue de la Grève	France	Saint-Lunaire	Terrace	https://cometesaintlunaire.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Comète is in the centre of the seaside resort, near the beach. Each dish by chef Victor Nicolas is a reminder of his Michelin-starred career in Paris and, more particularly, his time working for Christophe Pelé: the dishes are on the creative side, the ingredients top-notch, the no-frills preparations don't mess around, the sauces are elegant and the condiments punchy. For example, spider crab, fennel and strawberries^ roast brill, potatoes, chard and meunière sauce. The decoration of this small old-school bistro (old pine floorboards, salvaged and mismatched furniture, vintage-style light fittings) does the rest.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3333005019	Le Bistrot du Rocher	19 rue de Toulouse	France	Saint-Malo			Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	t	At a slight remove from the hustle and bustle of tourist activity, but still inside the ramparts, this simple, friendly restaurant is housed in a two-storey building typical of Saint-Malo. The restaurant is run by an enthusiastic chef, who called on Rennes-based artist MioSHe to paint frescoes on the walls. His cooking is inspired by the market (spider crab with curry and beetroot^ crépinette – pork sausage patties – and gnocchi^ poached pear and guanaja chocolate). Home-made bread and natural wines. Unbeatable lunch set menu during the week^ more extensive menu in the evening and at weekends.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3338575473	Ar Iniz	8 boulevard Hébert	France	Saint-Malo	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://ariniz.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The restaurant's menu is designed by chef Christian Le Squer. The cooking techniques are spot on, and the top-notch ingredients are expertly prepared, resulting in flavoursome dishes: delicate langoustine ravioli, beurre blanc with chives^ Hereford rib steak, home fries^ cheesecake-style crème brûlée. The bright, modern setting boasts an exceptional view of the beach, Plage du Sillon. In fine weather, the terrace is a must! A bargain set lunch menu is up for grabs on weekdays.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3335072553	Le Cambusier	6 rue des Cordiers	France	Saint-Malo		https://www.cambusier.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Welcome to this cheerful wine bar in the heart of the illustrious walled city. The owner, a sommelier, who is proud to be a “born and bred” Breton, scours France to unearth excellent tipples. In the kitchen, her husband celebrates local produce: ravioles of pork with pleurote mushrooms and a stock of heritage veggies^ loin of cod in smoked paprika with crunchy green cabbage and a lemon-ginger butter.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3332052851	Maison Vermer	79 boulevard de Rochebonne	France	Saint-Malo	Terrace	http://www.maisonvermer.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	In a spruce house a stone’s throw from Rochebonne beach, rather than a Dutch painter, you will find a chef whose culinary ambition is to unite land and sea (hence the pun: “ver(t)”/green for the land and “mer”/sea for the… sea!). In his open-plan kitchen, he works with locally sourced produce, delivering well-balanced dishes: cream of white asparagus with shellfish and andouille sausage^ soufflée of courgette flower and langoustine, tarragon emulsion^ a refreshing lemon and citron dessert… Market-fresh fare, sensibly priced lunchtime menu, more ambitious in the evenings with brunch on Sunday lunchtimes.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3334711788	Le Saint-Martial	Le Bourg	France	Saint-Martial-de-Nabirat	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.lesaintmartial.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Valérie and Jean-Marc Réal have been at the helm of this delightful restaurant in a peaceful Black Périgord village for over twenty years. The chef enhances seasonal produce, cleverly blending tradition and modernity, in particular courtesy of punchy gravies and carefully balanced combinations of ingredients. Examples include sautéed snails and calf’s head wrapped in green leaves, garnished with a watercress-flavoured crème of cep mushrooms. A warm welcome and an extensive wine cellar add the final flourish to a slap-up meal.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3334045156	George's	Hôtel de Toiras	France	Saint-Martin-de-Ré	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hotel-de-toiras.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Boasting an ideal location in the port of Saint-Martin-de-Ré, this chic brasserie has a seaside-inspired interior decor. Featuring alongside the unfussy dishes made with precisely prepared regional produce (freshly caught fish, Challans poultry) are some great French classics (pan-fried foie gras, baked snails). The pleasant terrace lounge and cocktail bar are popular. Attentive service.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3339933276	Le Serghi	15 quai Georges-Clemenceau	France	Saint-Martin-de-Ré	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://leserghi.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	t	On the old port, this restaurant (with its pleasant terrace at the front) belongs to the island's select club of restaurants that are open all year round. In the kitchen, a great chef, Philippe Tredgeu (previously at Entredgeu and Les Cocottes in Paris), crafts cuisine that calls to mind Parisian bistronomy. Fine ingredients, seasonal produce and indulgent dishes are the order of the day: green asparagus, egg mimosa, sauce parisienne or grilled and glazed confit pork belly with market-fresh vegetables. A joy from start to finish.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3339252390	Tandem Saveurs Nomades	50 avenue du Maréchal-de-Lattre-de-Tassigny	France	Saint-Maurice	Wheelchair access	http://www.tandemsaveursnomades.com	Nessun premio	Fusion	4.0	€€	f	f	The title says it all – a duo of chefs who trained under Thierry Marx and innovative fusion cuisine in which South American and Asian influences rub shoulders with pedigree French ingredients. The aubergines are underscored by miso sauce^ pollock is flanked by creamy green peas, risotto of quinoa and Thai herbs sprinkled with grilled buckwheat for a roasted flavour^ beef dumpling and a teriyaki sauce: everything is intelligently and patiently combined and assembled by our gourmet duo. This warm, colourful bistro, fully in tune with its era, is good news for the town centre of Saint-Maurice!	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3337124137	Bistrot 1936 - Domaine du Limonay	Lieu-dit Le Limonay	France	Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.domaine-du-limonay.com/fr/restaurants/bistrot.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	The latest addition to the Maison Tirel-Guérin stable (established back in 1936) is this bistro firmly rooted in the current century, with its lovely choice of materials (light-coloured wood and exposed beams) and its bay windows that invite the light to flood in. The menu, overseen by the chef of the fine dining restaurant, features mouthwatering top-quality ingredients, such as poularde, foie gras and spider crab. The delicious farm-reared pork – grilled belly and a wafer-thin slice of andouille – was a particular hit with its delicious Roscoff onion jus.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3334364365	Beau Boucot	119 boulevard de l'Océan	France	Saint-Michel-Chef-Chef		http://www.beauboucot.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Facing the Grande Plage de Tharon, this bright seaside bistro is an offshoot of chef Mathieu Guibert's restaurant, Anne de Bretagne. You can get a taste of the sea, both in the dishes (some of which, such as the seafood platters, are for sharing) and in the surrounding scenery. Vegetarian and meat options are also served. The impeccable quality of the dishes benefits from the chef's network of suppliers. From the fried prawn amuse-bouche to the new take on vitello tonnato, and not forgetting the smoked trout, everything is on point. The service, provided by a young, smiling team, is the epitome of professionalism and friendliness. The wine list is full of surprises. Excellent value for money on the set menu. A good job well done.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
