3336219978	Les Toits - Hôtel de Paris Saint-Tropez	1 traverse de la Gendarmerie	France	Saint-Tropez	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking	http://www.hoteldeparis-sainttropez.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	t	Timeless Saint Tropez remains as legendary as ever – this outdoor restaurant perched on the roof terrace of the fabled hotel is further proof of that. Gazing out over the bay and the tiled roofs of the village, you can savour cuisine inspired by the Mediterranean and Provence, with a few Italian touches thrown in for good measure (Sicilian gambas, tiramisu etc) – after all, the new chef, whose CV includes Il Carpaccio, Le Grand Véfour and Pierro TT in Paris, is Italian. A simpler set menu is proposed at lunchtime.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3332458667	La Ponche	5 rue des Remparts	France	Saint-Tropez	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://laponche.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Chef Thomas Danigo (formerly of the Galanga in Paris) signs the menu of this emblematic Saint-Tropez restaurant, located in the eponymous district facing the sea. The cuisine is Mediterranean, giving pride of place to the catch of the day and vegetables from the region, alongside premium joints of meat. The memory of his ceviche of seabream, citrus fruits and coriander-basil sorbet and the dessert of roasted figs with apple and myrtle balsamic, almond crumble and pistachio ice cream lingers with us still.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3336015413	Schorre	2 quai Lejoille	France	Saint-Valery-sur-Somme	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.schorre.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	The top floor of this entirely revamped 18C salt barn is home to a contemporary, ‘unfinished’, stripped-back restaurant which commands a panoramic view over the Somme Bay. According to the dictionary, a schorre (or a salt marsh) refers to an “upper coastal intertidal zone of thick mud, covered by grass and regularly flooded by high tides”. Our poached turbot was flanked by a crisp, salty salad of salt marsh plants (samphire, maritime asters, halimione). Chef François-Xavier Sailly regularly renews his creative gourmet score, illustrated by white asparagus and a tarragon-flavoured hollandaise sauce or a pear and Jerusalem artichoke dessert.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3338273868	La Table de Monrecour	Lieu-dit Monrecour	France	Saint-Vincent-de-Cosse	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.monrecour.com/restaurant	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This gourmet restaurant is housed in a contemporary extension at the heart of this estate overlooking the Périgord countryside. It is furnished in a resolutely classical style and reflects modern culinary tendencies with the skilfully prepared and flavoursome dishes. Perfect for hotel residents, and anyone else.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3339862254	Prélude	5 place Simone-Veil	France	Saint-Vit	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantprelude.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Far more than a prelude, this is a full-blown symphony! Now established in a spruce traditional building, Élodie Ouchelli and Thibault Étienne practiced their scales in top star restaurants, among which that of Romuald Fassenet. The virtuoso chef, whose talent is a masterclass in culinary subtlety, composes harmonious dishes in which first-class local produce plays the leading role. Several tables of the contemporary dining room provide a view of the chef at work in the kitchen.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3336862966	Le Doyenné	5 rue Saint-Antoine	France	Saint-Vrain	Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://ledoyennerestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	What are two Australian chefs (with stints at Yard, Spring, Bones and Au Passage) doing in the heart of the grounds of Saint Vrain Castle, more precisely in the tastefully refurbished former stables? Well, they are knocking up spot-on food that is sourced directly from the estate’s huge cottage garden, which actually existed before the restaurant, using fruit and vegetables that are only harvested when perfectly ripe. A fine dining experience that mingles rural charm and gourmet delights, overlooking the surrounding countryside. Booking compulsory.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3331035657	L'Attanum	64 place de la Nation	France	Saint-Yrieix-la-Perche	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://attanum.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€	t	f	The ground floor of this 19C sous-préfecture is now home to a restaurant that welcomes you with contemporary interior design and smiling service. At the helm is a seasoned chef with stints at some prestigious establishments to his name. A fan of local seasonal produce, his cooking demonstrates his stellar technique (illustrated by his venison terrine), spot-on cooking and reductions (see his duck fillet served with spelt and beetroot) and delicately balanced flavours. The attentive staff and excellent wine cellar add the final flourishes to this gourmet experience.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3334808437	L'Auberge - Maisons Glenn Anna	56 rue de Vannes	France	Sainte-Anne-d'Auray	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://maisons-glenn-anna.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Ste-Anne-d'Auray is known for its sanctuary and pilgrimages, and Pope John Paul II is said to have stopped off at this restaurant in 1996. But it is by no means stuck in the past: the new generation concocts delicious fare, in which premium seafood takes pride of place, as in the half-cooked tuna with a medley of tomatoes and béarnaise sauce.	calincolin	\N	\N
3331492627	Campagne, Vignes et Gourmandises	629 chemin des Terres	France	Sainte-Cécile-les-Vignes	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-cvg.com/	Nessun premio	Provençal	5.0	€€	f	f	With its atmosphere blending rustic charm (exposed stones, painted wooden furniture) and modern touches (contemporary paintings), this restaurant has bags of character. In the kitchen, chef Sylvain Fernandes prepares fresh ingredients in a subtle celebration of the flavours of the South of France. Extremely courteous service provided by Sylvia, the chef's wife!	orlandofernando	\N	\N
3336149091	L'Argence	Rue du Riols	France	Sainte-Geneviève-sur-Argence	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.largence.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of Aubrac, a couple of industry professionals have taken over this old inn dating from the early 1900s that has been completely renovated to sport a refined contemporary style. Chef Jonathan Riboulet, who has a wealth of MICHELIN-starred experience (Guérard, Pic, Lameloise and, above all, 12 years with Bras at Laguiole), serves up a cuisine in which he skilfully allies produce from the terroir (trout from the Monts d'Aubrac, escargots from Aveyron, entrecôte from Aubrac) with local herbs (meadowsweet, wild garlic, salad burnet). The result is playful, fresh and colourful – but also creative, a rare thing in these parts. The bright, modern dining area looks out onto a delightful terrace surrounded by a garden that bursts with blooms in season. Six guestrooms and two spacious, comfortable apartments provide a base from which to explore this pretty part of France.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3330091665	Le Chai	5 place d'Antioche	France	Sainte-Marie-de-Ré	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurantlechai.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Beautifully located on Sainte-Marie-de-Ré market square, this laidback eatery offers bistronomic fare with a distinct preference for local veg from mainly organic small market gardeners. The frequently changing concise menu stars seasonal ingredients, together with local fish and offal. Everything is fresh, well executed and good value for money, illustrated by a tender slab of pearlescent haddock or a 64°C poached egg in a creamy mushroom sauce topped with crispy bacon pieces.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3339545430	Auberge de Sainte-Maure	99 route de Méry	France	Sainte-Maure	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://auberge-saintemaure.ovh/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	The young owner, Victor Martin, and his chef Julien Drapier are now a well-established duo. The dishes tend towards an undeniable finesse, such as the roasted langoustine, fennel confit and shell jus. Add to that smiling service, good value for money, and a pleasant terrace by the water.	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3338048294	À Table ! Chez Éric Léautey	28 rue Porte-Saint-Martin	France	Thoiry	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://ericleautey.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Being at Chez Eric Léautey is a pleasure. The small porch prepares you for the tasting to come, and your taste buds stand to attention as you read the menu. The suggestions are deliberately down - to - earth, drawing on the seasons and local terroir, such as the veal chop, as tender and juicy as can be. So, what are you waiting for?	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3330178462	La Badiane	6 rue Fernand-Bessy	France	Sainte-Maxime	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-la-badiane.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Just a stone's throw from the covered market, this space with a pared-back decor has charm to spare, with wood and stone in perfect harmony above the nicely dressed untreated wood tables. Chef Geoffrey Poësson (trained under Roger Vergé at Le Moulin de Mougins) is quietly coming into his own, as he creates a fine modern cuisine in which vegetables and fish predominate (even if pigeon is his signature dish and lamb and beef are also served): fresh tomatoes with anchovies, marjoram velouté^ roast sea bream loin, saffron-steamed belly, a bouillabaisse-style stock with the fish head and seasonal vegetables. A simpler set lunchtime menu, except in summer.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3337420522	Les Épicuriens	Domaine de Barive	France	Sainte-Preuve	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.domainedebarive.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	The restaurant set in a period castle concocts delicate, up-to-date food whose exquisite plating will find favour with even the most discerning connoisseurs, illustrated by carpaccio of langoustines in citrus fruit, fennel and caviar. The enticing wine list naturally showcases champagnes and the stylish terrace overlooks the estate’s gardens. Pleasant rooms for overnight stays.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3335898730	Le Lassey - Château Sainte-Sabine	8 route de Semur	France	Sainte-Sabine	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.saintesabine.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This elegant restaurant in the historical setting of the Renaissance Château Sainte-Sabine stands out on account of its refined cuisine. A simpler set menu is available at lunchtime. The guestrooms invite you to unwind as you take in the lake and bucolic grounds, where deer roam.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3337321665	29	9 place Blair	France	Saintes	Terrace	https://www.restaurant29.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Chef Michael Durkin is a tattooed Englishman and rugby fan who has worked in some of the best restaurants in the world. He whips up creative modern bistro cuisine, for example seared cod, celeriac and capers – a well-presented and harmonious dish. Not only is the four-course set lunch menu unbeatable value, the small terrace is a real draw in fine weather.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3336117134	La Table du Relais du Bois Saint-Georges	132 cours Genet	France	Saintes	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.relaisdubois.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Fall under the spell of this restaurant housed in an old farmhouse, where the chef has a penchant for beautiful seasonal ingredients (sourced from local producers or the aromatic plant garden located in the grounds). Drink in the view of the terrace, fountain and small lake through the bay windows, as you savour calf sweetbread, spatchcock, elderberry – the soft juicy meat makes for a taste sensation!	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3330250064	Le Dallaison	30 rue du Bois-Taillis	France	Saintes	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.ledallaison.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	The beautiful exterior of this 18C manor house set in grounds gives little away. Inside, the 21C makes itself felt throughout the various dining nooks: designer furniture, original lights, white walls, wine cabinets. A place like this can only inspire Jérôme Dallet, a chef who has worked with Emmanuel Renaut (Megève) and Anne-Sophie Pic (Valence). Local produce is given pride of place (mogette beans, snails, Confolens lamb…) and the chef uses it to create wonderfully indulgent compositions. In fine weather, you can enjoy the terrace surrounded by greenery.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3332276434	Le Parvis	12 quai de l'Yser	France	Saintes	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-le-parvis.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This picturesque house on the banks of the Charente in downtown Saintes is where Pascal Yenk rustles up mouth - watering regional dishes using ingredients fresh from the market. Everything is homemade, including the sauces, to the delight of diners’ taste buds. Sheltered terrace in fine weather.	orlandofernando	\N	\N
3330534774	L'AbSix	2 rue de la Cerdagne	France	Saleilles	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-labsix.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Do not be misled by the colonial feel of this large building, you can trust the experienced chef to surprise your taste buds. With a single set menu that changes weekly, he cooks up modern and creative dishes that reflect the seasons: croustillant with parmesan, marinated chanterelles and a sweet garlic cream^ turbot fillet tempura, coconut, lemongrass and a ginger emulsion.	bianconathan	\N	\N
3331160285	Restaurant des Voisins	12 rue des Voisins	France	Salies-de-Béarn	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-des-voisins.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Here, charming old features are enhanced by an eye for designer details (contemporary art, open kitchen). Original, well-crafted cuisine (semi-cooked line-caught albacore tuna from the Basque country, cream of pumpkin soup with coconut milk^ cod confit ravioli, broth with herbs and spices, trout roe and sweet spice tuile), accompanied by a fine wine list. A master class in tastefully mixing the traditional and modern, in the decor as well as in the food.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3339538875	Cascade	26 cour de la Filature	France	Salles-la-Source	Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	What a pretty village clinging to a cliff and famous for its cooling waterfall! What a pleasant, convivial place, with its warm, colourful bistro decor, lovely old wooden floorboards, counter and arty posters on the walls (and let's not forget the terrace overlooking the courtyard in front of the town hall). In the kitchen, chef Marine Guichou cooks up a feast, using carefully selected local produce, which she skilfully prepares in a fresh, authentic bistro style. And with her almond pannacotta and chocolate mousse on a cocoa crumble, she has created the quintessential dessert for anyone with a sweet tooth!	martinooliver	\N	\N
3332301643	Le Lodge	20 route de Sixt	France	Samoëns	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant is run by a young couple who are passionate about what they do: chef Flavio Ricco and Lola Goudenove. In the heart of the village it has a cosy dining area done out in the style of a lodge. The blend of wood and stone makes for a relaxing feel. The chef prepares traditional cuisine with a measure of creativity, highlighting local ingredients on a set menu (with options). This lunchtime, the chef demonstrated his finesse when revisiting soupe châtrée – a rather hearty Samoëns speciality made with bread, Tomme de Savoie cheese and onion soup, that was followed by a fillet of sea bass with celery and beurre blanc with Génépi. For dessert, there was candied apple, vanilla cream and vanilla ice cream. The welcome and service are charming: in fact, the chef comes out of his kitchen from time to time to serve his guests.	langalice	\N	\N
3334433294	La Corniche	1 chemin di u Fornu (Hameau de Castagneto)	France	San-Martino-di-Lota	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.hotel-lacorniche.com/	Nessun premio	Corsican	5.0	€€	t	t	A family business clinging to the mountain with a splendid terrace shaded by plane trees overlooking the sea... Exquisite plating, delicious flavours with notes of Corsican saffron and confit of citron, twice-cooked mouth-watering veal or the decadent vacherin dessert perfumed with the one and only Madagascan vanilla, all of which washed down with locally grown vintages.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3333864887	Shin Yeh Taiwanese Cuisine	34-1 Shuangcheng Street	Taiwan	Taipei	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.shinyeh.com.tw/content/zh/Brand/Index.aspx?BrandId=1	Nessun premio	Taiwanese	4.0	$$	f	f	A household name in Taiwanese cuisine since 1977, it specialises in authentic home-style cooking that seems simple, but requires scrupulous care – just try the egg omelette with dried radish, pan-seared pork liver and flatbread rolls. Even their almond tofu dessert is made by three chefs from scratch. This branch boasts 110 tables and is ideal for banquets and parties of all sizes.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3335786740	La Pomme d'Or	1 rue de la Panneterie	France	Sancerre	Wheelchair access	https://lapommedorsancerre.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of a famous wine-growing village, a young couple from Brittany has opted to shine the spotlight on seafood to such an extent that you can almost smell the sea air. Their single set menu, whose dishes are intriguingly and poetically named, offers a choice of flawlessly fresh fish and shellfish, all of which are consummately cooked. The chef, who clearly knows his stuff, has his sights clearly focused on a single goal: taste. The wine list unsurprisingly gives the floor to Sancerre wines, and you'll hear no complaints from us. Cheerful, smiling service in an uncluttered, elegant interior.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
