3335784590	Les Jardins de Kerstéphanie	Route du Roaliguen	France	Sarzeau	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lesjardinsdekerstephanie.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	This old stone farmstead smothered in Virginia creeper and set in wooded grounds is home to the new headquarters of Emmanuel Kouri, previously encountered at Les Climats (Paris). Mindful of the provenance of his produce (line-caught fish, organic market gardeners, local dairy produce), he conjures up seafood dishes, like little tunny in kari-gosse, marinated cucumber and iced coriander soup or ikejime pollock, violin courgette in basil and a pistachio and lime sabayon. To be enjoyed on the shaded terrace in fine weather.	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3331126421	La Terrasse	11 cours du Docteur-Gervais	France	Saugues	Air conditioning	https://www.hotellaterrasse-saugues.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	Do not worry, the Beast of Gévaudan is no more! However, if you are as hungry as the wolf, this place is for you. The chef, Cyril Tardy, cooks a contemporary interpretation of cuisine du terroir using good, very fresh, locally sourced ingredients.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3338937707	Bistrot Loiseau du Morvan	Hostellerie de la Tour d’Auxois	France	Saulieu	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.bernard-loiseau.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Opposite the Loiseau family’s legendary Côte d’Or restaurant, this handsome 17C edifice is both a supremely comfortable traditional hostelry and a bistro, offering an appetising more casual alternative to its fine dining parent establishment. Here, local and regional recipes take pride of place, such as eggs in a red wine sauce or chicken à la Gaston Gérard. The rotunda dining room, which leads onto a terrace, is the epitome of country chic with old terracotta tiled flooring and a glorious timber ceiling, all of which in an unabashed, full-on Burgundy style.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3330507095	Masama	5 place de la Bilange	France	Saumur		http://www.masama.fr	Nessun premio	Fusion	3.0	€€	t	t	Experience a slice of South America behind this resplendent pistachio-green shopfront in the heart of Saumur. Colombian chef Marlon Medina made headlines in the local press when he coached his country's team for the Bocuse d'Or cooking contest in 2023. His cuisine may be multicultural, but it nevertheless shows clear South American leanings, which are sometimes allied with local ingredients (such as asparagus or mushrooms). For dinner, by means of a short and to-the-point menu, the chef proposes indulgent dishes such as an excellent picanha accompanied by an impeccable chimichurri condiment. Another signature dish is the ceviche, made with fish from the market. At lunchtime, there's a more typically French single set menu without options.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3330626327	L'Alchimiste	6 rue de Lorraine	France	Saumur	Terrace	https://www.lalchimiste-saumur.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Despite the name you won’t find any molecular cuisine here. Instead, enjoy good, no - nonsense dishes such as courgette and goat’s cheese flan, and poached pears. It is often full so it is best to book.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3336243265	L'Essentiel	11 rue Raspail	France	Saumur	Terrace	http://www.restaurant-lessentiel-saumur.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Nestled at the foot of the castle, this beautiful tuffeau-stone house sports charming dining rooms (parquet floors, exposed rafters and bare stone walls) and peaceful little patios. Chef Anthony Vaillant crafts food in the zeitgeist, jazzed up by a scattering of deft creative touches: start with a medley of asparagus and green peas, enhanced by a citrus fruit flavoured dressing followed by fabulously fresh cod flanked by a curry sauce and velvety mashed potato. Extremely attentive service. Regional tipples take pride of place on the wine list. An enjoyable culinary experience!	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3337207980	L'Instinct	42 rue du Maréchal-Leclerc	France	Saumur	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurant-linstinct-saumur.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In his aptly named contemporary restaurant, chef Romain Bersan shows a distinct talent for cooking up modern cuisine. Spices make a welcome appearance, perfectly dosed with a sure hand (a case in point being the poultry jus elevated with smoked paprika and sake). Vegetarians can rest assured that the chef also caters to their dietary requirements. His delicious starter of vitello tonnato was nothing short of an escapade to Italy.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3337987752	La Table du Château Gratien	94 route de Montsoreau	France	Saumur	Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-saumur-gratien.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	In the landscaped grounds of the Gratien and Meyer wine estate, this adorable late 19C château oozes character and cachet – herringbone parquet, glittering chandeliers and a fireplace. The cuisine deftly showcases the region's fine produce – white asparagus, black truffle and Val de Loire potatoes. Herbs from the garden, excellent home-made bread, warm madeleines served with coffee. A taste of the good life.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3333999636	L'Escargot	30 rue du Maréchal-Leclerc	France	Saumur	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lescargot49.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	A pleasant contemporary setting for traditional cuisine and emblematic dishes, such as snails in butter, garlic and parsley. Chef-owner Dominique Dubert jazzes up a traditional repertory with the odd dash of modernity (combava, ginger, curry, etc). It is a pleasure to linger over a meal on the terrace of this Snail in summer.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3339184544	Le Boeuf Noisette	29 rue Molière	France	Saumur		https://www.leboeufnoisette.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Take a seat in this vintage - style bistro, dotted with benches, marble tables and mirrors to sample a brief, well - designed menu focused on regional produce (particularly “Rouge des prés” beef). Ideally located behind the theatre, parallel with the Loir embankment and close to a large carpark. First - class, short food supply chain produce.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3337062587	La Table de Jeanne	14 avenue de la Grande-Motte	France	Tignes		https://www.les-suites-du-nevada.com/table-de-jeanne/	Nessun premio	Savoyard	4.0	€€€	t	f	This mountainside restaurant, the brainchild of the Bouvier family (of Les Suites, Ursus, Panoramic), is depicted by generous dishes in which country produce takes pride of place. Warm, welcoming and a fine selection of reasonably - priced wines.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3331983857	Le Cercle Guiraud	14 rue Principale	France	Sauternes	Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lecercleguiraud.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In the heart of the village, this traditional eatery offers a choice between a dining room whose countrified décor is dotted with the odd contemporary touch, or, in fine weather, a terrace shaded by mulberry plane trees that commands an exquisite view as far as Château Guiraud, which owns the restaurant. Yoann Amado, former chef of Maison Darroze in Langon, and his pastry chef partner, Juliette Bonnard, craft a scrumptious gourmet score that hits the spot every time: truly flavoursome oxheart tomatoes, burrata of goat’s cheese, infusion of tomato water and verbena^ trout marinated in miso and confit, baby spinach shoots, beurre blanc of pike roe^ vanilla-flavoured crème brûlée, apricots and an exquisite last-minute lemon thyme-flavoured sorbet.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3339282629	L'Hibiscus by Jérémy Lasserre	Hameau de Gesset	France	Sauveterre-de-Comminges	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park	http://www.hotel-dubarry.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	In his stronghold in the Hôtel du Barry, at the foot of the Pyrenees, is a chef who knows his stuff: his intelligent, technically sound cuisine (eg low-temperature cooking, espumas and dashi stock) also hints at the 14 years he spent in Asia. The onsen-style slow-cooked egg served with a trilogy of Tarbais beans and mushrooms is one of his specialities. Attentive service and comfortable guestrooms mean there's no reason not to prolong the experience.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3330165159	Le Sénéchal	Le Bourg	France	Sauveterre-de-Rouergue	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-senechal.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	In a remote little village in the Haut Ségala known for its 13C bastide house and arcaded square, this restaurant with a plush feel is accommodated in a half-timbered house. Michel Truchon has passed the baton to a family, originally from Normandy, who are perpetuating their predecessor's respect for the finest ingredients. For instance: spinach raviolo with Vieux Rodez cheese – Aveyron's answer to Parmesan – topped with a reduced meat jus and a cazette (Burgundy hazelnut) emulsion^ or red mullet cooked à la nacre topped with a rock fish jus and a delicate aubergine pulp. They also have a handful of guestrooms, should you wish to stay overnight.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3339527478	La Table Saint-Martin	17 place Saint-Martin	France	Sauxillanges	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://latable-stmartin.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	The Table Saint-Martin specialises in spot-on, tasty food that keeps pace with the seasons. Top-notch quality, consummate culinary skill and distinctive flavours – the stage is set for a fine dining experience. Patio in the inner courtyard.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3337155333	Hôtel du Phare	Quai Guerveur	France	Sauzon	Great view,Terrace	http://www.hotelduphare-belle-ile.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Belle-Île-en-Mer's emblematic Hôtel du Phare (1880) and its restaurant have been redesigned and revamped by a famous architect. The decor is original, juxtaposing bright colours with the black and white of the Breton flag. The menu focuses on marine flavours, with dishes such as spider crab in its shell, bisque, celeriac ravioli with spider crab^ viennoise of sea bass cooked on a stone, artichoke fricassee with clams and black garlic. As much as he can, the chef uses quality ingredients, often from the island (eg lamb reared in Bangor, honey, organic vegetables and fish from a local fisherman). There is a lovely terrace overlooking the harbour, and further dining options at Le Bistrot.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3337650210	Auberge Ramstein	1 rue du Riesling	France	Scherwiller	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hotelramstein.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The tradition of hospitality continues from one generation to the next at this family affair, surrounded by vineyards. The son, Lucas, who honed his craft in several prestigious restaurants, creates contemporary dishes with a nod to the Alsace terroir : barbecued beets with salmon trout from Sparsbach, or saddle of venison with celeriac, cocoa nibs and spaetzle. The welcome is warm, the service attentive and guestrooms prolong the pleasure.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3330027864	Côté Lac	2 place de Paris	France	Schiltigheim	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	This raw concrete and glass parallelepiped looks slightly incongrouous standing on the banks of a small lake in an industrial area in the north of the city. The interior has a distinct modern loft feel with its modern lighting and contemporary paintings. Enjoy the current and carefully prepared dishes from a menu that changes regularly.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
