3331369004	Le Banquet des Sophistes	5 rue d'Austerlitz	France	Strasbourg	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://le-banquet.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	It’s no mean feat to get a table at this bistrot in the Krutenau neighbourhood. A well-deserved success for this address that offers an unbeatable set menu at lunchtime and a more elaborate menu in the evenings: scallop tempura with ginger, avocado and pomegranate-lemon dressing, or Basque pork chop with stuffed cabbage and polenta. Well-crafted, fresh and aromatic dishes, prepared in a spirit of eclecticism that pushes gently into fusion cuisine. Stimulating for the tastebuds and a friendly atmosphere to boot, what’s not to like ?	guerravictor	\N	\N
3337904644	Léonor	11 rue de la Nuée-Bleue	France	Strasbourg	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.leonor-hotel.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	Behind a 19C façade and within 18C walls, this contemporary hotel designed by Jean-Philippe Nuel has its own lounge-style restaurant adjoining the bar. The menu is in keeping with the culinary zeitgeist: for example, tuna sashimi, mango, avocado, with soy and sesame sauce, or sautéed calf’s sweetbreads, celery and lovage. For tables of friends, there are large dishes designed to share (whole seabass, rib steak etc). For those with a sweet tooth, there’s a choice of plated desserts or pretty pastries laid out in the display cabinet.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3331939427	Mademoiselle 10	10 quai des Pêcheurs	France	Strasbourg	Air conditioning	https://www.mlle10.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	On the banks of the Ill, this charming restaurant delights its regulars with very reasonable prices, especially at lunchtime. Salmon and leek mosaic wrapped in nori, scallops with sweet potato and coconut cream, or fillet of duck, home-made cep gnocchi and “spicy cocoa” jus...	donatidiego	\N	\N
3338911926	Ondine	10 petite rue des Dentelles	France	Strasbourg		https://ondine-strasbourg.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	In the picturesque little streets of the Petite France neighbourhood, this tiny restaurant attracts those looking for a lively, meaningful culinary experience. At the helm are Noémie D'hooge, an art graduate turned chef, and her partner Marin Rémy, whose path has been more conventional. Their modern, predominantly plant-based set menu is full of finesse, featuring seasonal ingredients that have been carefully selected from small local producers. You'll be pleasantly struck by the variety of dishes, which are never repeated twice. The pair work in front of the customer in a pleasant, laid-back atmosphere. As for drinks, the Salvadoran sommelier serves a range of wines, often natural, as well as home-made kombuchas and other non-alcoholic concoctions.	stepanekgrace	\N	\N
3330681441	Zuem Ysehuet	21 quai Mullenheim	France	Strasbourg	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.zuem-ysehuet.com/fr/accueil/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In a neighbourhood on the bank of the Ill, this inn clad in Virginia creeper also has a quiet picturesque terrace. In the tasty dishes, seasonal ingredients take pride of place: vegetables grown by the chef's father and intelligently cooked by his son. The lamb fillet, osso buco-style vegetables and date condiment is a good example. Terrific wine list, with a particularly good choice of wines by the glass.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3336661177	Bistro Là-Haut	70 avenue Franklin-Roosevelt	France	Suresnes	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.bistrolahaut.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Thanks to the hilltop location on Mont Valérien, this loft-style restaurant commands a superb view of Paris. The à la carte menu boasts a tempting range of contemporary dishes, such as confit farmhouse pork belly grilled on the barbecue, sweet potato mousseline, roast pointed cabbage, grapes with verjuice. For dinnertime, booking is strongly recommended.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3332942067	Et Toque !	7 rue Émile-Duclaux	France	Suresnes	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantettoque.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of Suresnes, chef Maxime Salvi creates modern, well-crafted, bistronomic fare (gloriously reasonably priced lunchtime menu). The flawless dishes highlight seasonal and top-drawer produce – tarragon and pistachio pork and poultry pâté en croûte with pickles^ Bourbonnais pork belly, Jerusalem artichokes, carrots and red wine jus. In the evening, a more ambitious culinary score and a carte blanche menu that depends entirely on the chef’s mood await the diner.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3339572400	La Cage aux Fleurs	13 avenue Jean-Jaurès	France	Tain-l'Hermitage	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lacageauxfleurs.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Flowers and colours abound in this spruce-looking bistro, both in the decor (floral wallpaper, varnished porcelain knick-knacks) and on the plate: tuna tartare, pumpkin seeds, grilled butternut condiment, anchovies with green pepper^ roast fillet of sea bass, panisse (chickpea fries), saffron, fennel. This cuisine in tune with the zeitgeist is delivered by a professional couple – themselves the offspring of restaurant owners – who work in tandem. French classics that are the winegrowers' favourites and cuts of meat to share are also present and correct.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3333031518	Le Mangevins	7 rue des Herbes	France	Tain-l'Hermitage	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lemangevins.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Here, bistro spirit and modernity are skilfully allied in the decoration. The food, created by a young couple of self-taught chefs, fêtes the market and proves to be meticulously prepared. The single set menu changes every day and for lunch on this occasion we sampled the Bigorre black pork shoulder, mustard seed juice and a Breton buckwheat shortbread, chocolate cream and praline emulsion. The dishes are explained in a friendly atmosphere, and, as is fitting in such a place, the menu is accompanied by a fine selection of regional wines.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3336175989	Le Quai	17 rue Joseph-Peala	France	Tain-l'Hermitage	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.chabran.com/pages/le-quai	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	You could stay on this quayside for hours admiring the Rhône and the vineyards. On the terrace or in the bright dining area, you could almost be on an ocean liner! A modern-day bistro in which to enjoy generous dishes.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3330102633	Les Terrasses - Le Cottage Bise	390 route du Port	France	Talloires-Montmin	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cottagebise.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	A luxurious and smart restaurant, a lovely terrace shaded by chestnut trees with the lake as its horizon, and modern cooking seasoned to a T mean you will enjoy your dining experience here. The chef prepares trout gravlax with asparagus, monkfish glazed with carrot and turmeric jus, and picanha of Black Angus beef with crunchy vegetables.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3330859426	L'Empreinte	2 rue Gaston-Manent	France	Tarbes	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-empreinte.com	Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	€€	f	f	Solid oak tables, custom-made tableware and a warm welcome… This snug restaurant is the stomping ground of Manuel Godet, who harnesses his impeccable textbook skills to crafting creative recipes that shine the spotlight on local produce, sometimes with surprising twists. Examples include Pyrenean gravlax trout and whipped cream flavoured with locally brewed gin, or a kiwi from Adour with cocoa, buckwheat and truffles. Simple lunchtime menu, more ambitious in the evening.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3338239554	Le Petit Gourmand	62 avenue Bertrand-Barère	France	Tarbes	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://lepetitgourmand.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Near the city centre, this vintage bistro is now the lair of Mathieu Espagnacq, who has taken over from his father, who opened the establishment back in the eighties. Mathieu, a seasoned chef with stints in Paris working with top chefs under his belt, crafts food in the zeitgeist that respects tradition and stars premium country produce (farm-reared pork cheeks braised in red wine, vegetables confit in thyme and gnocchi in a smoky cream sauce). A treat for your tastebuds from start to finish – remember to book!	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3333448213	Popôte	112 rue de la Chaudronnerie	France	Tarbes	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.popote-tarbes.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€	f	t	This contemporary bistro is near the Arsenal, a neighbourhood undergoing a major rehabilitation. The couple at the helm is formed of a chef with a wealth of Michelin-star experience and his partner, who has changed tack to become a maître d' and sommelier. The cuisine draws on modern trends: wrasse fish stuffed with rabbit and tarragon on a poultry jus, sprinkled with roasted almonds^ lamb kofta, pita bread with fromage blanc, coriander sprouts, and chopped parsley for freshness. The chef takes a savvy approach to cooking, especially when it comes to the bargain lunch (different every week). The wine list features wines from independent winegrowers. Booking essential.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3338011557	La Courtille	208 chemin de Cravailleux	France	Tavel	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace		Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Trained by Raquel Carena at her Parisian institution, Le Baratin, Natalia Crozon serves deliciously down-to-earth regional cuisine in this restaurant accommodated in a converted silkworm farm built of white stone. Poached calf brains with lemon butter^ pan-fried bluefin tuna steak with tomato ragout^ apricot cake... plenty to whet the appetite. Take your pick from the appealing wine list that focuses on natural wines and local Tavel and Lirac labels. In summer, tables are laid out on the pretty terrace sheltered by an ancient cedar tree.	paganialex	\N	\N
3336941513	La Tour des Sens	Route de Theys	France	Tencin	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.latourdessens.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	f	f	On the upper reaches of Tencin, this Tower is a treat for the five senses! Run by the same chef since 2016 (2017 Top Chef winner), his creative, natural menus aim to stimulate the taste buds of diners and thus call upon their emotions. When the weather’s fine, why not enjoy the fabulous view of the Chartreuse range from the terrace?	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3339855323	Le Moulin de L'Imaginaire	1 avenue Charles-de-Gaulle	France	Terrasson-Lavilledieu	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.moulin-limaginaire.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Born and bred in nearby Brive, the chef is an advocate of hearty traditional cuisine, in which local ingredients abound: fried egg, crispy bacon and new-potato galette^ calf's head with ravigote sauce^ free-range guinea fowl with carrots^ moist walnut cake with crème anglaise. This converted mill on the banks of the Vézère (the old cogs can still be seen beneath the glass floor in the entrance hall) has been renovated and transformed into a contemporary bistro. It also boasts a terrace built over the river, facing the 12C Pont Vieux.	bianconathan	\N	\N
3337508397	Mareluna	55 avenue de Lérins	France	Théoule-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.chateau-de-theoule.com/fr/mareluna/	Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€€	t	t	This former 17C soap factory is now a luxury hotel with a superb terrace affording panoramic views over the Bay of Cannes, Théoule-sur-Mer, Cap d'Antibes and the Îles de Lérins. Decorated in the Mediterranean style with rattan furniture, its elegant fine dining restaurant is open for dinner only. Having trained at Le Meurice Alain Ducasse restaurant and with Ryuji Teshima at Pages, Italian chef Francesco Fezza cooks up a number of Italian and local ingredients with spirit and creativity. This modern cuisine may be unabashedly Mediterranean, but the recipes are enhanced by little Asian touches: asparagus yuzukosho with ikejime-killed matured yellowtail or Thai consommé with osso buco pasta.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3333243421	La Maréa	16 avenue du Trayas	France	Théoule-sur-Mer	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamarea.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	t	f	Opposite the sea and the ochre-coloured rocks of Esterel and looking down on the beach and port of La Figueirette, this restaurant was founded in the 1950s by a local fisherman. It has been happily taken over by Jérôme Cervera, former fishmonger. The chef whips up à la carte flawlessly fresh seafood and carefully crafted dishes, illustrated by roast loin of gilt-head bream with shrimps, paella-style stock and chorizo. The lunch and evening menus feature à la carte dishes, served alfresco or in the pretty dining room with a sea view.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3333957965	La Table du Clos	49 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Thiers	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.clos-st-eloi.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	On the way out of town, this eatery combines a peaceful, secluded setting with a modern, brasserie score. The dessert of green apple on a vanilla ganache with apples in a butterscotch sauce, for example, is heavenly! Pleasant terrace.	montanarijack	\N	\N
3336280733	Aux Poulbots Gourmets	9 place aux Fleurs	France	Thionville	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.poulbotsgourmets.com/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	The rascally, iconic poulbots (street urchins) of Montmartre have now been joined by those of Thionville! Large bay windows, Lloyd Loom chairs and modern light fixtures add to the timeless elegance. The menu features recipes such as lobster salad and seasonal vegetables or pan-fried frogs’ legs…	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3335006455	Auberge de l'Abbaye	15 rue du Commerce	France	Thiron-Gardais	Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.aubergedelabbaye.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€	f	t	Treat yourself to a meal in the country, in the professional hands of this couple who have set up shop in a pretty stone house overlooking the abbey and Royal College of Thiron - Gardais. Seasonal dishes and a new subtle version of classical recipes. Flawlessly prepared with distinctive flavours. Lovely!	martinifederico	\N	\N
3333608055	Le Panoramic	Glacier de la Grande Motte	France	Tignes	Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://maison-bouvier.com/le-panoramic-restaurant-tignes/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Grills	4.0	€€€€	t	t	Accessed by a funicular railway, this high-altitude restaurant (elevation: 3 032m!) promises a breath of fresh air as well as fine dining. In an inviting interior that is done out in wood, staff in traditional costume serve up authentic and delicious wood-fired dishes, including choice cuts of meat and fish to share (eg rib steak, pork shoulder and whole turbot). A delightful change of scene.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3338226231	Beam !	2 rue Hippolyte-Duprat	France	Toulon	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant.letelegraphe.org/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Beaming and buzzing! The kitchens of the Télégraphe, a high spot of Toulon’s cultural life, are all go! Energetic Arnaud Tabarec, born in Burgundy, honed his skills in prestigious establishments and was the star chef of the Five Hotel’s Roof in Cannes. Today he is acclaimed for his delicate, predominantly vegetarian cuisine, whose ingredients are of course sourced locally and combined boldly.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3336750115	Le Pastel	20 rue Victor Micholet - Square Léon Vérane	France	Toulon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-lepastel.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Just a stone's throw from the harbour, this restaurant is a great success. With dishes such as semi-salted skrei with mussels, spinach, a shellfish jus with curry and lemon leaf, the chef's cuisine is very much in tune with the times. A cordial welcome and professional service from the owner.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3333270341	Au Sourd	10 rue Molière	France	Toulon	Terrace	https://restaurantausourd.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€€	f	t	A true Toulon institution, created by an artilleryman of Napoleon III, who went deaf while fighting, as referenced in the name. You can't really argue with what the chef offers: his cooking draws whole shoals of fish-lovers (bouillabaisse and bourride made to order, fried red mullet, rainbow wrasse, sole etc, depending on the catch) in a chic and contemporary atmosphere.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3334775688	Le Saint Gabriel	334 avenue de la République	France	Toulon	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of Toulon, opposite the bronze statue Génie de la Navigation and in the shadow of the Frontale du Port (the 1950s listed buildings by Jean de Mailly that divide opinion), is chef Romain Janin's bistro. The menu celebrates the food culture of Provence, putting a twist on fresh local ingredients: Tamaris mussels au gratin^ wild prawn ravioli^ egg mayonnaise with summer truffles^ courgette flower fritters^ lamb shoulder confit^ textures of beef tongue. Each plate is brimming with generosity and suggests savoir-faire to spare. The atmosphere here is relaxed and friendly, with service provided by staff who move between the cast-iron bistro tables and rattan chairs in sailor-style stripy T-shirts. A really great place that won't break the bank.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3339870805	Genty Magre	3 rue Genty-Magre	France	Toulouse		https://www.legentymagre.com/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the street of the same name, this bistro adds a joyful, even delicate spin to French country cooking, with special mention for the house speciality: cassoulet with duck confit and sausages, served on ceramic plates. Flawless preparations and high-flying seasoning^ good value for money.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
