3330718606	Les Planeurs	56 boulevard des Minimes	France	Toulouse	Terrace	https://lesplaneurs.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€	t	f	A Japanese chef and his partner have opened this unusual establishment in a deliberately bohemian and offbeat setting. The French cuisine is precise, original, balanced and flavoursome, illustrated by a risotto of poultry and shellfish, rich in seafaring aromas or roast apricots in rosemary served with homemade yoghurt ice cream. Good value for money.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3339939945	Mantesino	8 rue Maury	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://mantesino.fr	Nessun premio	Italian, Campanian	4.0	€	t	t	The Naples-born chef, who used to be an engineer, has enthusiastically donned an apron (mantesino in Italian) and opened this small bistro in a street near the Église Saint-Aubin. He gives pride of place to his roots by tapping into the culinary traditions of Southern Italy, from Campania to Puglia. A far cry from stereotypical Italian fare, his no-nonsense bistro cuisine wins diners over by drawing solely on flavoursome, meticulously selected ingredients: mortadella from Bologna, hazelnuts from Piedmont, Ibaïama pork, as well as meat from Aveyron and vegetables from local growers. Uplifting!	dinusauru	\N	\N
3331068382	Acte 2 Yannick Delpech	1 rue Paneboeuf	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://yannickdelpech-acte2.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Yannick Delpech, previously chef of L'Amphitryon, returns to the stage for a second act with this atypical and charming restaurant. In a former sawmill, he combines fine dining with the bohemian spirit of a table d'hôtes. Soaking up an atmosphere created by music and a video projection, some 15 diners per seating are served a surprise set menu. Readable and indulgent, this authentic cuisine enhanced with robust-flavoured sauces and jus (the chef's trademark) never fails to make an impression: octopus cooked in red wine daube-style and married with lamb shoulder confit^ red mullet with bottarga butter^ offal toast^ beef cheek slowly simmered with braised leeks and slices of grilled rib steak… the names speak volumes! All the wines on the menu are organic and natural.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3337413596	Zum Loejelgucker	17 rue Principale	France	Traenheim	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://aubergedetraenheim.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian	4.0	€€	f	t	In a wine-growing village at the foot of the Vosges, this 18C Alsace farmhouse has bags of charm: tasty regional dishes, plus some more modern options, dark wood panelling, frescoes and a flower-decked courtyard in summer. Warm, friendly service and a family vibe.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3339216298	Agapes	7 rue de l'Industrie	France	Toulouse		https://www.agapes-toulouse.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This is a small neighbourhood bistro that hasn't been revamped for the purposes of Instagram. A young couple with impressive interstellar careers give free rein to their (delicious) inspiration: vitello tonnato, rocket, capers and meticulously seasoned parmesan^ excellent duck breast, koshihikari rice, Japanese ume plums, and raw and cooked quetsches, with their bittersweet flavours^ and for dessert, a deconstructed Bourdaloue tart that leaves no doubt about pastry chef Arnaud Darbas's credentials. Front of house, cordial, competent Virginie Béziaud has up her sleeve well-chosen wines from small winegrowers served by the glass.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3336042785	Au Pois Gourmand	3 rue Émile-Heybrard	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.pois-gourmand.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Extended and refurbished, the terrace of the Pois Gourmand, which commands a matchless view of the Garonne, offers a rural setting in the heart of town. The food is equally uplifting from semi-cooked duck foie gras in apricots to grilled Mediterranean croaker with fennel and orange confit. Simply delicious.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
