3333528889	Hito	26 rue de la Fonderie	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning	https://www.restauranthito.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Hitoshi Araki's restaurant is near Place des Salins. Working alone in the kitchen, the chef cooks up creative French cuisine enriched with passing references to Japan. His indisputably precise execution, remarkable cooking technique and bold flavours come through in dishes such as melt-in-the-mouth pork belly preserved in its own juices and lightly caramelised on the outside – delicious! The lunch menu is a steal.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3338110714	Le Cénacle	La Cour des Consuls	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.cite-hotels.com/fr/etablissements/restaurant-la-cenacle.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Le Cénacle has a plush, elegant atmosphere (superb 16C sculpted fireplace, a Caravaggio print, exposed beams). The chef takes pride in forging long-lasting partnerships with good regional producers: organic vegetables from Gers, lamb from Béarn, line-caught fish. Inventive cuisine with a Mediterranean flavour, and good value for money at lunchtime.	raduionela	\N	\N
3338085884	Les Sales Gosses	81 rue Riquet	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning	https://www.lessalesgosses.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Les Sales Gosses (naughty kids) chalks up its creative version of heart-warming bistro classics on large blackboards. The food is the work of chef Bruno, who is definitely top of the class! A great meal every time. And if it’s fully booked, there is now a Plan B: Le Bistrot, not far away, on Rue de l'Industrie.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3334437213	Les Têtes d'Ail	6 rue de la Fonderie	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This is the place for wholesome bistronomic fare from southwest France! Market-fresh, flavoursome dishes that keep pace with the seasons, well-selected local produce, excellent value for money (particularly at lunchtime), all of which in a busy shopping high street near Place des Carmes. Invariably packed, which is always a good sign!	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3333191804	Solides	38 rue des Polinaires	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning	https://www.solides.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant opposite the market stands out on account of its fine bistro food, delivered by a chef who is a proponent of short supply chains. It also boasts an excellent (and coherent) natural wine list. In a bohemian atmosphere, sample the house speciality: vol-au-vent with calf sweetbreads, cockerel combs and chicken sauce, as well as terrific cheeses from the region.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3337472913	L'Hippi'curien	62 chemin des Courses	France	Toulouse	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lhippicurien.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	At this small restaurant in an old building with exposed brick and pebble interior walls, diners have two options: excellent value for money at lunchtime or more elaborate cuisine in the evening with the single set menu. The new chef, who has a particular fondness for France's South-West, makes the best seasonal ingredients the focus of his set menus: grilled green asparagus, roast fillet of duckling, bluefin tuna from Saint-Jean-de-Luz etc. Attentive service.	salajakub	\N	\N
3331126597	Mas de Dardagna	1 chemin de Dardagna	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.masdedardagna.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Now, this is simple, well-made fare that does justice to its ingredients (the chef uses short supply chains as much as possible): guinea fowl and black Gascon pork charlotte, artichoke cream, full-bodied gravy and fresh mushrooms. No doubt about it, this typical Toulouse farmhouse is a haven for foodies! On sunny days, make the most of the terrace beneath the wisteria.	basileryan	\N	\N
3334603023	La Baratte	395 rue du Clinquet	France	Tourcoing	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.la-baratte.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	A small brick house in a residential neighbourhood has been home to this family-run eatery for four generations. The stylish, contemporary dining room opens onto a pretty garden and teak decked terrace. The chef impressively crafts enticing dishes, such as sautéed snails in a light frothy garlic and parsley emulsion and a bacon-flavoured cake. The after-dinner marshmallow treats are almost too pretty to eat!	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3336533903	Le Moulin de Trèbes	2 rue du Moulin-de-Trèbes	France	Trèbes	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.lemoulindetrebes.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This old mill is steeped in charm, illustrated by the terrace directly overlooking the Canal du Midi. The food is simple and modern, with a speciality of caramelised calf sweetbreads with sesame and stewed endives. A real pleasure to be sampled with one of the carefully selected local vintages.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3331217817	Le Puy Tilleul	La Borie d'Hélipse	France	Tournemire	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	http://www.laboriedhelipse.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Dominated by the feudal castle of Anjony (15C), the village of Tournemire has preserved its stone houses with stone slab roofs that are so typical of the Cantal region. This establishment, a splendid stone and corten steel complex, blends in perfectly. The contemporary dining space offers a breathtaking view of the sunset. The menu is an ode to marine ingredients. Sprinkled with seaweed and briny condiments, the menu is a meticulous showcase of fish and shellfish, and also takes in skilful surf-turf combinations. For all that, the Cantal terroir has not been overlooked: market gardeners, livestock farmers and local fish farmers are also well represented. An ambitious culinary affair.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3331891095	Le Terminus	21 avenue Gambetta	France	Tournus	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.hotel-terminus-tournus.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	The menu of this former 1900s station buffet features modern cuisine that places freshness above all other virtues! You can have lunch or dinner in the brasserie, in an intimate and cosy room, to enjoy the regional classics that have made the house so successful (pâté en croûte, quenelle de brochet, frogs' legs). There are a few guestrooms on the first floor.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3332513622	Le Quai	20 quai de Verdun	France	Tournus	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lequaitournus.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	On the banks of the Saône, this quayside brasserie boasts a very pleasant terrace right beside the river. In charge of proceedings is chef Valéry Meulien, who was trained by Jean Ducloux and Paul Bocuse, and later earned a Michelin star himself. His dishes focus on the region's classics, including pâté croûte, ham terrine with parsley, calf's head, and sweetbreads with morel cream. The flavoursome red wine sauce sprinkled with chopped parsley that accompanies the œufs en meurette is proof that the chef has by no means lost his touch.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3333801370	Clovis	21 Grande-Rue	France	Tourrettes-sur-Loup	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://clovisgourmand.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In this bistro in the heart of a medieval village, kick off your meal with a drink and nibbles, before sampling the chef’s unusual concept which involves several variations (starter & main course), all of which are based on one main ingredient (vegetable, meat or fish). Warm welcome and small private room.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3332098194	Spelt	6 Grand'Rue	France	Tourrettes-sur-Loup	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	http://www.spelt-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	Here in the historical heart of the fortified town, Raphaël (on savoury dishes) and Marion (desserts) delight diners with full-flavoured and tasty bistronomy creations: cod tempura, broccoli and tartar sauce^ lemon, sablé biscuit, meringue and tequila sorbet. In the evening, they serve a tasting menu that includes spelt risotto with lobster, the house's signature dish.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3333607727	Nobuki	3 rue Buffon	France	Tours	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.nobuki.fr/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€	f	f	A zen and minimalist interior all done out in pale wood sets the scene for traditional, seasonal Japanese cuisine that stands out for its fresh, unusual flavours: assortment of cold starters and tempura of the day, chirashi (traditional dish of raw fish), a hot dish of the day and miso soup. Booking essential.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3332045098	Casse-Cailloux	26 rue Jehan-Fouquet	France	Tours	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurantcassecailloux.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This gourmet bistro, so popular that it is often taken by storm (bookings advisable), is established in a residential neighbourhood near Prébendes garden and flanked by a summer patio. Sincerity depicts the seasonal dishes chalked up on a slate, all of which washed down with delicious Loire wines.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3330635333	La Deuvalière	18 rue de la Monnaie	France	Tours	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://la-deuvaliere-restaurant.metro.rest/?lang=fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Julien and Alexandra have poured every ounce of their enthusiasm into successfully wooing local and visiting gourmets. Their seasonal cuisine is a treasure trove of culinary gems. The charm of their old country house, appointed with bare beams, terracotta tiled floors and a fireplace, together with the odd contemporary detail, further adds to the experience!	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3335016262	La Rissole	51 place du Grand-Marché	France	Tours	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.larissole.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The name of this bistro pays tribute to a great chef of the last century and celebrates the joys of cooking. The concise menu highlights the changing seasons and regional produce (asparagus, snails, freshwater fish). A flair for seasoning makes for simple and tasty food, such as white asparagus mimosa, broccoli and vadouvan. There are only a few tables, so be sure to book!	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3335104946	Les Bartavelles	33 rue Colbert	France	Tours	Air conditioning	https://www.bartavelles.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Devoted to pleasure! First-rate, often local produce: smoked trout from the Moulin des Couvent or Touraine asparagus. Ingredients with crisp, legible flavours, such as rack of roast lamb, cocoa flavouring, roast fennel, potatoes and mushrooms. Chef Ghislain Damaye and his sister Véronique, who tends to the wellbeing of the front of house, pay tribute to the memory of French novelist Marcel Pagnol, in their smart, city centre bistro, courtesy of an ethos that seeks to share their love of good food.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3331730515	O&A	29 place Gaston-Paillhou	France	Tours	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://olivierarlot.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	At this pleasant 21C bistro opposite the Halles de Tours (the city's covered market), good food and relaxation reign supreme. Foodies, take note: there's no fuss or frills, just sincere, precise and generous cuisine (with butter!) that celebrates quality ingredients and authentic flavours. Examples include foie gras ravioli, truffle broth^ seared scallops, watercress cream, a delicious hazelnut butter, lemon-flavoured potatoes^ warm chocolate mousse, fleur de sel cookie chips. The food reflects the personality of chef-patron Olivier Arlot, a real people person who comes to every table to serve a dish or two, spreading good humour and smiles. The extensive wine list makes for rich pickings (including Loire and Burgundy labels).	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3331332096	La Roche Le Roy	55 route de Saint-Avertin	France	Tours	Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://larocheleroy.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	This pretty little manor house on the outskirts of town has recently been refurbished and modernised, all the way from the decoration to the kitchens, the domain of chef Maximilien Bridier. Taking an enthusiastic approach to high-quality ingredients, he presents elegant, precise dishes with no frills. Without fail, the menu features a vegetarian option. There is a fine selection of wines by the glass, and the service is attentive. Sit out on the terrace on warm days.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3330084162	Ty Mad	3 rue Saint-Jean	France	Tréboul	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.hoteltymad.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	t	t	On the heights of Tréboul in a quiet residential district, sample fresh dishes in which market availability and organic produce are much more than a fashionable concept. Dig into a buckwheat pie of aubergines and sheep’s cheese or black Guengat pork rich in local aromas, before making your way down the coastal path to the beach below for a nap! Vegan menu.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3336750146	La Table du Marché	30 rue Saint-André	France	Tréguier	Terrace	https://www.latabledumarche.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	t	The petrol-blue frontage of this restaurant between the River Jaudy and Cathédrale Saint-Tugdual draws the eyes of passers-by. Inside the small rustic-style space, with white roughcast walls, exposed beams and old stonework, an appetising market-fresh menu is served: foie gras marbled with red wine^ roast cod with Coco de Paimpol haricot beans^ financier with pan-fried apricots. The chef, who boasts a great CV, draws on both tradition and bistronomy to concoct dishes that are inspired by regional produce. Wide choice of wines by the glass. The bill won't break the bank.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3330394558	Bistrot de la Place	Le Bourg	France	Trémolat	Terrace	https://www.vieux-logis.com/le-bistrot/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	3.0	€	f	f	In the heart of the village where Chabrol filmed Le Boucher (1970). Old stonework, beams and tasty country cuisine including andouillette and confit de canard.	naldinadia	\N	\N
3331651988	Turbulent	1 rue Durand-Couyère	France	Trouville-sur-Mer	Interesting wine list	http://www.turbulent-trouville.com/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€	t	t	Just off the tourist trail, these premises, once a crêperie, are now the new headquarters of Jarvis Scott. The bad boy chef, previously at the helm of Liquide, flaunted his talents on French TV's Top Chef. There is a rock 'n' roll vibe to this stripped-back, minimalist space: an intimate first room centred on an open kitchen and, upstairs, a communal table seating 10 guests in a more refined atmosphere. Far from the culinary mores of a seaside resort, the chef shakes up diners' expectations with uninhibited pairings that make a statement: frog's legs teamed with merguez, whelks mingling with sauce algérienne. The chef's message is loud and clear: bold flavours delivered without unnecessary frills. The wine list gives pride of place to natural and organic wines. Be sure to book to save disappointment! Love at first bite.	rossidino	\N	\N
3339060917	Claire et Hugo	77 avenue du Général-Galliéni	France	Troyes	Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.claireethugo.fr	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	t	An enthusiastic self-taught young couple runs this restaurant with a subdued decor composed of raw materials. The premises also house a bakery and delicatessen leading onto a lovely terrace and indoor garden (including a citrus tree greenhouse). The ingredients, which are 95% organic, make for healthy, tasty and balanced dishes.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3335075192	Caffè Cosi - La trattoria de Bruno Caironi	5 rue Marie-Pascale-Ragueneau	France	Troyes	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.caffecosi-caironi.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€€	f	f	Of Italian and Mediterranean inspiration, this colourful contemporary trattoria, housed in a former art gallery, overlooks a cobbled courtyard. We fell in love with the risotto with French green peas and different textures of guanciale – to die for! Before leaving, pop into the gourmet grocery store and stock up on first-rate Italian goodies.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3331622843	Le Quai de Champagne	1 bis quai des Comtes-de-Champagne	France	Troyes	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lequaidechampagne.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	On the banks of the Cordé, this 19C mansion, tastefully refurbished in a modern vibe with two large dining rooms whose windows overlook the leafy, tree-lined garden, provides the perfect foil to chef Jean-Paul Braga’s spot-on, seasonal cuisine. Recipes which also feature the occasional nostalgic tribute (braised calf sweetbreads with morels, Rossini tournedos) or even a sprinkling of mouth-watering Portuguese delicacies from the chef’s homeland.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3339656887	Aux Crieurs de Vin	4 place Jean-Jaurès	France	Troyes	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.auxcrieursdevin.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€	t	f	The decor is trendy with bare bricks, polished concrete floors and bistro furniture, as is the concept... Choose a bottle of wine from the cellar, before pairing it with a good, simple dish with a focus on ingredients (artisan produced charcuterie, free - range meat, cheeses from Bordier etc). A tasty and friendly place.	calincolin	\N	\N
3337641442	Côté Sud	3395 route d'Orange	France	Uchaux	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantcotesud.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	You are bound to enjoy your visit to this stone house with a garden and pleasant terrace. The chef whips up intelligent recipes packed with regional tributes. Examples include a 64°C poached egg, mushrooms and foie gras, or a breast of guinea fowl marinated in garden thyme and garnished with sweet potatoes and an olive oil sauce. The wine list focuses on organic and biodynamic wines. Charming service.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3337197453	Le M - Château de Massillan	730 chemin de Massillan	France	Uchaux	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.chateaudemassillan.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	f	This beautiful 16C castle stands in extensive grounds surrounded by vineyards. The food aims to enhance the estate’s organic cottage garden and orchard produce. You can wash down your meal with a biodynamic wine from the Domaine de la Guicharde, which also produces the olive oil used in the kitchen. Slick, smiling service. In summer, take a seat in the courtyard adorned with a fountain, overlooking the garden.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3331459550	Le Temps de Vivre	322 route de Bollène	France	Uchaux	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.letempsdevivre-uchaux.com/	Nessun premio	Provençal	5.0	€€	f	f	This stone-built house, dating back to the 18C but with a contemporary decor, invites you to slow down and enjoy life, especially on its shaded terrace. The chef and his wife have the laws of hospitality down to a T. On the menu: the generosity of Provence, with vegetables grown by the father-in-law, in season^ aioli on Friday lunchtime in summer, and a set menu dedicated to truffles in winter.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3336470236	La Ferme Ilharregui Baita	70 chemin de Apezerreka	France	Urrugne	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://ferme-ilharregui-baita.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This 17C former farmhouse has been tastefully renovated both inside and out and now accommodates a contemporary Basque inn. Three set menus that focus on the Basque terroir set the tone: the first revolves around pulses, the second is based on seafood and the third showcases local ingredients. The colourful dishes taste as good as they look, a case in point being the lamb with Tarbais beans and smoked aubergine caviar.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3330741706	La Galupe	15 le Port	France	Urt	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lagalupe.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Moored on the banks of the Adour, this former bargemen's inn is said to be over three centuries old. It still proudly boasts its spruce white façade with the characteristic red shutters of the Basque Country and an interior with its cachet intact – stone flooring, exposed beams and an open fireplace. Even the original fish counter and the hooks for drying the fish are still present and correct. This restaurant, which for 30 years was run by famous Basque chef Christian Parra, now has Stéphane Besse at the helm. Very local ingredients are the foundation of his fresh, colourful cuisine^ the fishermen, duck and lamb farmers, the baker, the ceramist (who designed the plates) are all from the village.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3330225255	Le Landemer	2 rue des Douanes	France	Urville-Nacqueville	Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.le-landemer.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	This fine stone house with a shale roof has an undeniable charm. Inside, a pleasant young Dutch chef cooks up modern cuisine with a dose of creativity, out of which he devises several courses according to his whims. The ingredients are exclusively from Normandy – not least fish, vegetables, wild herbs and flowers. The dishes are precise and on point, as are the food and drink pairings (the drinks, too, are local). The restaurant has a breathtaking view of the sea and coastline, as do the delightful guestrooms – it would be a shame not to book an overnight stay!	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3332280954	Château du Theil	1 rue du Château-du-Theil	France	Ussel	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.chateaudutheil.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Nothing remains of the ruined château, the site of which has been given a new lease of life thanks to the vision of two childhood friends from the town. Now there are guestrooms, lodges and… a restaurant housed in the timber extension. The chef serves authentic cuisine that is beautifully fresh and packed with flavour: trout ceviche, cucumber aguachile with coriander oil^ pulled pork, seasonal vegetables and jus^ riz au lait (delectable!). They implement a sincerely eco-responsible approach: priority is given to local producers and an aquaponics greenhouse for growing their own vegetables is being developed.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3331754016	La Table du Marensin	115 rue de Castets	France	Uza	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://domaineduza.fr/la-table-du-marensin/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This former foundry, now a delightful restaurant, is set in a picturesque hamlet on the banks of the lake of Uza. The dining room sports workshop-style windows, rust-coloured tiling and comfy armchairs and leads onto a terrace overlooking the lake. The youthful chef, who honed his consummate technique at Auberge du Prieuré in Moirax, delivers creative cuisine based on a single set surprise menu that can be rolled out in different versions: girolle and brown mushroom ravioli in a frothy hazelnut concoction^ veal fillet, raspberry vinegar-flavoured gravy and a harissa of sweet peppers from the Landes.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3338281739	L'Unisens	250 route de Barjac	France	Vagnas	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lunisens.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This modern building just outside the village of Vagnas harks back to traditional Provençal architecture. In its spacious interior, which is done out in a contemporary style and has an open kitchen, sample the cuisine of Tarik Mezri-Charmasson, who ticks all the boxes, remaining true to the seasons and letting the ingredients speak for themselves.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3333396910	Les Lilas	12 rue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	Vagney	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantleslilas.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	In the village at the foot of the Vosges, this large salmon - pink building by the roadside is impossible to miss! Diners are warmly welcomed by Armelle, in the handsome Art deco conservatory, while Lionel, in the kitchens, turns out tasty, contemporary dishes with a sprinkling of creative touches. Pleasant terrace.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3332508450	Le Bateleur	1 place Théodore-Aubanel	France	Vaison-la-Romaine	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-lebateleur.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	A stone's throw from the Roman bridge, at the foot of the medieval town, the chef cooks up market-fresh cuisine. In tune with the seasons, it is often Provençal, and occasionally peppered with Italian or Mexican influences. To be enjoyed on the terrace when the weather is mild. A lovely place to sample dishes that are rich in flavours!	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3335709928	L'Altiplano	Le K2 Chogori	France	Val-d'Isère	Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://lek2chogori.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Peruvian	4.0	€€€€	f	f	We may be in the Alps, but this place fêtes an entirely different mountain range – the Andes! The culinary offering here is inspired by Peruvian history and cuisine: think barbecued specialities, condiments, dishes for sharing etc. Be transported to Peru, without even leaving this chic, intimate and friendly setting.	kralrosa	\N	\N
3339181980	Auberge de la Roche	La Roche	France	Valdeblore	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.laubergedelaroche.com	Nessun premio	Creative, Contemporary	4.0	€€€	t	f	In the heart of the Mercantour National Park, between the valleys of the Tinée River and Vésubie River, a duo with a longing for nature set their sights on this traditional stone-built inn. The calm beauty of the surrounding countryside won them over, as it will you, too. Our hosts serve a single set menu of natural, creative cuisine with a strong vegetable component, as well as local produce (including from their kitchen garden). There is a good selection of natural beers and wines.	landirobert	\N	\N
3333038840	Almacita	51 Grande-Rue	France	Valence	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.chabran.com	Nessun premio	Latin American	5.0	€€	f	f	It can get very hot in Valence! Designed by Louis Chabran, this restaurant, which serves South American cuisine prepared by bona fide Latin-American chefs, is just the ticket. As you might expect, the menu proposes tapas (pimientos, tacos de pollo, croquetas de chorizo) to whet the appetite, followed by sea bass ceviche with roasted apricot, red onion and dill, then octopus accompanied by chimichurri sauce and aubergine caviar infused with coconut milk. Diners delight in the exotic spices and aromas in a laid-back atmosphere that has plenty of soul (which translates to almacita in Spanish).	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3331970957	André	Pic	France	Valence	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://anne-sophie-pic.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	This bistro replete with history celebrates the signature dishes of each generation of the Pic family. These include, most memorably: Jacques's mosaic of red mullet and foie gras, a surf and turf creation as audacious as it is aesthetically pleasing, to which his daughter Anne-Sophie added the bouillabaisse jelly, or the vol au vent filled with crayfish, calf sweetbreads and Nantua sauce.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3333843155	Les Closeaux	Lieu-dit les Closeaux	France	Vallières-les-Grandes	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lescloseaux.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Under the Ancien Régime, Les Closeaux – set in a 10ha estate – was used as a hunting lodge by the kings of France. Nowadays, this farmhouse inn remains as secluded as ever in a bucolic setting surrounded by greenery. The chef, who champions local producers and is a proponent of short supply chains, creates delicious market-fresh cuisine at affordable prices: loin of saithe, green beans, black rice, tomato, parsley and shallot^ apricot and peach puff pastry, apricot ice cream. Lovely terrace.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
