3334826277	TISK	Neckarstraße 12	Germany	Berlin	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.tisk-speisekneipe.de/	Nessun premio	German, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Situated in a quiet side street of Neukölln, TISK (old German for table) calls itself a Speisekneipe (food pub) – and the description works well. It offers a young, urban ambience and modern German cuisine with pepped-up flavours. Options include set menus (e. g. with meatballs or knuckle of lamb) and roast chicken for two people.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3337652246	Loumi	Ritterstraße 2	Germany	Berlin	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.loumi-dining.com/loumi-dining	Nessun premio	International, Asian	4.0	€€€	f	t	Karl-Louis Kömmler, an ambitious chef who also happens to be self-taught, is at work in this small restaurant in Kreuzberg. His style of cooking is pleasingly pared back, cosmopolitan and entirely ingredient-led – and the quality of those ingredients deserves a mention. Choose between the four-course and eight-course set menus – courses include, for instance, a beautiful slice of grilled Challans duck breast from Maison Gérard Burgaud, harmoniously combined with the superb truffle aroma of the sauce Périgourdine and pleasingly firm maitake mushrooms. There are also various speciality upgrades. The wine list, although quite short, comprises a good selection. The team is charming and highly professional, and the chef himself serves and explains the dishes. The minimalist interior is inviting. Seats are split over two levels, with some at the counter, from which there is a view of the open kitchen. Small covered terrace in front of this corner building.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3339685169	Matthias	Kollwitzstraße 87	Germany	Berlin	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.matthiasrestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	International, French	4.0	€€€€	f	f	Set in an attractive building on a corner plot in the Prenzlauer Berg district, this highly inviting restaurant boasting a clean, modern look opened in October 2024. At the helm is a trio of industry professionals with a proven track record: owner Silvio Pfeufer (formerly head chef at einsunternull) presides in the kitchen, co-owner and maître d' Janine Woltaire heads up the friendly service team, which includes experienced sommelier Michael Stiel – the pair were colleagues at another Berlin restaurant, Horváth. There are two set menus (one is vegetarian), each comprising five or six courses. Alternatively, you can order from a range of à la carte options. Diners are presented with a modern, ingredient-led take on traditional French cuisine, a dish of kale, Roscoff onion and black chanterelle being a case in point. The name of this place is a nod to the chef's grandfather, who once had a butcher's shop in this neighbourhood.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3332175171	The Casual	Drakestraße 1	Germany	Berlin	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.so-berlin-das-stue.com/restaurants-bars/the-casual/	Nessun premio	International, Italian	5.0	€€€	t	f	Housed within SO/ Berlin Das Stue hotel, on the edge of the Großer Tiergarten and right next to the Spanish Embassy, The Casual is not to be missed. It also fully lives up to its name, with a modern, elegant and wonderfully cosy decor that creates a relaxed atmosphere and puts diners in mind of an upscale living room. Modern cuisine infused with Italian influences is served in the form of à la carte dishes. Mouth-watering options on the menu include: lightly smoked beef fillet carpaccio with mushrooms, mustard seeds and Parmesan^ classic veal Wiener schnitzel with a potato and cucumber salad, pumpkin seed oil and lingonberries. You can also sip on an aperitif or digestif in the Stue Bar directly adjacent to the restaurant. In fine weather, make a beeline for the quiet, leafy terrace in the inner courtyard – the exclusive access to the zoo (Zoo Berlin) that hotel patrons enjoy is a real highlight of staying here!	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
