3332724306	Roku - Japanese Dining & Wine	Schwerinstraße 34	Germany	Düsseldorf		https://www.restaurant-roku.de/	Nessun premio	Japanese Contemporary	4.0	€€€	f	f	This is the third restaurant to be opened by Yoshizumi Nagaya in the state capital. The atmosphere is trendy, modern and relaxed and dishes range from sushi and sashimi to tempura and Japanese fish and meat dishes. There is a good, predominantly German wine selection to go with the food.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3337779836	Yabase	Klosterstraße 70	Germany	Düsseldorf		http://yabase-ddf.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Asian	5.0	€€€	t	t	Calling all Japanese food aficionados! For an authentic experience, head to this restaurant in the centre of Düsseldorf's Japanese quarter. Behind a rather unassuming exterior an upscale minimalist-style space awaits. The service is friendly and professional. In the kitchen, top-notch fresh ingredients meet expert preparation techniques. The sushi and sashimi offer exceptional value, but more adventurous diners should try the unaju (rice bowl with barbecued eel) or the barbecued tuna head with vinegar for a real explosion of flavour. Complement your meal with some warm sake or Japanese beer. It is rare to get a table on the spur of the moment, so make sure you book in the evening. With a bit of luck, you can dine directly at the counter with its fish display case and watch the chefs at work. Lunch reservations are not possible – diners often queue at the entrance even before opening time.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3338240893	Celia	Gladbacherstraße 15	Germany	Düsseldorf		http://www.celiarestaurant.de	Nessun premio	Mexican	3.0	€€	t	t	For an authentic taste of Mexico in Düsseldorf, head to Celia in the bustling Bilker Kirche area. Rene Brauchle, of Mexican-German heritage and born in Venezuela, and Florentina Assis, a native Chilean, have been sharing their passion for Latin American cuisine here since summer 2024. The joy and enthusiasm of your cordial hosts is palpable, and they clearly love what they do: he is in charge of the kitchen, and she presides front-of-house. Once you have tried his mouthwatering dishes such as the taco pescado, the ceviche or the cochinita, you'll be hooked and eager to return. Fun fact: this friendly, modern restaurant is named after Rene's grandmother, who inspired his love of cooking.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3335133157	Grande Étoile	Bastionstraße 16	Germany	Düsseldorf	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.grande-etoile.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, French	3.0	€€€	t	t	This restaurant in the Carlstadt district is a masterclass in chic: shimmering gold, velvet, striking chandeliers and stylish Art Deco features create a trendy, elegant atmosphere. It serves up flavourful, well-executed dishes from a menu featuring French brasserie classics as well as Italian influences: beef bourguignon, beef tartare, pasta, vitello al limone... Service is professional and friendly. Head there in the evening for the cocktail bar and DJs, who underscore the Parisian club vibe.	longoethan	\N	\N
3339208236	Setzkasten	Berliner Allee 52	Germany	Düsseldorf	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.setzkasten-duesseldorf.de/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, International	4.0	€€€€	f	f	A fine dining restaurant in a supermarket? You can experience this novel culinary concept in the basement of The Crown, one of the largest food markets in Europe. It is not only the location that is worth mentioning: in addition to the smart decor and the partially open kitchen, the dedicated kitchen team turns out creative, modern and pleasingly pared-down dishes made using select produce. Chef Egor Hopp also successfully brings in influences from his Kazakhstan homeland, such as Smetana sauce or raschenka cream. There is a set menu comprising six courses in the evening and four at lunchtime. For a corkage fee, you can also consume wine brought from Zurheide Feine Kost. Top tip: If you really want to see what the kitchen can do, make a reservation at the chef's table. Those who arrive by car can make use of The Crown's multi-storey car park.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3332951266	20° RESTOBAR	Mutter-Ey-Platz 3	Germany	Düsseldorf	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	http://www.20grad.com	Nessun premio	Spanish Contemporary	5.0	€€	t	f	This modern, unpretentious restaurant with a terrace, bar and lovely inner courtyard is located in the centre of town. In a pleasantly lively atmosphere, you can enjoy Spanish-Mediterranean cuisine: in addition to fish, meat, rice and potato dishes, you will of course also find tapas, croquetas and the like. In keeping with the Mediterranean concept, the name refers to the average water temperature around the island of Mallorca.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3331994124	Kronenschlösschen	Rheinallee	Germany	Eltville am Rhein	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.kronenschloesschen.de/	Nessun premio	International, French Contemporary	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Here, diners can sit beneath a stylishly painted historical ceiling or out on the pretty terrace with adjoining garden. The kitchen draws on traditional French cuisine to propose creative dishes in the form of a four- to six-course menu. Plus the wine list is one of the best in Germany. Alternatively, try the bistro. Guests can also stay overnight in the hotel of the same name in cosy, well-appointed guestrooms.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3333616050	Adler Wirtschaft	Hauptstraße 31	Germany	Eltville am Rhein	Terrace	https://www.franzkeller.de/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Established in 1993, Franz Keller's family-run Adler Wirtschaft is an institution in the region. Inside this charming little half-timbered house, the atmosphere is cosy and down-to-earth – traditional tavern culture is still alive and well here. The concept: you choose dishes to make up your own fixed-price menu. There are also mouthwatering steak options. They use pork from Bentheim Black Pied pigs and beef from Charolais and Limousin cows, sourced from their own farm in the Taunus region (Falkenhof). NB: The whole table will be billed together^ credit cards not accepted.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3332999076	Zum Krug	Hauptstraße 34	Germany	Eltville am Rhein	Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.zum-krug-rheingau.de/	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	f	This place has a long history that stretches back to 1720, and the Laufer family has now been at the helm for three generations. Behind the gorgeous historical façade, the cosy dining spaces exude traditional charm. Theregional and international cuisine takes its cue from the seasons, and the menu includes dishes such as a Sauerbraten (marinated pot roast) of organic pasture-fed beef with potato dumplings and cranberries. The friendly and professional waitstaff will be happy to recommend fine Rheingau wines from the estate to accompany your meal. Delightful courtyard terrace. Smart guestrooms – some are especially modern.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3333157522	Die Pfarrwirtschaft	Hauptstraße 2	Germany	Endingen am Kaiserstuhl	Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.merkles-restaurant.de/pfarrwirtschaft/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, International	3.0	€€€	t	t	This is not just Thomas Merkle's second restaurant, but a hotspot in its own right. The tasty food is wonderfully unpretentious and based on very good ingredients. Tip: Try one of the Black Forest beef dishes. The burgers are also very popular. In addition, the restaurant proposes an interesting weekly menu. Your meal here is enhanced by friendly and attentive service, a pleasingly informal vibe and a really modern aesthetic with a rustic edge. Needless to say, guests find themselves drawn to the beautiful garden in summer. In short, a place that fosters a feeling of well-being!	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
