3337230990	Esthiō	7 Dimitrakopoulou	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Balkan	3.0	€€€	t	f	This restaurant, the name of which translates as “eat and treat” in Ancient Greek, occupies a charming neo-Classical building dating back to 1931 close to the heart of the city. Here, Albanian-born chef Elvi Dimitris Zyba curates Balkan-inspired cuisine which offers a fusion between different cultures and combines the traditional with the contemporary. His cooking takes its inspiration from recipes that his mother used to prepare when he was a child to which he adds a more sophisticated and refined touch. Examples include the traditional “Giaourtotavas”, made with lamb sweetbreads, yoghurt and rice, and various seafood-based options, such as the Octopus stew, wrapped in handmade filo pastry with a sublime salmon roe cream. Desserts also have a Balkan touch, such as the Grape juice cream served with grape must cookies.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3333736950	SENSE	5 Dionysiou Areopagitou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.senserestaurants.com	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€€	t	f	Located on the 7th floor of the AthensWas Hotel, SENSE boasts a stunning panoramic terrace with truly spectacular views of the Acropolis at sunset. The cuisine is centred around two tasting menus plus an additional vegetarian option, on which the innovative dishes are a fusion of international cooking and authentic Greek flavours, with plenty of creative detail as an added touch. Many of the aromatic herbs used in the dishes here are grown on the roof terrace.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3334326059	Simul	63 Ipsilantou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning	http://www.simul.gr	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€	f	t	Personality, irreverence, risk, youthfulness, technique and quality are the words that spring to mind when we think of Simul, a restaurant that is always focused on cuisine prepared “in-situ” with the very best seasonal ingredients. In the informal dining room, chef Nikos Thomas (perhaps better known for his appearances on MasterChef) offers his guests a choice between a continually evolving and creative à la carte and an impressive tasting menu.	basileryan	\N	\N
3330539734	VERi TABLE	8 Aggelou Sikelianou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://veritable-bistrot.gr/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	€€€	f	f	A pleasant French-style bistro away from this delightful city’s main tourist haunts but which comes as a pleasant surprise thanks to its cuisine and friendly service. In this informal space, which is nonetheless elegantly decorated in dark tones and bathed in subdued lighting, savour dishes inspired by Provençal cuisine with a Mediterranean touch. True gourmet-lover and chef Aladin Parodi infuses his dishes with superb technical skill, with a focus on top-quality ingredients, as witnessed by the duck à l’orange – an absolute must here. The dining room is overseen by his wife, Christine Parodi, who devotes herself to providing exquisite service as well as managing the enticing wine cellar, featuring an extensive choice of French labels.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3335135996	Le Pavillon	31 Perikleous Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.lepavillon.gr	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	€€€	t	f	(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) As soon as French-born chef Jean-Charles Métayer set eyes on this delightful whitewashed villa he is said to have fallen in love with it and immediately decided to set up a restaurant here. On his menus (one with 9 courses, the other 12), guests can savour contemporary cuisine that constantly interlinks French and Greek culinary influences, as both countries are key components of the chef’s unique career and life. The delicious and unusual “chocolate and mushroom textures” dessert definitely came as a surprise!	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3339897274	Aleria	57 Megalou Alexandrou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.aleria.gr/en	Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	€€€	t	t	Time seems to have stood still in this beautiful restaurant occupying a neo-Classical residence from the mid 1800s, where the delightful patio, contemporary decorative features and 19C spirit come as a pleasant surprise. Here, the focus is on updated Greek cuisine presented in two menus (both with 5- or 6-course options): one entitled Earth & Sea, the other, the vegetarian-based Garden & Nature.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3338922384	Vezené	11 Vrasida Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.vezene.gr	Nessun premio	Grills	3.0	€€€	t	t	If you’re a fan of wood-fired cuisine, we recommend a visit to Vezené (located next to the Evangelismos metro station), a bistro-style restaurant with plenty of elegant decorative touches and an impressive glass porch. The menu is based around traditional Greek cuisine, in which fire plays a key role and via which the majority of the ingredients are prepared, endowing dishes with their unique flavour. It also includes various types of seafood sourced from local producers, as well as aged meats and impressive pastas. At the weekend, the generously portioned Sunday roast is available, which can be enjoyed with all the family, along with the restaurant’s famous signature dessert and a real must: Ari's Deal Closer!	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3339594589	Ovio	4 Apollonos	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.ovio.gr/	Nessun premio	Italian Contemporary	4.0	€€	f	t	Run by celebrity chef Panos Ioannidis, this restaurant is, without doubt, an excellent choice for those exploring the busy streets of central Athens. In this spacious setting, divided into three dining areas (one on the ground floor, a few tables upstairs, plus a pleasant terrace) the chef offers a menu based around Italian cuisine. This includes homemade pastas, such as the delicious Gnocchi with a velvety sauce, diced pear, grated walnuts and finished with gorgonzola in two textures. These are complemented by meat dishes and pizzas cooked in the wood-fired oven, plus an extensive selection of Italian wines and a balcony where guests can savour an array of impressive cocktails.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3332251747	Aneton	3 Navarchou Nikodimou Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.aneton.gr	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Aneton moved from its previous location in Maroussi to this stylish, two-floored restaurant in the heart of the city, bringing with it its vibrant, eye-catching cooking. Lunch is light, with dinner providing the most interesting options, and the seasons lead the way. Service is friendly and engaging.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3335655128	GB Roof Garden	1A Vasileos Georgiou A street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.gbroofgarden.gr	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant that is a little bit special, this could be an excellent option on the 8th floor of the Hotel Grande Bretagne, thanks to its elegant setting and superb picture-postcard views of the Acropolis from both the delightful terrace and dining room. Despite not being overly extensive, the Mediterranean-inspired à la carte focuses specifically on fresh seasonal ingredients, with a special emphasis on Italian cooking, including a small section dedicated to pasta and risotto.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3338956383	Okio	3 Navarhou Nikodimou	Greece	Athens		http://www.okio.gr	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Okio comes with a cool atmosphere and a laid-back vibe^ order a cocktail and settle in to enjoy the experience. The chefs add touches of originality to traditional Mediterranean recipes to create vibrant, interesting dishes which feature some bold Asian flavours^ fish and shellfish feature highly.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3336766570	Dolli's	49 Mitropoleos	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.thedolli.com/fine-dining/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Asian	3.0	€€€	f	t	If the thought of enjoying a pleasant meal with an idyllic view appeals to you, then this could be the place. This restaurant is located on the fifth floor of the luxury The Dolli at Acropolis hotel, a historic mansion that has been completely remodelled and boasts picture-postcard views of the Acropolis. The menu here is a combination of Mediterranean cuisine with Asian options prepared by a chef who conjures up dishes within full view of guests in the dining room. Precise and meticulously presented, his dishes are always based around top-quality seasonal ingredients. The gourmet experience is more extensive in the evening and is complemented by the extensive array of wines, including labels from leading wine estates as well as artisanal vineyards.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
