3334574988	Gallina	49 Markou Mpotsari & 59 Falirou	Greece	Athens	Terrace	https://www.gallina.gr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	A fine-dining restaurant with a focus not just on the quality of the cuisine but also on a genuine connection between art and gastronomy. Here, chef Pavlos Kiriakis combines French and Greek culinary traditions in dishes that showcase fish and seafood in particular. This harmonious experience extends beyond the boundaries of food thanks to the team of mixologists who create sophisticated cocktails, each one of which is named in honour of a mythological character. In addition, the impressive wine list boasts over 800 labels from different countries. In this vibrant ambience, with its elegant marble tables and a completely open-view kitchen, it is possible to sit in front of the latter to watch the chefs in full action. The floor upstairs is available for a more exclusive and intimate dining experience.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3333535215	see|ds	14 Oumplianis	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	http://www.seedsrestaurant.gr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	A restaurant with plenty of personality located in a residential district of the city and which takes its name from the combinations of the word “see” and the initials of young chef Dimos Samouraki to create “Seeds”. The simple, modern cuisine, centred around locally sourced seasonal ingredients and a minimalist aesthetic, is showcased on two tasting menus (Short Talk and Long Story) that show French culinary influence and vary only in their number of courses. In addition, an interesting vegan option is also available. For those who prefer more exclusivity, the floor upstairs has a loft with an elegant dining space for 10 guests, where they can enjoy a more personalised experience seated next to the superb wine cellar.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3339194874	Cafe Bau	Shop 8	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park	https://lubuds.com/cafe-bau-wan-chai	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$	f	t	Cafe Bau, a new dining concept by the self-proclaimed “Demon Chef” Alvin Leung, is styled like a vintage brasserie dripping in retro glam. Sit at the bar and watch the bartender concoct exquisite beverages. On to the food, order the 3-course menu for traditional European fare, or opt for  the 8-course tasting extravaganza for more innovative, adventurous dishes. Local produce like oysters and fish is used to good effect. Service is off-the-cuff and to-the-point.	marinescumario	\N	\N
3331575610	Varoulko Seaside	54 Koumoundourou Coast	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.varoulko.gr	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	t	f	If you’re looking for a restaurant with an authentic maritime flavour, this eatery overlooking the small yet attractive port of Mikrolimano will come as a pleasant surprise. Here, the relaxing ambience is in perfect harmony with superb views of the fishing boats moored out front. Traditionally, Piraeus is known as the port of Athens, hence the plethora of tavernas and restaurants specialising in fish and seafood located here. Varoulko Seaside follows the same influence, although chef Lefteris Lazarou takes his maritime cuisine to another level. The freshest ingredients are key to his cuisine which is based around the catch of the day (sea bass, red mullet, grouper, tuna, shrimp, prawns etc) and presented on an à la carte and two tasting menus.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3338010302	Above & Beyond	28F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotel-icon.com/dining/above-beyond	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$$	t	f	The stylish décor, sweeping harbour views and extensive menu make this restaurant a popular choice for Cantonese dining. The chef puts a new spin on the dim sum tradition by melding imported ingredients with authentic local flavours. Signatures such as steamed Alaskan king crab dumplings, and scallop rice flour rolls with cordyceps flowers are nothing short of ingenious. The set lunch can be ordered individually with a vegan option.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3332123955	Celestial Court	2F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.celestialcourt.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	The astute chef has over 25 years of experience and was brought up in a family who owned a dried seafood business. His shrewd insights on sourcing and preparing those gourmet ingredients are reflected in the menu. The speciality roast whole suckling pig with pearl barley and black truffles needs pre-ordering. Scrambled egg with lobster and caviar is another highlight. The windowless dining room is nicely furnished with rich wood accents.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3331216983	China Tang	Shop 411-413	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://chinatang.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	f	This handsome restaurant was conceived and designed by the late Sir David Tang as a sister to the London branch, and mixes traditional Chinese art with contemporary Western design. Tables are set closely together and there are several private rooms. Dishes from Beijing, Sichuan and Canton feature and dim sum is popular. The chef has introduced a more modern element to the menu.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3332144537	Golden Bauhinia Sang Kee	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.hkcec.com.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	t	f	This space was taken over in 2021 by Sang Kee, a famous Cantonese restaurant with over 40 years of history. In addition to the same specialities from their Wan Chai flagship, the menu here boasts old-time artisan dishes exclusive to this branch. Barbecue chicken liver with pork is hard to find elsewhere^ pan-fried deboned fourfinger threadfin with scallion and sea salt entices with its deep umami. The panoramic harbour views are also delightful.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3331504519	Ho Lee Fook	3-5 Elgin Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.holeefook.com.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	f	t	Walls covered in gilded maneki-neko, mahjong tiles, pop art and red Chinese floral motifs make this a bold, unorthodox spot for a fun night out. The 80s Canto-pop soundtrack is also a proud expression of its local DNA. The open kitchen on ground level is a spectacle to behold and its creative Cantonese cooking harnesses bold distinctive flavours and wok hei. Try the crispy three-yellow chicken with sand ginger dip, and other wok-fries. Check ahead for dishes that need pre-ordering.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3336355469	Lei Garden (Wan Chai)	1F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking	https://leigarden.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	An inventory of restaurants in Wan Chai wouldn’t be complete without a Lei Garden. This branch is bigger than most and boasts a busy, bustling atmosphere, particularly at lunchtime. It follows the group’s tried-and-tested formula of offering an extensive menu with luxurious dishes alongside less elaborate but classic Cantonese specialities. Seafood enthusiasts should consider pre-ordering the Alaskan king crab or Brittany blue lobster.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3330336931	Luk Yu Tea House	24-26 Stanley Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	f	Large numbers of both regulars and tourists come to Luk Yu Tea House for the traditionally prepared and flavoursome dim sum, and its three floors fill up quickly. The animated atmosphere and subtle colonial decoration are appealing but no one really stays too long^ the serving team in white jackets have seen it all before and go about their work with alacrity. Popular dishes are crispy deep fried chicken and fried noodles with sliced beef.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3335278762	She Wong Hei	59 Percival Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	The manager that ran the famous snake soup shop She Wong Yee opened this restaurant on the same street. The classic snake soup is reworked with a slightly altered consistency, alongside fish maw, chicken, hand-sliced pork, dried tangerine peel, wood ear fungus and shiitake mushroom. Of course, you can still order barbecue meats, and glutinous rice to go with the soup. Duck liver sausage with snappy casing is certainly worth trying.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3330930999	Hong Kong Cuisine	1F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.1983hkc.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese Contemporary	3.0	$$$	f	t	This upstairs restaurant was rebranded and remodelled in 2022. Chef Li started cooking professionally in the UK at the age of 16 and his dishes are rooted in Chinese traditions, but underpinned by modern French techniques and novel food combinations. He has an affinity for perfumed oils and the use of fried tofu and pork rind in caramelised sweet and sour Iberico pork is ingenious. His aromatic smoked soy sauce chicken is also unmissable.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3338689195	Chiu Ka Banquet	8F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Chiu Chow	3.0	$$	f	f	The traditionally furnished room, which used to be a private club, now specialises in home-style cooking from Chiuchow. Pork tripe soup with salted mustard greens and peppercorns is creamy and rich. Braised goose in spiced soy marinade impresses with a robust meaty flavour and subtle herbal warmth and the buttery, velvety goose liver is a must. Ask about the catch of the day and consider pre-ordering dried seafood like abalone and fish maw.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
