3339096351	Chesa	1F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.peninsula.com/en/hong-kong/hotel-fine-dining/chesa-swiss-restaurant	Nessun premio	Swiss	3.0	$$$	t	t	Even since opening as a ‘pop-up’ restaurant created by the Swiss-born manager back in 1965, Chesa has been the go-to place in town for those wanting authentic Swiss cuisine. The Alpine chalet-style décor more than compensates for the room’s lack of windows, while the menu covers all bases, offering fondue, raclette and the famous Chemin de Fer wines. You can even specify how strong you want the brandy taste to be in your fondue.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3335911753	The Swiss Chalet	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	Swiss	4.0	$$	f	f	Despite moving next door, the room still retains the same quaint Alpine chalet ambiance with wood furniture and beams set nicely against whitewashed walls. The classic Swiss menu covers a variety of cured meats and sausages, over 20 cheeses, and of course the unmissable fondue made with five cheeses and kirsch, to be paired with their extensive selection of Swiss wines. Thinly sliced veal with white mushrooms in a cream sauce is also worth trying.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3330437758	Ippoh	39 Aberdeen Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.ippoh.com/hongkong.html	Nessun premio	Tempura	5.0	$$$	f	f	Now run by the fifth generation, this family business rooted in Osaka still strictly follows the traditional rules of making tempura. The owner-chef insists on battering and frying every morsel himself without delegating his duty. Seafood is flown in daily from Osaka and Toyosu fish market and they use flavourless safflower oil, so as not to overpower the ingredients’ natural tastes. The sauce is made to a secret recipe. Omakase is the best way to go. Bookings are essential.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3332015333	Mâm Amis	Shop A & B	Hong Kong	Hong Kong		https://mamamishk.com	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	3.0	$$	t	t	The smart wood panelled front contrasts sharply with the distressed walls, vintage lamps and hanging greenery inside. Vietnamese chefs are keen on bringing authentic Vietnamese food to Hong Kong, with chargrilled items and phở among the highlights. Try the chargrilled river prawns that boast bouncy, briny-sweet flesh and exceptional smokiness. Phở comes in generous portions with a flavour-packed soup base.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3330032569	Sếp	19F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.sep-hk.com	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	4.0	$$$	t	t	The executive chef spent seven years working in Vietnam where he fell in love with wood-fired cooking. He was keen to introduce the concept to Hong Kong audience when he returned home. His project Sếp specialises in modern Indochine Vietnamese fare using a wood-fired grill in the open kitchen. Menus with 8 or 10 courses feature must-tries like Hoi An poulet made with dry-aged local three-yellow chicken, and bún bò Huế with premium black angus beef.	berninialex	\N	\N
3331151968	Cuisine Cuisine at The Mira	3F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.themirahotel.com/hong-kong/en/dining/cuisine-cuisine/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$$	f	t	The striking chandelier with hundreds of glowing glass globes is set nicely against the calming green colour scheme and verdant views. Cantonese classics underpinned by solid, traditional techniques are revitalised by creative use of ingredients and modern twists. On top of special dim sum such as crispy frog legs with peppered salt, try also Mrs. Song’s fish soup made with fresh grouper fillet. Wine pairings are thoughtfully matched.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3336351452	One Harbour Road	7-8F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.hongkong.grand.hyattrestaurants.com/restaurants-and-bars/one-harbour-road/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$$	t	t	The split-level room affords sweeping harbour views, while the high ceiling and sound of the fountain exude serenity. Exquisite Cantonese cooking is the name of the game here. Start with the crispy and appetising deep-fried shiitake in osmanthus honey glaze^ for mains, opt for Wuxi-style Boston lobster that is spicy, tangy and sustainably sourced. Some dishes are available in smaller portions. Detailed and thoughtful service adds to the experience.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3335614109	Clarence	25F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.clarencehk.com	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	5.0	$$$	f	f	After working and living in Asia for over a decade, chef Olivier Elzer founded this restaurant that aims to allow new ways of enjoying French cuisine. He minted an original concept known as “Yakifrenchy” – a menu that serves French classics like duck confit, frogs’ legs and escargots on skewers, like Japanese yakitori. Local family table culture is taken to another level with meat and fish cooked whole on the bone, perfect for sharing.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3333034711	Prince and the Peacock	2F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.themagistracyhongkong.com/prince卜-and-the-peacock	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	$$	f	t	Chef Palash Mitra opened this lavish restaurant in a prison and police station-turned arts complex. Fit for royalty, the interior is matched by a menu inspired by the royal kitchens dotted around India. The chef collects lost recipes as he travels, recreating them as sharing plates for Hong Kong audience. Try his nalli gosht biryani – aged basmati with lamb shank and short ribs, plus minty raita to cut through the richness.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3330335823	Wing	29F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://wingrestaurant.hk	Nessun premio	Innovative	3.0	$$$$	t	t	The second venture from owner-chef Vicky Cheng who runs the well-acclaimed Vea upstairs, Wing is named after his Chinese name, meaning eternity. The tasting menu features contemporary Chinese courses made with mostly local ingredients but underpinned by European techniques. He reinterprets classic recipes and familiar flavours with creative twists and playful food combinations. Online reservations open at midnight for up to 28 days ahead.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3333989511	Testina	3F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.testina.hk	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$	f	f	Aptly named after its signature pig’s head dish, Testina is the collaboration between the Milanese trattoria Trippa Milano and a local hospitality group. Championing a nose-to-tail philosophy, the kitchen team serves every part of an animal to great effect. Besides pig’s head, expect to see tripe, bone marrow and veal tongue on the menu. For an authentic taste of Trippa Milano’s cooking, try homemade tagliatelle with duck ragù.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3331399773	Trattoria Felino	Shop 3&4	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.trattoriafelino.com	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	$$	f	f	The chef hails from Naples and his trattoria serves culinary gems from the Italian city, including his grandma's recipes. Start with the carbonara egg, aerated egg yolk with guanciale and pecorino in an eggcup on a bed of corn kernels. Then move on to the house-made pasta, which embodies the ethos of the trattoria. The tagliatelle with Wagyu beef ragout strikes the perfect balance between meaty and tangy. Book well ahead to secure a table.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3336684713	Jing Alley	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://flowerdrum.com.hk	Nessun premio	Sichuan	3.0	$$	f	t	The chef’s modern Sichuanese fare is made with ingredients from around the world: duck blood curd from Chengdu, chillies from Yunnan, pork from Japan, chitterlings from Spain… The signature water-boiled black pearl fish uses a green chilli and pork bone stock that doesn’t look red or oily like traditional ones^ the freshwater fish with springy flesh also adds to the texture and flavour. The chitterlings with mixed chillies are addictively tasty.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3335811014	Ho Kee Dessert (To Kwa Wan)	Shop 111 & 122	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	f	t	The staple in Mong Kok for over 30 years moved to this location in 2020. Rest assured their traditional sweet soups like black sesame paste, and glutinous rice balls in ginger syrup taste as good as ever.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3336023535	Hop Yik Tai	121 Kweilin Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	f	f	The menu at this always busy shop features Hong Kong-style snacks like fish balls, pork skin and braised radish. The hugely popular rice rolls are silky-smooth, with a hint of richness from the lard.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3335631676	Owl's	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Credit cards not accepted	http://www.owlschouxcream.com	Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	t	f	You’ll need to wait as the homemade choux pastries are filled on order with cream and custard of different flavours but, rest assured, the wait is worth it. Check out the occasional limited time offers. Take-out only.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3338028213	Toritama	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.toritama.hk	Nessun premio	Yakitori	4.0	$$	t	f	Tokyo restaurants keep opening branches in Hong Kong and this time it’s all about yakitori. Seats are limited so it’s worth booking ahead and asking for the counter to watch the expert preparation in the kitchen. 40-day-old chickens are used, and 28 different parts of the birds are offered – rare cuts such as sweetbread may need pre-ordering. Pickles made with different produce according to the season make the perfect side dish for the skewers.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3334304446	Farm House	1F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.farmhouse.com.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	f	The aquarium running the entire length of one wall certainly catches the eye. But it’s the traditional dishes painstakingly crafted with quality ingredients and gourmet dried seafood that win the hearts of the regulars. You must try their famous fried chicken wing stuffed with sticky rice. Baked sea whelks stuffed with foie gras, steamed rice with chicken, abalone and dried scallops are also deftly prepared. Friendly, thoughtful service.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3332848181	Tsui Hang Village (Tsim Sha Tsui)	Shop 507	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	http://www.miradining.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	t	A staple of the Tsim Sha Tsui restaurant scene since 1970s, this place is famous for its authentic Cantonese and Shun Tak fare, namely its bestselling honey-glazed char siu pork, braised beef ribs and shredded chicken, alongside some original creations by the head chef, such as fried king prawns in mango sauce topped with caviar. The dim sum is also good. Watching the chefs work their magic through the large window is all part of the experience.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3338696923	Yuè (Causeway Bay)	Shop 1301	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park	https://lubuds.com/yue-times-square-causeway-bay	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	f	t	Having worked in some prestigious kitchens in Japan and Macau for over 40 years, the chef designed a menu of refined Cantonese dishes using top-notch ingredients from around the world, such as Alaskan king crab, Japanese chillies and Taiwanese bird’s-nest fern. The classic sweet and sour pork is given a new spin with aged vinegar and dried plums, plus an option of plant-based ‘meat’. Private rooms in various sizes are perfect for parties.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3334440557	Yuè (Gold Coast)	LG	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.sino-hotels.com/en/hk/gold-coast-hotel	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	f	t	It’s not often one can enjoy Cantonese food surrounded by verdant scenery but here on the ground floor of the Gold Coast hotel that’s exactly what you get as this comfortable restaurant looks out onto a delightful garden. The menu includes both traditional and more contemporary dishes and it’s worth seeking out the chef’s specialities such as barbecued pork and double boiled pork lung soup with almond milk and fish maw, and deep-fried chicken with shrimp paste.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3332477213	Cornerstone	49 Hollywood Road	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace	https://cornerstonehk.net	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$	f	f	Owner-chef Shane Osborn of Arcane fame calls it an ‘Australian café’ – in fact, it feels more like a hip bistro with its faux-industrial décor. The small menu is a tapestry of global culinary cultures, including Aussie, European and Asian favourites. Though it changes a few times each month to keep things fresh, dishes are always competitively priced and loaded with big flavours and pleasing textures. Online reservations only.	beloveva	\N	\N
3337066863	Plaisance by Mauro Colagreco	1F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://plaisancehk.com	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	$$$$	t	f	Mother of pearl finishes, turquoise accents and a whirlpool of metal fish sculptures introduce the ocean theme. Begin the meal with Chef Mauro's grandma's recipe – house-made bread with his favourite olive oil. The seafood-led menu delivers spellbinding dishes that incorporate the best ingredients from around the world alongside local vegetables, all finessed by solid French skills. Ask the sommelier to pick a wine for you.	rossidino	\N	\N
3337218589	Leela	Shop 301-310	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.leela.hk	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	$$$	f	f	The room, furnished in a neoteric Indian style, sports a balcony for pre- or post-prandial drinks. The Indian head chef champions a menu starring specialities from all over India, with contemporary, creative twists. Every course tells a story and diners can truly experience India’s food culture from different perspectives. Try the tandoori dishes from the custom-made oven. With firm yet tender flesh, monkfish imported from France works a treat in the curry.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3330571265	Giando	Shop 1	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.giandorestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	$$	t	t	Italian chef Gianni Caprioli owns several restaurants in Hong Kong but this one, tucked away in a quiet corner between Wan Chai and Admiralty, is his jewel. Besides the booths along one side of the smart dining room, outdoor seating is also prized for an al-fresco Italian feast or just a glass of Italian wine pre- or post-dinner. Expect to see dishes from all over Italy, such as hand-rolled strozzapreti pasta, or Milanese-style veal chop.	benesemily	\N	\N
3336667157	Tuber Umberto Bombana	Shop 113A	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	http://www.octavo.com.hk	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	$$$$	f	f	This dining concept by the eponymous chef is dedicated to his favourite ingredient – the white and black gold of gastronomy^ its name also refers to the genus to which truffles belong. Only one degustation menu is served, combining the best seasonal ingredients from around the world with the prized fungus. Artisanal linguine with jumbo carabinero prawns from Spain stands out in particular, with the tomalley loaded with sweetness and umami.	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3331805893	Carbone	9F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.carbone.com.hk	Nessun premio	Italian-American	5.0	$$$	f	t	A nod to Manhattan’s American-Italian diners circa 1950s, this colourful spot celebrates the era in everything from the floor tiles and chandeliers, to the cutlery and servers’ uniforms. In the same way, the menu embraces classics like pastas and steaks, such as the signature Tasmanian lamb tomahawk. Portion sizes are more American than Italian, enough for a few to share. House-made limoncello makes great apéritifs and digestifs.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3332552576	Juno	GF	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.juno.hk/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	$$	t	t	The mint green façade with brushed brass trimming leads into a bright interior decked in wood, marble and travertine. Hailing from Barcelona, Spain, chef Jordi Vallés Claverol crafts a concise Mediterranean-inspired menu reminiscent of sunny southern Europe. Start your journey with house-made rosemary focaccia, best enjoyed with small sharing plates like charcoal peperonata. The baked Cote d’Azur seabass with crisp skin and juicy flesh is another must.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3331503359	Chuen Kee Seafood (Hoi Pong Street)	53 Hoi Pong Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	$$	f	t	Two family-run restaurants just a few minutes’ walk from each other have been in business since the 80s^ choose the one by the quay for the rooftop terrace and harbour views. A wide array of seafood is available from adjacent fishmongers: cuttlefish, crab, lobster, molluscs, shrimps…Select your meal from the tank and ask the servers the best ways to cook it. Abalone and mantis shrimp in peppered salt are the smash hits not to be missed.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3338480861	Hyde Park Garden	44 Hoi Pong Road Central	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.hydeparkdeli.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	$$	t	t	The owner also sells seafood from the opposite stall so diners can pick from a dazzling selection flown in daily. Ask servers for the best way to cook your meal^ for instance, razor clams are typically stir-fried in chilli black bean sauce, and abalone with ginger and scallion in a claypot. The signature fish soup is simmered for hours with freshwater fish and tofu. Try also the deep-fried eggplant, and tofu skin sweet soup with pearl barley.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
