3336451924	Rutin	Budapesti utca 51	Hungary	Budaörs	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://rutinbudaors.hu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Set in an affluent city suburb, this chic bistro comes with an appealing buzz and smiles all round. The owner cooks but also keeps a watchful eye over proceedings from his open kitchen near the entrance. Concise menus – supplemented by a few specials – come with creative modern touches and vibrant flavours. Their jazz evenings are very popular.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3332793468	Bilanx	Mérleg utca 10	Hungary	Budapest		https://bilanxbudapest.hu/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	€€	t	t	Located in an old townhouse midway between the Széchenyi Chain Bridge and St. Stephen's Basilica, Bilanx takes a fresh, modern approach to dining out. Its interior is sparsely decorated, with varnished wooden chairs set at white-tile-topped tables, while neon light strips create glowing archways above and loud pop music plays. The chef offers a tasting menu which comprises his two loves – Hungarian produce and classical French techniques, so you’ll find dishes like mangalitsa pork with choron sauce and parsley root cream. There’s also an interesting 3 course menu available at lunch.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3332985165	Hoppá! Bistro	Október 6. utca 15	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://hoppabistro.hu	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	f	This contemporary eatery stands out amongst the myriad choices on vibrant Október Street, both for its smooth service and its modern, well-presented cooking – and it's certainly a popular spot. Large blackboards announce the daily specials, which see traditional Hungarian recipes brought up-to-date, and the excellent value lunch menu is always a hit. Local beers and wines complete the picture.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3331877863	KOLLÁZS	Széchenyi István Tér 5	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access	https://www.kollazs.hu/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	€€€	f	t	The Four Seasons Gresham Palace hotel is a beautiful art nouveau building which was constructed in 1906 for the Gresham Life Assurance Company. Set in the heart of Budapest, directly opposite the Széchenyi Chain Bridge, its restaurant makes the perfect place to dine when visiting the city. The relaxed, cosy atmosphere is matched perfectly by a menu of familiar French brasserie classics, with a few Hungarian dishes thrown in. The steak tartare is made at the table, the roast chicken for two is carved in front of you and the rum baba is a hit.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3334144877	Szaletly	Stefánia Utca 93	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://szaletly.hu/	Nessun premio	Hungarian	3.0	€€	t	t	Whether you’re after a drink, a snack or a full meal, this neighbourhood spot is for you if you’re after a laid-back vibe. It’s a spacious place, with a large terrace-cum-garden to boot, but the efficient team cope well with the numbers. Dishes offer a diverse range of influences, but there’s always a Hungarian vein running through their hearts. The tasting menus with matching wines are worth ordering, the gödöllő chicken breast is delicious and, for dessert, it has to be the esterházy. You can even buy a post-dessert ice cream for the way home.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3337476397	Zazie Bistro	Dombóvári utca 28	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://zaziebistro.hu/	Nessun premio	Hungarian	4.0	€€	t	f	Zazie Bistro sits within the tallest skyscraper in Budapest, the MOL Campus, and offers some great views out over the city. It’s a spacious place that incorporates a large open restaurant, a terrace and even a café. The chef brings with him plenty of experience, which shines through in the well-executed, classically inspired, rustic dishes. These could include chilled fruit soups in the summer, or a top-class schnitzel with deliciously creamy potato salad – with the potatoes supplied by the chef’s brother-in-law. There’s also a great value business lunch on offer.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3331031887	Spago by Wolfgang Puck	Váci utca 36	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://spagobudapest.com/	Nessun premio	International	3.0	€€€	f	f	The Matild Palace Hotel – one of a pair of matching belle époque palaces bult by the Archduchess of Austria – is a grand building in a stunning setting beside the Elizabeth Bridge. It’s fitting then, that it’s home to a smart restaurant run by an Austrian Chef. Wolfgang Puck’s fun dining concept brings something a little different to Budapest’s culinary scene, with a selection of appealing, well-executed dishes that draw their inspiration from across the world. From Hungarian buffalo steak tartare and Austrian wiener schnitzel to scallop pad thai and some delicious pastas, everything is here.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3332779606	Umo	Ponty utca 1	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.umorestaurant.hu/	Nessun premio	International, South American	3.0	€€	t	t	Housed within a boutique hotel, Umo comprises two parts: a contemporary brasserie in the atrium, and an enclosed courtyard towards the back of the building. The latter was formerly a monastery and is a wonderful place to sit – it even comes complete with an open kitchen where dishes are cooked over flames and smoke. Menus showcase the best of Latin American flavours, with everything from a baja shrimp cocktail and delicious tacos – the mangalitsa ones are the best – to a selection of fire-cooked meats. A fine range of gins is on offer alongside the in-depth wine list.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3338886742	Alelí	Wekerle Sándor utca 3	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://aleli.hu	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	f	Romance is in the air at this elegant, high-ceilinged restaurant inside the newly opened Dorothea Hotel in the heart of Budapest. Start with a classic cocktail in the chic bar, then move on to Italian favourites, from delicious focaccias and salads dressed at the table to freshly made pizzas, pastas and risottos. The spaghetti cacio e pepe is not to be missed, and the tiramisu is large enough to share. Much of the produce is imported from Italy and the authentic flavours shine through. Service is friendly and professional, with the staff keen to recommend both dishes and wines.	dragomirpippo	\N	\N
3330505784	Nobu Budapest	Erzsébet tér 7-8	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://noburestaurants.com/budapest/home/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	€€€€	t	f	Set within a stylish hotel, this chic, minimalist restaurant features well-spaced wooden tables, Japanese lanterns, fretwork screens and an open kitchen. Authentic imported ingredients feature in a huge array of Japanese dishes. For lunch, choose the Bento box^ for dinner, the Omakase menu.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3336221634	FELIX Kitchen & Bar	Ybl Miklós Tér 9	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://felixbudapest.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	€€€	t	t	Felix sits behind the breathtaking neo-renaissance façade of the former Várkert Kiosk, in a building which once pumped water to the Royal Palace. It’s a plush place, with a stunningly restored ceiling and an air-conditioned terrace. The luxurious menu sees caviar sitting alongside signature dishes and grills.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3336518651	Cut & Barrel	Pacsirtamező Utca 41	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://cutandbarrel.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Latin American	5.0	€€€	t	t	Set away from the city centre in the old Goldberger textile factory, this lovely warehouse conversion comprises a wine shop, an impressive bar, a large dining room with a terrace and a smaller anteroom offering counter dining. The stunning shop comes complete with an incredible selection of wines from around the country – including from the owner’s vineyard (Haraszthy Wines in Etyek) – as well as a Harley Davidson, a Porsche and a Rolls Royce. The food has a strong Latin American base but it’s their own charcuterie and succulent steaks from the Josper grill that lead the way.	basileryan	\N	\N
3339003226	Hosszú Tányér	Fő utca 162	Hungary	Hosszúhetény	Air conditioning	https://hosszutanyer.hu	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Hungarian	5.0	€€	t	t	This pretty little restaurant sits in an attractive courtyard setting and is keenly run by its hands-on owners and their friendly team. Inside it’s cool and modern, with fresh flowers on the tables, and open fires feature both inside and out on the terrace. The menu is concise but provides plenty of appeal and the modern Hungarian dishes are full of bold, hearty flavours. A short, all-Hungarian wine list completes the picture.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3333829879	Arany Kaviár	Ostrom utca 19	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://aranykaviar.hu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	f	French and Russian influences guide the cooking here, with dishes ranging from the simple to the ambitious. Sit in the opulent, richly appointed dining room or the more modern extension which opens out onto the garden to sample the Chef’s Menu – or book the Chef’s Table to sample the more creative World Table Menu instead. Hungarian and Siberian caviar is a speciality, with plenty of options to choose from and two caviar tasting experiences are available to kick off your meal.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3331552264	Costes Downtown	Vigyázó Ferenc utca 5	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://costesdowntown.hu	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	f	f	Set on the ground floor of the Prestige Hotel, this strikingly decorated restaurant brings nature inside with its living wall and ceiling. Ask for one of the booths or sit at the chef’s table for a view of the kitchen. Set tasting menus offer modern interpretations of Hungarian favourites, with some ambitious flavour combinations and the occasional Asian influence.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3331246552	FLAVA	Október 6. utca. 26	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://flava.hu/en/home/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	On the ground floor of the Verno House hotel sits this bustling city hotspot, where elegantly dressed guests fill the room. Grab a seat on the charming street-side terrace and let the slick team guide you through the globally inspired menu where Hungarian, Japanese, Latin American and Middle Eastern influences collide. The contemporary cooking is full of flavour^ the steaks and racks of lamb are real draws – as are their smoking cocktails – and be sure to save room for the nougat babka.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3339578735	Mák	Vigyázó Ferenc utca 4	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://mak.hu	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Rustic charm abounds at this laid-back restaurant, from the décor to the vaulted brick ceiling. Seasonality is key here and Chef János takes time to visit his small, artisan suppliers personally. His travels inform the interesting set menu (go for the longer version), with vegetables treated as reverently as meat and fish, and curing, pickling and ageing all playing their part. Knowledgably prepared, consummately seasoned dishes have a delicate touch and could include grey catfish with buckwheat or duck with celery and pine. The unobtrusive, expertly paced service is spot-on too.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3331683202	Onyx Mühely	Vörösmarty tér 7-8	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://onyxmuhely.hu/en	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	t	The rebirth of Onyx is underway… starting with Onxy Mühely, a 16-seater test kitchen which offers dishes that will go on to form the core of the menu at the new Onyx. All guests arrive at the same time for drinks and nibbles, before being shown through to an elegant ‘workshop’ with a beautiful open kitchen and a glass-enclosed, galleried library. Diners are also invited to be critics and are encouraged to talk to the chefs and leave written feedback on the menu. Sustainability is a focus of the refined dishes, and the whole experience is interactive and engaging.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3330021498	St. Andrea	Bajcsy-Zsilinszky útca 78	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://standrearestaurant.hu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	f	t	This stylish bar-cum-restaurant with wine-themed décor is owned by a small boutique winery and the creative dishes are designed to match their wines – some of which aren’t sold anywhere else in the world! The evening sees an à la carte which appeals to all, while during the day there’s a great value set lunch menu that’s a hit with the local business community. Dishes are refined and well-presented, with a mix of local and international flavours. You might find beetroot with blueberries, rosehip and cheese^ mangalitsa tenderloin with letcho^ or duo of duck with carrot, orange and vanilla.	benesemily	\N	\N
3330084755	Tati	Dohány utca 58-62	Hungary	Budapest	Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://tatibudapest.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	The owners of this restaurant in the up-and-coming District 7 also have a farm on the outskirts of the city where they grow their own fruit and veg. Menus comprise a mix of meat, fish and plant-based creations, with a natural feel to both the appearance and flavour of the dishes. The use of traditional Hungarian recipes results in hearty, wholesome cooking on the dinner menu, while lunch takes on more of a 'brunch' style. The accompanying natural, bio and organic wines come from vineyards in close proximity to the city.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3335773432	Textúra	Sas utca 6	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://texturaetterem.hu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Set almost opposite its sister restaurant, Borkonyha Winekitchen, is this stylish, design-led brasserie with a relaxed atmosphere, a living wall of moss and a central wooden ‘tree’. Seasonally led dishes are ambitious and creative, and there are some real gems from Hungary on the wine list.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3338239132	VIRTU	MOL Campus	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	http://www.virturestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	Located on the 28th floor of the tallest building in Budapest, the MOL Campus, VIRTU affords stunning views out over this historic city and the River Danube. Start with cocktails in the smart bar, then head through to the spacious, two-roomed restaurant. The menu offers something for everyone, with a pleasing mix of modern and classical dishes. If it’s available, the catfish with river prawns is delicious, as is the mangalitsa chop with fresh pickles. A fine selection of wines and professional service from a caring team complete the picture.	paganialex	\N	\N
3331836694	White Salon	Erzsébet krt. 9	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.anantara.com/en/new-york-palace-budapest/dining/white-salon	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	f	t	The New York Palace Hotel provides baroque splendour in spades and its New York Café is the most photographed dining space in Budapest. However, above it, on a mezzanine level, hides this lesser-known jewel, where an enthusiastic team deliver refined dishes which take inspiration from the former Austro-Hungarian empire. Rich, hearty flavours are balanced by occasional international notes, which adds a welcome freshness to proceedings. The duck confit is not to be missed and it’s always worth considering the set menus. If you’re lucky, there may even be a string quartet playing.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3338222053	Brút	Radisson Blu 1919 Hotel	Iceland	Reykjavík	Brunch	https://brut.is	Nessun premio	Contemporary, Seafood	4.0	€€€	t	t	Seafood lovers will feel right at home at this celebration of wonderful fish and shellfish. The likes of marinated scallops and Icelandic whelks join a roll call of prime quality fish, cooked well by an able kitchen in pleasingly uncomplicated dishes that let the central ingredient shine. Stone floors, upholstered benches and open pipework give the dining room a simple, casual feel – and this is accompanied by a lively atmosphere.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3339835980	Zincenco Kitchen	Bihari Janos utca 20	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning	https://zincencokitchen.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€€	t	t	Offering something a little different, this restaurant is located within a residential apartment, but there’s certainly nothing amateurish or domestic about it^ it's even licensed. There are six tables – for a maximum of 14 diners – and all guests are asked to arrive at 7pm, which helps contribute to the supper party atmosphere. You ring doorbell 31 and are greeted by your hosts Zaida Inez Kiss and Igor Zincenco, who go on to fully explain each well-balanced, satisfying dish which features on the modern menu inspired by Hungarian classics.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3336271370	MoszkvaTéЯ Bisztró	Monastery Boutique Hotel	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning	https://www.moszkvaterbisztro.hu/hu	Nessun premio	Russian	4.0	€€	t	t	The younger sibling of Arany Kaviár sits on the ground floor of a characterful hotel that was once a monastery. The cuisine here, too, has a Russian theme, with plenty of favourites such as chicken Kiev and some delicious pelmeni (dumplings). The young team are bright and friendly, and a concise list of Hungarian wines completes the picture.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3332446984	Fricska 2.0	Dob utca 56-58	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning	http://www.fricska2.hu/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	When Fricska was reborn as Fricska 2.0, it took on something of a speakeasy vibe. Its unassuming exterior gives nothing away, but downstairs you’ll find a bright and trendy bar-cum-restaurant with a contemporary bistro feel. The food is a perfect match, with traditional dishes lightened and modernised to take on an appealingly fresh style. The lunch menu is a steal and the chocolate soufflé is a sure-fire hit. Service is smooth and attentive, and the friendly team will happily guide you through the fully Hungarian wine list.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3336609478	Stand25 Bisztró	Atilla útca 10	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://stand25.hu/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	There’s always a contented buzz to this neighbourhood bistro on the Buda side of the Danube. It’s owned by the same team as Stand, so their ethos around quality is the same, and you’ll be looked after by a slick team. Cooking focuses on Hungarian classics with a Mediterranean edge and, while dishes are hearty with robust flavours, they also have a refined edge.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3333062646	Csopaki Resti by Laurel	Kossuth utca 1	Hungary	Csopak	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://laurelbudapest.hu/csopaki-resti/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	There’s no denying that a meal at Csopaki Resti by Laurel provides something a little different: this tiny restaurant comprises just 10 seats and sits within the old village railway station. Little sister to Laurel in Budapest, its multi-course set menu follows the same ethos, with dishes taking on a modern edge while still keeping traditional Hungarian flavours to the fore. Because of its compact size, every diner can watch the chefs preparing the dishes in the on-view kitchen, but the four counter seats are undeniably the best place to be. Wherever you sit, the chefs will serve you personally.	ozmax	\N	\N
3335889987	Víg Molnár Csárda	Kőkorsó utca 1	Hungary	Csopak	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.vigmolnarcsarda.hu/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This traditional-looking tavern comes with plenty of character and is certainly a hit with the locals. There’s a rustic, slightly Mediterranean feel to the décor, which works well with its location near the lake, but the best place to sit is on the large terrace beside the working water wheel. Fairly priced, hearty Hungarian classics are the order of the day, with the meat-stuffed pancakes a speciality. Children have their own menu too, and you’ll be well looked after by the friendly owners and their team. It’s a place for every occasion, so can get very busy at peak times.	florescumelissa	\N	\N
