3334574179	Delahunt	39 Camden Street Lower	Ireland	Dublin City	Wheelchair access	https://delahunt.ie	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	f	Delahunt must surely be one of the most charming and characterful restaurants in Dublin. Exuding a sense of history throughout its quirky interiors, this old Victorian grocer's shop is mentioned in James Joyce’s ‘Ulysses’, and what was once the clerk’s snug is now a glass-enclosed private dining room. The cooking itself is a showcase for Irish produce, such as fine lamb from The Comeragh Mountains served with a punchy black olive ketchup. As the evening draws to a close, retire to the 'Sitting Room' for a digestif.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
