3336392946	Nikuryori Shibuya	193-1 Nishikodocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Beef	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Chef has been in the wagyu business for over half a century. He does not favour any particular region, prizing quality over brand. The menu starts with items that take full advantage of the freshness of their ingredients, such as tongue and heart. Parboiled tripe is followed by Yanagawa-style sirloin. It’s omakase, but customers can add items from the menu. The old-fashioned townhouse seems the perfect ambience for immersing in the world of wagyu. The banter between the kitchen craftsman father and the amiable hostess daughter is heartwarming.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3335132710	Yassan	347 Giommachi Kitagawa	Japan	Kyoto	Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Beef	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	This restaurant is currently operating in a temporary location for renovation. Address: 271-2-5 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto.Yassan is a meat kappo of long renown. The shop is busy night after night, filling up as soon as the shop curtain is posted outside. Staff use German as a sort of code, calling tongue ‘Zunge’, heart ‘Herz’, stomach ‘Magen’ and so on. The practice began at a time when many of its regulars were German physicians. ‘Yassan’ is an affectionate contraction of the restaurant’s original owner-chef’s name, ‘Yasuo-san’. Calabashes hang from the rafters around the counter, recalling that Yasuo-san liked sake in these gourds.	landirobert	\N	\N
3338192050	Hachiraku	428-5 Kamibentencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥	t	f	‘Urban Chinese’ that uses no garlic or lard. The starting point for Hachiraku is the spirit of graceful service as only the ancient capital can offer, so these ingredients are banned to prevent odours from transferring to the kimono of gentlemen, geishas and maikos. The chef applies the richness of top-grade soup stock to his cuisine to good effect. Stir-fries are paired with wasabi, fried rice with Kyoto pickled vegetables. Spice use is restrained, as befits the urbane refinement of Kyoto.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3339163392	hakubi	481-1 Kiyoicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Chinese cuisine with a modern interpretation. Lifting a page from the lavish entertainment of the imperial court, hakubi populates its prix fixe menus with multiple courses of small dishes. Rice vermicelli paired with caviar and chicken wing tips wrapped in foie gras signify cuisine unafraid of incorporating Western elements. Dressings of chilli sauce and mayonnaise for shrimp set up an interesting taste comparison. A whimsical spirit pervades the fare, setting the heart racing.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3333625932	Hirosawa	183 Fudocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Creative Chinese cuisine with the ambience of a Japanese villa. The cheerful sound of woks being tossed around reverberates in the interior. Fearful of wearing out guests’ tastebuds, the chef seasons with a light touch, drawing on his experience in Cantonese cooking. Oven-roasted pork fillet is a case in point. Ingredients suffused with premium shang tang Chinese soup stock to create soups and ankake served in hot clay pots are a Hirosawa trademark. The restaurant is a forum for his self-expression, so the chef named it after himself.	calincolin	\N	\N
3332491283	Kyochuka Makisada	565-5 Kawaracho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The brothers who run Kyochuka Makisada are following in the footsteps of their father, who was a chef at a Chinese restaurant. The sign beside the shop curtain was written by their father, a gift to celebrate their start of a new life. The “sada” part is common to both brothers’ names. The elder brother runs the kitchen, while the younger brother handles service. The counter is the place to sit to watch the spectacle of dishes being prepared, such as sizzling Peking duck. The brothers’ passion is driven by the family tie that binds them.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3331960791	COPPIE	367 Takatsuji Inokumacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list		Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	¥¥	f	f	The aproned staff greet arriving guests as if welcoming friends into their home. The nostalgic interior of this old Japanese-style house oozes serenity. The concept is fare that complements sake and wine. The chef, not binding himself to any genre, serves up an imaginative medley of Japanese, Chinese, Western and ethnic influences. Using fermentation to impart flavour and tartness is the chef’s forte. Enjoy pairing innovative cuisine with compatible sakes.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3331729233	Kyoen	570-118 Giommachi Minamigawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Japanese and Italian cuisine in two-part harmony. Prix fixe menus incorporating both styles are the focus, with unique twists thrown in. Soups are mostly traditional Japanese in style, pasta flavours true to Italian roots. To wrap up the meal, rice as well as beef cutlet or curry are served, ensuring a satisfying finish. Appropriately for a menu of Japanese and Western fare, both sake and wine are on offer. A banquet that leaves nothing to be desired.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3331535628	middle	5-3 Shimogamo Kamigawaracho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://middle.co.jp/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The Kamo River provides a serene backdrop to this house near Kitaoji Bridge. Inspired to become a chef in Paris, the chef studied French cooking in Osaka and Japanese cuisine in Kyoto. This life story is evident in his prix fixe menus, which blur the boundaries between Western and Japanese gastronomy. Sauces are lovingly prepared, fish and meat grilled over charcoal flame. The style is freely expressive, with hints of Middle Eastern and South American influences scattered here and there.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3337245040	Raiz	21-4 Murasakino Kamimonzencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://raiz-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The cuisine inherits a modern Spanish pedigree. The message is the delicious flavour of freshly picked vegetables. Raiz partners with local farmers to deliver the aroma and vibrancy of freshly harvested produce. Dishes are arranged with a simple, modern sensibility that puts the ingredients in the spotlight. The restaurant’s name means ‘roots’ in Spanish, and it is putting down roots in the Murasakino region and showcasing the appeal of the area’s produce.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
3339414771	TOKI	1F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelthemitsui.com/kyoto/restaurants-bar/toki/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Food born of experience with French cuisine and the famous waters of Kyoto. The chef has always prized soup stock and makes it a centrepiece of his work. As if to symbolise Kyoto, the ‘city of waters’, the prix fixe starts with hot water drawn from a spring. Even the amuse-bouche follows the soup-stock theme. Foie gras with Tango sake lees fuses Japanese and French culture^ local ingredients are served on Kyoyaki vessels. Feel the mood of the seasons in the ancient capital through the cuisine of TOKI.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3336828982	shiro	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://ido-kyoto.com/shiro/	Nessun premio	Contemporary, Italian	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The colour scheme speaks of immaculate purity. The white interior is refreshing^ the blank spaces left in the arrangements bring clarity of focus. Eager to share the attractions of his hometown with the world, the chef largely gets his ingredients from Hamada, Shimane Prefecture. Seafood arrives from former classmates^ fruit from farmers for his desserts. The style is Italian-based cuisine made with Japanese foodstuffs, bringing the delicious taste of quality ingredients to the fore.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3331824468	Kamoryori Tabuchi	33 Marutacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kamo-tabuchi.com/	Nessun premio	Duck Specialities	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Kamo-ryori means ‘duck specialities’ and that is what this niche restaurant delivers. The shop buys ducks whole, so it can serve a wide variety of cuts. The meal starts with items such as gizzard and liver. Tenderloin is pressed between two sheets of kombu kelp^ sirloin is smoked over charcoal, the fat melted into soup stock to heighten flavour. Nothing is wasted—a variety of techniques are applied to get the most out of every duck. The chopstick rests in the shape of a duck are charming.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3333223224	Benoit	The Hotel Seiryu Kyoto Kiyomizu	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.benoit-kyoto.com/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Benoit opened as a bistro in Paris in 1912. Later Alain Ducasse took over the reins and brought the spirit of ‘good old Benoit’ to Kyoto. The fare consists of familiar favourites such as pâté en croûte, duck confit and millefeuille. Though the walls are glass, the roof is tiled for a touch of Kyoto style and the dining room has a certain Parisian charm. Along with its views of Yasaka Pagoda, it creates a pleasing blend of French and Japanese in the ancient capital.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3336525329	L'aparté	247-3 Nishiwakamatsucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://laparte.net/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	L’aparté serves modern French cuisine by Anthony Bâcle, who has travelled the world. Using Japanese ingredients and French methods, Bâcle conjures an eclectic blend of both cuisines, creating harmony with numerous ingredients such as bean-curd skin, miso and nori seaweed. The XO soy sauce reflects his experience in Macao just as the Manhattan Cheesecake reflects his in New York., Loire wines are stocked in homage to his native region.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3337281570	le 14e	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	French	5.0	¥¥	f	t	There is a restaurant famous for its meat dishes in Paris’ 14th arrondissement. The chef says that when he tasted its beef, its flavour impressed him so much that he decided to work there. He sources lean, flavoursome wagyu and beef from cows that have calved^ seasonings are sparse, consisting of salt and pepper only. To lock in the flavour, the meat is pan-fried in copious oil, almost deep-fried. Food producers’ signs hang on the walls. Savour a simple deliciousness with a glass of organic red wine in one hand.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3336625016	Le cadeau	541-25 Suemarucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://www.le-cadeau2019.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Shinji Imoto apprenticed in Italian cuisine, but his desire to study sauces led him to French cooking. Fascinated by its depth and subtlety, Chef Imoto soon switched fully to French cuisine. He prizes combinations of familiar fare, such as apples paired with boudin noir sausages, navy beans with bacon, and oysters with spinach. The restaurant’s name means ‘The Gift’, and each dish brings to guests the chef’s devotion to his craft.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3332204377	Luca	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://luca-kyoto.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The restaurant name comes from lucas, ‘bringer of light’ in Latin, out of chef’s desire to make it a place of bright smiles. He strives to create fare based on the classic French cuisine which so impressed him during his apprenticeship, while keeping the flavours light. Food is served colourfully garnished with vegetables of Kyoto in season. The fare is both creative and richly expressive.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3334849261	MOTOÏ	186 Tawarayacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://kyoto-motoi.com/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Housed in a remodeled Taisho-era residence, with a dining room looking out on a courtyard, MOTOÏ is suffused with the atmosphere of Old Japan. Kyoto native Motoi Maeda boasts careers in both Chinese and French cuisine, so he assembles prix fixe menus applying Kyoto customs to Chinese and French techniques. Sichuan-style tofu mousse is a chilled hors d’oeuvre. During seasonal festivals, Motoi cheerfully mixes elements of traditional events into his dishes.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3332209252	Yamaji Yosuke	570-151 Giommachi Minamigawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.yosukeyamaji.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Yamaji Yosuke prizes originality, paying homage to French cuisine while blazing his own trail in gastronomy. Yamaji named his shop after himself to assert that individuality. His apprenticeship in France gave him a precious opportunity to build relationships with chefs from all over the world, learning about the cuisines of Italy, the Middle East, China and more. The squid carbonara recalls a co-creation with a chef in Paris.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3331094235	Jean-Georges at The Shinmonzen	1F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://theshinmonzen.com/jp/	Nessun premio	French, Contemporary	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Contemporary French cuisine that welcomes influences from other culinary cultures. The chef, Jean-Georges Vongerichten, proclaims to the world a borderless cuisine born of his experience living in Asia. Recipes come straight from the flagship restaurant in New York. Spices and herbs accentuate the aroma^ the tartness of citrus brings a light note. In the warmer months when the terrace is open, the tables beside the Shirakawa River, with their views of Kyoto scenery, fill up fast.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3333781715	Etto	47 Daikokuyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://e-tto.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Etto is Italian for ‘intimacy’. It’s hard to tell where the counter ends and the open kitchen begins, so guests and chef become entwined in a single, intimate space. Italian cuisine is accented by Japan’s four seasons. Antipasto misto, served on a Kiyomizu-yaki platter and strewn with leaves of the season, has a hassun sensibility. Five small dishes of salty and sour morsels keep the wine flowing.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3330685246	Germoglio	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.germogliokyoto.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The name is Italian for ‘bud’, expressing the desire to sprout, blossom and grow, restaurant and chef alike. The chef learned his craft in the Piedmont region, so northern Italian techniques are his speciality. Handmade pastas such as tajarin and tagliolini showcase his experience. Garlic is used sparingly so as not to mask the native flavours of ingredients. Vegetables from Ohara and duck from Kameoka are expressions of thanks for the bounty of Kyoto.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3330888959	Komatsu Cucina Italiana	557 Motohyakumambencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.komatsu-cucina-italiana.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The key to owner-chef Shinji Ishida’s recipes is texture. He searches for compatibilities among ingredients to draw out the aromas of each season. His two-course pasta menus are where his creativity shines^ for example, if the first pasta course is dry noodles, the second will be a pasta of different texture, such as hand-made ravioli or gnocchi. Examples of seasonal pairings are firefly squid, bamboo shoots and young pepper leaves with spaghetti in spring, and boar and burdock with ragu or tagliatelle in winter.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3332286600	Mescita Pane e Vino	277 Tenjinyamacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	¥¥	t	t	‘Mescita’ is an old Tuscan word for a bar or tavern. Come here to try the steak of aged beef and organic wine. The chef sources rump, aitchbone and rib roast, which he chargrills in the Florentine style. Seasoning is restricted to salt and pepper and portions start at 200g. Order appetisers to tide you over while the beef is grilled slowly. If you still have room, the pastas are recommended.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3339997494	ortensia	274 Demizucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The chef has gained experience in many parts of Italy, but Sicily remains closest to his heart. Pasta made with dried tuna roe, and ‘matalotta’, a stew of whitefish and vegetables, are traditional flavours. To grow a clientele that drops in casually, ortensia is decorated in a burnt-orange tone, recalling the blood oranges of the Mezzogiorno. Familiar items such as clam sauce pasta and spaghetti peperoncino grace the menu as well.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3331171590	OSTERIA IL CANTO DEL MAGGIO	512-2 Kikuyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	¥¥	f	f	An Italian eatery specialising in the flavours of Tuscan cuisine. The name and menu alike are an heirloom from the chef’s apprentice days. Located in the mountains outside Florence, the restaurant where Takashi Tamura learned his trade did not offer fish dishes, so nor does Tamura. Crostini of chicken liver, pappardelle of duck broth, steak à la Florentine: his dishes convey the flavours of Tuscany in homage to where he trained.	paganialex	\N	\N
3333648737	ristorante DONO	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://dono-kyoto.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The dining room overlooks the torii gate of Heian Shrine. Dono means ‘sharing with others what is given’, encapsulating gratitude for the bounty of nature and the seasons. In Italy, the chef learned the importance of taking pride in the fruits of the good earth, and he delights in tilling his own fields, raising vegetables and gathering edible wild plants in hill and dale. The chef, second son of the owner of Sojiki Nakahigashi, joins his father in protecting the food culture of the Kyoto region and carrying on the spirit of Italy.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3334329786	Zucchero	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	¥¥	t	f	As a seafood wholesaler, Zucchero offers seafood dishes in abundance and having worked in both markets and kappo, the chef has learned the skills of handling fish. The menu changes daily, with an impressive lineup of seafood in season. Dishes are simple, including fare such as carpaccio, fritters and stewed tomatoes. A point of pride is that dishes arrive piping hot. Oven-baked veggies served in the pot and steaming plates of pasta testify to the chef’s passion for his craft.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3337700719	Komedokoro Inamoto	534-1 Yawatacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	4.0	¥¥	t	t	The proprietor loves rice, so he named his establishment ‘Komedokoro’, meaning ‘Place of Rice’. Taste the freshly-cooked white rice and you’ll understand why it’s so famous. Dishes are served on small plates, encouraging you to try a variety. Order the platter of side dishes and you’re sure to eat more than intended. The chef sources seafood and citrus fruits from his native Ehime. Sake and nibbles served at this ‘place of rice’ vary by the day.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3333592172	Nijo Aritsune	694-3 Chojiyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://aritsune.jp/	Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Billing itself as ‘a kappo for grown-ups’, Nijo Aritsune maintains a dignified tenor while offering a broad range of à la carte items. While elaborate dishes are the establishment’s forte, familiar friends such as chargrilled chicken meatballs and croquettes are on offer too. In a fresh take on rice topped with raw egg, only the whites of the eggs are whipped. ‘Aritsune’ means ‘changing so that things will not change’. An evolution of Japanese cuisine through a modern sensibility.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3333405155	Nominokoji Yamagishi	293-1 Shimohakusancho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The chef borrows the good points of both kappo and izakaya places. Typical appetisers, soup dishes, shiizakana (kaiseki drinking snacks) and vegetables are offered along with whatever guests choose from the menu. Choices range widely from Japanese fare such as potato salad with smoked daikon pickles and stir-fried noodles with squid to Chinese items like crispy pork and gyoza dumplings. The name Nominokoji, ‘drinker’s alley’, is a play on Tominokoji, the pub that is this eatery’s parent. Cuisine with a playful spirit, accompanied by delicious spirits.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3338866314	Nonkiya Mune	127-5 Kinuyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥	t	f	In picture-perfect Kyoto style, Nonkiya Mune is tucked away at the end of a long blind alley. As you enter, the friendly owner-chef and his mother greet you. The heart and soul of the menu is fish and shellfish in season. The preparation of the fish as sashimi, grilled, sakamushi or other style is tailored to each type. Friendly service makes this restaurant easy to love, so naturally many of the customers are locals. Enjoy the harmonious atmosphere that enfolds you in this izakaya.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3339594919	Tsuneya Densuke	84 Kannoncho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://tsuneyadensuke.com/	Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The menu runs to over a hundred dishes. The policy of the restaurant is that every guest can eat what they like, in the quantity they like. Being spoilt for choice is part of the fun. The focus is on fish dishes, prepared in an izakaya style. Tilefish is served grilled or deep-fried^ mackerel is marinated and offered as sashimi or roll sushi. À la carte items to accompany sake are a must here, as are beef dishes such as simmered beef with tofu and beef cutlets.A primer on the diversity of Japanese cuisine.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3332659517	AKAI	430-2 Kamibentencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	A red shop curtain hangs at the doorway of a detached house. ‘AKAI’ indicates that a well related to Kūkai, founder of the Shingon sect of Buddhism, is on the property^ owner-chef Hiroki Abe feels a connection, as the shop which his parents ran was named Idoya, ‘well shop’, and good water is a cornerstone of Japanese cuisine. Abe incorporates Western ingredients while abiding by the tenets of kaiseki meals, anticipating an era of growing diversification of food. The chandelier in the Japanese-style room is a modern touch.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3333366648	Aoikonshin Yamada	12-1 Shimogamo Nishihommachi	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.aoikonshinyamada.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The owner-chef makes the extra effort to offer gorgeous presentations of elaborately prepared cuisine. The menu, which begins with a hassun appetiser, conveys a joyous love for the seasons. In sweetfish season, come for the rock garden platter. A clear stream and waterfall are drawn in salt on a black lacquer panel. The sweetfish on the platter is posed as if swimming upstream as mist rises from the spray of the waterfall, recalling the natural beauty of the valleys surrounding Kyoto. The scene imparts cooling thoughts as you dine.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3330019801	Chiso Aida	294 Benzaitencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Drawn by the elegance of Kyoto cuisine, the chef polished his skills in the city’s geisha quarter and keeps creative flourishes to a minimum. In spring he serves simmered bamboo shoots^ in summer, herring with eggplant^ in autumn, pike conger with matsutake mushrooms^ and in winter, steamed fish with grated turnip. Signature dishes of the ancient capital reassure you that you’ve come to the right place. In a pleasant twist, diners can choose the ingredients for takikomi-gohan. Their motto is ‘Continuity is Strength’, capturing their single-minded devotion to culinary excellence.	langalice	\N	\N
3339518981	en	15-2 Higashikujo Nishisannocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	His father was an artist specialising in maki-e, gold and silver decorations on lacquer^ his mother the latest in a long line of tea-ceremony instructors. Overseas, he spread the word about the virtues of shojin-ryori. ‘En’ means ‘swallow’^ the chef named his restaurant for this migratory bird in reference to himself, a man who had lived away from Japan but had come home to Kyoto. The menu is broad in scope and includes some dishes incorporating Western elements. The swallow is said to bring good fortune, and the chef’s personality and the reputation of his cooking bring customers flocking to him.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3331796510	Gion Rakumi	570-206 Giommachi Minamigawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	‘Delicious, fun flavours’ is Gion Rakumi’s motto. The bustling of the amiable young cooks in the kitchen is a pleasing sight. Items are à la carte but no set formula is followed, so there’s no menu. Instead, guests choose ingredients from a wooden box and consult with the chef on preferred ways of preparation. Being a Gion Sasaki-run place, the quality of ingredients is uncompromising. The playfulness of presentation and pub-like joviality make the mood cheerful and lively.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3335920865	Gion Rohan	232 Nijuikkencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	f	t	Gion Rohan runs the gamut from seasonal favourites to creative Japanese cuisine. Potato salad is paired with fermented crucian carp sushi as a drinking snack. Sandwiches of mackerel pickled in vinegar pique the interest. Fish of the day is served salt-grilled or stewed. A good choice is to choose one of the rice dishes in clay pots and supplement it with ginger-fried pork or sukiyaki. Quantities can be adjusted according to taste, so you’ll want to try a range of offerings.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3338393185	Gion Yamagishi	570-154 Giommachi Minamigawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The air of a tea arbour lingers in this kappo. Amid the spare furnishings, the staff take care to provide a comfortable dining experience. In a bid to make Japanese cuisine approachable, in addition to an omakase set meal, à la carte ordering is also available. In the evening, a prix fixe assortment is provided to which à la carte items can be added. At lunch, eager to acquaint guests with its dashi soup stock, the restaurant serves udon using Kujo leek or tofu skin. Appetisers and Kyoto sushi are also included in a welcome addition.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3330781762	Higashiyama Tsukasa	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.higashiyama-tsukasa.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥¥	f	f	Tsukasa Miyashita’s menu is the product of guidance from two mentors. At a ryotei, he learned that cuisine lives and breathes by its ingredients^ at a kappo, that nothing is more important than pleasing the customer. Inspired by these two lessons, Miyashita puts his own unique stamp on Japanese cuisine. Amuse-bouche between meals is a new endeavour, a gruel of vinegared rice. Fresh spring rolls of Japanese ingredients are wrapped in rice paper, adding an extra touch of Japanese sensibility. A dialogue between tradition and avant-garde.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3331518078	Hosun Nagashima	29-1 Nishinokyo Emmachi	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Emmachi is where the chef was born and raised. He turned the family home into a restaurant, pledging to contribute to the town he loves. ‘Hosun’ means ‘a little square’ or ‘the space occupied by my heart’^ the Japanese of old believed that the heart covered about 9 square centimetres, and the chef wants his shop to be a place where the hearts of guests and chef come together. Cuisine is focused on dashi, with harmony between ingredients and broth. The flavour of the seasoned first dashi in soup dishes derives from makombu seaweed. Char-grilled fish is paired with dashi paste.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3331961499	Isoyama	212-3 Nabeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Light streams from a small sign in a Pontocho back alley. Inside the cozy interior popular tunes from the Showa era play, creating a pub atmosphere. The omakase set menu is a series of numerous small plates and bowls. Sushi of vinegared mackerel, simmered octopus and roast duck are products of izakaya training, while soups and char-grilled items bring kappo experience to bear. Grilled fish is paired with shuto (pickled and seasoned fish entrails) and konowata (salted sea cucumber entrails) paste, carefully chosen for their affinity with sake.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3332165389	Jikiba Ono	2-267 Miyagawasuji	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥	f	f	‘Jikiba’ is the name of the region in Amakusa, Kumamoto, where the chef was born. Attesting to the richness of the seas of Kyūshū, seafood is sourced from local waters and from the Bungo Channel. To bring out the goodness, seasoning is minimal. Appetisers, decoratively arranged sashimi and soup dishes are all decided by the chef, out of a determination to impart the flavours of the season. After these, grilled and stewed items can be selected from the menu.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3337390766	Jikon Hiratate	352-1 Shoshoiotabicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The fare here isn’t omakase but it isn’t really à la carte either. Instead, in a trend that seems to be growing, a few de rigueur items are supplemented by dishes of the guest’s choice. We recommend the shiraae (salad dressed with white sesame, miso and tofu) in season. Jikon in the restaurant’s name means ‘live with all your heart in this moment’. This is a restaurant that focuses single-mindedly on cuisine, heart and soul.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3332450778	Kan	430-4 Tawarayacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	This single-character surname, Kan, meaning ‘interval’, refers to the chef as intermediary between cuisine and guest. The menu begins with a fruit salad with mashed tofu dressing, to whet the appetite with the tartness of the fruit. Wagyu red meat is served chargrilled or as deep-fried crumbed fillet^ potato salad is dressed with fried fat and called ‘Kanfu’ (‘Kan-style’). Technique and playfulness are on full display here.	calincolin	\N	\N
3338019227	Kanzan	465-2 Senshojicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Kazuma Yagi learned the spirit of devoted customer service at a succession of high-profile ryotei and ryokan. He thinks about his menus as he visits the fields of Shugakuin Imperial Villa in Kyoto. His vegetable takiawase impart the flavours of the season using the rich aroma of freshly harvested ingredients. The son of an antique store owner in Gion, Yagi also expresses the seasons through the elegant antique vessels on which he presents his dishes. Appetiser platters are served on rafts and baskets made by his own hands. Sincere devotion to details unseen by the eye underpins the cuisine here.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3331662393	Kappo Harada	290 Hokodencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Taught in the ways of old-school Japanese cooking, the owner-chef calls himself ‘a craftsman of the Showa years’. This shows in his honest, no-nonsense fare. Spring bamboo shoots join sea bream roe, simmered separately but served together^ summer pike conger is paired with water shield in soup dishes^ autumn matsutake mushrooms are cooked along with rice^ in winter, enjoy fried dumplings made from Kyoto yam. Indicate your preferences and the chef is happy to make impromptu adjustments. Enjoy à la carte or omakase set meals as the spirit moves you.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3332655813	Kappo Shinatomi	315-4 Shintomicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://shinatomi.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Keen to earn the affection of locals, the chef named his restaurant after the ancient word for this part of Kyoto. Offerings are determined by customers’ à la carte preferences, the chef’s omakase menus, and how he feels that day. The quality of the seafood Kappo Shinatomi sources is top-notch, so we recommend the sashimi assortment. Boiled greens redolent with bonito stock and stewed dishes warm the soul. The meal ends with sweets prepared by the lady of the house. The couple’s personality is stamped on the ambience of this kappo restaurant.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3332613542	Kappo Takohachi	498 Higashigawacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The ambience of mid-20th-century Japan remains along Takoyakushi Street. The cooking is as nostalgic as the shop, both a legacy from the chef’s father. Customers sit shoulder to shoulder while the owner couple work in perfect sync. The intimate space shortens the distance between people, enfolding all present in a harmonious mood. On the menu, only ingredients are listed: sea bream, squid, octopus. Ask the chef for that day’s recommendation—all part of the fun.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3337018233	Kappo Umetsu	347-93 Giommachi Kitagawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Kappo Umetsu offers an extensive list of à la carte dishes, the better to entertain diners. In a show of flexibility, staff cater to guests’ preferred preparation method—grilled, simmered, fried and much more. ‘Umetsu’ is the proprietor’s name, but the inclusion of ume, ‘plum’, is significant, as the shop marinates sour pickled apricots to make apricot soy sauce, which it uses to dress parboiled pike conger and beef cutlets. The proprietress in her apron and the finely coordinated service make you feel at home.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3332512188	Koryori Takaya	165 Nishisakaicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The charm of Koryori Takaya is that it’s a kappo, but with the comfortable familiarity of a neighbourhood eatery. Freshly cooked dishes and smiling conversation put diners in a good mood. For lunch, set meals with a variety of small side dishes are served^ in the evening, the chef displays his talent with omakase, concluding with rice in earthenware pots and accompaniments. A choice of pickled tuna, grilled fish or sukiyaki makes the end of the evening fun.	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3333340179	Kyo Ajiwa	455-2 Nishigomoncho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed	https://lit.link/kyoajiwa	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Amid the teahouses lining the streets of Miyagawacho stands this counter-style restaurant. The chef leavens his traditional kaiseki with an imaginative touch learned from his father. Seasoned broth used in soup dishes is prepared with an emphasis on aroma. One of the pleasures here is the dried bonito flakes, shaved in front of the customer and presented fresh. Parboiled pike conger is dressed with unripe apricot instead of shredded dried apricot for an original twist. The entrance is decorated with the uchiwa fans from geisha and maiko, expressing the charm and brilliant colour of the geisha quarter.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3337741653	Saryo Tesshin	321-2 Shinnyodocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://saryo-tessin.instatry.org/	Nessun premio	Soba	5.0	¥	t	t	The stately ceiling and 8-metre-wide gold-leaf painting stun visitors. The image features three tigers and two rabbits^ creating the effect of watching a stage. Saryo Tesshin stakes its reputation on its creative soba, and indeed the ‘Daigo Soba’ is renowned. The soba is slathered in a snowfall of Parmigiano Reggiano cheese, in imitation of ‘daigo’, an early form of cheese. Bonito soup and olive oil create a conversation between Japanese and Italian. The true pleasure of fusion cuisine.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3336711712	Kyoryori Hachisei	15-2 Chudoji Maedacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://www.hatisei.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Akiyuki Hasegawa learned from his mentor that good cooking comes from sincerity. His devotion to great dining is what sends him to the market every morning to check the ingredients. He constantly tinkers with his menu to ensure that guests can enjoy his fare no matter how many times they come. The appetisers are just as how his mentor prepared them. Meals end with takikomi-gohan (rice cooked together with other ingredients) because he loves its colourful appearance when he lifts the lid.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3330345741	Masaki	15-20 Mibu Bambacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kyoto-masaki.jp/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	As an apprentice, Shunsuke Masaki learned about the kaleidoscope of flavours that could be generated by combining ingredients. Today, Masaki uses those skills to pursue a cuisine all his own. Many dishes in small bowls, are soups of pureed vegetables. Multiple soup stocks, such as basic soup stock, clam stock and chicken stock, are combined to produce richly layered umami. Accompanied by rice, dried fish fry is mainly seasoned with pepper, but shredded dried plum is sometimes used for a twist.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3337565923	Masumasu Masuda	187-1 Hisashicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://masumasumasuda.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The name combines the owner’s surname, Masuda, with an expression meaning ‘more and more’ – it’s a prayer that the restaurant will prosper as family members support one another. The menu skews strongly towards the produce of Tochigi Prefecture, where the chef was born and raised. In addition to seasonal vegetables, the restaurant serves trout raised by a friend of the chef in Nikko as oshizushi, and Tochigi wagyu beef as cutlets. Rice cooked on a hearth is sourced in Tochigi as well. You’ll come to love it ‘more and more’.	salajakub	\N	\N
3330022422	Matakichi	570-120 Giommachi Minamigawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.gion-matayoshi.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	A sister to Gion Matayoshi, here guests can enjoy cuisine in a casual manner. At lunch, an ochazuke (green tea poured over rice) set menu is available, served with several dishes of obanzai, or Kyoto cuisine side-dishes. Evening fare is an omakase^ techniques passed on from the flagship establishment lends brilliance to both soup and grilled dishes. Hassun appetisers loaded with treats such as hijiki seaweed, croquettes and nanbanzuke are served simply. Shaved-ice treats served year-round are a popular sweet – especially loved is the matcha-flavoured shaved ice sweetened with wasanbon syrup.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3333716643	Matsu	21-26 Umezu Onawabacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Always take on challenges – that was the teaching of Toshio Matsuno’s tempura chef father – which is why Matsuno travelled to the USA to broaden his perspective. The experience prompted his recent changing of the family restaurant from tempura only to a general Japanese restaurant. Tilefish fried with its scales still on and served with egg yolk vinaigrette sauce and shaved black truffle on top testifies to his broad-minded approach. The one dish Matsuno never omits is his tempura, in respect for his father. ‘Matsuno cuisine’ is an evergreen that never fades.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3337211152	Miyagawacho Hotta	6-359-4 Miyagawasuji	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The look and feel of Old Kyoto permeates Miyagawacho. The owner-chef, who refined his skills in Gion, is also a qualified sommelier and holds a sake diploma, so he is an expert at pairings. While the set meal respects the basics of Japanese cuisine, the owner-chef adds playful details such as Worcestershire sauce in beef cutlet sandwiches. Shaved ice is served in summer^ cocktails made from fruit benefit from the owner-chef’s bartending experience.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3330676420	Miyawaki	122-1 Shikiamicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥¥	f	f	Japanese decor with Scandinavian chairs creates a harmonious modern Japanese interior. The chef respects the boundaries of Japanese cuisine while overlaying some creative touches. Tsukuri are dressed with salted kombu, enhancing umami. Tofu skin is grated and incorporated into pureed soup, coaxing out its sweetness. Pairing of fish and vegetables with fruit adds a lightness for a modern sensibility. Ingenious, yet true to the native flavours of the ingredients.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3332783929	Nakamitsu	496-2 Sambongi Gochome	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed	https://nakamitsu-kyoto.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The chef is an earnest devotee of everything that makes a restaurant great, thanks to careful study of ingredients, culinary technique and attention to every customer. Recipes are tested over and over to get the flavour just right. Knowing that the taste of dashi soup stock changes over time, the chef patiently rests his stock to draw out the flavour. While known to refer to traditional methods, alternations between new and old are a signature of Nakamitsu’s menus.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3333959289	Niomon MUI	41-1 Shimmarutacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Recalling the words of his mentor, ‘a chef must have a gentle spirit’, the chef devotes himself to his craft. To encourage patrons to trust him, he taught himself to be attentive to their needs and run a customer-first restaurant, in true kappo style. The menu is crammed with items, from reimagined dishes to simple preparations. ‘Mui’ in the shop’s name means ‘no contrivances, everything natural’. It’s fun to leave everything to the master and go with the flow.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3335347491	Nishijin Hashimoto	109 Kanzecho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.nishijin-hashimoto.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	A baseball fanatic since his youth, behind the counter the chef demonstrates the strength of will he developed on the baseball diamond. His favourite expression, then and now, is ikkyu nyukon: pour your heart and soul into every pitch. To broaden his menu, he prepares sushi and soba himself. The famous gomadofu is paired with pureed soup of vegetables in season. The proprietress’ handmade sweets make diners feel welcome and the couple’s genuine desire to make every customer happy is palpable.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3335142157	Oryori Maeshiro	234 Owaricho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	In the Kyoto dialect, ‘monmona-ryori’ means ‘as it is’. As with ‘kinari-ryori’ in Osaka, fussy over-preparation is avoided. The Osaka-apprenticed chef takes to heart the words of his mentor: ‘light, sweet and deep’, and let the ingredients do the talking. Though the custom at a Kyoto kappo is to do the cooking in the back, here the chef displays all his skills for guests to see.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3336123955	Ryo Kawashima	333-2 Nushiyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	As the stage for his culinary performances, Ryo Kawashima refurbished an old row house. Envisaging his eatery as an intimate gathering with a host and guests, he laid it out with no boundary between counter seating and kitchen. Drawing of dashi stock and arrangement of foodstuffs are done directly in front of customers, by Kawashima alone. His concept is to trust intuition while constantly inventing and improving. The restaurant’s name means (roughly) ‘food’ and is homonymous with Kawashima’s given name: Ryo no ryori, ‘Ryo’s cooking’.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3337206773	Ryori Rihaku	9-16 Nishinokyo Nagamotocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	f	f	To prioritise the fun of choosing at this counter-based kappo, the owner-chef focuses on à la carte dishes. Items featuring hamo and sabazushi are classic Kyoto mainstays. But the dishes that combine Japanese and Chinese gastronomy are also intriguing^ it turns out that the owner-chef’s father was a Chinese chef. Offerings include oysters drizzled in heated scallion oil and large shrimp dressed in mayonnaise. The connection between father and son lends the cuisine its distinctive character.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3330978039	Ryoriya Kanemitsu	368 Shijocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The beams of a merchant townhouse frame a soaring atrium with table seating. As conversation sparkles around the tables, the chef focuses squarely on his cooking, showing the respect for ingredients he learned as an apprentice. The chef visits farmers in Takagamine and Kamigamo, feeling the seasons in his bones as he carefully selects his veggies. Seafood is char-grilled and garnished with vegetables. Presentation is simple, yet the chef’s unique stamp on the fare is unmistakable.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3330753919	Ryoriya Otaya	456-2 Temmacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://otaya-kyoto.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥	f	f	A charming kappo on the banks of the Takase River. The chef’s aim is to create a restaurant that he himself would frequent, so let’s peruse the menu and gauge his tastes. His strong points are the inventiveness and patience he pours into his creations, such as salad dressed with heshiko (mackerel pickled in rice-bran paste). A native of Toyama, the chef serves seafood from Toyama Bay. Items such as firefly squid, glass shrimp and buri arrive in season. And don’t forget the regional sakes.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3331835073	SATOWA	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	A counter kappo that suggests a new age in dining. The modern interior imparts a contemporary feel, a nice counterpoint to the reassuring orthodoxy of the cuisine. Use of serving vessels created by young potters springs from a conviction that artists should nurture each other’s growth. ‘SATOWA’ comes from a Sanskrit word with a range of meanings^ the name here is spelled in characters that mean ‘hometown harmony’, reflecting the chef’s desire to have his customers feel the desire to return to the harmony (wa) of their own home.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3335068151	Senda	1038-16 Kamiyagawacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Ryuji Senda’s parents ran an eel restaurant in Fukui. Having helped with the family business from a young age, the path of a chef came naturally to him, and he made his way to Kyoto as his father and elder brother had apprenticed there. At dinner the pièce de resistance is the elegant appetiser. Senda learned from his mentors such points as how to use fresh ingredients in season and the origins and meanings of arrangements. The eel kabayaki, basted with sauce from the family recipe before broiling, is not to be missed.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3337243814	Shuhaku	392 Kinencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	In his early days as a cook, Nobuhisa Yoshida learned a freewheeling approach not beholden to any particular format, so the sensibilities of both French and Japanese cuisine play their parts in his menus. Steamed fish with grated turnip, chub mackerel sushi and rice cooked on a traditional stove called an okudosan (or kamado) are Kyoto to the hilt. French ideas are evidenced in abalone foie gras and black soybean Mont Blanc. This conversation between two food cultures results in an eclectic blend.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3339753014	Sokkon Fujimoto	580-1 Matsumotocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥¥	t	t	Sokkon is a Zen term denoting ‘treasuring the present moment’. By so naming his restaurant, the chef professes his devotion to serving delicious flavours fresh from the kitchen. He devotes himself to the tea ceremony, flower arrangement and calligraphy to hone his aesthetic sense and sensitivity. Annual events in the ancient capital are woven throughout his menu, conveying venerable cultural traditions. Rice is available either seasoned with assorted ingredients or topped, doubling the flavour elements to satisfy stomach and palate. An extensive array of offerings expresses the spirit of graceful service.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3334633845	Sosakukappo Otani	145 Takeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	t	f	The blending of Japanese and Western styles is the appeal of creative kappo cuisine here. With its pivot foot firmly in Japanese gastronomy, the restaurant moves imaginatively to incorporate Western elements. For example, the dashi is based on kombu and katsuo but, influenced by French chefs, mixes in fish fumet, the stock from the bones of white fish. To broaden its culinary range, the restaurant added an oven. Roasts and gratins now widen the scope of Otani’s Japanese cooking.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3331312059	Takehisa	141-1 Kameyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Takehisa prizes old-school techniques above all. Simmered items such as unripe plum simmered in sugar syrup and herring with eggplant are labours of patient love. Ingredients are prepared to bring out their natural flavours: edible wild plants find their way into tempura, sweetfish is salt-grilled, chestnuts brighten takikomi-gohan. In his early years, the chef was surrounded by the blessings of nature^ in tribute to that experience, and to convey the changing seasons, he garnishes his dishes with leaves collected from the mountains.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3333089893	Taketoko	475-10 Ryotonzushicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	t	t	This kappo stands inconspicuously at the end of an alley. Fresh-off-the-grill is the restaurant’s creed, so preparation is kept to a minimum. Natural flavours are presented plainly and honestly: greens are boiled, eel is grilled without seasoning and so on. As an apprentice, his mentor tasked him with making chawanmushi^ when he failed to heat them properly, the mentor banished him to the dishwashing pit for two years. Rebounding from this painful memory, today the chef of Taketoko makes his chawanmushi a point of pride.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3330922202	Takezaki	150 Takeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Seating consists of tatami mats around a sunken kotatsu counter. The intimate space closes the distance with the owner-chef, fostering a welcoming atmosphere. Fare is prepared from few ingredients, the better to draw out the flavour of each. Unusual fish species, indicative of the chef’s curiosity, are crafted as decorative sashimi and grilled items, in a search for novel flavours. All steps, from kitchen preparation to service at the table, are handled matter-of-factly by the chef alone.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3334176697	Takoyakushi Furukawa	300 Ichirenshacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	At the entrance is a branch of an izakaya chain, but walk through it to the back to find the sign and shop curtain for Takoyakushi Furukawa. The meal unfolds from the drawing of dashi stock, ensuring that you experience the beguiling aroma and taste of the basic clear stock. The menu is extensive, presenting the flavours of the season a little at a time. The meal wraps up with a rice dish such as white rice, takikomi-gohan or zosui. No effort is spared in expressing passion and pride in each dish.	langalice	\N	\N
3330977354	Tokuo	151 Tennocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://tokuwo.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	To usher in the next generation in kappo culture, Tokuo goes all in on à la carte items. Blanquillo, a staple of Kyoto cuisine, is served year-round: at times flame-grilled, at others deep-fried or as sakamushi (seasoned with sake and salt, then steamed). Duck meat dumplings, a heritage from the chef’s apprenticeship days, are lovingly prepared in homage to his culinary mentor. Rice enveloped in grated yam and bean curd skin has been devised as a treat that goes down easy in the summer months.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3330121355	Tsujifusa	155 Mukadeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Fusa means ‘linen’ or ‘hemp cloth’, which is used in Shinto rituals to symbolise cleanliness. The word was chosen for the restaurant’s name because, like Japanese cuisine, it developed from an origin as a sacred offering, and indeed the shop curtain hanging at the shop’s entrance is woven of pure linen. As part of his daily duties, the owner-chef prays at Ujiko Shrine and draws pure votive water from there. The proprietress, a qualified sommelier, suggests pairings of sake and wine.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3333012534	Tsuroku	51 Matsuyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The name derives from an old Kyoto word meaning ‘balance’ or ‘harmony’. Simple arrangements and friendly service make for a pleasant experience. The decision to make all menu items à la carte was taken so customers could drop in casually. The head chef excels in wanmono (dishes served in small bowls) using shinjo, as well as fried foods. Guji knife-scored to look pinecone-like and grilled and bowls of white miso soup are standard fare and quintessentially Kyoto.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3334031482	Wakasugi	5 Kinugasa Gaidocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Close to the World Heritage site of Kinkaku-ji Temple, a husband and wife who loved this location opened a counter-style restaurant serving traditional cuisine. Eager to add to the vitality of the region, they aimed to create an eatery where neighbours could gather^ more than a Japanese-style pub, but nothing as fancy as a high-class kappo restaurant. The emphasis is on à la carte items because they want to put their customers’ wishes first. Smoked salmon and herring-roe potato salad is standard fare. Lunch is kaiseki multi-course meal style only, so the couple can chat with customers as they serve them.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3332055532	WASHOKU TOKU	45-1 Murasakino Kamimonzencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.washoku-toku.jp/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	f	t	À la carte is the focus, so guests can freely sample the cuisine of the season. The menu ranges widely, beguiling diners with items from appetisers to more creative offerings. The sashimi plate is garnished with green peppercorns. Refreshing flavours draw out the sweetness of seafood. ‘Kamo Wasa’, quick-boiled duck tenderloin, draws inspiration from the yakitori technique. The wide range of items includes rice dishes, donburi, rice soup and fried rice. The flexibility to make portions larger or smaller is much appreciated.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3331685550	YOKOI	88 Manjujinakanocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed	https://kyo-yokoi.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥¥¥	t	f	Dreaming of following in the footsteps of his sushi chef father, the chef moved to Kyoto to learn the basics of Japanese cuisine. The welcome with a cup of deep-steamed green tea is a tip of the hat to the chef’s Shizuoka roots. Clasping to heart his father’s maxim that ‘cooking is self-expression’, he expresses himself through goma-ae made with freshly roasted, freshly ground sesame. The calligraphy of the restaurant’s name was written by the chef’s mother^ the vessels for sake were crafted by his father.	marinescumario	\N	\N
3338010652	Pontocho Masuda	200 Shimokorikicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Obanzai	4.0	¥¥	f	t	The mood is the Showa era, when Pontocho was a much sleepier place. Two generations, father and son, man the kitchen, displaying their talents in ryotei cooking. ‘Obanzai’, a style of cooking beloved by Kyoto families, exudes the warmth and familiarity of the good old days. Side dishes are simply simmered and unadorned: okara (soy pulp), hijiki (black seaweed), nishin-nasu (Pacific herring with eggplant). Grilled seafood and seasonal stews are popular. ‘Daimyotaki’, dried daikon pickled and simmered in dashi, was born of the wisdom of previous generations.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3333707274	Takocho	1-237 Miyakawasuji	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Oden	3.0	¥¥	t	f	This oden speciality shop has been in business for four generations, since the Meiji period (1880s-90s). The owner-chef in his bow tie and proprietress in her apron greet guests as they enter. Oden is seasoned with light dashi soup stock tinged with kombu kelp. Octopus (the ‘Tako’ in ‘Takocho’ means ‘octopus’), tofu skin and daikon radish are popular items. Ask about items not on the menu and start a conversation. A grilled octopus onigiri rice ball and chazuke in oden soup draws the meal to a close. Dashi drawn from a wide variety of sources adds depth to the flavour.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3336874782	CLIMA	22-1 Shimogamo Umenokicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Spanish	4.0	¥¥	f	f	The restaurant’s name is the Spanish word for climate. Through his work, the chef aims to convey the appeal of the towns he has visited in that country. The dinner menu is filled with dishes from every region of Spain^ Catalan-style salad with salted cod and onions, for example, and Valencia-style paella with rabbit and green beans. The traditional Basque wood-fire-grilled dishes are a speciality. The beef rib roast, grilled uncut, combines the umami of the red meat with the aroma of the smoke.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3331011201	Kikunoi Sushi Ao	463-30 Shimokawaracho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	4.0	¥¥¥¥	t	f	A ‘sushi kappo’ opened by the ryotei Kikunoi. Sushi is Japanese food, after all, so inventive steps are taken to incorporate sushi into the proceedings, interspersing nigiri into the flow of appetisers, sashimi and soup. Treatment of ingredients is unique: for example, Japanese tiger prawn is char-grilled and scorched in the shell, and conger eel is seasoned with black seven-spices and buds of the pepper tree. Another thing you won’t find elsewhere is the ability to choose from serving ware and sake decanters crafted by none other than legendary ceramicist and epicure Rosanjin.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3337474815	Kiyamachi Ran	212-6 Nabeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.sushi-ran.com/	Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	This sushi kappo is run by the third-generation owner-chef, who previously worked at Kitcho, and his mother. From below the ledge, water flows to rinse the fingers, stirring fond memories of Showa-era times. Orders are placed old-style too: patrons choose as they converse with the chef. Among the snacks, a favourite is sashimi of the fatty cut of tuna near the collarbone. Grated daikon is wrapped in fatty tuna to create a clean finish. Pickled nigiri oozes the culture of Kyoto.	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3337961942	Pontocho Sushi Ishiya	210 Nabeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	5.0	¥¥	t	t	This restaurant is tucked away at the end of Lane 24, Pontocho-dori, a narrow alley stretching to the west. It caters to customers’ desires by offering sushi and dishes that can be enjoyed à la carte. Unusually for a sushi restaurant, it serves beef dishes, including char-grilled wagyu beef and rolls of beef and sea urchin. Tuna, served at the perfect time to ensure the flavour is at its best, is a joy. The extensive menu amply fulfils the shop’s role as a counter-style restaurant serving traditional cuisine. Naturally, the omakase (daily changing set menu) set meal is recommended.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3333802124	Shimogamo Ichima	93-1 Shimogamo Nishihangicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The plump little orbs of temari sushi look adorable. The restaurant began when the chef’s grandfather, emulating the fine craftsmanship of saikuzushi, created sushi small enough for geisha and maiko to consume in a single bite. The range is impressive, encompassing sea bream, tuna, shrimp and much more. The chef shapes the temari sushi gently by hand, so the sushi rice delicately breaks apart in the mouth. Picking out the flavours as one eats is part of the enjoyment. In true Kyoto culinary style, mackerel sushi is offered in autumn, with steamed sushi in winter. A comprehensive range of à la carte items is available in the evenings.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3336913214	Hosu	17	Taiwan	Taipei	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Taiwanese contemporary	4.0	$$$	t	t	The rustic chic room is adorned by dried flowers, antiques and cast iron furniture, paying homage to Taiwan’s country life of yesteryear. The owner-chef pledges his love to his homeland on the menu, making reference to the seasonal changes in Taiwan’s mountains, seas, rivers and plains. Dishes pivot around his childhood memories using mostly produce from sustainable sources. Chargrilling techniques are deployed prominently and to great effect.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3330709278	Sushi Kawano	72-8 Shimogamo Higashihangicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	As a young man, Mitsutaka Kawano was a hurdler. Sushi preparation is much like hurdling, he says, as in both cases you try to deliver the best performance in the shortest possible time. Nigiri, a product of countless hours of forming practice, are relatively small, formed from relatively warm vinegared rice of just the right saltiness. The chef’s pet saying is that each day a sushi chef must improve his technique from the day before. In his quest for excellence, Mitsutaka Kawano will never stop hurdling.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3336920729	Gion Senryu	227-3 Nishinocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Tempura	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Service consists of tempura and decoratively arranged sashimi in season, with guests’ favoured tempura items added as desired – the relaxation of leaving the menu to the chef combined with the joy of choosing. The head chef is a vegetable expert, so the list of vegetables is extensive. As with wine pairings, sauces are sometimes chosen to suit particular tempura items. Rice is freshly cooked in an earthenware pot. Tendon (rice topped with tempura) and Tencha (rice served in a tea broth often with tempura) can both be enjoyed a little at a time.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3330863344	Miyagawacho Tensho	4-300-5 Miyagawasuji	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Tempura	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	An omakase feast of tempura and other delights of Japanese cuisine. Guided by his experience at a restaurant with attached inn, the chef starts the meal with sashimi and soup dishes before proceeding to tempura. To bring out their natural aroma, the pieces are lightly battered and deep-fried in pale soy oil. Perennial favourites such as shrimp and whiting are interspersed with creative items like scallops dressed with caviar. Kakiagedon of an all-in-one shrimp and vegetable tempura blend served atop white rice brings down the curtain.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3335397508	Tempura Mizuki	B1F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access	https://mizuki.ritzcarltonkyoto.com/tempura-mizuki	Nessun premio	Tempura	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Ingredients are presented before frying begins: vegetables from Takagamine and Shūgakuin, seafood from Awaji and Shizuoka. Safflower oil is used to achieve a light tempura coating. While some items, such as shrimp and conger eel, are fried on their own, other items are ingeniously paired, such as sesame tofu with sea urchin, wagyu with perilla leaf, and egg yolk with caviar. Gracious hospitality accompanies.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3330608238	Okuniya Mambei	534 Kikuyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only	https://manbei.bubu-unagi.com/	Nessun premio	Unagi / Freshwater Eel	4.0	¥¥	f	f	The chef opened Okuniya Mambei as the third-generation owner-chef of a river-fish restaurant in Nishiki Market. He realised his dream with the help of architects, calligraphers and potters. Décor of rustic simplicity, bold and vigorous calligraphy and tricolour earthenware pots exude a unique personality. The menu consists only of large kabayaki on rice. Eel is grilled with the fat intact and served with rice freshly cooked in an earthenware pot. In true Kyoto style, the leftover rice is topped with eel tsukudani (a preserve using sweetened soy sauce) and hojicha (roasted green tea) is poured over it.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3332221288	Torisho sai	237 Daimonjicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Yakitori	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Both charcoal and wood flames are in this restaurant’s arsenal. These ancient heat sources draw out the deliciousness of the free-range Hinai-jidori chicken. The meat is rested in a curing house, judiciously draining moisture to concentrate the flavour. Service begins with a single skewer of breast meat, the better to showcase the poultry’s delicious taste. The kagoyaki technique, which wreathes the meat in fire and smoke, is an idea borrowed from the yakitori traditions of Miyazaki. Dinner ends with a bowl of ginger rice in chicken broth, cooked over wood flame.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3331690358	Yakitori Kyoto Tachibana	B1F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Yakitori	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Tomonori Sakata turned his attention from Japanese cuisine to yakitori when he fell in love with Kyotamba chicken. Many dishes are served wrapped in skin, because of its tenderness and to bring out the flavour of the fat. Unique inspirations from Japanese cuisine include chicken meat marinated in kombu broth and chicken meatballs mixed with takikomi-gohan. In a clever twist, yakitori is served atop vegetables, which absorb flavour from the many types of skewer placed on top of them, then are grilled last.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3333442416	YOSHOKU OGATA	32-1 Tojijicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://youshoku-ogata.com/	Nessun premio	Yoshoku	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	‘A kappo-style yoshoku restaurant to satisfy the heart as well as the stomach’ is the concept here. The chef converses with guests at the counter while pouring all his skills into his food preparation. Determined to satisfy, he never compromises on quality, sourcing ingredients from a butcher in Shiga, a fishmonger in Shizuoka, and a farmer in Kyoto. Old yoshoku favourites such as deep-fried horse mackerel, sautéed pork and hamburger steak are popular. Flame technique and sauces draw on the chef’s experience with French cuisine.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3330838814	Nikutoieba Matsuda	2F	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Beef	4.0	¥¥	t	t	The owner-chef, a butcher, prepares wagyu. The set menu meal begins with a bold, hearty meat dish. He uses mostly Yamato beef for his customers to get a feel for Nara ingredients. His creative touches include slicing it thin and pressing it between sheets of kombu and making minced meat into gyoza dumpling. Even the last dish features wagyu, and includes chopped beef and curry. Creative dishes and attractive presentations make this a popular spot.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
