3334171056	Kasane	B1F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The dish Toyama native chef offers as his speciality is oden. Typically for Osaka, his is salty, to make a fitting companion for sake. Ma-kombu and katsuo-bushi exude a rich umami. The sardine dumplings look like they belong in a kaiseki soup. The items are abundantly varied: potatoes are seasoned with soy sauce flavour, for example. To wrap up the meal, udon in oden dashi is served. Etchu sake is brought in from his native prefecture, showing his love for his hometown.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3334770048	Shokudo Tanoshi	2F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The down-to-earth name, ‘Shokudo’ or ‘cafeteria’, was chosen because the restaurant aims to be one where people can drop in casually, while ‘Tanoshi’ (from tanoshii, ‘fun’) reflects the fun atmosphere created by Hirata, who handles service, and the chef. Indeed, it’s fun just to peruse the extensive menu. The inventive items, which weave together Japanese, Western and Chinese influences, offer no end of variety. Abalone-like shrimp croquettes and Chinese-style fried chicken-wing tips amply exemplify the spirit of Shokudo Tanoshi.	serrakevin	\N	\N
