3333534972	Kitashinchi Kushikatsu Bon	B1F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Kushiage	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Kitashinchi Kushikatsu Bon serves skewers of unstinting luxury, including chateaubriand and foie gras. Creative combinations of delicacies, such as ‘pregnant kombu’ (kombu kelp with Pacific herring roe attached) with sea urchin and caviar or name-brand pork with truffles, are especially fun. To ensure a light palate, items are coated in powder-fine breadcrumbs and deep-fried in cottonseed oil. Osaka soul food, enriched with uniquely conceived ingredients.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3332774690	milpa	1-16-25 Kitahorie	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Mexican, Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥¥	t	t	This is the place to sample modern Mexican cuisine. Respect for the traditions of the motherland are palpable as Japanese ingredients and modern techniques move the genre forward. Corn, the staple food, along with cacao and chili peppers, is sourced from Mexico, and, following tradition, the food is cooked over a wood-fired grill. Milpa is the name in the Nahuatl (Aztec) language for a farming system that enriches the earth^ the chef likens cooking techniques to farming, cultivating a new Mexican culinary culture in Osaka.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3333384713	Man-u	5F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.kagaman.co.jp/	Nessun premio	Oden	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Man-u’s ingenious oden, which borrows from other Japanese cuisines, is a whirlwind of flavour changes. Items are selected from a large pot and paired with condiments and broth to bring different flavours to the fore. Beef sinew is cooked with green onions^ octopus is paired with unripe pepper. Clams, wakame seaweed with bamboo shoots, and pike conger with matsutake mushrooms are served as soup dishes. Lettuce, tomato and figs dressed with starchy dashi soup stock sauce provide interesting alternatives. Painstaking preparation results in an oden with a unique finish.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3337058775	Yoshitaka	2F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.yoshitaka-osaka.jp/	Nessun premio	Oden	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Oden fashioned in the manner of a simmered dish in kaiseki fare. Toppings such as dried kombu shavings for tofu and ground sesame for soft-boiled eggs are served one piece at a time to offer a twist on familiar flavours. Each serving-dish is different, an influence from the chef’s experience in other cuisines. The meal ends with ramen flavoured with dashi or, taking a page from Edo cooking, peppered rice. Osaka has been a port of call for kombu merchants since the Edo period, and this is a place to savour stewed items from that rich dashi culture.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3339075351	Asador ROCA	2-6-4 Hiranomachi	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Spanish	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Asador ROCA offers a pairing prix fixe menu, showcasing Spanish food culture in all its delightful variety. Cuisine drawing on the uniqueness of the Basque region makes effective use of paprika and chilli. Combining the bounty of land and sea, asado of mushrooms and shrimp works its magic by forming a connection with the chef’s native Itoshima, hemmed between mountain and ocean. Hometown memories, nature, people he’s met – the chef’s life experiences are understood on a deeper level through his flavours.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3333834562	Claro	4-18 Matsuyamachi	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Spanish	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The chef creates modern Spanish fare with Japanese ingredients. Uniting two cultures, the chef combines foodstuffs like tortillas with seaweed, while other dishes feature elements such as sherry sauce and Daitokuji natto. Paella made with Japanese rice is another example: ingredients such as firefly squid, eel and crab tell of each season. The all-black interior is stylishly appointed with modern art. While lacking a bright mood during the daytime, it is nicely relaxing.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3335158223	DuKKAh	4-3-13 Nishitemma	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining	https://eiichimatumoto0321.wixsite.com/dukkah	Nessun premio	Spanish	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	A counter restaurant serving the cuisine of northern Spain. After spending considerable time in Galicia and the Basque Country, the chef drew inspiration from the guardians of those regions’ culture and food. Both regions face the Bay of Biscay, so their cuisines, blessed with bounties of sea and land, are delightfully varied. Overlaying these traditions with Japanese foods such as kudzu, soba and green pepper flower creates expressions of unique character. A marriage of Spanish local cuisine with Japanese ingredients.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3334146796	Ueroku wine	4-15 Higashikozucho	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Spanish	4.0	¥¥	t	f	A Spanish restaurant by Bordeaux vintner. Spain has two coasts, the Mediterranean and the Atlantic, and Japan is surrounded by seas on all four sides. These geographical features define the food culture and cooking on tap at Ueroku wine. The chef parlays Japan’s unique seafood into cuisine with a distinctive character. A selection of wines from many countries, including the owner’s own, Clos Leo, is available for your enjoyment.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3339389252	Kitashinchi Fukutatei	B1F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Steakhouse	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The steaks at Kitashinchi Fukutatei are grilled by the double action of Bincho charcoal flame stoked in a furnace and far-infrared photothermal heat. Beef is Japanese Black wagyu, heifer only. Tasting and comparing different cuts, such as tenderloin, rump and aitchbone, is part of the fun. To ensure you fully enjoy the fragrant, delicate quality of the meat, seasoning is limited to salt and pepper. While the meat is being patiently grilled, tuck into wagyu consommé soup and appetisers.	shirocky	\N	\N
3337868732	Sushi Enishi	11-1 Kurosakicho	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	The chef learned Japanese cooking at his childhood home, a restaurant with attached inn^ destiny led him down the path of the sushi master. Fish is from the markets of Temma and Kizu. Dashi soup stock is drawn from kombu kelp and dried bonito flakes^ the addition of vegetables stems from his experience in other disciplines of Japanese cuisine. To modulate the flavours, sushi topping temperatures are varied and the tartness of citrus is used. The service is an experience of a lifetime, even if you’re a first-time guest. The shop’s name, enishi, or ‘connection’, signals the importance the chef places on human relationships.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3339718701	Sushi Ichiei	B1F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Inheriting his father’s dream of independence, the chef followed him along the path of the sushi master. The signature item on the omakase menu is tsukuri of botan shrimp. The arrival of ginger wrapped in nori signals the transition from appetizers to sushi. Nigiri are orthodox, though the choice of sweet shrimp hits a distinctive note. The chef’s assured technique shows even in the thick rolled omelette. ‘Ichiei’ means something like ‘forever’, capturing his hope that you will treasure your encounter with his shop and remain a friend to it.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3335398740	Sushi Kyomachibori Sato	B1F	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Snacks and nigiri testify to the chef’s experience in Japanese cuisine. The meal begins simply, with handmade tofu or pureed vegetable soup. Tilefish scales are scored before the fish is grilled to make it look like a pinecone^ pike conger and longtooth grouper are served as shabu-shabu, adding hot dishes to the mix. Sushi toppings such as Orient clams and simmered conger eel attest to old-school craftsmanship. Keen to offer a wide range of flavours, the chef offers smaller portions of nigiri enhanced with red vinegar and salt.	popafarah	\N	\N
3335419199	Sushi Marumine	6-2-20 Tenjimbashi	Japan	Osaka	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The husband-and-wife team have previously managed a fishmonger and a caterer. As a discerning connoisseur, the chef’s ability to source great ingredients is impressive. The menu, written in a beautifully flowing hand, is crammed with a rich miscellany of fish. Many of the patrons are regulars, freely ordering snacks and nigiri with cups of sake^ they drop in for friendly conversation amid their daily lives in this intimate restaurant with its congenial atmosphere, a radio playing in the background.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
