3333019441	Chugokusai Kan	2-18-4 Shinkawa	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://chinese-restaurant-kan.tokyo/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥	f	t	Owner-chef, a Keio University graduate, became a chef from his dreams of being an artisan^ a person who can accomplish one thing can do anything. Flame-broiled items finished in the massive oven are a gift acquired through many labours as a hotel chef. Fujii cuts a deft and poised figure in the kitchen, master of both theory and practice. He claims his mother vehemently opposed his choice of career, but when he beholds the joy of his guests, his face is the picture of happiness.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3330883444	hatsune	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥	f	t	The chef works alone in this tiny restaurant. At lunchtime the predominant theme is noodle dishes, such as dandan noodles and hot-and-sour ramen. In the evening, both à la carte and set menu dining are available. Be sure to order the appetiser platter, as it’s packed with variety and the time and effort taken to prepare it are apparent. The spring rolls, a finger food, are also recommended. The ‘Yellow Mapo Tofu with Seafood’ intrigues with its unusual name and distinctive yellow colour.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3332537424	Hei Fung Terrace	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.peninsula.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The exotic atmosphere is suggestive of a Chinese garden. Being part of a Hong Kong group, the focus is on Cantonese cuisine. The dim sum master creates xiaolongbao and gyoza, while the grill master serves up chicken and pork baked in iron pots. From the cornucopia of ingredients, guests can decide the seasoning and cooking style, including stewed items in oyster sauce and stir-fried items with XO or black bean sauce. Ask to sit overlooking the outer garden of the Imperial Palace.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3333979234	Ji-Cube	3-18-10 Nishiazabu	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://ji-cube3.studio.site/	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Ji-Cube aspires to create Chinese cuisine that could only be made in Japan, using Japanese ingredients. For example, dim sum is dressed with sauces of sudachi and yuzu, two characteristically Japanese citrus fruits. Jellyfish salad paired with daikon smoked like iburigakko (smoked daikon pickles from Akita) is an intriguing innovation. The chef’s devotion to polishing his skills in Sichuan cooking shines in his mastery of cooking with Sichuan pepper and chilli pepper. Milt in mapo sauce is a dish to enjoy in winter.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3332684418	MIMOSA	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://mimosa-aoyama.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The counter seats are a uniform white, creating a sense of presence, and the sight of cooking right in front of you is reassuring. Amid the sounds and aromas of stir-frying in woks, the chef sometimes makes conversation with guests while plating their meals. Based on Shanghai cuisine, the dishes are set in front of you as soon as they are cooked. The restaurant’s name was chosen for the chef’s grandmother’s favourite flower. This is food created with loving thoughts of Grandma.	rossidino	\N	\N
3337768961	Nogizaka yui	1-23-12 Minamiaoyama	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥	t	f	The chef is passionate about ‘the ties that bind’. He chose the name ‘yui’, meaning ‘ties’ or ‘connections’, to mark his restaurant as a place that links guests with food producers^ people with people. The gracious service by the warm-hearted proprietress also conveys that spirit. Cuisine based on Sichuan traditions combines with vegetables delivered directly from farms. Nogizaka yui connects with Japan’s seasons as well, evidenced by sour soup of bamboo shoots and beef in spring and soy-sauce stir fry of organic maitake mushrooms in autumn. Seasoning is restrained to place ingredients centre stage.	basileryan	\N	\N
3337687296	Noyashichi	2-9 Arakicho	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://noyashichi.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Chinese cuisine overlaid with Japanese ingredients and techniques, such as kombu kelp and dried bonito flakes, is the theme here, with Shinya Yamamoto treading an original path that blends the two. The technique of steamed chicken with spicy sauce, for example, is applied to fish sashimi, which is spiced with chilli oil. Rice cooked in clay pots is topped with Sichuan-style bean curd or stir-fried beef. Kombu kelp in clear soup is an homage to Japanese preparation. Dishes are served on Japanese serving plates, highlighting the affinity between the cuisines.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3332042975	O2	2-15-12 Miyoshi	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥	f	f	‘O2’ (‘oh-two’) is a play on Chef Otsu’s name. Like his bow tie and denim apron, the pun is an Otsu trademark. Presented as Chinese cuisine, the fare at O2 really defies easy categories, making use of both Western and Japanese ingredients. The chef’s code is to use Chinese elements in both technique and seasoning. The playful interior also expresses Otsu’s unique vision.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3338004960	Sense	37F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list	https://www.mandarinoriental.co.jp/	Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The chef is thoroughly versed in Cantonese cuisine and his credo is to faithfully reproduce traditional cuisine. Specialities include deep-fried whole pigeon, double-boiled premium soup with dried mushrooms and quickly-steamed star grouper. We also recommend the dim sum. Enjoy orthodox Cantonese cuisine while taking in some of the best scenery in Tokyo – there’s nothing quite like a dinner in subdued lighting against a night cityscape.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3334204730	Shintomicho Yuasa	2-7-4 Shintomi	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://shintomi-yuasa.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	¥¥¥	f	t	The character for ‘food’ (食) is composed of the components for ‘person’ (人) and ‘good’ (良), signifying the power of food to make a person good. Daisuke Yuasa, who puts great store by the principles of a balanced diet and good food for good health, creates dishes he hopes will support his patrons’ health in both body and soul. Another of his wishes is that food should be fun, so he gained a sommelier qualification to help customers expand their enjoyment.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3338788752	Shunka Nakamura	2-11-7 Higashinihombashi	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://syunka-nakamura.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Relentless curiosity is the driving force of this chef. After going to Hong Kong to study Cantonese cuisine, he then worked at a kappo to learn about Japanese food. He calls the marriage of these two shunka, which roughly translates as ‘Chinese food with a seasonal sensibility’. Spring rolls of pike conger or conger eel are one example. The steamed chicken is a secret recipe passed on from his Hong Kong mentor. He presents the home-cooked flavours that Hongkongers love.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3336322844	Tokyo Chinese Ichirin	1-5-8 Tsukiji	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥¥	f	f	Sichuan cuisine that strives for a mellow spiciness. The evening prix fixe offering, which combines steamed spicy chicken with liver paté, is highly original. We recommend adding some of the distinctive à la carte items, such as shrimp chili sauce made with whole large shrimp, or fried egg and crab as airy as a soufflé. Weekday lunches are a set menu of twice-cooked pork and dandan noodles. A popular place, so queues form at times.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3331333580	Wakiya Ichiemicharo	6-11-10 Akasaka	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning	https://www.wakiya.co.jp/restaurants/ichiemi/	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The flagship restaurant of Yuji Wakiya, renowned pioneer of nouvelle chinois cuisine. With “tradition and creativity” as his motto, Wakiya professes a new style of Chinese cooking. The starter, ‘Nine Joys Assorted Appetiser’, is so named because nine is a number believed to bring good luck in China. The restaurant name means ‘once a day, let’s relax, laugh and have tea’. Cuisine and hospitality to bring a smile to your face.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3332103770	YAUMAY	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://yaumay.jp/	Nessun premio	Chinese, Dim Sum	4.0	¥¥¥	f	f	A specialist in dim sum, popular in cities around the world. The red exterior belies the classic dining experience within, which is lively on every visit. Enjoy the culture of dim sum with Chinese tea to your heart’s content. The full complement of authentic dishes includes jasmine-smoked pork, steamed scallop siu mai dumplings, steamed shrimp gyoza dumplings and rice-noodle rolls wrapped in fried tofu skin. If the weather’s nice, taking in the local ambience on the terrace is recommended.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3330233582	DEN KUSHI FLORI	B1F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://denkushiflori.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	A collab between the two restaurants Den, with its creative Japanese food, and Florilège, offering modern French cuisine. ‘Den’ and ‘Flori’ are joined by ‘Kushi’, meaning ‘skewer’. Yet despite the name, this is not a skewer restaurant^ rather, the name reflects the experience and friendship that joins the eatery’s two partners. The fare is Japanese-Western fusion: tempura with sherry, for example, or sweetfish in baked custard tart. Always evolving, never making the same dish twice, it shows the world that experimentation makes food more fun.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3331570883	HYÈNE	5-13-14 Jingumae	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://hyene.hviewgroup.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	Expect creative fare fusing Japanese, Korean and French culinary culture. A perfect reflection of Chef Yoko Kimoto’s life, as she carries both Japanese and Korean DNA and is schooled in French cuisine. Her speciality, potato fondant au chocolat, overlays a French dessert onto a Korean rice-cake snack her mother used to make her when she was little. Imbuing Japanese ingredients with Korean flavours using French techniques, Kimoto conjures a gastronomy that is all her own.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3332860416	JULIA	3-1-25 Jingumae	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.juliahospitalitygroup.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥¥	f	t	The wife is the chef, the husband the sommelier in this couple-run restaurant. The omakase set menu consists of pairings only. An evangelist to the world for Japan as a terroire, JULIA specialises in Japanese foodstuffs and Japanese wines. Most ingredients come from Ibaraki Prefecture, where the husband was born and the restaurant originated. Uniquely, the couple favours pairings of vegetables and fish with fruit. Self-taught and freewheeling, the cuisine is colourful and light.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3331435434	KIBUN	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kibuntokyo.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The chef came from France to study Japanese cuisine, and the tale of his journey is told in his prix fixe menus, which interweave French and Japanese culinary traditions. Japanese knife techniques shine in preparing squid and pike conger, finely sliced to cut up the bones, with sauces that raise the ingredients’ taste to a higher level. Fruit and herb flavours interlace to form a cuisine that knows no borders. The ‘ki’ in the name of the restaurant is the same as the Chinese ‘qi’. The essential taste of each ingredient, expressed with consummate sensitivity.	langalice	\N	\N
3339189245	KOKYU	2-13-9 Yokokawa	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://ko-kyu.jp/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	¥¥¥	f	f	A ‘food laboratory’ housed in a small, renovated warehouse. Only creative cuisine, fragrant with spices and suffused with the umami of tea, for pairing with cocktails is offered. Recipes take their inspiration from French cuisine and the restaurant’s name, which means ‘wither and decay’, is from the desire to breathe deeply of love for old cuisine before creating the new. Enjoy the fruits of experimentation in cooking and beverages.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3335746433	Margotto e Baciare	4-2-6 Nishiazabu	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.margotto.jp/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Whole truffles are on offer here, and indeed ‘Margotto’ is a creative spelling of marugoto, ‘the whole thing’. The concept is revolutionary: guests can choose a single bead of the truffle of their liking. The chef brings his Japanese cuisine experience to bear on a base of French cuisine. Consommé of kombu dashi is poured into wine glasses, the better to enjoy its fragrance. Truffles are even paired with fried eggs on toast and raw egg on rice. Enjoy this moment of mellowness to its fullest.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3333040305	Nebuka	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Nebuka was opened by the proprietor of a wine bar. It is said that the best grapevines are those with the deepest roots (‘ne-buka’), and deep are the connections Nebuka cultivates with producers and in ingredients and cuisine. Omakase set menus focus on vegetables and game. Experienced in both French and Japanese cuisine, the chef applies expertise in both schools, and even creates pasta dishes. Each dish is arranged simply, placing the ingredients centre stage. A young team provides bright and pleasant service.	semenovirene	\N	\N
3333506292	sio	1-35-3 Uehara	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning	https://sio-yoyogiuehara.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	Remixed music plays in the background of a dining room which has the feel of a vintage café. The venue is popular for its simple, casual style. The young, close-knit team puts guests at ease with their friendly service. Cuisine is based on French fare but interweaves influences from Italian and Japanese cooking. This is genre-free cuisine born of multinational creativity.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3336002200	Valinor	4-32-7 Ogikubo	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning	https://www.valinor2011.com/index.html	Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥¥	f	f	The chef aims for nothing less than unforgettable cuisine. His ingredients are the stars of his show, and to place them at centre stage, each dish uses as few as possible. While adding twists to texture and flavour, he leaves a vivid impression of each ingredient. Only those dishes that keep being made, keep being eaten, can be called classics. He puts his stamp on his food through simplifying the complexities of French cuisine.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3335809949	sio AOYAMA	2F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://sio-yoyogiuehara.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	¥¥¥	t	f	The Aoyama branch of sio fairly bubbles with imaginative power. The foundation is French, but the direction is creative, paying no attention to genre. Meats are grilled over a wood fire to draw out the full strength of their inherent flavours. If you sit at the counter, you can gaze into the flickering flames and enjoy the aroma of meat sizzling on the grill. The restaurant’s name, ‘sio’, is Japanese for ‘salt’, affirming the importance of this vital seasoning. The restaurant prides itself on salting with just the right touch to highlight flavours.	gavrilovnora	\N	\N
