3336810713	RISTORANTE Al Porto	B1F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning	https://www.alporto.jp/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	¥¥¥	f	t	Mamoru Kataoka is a pioneer who has broadened the appeal of Italian gastronomy in Japan. His passion for seafood stems was inspired by the seafood restaurants he encountered on a visit to Milan in the 1960s. Al Porto’s famous pasta is a seafood ragù prepared with lashings of clams and shrimp. Kataoka manages the kitchen and restaurant with his son. When time allows, father and son circulate among the tables, ever mindful of the importance of graceful service.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
3337797309	Ristorante HONDA	2-12-35 Kitaaoyama	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning	https://www.ristorantehonda.jp	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	¥¥¥	t	f	Seasonal foodstuffs are the theme at this modern Italian restaurant. Tetsuya Honda’s culinary creations link the traditional cuisine of Italy with the seasons of Japan. The speciality, ‘Sea Urchin Tagliolini’, uses no cream, relying instead on lashings of sea urchin to achieve a rich, satisfying flavour. Honda strives to elicit the flavour of each ingredient.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3335146073	RISTORANTE la primula	5-9-13 Hiro	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	¥¥¥	t	t	A counter-style Italian eatery presented by a chef who learnt his trade in northern Italy and an owner who loves all things Venetian. Tapestries recreate the canals of La Serenissima^ Venetian glass and Carnevale masks variegate the interior. The northern penchant for butter influences the chef’s culinary stylings. Homemade pasta is cut thick, after the chef’s preference: the tagliolini is the product of a seasoned artisan.	semenovirene	\N	\N
3334044012	Sanwa	B1F	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	¥¥¥	t	t	‘Sanwa’ means ‘three-part harmony’: harmony between producers, chefs and guests. Descending the stairs, your eye is caught by the three-ring logo, which is both the Watanabe family crest and the restaurant’s symbol. The menu lists producers by name, neatly linking them to guests through the chef. The name would not suggest an Italian restaurant, nor does its offering of char-grilled meats, but these speak to its unique character. The strength of three brings mutual prosperity.	berninialex	\N	\N
