3337038242	DIA	Maironio Street 9	Lithuania	Kaunas	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restoranasdia.lt	Nessun premio	International, Creative	5.0	$$	f	f	You’ll be surprised how busy this formally laid restaurant in a residential spot can get, but the experienced team cope well with the numbers – among which there are many returning guests. It sits within a tardis-like building, which also houses meeting rooms, and is smartly decked out with fine glassware and crockery. The menu is one of the most eclectic around and offers everything from a burger to fine steaks, with the popular daily specials including the likes of freshly caught fish. There really is something for everyone here.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3339734446	Uoksas	Maironio g. 28	Lithuania	Kaunas		https://uoksas.eu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	$$	f	t	In this chic, smartly furnished restaurant, things are both relaxed and lively at the same time. The team are pursuing their vision of redesigning Lithuanian cuisine and work with modern techniques following a Nordic style. Ingredients come mainly from the Baltic region, although there are some exceptions, resulting in dishes like beetroot taco with seabass ceviche, pickled onion and coriander or grilled veal chop with chive butter, grilled tomatoes, potato and ghee butter mash. Choose from the concise à la carte or order the tasting menu in advance to sample the full range of the kitchen’s talents.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3333464749	monai	Liepų Gatvė 4	Lithuania	Klaipeda		https://www.restoranasmonai.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$	t	t	The busy port city of Klaipėda plays host to this cosy restaurant where, once you’ve located the discreet entrance – a very warm welcome awaits. As you step over the threshold, a feeling of calm engulfs you, and you can drift away from the world outside. Lunch is a simple affair and represents great value, while at dinner, honest flavours shine through in modern dishes where fish is a highlight, such as in the roasted cod with coco beans, chorizo and cauliflower. This will quickly become one of your favourite new places to eat.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3336591311	Red Brick	Farmers Circle	Lithuania	Radiškis	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://red-brick.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	$$$	f	t	The Farmers Circle is a wonderfully remote 1,730 acre working farm situated an hour’s drive outside the capital. At its centre sits this beautifully restored period barn, now home to the Red Brick restaurant. Naturally, the majority of the produce comes from their farm, with the rest sourced nearby. Chef Arnór’s tasting menu is modern and hyper-seasonal, fully embracing the sustainable approach^ you’ll find elegant snacks followed by the likes of skrei with chicken sauce, then maybe mint, sea buckthorn and carrots – all of which will tantalise your tastebuds. The dishes are explained by the genial team and there are cosy bedrooms for a complete overnight experience.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3330152218	Apvalaus Stalo Klubo	Karaimų g. 53A	Lithuania	Trakai	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.asklubas.lt/restoranas.htm	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	$$	t	t	On the shores of Lake Galve, in the heart of a national park, you’ll find this intimate, modern restaurant, which affords incredible views over the water to the 14th-century Trakai Island Castle from its floor-to-ceiling windows. When the sun's shining, the lovely terrace is the place to be. Complex modern cooking is a reflection of the locale, exemplified by the likes of beetroot with goat’s cheese and flavour-packed lamb cutlets. Desserts are a highlight, with the ‘raspberries with raspberries’ always a surefire winner. Cheery service brings a smile to everyone’s face, and cosy bedrooms complete the picture.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3331595881	HeJi	Lukiškių Gatvė 3	Lithuania	Vilnius	Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://heji.lt	Nessun premio	Asian Influences	5.0	$$$	f	f	Having been five years in the making, this impressively opulent restaurant seems like it might be more at home in Dubai or Macau than Vilnius! The cavernous glass-roofed main dining room is overlooked by two ‘caged’ balconies and a champagne bar – and there’s an intimate, dimly lit cocktail bar serving innovative Asian creations. A wood-framed open kitchen takes centre stage, and captivating and intriguing design details abound. The original menu fuses East and West, with the dim sum a hit and the signature beef dishes cooked over charcoal a real highlight. The wine list features some fine growers and the whole place makes for a glamorous night out.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3332368866	Protėviai	Odminių Gatvė 3	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://proteviai.com/	Nessun premio	Barbecue	4.0	$$$	t	f	The name Protėviai translates as ‘ancestor’ and their tagline is “The legend of fire and steaks, inspired by the ancestors of the world”. As you may have guessed, this restaurant is all about the primeval method of cooking steaks over fire and smoke. The striking interior takes in huge wooden sculptures and a fire-effect central counter hewn out of a huge piece of wood. The steaks – some dry-aged for 60 days – are a mix of Lithuanian, USDA Prime rib-eye, Koji tenderloin and Wagyu from Japan and Australia, and are served by weight, cooked over glowing embers and rested with care.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3330882323	Stikliai	Gaono Gatvė 7	Lithuania	Vilnius		https://www.stikliai.com/gourmet-restaurant/	Nessun premio	Classic French	5.0	$$$$	t	t	For a comfortingly classical experience in the city, head to Stikliai, set within a hotel in the heart of the Old Town. Here, photos of famous faces who have visited over the years line the walls – including celebrities and Heads of State – and the glass-roofed room filled with greenery has an elegant feel. Matching the atmosphere, the food has a classical French base, with the sauces in particular being a strength. You might find lamb shoulder confit with bulgur wheat, tomato concasse and aubergine caviar or haddock fillet served with sweet potatoes, fennel, pak choi and beurre blanc.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3330317681	Da Antonio	Vilnius Gatvė 23	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$$	f	t	The Meschino family first opened this restaurant on the food-centric Vilnius Gatvė in 1996 as a pizzeria and, over the years, it has evolved into this smart, formal spot. Two small dining rooms are elegantly decked out with mirrors, chandeliers and linen-clad tables^ in summertime though, head for the flower-decked terrace. The chef may be Lithuanian, but you’d never know, as he follows the Italian principles of good ingredients, simple preparation and maximum flavour. The homemade pastas are a highlight – with the tagliatelle with shrimps, saffron and courgette a signature – and interesting Italian wines accompany.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3330132470	Justa Pasta	Vokiečių Gatvė 20	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning	https://justa-pasta.tablein.com/lt	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	$$	f	f	As you walk down the street you’ll see the chefs beavering away behind the windows of this shop conversion, crafting various types of pasta and gnocchi with 00 flour. Exposed brick walls lend the place a rustic air, yet the room is quite formally laid. Alongside the more familiar dishes such as meatballs or ravioli with a potato filling, you’ll find some different dishes such as a delicious tacchino tonnato^ the coconut panna cotta is a great choice for dessert. You’ll get a proper taste of Italy without breaking the bank.	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3334237574	Farmer & The Ocean	Vilniaus Gatvė 25-33	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning	https://www.facebook.com/farmerandtheocean/	Nessun premio	Meats and Seafood	3.0	$$	t	t	Located in a busy spot amongst many other eateries, it’s worth seeking out this basement restaurant. Inside it’s bright and colourful, with orange walls, designer touches and a large octopus hanging from the ceiling. The name says it all, with meat and seafood centric dishes including delicious beef, lamb shank, herring and a wonderful seafood stew. The snails on toast is a popular choice and the classical desserts – like crème brûlée – are always a hit. Be sure to book ahead though, as they do get busy.	baguettebenois	\N	\N
3335451733	Amandus	Užupio Gatvė 22	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.amandus.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$$$	t	t	Located a short walk from the Old Town, Amandus brings a touch of history to proceedings, yet also adds a relaxed, bohemian vibe. Guests arrive at 7pm, whereupon Chef-Owner Deivydas greets them personally, and there are further chances to interact when the chefs bring their dishes to the table. The surprise tasting menu draws its inspiration from historical recipes and flavours, which are brought together, updated and presented in a modern way^ the beetroot and rye bread served with paprika butter is a signature. If champagne and sparkling wine is your thing, forsake the wine pairings and choose from the main list.	dragomirpippo	\N	\N
3330165487	Augustin	Didžioji Gatvė 18	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://augustin.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	$$	t	f	Sister to Momo Grill and monai, this informal restaurant has a sleek modern style. Parquet floors sit below two striking circular faux-candle chandeliers hanging from a concrete ceiling, while shelves of wine fill vintage sideboards. Punchy, colourful dishes blend Mediterranean and Middle Eastern flavours and are offered in two different formats. The majority of the menu comprises modern plant-led small plates – three per person plus a dessert is about right – but there are also three main courses on offer which are based around fish or meat. Service is warm and friendly, and the courtyard terrace is a real boon in warmer months.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3336578159	Dine	Gedimino prospektas 35	Lithuania	Vilnius	Wheelchair access	https://dinerestaurant.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$$	f	f	Dine is one of those places which simply provides great enjoyment. The kitchen is rooted in the classical camp but has modern overtones – and keeps things simple by using fresh ingredients which are cleanly cooked and refrain from unnecessary adornment, as exemplified by the likes of cod with wild garlic purée, peas and mint oil in the summer. That being said, there’s some skill on display in elements like of the two-coloured ravioli dough. The regularly evolving wine list offers a good selection by the glass, as well as a strong selection of champagnes. They also offer themed tasting dinners.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3332864213	elven	L. Stuokos-Gucevičiaus Gatvė 7	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.elven.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	$$	f	t	Sister to Nüman in Kaunas, the name of this restaurant means ‘river’ in Norwegian, with the language being a clue both to the design of the room and the style of the food here. The traditional creamwashed façade of the heritage building is certainly in complete contrast to the sleek interior, which is an elegant space with a design-led style. The menu delivers a good range of creative, pared-back dishes with bold flavours, a blend of textures and eye-catching presentation, with sharing dishes for two also a feature. In summer, head for the rear terrace.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3336017147	Fabrikėlis	Pasakų Gatvė 9	Lithuania	Vilnius	Garden or park,Terrace	https://fabrikelis.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	$$$	f	f	It’s worth making the journey a few kilometres outside the city to eat at this friendly restaurant^ ask for a table on the enclosed veranda or in the garden to get a feeling of dining among the pine trees. The seven or so dishes are designed with sharing in mind and are overtly seasonal – in spring you might find a superb malted sourdough to begin with, followed by oysters with pine, scallops with buttermilk or roasted quail. There’s usually just one dessert on offer, but if it’s the coffee mille-feuille then you’re are in for a treat. Natural wines accompany the modern cooking.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3332229453	Momo Grill	Totorių Gatvė 1	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://momogrill.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$	f	f	It might be called a grill but it’s not all about steaks here^ meats in general are the focus, which is emphasised by the carcasses hanging in the chiller cabinet as you enter. Situated on the edge of the Old Town, the room has been given a faux-industrial look courtesy of exposed brick, plaster walls and quarry-tiled floors. The menu is short, seasonal and appealing, with the lunchtime burger on Saturdays changing ingredient from week to week. Care and pride are put into every one of the vibrant, colourful dishes, which come with international influences and bold, gutsy flavours.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3334180540	Pacai	Didžioji Gatvė 7	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.hotelpacai.com/en/pacai-restaurant	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	$$$	t	f	The owners here claim that this 17th Century baroque property in the heart of the Old Town was once the most magnificent mansion in the Grand Duchy of Lithuania^ today, it’s home to a boutique hotel complete with a spa and this stylish restaurant. Start with a drink in the large, retro-style cocktail bar, before moving on to interesting seasonal dishes with a strong Lithuanian base. The wine list is highly recommended, with some great vintages at every turn and a good selection of different wines by the glass. In the summer months, when the light lasts long into the evening, the central courtyard becomes an appealing oasis.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3330853809	Somm	Pylimo Gatvė 21	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://somm.lt	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	$$	t	t	The name Somm is an abbreviation of sommelier, giving a strong clue as to where Owner Narimantas Miežys’ passion lies. He is one of the top sommeliers in the Baltic region and, with over 500 bottles making up a truly global selection, this really is an oenophile’s paradise. Set opposite the MO modern art museum, it’s decorated with wine bottles and related memorabilia, and has a pleasingly unfussy, neighbourhood feel. This is a place where the sommeliers choose your wines for you – after discussing your preferences, of course – matching them with simple yet interesting dishes, some of which are prepared in the wood-burning oven	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3334207961	Telegrafas	Universiteto Gatvė 14	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.telegrafas.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$$	t	f	Built in 1900, this rather magnificent building – now home to a smart hotel – sits in a prime position overlooking Vilnius Cathedral and was once the city Telegraph office, hence the restaurant’s name. The contemporary ground floor space comes complete with a decked terrace and the personable service team cater for your every need. Modern menus offer plenty of appeal, with the Business Lunch representing great value for money. Dishes take on a straightforward approach and are carefully executed, with harmonious flavour combinations found in dishes such as salmon tartare with buttermilk panna cotta, compressed cucumber, bread & beer chips and dill emulsion.	toscanomarek	\N	\N
3339909798	Stebuklai	L. Stuokos-Gucevičiaus Gatvė 1	Lithuania	Vilnius	Terrace	https://www.stebuklai.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	$	t	f	Set in a hotel beside the Cathedral Square, you can expect an idyllic ambience here, complete with twinkling water fountains. When the weather’s good, the terrace is the place to be, as it faces the Square and the Cathedral, but the restaurant itself is also a beautiful place with a chic, modern ambience. The ambitious kitchen produce cosmopolitan dishes such as hamachi ceviche with strawberries, hibiscus, avocado and shiso or duck breast with carrot gratin, cherries, pickled onions and Pedro Ximenez sauce, which all arrive in attractive arrangements.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3334126428	The Ukai	46F	Taiwan	Taipei	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.ukai.co.jp/english/taipei/	Nessun premio	Teppanyaki	5.0	$$$$	t	t	This is the second Taiwanese outpost of its namesake in Japan, famous for its Western-style table experience delivered with teppanyaki techniques. There is no à la carte and the two set menus change with the seasons. Signatures include steamed abalone with rock salt, garlic fried rice, and Wagyu steak or tenderloin from Tamura farm. Finish in style with a choice of dessert made with seasonal fruit and served in the cosy lounge.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3331574916	Ertlio Namas	Šv. Jono Gatvé 7	Lithuania	Vilnius	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://ertlionamas.lt	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	$$$	t	t	Set over three floors of a historic townhouse in the city centre, this is a charming restaurant with wonderful wooden floors, fine period art on the walls and a historical menu to match. Choose either a 4 or 6 course set menu to experience interesting dishes from a bygone era – dating as far back as the 16th Century – which could include sorrel soup, salted and cured veal pekenfleišas or beef tart with beef broth sauce. Following each dish comes an explanation of its origins, providing sustenance for your brain as well as your body.	ozmax	\N	\N
3337165670	Restaurant Mathes	39 route du Vin	Luxembourg	Ahn	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-mathes.lu/	Nessun premio	Modern French, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	Today, the third generation of the family captains this lively restaurant, where the artwork adorning the walls cultivates a refined atmosphere. Try your best to snag a table with a view of the Moselle River, or one on the terrace. Foodies have flocked to Mathes for its classic cuisine since 1949, although it has moved with the times beautifully. The undisputed star of the menu is still the pike perch – oven-baked and finished with a delicate Riesling sauce. With an impressive array of Luxembourg wines on offer, this family restaurant cements its place as a highly-regarded establishment.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3339866788	La Manufacture	5 Rue des Mérovingiens	Luxembourg	Bertrange	Car park,Terrace	https://lamanufacture.lu/	Nessun premio	Fusion, Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€	f	t	This sprawling, industrial-inspired restaurant with a central, open-plan kitchen and a disco mirror ball amusingly hanging over the stoves lies behind the grocery store. Trendy and fashionable is the name of the game as the chefs’ open-minded, no-holds barred approach to Mediterranean fusion cuisine illustrates: creativity, top quality ingredients and consummate technique.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3338528579	Loxalis	150 Rue de la Libération	Luxembourg	Dudelange	Terrace	https://www.loxalis.lu	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Immense floor-to-ceiling windows command a splendid view of the surrounding countryside, with the bonus of a peaceful terrace (weather permitting): the scene of Loxalis is set. Diners are greeted by a genuine maitre d’, who carefully takes the time to explain the appetising menu. Chef Boccolini subtly adds a modern spin to characteristic Mediterranean recipes, such as his new take on vitello tonnato flanked by a characterful sauce. Familiar flavours abound but with intriguing new dimensions. The lunchtime menu is a best-seller!	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3330689851	Le Jardin de la Gaichel	Maison 5	Luxembourg	Eischen	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.lagaichel.lu/fr	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Le cosy Jardin de la Gaichel est en parfaite harmonie avec son environnement boisé (un cadre idéal pour passer une nuitée !). La cuisine d’inspiration bretonne va droit au but. Fruits de mer (sur réservation), foie gras, canard découpé en salle… Une vraie cuisine de produits classique.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3331881167	La Rameaudière	10 rue de la Gare	Luxembourg	Ellange	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.larameaudiere.lu/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Daniel Rameau is a connoisseur of luxury produce, among which foie gras, lobster and pigeon, which he prepares refreshingly simply in dishes that blend generosity and tradition. The equally enticing wine list features a savvy selection of Luxemburg vintages. This former village train station and its flower-decked terrace are steeped in vintage charm.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3338734808	Cômo	19 rue des Remparts	Luxembourg	Esch-sur-Alzette	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://comoresto.lu	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€	t	f	It is no coincidence that charming Renato Favaro named his restaurant after his birthplace. Inspired by his roots and genuine Mediterranean trattoria traditions, his lasagne alla bolognese and fettucine l ragù are to die for! A talented chef who works only with the very best produce.	langalice	\N	\N
3335149667	Bosque FeVi	50 rue Gaalgebierg	Luxembourg	Esch-sur-Alzette	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://fevi.lu/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	If your tastebuds start to tingle at the idea of biting into a “croquetas de jamón” and a “crema catalana” with a hint of citrus fruit, then book a table straight away in this exquisite restaurant, depicted by a striking “undulating” wooden wall-cum-artwork. Fernando Andreu conjures up a Mediterranean score with a dash of modernity by delving into his Spanish roots and the odd international influence like kimchi or tikka masala. If you’re in the mood for tapas, make a beeline for FeVi Gaudium, under the same roof of the Seven Hotel.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3335716954	La Maison Lefèvre	138 boulevard J.F. Kennedy	Luxembourg	Esch-sur-Alzette	Car park,Terrace	https://www.lamaisonlefevre.lu/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€€	t	t	L’élégance de la façade de cette maison de maître se confirme à l’intérieur, avec la splendeur de ses grands lustres. Un vaste établissement où l’on trouve pourtant aussi une belle intimité. Les cuissons traditionnelles se parent de touches de modernité riches en contrastes. Le chef aime travailler les légumes avec créativité, ce qui donne à chaque assiette une touche bien personnelle.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3335713957	Artis	407 Route de Thionville	Luxembourg	Hesperange	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.artis-restaurant.lu	Nessun premio	Modern French	3.0	€€	f	t	Hao Guo entirely redesigned the interior of Artis with a brand-new colour scheme of soft shades and a cornucopia of contemporary comforts. The food is emblematic of the veteran chef’s experiences in top establishments in Belgium and abroad. While the backbone of his cuisine may be Gallic, he doesn’t hesitate to add international influences. For example, his bouillabaisse reveals the full depth of the salty seafood and is underscored with a rich, yet subtle stock. Chef Guo has an undeniable knack for sauces and his culinary technique is second to none. The extensive menu impresses, as does the spot-on selection of French and Luxembourg wines.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3330016845	Aal Schoul	33 A	Luxembourg	Hobscheid	Terrace	https://www.aal-schoul.lu/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Country cooking	4.0	€€€	f	t	The school bench at the entrance and the blackboard pay tribute to Aal Schoul’s former vocation as a village school^ it is now a warm eatery adorned in huge works of art. Red meat is omnipresent on the menu, but the chef’s bold, unconventional recipes are what most intrigue. For example, his recipe for poultry breasts rolls out a whole series of cooking techniques, while his highly individual take on a Caesar Salad features a sweet-sour vinaigrette with pili that adds a distinctive kick to the entire dish. An intriguing meal awaits you at Aal Schoul!	martinooliver	\N	\N
3336675490	Les Jardins d'Anaïs	2 place Sainte Cunégonde	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.jardinsdanais.lu/	Nessun premio	Creative French	3.0	€€€€	t	t	These gardens are the epitome of posh elegance from the conservatory overlooking the lush greenery to the guestrooms, without forgetting the champagne trolley. All of which doesn’t prevent chef Parjouet from occasionally erring from the path of classicism and giving a free rein to his creative streak. Fillet of smoked sturgeon is paired with a striking gin and caviar sorbet and subtly offset by asparagus, foie gras and grapefruit. Bold, daring, spot-on cuisine!	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3335374508	Bick Stuff	95 rue de Clausen	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Air conditioning	https://bickstuff.lu/accueil.html	Nessun premio	Home Cooking	3.0	€€	f	f	A family-run establishment where you will instantly feel at home. Bick is a local word which literally means ‘beak’ in English but loosely translates as ‘food’. Owners Virginie and Denis Laissy have the same goal: to serve good food in a relaxed atmosphere. Chef Denis rustles up reassuringly classical recipes, adding his own distinctive touch. We recommend the set menu.	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3334817049	Roma	5 rue Louvigny	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://roma.lu/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€€	f	t	Opened in 1950, Roma was the first Italian restaurant of Luxembourg, and it remains true to its founding authentic values. Seventy years on, little has changed and the venue, adorned with Venetian chandeliers, is still as vibrant and colourful as the food is wholesome. The pasta is homemade and oozes with crisp Mediterranean accents. Examples include pasta stuffed with seafood and a velvety vongole-type sauce or why not order a melt-in-the-mouth medallion of lamb, flanked by a gutsy gravy, mashed potatoes and scamorza? Themed festivals and a varied menu with something for everyone transform each meal into a feast.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3336729427	OiO	48 Montée de Clausen	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Terrace	https://www.oio.lu/	Nessun premio	Italian, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	The pasta is prepared last minute, stuffed with a powerful ossobuco and then coated in a velvety parmesan and gremolata sauce. All the ingredients on the menu are as fresh as the homemade pasta. This fantastic Mediterranean osteria which boasts an exquisite riverside terrace on the banks of the Alzette, invites you to an Italian feast of great delicacy. Don’t miss the Negroni or the dessert trolley!	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3330288823	Amélys	12 boulevard Royal	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-amelys.lu/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This light, airy brasserie pleases everyone. It serves tasty, scrumptious food all day long. The varied menu features classical and more modern dishes, always with the chef’s surprising and distinctive hallmark. Delicious Sunday brunch.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3339797087	Equilibrium	107 Rue de la Tour Jacob	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Air conditioning	https://equilibriumrestaurant.lu	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Baptiste Heugens boldly steps outside the box to create unexpected, yet balanced dishes, pairing his consummate knowhow with unconventional associations. The chef likes to cook fish (from Brittany) simply and purely, adding a new dimension thanks to side dishes jazzed up with fresh, spicy or tangy notes for added depth and intensity. A fascinating quest for culinary balance. We advise choosing a table downstairs for a bird’s eye view of the zinc counter where the cold dishes are prepared.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3337015242	Grünewald Chef’s Table	2 Rue des Hauts-Fourneaux	Luxembourg	Luxembourg	Air conditioning	https://gct.lu	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€€	t	f	You cannot fail but remark the green marble counter that occupies the heart of this street corner building, appointed elegantly and tastefully. The chairs are positioned around the counter to better admire the chefs at work. Clovis Degrave and his team pour their creative talents into a set menu, rife with international accents, amusing textures and rugged sauces. An example: fillet of zander underscored by a caviar-flavoured beurre blanc and a velvety sauce of samphire and girolle mushrooms. A truly fascinating global experience.	testagabriel	\N	\N
