3335603186	Richard Rivalee	62 & 64 Lorong Macalister	Malaysia	George Town	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Peranakan	5.0	$$	t	t	Fashion designer Richard Rivalee shares his passion for Nyonya culture and Peranakan food in this smart vintage joint, whose knickknacks and heritage premises are a nod to the Baba-Nyonya culture. Deceptively simple, homespun dishes are finessed with spot-on seasoning and loads of punch. Otak-otak, or savoury fish egg custard, combines a velvety texture with just the right amount of heat. To reduce food waste, most items are available in two portion sizes.	kralrosa	\N	\N
3339481296	Bali Hai Seafood Market	90 Persiaran Gurney	Malaysia	George Town	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	$$	f	t	Bali Hai has been feeding seafood lovers with the freshest critters and best quality fish for over ten years. Pick your own catch at the live fish tank by the entrance. Specify the way you want them cooked – in Teochew, Nyonya or even Thai style. The must-try “cereal prawns” are tossed in butter and milky oat powder that forms a crispy crust. Stir-fried crab with salted egg yolks that strikes a balance between umami and saltiness is not to be missed.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3331959119	The Pinn	58 Pengkalan Weld	Malaysia	George Town	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	$	f	f	The Pinn moved to this spot opposite Lee Jetty in 2023. Like the room, the menu is small but powerful, offering Malaysian-Chinese dishes, dumplings and even some Taiwanese and Indonesian titbits. Homemade mackerel fish balls are their speciality and you can order noodles on top to make it a complete meal. The food tends to be slightly on the sweet side to suit local tastebuds.	shirocky	\N	\N
