3331910451	Ratatouille	Vischmarkt 6	Netherlands	Harderwijk	Terrace	http://www.rttll.nl	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	Ratatouille is cosy and convivial, and its spacious terrace on the historical Vischmarkt is understandably very popular. Hostess Cindy and chef Gerwin have gained a loyal following in a short period of time, and that is more than deserved. Whether you order à la carte or take a punt on the surprise menu, the value for money is second to none. The versatile chef is just as likely to serve up an oven-baked fillet of red mullet with a rich white wine sauce and a zingy antiboise as a vegetarian pie with sweet and sour nuances. His cuisine is sophisticated and very much on trend, and he puts a lot of thought into his vegetable accoutrements and his choice of suppliers.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3337561095	Savour	Rijksstraatweg 143	Netherlands	Haren	Air conditioning	https://restaurantsavour.nl/	Nessun premio	Modern French	5.0	€€€	f	f	Trijntje and Jaap are making waves in this vibrant little town just outside Groningen. They go the extra mile to make their diners feel welcome, and they are always on hand to provide help or advice. Chef Jaap works with a young and enthusiastic kitchen team, and it shows: their culinary creations are well-thought-out, sophisticated and technically accomplished. For instance, they give a perfectly medium-rare venison fillet extra nuances by pairing it with beetroot and elderflower in various guises. There are some great ideas behind the set menus – prepare to be blown away!	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3338348359	't Havenmantsje	Havenplein 1	Netherlands	Harlingen	Great view,Terrace	https://www.havenmantsje.nl/	Nessun premio	Modern French	4.0	€€€	t	t	A spot in the conservatory is an absolute must when you come to this restaurant in a converted courthouse – the view of the water and the passing boats is magnificent! The restaurant is open throughout the day, so you can come for lunch, high tea or dinner. The chef skilfully navigates his way between classic and modern culinary traditions. For instance, he won't do too much to a steak tartare, but then he will conjure up a vegetarian dish based on roasted fennel and an apple jus. Be sure to check out the Asian-inspired appetisers.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3333347509	Red Orchids	Zandvoortselaan 139	Netherlands	Heemstede	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.redorchids.nl	Nessun premio	Asian, Fusion	3.0	€€€	t	f	If you have a hard time making decisions, we suggest you head to this intimate, trendy restaurant where the menu brings together Japanese, Chinese, Thai and Indonesian specialities. The chef always manages to add just the right dose of spices, creating dishes full of rich flavours and crisp textures. Subtle Asian cuisine at reasonable prices.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3336405858	Landgoed Groenendaal	Groenendaal 3	Netherlands	Heemstede	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.landgoedgroenendaal.nl/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	What a magnificent location! Set in the beautiful Groenendaal forest, this former coach house exudes luxury and boasts a terrace that is among the loveliest in the region. The chef likes to draw on the finest ingredients when devising his set menus (one of which is vegetarian). Diners can therefore indulge in a rich terrine of foie gras as well as a carrot dish prepared with miso, pumpkin and yellow curry. This fresh and unfussy take on authentic flavours never disappoints.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3331271215	Zazie	ul. Józefa 34	Poland	Krakow	Air conditioning	https://www.zaziebistro.pl/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	€€	t	t	In the city's historic Jewish quarter of Kazimierz, you’ll find this busy little bistro with a bustling atmosphere that belies its residential location. Ask for a table in the characterful cellar, which mixes French memorabilia with brick and stone walls. The Gallic influence continues into the cooking, with dishes like beef Bourguignon and classic onion soup with Gruyère cheese among the gutsy and generously sized options on the menu.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3338118557	Brasserie Mijn Streek	Bongerd 18	Netherlands	Heerlen	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.mijn-streek.nl/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	t	f	Cold or hot dishes, whether to share with your dining companions or go solo, to opt for one of the many vegetarian options or plump for fish or meat… In this convivial brasserie on the fifth floor of the Glaspaleis, there are plenty of choices to be made. Brace yourself for an international culinary adventure that takes in ceviche, ravioli, strawberry Romanoff and many other mouth-watering treats. A visit to the Schunck Museum in the same building is a must if you visit the area.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3337170775	Kasteel Ter Worm	Terworm 5	Netherlands	Heerlen	Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.terworm.nl/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary, Asian Influences	5.0	€€€	t	t	This 14C castle is brimming with character, and a meal here promises an experience beyond compare. With its wooden floors, medieval paintings and old stone walls, the setting couldn't be more enchanting. The waterside terrace overlooking the verdant surroundings is an absolute delight! Dave Beckers's approach is refreshingly modern and his sophisticated creations frequently feature flavour profiles based on koji, yuzu and koshi. For instance, he adds extra depth to his lamb fillet and crispy braised lamb neck by incorporating powdered seaweed into the potato mousseline and kombu into the rich lamb jus. This is easy-to-enjoy cuisine that also pushes boundaries. An overnight stay in the castle makes for the ultimate grand finale.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3330735386	Nastrium	Mierloseweg 130	Netherlands	Helmond	Car park,Terrace	https://www.nastrium.nl/	Nessun premio	Asian Influences, World Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	(Temporary move to Paradijslaan 2-8 in Eindhoven) Two very different culinary traditions come together in this elegant villa, which is also home to the private Gani dining room. Here, chef Djailany’s Indian origins add spice to traditional French cuisine, with foie gras and langoustines served alongside ingredients such as soya and kombu, resulting in harmonious dishes full of subtle and exotic flavours.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3338281597	De Rozario	Markt 213	Netherlands	Helmond	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.derozario.nl/	Nessun premio	Creative, Asian Contemporary	4.0	€€€	t	f	With its street art-inspired decor and laid-back atmosphere, this restaurant couldn't be more hip. The quirky and creative self-taught chef fuses French culinary tradition with Indonesian influences. His wonderfully hot and spicy hot-and-cold rendang is a signature dish. But he just as deftly elevates sea bass fillet with grated Belper Knolle cheese and a rich jus seasoned with tom kha kai herbs. Jermain de Rozario is always on the hunt for unconventional flavours and is accompanied on his quest by an expert sommelier with a rock 'n' roll edge.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3338144439	Dudockx Bar & Kitchen	Vreelandseweg 50	Netherlands	Hilversum	Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://dudockx.nl/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€€	f	f	Architect Dudok is the designer behind this trendy 1930s pavilion. Each table overlooks the Hilversumse kanaal, which really is something to behold as you sit on the gorgeous terrace. The resolutely modern cuisine shows a preference for organic and local produce, yet remains down to earth. This is the place to come if you want an original take on wonton or a perfectly cooked cut of meat with an elegant sauce. The restaurant also rents out boats!	shirocky	\N	\N
3332639519	De Hinde	't Oost 4	Netherlands	Hindeloopen	Great view,Terrace	https://www.dehinde.nl/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Harmen Ligthart has converted his grandfather's café into a cosy restaurant with an endearing and authentic soul. The view over the IJsselmeer (also from the two luxury guestrooms) is truly stunning! A stroll through the village and down by the boats is a must. Whether you opt for fish or game, you can rest assured that the ingredients are locally sourced and that the classic sense of generosity is adhered to. The pâté and fine Riesling wines are firm favourites here.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
