3335574908	Curiosa by Jean-Georges	Four Seasons Hotel	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.fourseasons.com/doha/dining/restaurants/curiosa-by-jean-georges/	Nessun premio	Latin American	5.0	﷼﷼﷼	f	t	The eponymous Jean-Georges is none other than the world-famous Vongerichten, who has brought a sassy Latino vibe to the elegant Four Seasons Hotel. Ask for a table in the bar for the Gulf views, and then sit back and wait for the band to start playing as you enjoy a sparkling selection of Latin and globally influenced dishes. That could mean a classic ceviche, tacos and tortillas, sizzling shrimp or crispy fried chicken. End with the ‘Salted Impossible Flan’ or the vast passion fruit sundae and you’ll be gliding out happy.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3335747177	La Méditerranée Robuchon	Four Seasons Resort	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.lamediterraneerobuchondoha.com/about-us/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood	3.0	﷼﷼﷼﷼	t	f	As the name suggests, France and the Med are celebrated on the seafood-based menu here. Start with a shrimp or octopus skewer, or perhaps a ceviche or tiradito of seabream or sea bass. Then see if you can agree with your partner for one of the sharing dishes or indeed a whole fish, priced by weight and cooked to your liking^ failing that, go for the signature lobster spaghetti which will certainly help you feel transported to the south of France. Ask for a table on the terrace with its wonderfully far-reaching shoreline and city skyline views.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3331556489	Bayt Sharq	Al Doha Gardens	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.instagram.com/baytsharq.qa/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	5.0	﷼	f	f	This characterful, restored Al Khulaifi house is around 100 years old and even has its own little museum^ if you want a glimpse of Old Doha, this is where to come. It’s located just off the Corniche and offers a variety of seating options: in the restaurant or on its veranda, in the gardens or even in a cabin. The classic and authentic Qatari dishes are brimming with flavour and generosity, from mutabbel or majboos to delicious saffron mahalabia^ whatever you choose, the only certainty is that you won’t leave hungry!	novakmonica	\N	\N
3336432246	Desert Rose Café	Ground Floor	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access	https://nmoq.org.qa/en/visit/desert-rose-cafe/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	4.0	﷼	t	f	Beaming smiles greet you from behind the counter at this easy-going and friendly spot tucked away in the National Museum of Qatar. When it comes to ordering, start off with their arancini or ‘Dynamite shrimps’ then go traditional with keema, khabees and Chef Noof’s madrouba that’s made using a special recipe – and no visit here will be complete without the date cake. A great strawberry mojito or a cup from their vast array of speciality coffees will set you up nicely for your museum visit.	donatidiego	\N	\N
3338996099	Saasna	Barahat Msheireb street	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.instagram.com/saasnaqatar/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	3.0	﷼﷼	t	t	The dream of the late Sheikha Ahmed Al Meer – author of 'The Art of Qatari Cooking' – lives on through the proud and caring team who run this restaurant and who are determined to continue her desire to preserve and celebrate the country’s culinary past and to bring it into the 21st century. The traditional cooking is fresh and full of flavour^ start your visit with a samosa or the Saasna salad, then the majboos is a must for main course and the wonderful date ice cream is a great way to finish.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3333263430	SAWA by Sanad	Mohammed Bin Jassim Street	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://sanaddoha.com/en/sawa-restaurant/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	5.0	﷼﷼﷼	f	t	The first floor of a private members’ club in Doha’s rejuvenated downtown plays host to this impressively chic dining room. The menu offers a showcase of contemporary Levantine dishes, many of which are perfect for sharing. The kitchen takes things up a notch in the evening, including some dishes served from the trolley for an extra dash of theatre. You don’t need to be a member to eat here, but you’ll be tempted to join up after you’ve experienced the caring service and delicious food.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3339262048	SMAT	Oriental Pearl	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Valet parking	https://www.instagram.com/smatrestaurant/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	3.0	﷼﷼﷼	t	t	At the southern end of the Corniche sits this wonderfully decorated restaurant that features bold colours and an opulent edge, with comfortable sofa seating and polished tiled flooring adding to its appeal. The authentic Qatari and Gulf State dishes are generous in size, eye-catching in looks and yield refined flavours and textures. You could start your meal with crisp Mzatara Samboussa, then move onto one of the particularly good lamb main courses, before the Donafa Ain Helaitan provides a satisfying conclusion.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3332401521	Baron	Unit 46	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://eatdrinkbaron.com/pages/dear-doha	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern, Fusion	4.0	﷼﷼	f	f	Baron is sister to a well-known restaurant of the same name in Beirut and occupies a striking, pastel-pink property in the recently redeveloped Mina District, home of the Old Port. It’s a large place with exposed pipework adding a contemporary feel and an open kitchen that’s very much part of the room. The menu offers a wide choice of what they describe as ‘Mediterranean fusion’, which means the addition of some North African and even Asian influences. Dishes like capellini with crab and shrimp toum are generous in size and ideal for sharing.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3339733247	Dar Yema	Doha Oasis	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning	https://daryemarestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Moroccan	3.0	﷼﷼	f	t	Step into this beautiful and spacious dining room and you’ll be warmly welcomed by the gracious team. North African Maghrebian cuisine is the appeal here, with a particular focus on Morocco. Homemade breads are plentiful and delicious, with highlights of the traditional menu including Moroccan tagines – the chicken tagine with lemon and olives is particularly good – and Algerian boureks. The kitchen puts plenty of heart into the cooking and the team even make their own ice cream to satisfy sweet-toothed diners.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3331525899	Coya	W Doha Hotel & Residences	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.coyarestaurant.com/doha/	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	﷼﷼﷼﷼	t	t	Buzzy, colourful and lively, with a hint of Aztec style, this restaurant has all the ingredients for a fun night out. Take a seat in the moody and intimate split-level dining room, where you can see the chefs working in an open kitchen on a range of Peruvian-inspired dishes designed for sharing. Quality ingredients run throughout and there’s a freshness and vibrancy to the flavours. Engaging, attentive service completes the picture.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3331051184	Hock Hai (Hong Lim) Curry Chicken Noodle	Bedok Interchange Hawker Centre	Singapore	Singapore			Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	t	t	The curry broth may be only mildly hot, but its flavours are deep. The chicken is tender^ potato and tofu puffs soak up the sauces. Besides curry, there is satay chicken served on your choice from three varieties of noodles.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3339673903	La Mar by Gastón Acurio	Street 900	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://doha.intercontinental.com/la-mar/	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	﷼﷼﷼	f	t	Come for the beachfront location, stay for the vibrant Peruvian dishes at this whitewashed restaurant within the grounds of the InterContinental Hotel. Gastón Acurio is a fine ambassador for Peruvian food and all bases are covered here, from ceviches to anticuchos. The colourful, rustic dishes deliver plenty of punchy flavours and are perfect for sharing. As you sit and soak up the lively atmosphere, you’ll be struck by what a fun night out it all is. And the wallet-friendly prices make it even more appealing.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3331697281	TONO	6 La Croisette	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://linktr.ee/TONOQatar	Nessun premio	Peruvian, Japanese Contemporary	5.0	﷼﷼﷼	f	f	This restaurant’s narrow ground-floor entrance belies the glitzy, capacious dining room you’re greeted with two floors up. For wonderful waterfront views, you can also try to secure a table on the enviable terrace. The Nikkei cuisine, curated by international chef Akira Back, is a worthy match for the glamorous surroundings^ the ‘prawn cigar’ will raise a smile, while the classic sea bass ceviche should always be ordered. The smart service team are chatty and alert. Look out too for the weekly offers.	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
