3335734698	Chicago Rare	127 Porto Arabia Drive	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.chicagoraredoha.com/	Nessun premio	Steakhouse	3.0	﷼﷼﷼	t	f	If you’re craving a steak with all the trimmings, a glossy lamb shank, enormous crab legs or a fine lump crab cake then this restaurant within the Four Seasons Hotel is where to come. The Josper oven and grill are used to great effect and desserts also go all in, with the likes of ‘Campfire Alaska’^ you’ll certainly leave feeling comfortably satisfied. Live jazz adds to the Chicago atmosphere, while the team channel the Blues Brothers in their look and zip around the room providing attentive service.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3331542270	Na Ćošku	Beogradska 37	Serbia	Belgrade		https://www.nacosku.rs/	Nessun premio	Balkan, International	3.0	€€	f	f	Situated to the east of the city just outside the historic centre, this restaurant boasts an intimate ambience that comes as a surprise when compared to its exterior. The dining room has the feel of a French bistro, with small tables, background music (often French), and a few cubby-holes that are perfect for couples. The cuisine has solid roots in Balkan tradition, featuring traditional soups and stews, such as lamb in white wine served with mashed potato and seasonal vegetables, various fresh pastas and vegetarian options such as vegan curry with chickpeas, sweet potatoes and green beans.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3339557720	Klub Književnika by Branko Kisic	Francuska 7	Serbia	Belgrade	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://klubknjizevnika.rs/?lang=enhttps://klubknjizevnika.rs/?lang=en	Nessun premio	Balkan, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The young chef at this long-established restaurant popular with locals and tourists alike has been at the helm since 2019. Here, guests can choose to eat in a winter garden or in the dining room, where there’s often live music during the colder months. The menu features classic favourites, such as the Krempita dessert which has been served here since the restaurant opened in 1946, and traditional Serbian specialties (there’s a 25-minute wait for the savoury Gibanica dish), with the occasional interesting, personalised touch and a focus on careful presentation. Since its opening at the end of the Second World War, the restaurant has served as a gathering spot for writers, journalists, and politicians. It continues to host cultural events, including exhibitions and concerts. Careful attention is also paid to sustainable practices such as reducing food waste.	leonoscar	\N	\N
