3338983333	Crystal Jade Golden Palace	The Paragon	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.crystaljade.com/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	f	Opened in 2002, this is the most comfortable branch of this restaurant group and the only one which specialises in Teochew dishes, like cold crab and sugar-coated yam. Look out too for the Cantonese barbecue meat and assorted seafood dishes^ more contemporary offerings include chilled foie gras with sake and roasted suckling pig with black truffle. Their wine cellar includes a good international selection.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3337873358	Imperial Treasure Super Peking Duck (Paragon)	Paragon Shopping Centre	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.imperialtreasure.com/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	Considered the crown jewel of the group, this place stocks over 3 000 Peking ducks a month, yet still tends to sell out, so be sure to pre-order yours when booking your table. The restaurant is divided into three rooms and the roasted duck – a must-try with crispy skin and succulent meat – is carved tableside. Another signature dish is the velvety poached fish in shrimp stock on crispy rice^ the roast pork and slow-boiled soups are also worth trying.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3330582998	Jiang-Nan Chun	Four Seasons Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.fourseasons.com/singapore/dining/restaurants/jiang_nan_chun/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$$	t	f	This exquisite space, reached via a marble staircase, is warm and welcoming, with heavy leather chairs that are especially comfortable. The kitchen team excels in barbecue meats, double-boiled soups and seafood dishes that use the freshest ingredients of the best quality. Try wok-fried Australian beef tenderloin with portobello mushrooms. Set menus are a great way to sample the popular hits all at once.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3338059515	Majestic	Marina One	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://restaurantmajestic.com/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	f	t	Laid out beneath a glass roof, the airy dining area overlooks a garden. The food, which draws on modern techniques and time-honoured traditions, is exquisite in both taste and appearance. The claypot chicken with glutinous rice wine, ginger and wood ear fungus boasts silky, free-range meat and spellbinding aromas. The business clientele can opt for items in individual servings. Booking a week ahead recommended.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3335674642	Shang Palace	Shangri-La Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.shangri-la.com/singapore/shangrila/dining/restaurants/shang-palace/	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$$	t	f	With a graceful dining room reminiscent of a Chinese garden, Shang Palace serves an extensive menu dominated by old-time Cantonese classics that are hard to find elsewhere, such as grilled chicken liver and pork fat skewers, and deep-fried pork fat medallions stuffed with crabmeat. Order the deep-fried whole boneless chicken stuffed with glutinous rice one day ahead and ask the servers about the slow-boiled soups that exude rich deep flavours.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3330428048	Tunglok Heen	Hotel Michael	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.tunglokheen.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	t	f	Clever lighting, dark wood and shades of red lend this modern Chinese restaurant a slick, stylish feel. Amidst traditional recipes, novel dishes also feature on the menu. Either way, the food is always meticulously plated. Don’t miss the fish bone and fish maw soup, double-boiled with chicken and pork for six hours. Chilli crab served in a casserole boasts firm, flavoursome meat. Order deep-fried buns to mop up the knockout sauce.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3339192944	Wah Lok	Carlton Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	http://www.carltonhotel.sg	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	f	f	A loyal clientele has made this comfortable, classically decorated Cantonese restaurant their own. The chef was born in Guangzhou but really developed his culinary skills and honed his craft in Hong Kong. His Cantonese dishes range from banquet delicacies like abalone and bird’s nest soup to seafood dishes such as steamed fish. There are also Cantonese roast meats, claypot dishes and home-style items like steamed minced pork with salted fish.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3337633779	Yan Ting	The St. Regis Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.yantingrestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	f	f	Since the name translates as ‘Banquet Court’, it's no surprise to find a very comfortable space, ideal for impressing visitors and friends. The head chef has extensive experience when it comes to traditional dishes, especially Cantonese barbecue and double-boiled soups. Try his crispy roast pork belly for the ultimate indulgence. He's also an expert at preparing live fish – choose from 11 cooking styles. At lunch, don't miss his Hong Kong-style dim sum.	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3339380470	Min Jiang at Dempsey	7A & 7B Dempsey Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.goodwoodparkhotel.com/dining/min-jiang-dempsey	Nessun premio	Cantonese, Sichuan	5.0	$$	f	t	Amidst lush greenery, the one-storey colonial structure houses an airy dining room done up in a yellow, gold and green palette, boasting floor-to-ceiling windows, wood details and rattan furniture. The menu is Cantonese and Sichuanese with a touch of finesse and subtlety. Must-try items include turbot fish two ways, Beijing duck grilled in a wood-fire oven and various dim sum. There are also many good choices for vegetarians.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3334919179	Yì By Jereme Leung	Raffles Arcade	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	http://www.yi-restaurant.com.sg	Nessun premio	Chinese Contemporary	3.0	$$	t	f	The chef honed his remarkable skills while working in China for many years. He returned to Singapore and opened Yi – the Chinese word for art and craftsmanship, hence the fancy dining room adorned in exquisite paper art and the food that reflects eclectic influences from all over China. Steamed free range chicken in herbal broth impresses by its umami and mild herbal aftertaste. Also check out the seasonal menu bursting with creative twists.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3339705797	Bar-Roque Grill	165 Tanjong Pagar Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.stefanandnico.com/	Nessun premio	European	4.0	$$	t	f	The Alsace-born chef takes diners on a culinary journey to his homeland with authentic regional specialties such as choucroute garnie and tarte flambée aux escargots. International dishes are also popular, like Malaysian rotisserie free-range chicken and a selection of beefsteaks dry aged in-house and chargrilled to perfection. Service is attentive and helpful. Start or end the night with a drink on the terrace or at the bar.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3331362255	Brasserie Astoria	Victoria Concert Hall	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking	https://www.brasserieastoria.sg/	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	5.0	$$	f	t	An outpost of its namesake in Stockholm, this is the brainchild of the Swedish owner-chef Björn Frantzén. Nestled in the historical Victoria Concert Hall (1800s), its retro glamour complements the chef's new spin on brasserie classics, some with trolley or tableside service. Try the råraka, a Swedish potato cake topped with vendace roe, crème fraîche, chives and red onion. Toast Astoria with prawn, king crab and wasabi aioli is also unmissable.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3337841903	Ce Soir	#01-03	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park	http://cesoir.com.sg	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$$	t	t	Ce Soir wins kudos not only for its impossibly romantic floral theme and everything botanical, but also because of its deftly crafted French fare with strong Asian notes. Every course of both the lunch set and dinner tasting menus is visually stunning: like a garden on a plate, even the flowers are edible. The seafood stands out in particular. Everything down to the bread and the mignardises are made from scratch in-house.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3332221138	Cure	21 Keong Saik Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.curesingapore.com/	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$$	t	f	Inspired by bistro culture, chef-owner Walsh has devised a Nua Irish tasting menu that riffs on his Celtic roots and draws on local influences. The menu ranges from absolutely purist takes on the classics to small plates with playful touches. To a soundtrack of Irish rock, learn about exceptional homegrown ingredients from the map on the table, as you indulge in dishes informed by the history and wisdom of the Emerald Isle.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3330709419	Gordon Grill	Goodwood Park Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.goodwoodparkhotel.com/dining/gordon-grill	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$	f	t	A feature of Goodwood Park hotel since 1963, the restaurant is famed for its meat trolley service which is wheeled over to each table. Along with the meat and plentiful supplies of seafood from the grill, you can expect French-inspired classic dishes like lobster bisque, braised beef cheek, or Crêpes Suzette flambéed tableside. It’s a good choice for a quiet business lunch, a romantic dinner or weekend family outings.	shirocky	\N	\N
3338105340	Lolla	22 Ann Siang Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.lolla.com.sg	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	5.0	$$$	f	t	The turquoise tiled façade sets nicely against the faux-industrial interior. Seasonal Mediterranean dishes in generous portions for sharing are served by the chefs themselves. Flavours are bold and hearty, with occasional Asian touches. Ask for counter seats to see the chefs in action, or sit at the communal table in the basement which can be reserved for private parties. Only seven- or nine-course tasting menus are served on Friday and Saturday nights.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3335347492	Mag's Wine Kitchen	Kesa House	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace	http://www.magswinekitchen.com	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$	t	t	Two things catch your attention when you set foot in this long-standing household name – the small walk-in cellar and the bustling open kitchen, where chef-owner Mag can be seen working with her team. Octopus with tomato and chorizo coulis is a decadent start to the meal, followed by classics such as risotto with Boston lobster: for years a staple on the menu, it keeps regulars coming back. The perfect wine-and-dine spot for a Friday night out.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3330583595	Hoe Kee Kitchen	Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre	Singapore	Singapore	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	$	f	f	Steamed chicken rice with tender meat and flavourful rice is popular. Other options include reasonably priced char siew and roasted pork rice.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3333907267	Vue	OUE Bayfront	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.vue.com.sg	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	f	Aptly named after the French word for ‘view’, this romantic restaurant boasts one of the most stunning vistas of Marina Bay. Even the ceiling is designed to emanate light without casting reflections on the glass panes. The menu shows the culinary vision of the young head chef, with the four-course chef’s tasting menu being the most popular choice where diners may choose from a number of interesting options. Steaks and risotto are great for sharing. Executive set lunch is popular.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3335999178	Claudine	39C Harding Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://www.claudinerestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	$$	t	f	From chef Julien Royer of Odette fame comes a classic French brasserie, which he named after his mother. It’s housed in a lovely 1930s converted chapel, with an open kitchen at one end and a bar at the other. Those with a fondness for comforting French classics will find the rollcall of favourites very appealing, from onion soup to vol-au-vents and baba au rhum. If you’re willing to share, then go for the bouillabaisse or the pepper steak flambéed at your table.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3330271522	Fleur de Sel	#01-01	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.fleurdesel.com.sg/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	$$	f	f	In this stylish eatery with a bar and an open kitchen, you’ll find the eponymous artisanal French salt on each table – but you won’t need it thanks to the owner-chef’s spot-on sense of seasoning. At this ‘bistro de luxe’ he delivers classical French cuisine with a light, modern spin – making it easy to save room for his signature Baba. Two set menus - we recommend the tasting menu for a global experience.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3331383581	Maison Boulud	The Shoppes at Marina Bay Sands	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking	http://mbssg.com/maisonboulud-sg-fb	Nessun premio	French	4.0	$$	f	t	With executive chef Rémy Carmignani on board, Maison Boulud is located in the shopping mall at Marina Bay Sands. The patio on the upper level boasts stunning views – perfect for al fresco dining. The elegant main dining room (lower level) has an oversize wine cellar displaying impressive vintages. The menu is defined by classic French cuisine, with more sophisticated plating, as opposed to bistro-style fare. There is also their signature seafood platter.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3337810524	Nicolas	10 Teck Lim Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking	http://www.restaurantnicolas.com	Nessun premio	French	3.0	$$	f	t	The eponymous French chef has been quietly going about his business in this comfy and intimate little gem for some years now. Choose the Tasting menu to best experience his cooking, underpinned by classical French techniques and made with top-quality ingredients, like langoustines from New Zealand and pigeon from Brittany. Diners can watch the chefs at work in the kitchen through the glass wall. Don’t forget to check out the wine collection in the small walk-in cellar.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3335035783	Béni	Mandarin Gallery	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.beni-sg.com	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	t	The small, elegant restaurant boasts a minimalist décor, so as to keep the spotlight on its exquisite French cooking with a Japanese twist. Top-quality ingredients from France and Japan are transformed here, thanks to well-honed skills and meticulous attention to detail. The set menus change according to the availability of ingredients, such as seafood dishes are adapted to the catch of the day. Check with the sommelier for unusual choices not shown on the wine list.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3334655065	Roia	Singapore Botanic Gardens (Nassim Gate entrance)	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.roia.sg/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	$$$	t	f	Not only can you feast your eyes on the lush greenery, you can also taste the herbs and edible flowers grown in the garden and picked minutes before serving. In a refurbished historic edifice, chef-owner Priyam Chatterjee serves two tasting menus that are updated quarterly and feature modern French fare rooted in tradition and exquisitely plated. The top-notch produce comes from around the world and each course tells a story about its source.	longoethan	\N	\N
3332042247	Putien (Kitchener Road)	127 Kitchener Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking	http://www.putien.com	Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	$$	t	t	This first branch of the chain known for its friendly service opened in 2000. The menu showcases Fujian classics, with small plates and noodles being the highlights. Try the bian rou (Fujian wonton soup) – the translucent skin is made with pork pounded over 10,000 times into a paste. The lor mee, topped with an impressive array of seafood, is also popular. Don't miss the seasonal offerings, some using rare ingredients from the city of Putian.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3335089320	Mustard	32 Race Course Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning	https://www.mustardsingapore.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	$$	t	f	This halal restaurant specialising in Bengali and Punjabi cuisines is christened Mustard because the spice is used extensively in both cuisines. For instance, mustard oil is often used in place of coconut oil in Bengali cooking. Try their maacher cutlet – deep-fried fish croquettes served with a house-made fermented mustard sauce called Kashundi, which tastes strong and spicy. All food is made to order, but is so worth the wait.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3330168618	Zaap	6	Taiwan	Taipei	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	$$	f	t	With 10-plus years of experience in Thai cooking, the owner-chef insists on making all sauces and condiments from scratch. He doesn't hold back on the chillies, so taste first before dousing your food with sauces! Certain items, including the signature chargrilled Thai river prawns, and banana roti, need to be pre-ordered. The prawns are bursting with rich, creamy roe^ the flesh is springy and savoury. The house-made dip is the icing on the cake.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3331932694	Revolver	56 Tras Street	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	http://www.revolver.com.sg	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	$$$	t	t	Its name is a pun on how cooking revolves around the charcoal grill, brazier and tandoor. Whether you sit at the counter or in a booth, the chefs put on a show that is visible from all seats. Three tasting menus and a vegetarian menu are offered.  Dishes are rooted in different regions of India, but are reimagined and reborn over coals and fire. The distinctive smoky flavour  and layering of spices works magic, resulting in a delicate balance.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3337880835	Hokkien Man Hokkien Mee	Blk 19	Singapore	Singapore	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	f	f	As its name suggests, this stall specialises in Hokkien fried noodles in a garlicky broth made with prawn heads. Besides the typical toppings of prawns and squid, you may order others, like egg or abalone, at an additional cost.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3335835717	Tambuah Mas (Orchard)	Paragon	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.tambuahmas.com.sg/	Nessun premio	Indonesian	4.0	$$	f	f	Since 1981, the Indonesian chefs at Tambuah Mas have been making authentic home-style dishes from Padang, Sulawesi and Java. Family recipes with delicate blends of spices and precise preparations are closely guarded secrets, passed down over generations. The signature tahu telor (deep-fried egg-coated tofu cubes in a dark sweet sauce) boasts crispy skin and perfect briny-sweetness. Always round off a meal here with a cendol.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3337997934	Bam!	38-40 Tras Street	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.bam.sg	Nessun premio	Innovative	5.0	$$	f	t	Gone are the days when European dishes had to be paired with wine. Sake can complement any food when chosen wisely. Bam! champions a revolutionary way of appreciating the Japanese rice wine with exquisite modern culinary creations. The sommelier can also help you pick a wine. Though it proclaims itself as an omakase restaurant, you can also order à la carte. Ask for a counter seat to stay close to the action in the kitchen.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3336409680	Ibid	18 North Canal Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	http://www.restaurantibid.com	Nessun premio	Innovative	4.0	$$$	t	t	After winning a popular TV cooking contest, lawyer-turned-chef Woo opened Ibid in a remodelled shophouse. The passionate chef gets hands-on in every part of his venture, overlooking the kitchen, greeting guests warmly and serving dishes himself. French techniques and Asian twists are manifested in every course of the varied and exciting set menu. Prized counter seats are the best spots to interact with the chefs and watch the alchemy unfold.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3331200390	Imbue	32 Keong Saik Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://imbue.sg/	Nessun premio	Innovative	5.0	$$$	f	t	In this heritage shophouse updated with an open kitchen, the dishes are essentially European – but Asian ingredients and taste profiles lend a unique twist. The five- or eight-course dinner menu features Shaoxing-infused abalone from Jeju island, wrapped in kelp and ginger and steamed, served with ginkgo chawanmushi and accompanied by a shiitake reduction and ham jus. The sticky-sweet Malai bread with ginseng honey butter also delivers layers of flavours.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3331808482	Tippling Club	38 Tanjong Pagar Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	http://tipplingclub.com	Nessun premio	Innovative	4.0	$$$	t	t	If you thought fine dining had to be formal, think again. Ryan Clift's discreetly signed flagship restaurant has a casual clubbing vibe. A spot at the counter is best for watching the chefs in action^ a table in the dimly lit dining area offers more privacy. The tasting menu features well-crafted, nicely plated dishes made exclusively with ingredients from Japan. The delicious cocktails inspired by songs from different decades are a fun touch.	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3338738432	Open Farm Community	130E Minden Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.openfarmcommunity.com/	Nessun premio	International	4.0	$$	t	t	Adjacent to the Botanic Garden, this verdantly set glasshouse combines an urban farm and dining concept. The founder-chef advocates an eco-friendly philosophy and therefore designed a mostly plant-based menu. Produce may be sourced from local artisan farms as well as Malaysia, but the food shows eclectic technique and flavours from around the world. The menu offers vegan, vegetarian and gluten-free options to cater to different dietary needs.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3339768252	Buko Nero	126 Tanjong Pagar Road	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.bukonero.com.sg/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$	t	t	Diners flock to this small neighbourhood joint and it’s easy to understand why: the bubbly, charming hostess works seamlessly with her husband chef from Veneto, who in turn delivers simple, delicious Italian fare with subtle Asian twists. Try his tau kwa tower – an appetising mix of sautéed Italian-style greens and Singaporean dried tofu salad in a tangy Asian dressing. Hand-made pasta is another highlight, as are the weekly specials.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3333815474	Fiamma	Capella Hotel	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://capellahotels.com/en/capella-singapore/dining/fiamma	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$$	f	t	Eagerly anticipated by gourmets, this dining concept by the celebrated chef Mauro Colagreco opened in the ultra-luxury beach resort. The rustic chic room comes complete with an open kitchen, wood-fired oven and a terrace overlooking the pool and garden. The menu sees a good range of Italian classics, especially those from the South of the country. Start your meal with seabream carpaccio, followed by house-made pasta, and tiramisu for two to share.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3335538350	Garibaldi	#01-02	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://garibaldi.com.sg	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	$$	f	f	Ossobuco, costoletta alla Milanese and tiramisu are some of the signature dishes here, at one of the city’s best known Italian restaurants. The affable owner, though, wants everyone to be able to find their favourite dish which is why he offers such a large, all-encompassing menu. The impressive wine list, featuring around 7000 labels, is another feature for which this cosy and contemporary-styled restaurant is celebrated.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3336541390	Osteria Mozza	Hilton Orchard	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://osteriamozza.com.sg/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	$$	f	f	After a hiatus, the first Asian outpost of celebrity chef Nancy Silverton’s famed establishment Osteria Mozza reopened, now in a modern, rustic setting with a lively and inviting vibe. The small lunch menu features antipasti, salads, pizza and house-made pasta. The dinner menu steps up a gear to include her signature mozzarella dishes and other Italian specialties. The impressive wine list covers 280 labels from different regions of Italy.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3337443297	Solo	45 Amoy Street	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://soloristorante.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	$$	t	t	On Amoy Street where F&B outlets abound, Solo stands out with a relaxing vibe, an action-packed open kitchen and a regularly changing Italian menu that celebrates fresh, seasonal ingredients. The 5-course gourmet menu is a great way to sample some of its signature dishes, such as al dente homemade tagliolini topped with Japanese Bafun uni bursting with briny sweetness and umami. At lunch, the 3- or 4-course seasonal set offers great value.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3332627382	Hokkien Street Bak Kut Teh	Hong Lim Market and Food Centre	Singapore	Singapore			Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	$	t	f	The dark amber coloured bak kut teh from this stall is loaded in herbal goodness. Pair with pork knuckle, pork intestines, steamed fish, pork tail, pork kidney or pork liver on the side, as you prefer.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3339202221	Torno Subito	#01-02	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.tornosubitosg.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	$$	t	f	A nod to the heyday of Italian cinema, the interior takes you back to the Adriatic Riviera circa 1960s. The red-yellow-blue colour scheme is carried through from the walls to the tableware. The concept by celebrity chef Massimo Bottura involves whimsically and creatively harnessing Italian produce in signature dishes like artisan tortellini in a silky sauce made with parmigiano reggiano aged for 36 months. Stone-baked pizzas are delicious.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3338889702	La D'Oro	Mandarin Gallery	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.ladoro.sg/ladoro	Nessun premio	Italian Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	t	Rebranded in 2023, La D’oro now offers a single season-driven omakase menu that changes every two months. Hailing from Tokyo, Japan, the owner-chef Sasaki honed his skills in Italy. His ambitious, kappo-style cooking effortlessly blends Italian traditions with Japanese influences, delivering complex, original creations underpinned by modern techniques. Fresh ingredients flown in from Japan and Italy impart distinctive flavours.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3339777532	Shunsui	#01-01	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining	https://www.shunsui.sg/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	$$$	t	f	Formerly Kappo Shunsui, this atmospheric restaurant now serves three multicourse omakase menus, typically consisting of appetisers, sashimi, sushi, hot dish, main course and dessert. The interior is theatrically lit to showcase the food^ the wooden counter seats 20 diners who can chat and interact with the chefs. It goes without saying that all the ingredients are top notch^ the knife work is razor sharp and the sushi perfectly hand-pressed.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3333863773	Ushidoki Wagyu Kaiseki	#01-01	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	http://www.ushidoki.com	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	$$$$	f	f	This chef puts a new spin on classic kaiseki with two Wagyu set menus that honour a head-to-tail concept. He chooses Ozaki beef from Miyazaki, otherwise unavailable in Singapore, for its gutsy flavour. Various cuts from 32- to 36-month-old cattle are prepared in a myriad of ways to highlight their textures and umami. Most of the other ingredients are flown in from Japan to ensure authenticity. There is also an á la carte menu for add-on courses.	contimatteo	\N	\N
