3333640976	Julijana	Cesta Svobode 12	Slovenia	Bled	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.sava-hotels-resorts.com/en/sava-hoteli-bled/gastronomy/the-julijana-restaurant	Nessun premio	International	5.0	€€€	f	f	Housed in the Grand Hotel Toplice which stands amid some of the most popular landscapes in Slovenia, this restaurant boasts truly breathtaking views of Lake Bled from its dining room and its outdoor terrace. Here, the chef offers tasting menus of various lengths featuring meat and fish specialities with the occasional international influence, as well as a 4-course option (the Gorenjska selection menu) with a stronger regional focus. On the latter, the array of local ingredients is showcased via a delicious hazelnut crème brûlée served with ice-cream made from cherries soaked in Terrano liqueur.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3332827128	A3	Grad Rajhenburg	Slovenia	Brestanica	Car park	https://restavracija-a3.si/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	This restaurant, housed in the superbly restored 12C Rajhenburg castle overlooking the Sava river, takes its name from the huge inner courtyard that provides the perfect setting for an aperitif chosen from the many Slovenian sparkling wines served here. In the elegant and stylishly furnished dining room, enjoy a surprise tasting menu (4, 5, 6 or 7 courses) of modern dishes that are full of flavour – the zander with celeriac and the beef with Jerusalem artichoke are particularly delicious. The friendly staff are happy to offer tours of the castle, while the views from the outdoor terrace are truly delightful.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3338263109	Ošterija Debeluh	Trg izgnancev 7	Slovenia	Brezice	Interesting wine list	http://www.debeluh.si/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€€	f	t	Situated in inland Slovenia just a few miles from the border with Croatia, this is one of the most interesting restaurants in the region. Here, highly experienced owner-chef Jure Tomič has created an excellent network of suppliers from all over Slovenia. His meat and fish dishes are prepared with a modern, precise and technical touch that is unfussy and focuses on bringing out the full flavour of his ingredients. Traditional recipes and ingredients are reinterpreted with a personal twist: examples are the plum extract served with duck and the sweet “butter, honey and milk” dish that takes the ingredients of a typical local dessert and creates something new and original. You’ll have no problem finding the right wine to accompany your meal from the extensive wine list.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3336872540	Gostilna Vovko	Ratež 48	Slovenia	Brusnice	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://gostilna-vovko.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Comprising a bar, wine bar, restaurant and hotel, the Gostilna Vovko is a family-run business with more than 50 years of history behind it, where the traditionally furnished dining room includes a charming wood-fired stove. The cuisine is just as you would expect – authentic and regional, including dishes such as delicious local trout tartare served with horseradish and herbs, and thick, meaty pork chops which are perfect accompanied by a glass of velvety and intensely flavoured 2019 Modra Frankinja wine. The wine list pays tribute to regional labels.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3338204328	Gostilna Francl	Zagrad 77	Slovenia	Celje	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.gostilnafrancl.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Situated at the entrance to a tranquil valley, this restaurant dating back centuries now has young new managers at the helm with a focus on cuisine that has its roots in local traditions yet with a slightly modern twist. The portions are decidedly generous, with real attention paid to presentation and colour as well as substance and quality. Meat takes centre stage here, although fish dishes also feature on the menu. In summer, dine outdoors under the trees or the delightful pergola.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3331277317	Dvor Jezeršek	Zgornji Brnik 63	Slovenia	Cerklje na Gorenjskem	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.jezersek.si/en/locations/dvor-jezersek	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Situated in the quiet, bucolic village of Cerklje na Gorenjskem in the heart of the Kamnik and Savinja Alps around 40km from the Austrian border, these traditional old buildings have been converted by the Jezeršek family into a hotel with large rooms and a gourmet restaurant. The outdoor tables are particularly attractive, while the dining room has small windows allowing guests to observe the chefs at work in the kitchen. Among the desserts, don’t miss the Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake), which is served in a traditional steel pan. The restaurant also organises cookery courses and workshops on themes such as bread-making and finger food.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3337427894	Etna	Kolodvorska ulica 3/a	Slovenia	Divača	Air conditioning	https://www.etna.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Pizza	4.0	€	t	f	On its website, this modern restaurant describes itself as “the home of different flavours from the Karst region”. Its cuisine is generous and exciting, with a focus on top-quality ingredients that the chef skilfully transforms into delicious dishes. The pizzas are excellent, as are the highly recommended desserts.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3333788724	Gredič	Ceglo 9	Slovenia	Dobrovo v Brdih	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.gredic.si/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	f	To get to this imposing 17C castle, home to an elegant boutique hotel as well as this restaurant, you make your way through the delightful rolling hills of the Collio wine-producing region. The cuisine here reflects the multicultural character of the country, combining Mediterranean traditions and ingredients such as sea bass, cuttlefish and crayfish with other ingredients from Central Europe such as trout, carp and venison in imaginative dishes with a personalised touch. As this is one of Slovenia’s most important wine-producing regions, make sure you visit the vinotheque here.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3335948875	Restavracija Hotela Marina	Veliki Trg 11	Slovenia	Izola	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hotelmarina.si/sl/domov/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood	5.0	€€	f	t	Although its immediate setting may lack charm, the position of this restaurant facing the marina is delightful, with its superb sea views through its picture windows. The delicious, authentic and carefully prepared cuisine focuses on fish and seafood “straight from the sea to your plate”. Although there is an à la carte, ingredients are often subject to availability. Seafood, rock fish and pasta served with an array of original sauces are just some of the delicious classic dishes on the menu.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3333407328	Hiša Torkla	Korte 44b	Slovenia	Izola	Car park,Terrace	https://www.hisa-torkla.si	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Grills	3.0	€€	t	t	The view of the surrounding hills is one of the main attractions of this restaurant, along with the traditional open grill in the dining room. Although grilled meat dishes (Tomahawk and picanha steak, chops, fillets etc) naturally take centre stage, the menu also features first courses such as fuzi (a type of Istrian pasta) with various sauces, as well as some good raw fish options. An excellent setting in which to enjoy gourmet dining surrounded by unspoilt natural scenery.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3332281710	Špacapanova Hiša	Komen 85	Slovenia	Komen	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.spacapan.si/en/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€€	f	t	For more than 50 years, Špacapanova Hiša has been a bastion of Karst cuisine. The restaurant has been run by the Špacapan family since 1973, while its current success is largely due to son and brilliant manager Ago, who has taken the quality of the cuisine to a new level. The regional cuisine is prepared from local ingredients – staff are happy to provide information on the provenance of the ingredients and the human stories involved in their production. Depending on the time of year, don’t miss the lamb and kid, both of which are raised in the Karst and cooked in the oven, then served with cow’s milk curd ravioli. The traditions of the Karst are also alive and well in the wine cellar (the venue for tastings of wine, ham and cheese matured on site). If you’d like to prolong your stay here, the restaurant also offers a few guestrooms, some of which have been recently renovated with period furnishings.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3338228194	Kogo	Šmarska cesta 1	Slovenia	Koper	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://kogo.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Situated away from the busy tourist centre yet easily accessible by car, this restaurant is home to an elegant wine bar (on the right when you enter the building) and a modern dining room with a few designer-style features (on the left). Despite the contemporary ambience, the food at Kogo (the name is the Slovenian word for “cook”) is traditional and includes a huge selection of cheese and charcuterie (from Slovenia and further afield), followed by main courses that focus on meat (although fish dishes also feature). There’s also an impressive wine list with detailed descriptions on a tablet.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3330334977	Gostilna Krištof	Predoslje 22	Slovenia	Kranj	Car park,Terrace	https://gostilnakristof.si/en/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The Bolka family continues with their long-established tradition of hospitality in this authentic and welcoming restaurant that immediately warms the heart. The skilfully updated cuisine combines local recipes with a contemporary twist, as demonstrated by dishes such as trout tartare served with sweet and sour ginger, trout roe and a Bernese foam sauce. The menu changes with the seasons and showcases local ingredients such as Krškopolje pork, Carnolian sausage and locally farmed trout. The wine list has the same regional focus, with almost every Slovenian wine available by the glass.	shirocky	\N	\N
3339086781	Restavracija Shambala	Križevniška ulica 12	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Terrace	https://shambala.si/	Nessun premio	Asian	3.0	€	t	f	A “hidden oasis of peace, tranquillity and joy” right in the centre of Ljubljana, just a stone’s throw from the city’s bustling riverside promenade, Shambala serves Asian cuisine amid an Asian-influenced decor that is attractive without being overly decorative. The dishes on the menu (meat, fish and seafood, and vegetarian) are inspired by countries all over Asia, from Japan to Thailand and Vietnam. The desserts feature more European options such as panna cotta, which is served with a mango and date sauce that gives it a more exotic flavour.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3333823119	Breg	Breg 20	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restavracijabreg.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	f	t	Overlooking Ljubljana’s riverfront, this restaurant boasts one of the most famous and picturesque views of the city from its terrace in the summer months, while in the winter the historic building’s indoor dining rooms are equally attractive. The cuisine brings a breath of international creativity to the city, with influences from Italy, France and the Middle East in its dishes. A perfect example is the hummus served with lamb ragu, pita bread, pesto and pine nuts – a real culinary voyage around the Mediterranean!	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3336764758	Georgie Bistro	Čufarjeva ulica 5	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning	https://georgiebistro.si/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	€€	t	t	Just a stone’s throw from the heart of the historic centre, this relaxed, informal restaurant serves beautifully prepared contemporary-style dishes. Although there’s a focus on Slovenian ingredients here, the chef’s imagination is also inspired by influences from outside the country. Choose between an à la carte and tasting menus of varying lengths (three to nine courses). The pairing options include organic wines, as well as craft beers and home-made syrups. Popular for work lunches, and so very busy at lunchtime.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3333356638	PEN KLUB Restavracija	Tomšičeva ulica 12	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Terrace	https://www.kaval-group.si/pen-klub	Nessun premio	European, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Head up to the first floor to this retro-style restaurant, where you pass a welcoming lounge bar before moving into the main dining room adorned with an attractive fresco. The current managers and chef have brought the restaurant back into vogue thanks to a menu which includes some of the restaurant’s historic dishes (such as foie gras) alongside new meat and fish (both salt- and freshwater) dishes, such as the excellent trout marinated with oil and lemon and served with a dried egg yolk and green tea gel. The tiny summer terrace has just a few tables (book in advance), while the wine list features a selection of mainly regional labels.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3338282270	Landerik	Stari Trg 11	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://landerik.si/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This small restaurant on one of Ljubljana’s typical pedestrianised streets boasts a modern, minimalist-style dining room, as well as an attractive outdoor terrace from which to enjoy the views of this picturesque district in the heart of the city. To appreciate the cuisine to the full, we recommend choosing one of the tasting menus. The desserts include a lighter version of the traditional Kaiserschmarrn, featuring small portions of pancake, apricots and a truly mouthwatering vanilla cream.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3336977773	Sushimama	Wolfova ulica 12	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning	https://sushimama.si/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	€€	t	f	Situated not far from the castle and the riverside, in the city lively and pedestrianised tourist district, Sushimama serves elegant and precisely prepared Japanese dishes: sushi and sashimi, of course, in different combinations, but also soups (miso and others), tempura dishes, and cooked meat and fish options. In a simple furnished setting, the service is attentive and courteous.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3330842985	Restavracija CUBO	Šmartinska cesta 55	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.cubo.si/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Situated on the edge of the city in a district little visited by tourists, this modern restaurant dominated by a dark colour scheme serves Mediterranean-influenced yet eclectic cuisine with the occasional international flavour. The maize-crusted tuna fillet with fine vegetables and avocado is cooked to perfection – the tuna is pink and succulent and a green curry sauce adds an extra touch of character to the dish. An extensive wine list (with wines also available by the glass) adds to the appeal.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3330770236	Peti 181	Dvorni trg 1	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.peti181.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood	4.0	€€€	f	f	Although this restaurant’s excellent location is best appreciated in summer, with tables overlooking the river and charming views of the castle lit up at night, the attractive dining room also has an elegant and welcoming ambience influenced by the chef’s interior design skills. The cuisine is Mediterranean in style, with a focus on fish and seafood – the shellfish is excellent, as is the delicious grilled sea bass with buttered mashed potatoes, and the mouthwatering scampi soup with fried scampi tempura. The wines available by the glass are mainly Slovenian, although there’s also an interesting Riesling Gruss from Alsace that makes an excellent pairing with fish and seafood.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3338104636	AFTR	Nazorjeva ulica 2	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://aftr.si/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Situated in the heart of the city, AFTR is a trendy bistro with colourful, modern dining rooms and a charming outdoor space which is perfect for a slightly cooler dining experience away from the busy riverside promenade. The cuisine here, which includes Mediterranean dishes such as taramasalata and Central European options such as suckling pig with kiwi and fennel, is fresh and tasty, skilfully combining delicate ingredients with more intense flavours. Instead of the usual division of courses, the menu has sections dedicated to cold dishes, hot dishes and desserts. The small wine selection includes a number of wines also available by the glass. Our inspector recommends the Vitvoska di Kukanja, an organic white from the Karst which both fresh and mineral.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3333201546	JB Restavracija	Miklošičeva cesta 19	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://jb-slo.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	This restaurant, named after owner-chef Janez Bratovž, the father of modern Slovenian cuisine, occupies a Secessionist building dating from the 1920s and designed by architect Jože Plečnik. The building provides an intriguing setting for Bratovž’s cuisine, where the chef, assisted by his son Tomaž in the kitchen and the rest of his family front of house, combines regional ingredients and flavours with classic influences. Don’t miss the iconic JB ravioli (a permanent feature on the menu), which are stuffed with cheese and pistachio and served with goose liver and a veal jus. Bratovž has also published a book detailing his philosophy, his ingredients and forty of his most popular recipes.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3332867319	B-Restaurant	Slovenska Cesta 59	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.brestaurant.si/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, International	5.0	€€	f	t	This rooftop restaurant at the InterContinental hotel boasts stunning 180° views of the historic centre and castle through its floor-to-ceiling windows, especially at night when the illuminated castle is surrounded by the lights of the city. Inside the restaurant, the contemporary design and open-view kitchen provide the setting for a choice of dishes which is as extensive as the views. As a result, the restaurant has built a well-deserved reputation for its international cuisine, alongside Slovenian specialities. We particularly enjoyed the fresh red prawn ceviche served with a mango sorbet that enhanced the freshness of the prawns, and an excellent tapioca quail with green asparagus and a delicate jus. Before dinner, we recommend a cocktail in the adjacent bar to admire the views of the other half of the city!	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3334194926	Altrokè	Stari trg 19	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://altroke.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€	f	t	Inspired by Istria and the Mediterranean, the meat and fish dishes served at Altrokè are enhanced by the use of ingredients such as fruit, aromatic herbs and olive oil which are grown or produced on the restaurant’s own property in Plavje near Koper. The ambience here is pleasantly rustic, with exposed stonework and a brick-vaulted ceiling which blend in well with this old district of the city.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3335118580	Gostilna AS	Čopova ulica 5a	Slovenia	Ljubljana	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.gostilnaas.si/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	t	t	At this restaurant located in the centre of Ljubljana, choose between a dining room with a typical vaulted ceiling and, in summer, a delightful outdoor area surrounded by greenery with views of the castle. The traditional menu here features Slovenian meat dishes, with a particular focus on grilled options (such as the Cowboy steak of local beef which we particularly enjoyed), fish from the Adriatic, and home-made pasta.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3331809612	Restavracija Sedem	Cafova 7	Slovenia	Maribor	Air conditioning	https://sedem.si/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	f	f	In Slovenian, the word for “seven” (Sedem) also means sitting down at the table. An interesting option for either lunch or dinner, this restaurant is where students from a local tourism and catering college are trained under the watchful eye of their mentors and teachers. The original dishes on offer here are full of flavour and reflect the region and changing seasons and are presented on various tasting menus (including a vegan option) and an à la carte. You can also take a peek at the open kitchen, where a future culinary star may well be cooking your meal for you!	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3334920184	MAK	Osojnikova ulica 20	Slovenia	Maribor		https://www.restavracija-mak.si/	Nessun premio	Creative, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€€	t	f	Situated on the outskirts of Maribor, this restaurant with a slightly eccentric and very individual feel is home to owner-chef David Vračko. The two dining rooms here are decorated with a curious mix of furnishings and tables with attractively simple settings. There’s no à la carte, but instead a long tasting menu created by the chef that features colourful, playful dishes with unusual and occasionally contrasting textures. The theme here is creative, interesting cuisine, including a carefully prepared selection of appetisers, delicious salmon tartare with exotic fruit, superb prawns with cauliflower, and mouth-watering duck. Everything is served with a cheerful smile and a real sense of performance.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3333597309	City Terasa	Ulica kneza Koclja 22	Slovenia	Maribor	Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cityterasa.si/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Grills	4.0	€€	f	t	If you’re exploring Maribor, this restaurant is a great place to stop and take a break and has a real holiday feel with its spacious terrace boasting views of the town, the Drava river and the Pohorje mountains in the distance. The menu focuses on fish from the Adriatic (including shellfish and plenty of grilled options), as well as meat recipes that include grass-fed Slovenian beef. There’s a more concise menu at lunchtime, plus a café and the sky lounge, both of which are perfect settings in which to relax.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3334053606	Restavracija Calypso	Kidričeva ulica 7	Slovenia	Nova Gorica	Air conditioning,Car park	https://perla-novagorica.com/it	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Housed within the Perla Resort and Entertainment Centre on the Slovenian side of Gorizia, this renowned restaurant has an excellent reputation in the region for its fish and seafood cuisine. The classically prepared dishes are announced at your table, with options such as raw and baked fish taking pride of place here and a particular focus on fresh fish from the Adriatic.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3335681540	Restavracija Grad Otočec	Grajska cesta 2	Slovenia	Otočec na Krki	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.grad-otocec.com/en/restaurant	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	This luxury hotel and restaurant in a spectacular and tranquil location in the middle of the Krka river occupies a charming 13C castle that was demolished and then rebuilt for the purpose. Antiques, a delightful bar with a fireplace and soft comfortable sofas all combine to create the feel of bygone days in the attractive dining room. The cuisine is regional and traditional, featuring carefully prepared dishes (the chicken with fregola pasta is delicious) and fresh vegetables sourced from the restaurant’s organic kitchen garden. Both the à la carte and the tasting menus follow the seasons. To round off your visit in truly aristocratic style, stay in one of the hotel’s luxurious guestrooms.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3339852177	Galerija okusov	Novo Celje 9	Slovenia	Petrovče	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://galerijaokusov.si/en/home	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	This excellent restaurant, whose name translates as a “gallery of flavours”, boasts an attractive setting surrounded by a park with an 18C Baroque palace (formerly Novo Celje castle) at its centre. The welcoming dining room is decidedly more contemporary in style than its surroundings, as is the cuisine served here, which is prepared from local ingredients using imaginative techniques and presented on a single tasting menu (usually 10 courses) from which guests can choose individual dishes as they please. Careful attention is paid to reducing food waste: the trout served with asparagus is also accompanied by chips made from fish skin, while the jus uses butter and other leftovers. Most of the wines on the impressive wine list are also available by the glass.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3339360447	Miga	Plaza de España 7	Spain	A Coruña	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.migacoruna.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	An attractive bistro-style taberna featuring a terrace, a bar where guests can also choose to eat if they wish, and two dining rooms with stone walls. The updated take on traditional cuisine perfect for sharing includes seasonal and market-inspired dishes, daily suggestions and Miga’s signature dishes such as the langoustine salad, the exquisite aged-beef tartare, and the boneless tripe stew (“callos de Miga”).	piraspeter	\N	\N
3332962292	Stara Gostilna	Savudrijska ulica 2	Slovenia	Piran	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://stara-gostilna.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	3.0	€€€€	t	f	Situated just off the seafront in lovely Piran, this elegant, stylish restaurant greets guests with the aromas of fresh herbs planted in large vases. The pleasant, intimate dining room serves as a backdrop for two tasting menus and a concise à la carte, all of which feature local, Mediterranean cuisine with a modern touch. Try the lobster ravioli or local sea bass cooked to perfection, followed by a selection of delicious desserts. The wine list offers over 400 labels, all chosen for their excellent pairing potential, plus a fine selection of rums and brandies.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3334617327	Rizibizi	Obala 20	Slovenia	Portorož	Terrace	https://www.rizibizi.si	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Situated in an attractive location on the seafront promenade in Portorož, this restaurant boasts a classic-style interior and a pleasant summer terrace facing the beach and the sea. Most of the fish on the menu is local, and is served in simple, unfussy dishes that are full of flavour. Truffles make an appearance on the menu in season, adding their unique flavour to various dishes – don’t miss the delicious sea bass options (carpaccio and pan-fried). An impressive wine list completes the picture.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3334307667	Sophia	Obala 45	Slovenia	Portorož	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.kempinski.com/en/palace-portoroz/restaurants-bars/restaurant-sophia	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	Open in the evening, the gourmet restaurant at the exclusive Kempinski hotel offers an elegant tribute to the famous Italian actress Sophia Loren, whose unique beauty was as Mediterranean in style as the flavours that inspire the cuisine served here. Influences from Istria, Italy and even France combine harmoniously on a menu that focuses mainly on fish and seafood from the Adriatic (don’t miss the shellfish), although a few carefully selected, top-quality meat dishes and truffle specialities also feature. The turbot steak with prawns, leek and chive-flavoured extra-virgin olive oil is superb.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3336699535	Vila Podvin	Mošnje 1	Slovenia	Radovljica	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace	http://www.vilapodvin.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Nestled in the countryside around Radovljica, Vila Podvin is both a restaurant and a hotel. The beautiful garden is one of its attractions, along with its fresh, strongly flavoured cuisine which showcases local, seasonal ingredients from the Upper Carniola, a region influenced by Italian, Slavic and Germanic traditions – good examples are the open ravioli with Kosec cheese and sweet chestnuts, and the turbot with mussels and apples. The dining room is classic in style, plus there’s a niche with a few tables which is perfect for a romantic dinner. A good selection of Slovenian and international wines, including some excellent vintages, completes the picture.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3330847652	Gostilna Repovž	Šentjanž 14	Slovenia	Šentjanž	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://gostilna-repovz.si/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Regional European	3.0	€€	t	f	The Repovž family who run this restaurant are continuing a long family tradition that dates back centuries – it’s thought that the property has been in their hands for over 500 years, while there’s been a restaurant here for 300 years! Although it’s impossible to list the different generations that have worked here, one thing’s for sure – the current management has really made its mark. Both the dining room and kitchen staff work hard to ensure that guests enjoy the best regional ingredients and dishes (for example, there’s no fish on the menu), which feature on tasting menus of various lengths, with a careful balance of traditional recipes and more contemporary-style fare. The choice of delicious appetisers showcases an array of local traditional specialities, including locally bred trout, vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, rabbit with plum cream, and diced pork with a horseradish mousse. The impressive wine list focuses on Slovenian labels – make sure you try the Laški Riesling from Slovenian Styria, a natural wine, or perhaps the Frelih St. Rupert, a lightly macerated and elegant Sylvaner produced nearby.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3331803881	Hiša Krasna	Lokev 78	Slovenia	Sežana	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://krasna-hisa.si/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	f	Run by owners Dajana and Boris Škibin and situated just a few kilometres from the Italian border, Casa Krasna is a pleasant boutique hotel where the traditions and character of Istria and the Karst meet (she is from Istria, while he is from the Karst). The ambience and cuisine at the restaurant combine to provide one of the most interesting dining experiences in the area, with a menu that features a careful selection of the region’s gastronomic specialities, as well as home-made bread and pasta. Tasting evenings organised in conjunction with local wineries are held in the old wine cellar carved out of the rock.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3334371045	Danilo	Reteče 48	Slovenia	Škofja Loka	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.danilogostilna.si/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	f	f	Now run by the third generation of the Čarman family (opened by grandfather Danilo), this restaurant continues to offer cuisine that is much appreciated by its guests, with Nina at the helm in the kitchen and her brother Gašper front of house. The menu includes traditional dishes such as Loška smojka, Loška medla and Loška mešta (old peasant recipes from Škofja Loka – hence the adjective Loška – which are based on semolina and served with turnips, pork or potatoes), as well as a few more creative options that also have a regional flavour. Although meat takes centre stage, a few fish specialities from the Adriatic also feature on the menu.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3338260960	Kendov Dvorec	Na Griču 2	Slovenia	Spodnja Idrija	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.kendov-dvorec.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Organic	3.0	€€€	t	t	The history of this magnificent country mansion overlooking the Idrijca river valley dates back to the 14C. Today, the building houses a warm and elegant restaurant, with stylish rooms for winter dining and a beautiful terrace for the summer. The cuisine is traditional and full of authentic flavours, featuring two tasting menus – Katarina (fish) and Jakob (meat). We recommend the latter, especially if it includes the delicious “bati and bakalca” (steamed bread dough and lamb goulash). The entire wine list is dedicated to Slovenia, with all wines available by the glass – the Štemberger Malvazija is particularly good. Charming guestrooms complete the picture.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3333632280	Dim Tao	25 Udong 1-ro	South Korea	Busan			Nessun premio	Dim Sum	3.0	₩	f	t	Dim sum, a representative Cantonese dish, literally means “touch the heart,” implying that it’s not intended to fill your stomach, but is supposed to be a simple meal. Dim Tao focuses on the most famous dim sum dishes among its countless varieties, including juicy xiao long bao (soup dumplings)^ a dumpling filled with plump shrimp and chives^ wonton soup^ and barbeque pork buns. Traditionally, dim sum is served with tea. We recommend the pu’er and jasmine teas. A long line of customers outside makes this popular establishment in the Haeridan-gil area impossible to miss.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3336842633	Miza za štiri	Mariborska ulica 17	Slovenia	Zgornja Polskava	Car park	https://www.mizazastiri.si/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	The name of this restaurant (Table for 4) says it all. The business began a few years ago as a type of “table d’hôte” for just four guests, then in 2020, Jure and Mia Brložnik followed their dreams and moved from the city to the countryside. Their restaurant is divided into three rooms, each with just one table – the perfect setting for an intimate dinner! The chef offers a fixed menu of 5, 7 or 9 courses (to be ordered ahead of time) which showcases modern cuisine with its roots in the region and a focus on vegetables and features dishes such as beetroot with horseradish, trout with mushrooms and delicious desserts. For a unique bespoke experience, we recommend the pairing with local wines.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3336189135	Vila Planinka	Zgornje Jezersko 67	Slovenia	Zgornje Jezersko	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.vilaplaninka.com/en/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Innovative	5.0	€€€	t	f	Although it takes a while to get to this restaurant, following the magical Jezersko valley to a setting just a few kilometres from the Austrian border, once you’ve reached your destination you realise that the journey was well worth it! Surrounded by splendid mountain peaks, this boutique Alpine hotel and its excellent gourmet restaurant of the same name provide a warm, welcoming haven for guests. The chefs here create elegant, refined dishes that showcase the best Slovenian ingredients, paying careful attention to local recipes. Specialities include bear prosciutto served with bread crackers, hazelnut cream and pear, and smoked trout with camomile-flavoured frothed milk, carrot reduction and pickled celery. The menu always features a few vegetarian options, such as fried celeriac with pinenut butter, poached egg and hollandaise sauce.	longoethan	\N	\N
3335965727	Yulling	2F	South Korea	Busan	Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Barbecue	5.0	₩₩₩	t	t	Yulling sits on the second floor of the Mipo Oceanside Hotel at the beginning of Dalmaji-gil Road. The lengthy counter in this vast space commands a panoramic ocean view marked by the spectacular Dongbaekseom Island and Gwangandaegyo Bridge. The restaurant uses a wide array of only the choicest Korean beef cuts graded 1++ No. 9, the highest standard. On top of this, its fresh seafood dishes with an intriguing blend of Japanese and European elements create a menu brimming with impeccably balanced flavors – as suggested by the name Yulling, which denotes “harmony” and “balance.” And one more thing: Don’t miss the well-thought-out wine pairings.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3332878184	Eonyang Bulgogi Busanjip	32 Namcheonbada-ro	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Bulgogi	5.0	₩	t	t	More commonly known as just Busanjip, this eatery at Gwangalli Beach has long been a popular spot, always bustling with customers waiting to get in. After decades of business in its previous location, the restaurant moved to this location in 2018. Unlike Seoul-style bulgogi, where meat is cooked in broth, the Eonyang style features marinated meat grilled on a gridiron or over a fire. As for flavor, Seoul bulgogi tends to be sweet, whereas Eonyang bulgogi is less so, with more emphasis on the nutty taste of Korean beef sirloin enhanced by the acidic flavor of the sauce. In addition to its namesake dish, Busanjip serves up a diverse range of special beef cuts. Come and relish the beauty of the coastal waters off Gwangalli today – with each scrumptious bite of beef topped on rice!	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3331476238	Good morning Hongkong	19 Seojeon-ro 47 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	₩	t	f	If you pine for Hong Kong cuisine and want to experience a uniquely Hong Kong vibe, this diner deserves your full attention as it is inspired by cha chaan teng, or a Hong Kong-style café. The owner says he opened this joint merely out of his love for Hong Kong. It serves less-than-authentic Hong Kong dishes, slightly modified to suit the Korean palate. Still, their flavors and visuals are no less spectacular than those of the local Hong Kong cuisine. Signatures include pleasantly spicy tomato noodle soup with plenty of tomato and ham^ bread generously glazed with condensed milk and syrup^ sweet nai cha (milk tea)^ and dong ning cha (iced lemon tea). The diner’s Hong Kong-style visuals are a plus!	voicucatu	\N	\N
3330267094	Chaoran	5F Signiel	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Chinese, Cantonese	4.0	₩₩₩₩	f	f	Situated on the fifth floor of Signiel Busan, Chaoran serves authentic Cantonese cuisine – more precisely its Hong Kong variety, which is based on the former yet characterized by the harmony of new flavors resulting from the city’s culturally diverse geographical contexts. Take, for example, the dim sum: It consists of a gamut of splendid and scrumptious dishes, including har gow (shrimp dumplings), characterized by skin colored with squid ink and topped with gold leaf^ a vegetable dumpling filled with truffle, other mushrooms, and asparagus^ and a seafood dumpling stuffed with dried scallops in XO sauce and decorated with flying fish roe. Pork Barbeque with Honey Sauce and Crispy Pork Belly, the signature dishes, boast juicy meat and crispy skin accompanied by mild flavors conjured up by seasonings. Its décor, reminiscent of Hong Kong in the 1920s, and its spectacular view of the Haeundae area make this fine diner an optimal location to savor a delectable meal.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3336186771	Chef Gon	12 Junggu-ro 23 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Counter dining,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	₩₩	t	t	Situated in an alley near Jagalchi Market, this joint is run by a former hotel chef with years of experience. Every morning, the chef visits the market to buy fresh ingredients, with which he prepares the day’s seasonal menu. For this reason, the restaurant’s course meal is called “Jagalchi Chef’s Course Special.” Diners sitting near the kitchen can watch the chef in action while listening to his explanations about the ingredients. In addition to seafood offerings, the menu features a wide range of meat and a la carte dishes, as well as a well-balanced wine list, all of which await your indulgence.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3336418146	Le dorer	2F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park	http://www.ledorer.com	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	₩₩₩	t	t	Le Dorer’s Marine City location offers a gorgeous seascape. Dorer is a French word that means “to coat with gold.” The restaurant’s name therefore symbolizes its resolve to provide a swanky and beautiful dining experience. Le Dorer started off as a Korean restaurant, but now serves contemporary fare with a touch of French and Japanese cuisine. It also features a wine cellar that boasts a wide range of vintages and varietals. For those who prefer to focus on the union of food and wine, Le Dorer also offers an a la carte menu and a bar menu with a wine and cocktail list.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3334977070	La Taberna del Gourmet	San Fernando 10	Spain	Alacant	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.latabernadelgourmet.com	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	This taverna could almost be described as a tapas museum! Huge choice of tapas on display, all prepared using high quality ingredients, as well as an extensive selection of wines.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3333472096	Namakzip	#1068 A	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Dwaeji-gukbap	4.0	₩	f	f	Busan offers a wide variety of dwaeji-gukbap (pork and rice soup), befitting its position as the origin of this dish. Every restaurant adds its own twist to the soup’s broth while staying true to its authentic flavors. At Namakzip, the meat broth features a higher proportion of vegetable broth, so it tastes light and clean rather than heavy. In addition to this iconic soup, the menu includes kalguksu (hand-cut noodle soup) with meat^ kalguksu with fresh noodles, both featuring meat broth from dwaeji-gukbap^ boiled pork slices^ and grilled pork belly. For those wishing to enjoy, amidst a modern dining space, a satisfying dwaeji-gukbap with a minimal aftertaste, Namakzip is the way to go.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3331965376	Mustrue	29 Jwadongsunhwan-ro 433 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	European	5.0	₩₩	t	t	Mustrue is one of the representative fine dining spots in Busan. Helmed by Chef Jung Jae-yong, a Busan native, it is covertly tucked away in a back alley of Dalmaji-gil Road. Open the golden door, and you’ll be greeted with a bar counter, where the chef masterfully handles everything from cooking to serving. By using unique local ingredients, such as Korean angelica seeds and short-fruit pimpinella, he creates European cuisine with a Korean twist. Chef Jung is passionate about maintaining the harmony between his culinary creations and Korean ingredients. And his passion is uncompromising – just as Mustrue, the eatery’s name, suggests.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3337039274	Outro by Vito	18 Millakbondong-ro 19 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning	https://vito.kr/	Nessun premio	European	5.0	₩₩	t	f	With the new name Outro by Vito, the restaurant relocated from a location in the Haeridan-gil area to this spot near Gwangalli Beach. Not only did this fine purveyor of natural wine and cuisine change its name, but it also revamped its exterior and décor with a touch of contemporary elegance. Regardless, its pasta dishes, the quintessential offerings, have remained the same – only with enhanced flavors. The diner’s housemade pasta now features higher flour content and undergoes fermentation. The glutinous texture and impeccable pairing with the sauce make the pasta even more appetizing. In addition to a diverse array of pasta dishes, the menu features salads, meat, and various other scrumptious dishes. Come on down and savor your meal with a chef-recommended natural wine replete with a cultured vibe.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3339914383	Delibong	#110 Noblesse square	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	French	4.0	₩₩	f	t	A charcuterie course consisting of housemade meat products – doesn’t that pique your interest? After many years of running a French dining spot, the owner-chef Park Jeong-bong finally opened this little gem with a bar counter and tables that can seat only about ten people. With dim lighting and no sign, Delibong may be difficult for first-timers to find. Processed meats that require lengthy, meticulous curing and drying processes, as well as the polished dishes crafted with them, such as coppa, jambon, rillettes, and prosciutto, await. Aren’t you just a little bit curious? Reservations strongly advised.	grafpaola	\N	\N
3339750530	L'Essence	3F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	French	5.0	₩₩	t	f	L'Essence is a French restaurant set in a quiet alley near Namcheon Station. Here, Chef Jeon Ji-seong combines seasonal local ingredients with vibrant sauces to present French cuisine offering an outstanding balance of taste and aroma. Sometimes, the chef uses fermented ingredients, such as pickled vegetables and salted seafood, to add verve to his dishes, providing diners with the fun of spotting Korean flavors hidden amidst his delicate French cuisine. Though L'Essence usually offers only an a la carte menu, customers can enjoy its multi-course meal with a reservation at least a day in advance.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3338336014	L'étang	22 Seongji-ro	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	French	3.0	₩₩	f	f	L'étang is a French bistro located on one of the main roads in Yeonji-dong. Here, the owner-chef Jung Dong-won does everything single-handedly, from preparing the ingredients to cooking and serving. By revamping its menu every season to reflect seasonal ingredients, L'étang incorporates the flavors of the season into its French cuisine characterized by adherence to culinary basics and traditions as well as fresh and mild flavors. Since the bar counter facing the kitchen features limited seating, reservations are recommended.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3336715118	Ramsey	3F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	French	5.0	₩₩₩	t	f	Helmed by Chef Lee Gyu-jin, Ramsey pushes the boundaries of its classic French cuisine through inventive use of ingredients. Located in Millak-dong, the highly competitive dining battleground where eateries of diverse varieties keep popping up, this bistro is set apart from the pack with its alluring French fare. From the amuse-bouche, which combines diverse flavors to create culinary variations on a theme, to fantastic fish and meat dishes that highlight the chef’s seasoned cooking skills, Ramsey is well-versed in every element of a French course meal and focuses on fare that makes good use of sauce flavors. Come and enjoy a cozy meal at Ramsey accompanied by attentive and discreet service while relishing its inviting vibe to the fullest.	stepanekgrace	\N	\N
3338882703	Kumsu Bokguk	23 Jungdong 1-ro 43 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Car park,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Fugu / Pufferfish	3.0	₩₩	t	t	Kumsu Bokguk in Haeundae District is the head restaurant of a chain that has many outposts in Seoul and Busan. For more than 50 years since 1970, and across multiple generations, this eatery has delighted seafood lovers as a specialized puffer fish restaurant. It offers four types of puffer fish. Brown-backed puffer is chewy and has a nutty flavor. Globe puffer is large and often made into a spicy stew. Yellowfin puffer is sweet, so it is usually steamed or boiled. Ocellate puffer is the largest variety of the fish. Its firm texture makes the fish more suitable to be served raw. Safety is the first priority at this head restaurant as demonstrated by the hiring of dozens of chefs, all licensed to prepare puffer fish. So why not rest assured and visit this time-tested establishment for a gastronomic adventure?	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3338292409	Don Fadrique	Carretera de Salamanca	Spain	Alba de Tormes	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.donfadrique.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	At Don Fadrique, there’s a commonsense approach to the cuisine that makes its way from the kitchen to the table. This is showcased on an à la carte (including half portions), with an updated take on traditional cooking and a focus on the seasons, and two tasting menus: “Sabor de la Memoria”, with its homage to tradition and top-quality ingredients (including grilled fish and meat), and Instinto, a more personal and modern option which gives free rein to the chef’s creativity (prior booking required). The chef also presents and serves many of the dishes himself.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3332248913	Torafuguga	480 Jwadongsunhwan-ro	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Fugu / Pufferfish	5.0	₩₩	f	t	Located on a boulevard near Jungdong Intersection in the Haeundae District, Torafuguga stands out with its quaint wooden exterior and a small aquarium with live torafuku (tiger puffer) at the front. The eatery has no sign except for a small calligraphy of its name penned by the owner-chef Jung Seung-hun himself. Yet, these visual elements are enough to let you know that it’s a specialist puffer fish restaurant. Here, the chef’s precise hand movements bring out the variegated flavors of tiger puffer and deliver them, nonstop, to customers at the tables. Torafuguga’s Japanese-style puffer fish course features a wide array of faithful dishes that are parboiled, served raw in slices, fried, made into a soup, or crafted into a porridge. There are many restaurants that handle puffer fish, but few show commitment to presenting it in authentic Japanese style. In light of this, the chef’s earnestness in preparing and serving puffer fish testifies to his passion for culinary art.	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3330819275	Osteria Aboo	58 Dongcheon-ro	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	₩₩	f	t	As its sign suggests, Osteria Aboo in Jeonpo-dong oddly labels itself a Western gastropub. Since 2017, this establishment has strived to offer authentic Southern Italian cuisine, a cuisine characterized by ample use of seafood-based ingredients. Among all the exquisite items on the menu, we are partial to the bisque pasta, featuring al dente noodles and a sumptuous amount of fresh and savory red-banded lobster, as well as the newly added Mare (“sea”) course. When paired with a chef-recommended wine, the cuisine will astonish you with the rich flavors of Italy.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3338482775	Vigneto	55 Suyeong-ro 522 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning	http://www.vignetobusan.com	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	₩	f	f	Vigneto is the very first restaurant by an owner-chef couple who settled in Busan after studying Italian cuisine at ALMA, the renowned culinary school in Italy. The building is both their home and restaurant, with the wooden ceiling and furniture in the interior creating a cozy and warm vibe. An Italian wine bar, Vigneto combines authentic Italian cuisine with a rare Italian natural wine pairing. In particular, its pastas and hams, all housemade, boast exceptional textures and flavors. For foodies who seek to revel in food and wine amidst Vigneto’s snug ambiance, we recommend reservations (which are set at 30-minute intervals).	monticristian	\N	\N
3339479227	Eutteum Iroribata	20 Suyeong-ro 408 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	₩₩	t	f	Located near Namcheon station, this Japanese diner specializes in omakase dining prepared using irori (traditional Japanese hearth). Though not as authentic as the ones in old Japanese houses, the irori here is faithful to its role as kitchen equipment. The visual and aromatic appeal of grilling seasonal fish skewers, arranged in a row in front of the irori, adds to the diner’s culinary delight. An embodiment of Chef Jung Eu-tteum’s experience with Japanese cuisine and his personal gastronomic affinities, the eatery is a perfect haven to relish a diverse array of grilled fish. Clay pot rice and other dishes served during the omakase course boast a range of refined flavors that often characterize Japanese cuisine.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3335957963	Iwa	2F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	₩₩	t	f	The chef, who holds a patent for the aging of fish, prepares aged ingredients with clear intent. Such meticulous preparation, combined with diverse selections, produces stable flavors and gastronomic delights. Depending on the ingredients available and the chef’s tactics, the proportion of sushi, sashimi, and other Japanese dishes in the omakase can vary. All fish here are aged at least four days, and the chef carefully selects an optimal aging period for each fish based on its type, characteristics, and conditions. At Iwa, customers can enjoy at one sitting a wide variety of Japanese dishes, each prepared with aged ingredients with full-bodied flavors. And reasonable prices make this culinary feast all the more special.	basileryan	\N	\N
3331708716	Zero Base	2F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	₩₩₩	f	t	Zero Base is a new Japanese restaurant by Chef Yu Byeong-chan, who previously ran the izakaya Yoo No Woo with a stellar reputation. The chef’s unrelenting thirst for classy Japanese cuisine, which had never been fully quenched at his former spot, drove him to present his newly evolved cuisine at this up-and-coming eatery. His solid culinary skills turn ingredients into sumptuous variations on a classic theme, in a way that accentuates his sensibilities. The eatery pays special attention to selecting the freshest of seasonal ingredients. And it simply makes sense. The delicate juxtaposition between Zero Base’s contemporary décor and classic cuisine conjures up an exclusive vibe.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3335081703	Cha Ae Jeon Halmae Kalguksu	70 Gwajeong-ro 191 beonga-gil	South Korea	Busan			Nessun premio	Kalguksu	3.0	₩	t	f	Since 1982, this establishment has faithfully and unwaveringly continued to serve local customers with the simple yet hearty dish of kalguksu (hand-cut noodle soup). Though this humble dish can be found anywhere, the eatery’s variant has distinctive old-fashioned charm derived from its unpretentiousness. The broth is not thick, but mild and light. And instead of serving kimchi as a side dish, it is offered in the form of a uniquely spicy garnish mixed with onion. It is these and other intricacies that give this joint’s menu a singular flair. For an optimal dining experience, first, enjoy the mild broth and noodles in their natural state. Then, add in the garnish for a pleasant spiciness that slowly builds up. The menu features several varieties of kalguksu, including Halmae Kalguksu, the restaurant’s namesake signature dish^ bibim (spicy cold) kalguksu^ and kalguksu in cold soybean soup made from stone-ground soybeans, its summer special. Plus, you can even select the portion sizes that suit your mood.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3337613524	Sogonggan	4F	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Korean	3.0	₩₩	t	f	Sogonggan is a double entendre that can be read as “a small space” or “a space dealing with beef.” Its thoughtfully crafted menu is rooted in Korean cuisine. The chef spent many years perfecting his Western cuisine before making the switch to its Korean counterpart. He says the switching has made cooking more enjoyable and comforting as if he were finally wearing a tailored suit. Indeed, his sense of happiness is genuinely reflected in the fare. With Sogonggan’s elegant plating, original dishes, and refined Korean menu lineup, such as beef bone soup simmered in-house for 48 hours and pot rice, the “small space” moniker is unquestionably a misnomer.	berninialex	\N	\N
3333936057	Tony García Espacio Gastronómico	Avenida del Mediterráneo 281	Spain	Almería	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.tonygarciaespaciogastronomico.com/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	t	f	Choose between the informal gastro-bar and an attractive dining room where the fusion cuisine on offer combines the traditional and the contemporary. Products from Almería take centre-stage here.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3337244753	Yongkangzzie	10 Gwanganhaebyeon-ro 277 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Noodles, Taiwanese	4.0	₩	f	f	Situated near Gwangalli Beach at the beginning of an alley leading to Millak Golmok Market, Yongkangzzie is a Taiwanese spot best known for its beef noodle soup. The consistent design concepts that permeate both exterior and interior spaces, as well as the detailed décor, have done a remarkable job of reproducing a vibe that evokes Taiwan. The warmth of the signature soup goes well with the eatery’s casual and exotic ambiance. The broth, which offers up subtle sour flavors and umami, and the thick, pleasantly textured noodles make this iconic soup a comforting choice in any season. In addition to this signature dish, Yongkangzzie serves other noodle and side dishes that are guaranteed to please the palate. Please note that the restaurant has no parking lot.	costasergio	\N	\N
3331360084	Yakitori Haegong	30-5 Millakbondong-ro 19 beon-gil	South Korea	Busan	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Yakitori	5.0	₩₩	t	f	In an alley of a quiet residential neighborhood is a pink building with an unexpected tiny little sign that reads “Haegong.” This Japanese eatery specializes in yakitori (grilled chicken skewers) made with native Korean chicken. As part of the relocation to its present location in October 2022, some upgrades were made to its space to ensure a more sophisticated dining experience. Grilled hagfish, another gem of this establishment, is not a dish to miss, with each mouthful piece brimming with juice, oceanic minerality, and delightfully firm texture. Yakitori Haegong is a rare gem in Busan to savor yakitori in a serene vibe accentuated by its refined interior décor.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3337219163	Boreumsae	36 Teheran-ro 81-gil	South Korea	Seoul	Air conditioning,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Barbecue	3.0	₩₩	f	f	Beef restaurants are ubiquitous all over Korea, but this spot which opened in late 2015, offers something prized and uncommon: Jeju black cattle. Choose from a wide range of cuts including sirloin, tenderloin, chuck tail flap, outside skirt steak, brisket and two types of raw beef dishes: tartare and sashimi. The prime meat is flown in directly from the family-operated farm. Private rooms are available on the second floor.	contimatteo	\N	\N
