3335477801	Hotaru Madrid	Alcalá 99	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.hotarumadrid.com	Nessun premio	Japanese, Fusion	4.0	€€€	t	t	Hotaru is one of those places where you can experiment, savour and be guided in complete confidence by the sushi bar chef. Located opposite the Retiro park, and decorated in an elegantly authentic style, this restaurant bases its cuisine around two well-balanced Omakase menus and an extensive Japanese-inspired à la carte (maki, temaki, sashimi, nigiri etc) with interesting and somewhat surprising hints of fusion from Mexico.	ferrettivladislav	\N	\N
3335260748	Umiko	De Los Madrazo 6	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://umiko.es/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Fusion	3.0	€€€	t	t	If you’re keen to try a different type of dining experience, this restaurant will surprise you with its size and its choice of dining spaces (when you make your booking, you’ll need to choose either the restaurant itself, the sushi bar or the so-called “Zona Blanca”). The menu here features Japanese fusion cuisine that makes use of Spanish ingredients and showcases influences from different regions across Spain (particularly Madrid) and other countries (France, Italy etc). Umiko works with Japanese “koshihikari” rice that is flavoured with different vinegars. Its desserts always come as a surprise, reminding us of our childhood through reinterpreted takes on Spanish sweet delicacies such as “Pink Panther” and Phoskito (which they have renamed Phosmiko). Don’t miss the tuna belly nigiri with Wagyu fat or the “sam” of Iberian Señorío de Montanera pork ribs.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3336993588	Leña Madrid	Paseo de la Castellana 57	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking	https://grupodanigarcia.com/lena/madrid/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	€€€€	t	t	A restaurant with an attractive interior design and steakhouse philosophy under the baton of award-winning chef Dani García, who oversees everything here. The stars of the show are the dishes cooked on the open grill (the menu also includes plenty of starters and mains to share), with a few grilled fish options and a huge choice of different cuts and matured meats (beef ribeye, veal porterhouse, grilled sirloin, tomahawk etc). Occasionally, and for a limited period, it also serves a few of this famous Marbella chef’s iconic dishes.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3333978479	Los 33	Plaza de las Salesas 9	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.los33.net	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	€€€	f	f	Trends come and go and as such there are some restaurants, such as this one in the Salesas district of the city, that everyone is talking about and where you’ll find it difficult to book a table. The couple in charge, Nacho and Sara, have created a space that is particularly welcoming, with two highly distinct sections: a bar with tables for tapas, or enjoying a glass of wine or cocktail (no bookings are taken for these)^ and the dining room itself (you’ll need to book online) with its sturdy oak pillars, and an open grill visible behind the long bar counter. The enticing à la carte features contemporary dishes alongside more traditional recipes from Uruguay, all of which are prepared with top-quality meats. Make sure you try the bikini sandwich of grilled prosciutto.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3331665914	Rubaiyat Madrid	Juan Ramón Jiménez 37	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.gruporubaiyat.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	4.0	€€€	f	f	Discover the authentic flavours of São Paulo in this restaurant where you can order the typical “feijoada” (minimum of two guests) or its extensive selection of meats. Fantastic terrace featuring trees and plenty of greenery!	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3334450323	Rural	Marqués de Cubas 8	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.restauranterural.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	€€€	t	t	Are you familiar yet with Rafa Zafra’s new venture? The renowned chef in charge of Estimar, with restaurants in both Barcelona and Madrid (the latter just a few metres away from Rural), has teamed up with chef Alberto Pacheco to leave the sea (the leitmotif of his other businesses) behind him in order to focus on the land. In the dining rooms, with their subdued lighting and urban-style interior design, the cooking is focused on a choice of different meats (beef, ox, pork, lamb, poultry, game). This is showcased via premium Joselito cured hams, escabeches, sausages, delicious barbecued pinchos and specialities cooked on the Josper grill, the Basque parrilla, or in the traditional Castilian oven. An impressive and varied wine cellar completes the picture.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3331248914	Sua	Moratín 22	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://www.suabytriciclo.com/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	€€	f	f	Part of the Triciclo group, this modern “asador”-style restaurant, the name of which is a nod to Basque mythology, views itself as a “temple of fire” in the Spanish capital. Its most striking feature is its setting in a delightful winter garden in the heart of the Las Letras district. Although Sua offers an excellent choice of starters and grilled vegetables from the town of Tudela in Northern Spain, the star dishes here are those cooked on the open grill, including fish direct from the auction and an array of select meats (Galician T-bone, veal skirt, Iberian pork etc).	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3332742589	Mar Mía	Plaza de Isabel II 7	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.marmia.es	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	Located opposite the Teatro Real (in the Ocean Drive Madrid hotel), Mar Mía views itself as an “urban chiringuito” beach restaurant where everything revolves around the Mediterranean. The varied menu features plenty of options (recipes prepared raw, salted, marinated and with caviar, alongside preserves, tapas and rice and grilled dishes). Make sure you try the “gilda MarMía” pintxo and, for dessert, the most delicate of apple tarts! The restaurant also boats an internal terrace teeming with greenery.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3331596545	Barracuda MX	Valenzuela 7	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://www.barracudamx.es	Nessun premio	Mexican	5.0	€€	f	f	A casual and informal restaurant that showcases cuisine from Mexico’s Pacific coast, albeit with a lighter touch and a focus on fish and seafood. Enticing cocktail menu!	fioreerik	\N	\N
3338273720	Puntarena	Alberto Aguilera 20	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.puntarena.es	Nessun premio	Mexican	5.0	€€€	t	f	Occupying the Casa de México and taking its name from a beach back home, Puntarena offers dishes inspired by the country’s Pacific cuisine in a setting with a contemporary ambience. Choose between traditional fish dishes, fusion recipes and dishes made for sharing. The delicious “pulpo enamorado” (octopus) and innovative cocktails are a must!	vargalucia	\N	\N
3334241850	Ticuí	Cedaceros 6	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.ticui.es	Nessun premio	Mexican	3.0	€€€	t	f	If you‘re hankering for Mexican cuisine in the Spanish capital, at Ticuí (the sister restaurant of Puntarena) you’ll find the true essence of Mexican cooking in an attractively appointed and contemporary setting. The dishes on offer, combining tradition and modernity, are particularly made for sharing. Its corn tortillas are prepared here every morning on a traditional “comal” griddle.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3334890060	Alabaster	Montalbán 9	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://amicalia.es/alabaster	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	In an excellent location next to the Retiro park, Alabaster is home to a gastro-bar with high tables for an informal supper, an impressive glass-fronted wine cellar, and a spacious dining room complemented by two private spaces. Updated seasonal and traditional cuisine, with the menu divided into two parts (Comparte and Disfruta). Don’t miss the toasted meringue tart with lemon cream!	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3336708762	Barra Alta Madrid	Lagasca 19	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://www.barraalta.rest	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	t	t	In this modern and contemporary restaurant, you can enjoy an updated take on traditional cuisine with a nod to other cultures and a combination of main dishes, raciones and tapas. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus with options for sharing.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3334082833	BiBo Madrid	Paseo de la Castellana 52	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://grupodanigarcia.com/bibo/madrid/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	If you are keen to embark on a culinary journey to explore a magical gastronomic world of cosmopolitan cuisine at its finest, you don’t even need to leave Spain’s capital! This restaurant, decorated by the famous interior designer Lázaro Rosa-Violán, will surprise all and sundry with its fun aesthetic, dominated by some 7 000 light bulbs (that take us on a journey to the brilliance of the Málaga fair) and even an aerostatic globe! From a purely gourmet viewpoint, the contemporary, globally inspired cuisine (but with its roots in Andalucia), bears the hallmark of award-winning Marbella chef Dani García. The food here is very much designed for sharing in an informal atmosphere as a couple or with friends, and includes dishes such as foie gras and goat’s cheese millefeuille, almadraba-caught tuna tartare, fried hake, and 100% acorn-fed Iberian pork “pluma”. The à la carte also includes a small section dedicated to the chef’s signature dishes.	grafpaola	\N	\N
3333978690	La Llorería	San Lorenzo 4	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.lalloreriarestaurante.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	A restaurant that exudes a sense of freedom, excitement and youthful exuberance in equal measure – qualities which combine perfectly with consistency, technique and a passion for hard work. The setting, which takes on the appearance of a bar with just a few tables and has a counter set up for dining, is relatively simple, but this is compensated in spades by contemporary cuisine featuring flavours and textures that are always interesting. Choose between an à la carte particularly designed for sharing, with the option of “raciones” and half plates.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3336822983	Lúa	Eduardo Dato 5	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://www.restaurantelua.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	Although there are numerous Galician restaurants in Madrid, it’s unusual to find one that is so different and with such a highly personal and innovative approach. Here, the cuisine prepared by Orense-born chef Manuel Domínguez, the son of traditional “pulpeiros” (octopus cooks), is served in two dining rooms with a warm rustic feel and works of contemporary art, as well as on the attractive terrace. The dishes on the à la carte and the two tasting menus (Lúa and Lúa Chea) are focused around a fully contemporary culinary approach with a strong Celtic influence, and one which maximises the use of seasonal ingredients that bring out the best of each other. We particularly enjoyed the signature “Pulpo a feira” octopus dish and the “Tarta líquida de Santiago”, a new take on the classic dessert but one which pays homage to the chef’s roots. Luckily for us, this particular moon (lúa in Galician) is shining brightly in the Spanish capital!	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3330564415	Amós	Paseo de la Castellana 22	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.rosewoodhotels.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€€€	t	t	The Cantabrian flavours of award-winning chef Jesús Sánchez in the Spanish capital. Choose between the Memoria menu (including dishes chosen from the à la carte) and another tasting-style option called Esencia.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
3338968974	L'Atelier Robuchon	Paseo de la Castellana	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking	http://www.jrobuchonespana.com	Nessun premio	Modern French	3.0	€€€€	f	t	Whether you’re in Shanghai, Tokyo, Paris, Geneva, Dubai or Miami, every L'Atelier Robuchon restaurant around the world has the same aim: to perpetuate the culinary legacy of the late Joël Robuchon. This modern restaurant on the first floor of the Robuchon Madrid (a multi-faceted space where the “bar” concept takes centre stage and which includes other dining formats such as L'Ambassade and Le Speakeasy), follows the same aesthetic lines as its “siblings”, coupled with an informal ambience with a touch of luxury, plus a large open kitchen in the middle of the dining room. Here, French haute cuisine with touches of modernity is to the fore, yet without neglecting classic Spanish dishes. One dish that will remain imprinted on the memory is the so-called “Imperial Caviar”, which impressed us with its flavour and its exquisite presentation, which was akin to a work of art!	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3338287583	Llama Inn - Madrid	Conde de Xiquena 2	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	http://www.llamainnmadrid.com	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	€€	f	f	A restaurant with a relaxed, informal feel which sees itself as a clone of the original Llama Inn in Brooklyn (New York), the name of which pays homage to this typical Andean animal and to this traditional type of hostelry that always extends a warm welcome to guests. The aim of the cuisine here is to bring Peruvian flavours to the Spanish capital in dishes that are mainly designed for sharing (scallop ceviche, grouper tiradito, yakimeshi of king prawns etc), alongside others they describe as the “fiesta final” (sautéed beef and duck jerky with rice). A tasting menu, entitled “Trust The Chef” and served to the whole table, is also available.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3333183902	TAMPU	Prim 13	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://tampurestaurante.com/	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	€€	f	t	TAMPU’s decor stands out for its meticulous combination of slate, wood and wicker, as well for a name that is in reference to old lodgings built along the Inca Trail. Here, you will find classic Peruvian and fusion cuisine that has been adapted to Spanish palates, and portions that that are reasonably substantial. You’ll find lots of interesting dishes on the menu, including standout options such as the Amazon ceviche, “Pachamanquero” ceviche, “Chinese-Creole” sanguchito and the “Lúcuma en texturas”, a dessert based around an exotic fruit that is highly prized in Peru.	shirocky	\N	\N
3331573208	Bistronómika	Ibiza 44	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning	https://bistronomika.es/	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€€	t	t	Part of the Bulbiza (Bulevar de Ibiza) gastronomic project, Bistronómika offers a traditional “No Carta” menu featuring touches of contemporary detail. The specialities here are the top-quality fish and seafood (the catch is displayed here every day to whet our appetite) cooked with minimum intervention, mainly on the open grill. Make sure you try the Gilda kebab-style appetiser, prepared with red tuna from the Mediterranean.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3337947311	Estimar Madrid	Marqués de Cubas 18	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurante-estimar.com/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€€	f	t	The essence of the sea in the heart of the Spanish capital! Here, top-quality products take centre stage, with superbly prepared fish and seafood that can’t be bettered.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3331611336	Alcotán	Claudio Coello 96	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantealcotan.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	A classically elegant restaurant with a focus on traditional cuisine (à la carte only), top-quality ingredients, strong flavours and attentive old-style service!	romanosimone	\N	\N
3332885701	Amparito Roca	Juan Bravo 12	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restauranteamparitoroca.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	One of those restaurants that never fails to impress and feels as though it has been a long-standing fixture on the Madrid dining scene, establishing a hugely loyal following in the city in a short space of time, especially amongst its business community. Named after a famous pasodoble, it focuses on well-prepared honest and traditional cuisine on an à la carte featuring copious dishes that always includes one or two game-based escabeches. The decorative detail here comes as an added surprise!	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3335896719	Coquetto	Fortuny 2	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.coquettobar.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	f	This informal bistro-style eatery, where elegance has been put to one side, bears the indelible stamp of the Sandoval brothers who enjoy rave reviews daily for their famous two-Michelin-star restaurant Coque located nearby. Here, the emphasis is on traditional cooking (“migas” with free-range egg, “fighting bull” tartare with old-style mustard etc) and seasonal ingredients, plus a menu that covers breakfast, lunch and dinner. Almost every dish can be ordered as a half portion.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3336526302	Filandón	Carretera Fuencarral-El Pardo	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.filandon.es	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	If you’re looking for a restaurant in which to escape the stresses of daily life, Filandón guarantees a thoroughly tranquil experience on the edge of El Pardo, in the heart of the countryside but just a few minutes from the centre of the Spanish capital. In its pleasant, rustically inspired dining rooms, one of which stands on the terrace, savour traditional cuisine where the focus is always on the best-possible ingredients, ranging from superb fish sourced daily from the Pescaderías Coruñesas company to select cuts of meat and delicious rice. Many of the dishes here are cooked on the grill.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3336698032	Fonda de la Confianza	General Gallegos 1	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.fondalaconfianza.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	If you’re looking for impeccably prepared traditional cuisine and a focus on quality service, this restaurant is a splendid option, in large part thanks to the presence of Paco Patón, whose awards range from a National Gastronomy Prize to Best Front of House Manager. His cuisine, which is built around time-honoured stews, a few offal-based dishes, delicious rice options and superb escabeches, is complemented by a good selection of daily fish and meat options, with ingredients sourced directly from the auction.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3331527650	Tragatá Málaga	Alameda Principal 3	Spain	Malaga	Air conditioning	http://www.tragata.com	Nessun premio	Contemporary	4.0	€€	t	f	Located in the heart of the city, Tragatá boasts a modern setting with high tables and chairs and heralds the arrival in the city of famous chef Benito Gómez, who has brought his more casual and informal concept to Málaga from Ronda. Here, you can savour dishes such as his award-winning Russian salad, the popular squid sandwich, and the delicious grilled bone marrow with beef tartare. Since its arrival on the scene, it has been very well received by its new local clientele!	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3332909137	La Maruca - Castellana	Paseo de la Castellana 212	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.restaurantelamaruca.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	A restaurant with the same name as its older sibling in Calle Velázquez, although this one is located along an elegant section of the Castellana avenue! This spacious eatery is decorated in pleasant white tones and boasts two terraces (a smaller one by the entrance, and a second, much larger internal one designed in the style of a garden). The essence of the cooking here is rooted in tradition with a nod to Santander, the culinary DNA of the Cantabria region and, in particular, a desire to bring the authentic flavours of the sea to the Spanish capital. We highly recommend the fish soup, served two ways and teeming with flavour.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3334128391	La Maruca - López de Hoyos	López de Hoyos 42	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.restaurantelamaruca.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	In keeping with the focus in its sister restaurants along the city’s Castellana and Velázquez streets, the region of Cantabria takes complete centre-stage here. The standout features in this spacious, contemporary eatery with its large windows looking out onto the street are the welcoming terrace to the rear and an unwavering focus on time-honoured Cantabrian cooking. The latter is based around quality ingredients and simply prepared dishes that retain a strong emphasis on detail. Specialities include anchovies, Santander-style fried squid, brandade fritters, stews (mountain stew and Lebaniego stew from the town of Liébana), and Cachopo, a typical dish combining steak, ham and cheese.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3337567350	La Maruca - Velázquez	Velázquez 54	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurantelamaruca.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A restaurant that exudes a fresh, optimistic approach through two iconic themes, namely Santander and Cantabria. This lively and informal setting features a multi-purpose bar and contemporary dining spaces embellished with the occasional designer detail. Its à la carte reflects cuisine that is 100% traditional, with a predominance of Cantabrian dishes (Cantabrian anchovies, fried squid from Santander, hake direct from the fish auction etc) with an equal focus on preparation and high-quality ingredients. Make sure you try the famous Cañadío cheesecake, the recipe for which has remained unchanged since 1981.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3338335672	Rocacho Plaza	Plaza del Marqués de Salamanca 9	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://rocachoplaza.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Located in the heart of the city’s Salamanca district, Rocacho Plaza boasts a pleasant terrace and a menu that focuses on grilled dishes. Among its choice of meats, the selection from El Capricho, the famous farm in Jiménez de Jamuz in the province of León, are a real draw, including its premium “Selección José Gordón” ox chop and its beef chop aged for 90 days. It also offers market-inspired dishes, recipes featuring seasonal vegetables, superb grilled fish, and rice and fideuá options. It also occasionally hosts full-day food events such as those dedicated to the delicious oxtail.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3330719014	Taberna Pedraza	Recoletos 4	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.tabernapedraza.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	An attractive taberna renowned for its “cocido” (stew) and its Tortilla de Betanzos, the latter so famous that there is even a counter that shows how many omelettes have been served here since 2014!	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3330895809	Fismuler	Sagasta 29	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.fismuler.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	f	Gastronomy meets interior design in this restaurant with an austere retro-industrial feel. Despite this, the service and ambience is relaxed, with a menu that features pleasantly updated traditional cuisine.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3330151748	Nantes	Maestro Arbós 15	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantenantes.es	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This simple restaurant with an urban feel and a kitchen overlooking the dining room takes its name from the affection that the chef’s grandfather had for the Nantes variety of carrot that he used to grow in his vegetable garden, then transport in his vehicle to the city’s erstwhile Legazpi market. Here, traditional, seasonal cooking is to the fore, which is unpretentious yet delicious and impressively prepared. This is showcased on a good daily menu that is separate from the à la carte. In the vegetable section of the latter we particularly enjoyed the chickpea stew with cuttlefish and pig’s trotters.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3339862206	Mudrá	Recoletos 13	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	http://mudramadrid.com	Nessun premio	Vegetarian	4.0	€€	t	t	If you’re a fan of vegetarian cuisine, this centrally located restaurant (the name of which is the Sanskrit word for “gesture”, an important aspect of yoga postures) is the first international franchise in Europe that only uses vegetarian ingredients. Overseen by American chef Matthew Kenney, a leading name in this type of cuisine, it offers a vegetarian à la carte that follows the plant-based food philosophy, and features meticulously prepared dishes such as artichoke tiraditos, wild mushroom ceviche, Omakase nigiri etc.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3338941523	Tori-Key	Plaza del Descubridor Diego de Ordás 2	Spain	Madrid	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.torikey.com	Nessun premio	Yakitori	5.0	€€	t	t	A Japanese restaurant with a difference where the standard cold sushi is abandoned in favour of Yakitori-style cuisine, with a particular focus on grilled chicken kebabs.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
