3331747723	El Romero	Plaza de la Conquesta 5	Spain	Mahon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://elromero.bio/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€€	f	t	If you enjoy authentic market-inspired cuisine, this restaurant will definitely appeal to you. Located opposite the Santa María de Mahón church and run by a couple of Italian origin who fell in love with the island, it showcases recipes that are strongly based around Menorcan ingredients which they buy directly from fishing boats and local farms. However, you’ll also find nods to their homeland, including “passatelli”, a typical recipe from Emilia Romagna, which follows the recipe of the chef’s mother (with cheese from the island used instead of parmesan). Choose between several menus: Mar de la Isla, Mar de la Isla Plus, Huerta Gourmet and Mediodía Light. Gluten-free cooking that is suitable for coeliacs.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3339603075	Palodú	Sebastián Souvirón 7-9	Spain	Malaga	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	http://www.palodurestaurante.es	Nessun premio	Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	One of those restaurants you’ll love visiting thanks to its constant desire to improve, which resulted in the change of location to the centre of Málaga. The couple in charge (Cristina and Diego), helped by the continual support of all the family, have used the initials of their first names to come up with the concept of “Dual Cuisine”. Their cooking is focused on two tasting menus called Alcazul and Palodú, both with a wine-pairing option. The intensely flavoured “sequence” of “red mullet - gazpachuelo – potato” served together is particularly recommended.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3338569396	Cávala	Alameda de Colón 5	Spain	Malaga	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Creative	5.0	€€€	t	f	A contemporary restaurant that stands out for its open-view kitchen and striking wine cellar. The cuisine of Miguel Ángel Mayor, a Barcelona-born chef with Andalucian roots, is centred around two surprise tasting menus (Presagios and Recuerdos) that aim to add a modern perspective to typical Málaga dishes, with a nod to his childhood, while at the same time retaining the full essence of their flavour.	pingliu	\N	\N
