3337231010	Follia	Creu de Muntaner 17	Spain	Sant Joan Despí	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	http://www.follia.com	Nessun premio	Contemporary	3.0	€€	t	f	In this attractive stone property, featuring numerous designer details, the clear focus is on seasonal ingredients. These can be enjoyed in the glass-fronted dining room with views of the surrounding vineyards that produce the property’s own wine, and a small garden full of tomatoes, lettuce, fruit trees and aromatic plants. The cuisine here is centred around three seasonal menus (Seny, Rauxa and Follia), plus a tapas-style option called El Pot del Follia (that is usually served in the wine cellar or in the garden in fine weather). An added bonus is the bread baked on the premises.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3333012073	Ca's Milà	Playa de Cala Tarida	Spain	Sant Josep de sa Talaia	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurantecasmila.com/es/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	A restaurant in which to savour the flavours, aromas and sea views to the full. Along with its simplicity, Ca's Milà stands out for its homely atmosphere, attentive service and its location right by the beach, practically clinging to the cliff, along with charming terraces and romantic views. Its traditional Ibizan cuisine specialises in fish (mainly cooked à la plancha or on the grill) and rice dishes.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3330816348	The View	Puig Delfin	Spain	Sant Josep de sa Talaia	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking	http://www.7pines.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative	3.0	€€€€	t	f	If you’re looking for an elegant restaurant in a stunning location, The View will definitely fit the bill thanks to its clifftop setting boasting spectacular vistas of the azure Mediterranean and the islet of Es Vedrà, particularly at dusk, when the sun merges with the deep blue hue of the sea and dips gently below the horizon. Chef Óscar Salazar’s cuisine takes the form of well-executed dishes that are able to capture the full essence of the Mediterranean, starting from a strong commitment to local ingredients (red mullet, Ibizan red prawns, sustainably fished tuna, lamb from the island etc). Dining choices here include the à la carte, two tasting menus (a shorter version entitled Esencia del Mediterráneo, and a longer Sabor del Mediterráneo option) and, to cater to all tastes, the Experiencia Vegetariana. The live DJ in the chillout section is completely in keeping with the typical party vibe that is so typical of Ibiza.	costasergio	\N	\N
