3332984685	Casa Dirección	Avenida de la Constitución 98	Spain	Valverde del Camino	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurantecasadireccion.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	t	Very easy to find, thanks to its location next to the beautiful English-style mansion which now houses the ethnographic museum (also known as the Casa Dirección). The restaurant is home to a tapas bar where you can enjoy mini versions of à la carte dishes, a dining room that looks onto a delightful terrace, a landscaped area for private events, and even an amphitheatre! In the bright dining room, the walls of which are somewhat unusually adorned with an array of shoe moulds, choose from an à la carte of updated traditional dishes and several menus, all of which include a wine pairing.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3338576050	Hábitat Cigüeña Negra	Carretera EX-205	Spain	Valverde del Fresno	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://habitatcn.com/es/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Regional European	4.0	€€	f	t	This rural hotel for adults only shares the beauty of the Sierra de Gata with its guests. Taking its name from the black stork, a migratory bird which nests in several locations on an estate with over 220ha of holm oak and olive groves, it also features a gourmet boutique next to the bar’s lounge area, an organic olive oil mill and a hammam. In its asador-style restaurant, featuring a semi open-view kitchen and large windows through which guests can gaze out at its surrounding pastures, choose from a regionally inspired à la carte strong on grilled meats, especially those it rears itself, including goat, Iberian pork and RetWagyu beef (a cross between Retinto and Wagyu).	venturialessia	\N	\N
3335759975	Casa Pacheco	Avenida Peña de Francia 12	Spain	Vecinos	Air conditioning	https://restaurantecasapacheco.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This legendary restaurant in the Campo Charro area, which has been in the hands of the same family since 1916, is indelibly linked with the world of bullfighting and the matador Julio Robles (who was a friend of its owners), hence the rustic decor themed around this tradition and featuring unique photos of this “torero” as well as some of his bullfighting attire. The chefs at the helm, Cristina Martín and Sara Cámara, showcase traditional cuisine teeming with Iberian charcuterie, meat (including aged meat options), stews (such as the Pardina lentils from La Armuña with dewlap and chorizo picadillo), and delicious game options in season (we particularly enjoyed the loin of venison that is macerated in its own jus).	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
