3330205109	Ça marche	14 Jhengci Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	f	Ça marche opened in a quiet alley in 2021, with a modern classic room dotted by retro knickknacks. Honing his skills in Japan and France, the Taiwanese chef offers a 10-course prix-fixe menu that changes seasonally. French-Italian inspired dishes are tweaked slightly to cater to local palates, such as using Chinese-style dumpling skin in ravioli and Taiwanese basil instead of the sweet variety. Open only for dinner at 7 pm^ cash only.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3333282125	CRATAIN	306 Changsheng Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$$	f	f	Cratain is a portmanteau of Tasmania’s Cradle Mountain, which the owner once climbed. He draws a parallel between his restaurant and mountaineering, using the pristine white space as a blank canvas for dishes finessed with well-honed European techniques. The 5-course set menu offers flexible choices, together with á la carte options at dinner. Meat, chargrilled or pan-seared, is the main event, but the pasta is also a highlight.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3332855202	Marc L³	231 Renyi Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	t	After living abroad for 10-plus years, the chef opened a pop-up kitchen at Yancheng Market to much acclaim. In memory of his childhood friends, he opened Marc L³ in 2021 to serve fine dining food in a relaxed atmosphere. His 9-course menu comprises modern, Western dishes made with local seasonable produce, weaving layered flavours with his witty descriptions. The soundtrack of English and Taiwanese oldies adds to the experience. The cocktail designed in-house is worth trying.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3339813528	Nibbon	9 Longshuei 2nd Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning	http://nibbon.tw	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$$$	t	t	Though without a sign at the door, Nibbon has become one of the hardest restaurants to get a table in Kaohsiung since opening in 2020. The chef used to own a casual bistro, but after honing his skills in Japan, he settled for a fusion Japanese fare underpinned by French-Italian techniques. The menu changes every two months and is heavy in Japanese seafood and local veggies^ it always includes a hearty soupy rice halfway between risotto and zousui.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3333388285	Opus One Yin Yue	215 Wunci Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	$$$$	t	t	The dimly lit dining room is sleek and minimal, and the kitchen and service teams are small but efficient. Only one seasonal omakase menu is offered, with a choice of main from pork, beef and lobster, followed by a small portion of Japanese curry rice. The chef cleverly incorporates Asian influences in European-style dishes using ingredients like turmeric, lemongrass, huangjiu and kombu. Reservations are mandatory via social media.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3335786796	Majesty	11F	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	http://www.khhmarriott.com/Foods/Content/MAJESTY_RTR	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	$$$	t	t	The dining room is absolutely on a par with the luxury hotel brand^ the decor of crystal chandeliers, marble flooring and plush velvet-upholstered chairs is the perfect foil to the deftly crafted food. The young kitchen team delivers an eight- to nine-course French tasting menu that embraces seasonality. The romantic ambiance makes it the venue of choice for a dinner date or special occasion.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3333023598	Papillon	26F	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://papillondining.com	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	4.0	$$$$	f	f	Named after the French word for butterfly, the French chef strives to transform quality ingredients into radically different culinary gems. The spacious room, in muted wood tones, is dotted by butterfly motifs with a tree-like centrepiece being the focal point. Only one tasting menu is served and it’s inspired by the chef’s travel across three continents. Exotic elements come through subtly in his refined French cooking.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3338600000	Thomas Chien	11 Chenggong 2nd Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park	http://thomaschien.com	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	4.0	$$$	f	t	Not only has Chef Chien got culinary acumen and all the classic French techniques, but he also cares for his carbon footprint and sustainability of food sources. By eating here, you’ll be supporting small local farms and fishing communities. His set menus use mostly local, seasonal ingredients and his lunch menus change monthly to keep them fresh. From time to time, top guest chefs are invited from overseas to broaden diners’ gastronomic horizons.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3334683524	MU	128 Fuheng 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Innovative	5.0	$$$	f	t	The same owner couple has been running this snug, homely restaurant for 10 years, but the muted, monochromatic room doesn’t feel a bit dated. The 10-course tasting menu changes every 6 weeks, inspired by Taiwanese, Hakka and aboriginal recipes and demonstrates a flair for local Chinese herbs and spices. Most dishes are cooked over charcoal and the reduced sauces are free of starch. Try the chargrilled, smoked beef short ribs as a main dish.	popafarah	\N	\N
3331507652	Temperature Studio	50 Gongyuan East Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Innovative	5.0	$$	t	f	The owner-chef has over 10 years of experience in haute cuisine. He opened this 6-seater in 2021 because he believes temperature is at the core of all good food. The down-to-earth multi-course omakase menu uses European, Japanese and Taiwanese techniques to create dishes that are homely but layered with flavours and textures. Highlights include stuffed Portobello mushroom, and marinated milkfish on koshihikari rice.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3333357019	the FRONT HOUSE	132 Sianjheng Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Innovative	4.0	$$$	t	t	A palette of warm wood and soft neutral shades, soothing curves and rich textures set the scene. The veteran chef-manager has over 20 years of fine dining experience and his tasting menu relates his life and travels in Europe, Asia and the Americas. His clever use of local produce like starfruit, pickled cabbage and betel leaves adds a unique twist. A few private upstairs’ rooms overlooking a green balcony are ideal for small parties.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3338065152	Hai Guang	4 Nanda Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Jiangzhe	5.0	$$	t	f	Formerly an army club for entertaining the U.S. army and assorted VIPs, this is now a popular restaurant serving mostly Jiangzhe cuisine with a few Beijing and Sichuan items. Though the décor is nothing to write home about, signatures like pork ribs in orange glaze, and sea perch in chilli bean sauce are impeccably made. Don’t miss their scallion pancakes loaded with flavours and aromas. Reservations are recommended, especially at weekends.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3337012740	Cho	2F	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning	http://ssaw.com.tw	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	$$$	t	t	The pristine space in a serviced apartment tower is done out in brick-red hues and has trendy pendant lamps. Helmed by a Taiwanese head chef, the kitchen delivers a tasting menu that effortlessly unites local produce with influences from around the world. A dietician by training, the chef advocates healthy eating and a balanced diet, while keeping prices affordable. In addition to the main room, there are private rooms for parties and banquets.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3332495476	Cheng's Noodles	5	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	$	t	f	In Yancheng district famous for street snacks stands this 80-plus-year-old noodle shop. The third generation owner insists on using top-quality ingredients and keeping the room spotless. All food is served in porcelain tableware with vintage floral prints. The signature noodles swim in a flavourful broth made with pork bones, chicken and veggies, to be enjoyed with an array of side dishes such as blanched pork offal or sliced chicken.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3337192247	Crab's House	93 Minsheng 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	$$	f	f	Founded in 1976, this household name was the first restaurant in town specialising in live seafood shipped daily from the island county of Penghu. As you can tell from its name and the giant crab sign, crab is the signature dish, especially the spiced salt and pepper variety. Besides the eponymous crustacean, ask the friendly servers about the catch of the day. Try also the shrimp rolls wrapped in pork caul fat before being deep-fried.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3338221325	Good Crab House	696 Jiangong Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	$$	f	f	For over three decades, the owner-chef has been flying in the best ingredients from his home island of Penghu twice a day to serve his customers. The famous salt-baked virgin crab burst with buttery roe, while the baby octopus in dark brown sugar sauce boast tender flesh and deep caramel flavour. Fried fish tail tossed in salt and pepper is also hard to resist. Don’t miss the Feng-ju tea made with an herb native to Penghu.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3338807612	Kuca Seafood	55 Dewei Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	$$	t	f	Unlike many seafood joint, the room with blue-green walls and lots of greenery feels relaxed but also chic. The family business, run by a father and son, also stands out with a unique sense of humour in dish naming and the incorporation of Western produce in recipes like squid ink fried rice, which impresses with its strong, earthy aromas of truffle oil. Another popular dish, silky scrambled egg with sea urchin roe bursts with briny sweetness.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3339270653	Tain Chu	174 Jhong Dong Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Sichuan, Taiwanese	3.0	$$	f	t	Since 1971, the same couple has owned this nostalgic, elegant space clad in warm walnut wood. The wife helms the kitchen, and her Sichuanese and Taiwanese dishes, as well as original creations inspired by her travels have attracted a loyal following. Apart from the main menu, check out the daily specials – they never disappoint. Certain painstakingly prepared items need to be pre-ordered, and are big enough for a few people to share.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3331158270	Duck Zhen (Wufu 4th Road)	258 Wufu 4th Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	$	t	t	After opening its doors over 60 years ago, Duck Zhen now takes up two retail space, but still has barely enough room to seat the hordes of diners lining up for its duck dishes day and night. Its smoked duck platter is the must-try item, with juicy, flavourful meat to be dipped into the house-made garlic sauce, and best enjoyed with a bowl of braised pork rice. Portion sizes of assorted duck offal or duck soup can be tailored to your party size.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3331674302	Three Wheels	25	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	t	t	From a tricycle food cart in 1961, the third-generation family business has transformed itself into a no-frills booth, open from noon till dusk. This popular venue for Taiwan-style afternoon snacks is a stickler for tradition. The best-selling chargrilled pork sausage in intestine skin is mildly laced with five spices and sorghum wine. Fried shallot and peanuts give sticky rice sausage extra aromas, best enjoyed with the hearty sparerib soup.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3331206632	Capstone Steakhouse	1F	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Steakhouse	5.0	$$$	f	t	The first outpost of Danny’s Steakhouse outside of Taipei shares the same design motifs with its flagship – a high-ceilinged, spacious dining room with a mezzanine glass cellar and a show kitchen behind a glass wall. The set menu follows suit and is also the same as its Taipei sister, offering multiple choices for each course. The dry- or wet-aged U.S. beef steaks remain the culinary highlight. Private rooms are available.	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3336739589	A Fung's Harmony Cuisine	63 Jiangdu Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Taiwanese	4.0	$$	f	t	After more than 20 years away from home, Chef Lin is back in Kaohsiung, where he has opened this tiny gem with only four tables. His seasonal tasting menu champions a farm-to-table concept, showcasing produce from small local farms. Chef Lin declares his love of Taiwan, taking diners on a culinary voyage of the island as he highlights ethnic diversity in every dish. His wife, in charge of the front of house, explains the dishes in detail. Check social media for opening hours.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3336412663	Bo Home	183-1	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Taiwanese	4.0	$	t	f	The founder opened Bo Home in 1969 to feed hungry workers away from home with nutritious comfort food – braised pork rice, and giant grouper soup. Over time the menu grew bigger, but the drool-worthy signature rice topped with amber, luscious diced pork remains the key draw. On top of that, order stir-fried squid in salted egg yolk sauce, or stir-fried whelks if you want variety. Open till midnight, so it’s perfect for late night snacks.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3330596832	Chang Sheng 29	3 Hexi Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Taiwanese	3.0	$$	t	t	This restaurant, renowned for its home-style Taiwanese cooking, moved shop in 2024. The dining room is now spread over two levels and features a wood-rich space adorned in the owner’s collection of vintage crockery. The upper level commands unobstructed views of Love River. Two omakase menus are on offer and the dishes change daily depending on availability. Best sellers include deep-fried pork belly marinated in red rice wine lees and fish soup in a claypot.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
