3335788414	Praya Dining	Praya Palazzo 757/1 Soi Somdet Phra Pin Klao 2	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.prayapalazzo.com/restaurants	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Accessible only by boat, the Praya Palazzo hotel’s Praya Dining is located in a century-old Palladian-style mansion on the banks of the Chao Phraya River. Inside, it exudes historic charm to complement its culinary offerings. The menu unites iconic dishes from the Sukhothai and Ayutthaya Kingdoms with the Rattanakosin Kingdom and modern Bangkok^ Gaeng Rawang, a stir-fried beef curry flavoured with turmeric and lemongrass, stands out for its great aromatic spicing.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3331634477	Rongros	392/16 Maha Rat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Meaning ‘House of Flavours,’ Rongros preserves the taste of traditional Thai cuisine on the banks of the Chao Phraya River with a stunning view of Wat Arun. Highlights include the green curry with rib eye beef served with roti and the tangy glass noodle salad. The vintage décor, including the chandeliers, painted Chinese panels, and wooden furniture only add to the experience. Book a table on the terrace for dinner to take in the view at sunset. Keep in mind that this restaurant is a favorite spot for tourists, so it's a good idea to make a reservation in advance to secure your place.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
3337131439	Sang Thatien	75 Maha Rat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿฿	f	t	Formerly an ice factory, this small eatery retains some of the interior structure and incorporates vintage décor in a dining room decorated with basic wooden furniture and collectibles. The chef embraces seasonal Thai ingredients, especially fruit, to produce unique, signature dishes in a home-cooking style, such as strawberry salad with shrimp paste and caramelised pork and spicy plum mango salad. The crab meat with fresh herbs and spicy sauce is unmissable.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3336926192	Supanniga Eating Room (Phra Nakhon)	392/25-26 Maha Rat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://www.supannigaeatingroom.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	The homestyle Thai food at this casual restaurant comes with postcard-worthy views of the Chao Phraya River and iconic Wat Arun. Whether you’re sharing lunch with friends after touring the nearby Grand Palace or enjoying a romantic meal at sunset, try a flavoursome signature dish. The recipes come from the owner’s grandmother^ standouts include fried Chinese cabbage and braised pork belly with herbs and cowa leaves.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3330897485	ÎNT	Rooftop F	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Ascend to this rooftop restaurant to soak up an ambiance of elegant earthy tones blended with a subtle blue hue, all set against the warmth of an open kitchen. The tasting menu reflects Chef Patin 'Knock' Promsawadi and his team's unique, artistic approach to simplicity. Using French culinary techniques, he strikes a masterful balance between Thai and French ingredients to produce contemporary dishes that capture the essence of Thai cuisine. Advance booking necessary!	beckerradu	\N	\N
3333951904	Lahnyai	31 Soi Suan Phlu 2	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.lahnyai.com	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿฿	t	f	Initially conceived as a tribute to the owner's grandmother, Lahnyai showcases modern interpretations of royal Thai cuisine sourced from the cremation cookbooks of princesses from 1987 to 1992. The refined dining room delivers an intimate ambiance with velvet walls and Jacquard-covered furniture. Infusing a contemporary twist into historical recipes, dishes satisfy with tried-and-tested flavours, like a great massaman curry that strikes a fine balance between spice and sweetness.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3333924151	Nusara	336 Maha Rat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Great view	https://www.nusarabkk.com	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	4.0	฿฿฿฿	f	f	Chef Thitid 'Ton' Tassanakajohn, renowned for his work at Le Du, leads this inviting restaurant, presenting classic Thai cuisine with a modern twist. The cooking style leans more towards tradition, paying homage to Ton's grandmother and family recipes. Quality ingredients from across Thailand shine in impressive dishes, paired ideally with diverse wines. The top-floor lounge offers a perfect spot for pre-dinner champagne with a view of Wat Pho.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3333401749	Royal Osha	99 Wireless Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.royalosha.com	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿	t	f	A majestic twist on its sister restaurant in San Francisco, Royal Osha aims to engage the senses with enticing flavours, aromas, textures, sights and sounds. The setting is a sleek, modern dining room decorated with Thai art. Start with a cocktail inspired by Ramakien characters, before enjoying dishes like the excellent tom yum kung mae nam (spicy, sour soup with river prawns infused with Thai herbs) and the (seasonal) chilled rice served with accompaniments.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3335418950	Sra Bua by Kiin Kiin	GF	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.srabuabykiinkiin.com/en	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	5.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Inspired by its sister restaurant, Copenhagen's Kiin Kiin, Sra Bua is one of Bangkok’s original purveyors of modern, innovative Thai cuisine. À la carte and tasting menus are available, with their dishes – from street food starter to dessert – proving creative and original, yet respectful of traditional Thai flavours. Premium international ingredients are used throughout, while both alcoholic and non-alcoholic pairings are available to complete the experience.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3338164877	Vilas	F207	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.vilasbangkok.com	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿฿	f	t	Their seasonal menu here is themed around different regions of Thailand, while expertly combining imported European produce with local ingredients. The modern and original interpretations of classic Thai dishes are executed using contemporary techniques and deliver well-judged spicing and layers of texture. There is a casual feel to the dining room, with simple décor and whitewashed walls^ there’s a lively open kitchen too, so ensure you sit at the counter to watch the chefs in action.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3337938525	Chop Chop Cook Shop	328 Yaowarat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.goldsmithbkk.com/chop-chop-cook-shop	Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	4.0	฿฿	t	t	Housed in a five-storey Art Deco building, this eatery pays homage to its goldsmith heritage through its design. Chef David Thompson has been garnering acclaim for his Chinese cuisine with Thai touches since opening in 2023. High-quality ingredients that elevate tradition go into his refined yet honest food. Start with the crispy prawn wafer, and don't miss the roasted duck soup… but save room for the ginger milk curd – as simple as it is delightful.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3332747046	Jok's Kitchen (Pom Prap Sattru Phai)	23 Soi Charoen Krung 21	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿฿฿	t	f	In the debate between quality and quantity, this Thai-Chinese spot hidden in a wet market sides with quality. Starting with a single table, it has since expanded to five. The skilled chef, whose family has sold crabs for over 80 years, sources quality ingredients to create an Omakase set menu which he cooks chef’s table-style. The shrimp wonton, deep-fried snow fish with soy sauce and stir-fried kale with salted halibut are recommended. Booking is mandatory.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3335717377	Kor Chun Huad	864 Soi Somdet Phrachao Taksin 34	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	3.0	฿฿	t	t	For more than five decades, Koa Chun Huad has been attracting throngs of locals. Named after the chef-owner who has worked in many a kitchen in Chinatown, it serves classic Thai-Chinese dishes at appealingly low prices. The highlights are the boiled pork slices, perfectly complemented by a soybean sauce, and the intense stewed pork with sweet-salty five spice gravy.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3333060898	Somboon Seafood (Bang Rak)	169	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.somboonseafood.com/en	Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Known for its fried crab curry, Somboon first put its name on the global culinary map in 1969. Fresh ingredients, impeccable cooking and reasonable prices keep it there. They now have 8 branches around town, but this is the best and the largest, seating up to 200 people. In addition to their famous crab curry, we recommend the deep-fried seabass with sweet fish sauce and Thai seafood spicy soup. Flawlessly fresh seafood and generous portions.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3332963553	Saigon Recipe	Piman 49	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.saigon-recipe.com	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	5.0	฿฿	f	f	With its canary-yellow walls, vintage posters and Indochinese décor, this place feels like a home in Saigon, if it was staffed by capable Vietnamese chefs. They carefully select ingredients, including rice wrappers and noodles from Vietnam, to create flavourful rice and noodle dishes, salads and rolls the owner might serve family and friends. Weekday lunches offer set menus that please even the time-pressed. Coffee fans should try the authentic Vietnamese brew.	langalice	\N	\N
3330221244	Pari-	8-10 Samlarn Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Asian	5.0	฿฿	f	t	The cosy design and small counter foster a vibrant, relaxed dining experience. The small yet high-quality dishes combine Japanese Izakaya style with Thai ingredients, enhanced with wasabi or yuzu. The ham comes from a Yunnan village in Chiang Mai, perilla from Mae Hong Son, sashimi-grade fish from the south, and meat from organic farms. We recommend the corn-fried rice Yunnan ham and the house-made ponzu sauce, elevated by a refreshing Somsa citrus oil.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3336416166	Blackitch	27/1 Nimmanahaeminda Soi 7 Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.blackitch.com	Nessun premio	Asian Contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿	t	f	Hidden in the city centre in plain sight, this second floor 16-seater is decorated with stone, wood and local blue fabrics in a minimalist style. The creative chef, Phanuphol Bulsuwan, honed his skills under his restaurateur grandmother. He constantly adapts his 10-course meal using Thailand’s seasonal ingredients, uniting Thai, Japanese and Chinese influences. He also ferments kitchen scraps to season his dishes and brews beers and sake for food pairing.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3339459483	Yangzi Jiang	10 Nimmanahaeminda Road Soi 5	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	After years working in various hotels and living for over a decade in Thailand, chef Chan went back to his Hong Kong roots to open this simply decorated Chinese restaurant inside a contemporary Lanna house in trendy Nimmanahaeminda. His cooking is fresh, clean and well-executed^ the menu includes a variety of house-made dim sum alongside dishes like Chinese stir-fried prawns and a stand-out crispy pork belly. Advanced booking is highly recommended.	carlinikita	\N	\N
3330741399	Friend's Table	125 Mu 6	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Creative	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Friend's Table follows a chef's table concept in the glass-enclosed dining wing of the owner's home. Diners can chat with the chefs at work in this stylish interior, dimly lit with a red hue. Collaborating on each dish, the duo of chefs strive for perfection: the food is refined, creatively presented, and packed with flavour, possessing an intensity that is true to the Asian palate. Be sure to be punctual^ dinner will start at 7 pm.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3331454228	NAVAN NAVAN	55 Mu 7	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park		Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Surrounded by rice fields, this stand-alone cement building affords a clear view of the open kitchen. The chef draws on various cuisines and uses a charcoal grill to cook local ingredients. His unpretentious style promotes healthy eating, and each dish highlights the natural flavours of the ingredients. Arrive before sunset to see the beautiful garden.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3339743476	Cuisine de Garden	99 Mu 11	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining	https://www.cuisinedegardencnx.com	Nessun premio	Innovative	5.0	฿฿฿	f	t	Self-taught Chef Nan uses a wide range of modern culinary techniques to transform local produce into seasonal lunch and dinner tasting menus. Both change according to what’s obtainable and are ambitious, playful, and delivered in a rapid cadence^ a highlight is ‘Nest’, available year-round. Along with the cutting-edge cooking and theatrical presentation come sleek, modern Scandic décor and warm, friendly service. Enhance your experience with the wine pairing.	taddeisimone	\N	\N
3332961171	Aquila	226/4 Soi Surapol 1	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	฿฿	f	t	A 10-minute drive is all it takes to escape the city for heartening Italian food, surrounded by plenty of greenery. Despite its industrial design, it’s a casual setting with an expansive view of the garden. The pizza dough, gnocchi and fettucine are all homemade. The squid fettuccine has an enlivening ponzu dressing^ and the baked snow fish in a buttery fish broth   beats all expectations with large, slow-cooked pieces that are meltingly soft in a sweet, homemade broth.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3333960838	Favola	2F	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.favolachiangmai.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	฿฿฿	t	t	At Favola, Chiang Mai Marriott Hotel presents authentic Italian cuisine, featuring homemade pasta and ravioli crafted by the Italian head chef, all served in a dining room that blends contemporary style with a classic Italian restaurant ambience. Among the dishes, the pizzas stand out. Feel free to order half or smaller sizes, perfect for when you’re in the mood to try multiple dishes. The excellent wine selection further enhances the experience.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3330621756	Thana Ocha	29 Ratchawong Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	฿	t	f	Every day at lunch long lines form in front of this decades-old shop selling Hakka-style noodles. House-made Hakka stuffed tofu, fish sausage and crispy wontons find their way into every dish including tom yum noodles and the classic Yentafo. The latter is highly recommended, with a well-seasoned soup made from fermented bean curd and fresh chilli.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3333312467	Chum (Saraphi)	1/1 Mu 7	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Chum serves Northern Thai cuisine cooked from the recipes of the family's grandmother. The colourful restaurant is simply decorated with red and yellow walls and brightly coloured parasols of Northern Thai design hanging from the ceilings. The stir-fried pork and liver is well cooked, and packed with Thai herbs, wild pepper and coriander. The mixed Northern Thai starter uses a tasty young chili relish with the scent of green chili that isn’t too spicy.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3338485159	Kinlum Kindee	172 Mu 3	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Garden or park,Great view		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	f	Truth in advertising may be rare, but Kin Lum Kin Dee, which means “to eat delicious food and eat well” in Lanna, allows Northern Thai food lovers to do just that. Formerly downtown, the restaurant is now in a quiet pavilion in San Sai surrounded by gardens, trees, and fields. Dishes are marked by authentic flavours and fresh ingredients, with some from the garden. Grilled field crab innards with egg yolks and northern Thai herb soup with pork are must-tries.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3336981322	Kiti Panit	19 Tha Phae Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning	https://www.kitipanit.com	Nessun premio	Northern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Turning their great-great-grandparents’ 1880s mansion into a restaurant, Kiti Panit’s owners decided to create an updated take on traditional Lanna cuisine. The results include intense and complex Hang Le, or northern Thai curry, and savoury grilled chicken salad with coriander. Also recommended are the signature Khao Mao Gorn Rad Gati, or unripe rice with coconut milk, and the creative seasonal desserts.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3332990325	Krua Phech Doi Ngam	267/1 Mu 2	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	f	This popular open-air eatery serves well-sized northern Thai favourites at fair prices. Kang Liang, the peppery curry paste in spicy mixed vegetables goes well with the prawns’ natural sweetness^ while the local fish marinated in herbs and spices is grilled in a bamboo tube until soft, with a smoky aroma. Do check the blackboard for specials of the day, which often focus on seasonal dishes.	ozmax	\N	\N
3333614438	Larb Duang Dee Mee Sook	74 Soi Ban Huai Sai	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	t	With its simple, rustic look, this quaint eatery specialises in northern larb dishes, paired with a local chaeo dipping sauce with the aroma of toasted sticky rice. The spicy, sour and fragrant beef soup is a must.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3330515895	Lumdee Te Khuadang	V Community	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Bearing a loose resemblance to San Francisco’s Golden Gate Bridge, the bridge in this restaurant’s name (which translates as 'delicious at the red bridge') forms an iconic landmark while also providing guests with a pleasant spot for dining after dark. The range of healthy Northern Thai dishes provides intense flavours^ their biotechnology-derived fermented pork has the highest levels of hygiene and quality, and is used in many of the dishes.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3332778340	Withee Laab	94-120 Charoen Muang Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	4.0	฿	f	t	This charming wooden building down a narrow alley has been serving delicious laab for years. The spicy minced buffalo meat and zesty cooked minced pork are sure to impress. With surprisingly affordable prices, this is a gem worth seeking out.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3334665046	Maadae	86-88 Thapae Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Meaning ‘come’ in the Southern language, ‘Maadae’ invites you to enjoy delightful seafood in a welcoming atmosphere. Supporting local Chumphon fishermen and sourcing seasonal organic produce, their menu rotates with fresh ingredients. The evening selection offers diverse options, including superb freshly grilled seafood paired with a spicy sauce.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3336680866	Kang	Jing Jai Market	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	South East Asian	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Opened in 2023, Kang is a fresh addition to Jing Jai Market. It offers a cosy retreat with a laid-back approach to dining, plus a menu that's ideal for sharing the highlights of Indonesian, Malaysian and Thai cuisine with friends. We suggest opting for their signature Nasi Lemak, or one of the bold, aromatic curries. All dishes are made to order, so diners may need to have a little patience while waiting for their delicious meals.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3333152717	Talung	8 Chotana Road Soi 12	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Having recently relocated to this ground floor eatery under a residential apartment, Talung is simply decorated with air conditioning, a lively bar and serves Southern Thai. It’s a small family business, the staff are friendly and attentive, and help each other from kitchen to table. The stir-fried squid with squid ink has a rich, well-seasoned sauce and herbal scent. The stir-fried prawns come with a homemade southern Thai shrimp paste and young bitter beans.	pavlovsabrina	\N	\N
3339689819	Aunt Aoy Kitchen	377 2 Chiang Rai Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿	t	f	The décor is simple, with a display of photos and messages on post-it notes from customers gone by. Aunt Aoy spent much of her career cooking in hotel kitchens. Her expertise is realised in the fluffy yet crispy Chef Omelette with stir-fried minced pork, salted egg and pork crackling.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3332810871	Baan Landai	252/13-14 Phra Pok Klao Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Don’t let the slightly unkempt exterior keep you from visiting Chef Landai’s restaurant. The interior exudes charm with its eclectic décor and a window into the kitchen, where chefs whip up pan-Thai dishes like flavourful pork ribs with red wine sauce. The portions are suitable for sharing with friends, and don’t forget to save room for their traditional Thai desserts.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3337682156	Baan Suan Mae Rim	261 Mu 2	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.baansuanmaerim.com	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	t	Although this restaurant is outside the city centre, it’s worth the drive for its Thai cuisine, and especially its northern dishes, served in a beautiful, natural setting. Open for more than a decade, the place consists of several northern Thai-style pavilions, which all face a pond – and you can also dine in the open air. Either way, there are tranquil views of the trees, pond, and rice fields. Deep-fried snakehead fish with hot and spicy sauce is recommended.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3332634714	Food For You	25 Mu 3	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Food For You has been creating flavoursome Thai food using fresh seasonal ingredients from local farms for over 20 years. Meals here are served chef’s table style, from a menu that changes according to the season and customer requests. The crab meat salad with mixed fruit is highly recommended and comes with a dressing that’s the perfect balance of sweet, sour, and salty. As seating is limited, reservations are essential.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3331136317	Khao	Four Seasons Resort	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.fourseasons.com/chiangmai/dining/restaurants/khao	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿฿฿	f	t	Khao serves Northern Thai cuisine, along with some dishes from other regions. The chef, a prestigious culinary school graduate with 10 years of luxury hotel experience, brings an international perspective and a modern identity to traditional Thai dishes. The dining room is contemporary and inviting – crystal chandeliers coexist with carved teak panelling – and the terrace offers serene views of rice fields and hills.	caldarolacagilio	\N	\N
