3339621976	Neon Boat Noodles	395/7 Pattaya	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	t	f	Traditional boat noodles are served here with various toppings in a bold and savoury soup. We also recommend the spicy boiled pork and pork condiments, which have an intensely flavoured sauce and the aroma of fried garlic.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3334039327	Noodles Soi 12 (Ban Suan)	44/8-9 Mu 6	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	f	t	With its wooden furniture and rustic charm, this is a delightful spot for an early breakfast or lunch. The real star here is the soup with aromatic dried squid and pork ribs imparting rich flavour. Each tasty spoonful is testament to the traditional recipe.	dragomirpippo	\N	\N
3332751421	Fish Club	Andaz Pattaya Jomtien Beach  345 Mu 3	Thailand	Chon Buri	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view	https://www.hyatt.com/andaz/utpaz-hyatt-andaz-pattaya-jomtien-beach/dining/fish-club	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Fish Club's location on a serene beach sets it apart from the typical Pattaya dining scene. With indoor and outdoor dining, the restaurant combines a pleasant view with a lively atmosphere. The menu reveals Western and Asian influences, and the chefs excel at grilling, controlling temperatures perfectly. The peanutty sriracha sauce pairs impeccably with your steamed or grilled seafood.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3334547816	Khrua Ban Po Ta	23 Soi Pattaya Tai 8	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	฿฿	t	f	The breezy, spacious dining room surrounded by vines and plants makes for a relaxing and laidback coastal ambience. The seafood-based menu features shrimp, squid and crab options cooked several ways. The stir-fried squid with black ink sauce is a showstopper, but diners also enjoy shelling the stir-fried whole crab with curry powder. The sweet local seasoning enhances the food's natural umami.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3338965520	Khao Tom Ped Jek Tong	421/1 Vachira Prakarn Road	Thailand	Chon Buri	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	฿	f	f	For a taste of long-established local fare, this eight-decade-old gem that holds itself to exacting standards of cleanliness is a must. Tender braised duck meat with savoury gravy is the signature, best enjoyed with rice^ fans of spicy food will relish the house-made dipping condiments.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3339421700	Mae Pong Sri	42/99 Mu 9	Thailand	Chon Buri	Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	฿	f	f	The go-to spot in Pattaya for pork offal soup with boiled sweet leaf bush, this eatery draws inspiration from Thai cuisine nationwide to offer a plethora of quick street food dishes. From the many noodle and rice options, the stir-fried glass noodles with seafood stand out.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3335786218	Chom Tawan	79 Mu 3	Thailand	Chon Buri	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Despite its rustic-looking exterior, Chom Tawan has a certain charm, and prices are reasonable, especially considering the freshness and quality of the seafood. The delicious stir-fried squid with minced pork filling and garlic is tempting, but also ask about the special of the day.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3330816360	Jay Jew Talew Bin	117/17 Mu 2	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	f	This local favourite offers the freshest seafood with bold Thai flavours, cooked home-style. The restaurant is simple, without air conditioning. The menu primarily focuses on seafood options, and the chef excels at deep-fried and stir-fried dishes. The rice dishes and daily catch are listed on the blackboard at the front of the shop. Bookings are only taken for groups of 10 or more. Expect to wait for a table on weekends.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3332096286	Klai Lib	126 Bangsaenlang Road	Thailand	Chon Buri	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿	t	f	Attracting younger diners, this eatery has a reputation for fresh, affordable Thai seafood of uncompromising quality. The generous portions with sweet seasonings are good for sharing^ the deep-fried mackerel with fish sauce is a must for its crispy skin and tender meat.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3339975706	Krua Pla Tu Tid Oun	8/1 Nadedee Road Soi 5	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	This place near Bang Saen beach has been popular with tourists for decades. The signature is, of course, pla tu (Thai mackerel), but the menu extends from seafood options such as sillago, sea bass and local scallops – all cooked in classic Thai style – to crispy deep-fried mackerel cheek with a chilli-garlic aroma that's addictive. If you prefer a milder taste, the staff are happy to adjust the spice level to suit your palate.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3338158141	Wansuk	129/10 Mu 1	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	In a vintage decor featuring wooden accents, music from the 1980s and 1990s sets the mood. At this locally renowned Thai restaurant, the chef-owner's uniquely creative menu boasts intensely flavoured, unapologetically spicy dishes – though milder versions are available upon request. Seafood is the star, with fresh, expertly cooked offerings served at perfect temperatures. Instead of regular rice, we suggest ordering the signature fried rice with salt.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3334852986	Radna Suanmak	282 Phoklang Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	฿	f	f	In over 30 years serving the community, this humble noodle spot has won local awards and built up a dedicated following. Expect a wait for their lovingly prepared dishes, which include deep-fried fish with thick noodles, and flavoursome crispy noodle stir-fry with holy basil.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3330882652	Klang Na Pla Khao	5 Mu 9	Thailand	Chon Buri	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai, Isan	5.0	฿฿	f	f	This country-style restaurant serves up a splendid array of Isan dishes and Eastern Thai specialties from land and sea. The highlight is a spicy stir-fry with an original curry paste recipe from Chanthaburi province, capturing the authentic essence of Thai cuisine. There's no compromise on bold, genuine Thai flavours. The tranquil outdoor setting affords views of lush green rice fields, and the relaxed atmosphere makes it perfect for friend and family gatherings.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3338239448	Kai Yang Wanna	271 Mu 11	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿	t	f	Grilled chicken is the name of the game at this Isan shophouse restaurant. Launched in 1973 by the current owner’s father, it uses a local breed, spices them using a family recipe and skilfully grills them over charcoal. They only make 200 a day, which always sell out, so reserve a bird or arrive early. Also on the menu are simple Isan dishes, including delicious pork larb. Seating is available inside with or without AC and outside on the veranda.	longoethan	\N	\N
3332580298	Sookjailand	98 Mu 7	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Great view		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Time drifts past at this tranquil Isan restaurant, where diners eat in private bamboo pavilions dotting a large rice field. There are no tables—meals are served on woven mats on the floor, local style. And the food, which comes in both shareable set menus and à la carte dishes, is just as authentic as the setting. Made from quality, fresh ingredients, simple dishes like the grilled snakehead fish set and the local crab soup with veggies, are highly recommended.	buonvinogino	\N	\N
3332516281	Tumkratoei Sagate	88-89 Mu 20	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿฿	f	t	The owner is from Roi Et Province (formerly Sagate Province). The place offers flavourful food, warm service and wallet-friendly prices in a relaxed setting. The signature spicy seafood salad with fermented fish sauce is recommended, and beyond the Som Tum dishes, standouts include fried sour fish and spicy chicken soup with glass noodles. Indoors and outdoor seating are available. Nightly live music adds to the experience.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3336727966	Vacca	99 Mu 20	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Italian chef-owner Fabio Colautti's restaurant near Khon Kaen Airport offers authentic Italian flavours with homemade pasta, wood-fired pizzas, and grilled meats. Opened in 2015, it boasts a classic Italian ambience with a cosy white interior, a large wine cellar, and an open kitchen. Highlights include the Vacca pizza and the grilled Wagyu rib-eye.	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3334100128	Guang Tang Noodles	18/15 Pimpasut Road	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	฿	t	f	The history of this egg noodle soup spot stretches back more than 70 years to the owner’s grandfather. Today, it still satisfies — especially the noodle soup with wontons and barbecue pork (the noodles and wontons are homemade) and the deep-fried noodles with gravy and pork or beef.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3339985196	Kao Lao Siang Ji	8 Sathityutitham Road	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	฿	f	t	Started 50 years ago in a hawker stall by the owner’s grandfather, this shop continues to serve delicious pork blood and offal soup following the founder’s recipe. Pork balls make a tasty addition^ organs can be added or subtracted. Also recommended are the deep-fried shrimp wontons.	kralrosa	\N	\N
3336935419	Krua Supanniga by Khunyai Somsie	Supanniga Home	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Car park,Garden or park	https://www.secret-retreats.com/tables/krua-supanniga-by-khun-yai	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Named after the Supanniga flower, this cute shop offers delightful dishes blending flavours from the eastern seaboard and Isan cuisine. Grandma's recipes inspire the food here. Don't miss the must-order chamuang pork—a juicy stewed pork infused with Chamuang leaf's slightly sour flavour. The restaurant provides indoor and outdoor seating, including shaded tables in the tree house.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3338932098	See Na Nuan Café	164/160 Mu 14	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	f	This 500-seat crowd pleaser close to Khon Kaen University serves flavoursome central Thai fare and Isan dishes in an industrial-style house with a huge outdoor dining area. Inside is all brick and black steel^ outside, the steel continues in a birdcage-like dining area next to more seating centred around a lawn. Seafood tanks attest to the food’s freshness^ the grilled snakehead fish served with spicy dip is recommended. Chill live music features nightly.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3339936595	Song 24 Nor	Nikorn Samran Road	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	The menu at this boiled rice spot boasts over 200 items, but the sour soup with deep-fried snakehead fish is a must. Like other dishes, it’s fresh, well-cooked and wallet friendly. Seating is available at two dining areas across the street from each other^ closing time is midnight.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3335236626	Kaen	140/64 Adunyaram Soi 7	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Car park		Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	4.0	฿฿	t	f	‘Kaen’ in Thai is a homonym with many meanings. Owner Chef Paisarn, who worked as executive chef at a 5-star resort, infuses those meanings into this restaurant in his hometown (Khon Kaen). The cuisine is contemporary Thai at its core (kaen), yet also playful, (kaen kaew), as in the recommended Massaman curry with lamb shank. Even the dining room reflects it — a large table with exposed heartwood (kaen mai) made at his family’s wood shop is a centrepiece.	pingliu	\N	\N
3338993703	Mana	420 Mu 21	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿฿	f	t	After working for years at Thai-Chinese restaurants in Bangkok, chef-owner Mana returned home to open his own outlet. He’s now been serving flavoursome Thai-Chinese-style seafood dishes that are easy on the pocketbook for over a decade. Inside his restaurant’s one-storey white building are two dining areas, one with AC and another open-air one. The oyster omelette and crispy salad with fish maw, shrimp and cashews are recommended.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3338726217	FishHouse	Kimpton Kitalay Samui	Thailand	Ko Samui	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view	https://www.kimptonkitalaysamui.com/koh-samui-restaurants/fish-house-restaurant-and-bar	Nessun premio	European	3.0	฿฿฿	t	t	Set inside the Kimpton Kitalay resort, FishHouse crafts à la carte European recipes using the freshest local ingredients. Take a seat on the deck overlooking the beach and enjoy the sea breeze and the lively atmosphere by the pool where sunbathers sip cocktails. Start with ceviche, bursting with fresh tropical passionfruit flavours and perfectly marinated diced seabass. The Black Paella with squid and squid ink is ideal to share.	paganialex	\N	\N
3334879476	Bang Por Seafood Takho	56/4 Mu 6	Thailand	Ko Samui	Great view		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Bang Por boasts an experienced kitchen team composed of local chefs who have worked here for many years. This simple beach-front restaurant is depicted by holiday vibes and Southern Thai seafood fare. The spicy stir-fried squid with herbs is cooked in a spicy curry paste and the grilled fish is sprinkled with mixed Thai herbs. The house shrimp paste is packed with aromatic plants and coconut chili and grilled before serving, hence the pungent aroma.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3330988025	Khao Horm	34/36 Mu 4	Thailand	Ko Samui	Car park		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Just 5 minutes from the airport, Khao Horm is a great spot to get your last-minute fill of delicious Southern Thai and local recipes before flying home. The family recipes have been passed down from generation to generation for over a century. We recommend the stir-fried minced pork whose yellow curry paste features a gutsy mix of spices. The main dining room is set in a large open-air pavilion. They also offer AC indoor dining and plenty of parking too.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3333523484	Long Dtai	Cape Fahn Hotel	Thailand	Ko Samui	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.longdtai.com	Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿฿	f	f	After crossing shallow waters, you reach this private island resort off Samui’s east coast. From the restaurant’s terrace, diners enjoy panoramic views of the bay as they sample chef David Thompson’s fab creations. His Southern Thai menu is deceptively simple and his consummate culinary talent is revealed in the details. Start with grilled squid, marinated in turmeric and coconut milk to accentuate its freshness. Marine sustainability is the name of the game here.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3337124497	The Ranch	The Ritz-Carlton Koh Samui	Thailand	Ko Samui	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/usmrz-the-ritz-carlton-koh-samui/dining	Nessun premio	Steakhouse	4.0	฿฿฿฿	t	f	The Ranch at The Ritz-Carlton Koh Samui is the place for meat lovers and the only real steakhouse on the island. The premium Australian beef is dry-aged in-house and served on hot plates with a wide range of sauces and side dishes, without forgetting a knockout line-up of grilled dishes and seafood options. High ceilings, wooden furnishings and a splendid display of old and new world wines set the scene in the smart dining room.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3337872685	Koh Thai Kitchen	Four Seasons Resort Koh Samui	Thailand	Ko Samui	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.fourseasons.com/kohsamui/dining/restaurants/koh	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿฿	t	t	Koh Thai Kitchen is located on a hilltop within the Four Seasons Hotel. The restaurant's alfresco dining areas sport a rustic style. Diners can enjoy southern and central Thai dishes made with premium ingredients such as local seafood, Australian lamb and Wagyu beef. All of which while breathing in the fresh air as you admire the drop-dead vista of sprawling jungle and blue sea dotted with nearby islands, as you snap the dramatic Instagram-perfect sunsets.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3336550528	Saffron	Banyan Tree Samui	Thailand	Ko Samui	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://www.banyantree.com/thailand/samui/dining/saffron	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	Elegantly appointed with floor-to-ceiling windows, contemporary lighting and dark wooden furnishings, Saffron also offers alfresco dining with a fantastic view. You can choose from à la carte and tasting menus. The roast duck red curry is paired with a thick sweet and spicy sauce, a fresh lychee and pineapple compote and roasted skin that excite the tastebuds. The fried softshell crab salad with lychee and passionfruit is also a must.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3334304434	Phensiri	80/30 Mu 3	Thailand	Ko Samui	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.phensiri.com	Nessun premio	Thai, Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Phensiri is a must-visit for Thai and Southern Thai cuisine. Using high-quality local ingredients, the chef-owner ensures each dish is well-balanced and flavourful. A no-fuss approach delivers authentic flavours, with the spice level adjustable to your liking. The welcoming atmosphere is enhanced by Thai-style décor, and the attentive staff, fluent in English, make things easy for tourists. Popular with both locals and visitors, it is especially busy at lunchtime and dinner.	scarpatacco	\N	\N
3337826259	Banrimbung	372/21 Mu 2	Thailand	Nakhon Pathom	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Serving family-style Thai cuisine on a large pond in Nakhon Pathom since 2001, the spacious restaurant offers waterside seating in five distinct seating areas with live music during dinner. Everything on the menu is fresh, with the fish and seafood kept alive until cooked. Two highlights are stir-fried prawns with shrimp oil and fried seabass with fish sauce and spicy green mango salad. The restaurant is family-friendly, with a kids’ zone in the garden for young diners to enjoy.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3331495795	Loong Loy Pa Lan	1010 Phet Kasem Road	Thailand	Nakhon Pathom	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	A passion for wild ingredients like wild boar, frogs, seafood, and even greens, along with a zeal for local flavours—intense, tangy, and spicy—shapes everything on the menu here. The stir-fried wild boar with chilies and the tom yam soup with snakehead fish are both recommended, as is the seafood cooked according to local recipes. The atmosphere is relaxed and homely, with air-conditioned dining rooms and outdoor seating available.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3337676024	Somchai Go Tae (Bang Len)	18/13 Mu 1	Thailand	Nakhon Pathom	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese, Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Go Tae, the owner of this Thai-Chinese restaurant, got his start almost 80 years ago selling stewed duck noodle soup on a boat, before heading to dry land to open this place. Inside the three-storey building (topped with a giant rooftop duck statue), the simple dining room has a roasting and stewing station. The menu features old-school Thai-Chinese fare, including the recommended stewed duck and live river prawn cooked to your preference.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3330548803	Jum Khao	104/4 Thetsaban 26 Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Great view		Nessun premio	Isan	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Modestly designed, Jum Khao embraces local influences and serves Isan fare with a little flair. There are a few à la carte and seasonal dishes but a wide variety of som tum options, popular comfort food like crispy grilled chicken wings, golden-brown garlic chips and Korat-style stir-fried rice noodles. The tricolour sticky rice combines butterfly pea purple, turmeric yellow and the natural white and is served with three dips and raw vegetables in a cute bamboo basket.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3337217887	Kai Yang Sueb Siri	49 Sueb Siri Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	3.0	฿฿	t	t	This 50-year-old family-run business has a large cooking station at the front that radiates a welcoming smell of grilled chicken. Most customers come in big groups to share popular Isan dishes. Three varieties of tender chicken are served^ the crowd favourite is their signature barbequed chicken marinated in Thai herbs. The fermented fish sauce, made daily, emits an encapsulating aroma and the papaya salad hits the perfect balance between spicy and sour.	shirocky	\N	\N
3337554228	Yong Poo Ob	1844/1 Mittraphap Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	฿฿	f	f	It’s hard to miss this restaurant with its large orange crab statue out front. And you wouldn’t want to miss eating here either. Inside is a mix of industrial and rustic décor, with a stage for live music. A small English-style garden with a water fountain surrounded by trees provides tranquil outdoor dining. The fresh catch of shrimp, prawns and crabs are as fresh as can be, swimming in their tanks up until an order comes in. The signature baked glass noodles with hot pot crab is superb in a herby gravy^ the grilled tiger prawns and Thai spicy seafood sauce is also delightful.	raduionela	\N	\N
3333924720	Yommarat O-Cha	9-11 Yommarat Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	฿	t	t	The standout dish at this local favourite is the yentafo soup with fish balls, soy sauce and tofu. The flavour is pleasantly sweet and sour but this isn’t the spicy yentafo tomyum common in Bangkok. The soup is cooked fresh using a vibrant mix of condiments. Dry and wet options are available and all the great toppings are homemade.	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3338172755	Yung Khao	111 Mu 4	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Originally from Bangkok, they relocated to Pak Chong 10 years ago. The building is made from wood and bamboo, like many rural rice granaries (yung khao). On offer is southern-Thai dishes, using ingredients from the south as well as their own curry paste, to cook grandmother’s recipes. The deep-fried sand fish is a great starter and the yellow curry seabass emits a gloriously pungent turmeric aroma. Diners on the outdoor terrace enjoy a view of the mountains.	ferraroedoardo	\N	\N
3332589394	Khanom Jeen Mae Ploy	7/1 Mu 6	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	฿	f	f	The secret to Mae Ploy’s bouncy yet gooey noodles is the fermented rice flour from Ban Pra Dok. There’s a creamy, peppery spicy fish curry with coconut cream, a red chicken curry with offal, and a sweet, nutty peanut curry. The spicy fish curry has a lovely, aromatic fermented taste.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3339511673	Jay Noi Kratoke	115 Pibool La-lad Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿	f	f	This three-storey house with simple décor is family run and in its second generation. Jay Noi's house special of hao-dong is a popular local treat using sliced pork and spicy Isan sauce, chilli and roasted rice. The four pad mee Korat is also recommended. Its sticky rice noodles are fresh and go really well with the sweet and sour sauce, fresh bean sprouts and chives. You can order the homemade curry puff for take away, with a variety of optional sides.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3335843740	Chuan Kitchen	50/666 Mu 6	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	South East Asian	5.0	฿฿	f	f	With Singaporean chicken rice, Indonesian laksa and Malaysian Bak Kut Teh the highlights, Chuan Kitchen is the only restaurant in Nonthaburi offering this mix of national cuisine. Its stylish design is welcoming, with a high wooden ceiling, and floor-to-ceiling windows, accentuated by black stainless-steel frames and lighting. The fried typhoon soft shell crab stands out with its light crispy texture with a chilli, deep-fried crispy garlic and onion black bean sauce.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3339227515	Fried Banana Rama 5 (Bang Kruai - Sai Noi Road)	116 Bang Kruai - Sai Noi Road	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	฿	t	f	This spot is best known for its deep-fried bananas. Coated in crispy batter made from coconut and white sesame, they exude a rich coconut aroma. The sweet potato balls are another standout. Be prepared for queues during peak hours.	salajakub	\N	\N
3338955230	Banya	317 Tiwanon Road	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Banya, or ‘Grandma’s house’ in Thai, embodies this maternal spirit. The menu, conceived by acclaimed culinary teacher Rachadapa Amatayakul, comprises typical Thai fare, some rarer recipes and their famous homely signature – Khao Chae. Also popular is the homemade spotted knifefish with green curry^ the tender fish is an umami pleasure in an intense mix of herbs broiled in rich Thai curry. No wonder this place is always crowded with locals and foreigners.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3339637109	Dhabkwan	Dhabkwan Resort	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.dhabkwan.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Located in a teak house in the middle of Dhabkwan Resort, this traditional Thai restaurant opens onto a tranquil lotus pond and inviting gardens. The atmosphere perfectly matches the authentic Thai menu, which includes hard-to-find dishes like Miang Kam with lotus petals and santol curry with roasted pork. Making it even more authentic, meals are served on Benjarong porcelain. Dhabkwan also offers Thai cookery classes and is available for events.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3337426941	Kaithong Original	164/13-15 Soi Chaeng Watthana-Pak Kret 33	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	4.0	฿฿	f	f	This family-run establishment is renowned for its traditional recipes, serving fresh meat and seafood flavours in simple yet refined and lightly seasoned dishes. Catering to different tastes, the stir-fried liver with garlic is made with either pork or chicken liver. The inviting, comfortable space can also accommodate larger groups.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3330328717	Beach Grill and Bar	Devasom Khao Lak Beach Resort & Villas	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.devasom.com/khaolak/dining/devasom-beach-grill-and-bar	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	฿฿฿	f	t	Offering a relaxing setting with indoor and outdoor seating perfect for enjoying cocktails and a delightful mix of Mediterranean dishes, against the backdrop of the evening sunset. Specialising in fresh seafood grilled over a wood-burning stove, the restaurant's standout dish is a seafood pizza with shrimp, squid, mussels, and mozzarella. Complete your dining experience with a delicious dessert like crispy fried bananas served with coconut milk ice cream.	ruggieripablo	\N	\N
3331856067	Khanom Chin Pa Son	3 Borirak Bamrung Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	t	f	Across from a Chinese shrine, this self-service buffet has been drawing devotees for over 30 years with its tasty khanom chin and four curry options to mix and match. Pick from a wide range of condiments, fresh vegetables, boiled egg and crispy anchovies. Lunchtime is always busy, so arrive early.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3331489815	Khanom Jeen Baan Bang Kan	Mu 4	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	฿	t	t	For over 20 years, locals have enjoyed this shop’s Khanom Jeen, or rice noodles, which are served with a choice of three curries and more than 20 types of fresh or pickled veggies. Noodles are unlimited, but save room for the refreshing cendol in coconut milk. Closed Thursday and Friday.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3336940496	Juumpo	GF	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park	https://www.hotelgahn.com/eat-and-drink/juumpo-family-recipes	Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	f	The cuisine of the local Baba (Chinese-Thai) people lives on here. Named in honour of the owner’s grandfather, a 'Juumpo' or chef on a Chinese boat more than 80 years ago and the source of many unique recipes, the open-air restaurant is fitted out with décor that reflects Chino-Portuguese design and culture. Baba-style coconut milk soup with shrimps and Thai herbs, chilli dip with shrimp, and fried fish with sweet and sour sauce are all recommended.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3332455538	Anuwat	201 Mu 4	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	f	f	There may be a big sign out front, but it’s the aromatic pork that’s been luring in the locals for more than 40 years. The grilled pork, BBQ pork and crispy pork belly are well marinated and grilled till succulent. Try any or all — plus steamed chicken — on a single plate served with rice.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3331090429	Bang Dean	16/10 Mu 1	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	t	f	Nearby the Takua Pa Government Office, this street food place serves Thai-Muslim dishes, including excellent chicken biryani, plus crispy rotis paired with savoury curries or sweet condensed milk and banana. Open for breakfast through late lunch, it closes when the food runs out.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3333797275	Khun Thip's Satay	184 Phet Kasem Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga			Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	f	f	Serving satay, and only satay, since 1975 – it’s now Phang-Nga’s iconic food. The 2-day marinated sauce smothers charcoal-grilled chicken, pork, pork intestine or shrimp. Our favourite is the tender pork satay with coconut aroma, rich peanut flavour and fresh cucumber relish.	popafarah	\N	\N
3334581430	Khrua Nong	132/8 Phet Kasem Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	The husband-and-wife team go to market every day to select fresh, local ingredients and seafood and offer a wide selection of Thai dishes. Check the blackboard for the specials which change every day, but the crispy softshell crab with a peppery chilli sauce is unmissable.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3332345999	Nern Khao View Talay	18/6 Mu 10	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.nernkhaoviewtalay.rnanagrand.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Nern Khao View Talay offers stunning views of mountains and sea from up high on a hill. Serving Thai and southern cuisine, the stir-fried pork with shrimp paste is a highlight. The aromatic paste mixes nicely with herbal notes and deep-fried shallot, while the thick sour curry soup with shrimp has a deep orange colour, tasty acacia omelette and plump shrimps. What about tackling that steep slope? There’s a shuttle service from the car park at the foot of the hill.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3332746621	Phi Sao	136/79 Mu 9	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	Delicious meals have been enjoyed at P’Saw for more than 40 years. Under a whitewashed pavilion-like structure, diners can enjoy the sea breeze, a view of the beach and southern-style dishes. The recipes, passed from the restaurant’s founder to her younger sister, offer something more personal and familial than their neighbouring restaurants. The baegu leaf salad with crispy shrimp and tom yum clear soup with young coconut deliver a delightful and flavourful experience.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3336058789	Thian Leng Bak Kut Teh	35 Mu 4	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	4.0	฿	f	t	Using heavenly recipes from Kedah, Malaysian Bak Kut Teh is a divine pork rib soup with Chinese herbs, served in a clay pot. The succulent slow-cooked meat simply slips off the bone. The chef is so confident about its tastiness, there’s a money-back guarantee for those who disagree!	gavrilovnora	\N	\N
3331763902	Gu Cherng	2F	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.krungsririver.com	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	฿฿฿	t	f	Gu cherng refers to the country’s former capital and the dining room, renovated in 2021, mixes elegant modern Chinese style with flashes of the traditional. Popular dishes include a variety of tasty dim-sum. The steamed prawn dumplings with seaweed and steamed rice noodles stuffed with deep-fried prawns use quality ingredients with delicately balanced flavours. The signature Peking duck pancakes use choice cuts of meat, thinly sliced, crispy and with no fat.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3339640821	Kampun Gai Yang	94/7 Mu 6	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿฿	t	t	Opened in 2017, this restaurant serves authentic Isan food in a commercial building on Rochana Road. Air-conditioned and filling two floors, the casual dining room is decorated with wood panels and other touches that suggest traditional Thai houses. The skilled chef cooks halal-friendly food following recipes from his grandmother, who is from Nakhon Phanom. His signature dish, Kampun grilled chicken, is recommended. The quality of service adds to the experience.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
