3333459202	Tonnam Riverview	26/7 Ban Len	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park,Great view		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Known for the grilled river prawns it has served since 1991, this family-friendly restaurant on the Chao Phraya River has two dining areas: on a raft and boat, respectively. Either way, diners enjoy gentle breezes and scenic views with their meals. The culinary offerings, which have grown since the restaurant first opened, are skilfully cooked using fresh local ingredients. The speciality, grilled river prawns served with a flavourful spicy sauce, is a must-try.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3334633832	Angeum	55/17 Mu 7	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park		Nessun premio	Vietnamese	5.0	฿฿	t	t	The story of Vietnamese food in Ayutthaya started over 150 years ago with the Vietnamese community in Bang Sai District. It continues at this modern two-floor restaurant smartly decorated with wooden walls, colourful paintings and a stylish bar. The menu may be short but it’s packed with authentic Vietnamese dishes. The skilled chef prepares everything using fresh quality ingredients. The signature dish, Nem Nuong is a delight to assemble and eat.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3333941173	Heh	158 Yaowarat Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning	https://www.hehphuket.com	Nessun premio	Australian Contemporary	4.0	฿฿฿	t	t	‘Heh’ is an expression of curiosity, according to the chef-owner who leads a youthful and creative kitchen. The aim is to bring Melbourne to the Andaman, combining quality ingredients from the Andaman Sea with Australian imports. The chef injects excitement into the unique menu without ever overcomplicating it. The charred broccoli with anchovy-miso sauce and crispy fish scales, and succulent charcoal-grilled Australian Wagyu short ribs are recommended.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
