3338704628	La Gaetana	352 Phuket Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	฿฿	f	t	It may be tiny, with 6 tables, but La Gaetana, decorated like an Italian house in warm colours, provides a warm welcome and is big on charm. They import most ingredients from Italy and make the sourdough, pasta, gelato and limoncello in-house. Chef Gianni cooks the fettucine with tomato sauce and crab meat using his family recipe from Campania. The menu is largely influenced by such southern classics. As Gianni takes a summer holiday each year, call ahead first.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3331593368	hom	InterContinental Phuket Resort	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park	https://www.hom-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	After a stroll through a serene garden walkway, you will find this restaurant inside the InterContinental Resort. The Portuguese chef showcases a fermentation-heavy concept on the menu, highlighting new sides to local produce. Leeks, betel leaves and pandan are just some of the ingredients that are given the fermentation treatment, in delicately executed dishes. The natural wine list is in keeping with the restaurant’s ethos, and the intimate atmosphere makes it ideal for a romantic dinner.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3336416681	O Cha Rot	72/1 Yaowarat Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	฿	f	f	In Old Phuket Town, a red sign sits above the white façade^ its Thai name in gold lettering declares: Delicious. The plump beef balls are packed with flavour^ beef slices tender^ bone broth fragrant^ and the soft noodles are perfectly cooked. Arrive early for lunch before it runs out.	shirocky	\N	\N
3333576311	Shrimp Noodles Ao Kae	76 Phoonphol Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	t	f	It has been crafting meticulous shrimp noodle bowls for over a decade. Tom yum and original shrimp flavour noodles, available as wet and dry options, come with the perfect number of condiments. Pork wontons are the standout! For intense flavour, try the dry tom yum noodles.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3331608874	Go Ang Seafood	226 Mu 2	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	฿฿฿	t	f	From humble origins as a small shop with a zinc roof, it’s now one of the most popular seafood restaurants with a comfortable interior and Chinese décor. Chef-owner Go Ang cooks the entire southern Thai menu. The blue swimming crab, horseshoe crab and mantis shrimp are sourced daily from 5 markets. The steamed crab with tangy seafood dip and fried mantis shrimp with garlic are delightful, while the Southern Thai spicy sour soup with seabass is also a must-try.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
3335351878	Kruvit Raft (Ban Laem Hin)	98/7  Ko Maphrao	Thailand	Phuket	Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	฿฿	f	f	To reach this floating restaurant near Ko Maphrao, take a 5-min boat ride across sparkling waters reflecting the sunshine. Onboard, panoramic views, a gentle breeze and uber-fresh seafood await. The distance from sea to plate couldn’t be shorter. Start with a freshly picked coconut before tucking into delicious southern and central Thai seafood. The grouper soup with Chinese soybean paste and stir-fried black tiger prawns with salt and chilli are highlights.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3336385847	Mook Manee	1120 Wiset Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Located near Rawai Beach, Mook Manee stands out for its array of live seafood for diners to choose from, including squid, tiger prawns, a variety of crabs, and 3kg Phuket rainbow lobster. The restaurant holds up to 300, but the best seats offer views of the vibrant seafood market trading outside. Menu highlights include the fragrant stir-fried clams with chilli paste. A wooden terrace on the beach is also available.	basileryan	\N	\N
3337267950	Go La	11 Kra Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	฿	t	t	In its third generation of family ownership, this is one of Phuket’s best Hokkien-style fried noodle joints. Its charm is conjured up by a concoction of special flavours, the sounds of the wok and charcoal smells. Order the yellow hokkien noodles with an extra egg for a creamier texture.	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3333558890	Loba Bang Niao	18/61 Mae Luan Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	฿	t	f	Loba was a traditional snack for Fujian Chinese in Phuket and this shop has remained consistent since day one. The semi-crispy pork offal and aromatic spices of the mixed loba blend well with a sweet chilli and crushed peanut sauce. The 4 deep-fried dishes are also mouth-watering treats.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3336970422	Chom Chan	242/2 Yaowarat Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	f	Chom Chan has flourished with its own charming character and refreshing ambiance. Situated in a small white house with a leafy façade, the interior is a blend of modern Sino-Portuguese with antique decoration. Some dishes are shared with the other restaurants but do try the fried crab’s spawn with chilli, pepper and garlic^ steamed minced pork with salty egg^ and deep-fried pork belly with salt.	ozmax	\N	\N
3330244589	Khrua Ohm	2/99 Mu 2	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	After a decade as a musician with a side gig of cooking for bandmates, these days Somphop finds himself enjoying daily walks through the market for fresh catches of the day and hand-cutting them for various southern Thai dishes served at his small, casual restaurant. Braised fish in salted soybean sauce^ prawns with salted eggs and acacia^ and wok-fried pork featuring the tender, succulent ‘armpit cut’ between the picnic shoulder and belly are not to be missed.	salajakub	\N	\N
3336405179	Samut	14/119 Mu 1	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.samutphuket.com	Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿฿฿฿	t	f	Samut (or ocean) is set in a traditional Thai-Chinese building decorated in an Oriental style, with dark teak wood. Previously the lobby of the adjacent hotel, it’s now a gastronomic destination. The set menu, with more than 10 dishes, tours the island’s coastline, offering seafood caught by local fishermen. The chef respects the traditions of the island, selecting flavours and fruits inspired by local creativity, including a reinterpretation of Phuket dim sum.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3335353821	Park Chinois	17 Berkeley Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://parkchinois.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	££££	t	f	Old fashioned glamour, strikingly rich surroundings and live music combine to great effect at this sumptuously decorated restaurant. The menu traverses the length of China, with dim sum at lunchtimes and afternoon tea at weekends. The delicious 'Duck de Chine' is roasted to order.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3336209759	Nitan	177/38 Mu 6	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.nitanphuket.com	Nessun premio	Southern Thai, Contemporary	5.0	฿฿฿	f	t	Nitan, or ’determination’ in Thai, may refer to the chef’s aim of creating a real gastronomic experience. This is most evident in the tasting menu and wine pairing, where quality seasonal and local ingredients inform the cooking. Contemporary techniques are used to prepare classic Southern Thai dishes, with well-balanced flavours and a dash of creativity. The restaurant has a warm vibe and is minimally decorated, with wooden furniture and a window into the kitchen.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3331776640	Royd	95/1 Dibuk Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining	https://www.restaurantroyd.com	Nessun premio	Southern Thai, Contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿	t	t	There are many courses and many delights to be found on the tasting menu at this cosy little restaurant. Seating is divided between tables and the counter, with room for just 12 guests in total^ there is an excellent flow to the parade of innovative Southern Thai dishes like crispy bee hoon topped with morning glory, which are all attractively presented and delivered by a likeable team. Accompany the fabulous cooking with a well-crafted cocktail pairing that uses techniques such as fermentation to make interesting drinks that complement the food well.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3330720322	Wagyu Steakhouse	Twinpalms Phuket Resort	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list	https://www.wagyuphuket.com	Nessun premio	Steakhouse	5.0	฿฿฿	t	t	Spanning two floors of the Twinpalms hotel, this restaurant’s elegant yet earthy interior and dimmed lighting make it the perfect setting for steak and wine lovers. Everything is on display: from the chefs in the open kitchen and the nice beef showcase with a small oyster bar, to the choice cuts of top-quality imported meats. Guests can choose their steak from the fridge before it is expertly grilled by the chefs. A choice of five high-end brands of knives is also on offer.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3338597121	Jadjan	4/27 Sakdidet Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	f	t	Chef Suthee, a former 5-star hotel chef, uses expertise to produce simple southern Thai fare that’s packed with flavour. The crab meat curry with betel leaves and southern Thai sour curry with fresh local fish and pineapple get our nod of approval.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3335785504	O Tao Bang Niao	362 Phuket Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	t	t	Since 1982, this family-run spot has been serving flavoursome O Tao, a stir-fried dish found only in Phuket. Made with seafood and battered taro, O Tao is cooked over a charcoal flame and boasts a combination of soft, gooey and crispy textures. They are well-balanced here, and the smoky aroma from the charcoal also helps to elevate the dish. Other options available include a fried crispy seafood omelette that is well worth ordering.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3337509421	Blue Elephant	96 Krabi Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.blueelephant.com/restaurant/phuket-restaurant	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿฿	t	t	Following the lead of Bangkok’s flagship, their colonial-style mansion with wood-panelled interior, wicker furnishings and louver shutters, set in lush gardens, pulls in the crowds. They serve a roll call of Thai classics, but the main attraction, the Peranakan Menu, for couples to share, is unique to Phuket. The signature Peranakan Tumee King Mackerel comes in large pieces of fish in a rich coconut curry with crispy okra. They also have a great cocktail selection.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3336921776	Buabok	Amanpuri Resort 118	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Great view,Valet parking	https://www.aman.com/resorts/amanpuri/dining/buabok	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿฿	t	f	Buabok is set in a tranquil resort that features reflective pools and swaying palms, creating the perfect backdrop for dining. Enjoy aromatic Thai cuisine beneath the pitched roof of an elegant wooden villa. From Thai salads to smooth curries, the menu is crafted from fresh local produce. Arrive before sunset to embrace the gentle pace of nature and stunning views of the Andaman Sea. Don't miss their rich, flavourful Panaeng Nuea, an Angus beef red curry.	longoethan	\N	\N
3339300617	Gorjan	161 Kra Road	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	t	If you're near Gorjan Bridge, consider this simple family-run eatery. Every dish is rife with rich flavours, and many are created from their own recipes. The owner is poised to cook your food to order, which ensures a personalised dining experience.	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3337894445	Hong Khao Tom Pla	5 Kra Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	There is always a queue in front of this small shop. The mainstay on the menu is seafood. Dishes are carefully prepared by the owner, and the fresh prawns are a must. Check the whiteboard for the daily catch.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3331703036	Jongjit Kitchen	9/1 Mu 4	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿	f	f	Southern recipes, affordable prices and down-to-earth hospitality – this is why locals pack out this family-run business at lunch and dinner. Their family recipes pack great intensity. The Phuketian stir-fried pork rump with salt is lovely, with tender meat and lip-smacking pork skin.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3338733911	Lertrod	17/7 Nai Yang Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Across from the airport, this bright air-conditioned restaurant flies under the radar but lands simple, satisfying central and southern Thai fare. The skilled chef sources quality ingredients from local farmers and fishermen. The deep-fried seabass with fish sauce never disappoints. For the spicy southern-Thai sour curry, choose from pickled bamboo, coconut shoots or pineapple. The photo-filled menu, written in Thai, English and Chinese, makes it easy for everyone.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3335843013	Peang-Prai	101/18 Soi Namtok Bang Toei	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	In the depths of the forest at the entrance to Bang Pae waterfall, two wooden pavilions stand connected by a terrace walkway. Here, a family-run restaurant faces a lagoon and a verdant wall of forest, while diners are accompanied by the welcoming calls of birds and gibbons. The tranquil ambiance is joined by traditional Thai and Southern Thai cooking, with local Phuket dishes standing out. Seasonal local clams are delicious and can be cooked many ways, including stir-fried with chilli paste.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3331348742	Sang Ka Sri	262/8 Yaowarat Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	This outlet with a red-brown zinc roof offers a menu of both individual and sharing dishes, with nicely balanced flavours. Despite its humble guise, Sang Ka Sri attracts a crowd, so be prepared to wait for a table before enjoying the fresh squid with herbs and tangy dressing.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3338108864	Royal China Club	40-42 Baker Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.royalchinagroup.co.uk/royalchinaclub	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	£££	f	f	Service is fast-paced and to the point, which is understandable considering how busy this restaurant always is. The large menu offers something for everyone and the lunchtime dim sum is very good^ at dinner try their more unusual Cantonese dishes.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3332749935	Ta Khai	Rosewood Hotel	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/phuket/dining/ta-khai	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿฿	t	f	Ta Khai means ‘fishing net’, and here diners can choose live seafood from the restaurant’s tank before a chef scoops it up and cooks it. Dishes, including the deep-fried white snapper with fish sauce, are flavoursome, with spicing slightly toned down if you wish, while two set menus offer a variety of items to try. Ask for a table on the lovely terrace for a panoramic view of the bay and cityscape beyond – or for something different, book a BBQ sala.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3332414398	Talung Thai	GF	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.paresaresorts.com/dining	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿฿	f	t	The views from Paresa Resort, high on a clifftop, are breathtaking at sunset. It’s an idyllic spot to sip cocktails, before moving to the terrace for sumptuous southern and central Thai cuisine. Start with mixed Thai canapés or the soft shell crab miang, followed by the fragrant stir-fried Phuket lobster. Don't forget to save room for the Thai-styled dessert.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3334010488	The Thai Library	Trisara Resort	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.trisara.com/sat-at-trisara	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿฿	t	t	Inspired by local recipes and ingredients, The Thai Library has created a refined, southern menu. Take the Massaman Plamuek for example, which uses local Andaman octopus in a sweet and creamy sauce, while the stir-fried jumbo black tiger prawns, with crispy garlic and chilli, sing subtle herbal notes. To top it off, it’s the perfect romantic experience with an intimate setting indoors and breezy sunset views on the outdoor terrace overlooking a secluded beach.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3331927637	Jaras	InterContinental Phuket Resort	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://phuket.intercontinental.com/dining/jaras	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Despite the luxury setting, Jaras retains honest roots. The intimate design draws influence from the Li Thai, Sukhothai era. The restaurant is named after the owner's grandma whose cooking inspired some of the recipes. Today’s chef embraces sustainability, serving a modern showcase of Thai flavours sourced locally, including microgreens grown on-site. For the full experience, request the Taste of Jaras tasting menu with wine pairing. Book at least 24 hours in advance.	donatidiego	\N	\N
3338628250	Suay	Baan Wana Park	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.suayrestaurant.com/suay-cherngtalay	Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	3.0	฿฿฿	f	f	The acronym of ‘sassy, unique, authentic and yummy’ may sound kitsch, but the airy and bright interior with its Portuguese-tiled floor is anything but. Outdoor seating with garden and live music is equally pleasant. Owner-chef Tammasak skilfully updates Thai food with modern techniques and artsy presentation. Dishes, including the signature grilled lemongrass lamb chops with papaya salsa, are seasoned with bold but well-judged spicing. Also try the crab cakes with Sriracha chili aioli and mango chutney.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3339942414	Meesapam Khun Yai Chian	56/8	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.meesapam.com	Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Grandma Chian opened this Hokkien restaurant in 1952. Her great-great grandchildren have stayed loyal to her recipes and proudly exhibit her cooking utensils. Serving Phuket favourites, the Mee Sapam, stir-fried Hokkien noodles with seafood, is great. The stir-fried oysters with crispy egg roll are beautifully crafted with beansprouts, kale and a tasty chilli sauce.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3335299991	Rabiang Talay	887 Soi Thetsaban Bang Pu 104	Thailand	Samut Prakan	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.rabiengta-le.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	฿฿	f	f	Opened in 1992, this restaurant serves flavourful seafood in a Lanna-style pavilion with relaxing views of mangroves and the sea, especially at sunset. There are three dining areas: one with AC, one open-air under high ceilings and hanging Northern Thai lamps, and one on the terrace. The food is prepared in an open kitchen and made with fresh ingredients, including some from onsite seafood tanks^ the signature stir-fried crab with salted egg is recommended.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3333886984	Day & Night	83/25 Liang Mueang Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park	https://www.dayandnight.co.th	Nessun premio	International	3.0	฿฿	f	f	This enchanting, almost English-looking country pub draws tourists like bees to honey. Boasting a bright, breezy vibe, it serves international favourites, from steak to pizzas and light snacks, with a tempting array of cocktails and craft beers. The fresh watermelon topped with dry salmon and served with a spicy salad dressing is sweet and juicy, while another popular local delicacy, bingsu, salted egg yolk, offers a creamy scent and texture. Smooth live music in the evenings.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3335614035	Lam Phu 2	23/1 Mu 3	Thailand	Surat Thani	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view		Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Watch the fishing boats on Tapi River while enjoying a bright and airy setting and local seafood cooked southern style. The oyster omelette is gorgeous with a crispy egg base, spot-on seasoning and fresh local oysters^ it goes well with steamed rice. The tender stir-fried squid with salted eggs is packed with flavour and flanked by an impressively creamy sauce. With over 100 seats, there is ample room for large groups to enjoy the scenic view.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3335730711	Khao Kriab Pak Mor Talat Na San Jao	Na San Jao Market	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	f	f	The veteran stall-owner has been making her delicious dumplings for decades in this famous food cart in Na San Jao market. The thin steamed rice dumplings combine a sweet, gooey texture with a savoury filling, made with minced pork, crushed peanuts and herbs in creamy coconut milk.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3330252965	Heng Khao Moo Daeng	428/1 Namueang Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿	t	t	This simple eatery is always bustling at lunchtime with queues for both dine-in and takeout. The owner's inviting and chatty demeanour sets the scene. His signature barbeque pork comes with crispy pork and sweet sausage inside and a large portion only costs 40 baht.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3331720504	Krua Samchai	282/1 Phalochai Road	Thailand	Ubon Ratchathani	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Two roosters stand guard at the entrance. Krua Samchai is famous for serving iconic Isan food befitting of the region. Fresh fish from the Mekong and Mun rivers is cooked using the chef's secret mix of herbs and spices that produces a powerful aroma. The grilled chicken has a crispy golden skin from the charcoal flame but retains its juicy meat. The Isan-style spicy fish maw and bamboo shoot soup uses tiliacora juice to perfection.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3333554992	Chomjan	119/1 Mu 8	Thailand	Ubon Ratchathani	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	On the banks of the Mun River, next to a 100-year-old bridge, sits Chomjan, popular with locals and non-locals enjoying penetrating sunsets, a fresh river breeze and live music across different themed dining areas. It caters for everyone, serving classic Thai, Isan and international dishes and fresh local fish. The deep-fried snakehead fish with stir-fried eggplant is recommended^ the juicy giant catfish with fresh herbal soup is also delightful.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3335915327	Santi	101-17 Chawala Nok Road	Thailand	Ubon Ratchathani	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Diners can sit inside or roadside in this simple, open-air restaurant. Thai-Chinese is the fare and dishes are prepared at the front. The sound of the wok and sight of the flames make an impressive spectacle. The stir-fried minced pork with olives is a must for its smoky, intense flavours. The deep-fried seabass with sweet fish sauce takes a little longer to prepare but the result is a fantastically crispy skin that goes well with the homemade spicy sauce.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3338436611	Lab Mu Worachai	26/3 Posri Road	Thailand	Udon Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Pork reigns supreme at this traditional Isan eatery, which may be renowned for its namesake Lab Mu – minced pork, skin and liver – but the flavourful Somtum Lao is another standout. Lunchtime can get hectic, but service is swift. The sharing sets of four to six dishes are perfect for groups.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3337750297	Som Tum Jae Kai (Asavamit Road)	230/28 Asavamit Road	Thailand	Udon Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	4.0	฿	t	f	This family-operated lunch spot has been a popular haunt for half a century. The dishes get their distinctive flavour from their home-made fermented fish sauce. This tasty addition elevates favourites such as mixed som tum with pork crackling and fermented sausage.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3335998900	Baan Chik Pork Noodles	89/3-4 Naresoun Road	Thailand	Udon Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	฿	f	f	This eatery has thrived in a traditional shophouse for over 30 years. Choose between the original flavour and tasty tom yum with its fresh lime and roasted peanut aroma, served with or without soup.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3331118195	Pa Noi Beef Noodles	57/8 Sisuttha Road	Thailand	Udon Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	f	f	The aroma of beef noodle soup greets diners at this popular eatery. The distinctive tamarind chilli paste pairs perfectly with deep-fried chicken skin or mixed into the noodles. The boat noodles with rich flavours are also a must-try.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3338087456	Rabiang Patchanee	53/1 Bannon Road	Thailand	Udon Thani	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Popular with local families, this restaurant focuses primarily on meat and freshwater fish, serving Chinese, Vietnamese, and Thai fare. They trade on authentic Thai flavours and daily specials featuring the freshest ingredients. The highlight dishes, which have been passed down for 30 years, are crispy duck topped with crab meat and gravy, and Vietnamese stuffed omelette. Make sure to book outdoor seats with a view of the pond.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3333009306	Hakkasan Bodrum	Gölköy Mahallesi	Türkiye	Bodrum	Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking	https://hakkasan.com/bodrum/	Nessun premio	Cantonese, Modern Cuisine	4.0	₺₺₺	t	t	Located in the Mandarin Oriental hotel against the wonderful backdrop of the glistening Aegean Sea, and with an elegant dining space done out in wood, this floating open-air restaurant is stunning. Hakkasan is a renowned chain bringing a luxurious take on Cantonese cuisine to your table. Think authentic Peking duck or grilled lamb chops, but elevated with fresh garnishes and rich sauces. For a chic night out, Hakkasan is just the place!	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3333386160	Mezra Yalıkavak	Dirmil Mahallesi	Türkiye	Bodrum	Counter dining	https://www.mezrayalikavak.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Turkish	3.0	₺₺₺₺	f	t	Large glass façades lend an open feel to give this stylish industrial-style space. On the way to your table, you walk past the lounge bar and the stage where concerts are occasionally held. Right outside the restaurant, there is a vegetable garden and some livestock^ the chef also has his own farm a short distance away. Local produce is central to the modern take on Turkish cuisine served here. Open-fire cooking and preservation techniques such as pickling complement new culinary trends. For example, the chef marinates lamb saddle in a poppy seed crust and then flame-grills it. This is accompanied by a cauliflower cream, an intense lamb jus and garlic-infused oil. The attention to detail is captivating.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3332227421	Oi Filoi	Koyunbaba	Türkiye	Bodrum	Interesting wine list,Terrace		Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	₺₺	t	t	Oi Filoi is an open-air restaurant shaded by two overarching trees. The charm of this setting is accentuated by warm lighting and Greek background music. The latter is no accident: the kitchen team here specialise in serving up classic Greek dishes with subtle contemporary twists. Think medium-rare lamb souvlaki with fresh tzatziki, barbecued sweet peppers and a toasted bun drenched in meat jus. If you would prefer moussaka, you will also, naturally, find that on the menu. And be sure to take advantage of the sommelier's knowledge – her carefully selected Turkish gems are a perfect match for this cuisine.	ozmax	\N	\N
3335018325	Isola Manzara	Eskiçeşme Mahallesi	Türkiye	Bodrum	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.isolarestaurant.com/bodrum/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	₺₺	t	t	When you take a seat on the terrace overlooking the beautiful Bodrum Castle, you will feel like you are on an island. For the time of a meal, you are cut off from the rest of the world here, your only task being to enjoy delicious southern Italian cuisine. Parmigiana di melanzane, creamy risotto ai gamberi, sea bass with tomato and capers: the menu features all the classics brimming with those familiar flavours that will transport you to the heart of Italy.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
