3332205025	Bar des Prés - Mayfair	16 Albemarle Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.bardespres.com/london-restaurant/	Nessun premio	Asian	5.0	££££	t	f	From the Mayfair postcode to the impressive marble counter, there is a luxury feel to this first international venture from French celebrity chef Cyril Lignac. Sharing a name with its pre-cursor in Saint-Germain, it also mirrors that restaurant's Japanese-influenced approach – expect maki, sashimi and miso black cod. For the terrific desserts, you travel back to France for classics like mille-feuille, tarte fine and profiteroles.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3338028946	Lucky Cat by Gordon Ramsay	10 Grosvenor Square	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.gordonramsayrestaurants.com/lucky-cat	Nessun premio	Asian	5.0	£££	t	t	Gordon Ramsay’s foray into Asian culture is a moody, masculine space in the former Maze, with a chef's table, a striking bar, a banging soundtrack and a fun feel. Accomplished Japanese and Chinese dishes blend British ingredients and are designed for sharing^ the bonito fried duck leg bao is a must-try.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3338305378	Sexy Fish	4-6 Berkeley Square	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://sexyfish.com/	Nessun premio	Asian	5.0	£££	f	t	Everyone will have an opinion about the name but what’s indisputable is that this is a very good looking restaurant, with works by Frank Gehry and Damien Hirst, and a stunning ceiling by Michael Roberts. The fish comes with various Asian influences but don’t ignore the meat dishes like the beef rib skewers.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3339409866	YiQi	14 Lisle Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	http://www.yiqipanasia.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Asian	4.0	££	t	t	Thailand, Malaysia and Singapore are the three countries that feature most prominently at this relative newcomer to Chinatown, which opened in 2024. Spread over two floors, it’s run by an eager and professional team who provide attentive service and offer helpful advice when you’re leafing through the extensive menu. The highlights of that menu include moreish salt and pepper squid, flavoursome whole grilled silver pomfret, street food style morning glory and succulent charcoal chicken wings – they’re all generous in size, so come with family or friends and share.	monticristian	\N	\N
3338198648	Fischer's	50 Marylebone High Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.fischers.co.uk	Nessun premio	Austrian	5.0	£££	t	t	The spirit of old Vienna is alive and well at this Austrian café and konditorei that comes from the same stable as The Wolseley and Brasserie Zédel, meaning it’s a slick and well-run sort of place. It’s perennially packed too, whether people are coming in for eggs and viennoiserie at brunch or cake in the afternoon. At lunch and dinner, the menu is a roll-call of Central European favourites, including a selection of sausages and some cracking schnitzels that are well worth getting with the Holstein garnish.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3336466593	Ibai	90 Bartholomew Close	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://ibai.london/	Nessun premio	Basque	3.0	£££	t	f	Large, airy and with an industrial-chic vibe that perfectly matches the buzz of its open kitchen, there’s something quite cool about Ibai. Backed by one of the co-owners of Lurra and Donostia, it takes those restaurants’ love of Basque cooking and leans it further towards the region’s French influences. The signature ‘Croque Ibai’ is a prime example and a delicious pintxo to start your meal with. Quality ingredients are used throughout, treated with care and often cooked over fire. Wine enthusiasts will be impressed by the well-stocked cellar.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3335238571	Lurra	9 Seymour Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.lurra.co.uk	Nessun premio	Basque	5.0	££££	t	f	Its name means ‘land’ in Basque and reflects their use of the freshest produce, cooked over a charcoal grill. Choose tasty nibbles or sharing plates like 14 year old Galician beef, whole grilled turbot or slow-cooked shoulder of lamb.	monticristian	\N	\N
3332122701	Donostia	10 Seymour Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.donostia.co.uk	Nessun premio	Basque, Spanish	3.0	£££	t	t	Perch at the counter or sit at one of the tables in this fun, warmly run little spot and enjoy a selection of pintxos and tapas inspired by the food of San Sebastián. House specialities such as gilda, bacalao and txuleta are always worth ordering. Just one dessert is offered, but when it’s Basque cheesecake as wonderfully creamy as this, who would want anything else?	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3331922719	Café Deco	43 Store Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.cafe-deco.co.uk/	Nessun premio	British Contemporary	3.0	££	f	f	The chefs also get involved in the service here at this simply furnished, intimate restaurant. Their dishes are fresh, seasonal, appealingly straightforward and packed with flavour, whether that’s cured ham hock, a lovely smoked eel pie or their delicious chicken. It's one of those relaxed restaurants where you know you’re in the hands of a clued-up and experienced team.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3336703105	Cora Pearl	30 Henrietta Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.corapearl.co.uk	Nessun premio	British Contemporary	5.0	££	t	t	Named after an infamous courtesan, this elegant restaurant is set in a characterful townhouse just round the corner from what's affectionately known as “The Actors’ Church”. Inside, there’s a buzz to the atmosphere and a rich, cosy bistro feel^ the concise menu focuses on seasonal British produce in fresh, unfussy and boldly flavoured dishes. Make sure you order a side of the kitchen's clever, original take on simple chips, which are utterly delicious. The smooth and attentive service team do a great job with such a busy restaurant.	serafinidmitri	\N	\N
3333718098	The Grill	53 Park Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.dorchestercollection.com/en/london/the-dorchester/restaurants-bars/the-grill-at-the-dorchester/	Nessun premio	British Contemporary	3.0	£££	f	t	The Grill at The Dorchester Hotel might be carrying a name loaded with history, but that’s no indication of the look or the food. Bright, modern décor and a formal team make you feel cossetted, while the ornate ceiling is something of a talking point. The cooking mixes classical flavours with modern techniques, on a menu that features luxury dishes to share like skate wing, rib-eye steak and 'all the chicken'. The set lunch menu offers value for money and they list some unusual wines by the glass.	polakcristina	\N	\N
3335312847	Canton Blue	1 Grosvenor Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://www.peninsula.com/en/london/hotel-fine-dining/canton-blue	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	££££	f	t	Housed inside the spectacular Peninsula Hotel, this Cantonese restaurant is part of a brand housed inside their hotels around the world. The London version boasts its own entrance at the side of the hotel and a sumptuous cocktail bar, Little Blue, which is the perfect way to kick off a rather glamorous evening. The restaurant itself is equally stylish, and the extensive menu offers a wide selection of authentic, flavoursome dishes, from finely executed dim sum to Peking duck for two. The interesting wine list includes a selection of Chinese rice wines by the glass.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3339433152	Dim Sum Duck	124 King's Cross Road	United Kingdom	London			Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	£	t	f	If you're thinking of eating at this small, family owned 'simple shop', do ensure you get here early as it doesn't take bookings and is deservedly popular. A one-hour wait is not unusual but the team manage the queue well and once you're sat either in the lively interior or under the pavement gazebo, you can dive into the wide-ranging Cantonese menu. The authentic dishes are carefully cooked using good quality ingredients, with bold and well-defined flavours present in options like the xiaolong bao and the cheung fun.	salajakub	\N	\N
3330742178	Barshu	28 Frith Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://barshurestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	££	f	f	The fiery flavours of China's Sichuan province are the draw here, although numerous other regions of China are well catered for too. The menu highlights both new and signature dishes, enlivened by authentic spicing – the legendary chillies and peppers are imported directly from China – and plenty of these generously proportioned dishes are great for sharing. Carved wood and lanterns decorate the room.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3337830057	Hakkasan Hanway Place	8 Hanway Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://hakkasan.com	Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	££££	f	f	The very first Hakkasan continues to offer a great night out, thanks to its moody, sensual looks and glamorous, energetic atmosphere. It's well-suited to both a romantic date or a group celebration, and it's certainly worth arriving early for a cocktail or two in the bar. Luxury Cantonese specialities are plentiful across the choice of menus, with the set 'Signature' options representing the best value for money.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3335257583	Hakkasan Mayfair	17 Bruton Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://hakkasan.com	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	££££	f	t	This seductive subterranean spot beckons you in through its discreet entrance on Bruton Street, immediately transporting you to somewhere altogether more thrilling. The ground floor is great for lunchtime dim sum, but if you’re here for dinner ask for a table on the lower floor, which has a more energising atmosphere. The extensive menus feature a roll-call of luxury ingredients, from whole native lobster to black truffle roasted duck.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3336492896	Imperial Treasure	9 Waterloo Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.imperialtreasure.com/uk/	Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	££££	f	f	The first London outpost of this globally renowned group is housed in an imposing former bank, which provides a luxurious backdrop for the traditional, mostly Cantonese cooking. White leather, onyx walls and wood partitions provide some intimacy amongst the opulence, and the extensive selection of dishes offer ample flavour. If you’re after money-is-no-object luxury, look no further than their signature Peking duck with caviar, but you'll still have a great time with the crispy pork belly and honey-glazed char siu pork.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3330178837	Labri	2F	Vietnam	Hanoi	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.labribistro.com	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	₫₫₫	f	f	A neon sign in the upstairs window is the clue to finding this modern-day bistro, tucked away on the 2nd floor of a nondescript building. Abri is French for shelter and the restaurant imbues a sense of cosy luxury. The open kitchen takes centre stage and four huge crystal chandeliers hang from the ceiling. The chef delivers virtuoso cuisine using French techniques and Vietnamese ingredients. For the full experience, opt for the 7-course menu.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3330721826	MiMi Mei Fair	55 Curzon Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://mimimeifair.com	Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	£££	t	t	An opulent Georgian Townhouse whose décor takes its inspiration from early 20C Chinese interiors. Sit in one of the ground floor booths or in the brighter first floor 'Parlour'. The wide-ranging menu offers classic Chinese dishes^ wood-fire roasted Peking Duck is the specialty and sharing is encouraged.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3337493549	Yauatcha Soho	15 Broadwick Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://yauatcha.com/soho/	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	£££	f	f	The ground floor of this lively, contemporary Chinese restaurant features cabinets full of pastries and chocolates – but ask to sit in the more atmospheric basement, with its celestial ceiling lights, tropical fish tanks and glimpses into the busy kitchen. The extensive menu offers something for everyone, and over-ordering is easy to do.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3334109758	Langan's Brasserie	Stratton Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.langansbrasserie.com	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	5.0	££	t	f	Few London restaurants can boast quite as colourful a history as this Mayfair institution, which was a veritable trailblazer when it opened back in the 1970s. Now refreshed and relaunched, it retains much of what made it so popular in its heyday, particularly when it comes to its menu^ it has something for everyone and every occasion, so you can expect to find all the brasserie classics, from Caesar salad and fish pie, to beef Rossini and rum baba.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3336160505	Kinkally	43 Charlotte Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kinkally.co.uk	Nessun premio	Eastern European	5.0	££	t	f	Offering something original to the Charlotte Street dining scene, this trendy restaurant takes its name from the Georgian dish khinkali. These dumplings come with a ‘handle’ at the top and fillings could include langoustines, pumpkin or beef. Accompanying the khinkali are a selection of Georgian-influenced small and large plates, from chkmeruli to pkhali. Keep the night going with a trip to Kinky, their basement bar serving a selection of creative cocktails, accompanied by a techno soundtrack and the same fabulous buzz as the restaurant.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3330351838	Arlington	20 Arlington Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.arlington.london/	Nessun premio	European	5.0	£££	f	t	The much-missed Le Caprice, a celebrity-laden London icon in the affluent environs of St James’s, has been reborn as Arlington. It has the same charming décor as its predecessor, all black-and-white photographs and ’20s elegance, with the banquettes at the back the best seats in the house. The menu dispenses with anything too trendy and instead keeps things classic and wholly enjoyable – think dressed Dorset crab, chicken Milanese and one of the best fishcakes in London. The service team play their part by running the place with a terrific efficiency.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3336040081	Dovetale	3 Berkeley Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.1hotels.com/mayfair/taste/dovetale	Nessun premio	European	5.0	£££	t	t	Like the hotel in which it sits – 1 Hotel Mayfair – Dovetale makes good use of natural materials and plenty of plants to create a warm, bright environment. It also has a great terrace and a welcoming atmosphere. The menu looks to Europe for its contemporary dishes^ go for one to be shared, like the whole roasted 'Somerset Saxon' chicken. If you’re after a bit of nostalgia, you can design your own Knickerbocker Glory for dessert.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3339822283	Six Portland Road	6 Portland Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://sixportlandroad.com	Nessun premio	European	5.0	£££	f	t	Tucked away off Holland Park Avenue, this intimate neighbourhood bistro is sure to become one of your favourite haunts. The concise European menu changes according to the ingredients available and dishes are robust, skilfully constructed and easy-to-eat.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3332800655	The Wolseley	160 Piccadilly	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.thewolseley.com	Nessun premio	European	5.0	£££	f	t	Like the other restaurants in this group, The Wolseley serves classic European dishes in an elegant setting with a buzzing atmosphere – well-organised service ensures that everything runs like clockwork even in a packed dining room. The extensive menu features top quality seafood dishes, from clams and oysters to crevettes and caviar. The sweet-toothed among you will not be disappointed by a large dessert menu that includes apple strudel and a choice of coupes.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3336424581	Caia	46 Golborne Road	United Kingdom	London		https://caia.london	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	£££	f	f	‘Fire, wine, vinyl’ it says outside this cool Notting Hill spot – and that pretty much sums it up. The sharing plates benefit from the kitchen’s skill at cooking over an open fire – don’t miss the black carrot with sea urchin sauce^ wines are varied and well chosen^ and downstairs a DJ delves deep into a diverse album collection. Come with friends for a fun night out.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3339723961	Levan	12-16 Blenheim Grove	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.levanlondon.co.uk	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	££	t	f	You can expect a good soundtrack playing over the speakers at this lively, friendly local restaurant named after DJ Larry Levan. The menu is a sharing plates affair – with dishes of mostly European influence – but there's also a tasting menu option, which allows you to sample more of the carefully prepared, original dishes. Be sure to start with the comté fries, and look out for the range of natural wines from smaller producers – more of which are available in Bar Levan next door. The friendly, attentive service team ensure there's a laid-back vibe to proceedings.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3332422261	Sesta	52 Wilton Way	United Kingdom	London		https://www.sesta.co.uk	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	£££	f	t	Fans of Pidgin had little time to mourn its closure in 2024 as it quickly reopened as Sesta, thanks to the original restaurant’s former chef. The look of the room is similar, but gone is the tasting menu and in its place is an appealing à la carte, which includes delicious snacks such as pea and ham fritters and a beef ragu toastie. British ingredients like Yorkshire chicken and Chalkstream trout sit alongside European and Asian influences from dolma to tempura. There’s a short but terrific cocktail list and plenty of natural wines – and the delightful staff sashay around the small space in an impressively efficient way.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3336733660	Sune	129A Pritchard's Road	United Kingdom	London	Counter dining	https://www.sune.restaurant	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	£££	t	t	Sune (pronounced ‘sooner’) has the feel of a small wine bar, but the heart of a great neighbourhood restaurant. Its fluid menu lists around 14 sharing plates, which show an admirable restraint so that dishes are never overcrowded^ the focus is on simple combinations of complementary flavours that are robust and satisfying. So, succulent pork collar might be paired with crisp, bitter tardive, and wild sea bass with charred greens. The delightful young service team ensure the arrival of dishes is well paced, so one never has to resort to the sort of plate shuffling choreography that sometimes blights similar places.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3335389445	The Baring	55 Baring Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.thebaring.co.uk/	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	££	t	t	It may look like just another renovated pub in a smart residential street, but the food here displays far more imagination and ability that usual gastropub fare. There are influences from across Europe, with dishes that are uncluttered yet full of flavour^ the quail shish is already a favourite starter for many. They’ve gone for cool simplicity with the décor^ and service that is warm and outgoing.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3332490541	Caractère	209 Westbourne Park Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.caractererestaurant.com	Nessun premio	European Contemporary, European	5.0	££££	f	t	Never judge a book by its cover' certainly rings true here, as within this former pub sits a convivial and really quite stylish restaurant, where sophisticated cooking combines with efficient, unstuffy service. Alongside an à la carte, you have the option to ‘build your own’ 5 course tasting menu by selecting one dish from each of their ‘character’ profiles^ these range from 'Subtle' (such as Acquerello risotto) to 'Robust' (roast lamb, perhaps) and finish with 'Greedy' for dessert. Top-notch ingredients and strong classical technique run throughout.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3333237153	Donia	2.14 Top Floor Kingly Court	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.doniarestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Filipino	3.0	££	t	f	Occupying the site where its neighbours Imad’s Syrian Kitchen and Darjeeling Express both started out, Donia is a hugely likeable Filipino restaurant that’ll have you googling flights to Manila before you know it. The young, Filipino-born owner grew up in the UK so expect to see plenty of homegrown produce along with those sweet and sour flavours. Crisp adobo mushroom croquetas are a must, as are the succulent chicken Inasal and the lechon (suckling pig) served with a lovely liver and peppercorn sauce. Bring friends, ignore the slightly testing acoustics and share the love.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3335795394	64 Goodge Street	64 Goodge Street	United Kingdom	London	Interesting wine list	https://64goodgestreet.co.uk	Nessun premio	French	4.0	£££	t	f	Sister restaurant to Portland and Clipstone, this small bistro deluxe delivers intimate, relaxed surroundings in which to enjoy a menu based around classical French cooking. British Racing Green walls blend with simple polished wood, candle-lit tables and wicker chairs, while the semi-open kitchen brings a livelier atmosphere to one end of the room. Fine ingredients are used to excellent effect in bold, gutsy combinations that deliver simply delicious results^ ensure you save room to finish with the greengage Tatin or the textbook Paris-Brest. Wine connoisseurs should look out for the 'Cellar List' and its many gems.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3331547365	Bob Bob Ricard City	Level 3	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://bobbobricard.com/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	£££	f	f	Sister to the iconic Soho original is this impressively ostentatious brasserie deluxe, set on the third level of the Cheesegrater building. Ensconce yourself in a booth, find the button and ‘Press for Champagne’. The classic French dishes are hearty and full of flavour with some luxury touches^ for dessert, the tarte Tatin is a must.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3333193366	Bouchon Racine	66 Cowcross Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.bouchonracine.com	Nessun premio	French	5.0	££	f	t	Those with fond memories of the original Racine in Knightsbridge rejoiced when chef Henry Harris opened a new version in 2022. Racine Mark II is just a few steps from Farringdon Station, located above the Three Compasses pub. The blackboard menu is a veritable rollcall of classic French bistro dishes, from escargots to rabbit, duck confit to steak tartare. There are so many tempting dishes^ just be sure to end with the terrific crème caramel.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3335203546	Brasserie Zédel	20 Sherwood Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.brasseriezedel.com/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	££	t	t	With all its art deco flourishes and distinctively French glamour, Zédel is a restaurant that still delivers a certain expectant excitement as you descend the stairs towards the grand basement brasserie. Expect a roll-call of classic French dishes on the extensive menu, from snails to coq au vin, duck confit to profiteroles. It’s a permanently bustling place with live music and plenty of atmosphere, plus both a cocktail bar and cabaret venue attached.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3331280543	Cabotte	48 Gresham Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.cabotte.co.uk	Nessun premio	French	3.0	£££	t	t	Classic French cooking yields plenty of flavour at this appealing bistro de luxe with distressed décor and plenty of rustic charm. Despite some seasonal Mediterranean touches, the Gallic influence is clear to see on the menu, so look out for dishes like pâté-en-croûte. Quality produce is key to the ingredient-led cooking, to which the chefs bring an assured, accomplished hand. It’s owned by two master sommeliers who share a passion for the wines of Burgundy, so the stunning wine list understandably offers a top-notch selection.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3339132255	Camille	2-3 Stoney Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.camillerestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	£££	t	f	Situated at the entrance to the foodie wonderland that is Borough Market, this intimate French bistro is rooted in an ethos of unpretentious, pared-back cooking that perfectly suits its rustic interior design. The blackboard-written menu is regularly changing, and you can expect straightforward yet eminently satisfying dishes like pâté-en-croûte or whole mackerel with café de Paris butter. A friendly welcome and cheery service ensure you’ll be dining with a smile on your face.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3333748262	Clos Maggiore	33 King Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.closmaggiore.com	Nessun premio	French	3.0	£££	t	f	Bright and airy in summer and cosy in winter, Clos Maggiore is one of London’s most romantic restaurants^ be sure to ask for a spot in the enchanting conservatory with its retractable roof. Seasonal, French-inspired dishes are joined by a wine list of considerable depth. The lunchtime and pre/post theatre menus are great value and are a hit with one and all.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3338918635	Colbert	50-52 Sloane Square	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.colbertchelsea.com	Nessun premio	French	4.0	£££	f	t	With its posters, chessboard tiles and red leather seats, Colbert bears more than a passing resemblance to a Parisian pavement café. It’s an all-day, every day operation and the menu lists all the French classics, so you can pop in for breakfast or a croque monsieur or linger over a steak Diane.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3333124021	Le Pont de la Tour	36d Shad Thames	United Kingdom	London	Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lepontdelatour.co.uk/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	£££	f	f	Few restaurants in London can claim to have a better location than this. For over 30 years, Le Pont de la Tour has been wowing diners with its jaw-dropping views of Tower Bridge, best appreciated from the terrace on a warm summer's day. The restaurant itself, as the name suggests, is thoroughly French at heart: expect confidently executed classics from ratatouille Niçoise to gratin Normande. The carefully chosen wine list offers a broad and interesting selection, of both the classic and the esoteric varieties.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3334099149	Le Vacherin	76-77 South Parade	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.levacherin.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	££	t	t	With its part-mirrored walls, belle époque pictures and vintage brasserie styling, Le Vacherin brings a little bit of France to its West London neighbourhood. The menu has the classical French slant you would expect, allowing you to get your fix of 'escargots' or 'longe de lapin' without leaving the country. It's all fresh, flavoursome and prepared with obvious care, while the 'prix fixe' menu offers great value for money. The chateaubriand to share is a popular choice.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
3332141710	Les 110 de Taillevent	16 Cavendish Square	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.les-110-taillevent-london.com/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	£££	t	t	Ornate high ceilings and deep green banquettes create an elegant look for this formal French restaurant, which is more food orientated than the Paris original. Attractively presented, modern French dishes are accompanied by an exceptional wine list, which includes Château Lafite Rothschild back to 1897 and Château d'Yquem back to 1924. There are also 110 wines available by the glass, with 4 different pairings (covering 4 price brackets and 2 sizes), suggested for each dish.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3332480642	Mignonette	109 Kew Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.mignonettebistro.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	££	t	f	How lucky are the residents of Kew? Not only do they have the world-famous gardens on their doorstep, but they’re also the beneficiaries of this terrific little restaurant. Simple, homely and French to its core, this is the epitome of a neighbourhood bistro. The cooking is uncomplicated, hearty fare^ bookend your meal with the homemade bread and the pear tarte Tatin, which is well worth the 20-minute wait. Come in the day for the exceptionally well-priced lunch menu, where the dishes are just as delicious and generous.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3330488633	Paulette	18 Formosa Street	United Kingdom	London	Interesting wine list	https://www.paulettelondon.com/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	££	t	f	Named after the grandmother of one of the owners, Paulette is the sort of cosy, traditional French bistro everyone laments as no longer existing. The atmosphere is convivial – you get the feeling most customers walked here – and the menu is hugely appealing^ expect everything from escargots and moules marinière to filet de boeuf and chocolate soufflé. Add in a cleverly curated all-French wine list that’s great value, along with a fridge full of produce to buy and take home, and you have the recipe for a very satisfying night out.	florescumelissa	\N	\N
3339538101	Savoy Grill	Strand	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.gordonramsayrestaurants.com/savoy-grill/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	£££	f	f	There's something undeniably decadent about dining at this iconic restaurant. From the moment you enter via the hotel's beautiful lobby, the décor is elegant and opulent in equal measure with the chandeliers setting the tone for a dining room that's unsurprisingly popular with celebratory couples. The menu follows in these luxury footsteps, offering a mix of French and British classics that put premium produce front and centre, whether that be caviar, Dover sole or excellent quality beef for the signature Wellington.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3333611506	Soif	27 Battersea Rise	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.soif.co	Nessun premio	French	4.0	££	f	t	A classic French bistro and wine shop are rolled into one appealing package at this rustic neighbourhood operation run by a friendly team. The satisfying dishes have a largely French accent, with some Mediterranean influences also coming into play, be it burrata or kalamata olives. The rotisserie chicken to share is something of a speciality, while the thoughtfully compiled wine list includes plenty of natural wines from artisan winemakers.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3339611076	Louie	13-15 West Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://louie-london.com/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	£££	f	f	There’s a decidedly French feel to this smart brasserie spread over two floors. Sit downstairs during the week, where the elegant surroundings include a shellfish counter, banquettes and a lovely old jukebox. The more formal, intimate upstairs dining room opens at the weekend. The menu comprises skilfully cooked French-influenced dishes, including sharing options like sole meunière and côte de boeuf. Desserts are a straightforward, classic affair, with choices like chocolate fondant, tarte Tatin and a cracking pecan pie. Head up to The Alligator Bar for a cocktail after dining.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3338546008	AGORA	4 Bedale Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.agora.london/	Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	££	f	f	Located on the edge of Borough Market, underneath its sister restaurant OMA, is this simple yet brilliantly effective ‘souvla bar’. Skewers are at the core of the menu – like the excellent slow-roast pork souvlaki – but it would be foolish to overlook the wonderful range of dips and beautifully puffed flatbreads served straight from the oven. It’s stripped-back cooking done with great skill, resulting in dishes so satisfying you’ll want to order them twice. They're deservedly busy, so make sure you snap up one of the limited bookings or get here for midday when they open.	pingliu	\N	\N
3331184650	Mazi	12-14 Hillgate Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.mazi.co.uk	Nessun premio	Greek	4.0	£££	t	f	A real neighbourhood restaurant with a pure Greek heart, there is a wonderful buzz to the intimate Mazi. It’s one of those places where you can leave the decision making to the passionate, engaging team, who are ready to recommend their favourite Greek wines and dishes. The menu is designed for sharing and mixes classic choices with more modern creations^ for dessert however, it’s hard to look past the loukoumades. A small front terrace and larger rear one add to the appeal – if the weather’s good enough, you can pretend you’re in Athens.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3336994805	Where there's Smoke	7 Silver Street	United Kingdom	Masham		https://www.wts.restaurant	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	£££	f	f	Cooking over coals is the USP here – hence the name – and the lovely aroma will hit you the moment you enter this good-looking restaurant. It sits in a delightful market town, and the seasonal set menu is comforting, easy to enjoy and comes from an honest heart. The chef-owner is also a potter, so take time to admire his creations^ oh, and the bespoke wooden table-tops, he made those too!	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3333207726	OMA	3 Bedale Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.oma.london/	Nessun premio	Greek	5.0	£££	t	t	Find the subtle little sign and then head upstairs to this lively, hugely fun restaurant serving thrilling cooking from Greece and beyond. This is the spot that the capital’s Hellenic food enthusiasts have been crying out for, with utterly delicious sharing dishes that include spreads and breads, tuna in various forms, plenty from the charcoal grill and standouts like spanakopita and giouvetsi. The covered terrace overlooks Borough Market, the pacing from the kitchen is spot on and the young service team are both warm and helpful. The list of coastal wines is great too.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3336388348	Ambassadors Clubhouse	25 Heddon Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://ambassadorsclubhouse.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	£££	f	f	There’s opulence to spare at this lavishly furnished, no-expense-spared restaurant from the team behind Gymkhana. Soft lighting, wood panelling and colourful décor all add to the atmosphere, which takes its cues from the ‘party mansions’ of the former undivided Punjab. Northern India and Pakistan inspire the menu, which provides a showcase for the chefs’ quality produce and abundant technical skill – both of which are evident in the superb mooli methi bream cooked on the sigri stove. Downstairs, in Ambassy, guest DJs curate a late-night rotation of Punjabi and British dance music.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3334312954	Black Salt	505-507 Upper Richmond Road West	United Kingdom	London	Terrace	https://blacksaltsheen.com	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	££	f	t	Little sister to Dastaan in Ewell is this modestly decorated neighbourhood restaurant with exposed brick walls, stripped wooden floors and blonde wood tables. Vibrant Indian cooking includes plenty of street food inspired dishes. Curries are highlight and the naan bread and kulfi are must-haves.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3333130352	Bombay Bustle	29 Maddox Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://bombaybustle.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	££	f	f	A charming train theme runs through this Indian restaurant, where the ground floor is the livelier area and downstairs is more ‘first class’. Mumbai is known for its chaat so – before a prawn curry, chicken biryani or succulent lamb chops from the tandoor – order some to share, like their wonderfully crisp and colourful Raj Kachori. And they make a fine rice pudding for dessert.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3339472390	Brigadiers	1-5 Bloomberg Arcade	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://brigadierslondon.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	££	t	f	The army mess clubs of India provide the theme for this large restaurant spread across several rooms on the ground floor of the Bloomberg building. The cooking has a strong live fire element, blending street food dishes and those cooked on the barbecue, like the delicious goat tikki bun kebab. 'Feast' menus are available if you're in a big group and there's a decent selection of beers and whiskies too. It's a perennially busy place and they have several screens for showing sport, so the atmosphere is predictably loud and lively.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3330672825	Café Spice Namasté	1-2 Lower Dock Walk	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.cafespice.co.uk	Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	£	f	f	Owners Cyrus and Pervin Todiwala are charming, welcoming hosts who have formed part of London's Indian dining scene for decades. The current incarnation of their restaurant is located in the east of the city, occupying the ground floor of a modern apartment building in the Docklands development overlooking the Royal Albert Wharf. Cyrus and his kitchen team produce an extensive menu of colourful small plates to share, including a few dishes from Cyrus's native Goa.	dumitresculara	\N	\N
3332442331	Chatora	100 Kew Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.chatora.co.uk	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	££	t	f	With dining on 3 levels and bifold doors leading onto a small terrace, you can sit somewhere different every time you come. The experienced owner and 3 chefs represent the North, East, South and West of India. Generously proportioned, original dishes are authentically spiced and burst with flavour.	popafarah	\N	\N
3331327734	Chutney Mary	73 St James's Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.chutneymary.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	£££	t	t	This long-standing, popular Indian restaurant comes from the same stable as Veeraswamy and Amaya, and its stylish dining room may be the jewel in the group’s crown. A certain luxury is to be expected when Buckingham Palace is just a short walk away, but there’s a relaxed, fashionable feel to the surroundings here too. The appealing menu offers lots of choice and the well-judged, flavourful dishes (mostly from northern India) have been subtly updated, while still respecting the foundations of the cuisine.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3332176979	Cinnamon Bazaar	28 Maiden Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://cinnamon-bazaar.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	££	f	f	Vivek Singh’s Covent Garden restaurant provides relaxed, all-day Indian dining in a bright, colourful space with a marketplace atmosphere. The extensive menus are influenced by the trade routes of the subcontinent, with twists that encompass Afghanistan, Punjab and the Middle East. Start off with a selection of snacks and chaat, before moving on to larger plates like lamb rogan josh ‘shepherd’s pie’, which has become something of a signature.	shirocky	\N	\N
3337099845	Darjeeling Express	2.1-2.4 Kingly Court	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.darjeeling-express.com	Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	£££	f	f	The cooking of Kolkata and chef-owner Asma Khan’s Mughal ancestry inform the menu at this bright and breezy restaurant on the top floor of the perennially busy Kingly Court. Asma can be found chatting away with diners while the all-female kitchen team create authentic, vibrant dishes where careful spicing enhances the central ingredient. The menu is presented as an à la carte at lunch and served all together as a thali at dinner.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3333081832	Heritage Dulwich	101 Rosendale Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.heritagedulwich.co.uk	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	££	f	t	‘Heritage’ is key to the cooking at this Indian restaurant in a smart suburban shopping parade, where skilfully prepared dishes are knowledgably balanced, well-spiced and packed with authentic flavours. Dayashankar Sharma – who has led many of London’s best Indian kitchens – cooks alongside his son Anmol.	costasergio	\N	\N
3336768798	Kahani	1 Wilbraham Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.kahanilondon.com/	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	£££	t	t	Service is charming at this smart, modern, easy-going basement restaurant. It’s name means ‘Story’ in Hindi^ the story in question being that of chef-owner Peter Joseph, whose influences include his Indian heritage, the concept of sharing food picked up on his travels in Spain and the best of British produce.	popafarah	\N	\N
3337605912	Kanishka	17-19 Maddox Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://kanishkarestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	£££	t	f	Owner Atul Kochhar’s signature style is writ large across the choice of menus at this smart Mayfair restaurant. Anglo-infused Indian dishes – epitomised by the signature chicken tikka pie – provide plenty of interesting options, with the north-east of India receiving particular attention. There’s a feeling of glamour to the surroundings that would suit a special occasion, and the ground floor is the most fun place to sit.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3334635859	Kutir	10 Lincoln Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://kutir.co.uk	Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	£££	f	f	A pretty end-of-terrace townhouse in an elegant Chelsea street is the setting for this relaxed, stylish Indian restaurant. There’s a lively buzz throughout the various smart yet cosy rooms, with the more intimate upstairs the best choice if you’re on a date. The interesting style of cooking draws from multiple regions of India and offers a wide choice of dishes, from tandoori broccoli to duck madras. The extensive choice of menus cater for a range of diners, with proper vegan and gluten-free options among them.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3331782926	Tamarind	20 Queen Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.tamarindrestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	£££	f	f	Found in the smart streets of Mayfair, this long-standing Indian restaurant is split over two levels: the basement presents the opportunity to watch the chefs working at the tandoor counter^ while the light, airy first floor space comes with a lovely attached terrace, which is heated in the winter and has a retractable roof should it rain. Tasting menus are available, but so is an extensive à la carte of generous dishes perfect for sharing, with a selection of small plates like Rajasthani churi chaat to start, and a good selection of curries and biryanis for the main course.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3338898515	Tamarind Kitchen	167-169 Wardour Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://tamarindkitchen.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Indian	4.0	££	t	t	Walk down Wardour Street and you’ll find yourself being drawn to this Indian restaurant by the warm and inviting glow it emits. A more relaxed sister to Tamarind in Mayfair, this elegant spot is run by an endearingly willing team and the atmosphere is always equally infectious. The menu traverses India and offers something for everyone, from an excellent biryani to a creamy lobster Malabar curry. Equal care goes into the cocktails^ the 'Passion Chilli Sour' will brighten any day.	longoethan	\N	\N
