3336950714	Bala Baya	Arch 25	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://balabaya.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Israeli	3.0	£££	f	t	The atmosphere is loud and lively at this infectiously fun restaurant celebrating the Middle Eastern heritage of its passionate chef-owner. The bright, modern interior is inspired by the Bauhaus architecture of Tel Aviv, while the counter is the best place to sit if you want to feel an even greater buzz and watch the chefs as they cook. Dishes are fresh, vibrant and designed for sharing, with the signature Cauliflower Steak Crumble proving an absolute treat that works wonders with an often overlooked vegetable.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3331580465	Archway	Arch 65	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://archwaybattersea.co.uk	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	££	f	t	As the name suggests, this restaurant is nestled underneath the railway arches close to Battersea Park and the chic Battersea Power Station development. You may hear the rumble of trains overhead, but it’s often replaced by the buzz of diners flocking here to try the rustic Italian cooking with an appealing simplicity. Their focaccia is a stand out, while dishes like charred octopus with paprika romesco sauce put quality ingredients front and centre. The personable, engaging service team will make your visit even more enjoyable.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3337211872	Artusi	161 Bellenden Road	United Kingdom	London		https://artusi.co.uk	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	££	t	f	Peckham may not be the first place you expect to find the spirit of Italian cooking alive and well, but there's no denying the straightforward joys to be found at this enthusiastically run neighbourhood bistro – which is named after Pellegrino Artusi, who wrote ‘The Science of Cooking and the Art of Fine Dining’ back in 1891. It's a small, sweet restaurant where the cooking is simple, honest and downright delicious, with the homemade pasta a definite highlight. The prices are fair, the portions are generous and the flavours are abundant – what more could you ask for?	gentilenoah	\N	\N
