3337784031	Cantinetta Antinori	4 Harriet Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list	https://cantinetta-antinori.uk	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	£££	f	f	The Antinori family have owned vineyards in Tuscany since the 12C, producing their own world-renowned red wine, as well as having a hand in numerous other estates. It should come as no surprise, then, that the wine list here is something to behold. It’s joined by classic Italian cooking, pairing a notable simplicity with plenty of Tuscan ingredients and rich, hearty flavours. The delicious torta caprese is a wonderful way to round out your visit.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3330595325	Franco's	61 Jermyn Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.francoslondon.com	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	£££	t	t	One of London’s oldest Italian restaurants, this reliably enjoyable spot has benefitted from the years of practice. The kitchen focuses on an extensive menu of classically based dishes like veal and beef lasagne or linguine with lobster, with each one proving to be uncomplicated and well-executed. The many regulars come back time and again for their favourite dishes and the intimate, cosy atmosphere. The wine list is joyfully Italian, with some wonderful barolos among the choices.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3330858042	Giulia	77 Askew Road	United Kingdom	London		https://giuliarestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	££	f	t	There’s an authentic, honest feel to this small Italian neighbourhood restaurant. The eponymous owner Giulia can be seen chatting away to guests in her native language and offering great hospitality alongside the cooking. Her partner Endris is in the kitchen following the ethos of pure, ingredient-led cooking with a seasonal focus. Pasta is offered as a separate course, including classic dishes like spaghetti alle vongole. The wine list is sensibly priced and, unsurprisingly, all Italian.	caputostefan	\N	\N
