3330352621	Margot	45 Great Queen Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.margotrestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	£££	f	t	The service and the surroundings are equally slick at this plush Italian restaurant on the edge of Covent Garden. The menu offers an appealing choice of dishes, from simply prepared fish of the day to veal-based classics like ossobuco and vitello alla Milanese – and top quality ingredients and bold flavours run throughout. Take time to study the well-chosen wine list, which has a strong focus on the regional wines of Italy.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3332040784	Maria G's	Coe House	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://mariags.co.uk/kensington/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	££	f	f	Memories of living and working on the Amalfi Coast provided the inspiration behind this restaurant from chef Robin Gill. The short seasonal menu certainly follows the Italian culinary philosophy of using prime ingredients paired simply and intelligently to create complementary flavours. The room is stylish and there's also an intimate cocktail bar and a delightful garden terrace.	caldarolacagilio	\N	\N
3331539120	Noci	4-6 Islington Green	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://nocirestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	£	t	t	Start with the delicious homemade focaccia and share some starters before ordering the USP: generous pasta dishes which invariably hit the spot, such as veal & pork Genovese ragu or brown butter cacio e pepe. The menus are fairly priced, as are the cocktails, making this a useful pitstop in this busy part of Islington. You’ll leave feeling sated and satisfied.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3336315869	Pollini at Ladbroke Hall	79 Barlby Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace	https://ladbrokehall.com/restaurant/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	£££	t	t	The former head office of car manufacturer The Rootes Group is perhaps not where you’d expect to find an Italian restaurant, but Ladbroke Hall is no ordinary venue. Located at the top of Ladbroke Grove, it’s a restored Edwardian building that is now a haven for artistic types, holding exhibitions, workshops and music events within its century-old walls. The cooking is textbook Italian, with an ingredient-led simplicity and terrific homemade pastas such as spinach and mozzarella tortellini.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3330451329	Pophams	197 Richmond Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.pophamsbakery.com/pasta	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	££	f	f	Pophams is an artisan bakery during the day but, on four evenings a week, it morphs into an appealingly simple Italian restaurant. Dishes are bright and carefully prepared, with the pasta dishes the stars of the show. A stool at the stone counter looking into the open kitchen is the place to sit, although the pavement terrace is perfect on summer days.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3333701267	Sorella	148 Clapham Manor Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.sorellarestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	££	t	t	His years spent working on Italy’s Amalfi Coast inspired this operation from experienced London restaurateur Robin Gill. The menu is divided into the classic format of cicchetti, antipasti, primi and secondi, and the selection of dishes includes traditional heavy hitters like aubergine parmigiana, ossobuco and tiramisu. Make sure you kick off with some of the arancini though, as they're certainly a highlight. There's a great buzz to the place and the service is friendly.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3337079414	Spring	New Wing	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://springrestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	£££	f	f	Sporting fresh, bright décor that's befitting of its name, Spring occupies an undeniably gorgeous room in the 'New Wing' of Somerset House, that for many years was inhabited by the Inland Revenue. Under the aegis of Chef Skye Gyngell, it serves unfussy, Italian-influenced and ingredient-led food that you feel is doing you good as you eat it. For great value, go for the midweek set lunch or the 'Scratch' menu composed of ingredients that would ordinarily be thrown away and featuring dishes like a bread and butter pudding made using 'yesterday's sourdough'.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3332824883	Trullo	300-302 St Paul's Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.trullorestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	££	t	f	A stalwart of the local dining scene, this split-level restaurant is a hit with the locals and has a true neighbourhood feel. An open kitchen contributes to the light, buzzy atmosphere and the casually dressed service team are a perfect fit for the style of the place. The daily changing menu of rustic Italian dishes makes great use of the charcoal grill and the delicious pasta is hand-rolled before each service.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
3331446820	Wild Tavern	2 Elystan Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.wildtavern.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	£££	t	t	Set overlooking the tiny Chelsea Green, this homely neighbourhood restaurant has the enticing feel of a warm Tuscan trattoria, with its waxed wooden floors and terracotta hues. True to the ethos of Italian cuisine, the dishes are ingredient-led and rely on the natural flavours of the produce – an approach extended to the raw bar of oysters, tartares and carpaccios. Alongside the prime cuts of meat and fish cooked over the grill, there are some terrific homemade pastas you'd be a fool to miss, especially the 'Tavern Tortelli' with Wagyu oxtail.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3334018079	Zafferano	16-18 Lowndes Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace	https://zafferanorestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	££££	t	f	This long-standing Italian restaurant with a pavement terrace has become something of a Belgravia institution. The reassuringly familiar – if rather steeply priced – dishes take their inspiration from all over Italy, bringing together just a handful of top quality ingredients and allowing them to shine.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3334980065	Angelina	56 Dalston Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.angelina.london	Nessun premio	Italian, Japanese Contemporary	3.0	£££	t	f	Few people would think of combining Italian and Japanese cuisine, but the unusual fusion works a treat at this fun neighbourhood spot owned by two friends. Sit at the marble counter to watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen, as they craft a kaiseki-style tasting menu which could include such creations as rosemary and nori focaccia or chawanmushi flavoured with datterini tomatoes. Keep an eye out for the pasta dishes, as they're a highlight.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3339534795	Norma	8 Charlotte Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://normalondon.com	Nessun premio	Italian, Sicilian	5.0	£££	f	t	This Fitzrovian townhouse has been transformed into a handsome, intimate restaurant spread over three floors, with Moroccan tiles and cosy booths. The food of Sicily and its Moorish influences inform the menu, with the 'primi' options including the dish that gave the restaurant its name: pasta alla norma. Generous portions add to the appeal, particularly the immensely satisfying fritto misto and the super-sized cannoli for dessert.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3337651396	Akira	Japan House	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Notable sake list	https://akira-restaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	£££	f	t	Japan House promotes all things Japanese, so it’s appropriate that upstairs there’s a stylish, buzzing restaurant celebrating the country’s cuisine. The open kitchen is the focal point of the room, which offers both counter and table seating from which to enjoy the extensive selection of Japanese food. There’s a wide range of sushi, but it’s the skewers from the robata charcoal grill that are the highlight – such as asparagus wrapped with bacon or chicken and shiso meatballs.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3330703247	Ginza St James's	15 Bury Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.ginza-stjames.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	££££	t	t	In one of London's swishest districts, this is an appropriately elegant spot to celebrate the joys of Japanese cuisine. A large cocktail bar will greet you as you enter, before you head down to the equally stylish restaurant where the seating options include teppanyaki and sushi counters. The vast à la carte is so appealing, with everything from sashimi to tempura, but if you can't decide then go for one of the well-priced set options – and don't miss the chance to have the delicious 'nasu dengaku'. The sake list is one of the best in London.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3332712246	Hannah	County Hall Building	United Kingdom	London	Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.hannahrestaurant.london	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	££££	t	t	Never judge a book by its cover – or a restaurant by its entrance! It may be quite quirky in its looks, but this sweetly run Japanese eatery provides an enjoyable and well-rounded omakase experience. It's led by Chef-Owner Daisuke Shimoyama, who shows off his impressive knife skills when preparing a procession of high quality ingredients, be it Wagyu beef, sea bream or lobster. The sake list provides the ideal accompaniment to the cooking.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3334986935	Mayha	43 Chiltern Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://mayhalondon.com	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	££££	f	f	There’s a real sense of style to this small Japanese restaurant that relocated from Beirut to London. The chic interior is dominated by a curved wooden counter where the chefs take centre stage, producing a highly seasonal omakase menu. Tree-inspired lights above the counter cast an intimate glow, while a sense of theatre runs throughout the dishes. Luxury ingredients are to the fore and the menu is dominated by a succession of sushi.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3330285014	NIJŪ	20 Berkeley Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://nijulondon.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	£££	t	f	The Japanese concept of ‘katei ryōri’ – home-style family dining – is the driving force behind this slick Mayfair operation. Diners are split across two rooms, one more moody and clubby, the other brighter and featuring a small sushi counter. Endo Kazutoshi has designed the menus, which combine the katei ryōri sharing dishes with a sushi selection and Japanese beef cooked over charcoal. Unifying it all is an attention to prime produce, be it the wagyu, the hamachi for the sushi or roasted turbot with furikake and miso butter. Bookend your visit with a drink in the Nipperkin cocktail bar.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3336897735	Nobu London Old Park Lane	19 Old Park Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.noburestaurants.com/london-old-park-lane/home/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	£££	t	t	There are now Nobu restaurants stretching from Dallas to Dubai and Mexico to Melbourne, but this one was Europe’s first when it opened back in 1997. Like seeing a favourite popstar on stage, you can expect all the greatest hits, from seafood toban yaki to rock shrimp tempura and, of course, the dish that’s been copied a thousand times: black cod miso. There’s a decently priced weekday lunch menu and the service is smooth and confident.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3333686669	Roketsu	12 New Quebec Street	United Kingdom	London	Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.roketsu.co.uk	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	££££	f	f	Chef-Owner Daisuke Hayashi has created a little slice of Kyoto life here in New Quebec Street. His culinary training and background may have been traditional but he’s not averse to introducing the occasional contemporary touch to some elements of his 10 course kaiseki menu. If you want to make your own choices, there's also an à la carte available, along with a set lunch menu on certain days. The charming welcome, attentive service and the counter fashioned from 100-year old hinoki wood will transport you away from the hurly burly of city life.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3336170277	Sumi	157 Westbourne Grove	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace	https://www.sushisumi.com	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	£££	f	f	There’s a plethora of restaurants on Westbourne Grove but few are ever as busy as Sumi. In 2022 this modern Japanese restaurant from Endo Kazutoshi – which he named after his mother – expanded into next door and the new seating quickly filled up. The atmosphere is always lively thanks to the young crowd and the great cocktail list. The menu is not overly long^ the robata dishes are the standouts, but just keep half an eye on the bill as it can quickly expand.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3335911072	Takahashi	228 Merton Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Notable sake list	https://www.takahashi-restaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	££££	t	t	There's an endearingly personal touch to this intimate Japanese restaurant run by a husband-and-wife team. The menu takes an omakase format, beginning with a series of otsumami dishes and followed by nigiri sushi. It's the latter that proves to be the stand-out, each individual piece delivered one by one to the enraptured diners^ you can expect the pure, delicately flavoured seafood produce to include the likes of chutoro, otoro, hamachi and scallop. There's a sake pairing available for pre-order if you want to enhance the experience.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3334835167	The Fuji Grill	115 Sloane Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.beaverbrooktownhouse.co.uk/the-fuji-grill-sushi-bar/	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	££££	t	t	The discreetly stylish Beaverbrook Town House is home to this warm, elegant restaurant that’s something of a hidden gem. The framed Japanese prints on the walls and lacquered furniture help make it a lovely place to dine, while there’s plenty to entice on the wide choice of menus, from a full omakase – which should naturally be enjoyed at the counter – to bento box deals and an extensive à la carte featuring skilfully made nigiri. A good sake selection adds to the authentic Japanese appeal – albeit inside an English townhouse.	morozovmegan	\N	\N
3336586959	Zuma	5 Raphael Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://zumarestaurant.com/locations/london/	Nessun premio	Japanese Contemporary	3.0	£££	t	t	Zuma may now be a global brand, but this long-standing Knightsbridge restaurant was the originator of its informal, izakaya-inspired Japanese cuisine. Managing to still feel fresh over 20 years after opening, its home to a glamorous clientele who fit right in with the striking surroundings and bustling atmosphere. Sharing is a great way to experience as much of the extensive menu as possible – but if you have to prioritise, make sure you try the array of produce cooked on the robata grill, from tofu to chicken wings.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3334673852	Kioku by Endo	Raffles London at The OWO	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://kiokubyendo.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	££££	t	t	Enjoy a cocktail or two in the elegant ground-floor bar before heading up to this restaurant at the top of the Raffles hotel inside the spectacular Old War Office. Superb city skyline views await you, while a seat on the terrace is a must in warmer weather. With a name meaning ‘memories’, the menu fuses Endo Kazutoshi’s Japanese heritage with his Mediterranean training, resulting in dishes ranging from lobster fregola to stand-out nigiri. For a special occasion, book the chef’s table or even the private room in a turret.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3332197664	Aragawa	38 Clarges Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://aragawa-uk.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese Steakhouse	3.0	££££	t	f	It’s all about the beef at this elegant Mayfair restaurant. Luckily, it’s beef of such extreme quality – so succulent, so naturally flavoursome and so expertly cooked over binchotan charcoal – that you’ll forever be wishing every steak was this good. The available cuts are all Tajima Wagyu, one of the most delicious and highly prized meats in the world, with only salt and pepper used to season the meat. The restaurant itself feels like stepping into someone’s (extremely well-decorated) living room.	cattaneomiguel	\N	\N
3336457002	Maru	18 Shepherd Market	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list	https://www.marulondon.com	Nessun premio	Japanese, Sushi	5.0	££££	t	f	Discreetly tucked away in Shepherd Market, it's easy to miss the entrance to the earnestly run Maru. As with many a good sushi restaurant, the high quality of the produce helps provide plenty of flavour^ the ingredients are largely British, including seafood from Cornish waters. The menu takes an omakase approach, made up of around 20 different servings, and the sake pairing makes for a good accompaniment. There are two sittings at dinner, so arrive on time^ you pay when you book.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3337259487	DOSA	Mandarin Oriental Mayfair	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access	https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/london/mayfair/dine/dosa	Nessun premio	Korean	4.0	££££	t	f	Its stunning marble counter is an instant signal of the quality you will find at this Korean restaurant in the basement of the Mandarin Oriental Mayfair hotel. Students of the cuisine will recognise several elements, from kimchi and bibimbap to multiple forms of jang made in-house. It’s all executed with utmost skill and the mostly British produce is of superb quality. The chefs and well-versed service team work in impressive harmony and have a real desire for you to understand the cuisine, but most importantly to enjoy it – and you very much will.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3337612685	Miga	1 Mare Street	United Kingdom	London		https://www.instagram.com/miga.restaurant/	Nessun premio	Korean	4.0	££	f	t	There’s always a certain joyfulness to family owned and run restaurants – and Miga is truly a family affair, with dad running things in the open kitchen and the younger generation looking after guests in the bright, airy room. If you want to find out more about them, check out the family history as described on the wall outside. ‘A modern take on Korean cuisine’ is their tagline and this is borne out by fresh-tasting dishes like delicious soy-braised short ribs – already a fans’ favourite – and spicy noodles with crispy beef jeon. The generous prices, especially at lunch, allow for enthusiastic ordering – which you won’t regret.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3333140002	Sucre	47B Great Marlborough Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.sucrerestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Latin American, European Contemporary	5.0	£££	f	t	20 years after opening in Buenos Aires, Argentinian chef-restaurateur Fernando Trocca opened this buzzy restaurant in an attractive former concert hall in London. Contemporary Latin American inspired dishes are cooked over the open fire of the parrilla. Start with a drink in the moody basement bar.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3333767360	Josephine Bouchon	315 Fulham Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://josephinebouchon.com/	Nessun premio	Lyonnaise, French	3.0	££	f	f	Chef Claude Bosi returns to his Lyonnaise roots with this buzzy ‘bouchon’, where the tables are tightly packed and the walls are adorned with colourful posters. The menu could scarcely be more French if it was emblazoned with the tricolore: vol-au-vent, andouillete, frog’s legs… take your pick. It’s all executed with great skill and packs in plenty of flavour, while the service is delivered with a certain ‘bonne humeur’. The set menu is remarkably good value and the well-chosen wine list contains some notable French producers.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3335171364	Mambow	78 Lower Clapton Road	United Kingdom	London	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.mambow.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Malaysian	3.0	££	f	f	‘Malaysian Heat + Juicy Wines’ is the strapline of Vanessa Fernandes and Abby Lee’s restaurant – that means exhilarating dishes inspired by Abby's family recipes, alongside natural wines. Start with the terrific '100+ Sour' cocktail and then order plenty of the delicious food to share. While the menu changes frequently, expect eminently satisfying dishes like Otak-Otak prawn toast or squid stuffed with pork belly mince – and don’t ignore the Kerabu section. There's a great atmosphere around the room and there are also a few seats on a semi-covered terrace at the back.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3334592364	CUT at 45 Park Lane	45 Park Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.dorchestercollection.com/en/london/45-park-lane/restaurants-bars/cut-45-park-lane/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	3.0	££££	f	f	This sumptuous restaurant on the ground floor of the 45 Park Lane Hotel comes with moody décor, rich red leather backed seating and Damien Hirst artwork. Some of the best steaks in London – including British, imported USDA prime beef and Japanese Wagyu – are on offer alongside a premium wine list.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3339979851	Hawksmoor	157a Commercial Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://thehawksmoor.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	5.0	£££	t	t	This is where the now trans-Atlantic Hawksmoor brand began and, despite their expansion, the team have managed to hold onto their founding ethos of quality, hand-butchered British meats. This is a restaurant that has always been about keeping things simple and doing the basics well^ so expect an enticing selection of cuts expertly cooked and delivering bags of flavour. To start, the bone marrow and onions with sourdough toast sums up the place up perfectly. The in-depth wine list has some lovely reds to complement your steak.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3339569231	Quality Chop House	91-94 Farringdon Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://thequalitychophouse.com	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Traditional British	5.0	£££	f	t	A landmark London restaurant with a history dating back to 1869, this ‘progressive working class caterer’ champions quality British produce, with the focus on steaks and chops, like Belted Galloway rib-eye, Mangalitsa loin and Barnsley chops^ just be sure to also order their deliciously crunchy confit potatoes. The booths are the prized seats and the wine list contains lots of gems, more of which are available at their wine bar just next door.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3338314256	Bellanger	9 Islington Green	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://bellanger.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	££	f	f	With awnings stretching over the pavement and walls festooned with classic posters, Bellanger has the feel of a Parisian grand café. The cooking, however, looks more broadly to the Mediterranean for inspiration^ the Italian influences are clear, with dishes such as chicken Milanese sitting alongside the ubiquitous French classics like steak frites. The vibe is very much that of a neighbourhood restaurant, despite a well-organised formality to the service, and the large cocktail bar is perfect for an aperitif.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3330351837	Lita	7-9 Paddington Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://litamarylebone.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	££££	f	f	Cooking with fire is all the rage these days and Lita, which opened in 2024, is another expert practitioner, although it also offers so much more. While there’s a strong Mediterranean and southern European element to the menu, prime British ingredients – such as Scottish langoustines and Norfolk quail – along with big, bold flavours and well-made sauces really make the dishes sing. Many of the plates are designed for sharing, like succulent Cornish lamb with smoked aubergine and sheep’s milk. This is roll-up-your-sleeves sort of food – the type that leaves you licking your lips and planning your return.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3333391848	Morchella	84-86 Rosebery Avenue	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.morchelladining.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	££	f	f	Set in a converted former bank, Morchella sports a small but well-stocked wine bar to one side, offering largely natural and biodynamic options that the wine list describes as either ‘Classic’, ‘Coastal’ or ‘Funky’. On the food side of things, the menu has a Mediterranean slant and is designed for sharing – although if the spaghetti alle vongole is available, you’ll be loath to give any up. Service is bright and breezy, while the great value lunch menu means you can dine without breaking the bank, so to speak.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3336061504	Moro	34-36 Exmouth Market	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://moro.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	££	f	f	Full of customers and full of life, with service that is engaging and on-the-ball, Moro remains as popular as ever and is the perfect fit for the increasingly busy Exmouth Market. The Moorish menu is full of interesting, flavour-packed dishes, but the wood-roasted options are the ones to go for. The open kitchen adds to the atmosphere of the animated room, and their next-door tapas bar, Morito, is also worth visiting.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3338548743	Peckham Cellars	125 Queens Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://peckhamcellars.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	££	f	t	This neighbourhood bistro and wine bar is run by three friends, who all hail from this part of South East London. Original small plates have a rustic style^ they’re made for sharing, so choose three or four per person – if you’re in a group, consider ordering the whole menu. The wine list features some interesting small producers and they even have some wines on tap.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3339002089	Salt Yard	54 Goodge Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.saltyardgroup.co.uk/restaurants/salt-yard	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	££	t	f	Having opened it 2005, this buzzy basement restaurant was one of the first in the city to offer small plates and promote the sharing philosophy. Spanish and Italian flavours lead the way, with top-notch ingredients showcased in a mix of traditional and more imaginative dishes. Plenty of Spanish wines and sherries are there to accompany, and the serving team are enthusiastic and sincere. The booths at the back are a great spot.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3336424941	The Petersham	2 Floral Court	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://thepetershamcoventgarden.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	£££	t	t	Nestled in the 'Floral Court' section of Covent Garden is this elegant restaurant adorned with fresh flowers and Murano glass. It comes from the same stable as Petersham Nurseries Café and uses produce from their Richmond nursery as well as their Devon farm. The Italian-based dishes, like vegetables pinzimonio, show off the ingredients beautifully. The lovely terrace is shared with La Goccia, their more informal spot for sharing plates, and they also have a neighbouring wine bar and deli. From Thursday to Sunday, their afternoon teas become something of an event.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3338275430	The Twenty Two	22 Grosvenor Square	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://the22.london/restaurant-bar	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	£££	f	f	There’s an appealingly secretive feel to the restaurant at this converted Edwardian house. Sitting in a prime Mayfair location, it’s also home to a private members’ club. The menu offers something for everyone, with its extensive selection of largely Mediterranean dishes, some of which are designed for sharing. Service is eager and on the ball.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3337141747	Wild by Tart	3-4 Eccleston Yards	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.wildbytart.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	££	t	t	This laid-back brasserie is located in a former power station and coal store^ the lofty glass roof ensures it’s light and airy, and the open kitchen gives it a real buzz. Rustic, Mediterranean-influenced dishes are tasty and satisfying, with bold flavours and the occasional Asian touch.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3331574996	Wildflowers	57 Pimlico Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.wildflowersrestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	£££	t	f	Newson's Yard is a stylish development just off Ebury Street and among its high-end inhabitants is this split-level restaurant. An open kitchen adds to its homely feel, while the bar tucked under the first-floor eaves is perfect for a cosy drink. There’s a firmly Mediterranean heart to the menu, with the produce-driven and slightly rustic dishes proving to be comforting and full-flavoured. One slice of the homemade focaccia will leave you wanting more and the Italian citrus tart is a refreshing way to end. Genuine, friendly service adds to the joy.	coppolaartem	\N	\N
3334723661	Oren	89 Shacklewell Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.orenlondon.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Middle Eastern	5.0	££	t	t	Named after Chef-Owner Oded Oren, this small, bustling bistro might not look like much from the outside, but it's clearly a winner with the locals. The menu is made up of appealing Eastern Mediterranean sharing plates^ many ingredients are cooked over the chargrill, such as pork chop, chicken thighs or lamb sweetbreads with lemon and za'atar. The wine list is bang on-trend, including lots of low-intervention choices and a decently sized selection of orange wine.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3331761470	Arros QD	64 Eastcastle Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.arrosqd.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Rice Dishes	3.0	£££	f	t	Rice, and lots of it, is what you can expect to find at this huge, strikingly decorated restaurant from the mind of Spanish Chef Quique Dacosta. Specifically, the menu offers an array of takes on the classic Valencian paella, from pork knuckle to tofu & sea lettuce, but plenty of other dishes are available too, including several cuts of meat and fish cooked over fire. There’s a real theatrical element to the place, so ask for a table on the ground floor where you can watch the action in the open kitchen and see the flames from the wood-fired stoves.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3332794049	Jolene	21  Newington Green	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.jolenen16.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional British	4.0	££	t	f	Jolene is the sort of place that we'd all love to have at the end of our street. It's a bakery first and foremost, selling wonderful pastries, biscuits and cakes – as well as delicious bread from flour they mill themselves. There's also a daily written blackboard menu of confidently executed sharing plates, with their house-made pasta something of a feature. The vibe is relaxed and the friendly service team will ensure you're well looked after. You can find more of the same at their Hornsey Road branch.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3338611172	Cavita	56-60 Wigmore Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining	https://www.cavitarestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Mexican	4.0	£££	t	t	Head to the basement bar for a cocktail before taking a seat in this bright, friendly ground floor restaurant with a view of the chefs at work in the open kitchen. The menu brims with punchy, vibrant Mexican choices, including raw dishes such as hamachi tostadas and street food options like a concise range of tacos. Make sure you bring some friends to make the most of the main course platters to share. There's an enticing brunch offering too, where the mezcal and margaritas are bound to be flowing.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3334789146	El Pastor	7a Stoney Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.tacoselpastor.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mexican	3.0	££	t	t	A lively, informal restaurant under the railway arches at London Bridge^ inspired by the taquerias of Mexico City. Flavours are beautifully fresh, fragrant and spicy^ don’t miss the Taco Al Pastór after which the restaurant is named.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3337181878	Stones Restaurant	1c Dale Road	United Kingdom	Matlock	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.stones-restaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	t	t	Negotiate the steep steps down to this small riverside restaurant and head for the front room with its floor to ceiling windows or the delightful rear terrace which offers wonderful views. Unfussy, modern British dishes are attractively presented and display the odd Mediterranean touch.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3335346192	Fonda	12 Heddon Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://fondalondon.com/	Nessun premio	Mexican	5.0	££	t	f	The foodie hotspot of Heddon Street, tucked away on the edge of Soho, is the setting for this busy Mexican restaurant from KOL founder Santiago Lastra. In Mexico, a ‘fonda’ is a family-owned spot usually with just a few tables – here they have supersized the concept, with diners spread across two floors of the bright, airy restaurant decorated with light wood, foliage and colourful ceramic tiles. Kick off with a cocktail from the extensive list before sharing dishes like slow-cooked carnitas with fresh tortillas. Santiago’s signature cheesecake is a great way to finish.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3334001202	Santo Remedio	152 Tooley Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch	https://www.santoremedio.co.uk	Nessun premio	Mexican	3.0	££	f	t	The cooking inspiration comes from the owner’s time spent in Mexico City, the Yucatan and Oaxaca. Ingredients are a mix of imported – like grasshoppers to liven up the guacamole – and home-grown like Hertfordshire pork. Spread over two floors, the rooms are as colourful as the food.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3331726731	Honey & Co	54 Lamb's Conduit Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://honeyandco.co.uk	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	3.0	££	t	f	Same concept^ new, brighter, larger location: Honey & Co has been reborn and fans of the original will be delighted. Vibrant, colourful dishes offer the classic flavours and textures of Middle Eastern cooking and are designed for sharing. If you can’t decide on what to have, go for the tasting option, which offers a small portion of every dish on the menu.	langalice	\N	\N
3330267140	Bubala	65 Commercial Street	United Kingdom	London	Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://bubala.co.uk	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern, Vegetarian	3.0	££	f	f	Start with a freshly cooked laffa flatbread and one of their delicious dips before feasting on Middle Eastern-inspired vegan and vegetarian sharing plates, which are elevated by their delicate spicing. Wines are mostly unfiltered, natural and orange – and service is charming and attentive.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3337864897	Bistrot at Wild Honey	8 Pall Mall	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.wildhoneylondon.co.uk/bistrotatwildhoney/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	££	t	f	Occupying the ground floor of a Grade II listed former banking hall inside the Sofitel hotel, this restaurant aims to provide a more relaxed and keenly priced alternative to the adjoining Wild Honey St James. The team are undoubtedly succeeding in their mission, with lashings of flavour packed into every deceptively simple dish. Sit at the counter or in one of the dramatically red banquettes, which add to the French bistro feel. The menu incorporates a fair few Mediterranean influences alongside the Gallic staples, and the ‘prix fixe’ is an absolute steal.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3331439660	Charlie's	33 Albemarle Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.roccofortehotels.com/hotels-and-resorts/brown-s-hotel/dining/charlies-at-browns/	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	f	t	Located inside Brown's, a quintessential English hotel, this intimate restaurant is one of the most beautiful traditional dining rooms in London, thanks to the keen eye of hotelier and designer Olga Polizzi. Wood panelling and deep armchairs combine with bright splashes of colour, including animal-adorned wallpaper that pays homage to The Jungle Book, which was apparently written by Rudyard Kipling when he stayed at the hotel. The menu, overseen by Adam Byatt, is British with a Mediterranean slant, meaning you'd do well to order the homemade pasta.	serafinidmitri	\N	\N
3330013303	Corrigan's Mayfair	28 Upper Grosvenor Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.corrigansmayfair.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	£££	f	t	This smart spot, with its central Mayfair address and leather banquettes, makes a fitting flagship for the eponymous Chef-Owner. There's a clubby feel to the place, with dimmed lighting adding to the intimacy and Dickies Bar on hand if you're partial to a pre-dinner cocktail. Although there are subtle modern touches, the menu is largely guided by classical French techniques (pommes Anna, vin jaune sauce) and a pleasingly retro approach in dishes like the royal seafood cocktail, filled with sweet and meaty prawns.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3330154056	Fallow	2 St James’s Market	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.fallowrestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	£££	t	t	Thanks to a combination of interesting food and innovative use of social media, you can be sure that you’ll be walking into a packed and lively restaurant here, whatever the time of day or night. The large, open kitchen counter takes centre stage, while there’s also a heated terrace if you can’t get a table in the main room. The menu offers a large and appealing selection, from snacks to sharing plates, along with vegetarian choices. There’s a discernible nose-to-tail ethos too^ do try the smoked cod’s head with Sriracha sauce, a house speciality. The corn ribs are great with a cocktail.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3332695951	Garrison	99-101 Bermondsey Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://thegarrison.co.uk/wp/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	££	f	f	Something of a Bermondsey institution, this charming pub is known for its vintage look and relaxed, buzzy atmosphere. Get comfy in one of the cosy booths to enjoy contemporary British dishes made from good quality seasonal produce. Roasts are a big hit on Sundays and the daily changing menu makes a feature of the fresh fish specials, such as a fabulous John Dory to share. The friendly, organised service team have an eye for detail that further enhances the experience.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3335476909	Hatched	189 St John's Hill	United Kingdom	London		https://www.hatchedsw11.com/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	f	t	The large open kitchen is the focus of this relaxed, simply styled neighbourhood restaurant. Behind the counter is Chef-Owner Shane Marshall, who runs the place with generosity and genuine warmth. His cooking is founded on quality ingredients and features an eclectic mix of influences from around the world, in dishes of both a classic and modern bent. If you're one for puddings, then the pain perdu is an absolute treat.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3339590357	Julie's	135 Portland Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.juliesrestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	££	f	f	Judging by the amount of diners flooding through its doors, the residents of Notting Hill are glad to have this bright bistro de-luxe among their roster of neighbourhood haunts. Inside, it’s an eye-catching place with rich, warming colours and booths that are perfect for date night. The menu offers an appealing range of dishes, from the light (chopped salad of the day) to the luxurious (lobster soufflé). The extensive wine list and cocktails from the trolley will ensure you’re well-refreshed, while the service team are friendly and engaging.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3338727651	Lasdun	National Theatre	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.lasdunrestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	££	f	f	Inside the Brutalist blocks of the National Theatre, lies this buzzy brasserie named after the building’s architect, Denys Lasdun. The sparse modern décor is accompanied by an abundance of exposed concrete, while the cooking has the same seasonal British ethos as the Marksman pub, which comes from the same owners. A good dose of flavour is extracted from the quality produce, while sharing dishes – like chicken, leek and girolles pie – are also on offer.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3331402007	Little Social	5 Pollen Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.littlesocial.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	t	f	Little Social has a clubby, comforting feel and a smart, stylish look, with on-trend copper, dark wood, and duck egg blue upholstery ensuring it fits in perfectly with its Mayfair surroundings. The seasonal British menu offers something for everyone, and its creative modern dishes are full of flavour.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3337767639	Mary's	8-10 Pollen Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.maryslondon.co.uk/#	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	f	f	The one-time site of Pollen Street Social is now home to this relaxed and accessible member of the Jason Atherton stable. Its aim is to cater to all-comers and the chefs pull it off with aplomb. Those in a hurry can sit in The Blind Pig bar area with a Cumbrian beef burger and one of “Mary’s Blood Marys”, while a prix fixe menu offers good value and there’s a vegan offering too. The main à la carte is centred around prime cuts of British meat and fish cooked over the wood-fired grill with impressive technique.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3331710434	Mount St.	First Floor	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://mountstrestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	f	There’s nothing anodyne about the art in this particular restaurant, which is hardly a surprise when you discover that art gallery group Hauser & Wirth are behind it. It’s a striking room with a stunning collection of pieces, from Matisse to Man Ray. The menu offers satisfying, classic British dishes like omelette Arnold Bennett and others inspired by the capital, such as ‘Pigeons in Pimlico’. If you’re early, you can always nip into The Audley pub downstairs.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3331062864	Nest	374-378 Old Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.nestfood.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	t	t	Three friends founded this restaurant and they run the place with obvious pride. A move form Hackney to Shoreditch brought with it a larger premises, lovely vintage décor and the Nest Cellar bar, which also serves a selection of snacks. The set menu is based around British produce and changes regularly, focusing on a season or a particular theme – such as game, beef or seafood – and everything is handled with aplomb by the chefs. Service from the friendly team is smooth and efficient.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3331147882	Piazza	5th Floor	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.roh.org.uk/eat-and-drink/piazza	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	f	t	If you’re coming to see an opera or a ballet at the Royal Opera House, plan ahead and eat here on the 5th floor – either before or after the performance – to really take in its full splendour and magnificence. The room has the feel of a brasserie and its terrific terrace has great views over Covent Garden. The dishes are modern and exactingly prepared^ the fish dishes are especially good, as are their sauces.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3334481564	Pig and Butcher	80 Liverpool Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://thepigandbutcher.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	f	f	In-house butchered meats reign supreme at this rustic, mid-19th Century pub, which is filled with diners and drinkers alike, all contributing to the lively atmosphere. 'Seasonal' and 'British' are the guiding principles behind produce ranging from Aberdeen Angus to Sutton Hoo chicken. The deeply addictive beef dripping served with the bread is one of the highlights of the experience, but it faces stiff competition from the likes of melt-in-the-mouth braised short rib.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3332643969	Planque	322-324 Acton Mews	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://planque.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	t	Set under two railway arches, this boldly styled restaurant is centred around a huge communal table. Listed in size order, the modern British dishes are far more complex than they first appear and show tremendous skill from the kitchen. They are often comprised of three main ingredients, all working in perfect harmony to achieve a great balance of flavours: succulent guinea fowl, for example, might be complemented by earthy Jerusalem artichoke and a hint of bitterness from radicchio. The interesting wine list has an emphasis on small-scale and low-intervention producers.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3336131489	Roast	The Floral Hall	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.roast-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	f	f	Of all the restaurants dotted in and around Borough Market, few are as heavily embedded in the famed food emporium as Roast. It sits inside the historic Floral Hall, with the large windows allowing for some fabulous people-watching among the market stalls below. The menu is British to its core, a fact easily identified by their signature dishes being a scotch egg and beef Wellington. And it will come as a surprise to nobody that the kitchen offers a good range of Sunday roasts, with six different variations to choose from.	georgesculalla	\N	\N
3337195514	Roe	5 Park Drive	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://roerestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	f	f	Launched by the team behind Fallow, this vast restaurant can house up to 500 diners in the heart of Canary Wharf, all while being run with impressive slickness. Guests are spread across several dining rooms, some with counter seating, plus a lovely wrap-around terrace that boasts commanding views of South Dock. The wide-ranging menu offers something for everyone, including playful takes on British classics like maitake Cornish pasty or market fish served with parsley liquor, that's reminiscent of an East End pie and mash.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3336230137	Rondo	199-206 High Holborn	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://thehoxton.com/london/holborn/rondo-restaurant/	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	££	f	f	Rondo with its open kitchen all down one side occupies a fair chunk of ground floor acreage within the Hoxton hotel and offers a fun night out. The chef is an alumnus of St John so expect cooking that is robust and satisfying, although the menu here is a little more international in its influences.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3331893276	Sam's Riverside	1 Crisp Walk	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://samsriverside.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	f	t	Experienced restaurateur Sam Harrison is behind this modern riverside brasserie beside Hammersmith Bridge. It's an enduringly popular place and you can see why from the appealing, pleasingly varied menu that might incorporate a range of influences but doesn't lose sight of the flavour gained by using quality produce. British ingredients from land and sea are cooked with precision and there's a whole section of the menu for oysters and other shellfish. Stock up on provisions at Sam’s Larder before you leave.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3336526853	Silver Birch	142 Chiswick High Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://silverbirchchiswick.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	f	t	Among the numerous eateries on bustling Chiswick High Street, Silver Birch stands out – thanks to its appealing dishes that celebrate the wonderful ingredients we produce in the British Isles, whether that be meaty smoked eel from Devon, sweet scallops from the Isle of Mull, creamy Shetland cod or superb Lancashire fruit. There’s also a good choice of sensibly priced wines by the glass or carafe to accompany these seasonal dishes.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3333664469	Stanley's	151 Sydney Street	United Kingdom	London	Terrace	https://www.stanleyschelsea.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	£££	t	t	In the very heart of Chelsea, the hidden-away Stanley's feels like a perfect fit for the neighbourhood. Plenty of regulars are among the diners seated in either a sheltered, flower-festooned courtyard or inside a lean-to glasshouse. Vibrantly colourful dishes are overtly seasonal and deliver bags of pure, unadulterated flavour thanks to great ingredients – from leeks to pork chops – which are allowed to shine by the chef's understated compositions. When the sun comes out, there's few places better for lunch on a summer's day.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3330246664	Story Cellar	17 Neal's Yard	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://storycellar.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	t	A lively younger sibling to Story, this bistro de luxe in the heart of Covent Garden offers a relaxed experience with an emphasis on counter dining. There are tables available, but overlooking the open kitchen is the place to be for a view of the grill-centric cooking. The whole menu is so utterly enticing you'll have trouble choosing, but highlights include the sweet, luscious snail bolognese on toast and the signature rotisserie chicken brined in bacon stock. The combination of bold flavours, generous portions and consummate technical skill means you're sure to leave satisfied.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3335029971	Straker's	91 Golborne Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://strakers.london	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	f	t	This is a tale of our times: a chef creates a large fanbase by giving cooking demos on TikTok during lockdown and then opens a small restaurant in Notting Hill so that they can come and experience his cooking first-hand. It’s a very likeable place, with no frills, easy-to-eat cooking that’s modern British by way of Italy^ always start by ordering one of the flatbreads – and the sweetbreads are always a good bet too. Low intervention wines are a feature.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3337235248	The George	55 Great Portland Street	United Kingdom	London		https://thegeorge.london	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	f	f	This handsome, Grade II listed Victorian pub boasts original 18th century features including marble fireplaces and ornate plasterwork, bringing a fair amount of period charm to proceedings. The concise British menu offers dishes like beef & Guinness pie and rice pudding with rum soaked prunes, which are generously sized and eminently satisfying. The English-dominated wine list is another big draw.	carusoleonardo	\N	\N
3338071963	The Lanesborough Grill	Hyde Park Corner	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.oetkercollection.com/hotels/the-lanesborough/restaurants-bars/the-lanesborough-grill/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	t	This ornately decorated restaurant sits at the heart of the Lanesborough Hotel. Its menu moves with the seasons, offering modern British dishes brimming with prime ingredients, and includes lighter options as well as plenty for carnivores. Old school desserts are delivered with a degree of refinement, as befits the surroundings. Weekend dinners come with musical accompaniment.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3331429185	The Parakeet	256 Kentish Town Road	United Kingdom	London	Wheelchair access	https://theparakeetpub.com	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	f	Take a 19th-century pub, add wood-fired grilling, then finish with the buzz of a semi-open kitchen – and you have The Parakeet. It’s still firmly a public house, with drinkers far from neglected thanks to the large bar that dominates the front section^ head to the rear to indulge in snacks and sharing plates that have big, gutsy flavours in abundance. A lick of smoke and fire adds to the appeal of many dishes, with grilled fish a particular highlight. A traditional roast is available on Sundays and service is relaxed yet engaging.	ferraroedoardo	\N	\N
3331686212	The Pem	22-28 Broadway	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://thepemrestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	f	t	Set in the elegant surroundings of the Conrad London St. James Hotel, The Pem is named after suffragette Emily Wilding Davison's nickname. Chef-Director Sally Abé’s experience shines through in cooking that's British in inspiration, using produce like Porthilly oysters and Cotswold venison. Dishes are contemporary in style and accomplished in technique, such as crisp red mullet with a powerful tomato, red pepper and pine nut sauce. Ask the personable sommelier for recommendations.	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3339732483	Through the Woods	212 Middle Lane	United Kingdom	London	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.throughthewoods.london/	Nessun premio	Modern British	5.0	£££	t	f	With seating for just 18 people and a logo rather than a sign outside, it’s clear that understatement and simplicity lie at the core of this cosy and very likeable restaurant. Diners are asked to arrive at 7.30pm as dinner is served to everyone at 8pm^ the 4 course, weekly-changing menu offers no choice and you pay when you book. From the tiny open kitchen you can expect nourishing and heartwarming dishes like succulent Blackface lamb with Hasselback potatoes and wonderfully light blood orange & brioche pudding.	rinaldisamuel	\N	\N
3331915942	Townsend	Whitechapel Gallery	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.townsendrestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern British	3.0	££	t	t	Set within the Whitechapel Gallery, this small, light-filled room has a classic feel and is named in honour of its architect, Charles Harrison Townsend. The menu screams seasonality and flavours burst through – and while it’s evident there’s a confident chef at the helm, no dish is over-engineered.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3339689457	Victoria	10 West Temple Sheen	United Kingdom	London	Car park,Terrace	https://victoriasheen.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££	t	t	With its Sunday lunches, quiz nights and sensible prices, this remains a proper neighbourhood pub – albeit in a very smart neighbourhood. There's a pleasantly lived-in feel to the place^ if you're here to eat, head for the conservatory which overlooks the terrace. The appealing menu mixes steaks and pubby favourites like fish & chips with a good range of Mediterranean-influenced dishes such as grilled sardines with caponata. Do try the apple cake for dessert, which is Polish Chef Damian's take on his mother's recipe.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3332998726	Water House Project	1 Corbridge Crescent	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.thewaterhouseproject.com	Nessun premio	Modern British	4.0	££££	f	f	As soon as you walk into this calm, Nordic-style restaurant with an open kitchen and smiling team, you just know you’re going to have a good time. Sit back and enjoy the house aperitif and some fabulous snacks before beginning a tasting menu founded on the finest British ingredients. The produce is treated with a deft touch in elegant dishes that offer refined, balanced flavours – such as West Country mussels with native seaweed and koji. The cooking can be accompanied by either a bespoke wine pairing or a homemade non-alcoholic option.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3332909713	No. Fifty Cheyne	50 Cheyne Walk	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://fiftycheyne.com	Nessun premio	Modern British, Modern Cuisine	3.0	£££	t	f	This brightly painted, flower-festooned former pub looks very much at home in its smart Chelsea location, and the indulgent theme carries on inside with plush dining spaces set over two floors. The menu offers hearty, modern British dishes, with fish and meats cooked over the grill a speciality. In true neighbourhood style, they also offer relaxed Saturday brunches and traditional Sunday lunches.	bernardiliam	\N	\N
3337388495	Cornus	27c Eccleston Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cornusrestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern British, Seafood	3.0	££££	f	f	There’s a wonderful fusion of setting and cooking at Cornus. A sister to long-standing Chelsea restaurant Medlar, it’s a refined, simply decorated restaurant with linen-laid tables and understated quality. The same goes for the dishes, which are based around superb produce, much of it seafood from the south-west coast. The likes of sweet Devon crab and beautiful Newlyn cod are made all the more delicious by the kitchen’s restrained approach and consummate technical skill. The chefs know they’re using brilliant ingredients, so never overcomplicate matters.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3338343584	104	104 Chepstow Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.104restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	££££	f	t	It might only have six tables but the cosy 104 certainly proves that great things can come in small packages. The Chef-Owner works alone preparing a surprise tasting menu of sophisticated dishes with smart flavour combinations and stand-out sauces. Underlining the modernity in the cooking, there is a pleasing simplicity to each dish, allowing superb luxury ingredients like Cornish turbot or Scottish XL langoustine to shine. For dessert, look out for the deliciously rich signature '104 chocolate bar'.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3333450948	Cafe Cecilia	Canal Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.cafececilia.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	££	f	t	Don’t be fooled by the name, for this popular local spot is less a café, more a pared-back, industrial-style restaurant with a modern bistro feel. The chef previously worked at St John and the River Café, and now mixes these influences with his Irish heritage. The Guinness Bread ice cream is sublime.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3334568794	Chapter One	Farnborough Common	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://chapteronerestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	£££	t	f	They’ve got a loyal following at this long-standing restaurant that offers an extensive and appealing menu of modern European dishes. The cooking has some light, delicate touches and prime British produce cooked on the Mibrasa grill is a feature, like Cornish monkfish or Angus rib-eye. It’s all delivered inside a property that dates back to the 1930s and there are subtle references to this period in the elegant décor. The service team bring an enthusiastic smile and real care to their work.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3336857678	Clarke's	124 Kensington Church Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.sallyclarke.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	£££	f	t	It's been over 40 years since Sally Clarke opened her eponymous restaurant, and the loyalty of her many regular diners is testament to the warmth of the place and her kind-hearted hospitality. The seasonal menu is a combination of British and Mediterranean influences, and the kitchen displays a light touch and a healthy respect for the quality ingredients, be it lemon sole or loin of fallow deer. If you want to take something home, check out her shop across the road.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3336340582	Clipstone	5 Clipstone Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://clipstonerestaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	££	f	t	Sister to fellow neighbourhood spots Portland and 64 Goodge Street, this well-run restaurant provides a great all-round package. The young team are full of smiles, the wine list is cleverly conceived and there’s a pleasing buzz to the atmosphere. The cooking, for its part, showcases quality ingredients and an original touch in somewhat delicate dishes.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3339097046	Cord by Le Cordon Bleu	85 Fleet Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.cordrestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	£££	t	f	Famous for their cookery schools, Le Cordon Bleu also operate restaurants, including this one in a Grade II listed building originally designed by Sir Edwin Lutyens for the Press Association. The room is stylishly decorated in soothing blues and whites, and the impeccably attired chefs are on show in the glass-fronted kitchen. The cooking shows a strong classical bent, with dishes such as venison en croûte and a reimagined Black Forest gateau presented in an eye-catching, modern style.	stepanekgrace	\N	\N
3338322735	Counter 71	71 Nile Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.counter71.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	££££	f	f	What was once a well-known local boozer is now a swish dining experience complete with a tasting menu and a Spanish marble counter. Dinner is served to all guests at 7.15pm, so be sure to arrive on time or you’ll miss out on the boldly flavoured, modern British cooking. Cornish seafood and Lancashire Goosnargh duck are among the top quality ingredients on offer, and are brought to life using mostly classic combinations. The bar stays open late, so a post-dinner cocktail is always on the cards.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3330737074	Ekstedt at The Yard	3-5 Great Scotland Yard	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.ekstedtattheyard.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	££££	f	f	Niklas Ekstedt’s first restaurant outside Sweden is this cosy, designer-rustic spot in the Great Scotland Yard Hotel. The chef has become synonymous with his wood-fired cooking techniques, so expect dishes cooked over or immersed into the embers – whether its seaweed-baked langoustine or pine-smoked wild duck breast. Plenty of pickled, fermented and cured ingredients also do their bit to transport Nordic flavours to central London. Choose between a 5 or 7 course tasting menu, or treat yourself at the Chef's Table for a special occasion.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3333487500	Elis	Patriot Square	United Kingdom	London		https://www.restaurantelis.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	£££	f	f	Rafael Cagali, chef-owner of Da Terra, named his second restaurant, located in the Town Hall Hotel, after Brazilian jazz singer Elis Regina. The bright and lively 12-tabled room on the first floor reflects Rafael’s Italian and Brazilian heritage, so expect to see sharing dishes like 'bolinhos de bacalhau' vie with panzanella salad, and picanha skewer with crab linguini.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3332161199	Kitty Fisher's	10 Shepherd Market	United Kingdom	London	Terrace	https://www.kittyfishers.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	£££	t	f	Named after an 18C courtesan, Kitty Fisher’s is a cosy, intimate and refreshingly unpretentious bistro^ ask for a seat downstairs, in the somewhat Dickensian style room. Fresh, unfussy dishes are all about flavour – those cooked on the wood grill have added depth and character.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3335882427	Lorne	76 Wilton Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.lornerestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	£££	t	t	They keep things honest at this narrow little restaurant and you can see the pay-off: a dining room full of happy customers, who are a mix of locals, tourists and business types. Staff are on the ball and well-versed on the menu, while the classically trained kitchen sends forth reliable and consistently good dishes, like Cornish cod with smoked eel, and chocolate delice with cookie crumble. The lunch and early evening menus are very good value.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3338108300	Mauro Colagreco at Raffles London at The OWO	Whitehall	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.raffles.com/london/dining/mauro-colagreco/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	££££	f	t	On the ground floor of the mightily impressive Raffles hotel – which opened in 2023 and occupies The Old War Office – sits this elegant, comfortable and discreet dining room. The sophisticated, technically elaborate cooking offers intriguing flavour and texture combinations, while displaying an emphasis on over 70 varieties of British fruit and vegetables –  the plant produce is always listed first on the menu. The wine list is comprehensive, the pairings are well-considered and the service is pitched just right, being both structured and relaxed.	magnanipavel	\N	\N
3330753714	Medlar	438 King's Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.medlarrestaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	£££	t	t	After more than a decade of service, this neighbourhood spot is becoming something of a Cheslea institution. The locals keep it well-patronised and it's easy to see why, thanks to the relaxed air and spring-like decoration with apple green banquettes and faux blossoming trees. The kitchen doesn't compromise on ingredient quality, with fine produce used in classic dishes like crab raviolo or roast quail with a textbook potato terrine. The wine list is knowledgably curated and pairings are suggested for every dish.	longoethan	\N	\N
3332276903	Ochre	The National Gallery	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access	https://www.ochre.london	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	££	t	f	Situated on the ground floor of the iconic William Wilkins building, this smart, comfortable bistro deluxe is revolutionising museum dining. All-day menus offer something for everyone, from brunch to dinner, via afternoon tea. Small and large plates have sharing in mind^ flavours are vivid and international influences abound.	tottifrancesco	\N	\N
3336264433	Orrery	55 Marylebone High Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.orrery-restaurant.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	£££	f	f	A comfortable and handsome D&D restaurant located in converted stables that date from the 19C^ it’s worth having a drink beforehand in the bar or on the terrace. Expect quite elaborate, modern European cooking^ strong on presentation and with the occasional twist.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3332788557	Petersham Nurseries Café	Church Lane	United Kingdom	London	Terrace	https://petershamnurseries.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	£££	t	t	As you sit in the greenhouse with sand at your feet, surrounded by fresh flowers which even in the winter months perfume the air, it feels as though all is right with the world. A unique spot within the capital's dining scene, this restaurant forms part of the wider Petersham Nurseries complex, where you can buy plants and homeware to spruce up your abode. The cooking is informed by their own fresh produce – try a seasonal vegetable medley to make the most of it – and has a clear Italian accent, from crudo to tortellini.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
