3337691131	Paradise	61 Rupert Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://paradisesoho.com/	Nessun premio	Sri Lankan, Contemporary	3.0	£££	f	t	It was out with the old and in with the new in mid-2024 for this Sri Lankan restaurant, as it underwent a refit and changed its menu offering. There’s now a choice of three tasting menus: one with fish and meat, one with fish and veg, and one exclusively vegetarian. Traditional Sri Lankan spices and flavours are added to largely British ingredients like Cornish pollock and Brixham crab to create attractive, colourful dishes that are thoughtfully constructed, and then proudly explained by the service team. The cooling greys of the intimate room provide a stylishly understated backdrop to the creative cuisine.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3339427838	AngloThai	22 Seymour Place	United Kingdom	London		https://anglothai.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	£££	t	f	‘Rooted in Thailand, Uniquely British’ is the tagline of this joyfully run restaurant from John and Desiree Chantarasak – John is half-Thai, half-British, a duality that informs his cuisine. The exemplary ingredients – from crab to venison – are sourced from across the UK, including from Desiree’s family’s farm, but you can certainly expect more than British ingredients simply married with Thai flavours. There are reimagined and innovative dishes aplenty here too, such as Brixham crab with caviar and coconut ash cracker. Clever sourcing also extends to the furniture, with the tables made from Chamchuri wood by craftsmen in Chiang Mai.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3336141801	Kolae	6 Park Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kolae.com	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	££	f	t	The cuisine of southern Thailand provides the inspiration for this bustling restaurant in the equally bustling Borough Market. It’s an extremely popular place and rightly so, with attractive pricing, efficient service and downright delicious cooking. The menu lends itself to sharing and each dish is packed with flavour, including the terrific grilled mussel skewers and some lip-tingling curries. If you can’t decide, opt for the set menu to share – which is also available in a vegan form.	salajakub	\N	\N
3332754109	45 Jermyn St	45 Jermyn Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://45jermynst.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional British	3.0	£££	t	t	Style and comfort go hand in hand at this bright, contemporary brasserie that delivers the classics with aplomb. The menu is a mix of European and British dishes, with the beef Wellington and lobster spaghetti both finished off at your table, while coupes and floats for dessert bring an old-school touch and pay tribute to its past as Fortnum’s Fountain restaurant. Slick service and the undeniably luxurious surroundings make a visit even more appealing, as does the extensive cocktail menu, which is well worth exploring.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3332494434	Brawn	49 Columbia Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.brawn.co	Nessun premio	Traditional British	4.0	£££	t	t	Offering a warm welcome and robust, flavour-packed cooking, this is the kind of place everyone needs in their neighbourhood. The passionate team run it with a relaxed, upbeat vibe – sit in the back room to enjoy the buzz from the kitchen – and serve reliably tasty food that evolves with the seasons. The interesting wine list includes a number of organic options, as well as smaller producers and a good choice of orange wines.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3338542098	Bull & Last	168 Highgate Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://thebullandlast.co.uk	Nessun premio	Traditional British	5.0	££	f	t	Hearty British dishes which are big on flavour are the order of the day at this sympathetically refurbished Victorian pub. The ground floor bar has a lively buzz and the more sedate first floor dining room opens later in the week. The terrific mushroom tempura is a prime example of what this kitchen does well: straightforward, moreish dishes that come in generous portions. Lovely bedrooms and a friendly, attentive team complete the picture.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3332811236	Drapers Arms	44 Barnsbury Street	United Kingdom	London	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.thedrapersarms.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional British	4.0	££	t	f	A stalwart of London's pub dining scene, Islington continues to be well-served by this imposing neighbourhood local. Not much has changed over the years and it's all the better for it^ rustic décor, eager-to-please staff and a relaxed, unpretentious approach ensure the perfect pub atmosphere. The cooking is as hearty and satisfying as ever, but these days the traditionally British (steak & ale pie) sits alongside French influences (braised rabbit leg), courtesy of a Breton-born Chef. The courtyard garden is a great place to enjoy a glass from the superb wine list.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3332938288	Llewelyn's	293-295 Railton Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://llewelyns-restaurant.co.uk	Nessun premio	Traditional British	3.0	£££	t	f	Sitting just outside Herne Hill station, with its large windows letting diners look out and passers-by to look in, Llewellyn’s feels like a proper neighbourhood restaurant at the heart of the local community. The menu offers an appealing mix of dishes with a Mediterranean accent which focus on the freshness of the ingredients, and service is young and endearing.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3333503574	Rules	35 Maiden Lane	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://rules.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Traditional British	5.0	£££	f	f	Rules delivers all the charm and character you’d expect of London’s oldest restaurant. Start with a drink upstairs in the glorious cocktail bar, before winding your way down to the ground floor with its assortment of rooms decorated with antique cartoons, drawings and paintings. The menu is unashamedly traditional – game from their own estate is a highlight, along with classics like braised rabbit, steak and kidney pudding, and classic desserts from the nursery end.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3333395039	Sael	1 St James's Market	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.saellondon.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional British	3.0	£££	t	t	Britain, its seasons and its produce are the inspiration behind this Jason Atherton venture that comes with elegant brasserie décor and an overtly seasonal menu of comforting dishes you really want to eat. Kick off with the Marmite custard tart and keep things retro for dessert with jam roly poly or bread and butter pudding. The well-constructed wine list has real depth and quality, while coming with the eye-catching quirk of letting you order by the pint. Head upstairs to the Apples & Pears bar if you want to make it a late one.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3338866318	The Devonshire	17-19  Denman Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.devonshiresoho.co.uk	Nessun premio	Traditional British	3.0	££	t	t	One of the hottest tickets in town, The Devonshire is a 'proper' London pub that's been restored to its former glory. On the ground floor, and spilling out onto the pavement, you find the drinkers seeing off pints of Guinness, with food served upstairs. Most of the cooking takes place on the first floor, in the aptly named Grill Room, with the top-floor Claret Room providing a little more calm. Dishes are traditional in style and robust in flavour, with the quality of the produce shining through. Highly personable service rounds out the experience.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3333674633	The Holland	25 Earls Court Road	United Kingdom	London		https://thehollandkensington.co.uk	Nessun premio	Traditional British	4.0	££	f	t	It may have been renamed and rebranded, but this is still a proper neighbourhood pub, with local drinkers in with their dogs, families out for dinner and friends catching up. It’s all very comfy and the relaxed air owes much to the warm and caring staff. The seasonal menu is thoughtfully compiled and the cooking hearty and satisfying^ the pork collar is good and, if the almond tart is on the menu, don’t hesitate.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3330349467	The Wigmore	15 Langham Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://the-wigmore.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Traditional British	4.0	££	f	f	The menu at this smart ‘pub’ attached to The Langham hotel is cleverly designed to appeal equally to those just in for a pint (and there are many of them early evening) and those wanting a full meal. That means an appealing range of snacks, a signature 'Stovetop Toastie' and fat chips that simply must be ordered. For mains, there are burgers but also more adventurous choices like roast cod with mussel chowder or braised venison with hispi cabbage. The main room with its high ceiling hints at its previous life as a bank^ if you want more intimacy, ask for the Green Room.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3330276806	Cloth	44 Cloth Fair	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.clothrestaurants.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	£££	f	t	A hidden gem within the City of London, this sweetly run restaurant is just a stone’s throw from Smithfield Market, tucked down a narrow lane inside a period house which was once home to the poet Sir John Betjeman. It’s now under the watchful eye of Chef Tom Hurst and wine merchants Joe and Ben, who operate the tightly packed space as part bar, part restaurant, but all full of atmosphere. The cooking is pared-back and ingredient-led, with fine produce like Dorset crab and Somerset lamb given the space to shine. The wine list, as you’d expect, is extensive and full of interesting choices.	leonechristian	\N	\N
3337048038	The Clarence Tavern	102 Stoke Newington Church Street	United Kingdom	London	Terrace	https://www.clarencetavern.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	££	f	f	A classic Victorian-era London pub, The Clarence Tavern comes with a real characterful charm, courtesy of its 19th-century architecture fused with more contemporary details. Head past the bar to the part-panelled, part-brick dining area, where the doors open out onto a courtyard terrace. Many of the boldly flavoured dishes come from the pub classics school – like chicken, leek and bacon pie to share – and arrive in pleasingly gutsy portions. Try one of the natural wines and be sure to visit the deli before you leave.	salajakub	\N	\N
3333556416	The Hero	55 Shirland Road	United Kingdom	London		https://theherow9.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	££	f	f	Maida Vale residents hit the jackpot when the owners of Notting Hill’s The Pelican and The Bull in Charlbury chose this neighbourhood for the location for their third venture. The Hero is like a blueprint for how to sympathetically restore and update a pub, and has been understandably packed since Day One. The ground floor offers a great value list of classic pub dishes, from fish pie to sausage and mash. Upstairs is ‘The Grill’, where things are taken up a level with dishes like sweetbreads and lobster gravy.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3331221898	Noble Rot	51 Lamb’s Conduit Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://noblerot.co.uk	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Classic French	4.0	££	f	t	With its dark, rough-lacquered wood and tiny candles, there is something pleasingly intimate about this wine bar and restaurant, where the walls are adorned with covers of the owners' Noble Rot magazine. This really is an oenophile's paradise, with the enthusiastic, clued-up team happy to suggest a smart, sometimes surprising, pairing to go with your meal. The cooking itself is decidedly classical, unfussy and more than a little French. The braised turbot with vin jaune sauce epitomises this spirit, which comes in tandem with gutsy, satisfying flavours.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3330326310	yeni	55 Beak Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning	https://www.yeni.london/	Nessun premio	Turkish	4.0	££££	f	t	Anatolian-inspired cooking from experienced chef-owner Civan Er, who made his name at acclaimed sister restaurant Yeni Lokanta in his home city of Istanbul. Daily changing menu of vibrant, gutsy, flavoursome sharing plates^ techniques are rooted in tradition, with dishes cooked over oak in the Josper oven.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3331388086	Zahter	30-32 Foubert’s Place	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://zahter.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Turkish	5.0	££	f	f	If you’ve just returned from Istanbul and want to keep that holiday spirit alive, then get along to this colourful Turkish restaurant just off Carnaby Street and sit at the counter for extra atmosphere. The chargrill and wood-burning oven are used to good effect, whether it's the potatoes with red onions or the prawns with chilli and garlic. Hummus comes with crispy fried chickpeas and is a great way to kick off, while the chicken thighs with peppers and tomato are succulent and flavoursome.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3332966292	Gauthier - Soho	21 Romilly Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.gauthiersoho.co.uk	Nessun premio	Vegan	4.0	££££	f	t	Right in the heart of Soho is this charming Regency townhouse, offering intimate, formal dining spread that is rarely found in a fully vegan restaurant – yet it's just what Chef-Owner Alexis Gauthier has set out to achieve. His tasting menu combines original dishes – like kohlrabi with aubergine, kamalata olive, spring greens and confit lemon – with classical French touches such as Landes asparagus with morels and a rich, glossy sauce. The ‘Petit Dîner’ menu, served early evening and Saturday lunchtime, offers a shorter experience and good value.	palombogiada	\N	\N
3333191226	Holy Carrot	156 Portobello Road	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.holycarrot.co.uk/	Nessun premio	Vegan	3.0	££	f	t	London’s constantly expanding vegan food scene received another boost when this former pop-up and supper club opened up permanently on Portobello Road. It’s the ideal place for convincing your carnivorous friends of the virtues of plant-based cuisine, as each dish bursts with colour and creativity. The ‘small’ and ‘large’ plates are best shared to sample the broad range of cooking techniques, from barbecued carrot to coal-roasted leeks. The dining room itself – filled with polished concrete and light Mediterranean colours – provides a soothing backdrop that enhances the experience.	grecodavide	\N	\N
