3338734689	Tendril	5 Princes Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.tendrilkitchen.co.uk	Nessun premio	Vegetarian, Vegan	4.0	££	t	f	There are a range of global influences to be found across the vegetable-led dishes at this ‘mostly vegan’ restaurant, from the massaman sauce with pak choi to the ‘Chinatown’ purple potatoes. There’s technical skill on display too and a strong understanding of textures in particular. It’s a smart place, with the feel of a neighbourhood restaurant^ the front room, with plenty of natural light, is best for lunch, while the slightly moodier rear makes for a more intimate dinner.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3333918521	Chiltern Firehouse	1 Chiltern Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.chilternfirehouse.com	Nessun premio	World Cuisine	4.0	£££	f	f	It’s easy to be cynical about celebrity-driven restaurants but this one has substance. The atmosphere remains glamorous and contagiously fun and it’s all run with understated efficiency. The menu focuses on North and South American dishes that are strong on flavour, with the grill used to good effect.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3334795993	Nopi	21-22 Warwick Street	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://ottolenghi.co.uk/restaurants/nopi	Nessun premio	World Cuisine	5.0	£££	t	f	It's not just fans of Yotam Ottolenghi and his cookbooks who have made his Soho restaurant so successful. The menu has something for everyone, featuring an array of flavoursome and colourful dishes, with influences from the Middle East, Mediterranean and across Asia. You can go for your own main course, like sea bass with coconut sauce Véronique, or share a few dishes, such as crispy mushrooms with basil aioli or succulent soy-glazed pork belly with pear mostarda. The room is bright and animated – and if you opt for one of the shared tables downstairs you can watch the kitchen team in action.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3338693830	Scully	4 St. James's Market	United Kingdom	London	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.scullyrestaurant.com	Nessun premio	World Cuisine	5.0	£££	f	f	With a diverse heritage and having lived and worked all over the world, it's no surprise that Ramael Scully brings an array of international influences to his self-titled restaurant. From Malaysia to Moscow via India and China, you'll go on a culinary journey throughout the chef's complex and distinctive dishes. Unlike little else you'll find in the UK, the cooking has an appealing vitality thanks to its punchy flavours and the shelves laden with spices, pickles, preserves and oils. The tasting menu leads the way, but there’s also a shorter option available Tuesday to Saturday.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
