3332222310	Antichi Sapori	piazza Sant'Isidoro 10	Italy	Montegrosso	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.pietrozito.it/	Nessun premio	Apulian	4.0	€€	f	t	For the past thirty years, this fine restaurant with a charming and beautifully kept dining room has been serving regional dishes from the Murge, all prepared using top-quality ingredients. The desserts, in particular, are truly delicious and not to be missed. Given the restaurant’s popularity in the region, booking is highly recommended.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3331871863	Futura Osteria	largo Garfonda 10	Italy	Monteriggioni	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.futuraosteria.it/it	Nessun premio	Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Situated along the Via Francigena near Monteriggioni the small medieval village of Abbadia Isola boasts a superb Romanesque church and a group of old buildings that once housed a monastery and its outbuildings. The Futura Osteria occupies the cellars where the monks once stored their wines, which now provides the setting for simple, delicious and resolutely seasonal Tuscan-inspired cuisine offering good value for money. The refined wine list, simple service and secluded terrace complete the picture.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3334554781	Trattoria della Fortuna	Via Salaria 57	Italy	Monterotondo	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.trattoriadellafortuna.it	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This interior of this trattoria occupying an anonymous rural building at a road junction just outside the village comes as something of a surprise. Inside, the dining room has a warm ambience, with a friendly welcome offered by the female staff. The dishes here are authentic and full of flavour, with a focus on regional Italian traditions and top-quality local ingredients – all the pasta and desserts are homemade. We particularly recommend two of the specialities, namely the “Girella e Cartellata” (made using 36 egg yolks) stuffed with ricotta and goat’s cheese and served with a “ciauscolo” (a type of sausage typical of the Marche and Umbria) ragu and a red wine reduction. A small, simple pergola-shaded outdoor space completes the picture.	martinooliver	\N	\N
