3339835844	L'épicerie Nomad	Rue Keyenveld 56	Belgium	Ixelles		https://epicerie-nomad.be/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Cosmopolitan par excellence, Brussels’ international character is emblematic of this bustling eatery which features tightly packed tables and a slate menu that makes no distinction between starters and main courses. How about a fresh, bitter ceviche of seabass with mango and passion fruit, a Spanish zarzuela of seafood, or shakshuka - a vegetarian one-pan savoury dish? The chef’s creativity, which knows no bounds, is further enhanced by his superlative knack for marrying flavours. Pair this culinary journey with one of the carefully curated tipples to make the most of this fascinating experience.	ricciardisimone	\N	\N
3335358523	French Kiss	rue Léopold I 470	Belgium	Jette	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.restaurantfrenchkiss.com/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	A pleasant restaurant renowned for its excellent grilled dishes and impressive wine list. Dining area with a low ceiling and bright paintings adding colour to the brick walls.	criscuololorenzo	\N	\N
3334361995	Le Sixième	Avenue Fernand Charlot 2	Belgium	Jodoigne		https://www.lesixieme.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	There is something for everyone in this modern bistro. Chef Clément draws his inspiration from top-notch ingredients, to which he adds a subtle personal spin. Asian influences, the authentic flavour of marinated beetroot, a velvety beurre blanc and the subtle smoky hints of the wood-fired Josper oven… Splendid harmonies and great value for money. A word of advice: if you would prefer a more romantic vibe, ask for a table in the second room.	pagliucahans	\N	\N
3334712476	De Garage	Aalbeeksesteenweg 64	Belgium	Kortrijk	Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.degaragekortrijk.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	f	You will probably have guessed from the name and the industrial look that this space to be a garage. Now reimagined as a bistro, the blend of untreated materials and vintage design elements creates a unique atmosphere. The menu puts the emphasis squarely on authentic and familiar flavours, eschewing any unnecessary frills. Think braised pork cheek in a robust sauce, sole meunière with pommes frites or even vegan green curry. Sommelier Fitzgerald Rigole's recommendations are always spot on – and his enthusiasm is infectious!	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3335712901	Station 3	Statieplaats 3	Belgium	Kraainem		https://www.station3.be	Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	€€	t	f	Station 3 is a no-frills restaurant serving up popular specialties from the diverse Chinese culinary landscape. Rich sauces, exotic seasonings, and occasional bursts of sweet and sour are combined with a sure hand. The sea bass steamed whole and paired with an exquisite sauce based on rice vinegar and soy sauce is a must-try for any seafood lover. With so many lobster dishes and vegetarian options to choose from, you're sure to find something to your taste. The har gow – steamed dim sum – are made fresh using traditional methods and delicately seasoned with ginger. A golden opportunity to discover Chinese generosity in all its glory!	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3333482367	So	15 rue Amiral-Roussin	France	Dijon	Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	After notching up experience in some fine establishments, Japanese chef So Takahashi works alone in the kitchen, and his partner, Rie, is front of house. He uses ingredients that are bought directly at the market to concoct French cuisine interspersed with Japanese inspiration. The result is finely executed, light and flavoursome. So good!	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3332405920	Stay Here	Shop 2	China Mainland	Guangzhou	Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Chao Zhou	4.0	¥¥	f	t	This tiny gem has changed hands, but the kitchen is still run by Chaoshan natives. The small menu stars all the greatest hits of Chaoshan cuisine, with raw marinated mud crab that packs tons of oomph standing out in particular. Diners need to book via a texting app and pre-order their food, which does streamline the process immensely. To round out your meal, try the ‘ginger potato’ and split mung bean sweet soup.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3330096258	Au Cœur de Lacuisine	rue du Fond des Naux 7	Belgium	Lacuisine	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.aucoeurdelacuisine.be/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	The sleepy village of Lacuisine makes the perfect base camp to explore the Ardennes. Don’t miss Ronny and Christel’s stylish establishment which combines a friendly vibe with modern comforts. The chef cooks regional produce, most of which from scratch, with lashings of generosity. For example, you may taste a terrine of foie gras with smoked duck magret or a fillet of plaice with a pastis-flavoured jus. The enticing range of set menus means that there is something to suit every palate. Even better, stay overnight and jump into the pool before or after breakfast next morning.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3338576694	Magnific	Tournebride 35	Belgium	Lanaken	Car park	https://sites.google.com/view/restaurantmagnific	Nessun premio	Modern French, Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Lounge music in the background, trendy urban wall graffiti and the warm hospitality of Limburg: a meal at Magnific is always a treat. All the more so, as the chef cleverly juggles with French and Italian recipes, throwing in the odd Asian theme. Whether you start with cannelloni or continue with a venison steak and a cranberry sauce, you can rely on the stellar craftsmanship and full-bodied flavours to come up trumps every time! The set menu with choices is highly recommended.	impeiluca	\N	\N
3337031805	L'Echappée Belle	rue de Lanaye 121	Belgium	Lanaye	Car park,Terrace	https://eb-restaurant.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	The quintessence of a Bib Gourmand, this eatery is embodied by Grégory and Camille’s warm friendly welcome. The couple has created strong ties with local producers, such as Ferme d’Artagnan and Ferme Fourchette, who have become part of the family. The chef crafts their excellent ingredients generously and creatively, underscoring the distinctive flavour of Belgian endive with braised beef cheeks, crunchy celeriac and marinated onion. Authentic Liège recipes and a fine view of the cottage garden from the terrace.	giulianijames	\N	\N
3331813599	Le Bistrot d'en Face	rue de la Goffe 8	Belgium	Liège	Terrace	https://lebistrotdenface.be/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	A nostalgic friendly vibe and good food are the backbone of this inviting local version of a “bouchon lyonnais”. The traditional, extensive menu takes you back in time with dishes such as confit of duck and salardaise potatoes or boulets à la liégoise (meatballs) – among the best in town! Heartwarming, no-nonsense food, served generously and prepared with respect for time-honoured recipes. Spot on every time.	marchettimarko	\N	\N
3338221758	Magma	Rue Porte aux Oies 43	Belgium	Liège	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://magma-liege.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	t	It is heaven to spend time in this hip, upbeat eatery. Tom Foguenne has creatively sourced a lineup of local organic produce out of which he crafts mind-blowing flavours. He might mix smoked trout and tomato with subtly spicy oils, or serve fried chickpeas with cream of yoghurt. Each dish is steeped in unusual tastes and savours, further enhanced by the knockout organic, natural wine list. Instinctive cuisine and a frequently changing menu.	leonechristian	\N	\N
3331128794	Enoteca	rue de la Casquette 5	Belgium	Liège	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://enoteca.be/fr	Nessun premio	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	You will immediately feel at home at the Enoteca, which is depicted by tightly packed tables, a friendly vibe and cheerful service. Food lovers have been flocking here for over thirty years, lured by the unbeatable value for money and the text-book perfect Italian nosh. Farfalle al dente with fresh shrimp, preserved lemons and a knockout tomato sauce – authenticity is the goal! Order the chef’s daily special with your eyes closed and don’t forget the enticing wine list.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3332968827	Le Cabochon	Boulevard Emile de Laveleye 191	Belgium	Liège	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lecabochon.be/	Nessun premio	Modern French, Cuisine from the Marches	4.0	€€	f	f	Le Cabochon is always a safe bet for a slap-up lunch in downtown Liège. The concise selection of dishes on the set menu is flanked by daily suggestions that vary according to the seasons and market availability. Traditional textbook technique (such as mouth-wateringly tender beef cheeks and subtle homemade sauces) is married with side dishes oozing with an abundance of diverse influences. Food that hits the spot every time, to the delight of its many regulars.	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3336970409	La Cuisine de Yannick	En Féronstrée 111	Belgium	Liège			Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking	3.0	€€	f	t	Red and white tablecloths set the warm bistro scene, reinforced by a soundtrack starring the likes of Jacques Brel and Georges Brassens and, above all, the personality of exuberant, fun-loving Joelle in the front of house. It is the perfect spot to (re)discover the importance of home-made cooking and the sheer strength of traditional flavours. The regularly renewed menu shines the spotlight on a line-up of classics ranging from beef tongue in Madeira sauce to a consummately crafted, oozing with taste kidney stew. The reasonably priced wine list is equally awesome.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3330285162	Monsieur V	Dapperensquare 19	Belgium	Linkebeek	Terrace	https://www.monsieurv.be	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Jan Verhaert cooks what he himself likes to eat: traditional Gallic dishes with the occasional nod to Italy. His cosy neighbourhood restaurant specialises in bistro classics such as pâté en croûte and risotto with seasonal vegetables, and crispy millefeuille with vanilla-rich crème pâtissière for dessert. The flawless precision of the cooking and the chef's penchant for gutsy flavours are truly noteworthy. A champion of French culinary tradition, Monsieur Verhaert delivers exceptional food at a price that won't break the bank.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3335034409	Bienvenue	Markt 20	Belgium	Maaseik	Terrace	https://www.restaurant-bienvenue.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	John van Leerzem is a fan of tradition and of the ingredient before all else. This institution on the main square of Maaseik does far more than showcase time-honoured classics. The chef happily subverts traditional recipes, particularly thanks to carefully devised side dishes, such as a terrine of veal cheek and tongue that he subtly contrasts with sweet-sour chutney. His stamp can also be tasted in the tournedos and stroganoff sauce that strikes a perfect balance of flavours. A feast for foodies!	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3331417468	Les 4 Saisons	Rue de Bastogne 108	Belgium	Marche-en-Famenne	Car park,Terrace	https://www.les4saisons.be/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The charm of this Ardennes house is encapsulated by the landscaped garden, providing the perfect foil to the warm, inviting interior. Ingredients take the star role in gutsy nostalgic recipes, albeit with a scattering of refreshing creative twists. For example, the chef’s perfectly cooked veal in truffles with Asian flavours. The menu with options is a model of full-bodied generosity. Deliciously eater friendly prices!	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3339207536	Brasserie N4	La Roche Percée 1	Belgium	Martelange	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.brasserie-n4.com	Nessun premio	Modern French, Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This friendly family brasserie abuts the busy N4 highway, but as soon as you see the rolling Ardennes countryside to the rear, your peace of mind is restored (don’t hesitate to book a room here if you would like to explore the region). Frédéric Bolis finds his inspiration in purebred French classics, to which he is not averse to adding a personal spin. Terrine of foie gras with savoury sides, entrecote steak in a Josper charcoal oven, fresh pasta with truffles: the enticing dishes on the set menu and the à la carte offering of this seasoned chef will win over the most discerning foodies!	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3335995300	Origines	Rue de la Coupe 25	Belgium	Mons	Terrace	https://originesbyceline.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	A narrow lane near the main square of Mons leads to the endearing restaurant of Céline, the charming and ever cheerful lady of the house. The sunny rear patio features an olive tree in its centre. Chef Watteyne crafts a menu dictated by market availability, the seasons and his innovative ideas. Examples include his personal take on vitello tonnato or a fascinating tomato-strawberry-burrata dessert. Bold, distinctive cuisine crafted by a chef who takes pride in ensuring that each flavour is spot on and punchy.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3336221224	La Table du Boucher	rue d'Havré 49	Belgium	Mons	Air conditioning	https://www.latableduboucher.be/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Classic French	3.0	€€	t	f	Luc Broutard avows a passion for top quality produce, red meat in particular, as you will immediately realise when you cross the threshold of this buzzy brasserie. Seared foie gras, tartare of Salers beef, marinated pork cheeks or grilled tenderloin: carnivores will be in seventh heaven as they drool over the extensive menu. Rich, spot-on cooking, happily free of gimmicks and there are even a few fish dishes. Everyone feels at home at the Table du Boucher, to such an extent that many return in their droves.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
