3334091311	Tero	rue Saint Bernard 1	Belgium	Saint-Gilles	Terrace	https://www.tero.be	Nessun premio	Organic, Vegetarian	3.0	€€	t	t	Tero pays tribute to the land and demonstrates great respect for produce like the veggies and pork from its own farm (Rabanisse farm). Each ingredient is assembled in intelligently curated, light dishes that favour a natural approach. A 63° egg with a personal version of shakshouka and croutons. Playful, flavoursome and bang on target. The former workshop of artist Fernand Khnopff provides the backdrop to this sparkling foodie parenthesis so in tune with the zeitgeist.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3331786190	La Charcuterie	avenue Paul Dejaer 16	Belgium	Saint-Gilles	Terrace	https://lacharcuterie.be/	Nessun premio	Sharing, Country cooking	5.0	€€	t	f	The vintage charm of this former butcher's with its olde worlde tiles and wood panelling is eminently friendly. Walk past the delicatessen-cum-grocery store counter into the teeny bistro. Premium produce, wholesome, unpretentious cooking and mind-blowing flavours. Dishes to share, washed down with a glass of fine wine.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3332069535	Nénu	Rue Dejoncker 21	Belgium	Saint-Gilles	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.nenu.be/	Nessun premio	Vietnamese Contemporary	3.0	€€	t	t	It is neither its sober contemporary décor nor its casual vibe that set Nénu apart from the many restaurants in the Avenue Louise neighbourhood, but its anh nhau concept. This Vietnamese tradition consists in sharing small and large dishes and a fine bottle of wine with friends and family. The kitchen team adds a modern twist to traditional flavours, creating a mouth-watering menu (choose at least three dishes). Spicy wontons, vegetarian red curry, grilled salmon head with sweet-sour flavours and traditional spices…Superlative Vietnamese fusion cooking…	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3330740717	Yoka Tomo	Avenue Félix Marchal 26	Belgium	Schaerbeek		https://yokatomo.brussels	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€	t	t	A friendly restaurant in a residential neighbourhood with limited seating and a chef who crafts dishes from Southern Japan in his open-plan kitchen. Rather than decadent ingredients, you can expect authentic craftsmanship and seasonings that stimulate the tastebuds. Crispy chicken with a sweet-sour sauce is paired with crunchy vegetables and a rémoulade sauce in a tasty, almost addictive dish. Tomoyuki Ohara has no qualms about surprising us, whilst religiously respecting Japanese culinary traditions. Truly irresistible!	huberflorin	\N	\N
3331849135	BORIS & MAURICE	Antwerpsesteenweg 329	Belgium	Sint-Amandsberg	Counter dining,Terrace	https://boris-maurice.be/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	t	It is crystal clear that Boris and Maurice have worked together before (at Bodo). Their friendly neighbourhood eatery with a long counter offers tasty bistro fare with a twist. For example, you may start with deep-fried bites of sole and tartare sauce, followed by a juicy breast of chicken and a masterful Archiduc sauce (mushrooms and cream), finishing with a chocolate mousse. The French wine list adds the final flourish to this appetising banquet.	mazzaviktor	\N	\N
