3333917299	Si Xia Li (Huli)	2F	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The chef-owner has almost 30 years' experience under his belt, with notable stints in various hotel restaurants. Respecting traditions while re-inventing Minnan cuisine by incorporating Western techniques and creative touches, he has come up with a menu that is familiar and fresh at the same time. Try his oyster omelette, in which umami meets the crispness of water chestnut and celery. The slow-cooked pork belly with shiitake is another treat.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3334036948	Tong'an Fan Dian (Huachang Road)	A103	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	¥¥	f	t	Founded in 2003, this restaurant was named after Tongan, the cradle of Xiamen culture. The space is bright and airy, with a wall of oyster shell collage as a focal point. Formerly a fisherman, the owner is picky about his fish. Try the boneless giant mottled eel in claypot – the rich sauce complements the oily fish nicely. The quintessential Tongan classic of seared pork belly with dried oysters, chestnuts and shiitake is also recommended.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3331126649	Xiang Mo Jin Nian (Siming)	224-103 Lvling Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Fujian	3.0	¥¥	f	f	Its façade may be nondescript but its open-air kitchen provides quite a spectacle. Minnan-style soups are slow-cooked over heated sand on clay stoves for three to four hours so need to be pre-ordered^ the availability of some soups is limited. Signatures include Muscovy duck soup with mud crab, which combines seafood umami with meaty flavours, and braised soft-shelled tortoise seasoned with ginger and green Sichuan peppercorns.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3337196706	Xiao Cheng Xi	4F	China Mainland	Xiamen	Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Fujian	5.0	¥¥	t	f	By the pier, this roof-top dining room commands gorgeous views of Gulangyu. The owner chose to re-create the ancient Fujian-style architecture and landscaping in his stunning venue, complete with a water feature, lush greenery and stone arches. The menu is focused on Minnan fare, illustrated by deep-fried taro dumplings with pork filling. Salt-baked Japanese scad accentuates its oily, natural flavour. Don’t miss the puppet show at night.	ferraririccardo	\N	\N
3330163994	Z&D Cuisine	Shop 306	China Mainland	Xiamen	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Fujian	4.0	¥¥	t	t	This restaurant focuses on the cuisine found in the catchment area of Jiulong River in the prefecture of Zhangzhou, Fujian. Most of the seafood is sourced from the estuary where it flows into the sea. Bittern tofu simmered with russula mushrooms, clams and dried squid comes in an umami-laden broth. Spicy swimming crab with grated ginger exudes spellbinding aromas. Don’t miss the handmade Xiang Pu cake made with mung bean flour.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3339013334	Zhen Zhen Hai Li Jian	184 Xiahe Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Fujian	5.0	¥	t	f	Zhen Zhen runs the whole place alone: she's the owner, server and chef. She's picky about seafood, having it delivered a few times daily to ensure freshness. The well-made dishes at bargain prices have secured a loyal fan base. The menu comprises 20 items, mostly small plates, such as braised pork rice, and shrimp ball soup. Her oyster omelette is packed with plump oysters and garlic sprouts.	orlandofernando	\N	\N
3334376734	Lu Niang Zi (Huli)	161 Jiangtou West Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	¥	t	t	This simple shop is famous for beef noodle soup and noodles dressed in beef ragout. The signature beef noodle soup with pickled cabbage is a must – the beef long loin is perfectly cooked to be tender but firm. The beef bone stock is flavoursome, and the pickle cuts through the richness. The red-braised beef noodle soup, and the marinated meat platter with dried tofu, hard-boiled eggs, beef tripe, intestine and shin are also popular.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3338140984	Ming Yue Xia Mian (Xiahe Road)	180-101 Xiahe Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	¥	t	f	In the old town, this noodle shop with over 20 years of history is always bustling with diners who come for its prawn noodles. Hundreds of prawn heads are used to make the umami-laden broth with orange oil from the tomalley floating on top. Grated garlic adds depth and aromas. In addition to shelled prawns, the noodles are topped with prawn balls, lean pork, char siu, pork intestine and bean sprouts. The prawn ball soup is also popular.	lorenziarthur	\N	\N
3331016793	Wu Lan Sha Cha Mian	300-1 Jiaotang Street	China Mainland	Xiamen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	¥	f	f	Tucked away in a nondescript alley, this simple shop with its bright red wall can't be missed. Owner Wu Lan has been making sha cha noodles for decades, with a foothold on this spot for over 20 years. She makes her sweet, mildly spicy and deeply nutty broth every morning. Complemented by toppings such as pork liver, shrimps and even abalone, it is addictive! In addition to the sha cha noodles, try her golden and crispy oyster omelette.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3330148116	Wu Tang Sha Cha Mian	76 Minzu Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	¥	t	t	With decades of history to its name, this noodle shop is always busy. There is just one thing on the menu – sha cha noodles – but over 20 different toppings to choose from: an array of seafood, including plump razor clams and creamy oysters, and pork offal – even pork heart and pork tripe – are solid options. Less garlicky than its counterparts, its broth is made from toasted, not fried, peanuts to accentuate nuttiness and umami.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3330499100	Yue Hua Sha Cha Mian	78 Zhenbang Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	¥	t	t	This noodle shop has been around for more than 40 years. What it lacks in space and grandeur, it makes up for in good food. Besides the secret sha cha broth bursting with a deep peanut flavour, diners also appreciate the dazzling and almost infinite array of toppings – pork intestine, pork bladder, dried tofu, fish balls, duck blood curd, pork liver, lean pork... Pair the noodles with roast pork sticky rice dumpling for a truly filling meal.	marinotommaso	\N	\N
3334202886	Hao Shi Lai	24 Hubin South Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	¥¥	t	f	Into the second generation, this family business founded in 1993 features in many Xiamenians' childhood memories. It prides itself on Minnan cooking, especially fresh seafood dishes. The threadfin blanched in claypot has oily, silky flesh and remarkable umami. The deep-fried baby eels in peppered salt are crispy and flavoursome, the mildly spicy kick making them a perfect companion for alcoholic drinks. The friendly service is a plus.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3336168019	Xian Xiong Qi	29 Houjiangdai Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	¥¥	f	t	With live fish tanks lining the entrance, this is clearly the place to be for fresh seafood. The owner sources his fish directly from local fishermen, ensuring his catch is always the best. Minnan-style seafood defines the menu, and the peanut worm salad in a mustard dressing makes for an interesting start. The braised carpet shark belly and liver is another must-try: the liver is creamy, like tofu, and the belly has a fine, springy texture.	de santistobias	\N	\N
3334854842	Panda's	170 Xiangdianli	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace		Nessun premio	Sichuan	3.0	¥¥	t	f	This restaurant is set up in a Fujian red-brick mansion, with a black, white and wood colour scheme punctuated by pops of bright red. Both the owner and the chef are Sichuan natives, specialising in cuisine from the city of Zigong, famous for its salt industry. To ensure authenticity, most condiments are shipped from Sichuan. Try the chilli fish roes and fish maws with pickled cabbage and ginger, or diced rabbit hot pot in Sichuan pepper sauce.	beloveva	\N	\N
3330353160	Lai Cuo Cheng Bian Shi Dian	8 Dayuan Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	¥	t	t	This place dates back to the 1940s, when the founder would carry her mobile kitchen on a bamboo pole balanced on her shoulder and sell her bianshi dumplings on the go. She then settled at this spot and has stayed put ever since. Now run by her son, it has built a loyal following for dumplings – handmade like in the old days. The signature has always been shrimp bianshi soup with springy noodles dressed in peanut and fermented tofu sauce.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3337917913	Pan Ya Yuan	Inside Huihe Stone Cultural Park	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Vegetarian	3.0	¥¥	t	t	Deep inside a cultural park, this restaurant is reached easily by following the signs. Its idyllic, lush location is part of the charm^ the Zen-inspired interior is equally serene. Changing twice a month, the single set menu follows the Chinese calendar's 24 solar terms. The 10 courses go from light to heavy flavours with the climax being the minced mushroom patty in a black pepper sauce. The private rooms of various sizes must be booked in advance.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3338601571	Wuwei Natural Food	290 Island Ring South Boulevard	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Vegetarian	5.0	¥¥	f	f	Connected to a beachside promenade, this villa restaurant prides itself on its breathtaking ocean views, but also a Zen-inspired decor and plant-based cooking with a touch of finesse. It serves two set menus, both featuring season-driven dishes. Inspired by the Fujian classic Buddha Jumps Over the Wall, the rich and flavoursome Six-Treasure Soup is made with six different mushrooms. Ask for a table on the patio on a balmy night.	basileryan	\N	\N
3331713219	Dai Tai	20 Jianye Road	China Mainland	Xiamen	Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Yunnanese	3.0	¥¥	t	f	Dai Tai opened its doors in 2011, specialising in Yunnanese home-style cooking, especially the cuisine of the Dai ethnic group. The all-Yunnanese kitchen team has most ingredients shipped from their home province to ensure authenticity. The food is mostly spicy, but diners can ask the chefs to tone it down. Try the Dai-style deep-fried pork skin starter – a crunchy, zesty treat. Follow up with fresh sweet bamboo shoots stir-fried with Yunnan ham.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3338814112	Batelina	Čimulje 25	Croatia	Banjole	Credit cards not accepted,Terrace		Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	f	f	Although advance booking is required and the restaurant doesn’t take credit cards, Batelina’s fame extends well beyond Istria, and for good reason – for the past 20 years, this inn run by owner-chef and fisherman Danilo Skoko has been renowned for the high quality of its freshly caught fish. The focus here is on using the fish in its entirety, from the prestigious cuts and fillets to the entrails which are transformed into delicious appetisers.	krausmartina	\N	\N
3338974767	Paul-Arthur	23-25 place de la Pucelle	France	Rouen	Terrace	http://www.paul-arthurrestaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This former Top Chef contestant, who hails from the South of France, has set up shop in this half-timbered house on Place de la Pucelle. In this contemporary bistro, which still boasts its period beams, the chef cooks up a pressé of veal shank and foie gras with pistachio pistou^ hake confit in semi-salted butter, sweet potato and smoked hollandaise^ banoffee pie, dulce de leche and caramelised pecans. The style is the right degree of modern, the ingredients are seasonal, and the dinner menu is more ambitious than that at lunchtime.	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3338107491	Konoba Malo Selo	Fratrija 1	Croatia	Buje	Car park,Terrace		Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine, Meats and Grills	3.0	€€	f	f	You’re immediately struck by the typical Istrian ambience at this restaurant, which occupies an old stone building with two small dining rooms and an outdoor space and boasts a fireplace used for traditional cooking. We recommend ordering half-portions here so that you can sample different specialities such as the excellent Istrian cured ham (unique in flavour thanks to the way it is aged in the Bora wind), home-made fuzi pasta or tagliatelle served with a mushroom sauce, and fillet of Fiorentina steak grilled over the open fire.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3334043156	anx	Oddervej 19-21	Denmark	Aarhus	Car park,Terrace	https://www.frederikshoj.com/anx	Nessun premio	Smørrebrød	3.0	€	t	t	This nicely styled, well-run annexe to Frederikshøj serves sophisticated yet well-priced smørrebrød, which are classic in their ingredients and modern in their presentation. Contemporary art punctuates the walls and service is charming and efficient.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3331540131	Taj Mahal	Nikole Gučetića 2	Croatia	Dubrovnik	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.tajmahal-dubrovnik.com	Nessun premio	Balkan, Meats and Grills	3.0	€€	t	f	Despite the name Taj Mahal, the cuisine at this restaurant is not Indian^ instead, both the menu and the decor here evoke the simple flavours and traditions of Bosnia and the Balkans, with a couple of pages on the menu dedicated to traditional dishes. There is a focus on grilled meats (chosen from the restaurant’s own butcher’s) and vegetables, while a choice of simple cocktails is available alongside the wine list. This is a good place to try baklava, especially the one made with plums which is prepared by the owner’s mother and is truly delicious! Situated in the heart of the old town, the restaurant gets extremely busy, so booking is recommended. A second restaurant with the same name can be found a couple of kilometres north of the town centre in the more modern setting of the Hotel Lero.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3339041728	Konoba Vinko	Uz Cestu 57	Croatia	Konjevrate	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://www.konobavinko.hr/	Nessun premio	Country cooking	3.0	€	f	t	A well-run and welcoming country inn where meat takes pride of place on the menu. The simple, delicious cuisine is generously portioned and includes stand-out specialities such as suckling pig. In summer, there’s also a charming outdoor space for which booking in advance is recommended.	longoethan	\N	\N
3332076238	Konoba Mate	Pupnat 28	Croatia	Korcula	Terrace	https://www.konobamate.com/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This traditional inn situated in the small village of Pupnat, about 10km from Korčula, is run by a friendly and welcoming family. The menu features charcuterie produced by the family, goat’s cheese matured on site, home-grown vegetables and local wine and olive oil. One of the most delicious dishes is the home-made ravioli with goat’s cheese and sage sauce. The covered terrace is particularly attractive with its solid wood tables and lighting provided by lanterns.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3330847528	Vuglec Breg	Škaričevo 151	Croatia	Krapina	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.vuglec-breg.hr/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Immersed in the countryside just a few minutes’ drive from the capital, this rural restaurant perched on the top of a hill also offers comfortable guestrooms and a modern swimming pool. The traditional regional cuisine includes local specialities such as Zagorska soup flavoured with mushrooms and bacon, and snails baked in the oven with butter and aromatic herbs. The wine produced by the family themselves is a must, as are the delicious desserts and ice creams.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3333599940	Fakin	Trg Svetog Trojstva 53	Croatia	Legrad	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.fakin.hr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Ever since it opened a few years ago, this restaurant has helped to raise the profile of Legrad, a village in northern Croatia. Situated next to the church, the restaurant overlooks the village square and boasts a spacious terrace that is very popular on summer evenings. The interior decor has the same simple, elegant and modern feel as the cuisine, which features dishes from Croatia and Central Europe. Local ingredients plus delicious clean flavours, a hint of creativity and reasonable prices all add to the appeal. The smoked trout with horseradish mousse, barley popcorn and pumpkin oil is excellent. The 11 guestrooms are particularly popular with cyclists, as Legrad is the start and finish of one of Croatia’s popular cycling routes.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
