3339846018	Les Coloquintes	18 quai de l'Ardèche	France	Aubenas	Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.les-coloquintes.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€	t	t	This restaurant installed in a former silk - throwing factory is run by a young couple – he in the kitchen, she front of house. They propose contemporary cuisine, aiming to keep supply channels short and respecting local produce, trout, chestnuts, fruits etc. In summer, get a table in the shade of the lime trees.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3332609674	Orizhon	2 quai Jacques-de-Thézac	France	Audierne	Terrace	https://orizhon-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Seafood	4.0	€€	t	t	In their restaurant next to the port of Audierne, this pair certainly open up new culinary horizons. The chef is from Brazil, the floor manager hails from Finistère and together they serve up delicious, aromatic cuisine that will make you happy you came. The chef, of course, draws on the local pantry – most notably fish and seafood, to which she judiciously adds modern and exotic touches. Buckwheat pancakes taco style, pork confit, lovage^ tuna tart, tomato chutney with spices^ grilled octopus, beetroot, fresh goat's cheese, red wine vinaigrette. Pleasantly colourful and contemporary interior decor^ terrace with a view of the port.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3336272053	La Plage	21 rue Gustave-Danquin	France	Audresselles	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.hoteldelaplage-audresselles.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This small hotel-restaurant in a coastal village between Cap Gris-Nez and Cap Blanc-Nez is just the ticket on the Opal Coast. Young chef Solène Elliott, helped in the dining room by her partner, who provides friendly service, has concocted a tempting menu with a focus on fish (sea bream, mackerel, pollack). There are also other delicious and beautifully presented dishes: free-range egg mayonnaise with chives, ravigote, salsify, gherkin chutney^ shredded chicken leg, creamy parsnip, mint remoulade…	testagabriel	\N	\N
3338307755	Auberge des Aryelets	Place du Village	France	Aulon	Terrace	https://www.aubergedesaryelets.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	You have to gain a little altitude to reach this village high up in the Pyrenees, which champions its exceptional natural heritage with understandable pride. On the central square, a young couple has injected a sense of enthusiasm into this place, honouring the region's traditions and produce: free-range slow-cooked egg with Noir de Bigorre ham. Other dishes are more contemporary, such as royal sea bream with sashimi and asparagus. The appealing wine list boasts almost 500 wines.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3334460789	La Gabale	10 route du Languedoc	France	Aumont-Aubrac	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	With this brasserie, Cyril Attrazic has created the ideal offshoot of his gourmet establishment. The modern decor, adorned with panoramic photos of Aubrac landscapes, provides the perfect foil to sample full-flavoured, well-crafted dishes, whether indoors or on the shaded alfresco area out front. A few dishes you may sample include poultry and foie gras pâté en croûte with vegetable pickles^ sautéed fillet of hake, red Camargue rice and pistou of herbs^ strawberries, elderflower lactic sorbet and miniature waffles.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3339817755	La Chebaudière	6 rue Abbé-Joseph-Martin	France	Auray			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	A cosy and newly refurbished interior – wooden floorboards, green and white walls with a few wooden crates affixed to them, modern tables, brown leather chairs – is the showcase for the talents of the chef-patron. His affordable market-fresh cuisine is sure to tantalise the taste buds, thanks to impeccably fresh ingredients teamed with precise cooking and distinct flavours: just-grilled mackerel, aubergine and green olives^ catch of the day, mussel cream and artichoke satay.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3331294414	Le P'tit Goustan	9 place Saint-Sauveur	France	Auray	Terrace	https://www.restaurantleptitgoustan.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	The chef at Le P'tit Goustan takes pride in sourcing his ingredients locally, whether fish or meat, fruit or vegetables, before putting together a feast of tuna tartare, tarragon pesto, cucumber with fresh goat's cheese, manioc chips, cucumber sorbet and gazpacho^ roast pollack with turmeric and saffron, panisse, mussels two ways^ strawberry tartare... The best of Brittany inspires him to create original, masterful dishes, to be enjoyed in one of the two cosy, contemporary dining spaces. The terrace of this charming establishment has a view of the small port.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3336590705	Les Quatre Saisons	10 rue Jean-Baptiste-Champeil	France	Aurillac	Air conditioning	https://www.quatresaisons.onlc.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	The cooking of Didier Guibert, whose restaurant is located in a quiet little street in the city centre, is sincere and nicely done. He only works with fresh produce – and in particular meat supplied by his two brothers, butchers by trade. A well-run place.	rossidino	\N	\N
3333494314	Auberge de La Mère Duval	Impasse de la Linerie	France	Auzouville-sur-Saâne	Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.lamereduval.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Alexandre and Mélanie Baranzelli are thriving in a new venue oozing with country charm: picture a stream spanned by two bridges and a watermill! The chef, after honing his skills in top establishments, demonstrates his fondness for traditional recipes from his native Normandy, to which he is increasingly adding his own distinctive culinary hallmark.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3338564135	La Chatellenie	1 rue du Commerce	France	Availles-Limouzine	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lachatellenie.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Talented pair Emilie and Thomas Fournier have thrown themselves wholeheartedly into running this charming inn hidden deep in the Vienne, which gives pride of place to local producers. The delicious dishes are artfully plated and are good value for money. For example: asparagus and duck confit, served with a warm vinaigrette, or their version of devilled egg – flavoured with wild garlic. Well worth the detour.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3335739523	Italie là-bas	23 rue de la Bancasse	France	Avignon	Terrace	https://www.italielabas.fr/	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€	f	t	This enthusiastic Italian couple is living proof that Italians do it better. While he pampers guests front of house, she rustles up delicious Italian dishes, some highly creative, to propose tasting menus that include a vegetarian option. Buon appetito!	nikiforovevelyn	\N	\N
3339579475	Bibendum	83 rue Joseph-Vernet	France	Avignon	Terrace	http://www.bibendumavignon.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Previously a cloister, this fine historical building is full of character. It now houses a restaurant, wine bar and cocktail bar, plus tables laid out in the inner courtyard – bliss on those balmy summer evenings. Mathieu Desmarest, chef of MICHELIN-starred restaurant Pollen, devises the menu^ his wife Émilie, meanwhile, takes care of the music at this friendly, party-loving venue. As for the food, the contemporary repertoire is prepared to order, using fresh, seasonal ingredients, with Mediterranean undertones, eg sea bream ceviche, fennel and cherries^ Ardèche trout, almonds, roast white asparagus and white wine sauce.	leonechristian	\N	\N
3334136233	L'Agape	21 place des Corps-Saints	France	Avignon	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-agape-avignon.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Julien Gleize set up his restaurant on this pleasant square in the heart of the Cité des Papes in June 2014. The chef looks totally fulfilled as he works away in the kitchens, composing hearty, cleverly devised dishes, in which seasonal products are nicely showcased.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3333513901	La Chaumière de Pomper	Le Moulin de Pomper	France	Baden	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lachaumieredepomper.fr/	Nessun premio	Breton	4.0	€	f	f	Well - known in the region, this pancake house rustles up crêpes made from 90% organic buckwheat flour and 10% wheat flour, resulting in a mixture so light and airy the crêpes are even crispier than the norm. In fact, it even has a name in Breton kraz! If you can’t make your choice, we suggest sticking to the classics! Impressive list of ciders.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3335796714	La Table Bâgésienne	19 Grande-Rue	France	Bâgé-le-Châtel	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.latablebagesienne.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Behind the façade of this former coaching inn lies a contemporary interior, complete with a glazed wine cellar, and hearty Bresse cuisine to make your mouth water… Pommes Anna with frogs' legs sautéed with a garlic butter cream, Bresse poultry with cream and vin jaune, or the traditional nougat glacé. Pleasant, quiet terrace to the rear.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3338252637	O2C	20 place de Strasbourg	France	Bagnères-de-Bigorre	Terrace	https://o2c-restaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	A former helicopter pilot who now devotes himself body and soul to cooking, Christophe Bellegaud is at the controls of this restaurant, which sports a tasteful cream and chocolate colour scheme. He uses local ingredients to create 100% homemade up-to-the-minute market cuisine that is always spot on. Chantal, the second “c” of this o2c, gracefully caters to diner’s needs.	cernyfrida	\N	\N
3334411818	Au Clair de la Vigne	25 rue du Docteur-Louis-Marçon	France	Bandol	Terrace	http://www.au-clair-de-la-vigne-restaurant-bandol.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Run by an enthusiastic wine buff, this gourmet bistro also benefits from the culinary talent of a former chef of Christophe Bacquié. The food is authentic, generous and delicious. The regularly renewed slate menu stars a traditional bistro line-up, albeit with an updated Mediterranean tang: mint-flavoured courgette gazpacho and courgette flowers stuffed with Brousse cow’s cheese^ roast Mediterranean dentex (fish) and risotto-style celeriac^ pistachio-flavoured financier with strawberry soup… Located in a semi-pedestrian street just behind the waterfront, it is thankfully and peacefully off the beaten tourist track.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3339097034	L'Angle Saint-Laurent	2 rue des Bouchers	France	Bayeux		https://www.langlesaintlaurent.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The arrival of a new couple at the helm, who worked for many years alongside the former owners, has changed nothing in terms of the establishment’s concept or philosophy: regional produce is cast in the leading role (Bayeux pork, Normandy oysters, Carrouges gruyere) of the appetising lineup. On the corner of Rue St Laurent and Rue des Bouchers, the setting is also as appealing as ever with exposed stone, painted beams and soft lighting. What’s not to like?	gattimauro	\N	\N
3336829670	La Rapière	53 rue Saint-Jean	France	Bayeux	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.larapiere.net/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This restaurant in a 15C building, tucked away in a picturesque side street, is the lair of a cheerful couple, Simon and Linda Boudet. He crafts flavoursome seasonal nosh that celebrates Gallic culinary traditions. Good country cooking with the odd more contemporary touch: salmon gravlax, dill, beetroot and wasabi^ chicken breast, roast apricot, polenta fries and rosemary-flavoured poultry gravy. The 100% homemade profiterole is an exquisite blend of fluffy and crunchy – to die for!	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3335469351	Le Café des Arts	2 rue de la Poste	France	Beaulieu-sous-la-Roche	Wheelchair access	https://www.lecafedesarts-beaulieu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	In this peaceful village in the Vendée countryside, Virginie and Antoine Préteux run this beautifully renovated former village café-restaurant. The young couple has a proven track record that includes Michelin-starred establishments. Consolidating the sound classical foundations he has learnt throughout his career, Antoine concocts delicious contemporary cuisine, inspired by the market and making the most of regional produce (vegetable platter, creamy and spicy broth^ fresh pollack in a miso crust^ his tasty take on the chestnut mont blanc dessert). The interior decor is cosy and intimate (with seating for no more than 12, so book in advance!), enhanced by Virginie's particularly attentive service.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3333895337	La Table du Square	26 boulevard du Maréchal-Foch	France	Beaune	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.tabledusquare.com	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	t	This bistro on the main boulevard sports a distinctive contemporary decor complete with wooden floors, black and white striped walls and photos of the stars of French cinema enjoying good food. Cooking has no secrets for the chef who rustles up a spot-on, frequently renewed market-fresh menu. Given the location in Beaune, you won't be surprised to learn that the cellar boasts over 1000 labels – so drink up!	haascamilla	\N	\N
3334488548	Le Beaujolais	40 rue du Maréchal-Foch	France	Belleville-en-Beaujolais	Air conditioning,Car park	https://www.restaurant-le-beaujolais.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	With such a name, this Beaujolais could not do otherwise than pay tribute to a region famous for its fine food and wines! The friendly couple that runs this house has hit the nail on the head with hearty wholesome fare. Examples include traditional andouillette, whole grain mustard sauce and sautéed potatoes.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3332550786	Le Bistro d'en Face	1 rue Fénelon	France	Bergerac	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€	f	f	Aurore and Hugo Brégeon's restaurant boasts a terrace with a breathtaking panoramic view over the old town, the Dordogne River and its traditional boats. The tasty, well-crafted food does the vista justice: dynamic neo-bistro cuisine that brilliantly revisits some of the French classics. It is unbeatable value, and there is a good choice of wines by the glass.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3338878602	La Cour de Rémi	1 rue Baillet	France	Bermicourt	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lacourderemi.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	After pursuing a career abroad, the chef has returned to his roots, to the family's former hunting lodge, to devote himself to cooking – his earliest passion. In this convivial place, he has perfectly mastered generous traditional cuisine, from cooking to seasoning. We love the terrine with home-made sourdough bread and gherkins from the estate in vinegar. The plus: overnight accommodation in a cabin on stilts!	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3330392213	Le Moulin Fouret	2 route du Moulin-Fouret	France	Bernay	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.lemoulinfouret.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	In an Instagram-perfect picture of the French countryside outside Bernay, we fell head over heels with this imposing country house smothered in Virginia Creeper and its waterside terrace shaded by birch trees, without forgetting the historic mill, whose cogwheels are still intact. This idyllic venue is even more so by the fireside in wintertime, providing the perfect foil to chef Cédric Auger’s culinary ethos: first-rate fresh ingredients, consummate craftsmanship and cooking and polished table arts. The regularly changing seasonal menus pay tribute to the chef’s homeland, Normandy. Cosy guestrooms to make the most of this rural paradise.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3336639928	L'Arbre Vert	96 rue Principale	France	Berrwiller	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-koenig.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The tree mentioned in the name of this restaurant could well be a genealogical one, so closely is its history bound up with that of the Koenig family. Now run by the fifth generation of this family, the restaurant serves specialities from Alsace, which are accompanied by good regional wines.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3333095872	Pica Pica	20 boulevard Jean-Jaurès	France	Béziers	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.pica-pica.fr/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	In this friendly brasserie, they serve up uninhibited Mediterranean cuisine, cleverly blended with other influences. The menu features a selection of tapas (hummus with cumin and pita bread^ croquetas de jamón), picas such as lamb kebab with za'atar and sumac, or grilled octopus. More elaborate dishes include semi-salted cod, watercress and gnocchi, lemon and caviar emulsion. And then there are the tasty desserts. A down-to-earth concept, with sharing in mind. The lunch menu is a steal. A resounding success.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3337209251	AHPĒ	34 avenue du Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy	France	Biarritz	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	httpss://ahpe-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In a neighbourhood at a remove from the centre, this colourful, bustling bistro with caramel-toned walls and cheerfully mismatched furniture celebrates each season (the name is made up of the first letters of the four seasons) in a light-hearted atmosphere. Chef Idir Fseil is a fan of fermentation, but also of open-fire and a la plancha cooking, and he prepares a good market cuisine: white tuna, cucumber water and orange in brine^ pork belly with green chilli, raw cream and beetroot^ beef tartare, fermented black radish, bottarga and grenaille potatoes. Booking is essential.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
