3339371645	In-Fine	2 rue de l'Hôtel-de-Ville	France	Frontignan	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://infinerestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€	t	f	In this sleek restaurant in the centre of Frontignan, the youthful, high-spirited brigade of self-taught chef Grégory Doucey sources top-drawer produce to craft an appetising lineup of no-nonsense family favourites. Big-boned bistronomic fare that wavers between rusticity and modernity, with flavour as the underlying goal: egg meurette (in red wine)^ calf’s head with ravigote sauce^ fillet of mullet and aïgo boulido^ paris-brest pastry...	gattimauro	\N	\N
3331315255	Ô Moulin	1 place Martin-Dolt	France	Carsac-Aillac	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.latabledumoulin.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This couple who earned their stripes in the industry have transformed this charming Périgord mill – a water-powered sawmill, to be precise – into a peaceful country restaurant. The stream that drives the cogs can be seen beneath the restaurant through the glass floor panels. The chef rustles up delicious food that is very much in tune with the times – eg fillet of roast Limousin beef, topped with a good red wine jus and accompanied by Noirmoutier potatoes. They have a lovely shaded terrace, and the proprietress provides attentive service.	voicucatu	\N	\N
3330895897	Bistrot Saveurs	5 rue Sainte-Foy	France	Castres	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://bistrot-saveurs-81.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	British chef Simon Scott worked his way from London to Provence, before setting up shop here in the Tarn département. The vivid red façade leads diners into a vibrant and cosy pop-inspired decor. This eclectic chef and master craftsman works exclusively with good-quality (local) ingredients, in a bid to serve his guests precise, colourful and tasty dishes, such as just-seared bluefin tuna, flame-burnt aubergine caviar, quinoa with three vegetables and shellfish broth with Middle Eastern spices. This Bistrot des Saveurs is certainly aptly named!	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
