3339544876	L'Aillet	16 place Gambetta	France	La Teste-de-Buch	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	f	The chef may profess a simple, local approach to cooking, but his food finds its place among its trendy bistro peers on account of its definitively contemporary look. A starter of cauliflower, herring, tarragon and peanuts boasts a pared-back presentation and well-balanced flavours. The chef is also a past master in the art of tradition and roasting joints, a skill set we can only applaud! A welcome addition to the Arcachon Bay culinary scene.	grafpaola	\N	\N
3330769555	Café de la Fontaine	4 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle	France	La Turbie	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.hostellerie-jerome.com/	Nessun premio	Provençal	3.0	€€	f	f	A convivial atmosphere, good choice of unpretentious, enjoyable wines, as well as tasty and generous market sourced cuisine of Provencal inspiration. All chalked up on the slate. A memorable culinary experience guaranteed!	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3334559484	La Rochette	500 lieu-dit La Rochette	France	Labaroche	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.larochette-hotel.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Alsatian	5.0	€€	t	f	This contemporary restaurant is a real find. A father and son team prepares tasty and refined dishes, such as chicken breast from Alsace with a pumpkin-seed crust and airy dumplings… Attentive service, a good selection of wines and guestrooms to prolong the stay complete the picture.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3331683357	L'Atelier Flavien Valère	62 cours des Fossés	France	Langon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurant-latelierfv.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	After honing his talents around southwest France, Flavien Valère has decided to treat Langon to his culinary flair. He knows his stuff, no doubt about that: impeccable cooking techniques, perfect seasonings, premium produce and carefully crafted recipes – everything is from scratch, to our delight! Eater-friendly priced lunchtime menu. Bookings advisable.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3335785219	La Falène Bleue	121 place de l'Armagnac	France	Lannepax	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lafalenebleue.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Fabien, in the kitchen, and Hélène, front of house, have combined their two first names and come up with La Falène Bleue, where life is good and so is the food. Everything is both simple and delightful, from the carefully presented dishes (featuring ingredients sourced entirely from local producers) to the interior, decorated with paintings and vintage objects. This restaurant in the small village of Lannepax is surrounded by vineyards and has a pleasant terrace to the rear. The lunch set menu changes weekly and is good value for money.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3330931608	Le Brélévenez	1 rue Stang-Ar-Béo	France	Lannion	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lebrelevenez.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This pretty stone house in Brélévenez (a neighbourhood in Lannion) is run by Monsieur and Madame Le Marrec. Business is going strong, and this is not by chance: the well thought-out and tasty food is in tune with the land and the seasons. One last thing, the space is modern, refined and a pleasant place to be.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3331153202	L'Araignée Gourmande	8 rue de la Paix	France	Laragne-Montéglin	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.laraignee-gourmande.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Settle at your table in this bright, modern interior and experience the talent of Thierry Chouin. This Breton chef may have a particular penchant for fish - based fare, but that doesn't mean he snubs lamb and potatoes. He fetes the ingredients with nicely turned - out dishes, each a lovely homage to tradition.	grecodavide	\N	\N
3336400933	Côté Saisons	10 avenue de la Côte-Vermeille	France	Laroque-des-Albères	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cotesaisons.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Let's set the scene: a 19C building surrounded by greenery, with large bay windows, a flower-decked garden and a pretty terrace to cater to all seasons. On the menu are tasty, well-crafted dishes, eg warm calf's head with Charroux mustard, Cerdagne pig confit with honey-ginger, tender chuck of beef and pan-fried foie gras. In addition, the service is all smiles.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3339756842	Une Table à Deux	10 rue de la Pleau	France	Toulouse	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.unetableadeux.fr/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	After learning the ropes in Toulouse, Morgane and Nicolas made a beeline for Korea and Malaysia to research new flavours. Back in their hometown, they have chosen the Carmes district to regale diners with playful recipes that blend Mediterranean and tropical flavours, resulting in impressively curated and beautifully balanced dishes. Fantastic value for money lunchtime menu.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3334478167	Le Temps d'Aime	2 rue des Consuls	France	Lattes	Terrace	http://www.restaurant-tempsdaime.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Overlooking the marina of Port Ariane, this family restaurant, run by a father and son team, is always a safe bet. Whether you opt to eat alfresco on the terrace or indoors in the contemporary dining room, the concise market-fresh menu changes weekly and is very reasonably priced. The enticing lineup stars an intelligent blend of distinctive flavours without falling into the trap of excessive complexity: velvety parsnip, goat’s cheese, black olive and hazelnut soup^ fish of the day with celery and bacon risotto^ apple sorbet, vanilla, pecan and caramel cream. The evening menu is more elaborate.	calincolin	\N	\N
3336647426	Clément Artisan Culinaire	6 rue Eugène-Mazélie	France	Lauzun	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	This picturesque village of Lot-et-Garonne, which boasts a rich and chequered history, is home to chef Clément Papillaud. Having worked in top restaurants, this craftsman has a sure touch when it comes to crafting dishes such as chicken supreme from the Batailles farm lacquered with wild garlic and served with white asparagus from Fargues and parmesan milk. The chef seems to have a particular penchant for roasted notes such as coffee, in both the main course and the dessert. The country chic interior sports an open kitchen, a coffered ceiling and bare stone walls and rafters.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3332676449	Bistrot des Anges	Rue de l'Ouest	France	Le Cannet	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.bruno-oger.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This brasserie, run by the team from Villa Archange, sports a modern decor, a friendly vibe and set menus inspired by sunny climes! Tuck into artichokes stuffed with egg mayo, Florentine cream and basil or veal kidneys with mushrooms. For dessert, make your choice from a wickedly tempting sweets trolley filled with treats. You'll be in seventh heaven!	moltenirene	\N	\N
3331867471	L'Atelier Locavore	2 avenue de la Libération	France	Le Coteau	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.atelier-locavore.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	On the banks of the Loire, this establishment is now in the hands of a local lad. He aims to serve market-fresh dishes throbbing in flavour with a bargain-priced lunchtime menu and a more elaborate monthly menu. The majority of his ingredients come from within a radius of 200km, albeit with the occasional saltwater fish: his Brittany monkfish spiked with langoustine is truly mind-blowing!	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3331985056	L'Estacade	4 quai du Lénigo	France	Le Croisic	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lestacade.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	This pleasant eatery on the quayside, opposite the fish market, is managed by two young people with experience in some elite establishments. They propose hearty and meticulously made food that makes good use of regional produce (fish, shellfish and seaweed, of course, but also meat). The lady of the house is a radiant hostess. Smiling staff and attentive service.	moldovanmelly	\N	\N
3339184574	Le Relais des Salines	Port des Salines	France	Le Grand-Village-Plage	Terrace	https://le-relaisdessalines.fr	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	f	t	This waterside bistro showcases seafood flavours and super-fresh produce. The menu sails between timeless classics (oysters, confit of octopus, lentils, mustard-flavoured sabayon and the chef’s lemon pie) and more spur-of-the-moment recipes. Inside, this former oyster shed upholds its heritage, while the terrace overlooking the marshes is blissful.	martinooliver	\N	\N
3336114358	Le Margote	50 quai Michel-Féré	France	Le Havre	Terrace	https://www.lemargote.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	5.0	€€	f	f	In his restaurant overlooking the Bassin du Roi, chef Gauthier Teissere is assisted by Marguerite (his wife) front of house. He delivers contemporary, creative cuisine, jazzed up with the occasional nod to Asia. The stylish, snug interior is the perfect foil for dishes that reverently respect the seasons. Each dish is a masterpiece – not least the tender pork belly with a celeriac purée and smoked emulsion, or the generous pollack with cauliflower and capers.	landirobert	\N	\N
3333040775	Le Bouche à Oreille	19 rue Paul-Doumer	France	Le Havre			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This top-notch establishment is laid out behind a tasteful glazed façade. The chef adheres to tradition when crafting his bold, generous and flavourful cuisine but puts his own stamp on dishes with the odd touch of originality – think prawn tartare, prawn gyoza with coriander and lemongrass, bisque and cashew nuts. His friendly and efficient wife takes care of things front of house, dispensing insightful wine tips along the way.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3333054849	La Croix d'Or	6 rue de la Herse	France	Le Pin-la-Garenne	Car park,Terrace	http://lacroixdor.free.fr	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This welcoming hostelry, which belonged to the chef’s great grandparents, boasts an authentic family atmosphere. After learning the ropes in prestigious restaurants, the chef has returned to his roots in the company of his wife, who hails from the southwest as you might be able to guess from her accent. A quintessential French country inn, particularly when lunching on the small patio in fine weather.	monticristian	\N	\N
3339432183	Le Rousseau	16 bis cours Saint-André	France	Le Pont-de-Claix	Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lerousseaugrenoble.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In low-key, tasteful and contemporary premises, the new Le Rousseau is now more spacious and boasts a quiet alfresco area to the rear. Chef Élie Michel-Villaz, who remains forever faithful to his defining mantra, simplicity, rolls out a fresh, carefully crafted repertory, paired with lovingly selected wines (several hundred references – many natural or biodynamic), served in a casual atmosphere. A short supply chain business that is going strong. Simpler menu at lunchtime.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3338051093	La Petite Verrière	16 avenue de la Bourgade	France	Le Puy-Sainte-Réparade	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.restaurantlapetiteverriere.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	Seating around 30 diners, this gorgeous spot with huge windows set in green metal frames is not as small as its name suggests. A couple who are industry professionals prepare delicious, generous cuisine inspired by and made with fresh, market-sourced ingredients (including bread from the village baker). Think dishes such as arborio risotto with squash^ roast duck with spices, figs and seasonal mushrooms, apple and banana tarte Tatin. The menu changes every week. Good-value lunch deal.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3334752112	Sauf Imprévu	40 rue Pierre-Corneille	France	Lyon		https://www.sauf-imprevu.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	3.0	€€	t	f	Félix Gagnaire, a pastry chef by training and son of multi-starred Pierre Gagnaire, whose international renown needs no introduction, deserves our respect for this restaurant (open mainly at lunchtime) in the Brotteaux district. Wholesome food founded on pedigree French traditions: warm pâté en croûte^ thyme-flavoured roast veal, mashed sweet potatoes with chorizo^ rum and citrus fruit baba. The regulars joyfully dig into high-flying, yet heartwarming dishes oozing with respect for the region. Everything is fresh and entirely made from scratch. What’s not to like?	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3333700984	La Chartreuse	622 route de Béol	France	Le Reposoir	Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.lachartreuse74.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This village on the road to the Alps has long benefited from the generosity of the Carthusian monks, after whom the restaurant is named. The menu features well-executed modern cuisine that makes the most of seasonal (and often local) ingredients. The ever-popular 64°C egg is beautifully paired with a tempting medley of mushrooms^ the classic beef chuck is slowly simmered in Mondeuse and gentian as well as cervelle de canut (a herby cheese spread)^ the craquelin chou pastry is served with Grenoble walnut praline, hazelnut ice cream and melted chocolate – comfort food that uplifts the spirits! Vegetarian menu available. Large terrace in the heart of the village.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3333971785	L'Alicanta	Route de Meyrueis	France	Le Rozier	Car park,Garden or park	https://www.hotel-restaurant-gorgesdutarn.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	L'Alicanta has been on the scene for a while, perched on the banks of the River Jonte, in the exceptional setting of the Gorges du Tarn. The chef puts in a solid performance, his cooking is replete with distinct flavours and his dishes are brilliantly assembled. Everything here is home-made and the menu changes with every season. Absolutely delicious!	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3338680109	L'Auberge des Gourmets	9 place de l'Église	France	Le Villars	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://laubergedesgourmets.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	In a charming village above the River Saône, this restaurant has a traditional decor (exposed stones and beams, large colourful frescoes). Guillaume Laublanc, a native of these parts, sets about cooking his bistronomy-style cuisine with locally sourced ingredients and infectious enthusiasm. Cooked at low temperature, the Bresse chicken (from Johan Morand's farm) stuffed with morels and vin jaune cream is sure to win you over!	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3330193064	Le Bistro des Glycines	4 avenue de Laugerie	France	Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.les-glycines-dordogne.com/fr/hotel-les-eyzies	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	One of the undeniable bonuses of this hotel is its excellent bistro! The dining room-conservatory serves (lunchtime only) sensibly priced menus in tune with the zeitgeist, such as gravlax of Eyzies trout with a smoked cream cheese sauce or shoulder of lamb, confit and smoked in a casserole dish. Flavour, generosity and respect for the seasons set the tone for chef Pascal Lombard’s creative and enticing culinary score – we’ll be back for more!	popafarah	\N	\N
3338783056	L'Envers du Décor	23 rue de la Bienfaisance	France	Les Herbiers	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	http://envers-du-decor.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This old bakery has been transformed into a smart, contemporary restaurant that sports a minimalist vibe. Chef Aurélien Jousseaume earned his stripes in Michelin-starred kitchens with the likes of Etchebest, Guy Savoy and Guy Martin. To-ing and fro-ing between his open kitchen and the restaurant floor, the chef, who is clearly having a ball, takes the orders and presents the dishes himself. His delicious seasonal cuisine showcases his flair for creating remarkable sauces and jus: creamy jus of trout roe, sabayon enhanced with smoked salt, watercress and horseradish sauce, veal jus with lovage.	popovchloe	\N	\N
3336111685	sonoba	533-3 Motoshiogamacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Soba	3.0	¥	t	f	‘A soba shop that makes pottery’ by a chef from an arts university. The interior sports an industrial décor, with pendant lights hanging from a ceiling made of recycled wood^ a pottery studio is adjacent. Having majored in interior design, the chef was involved in the restaurant’s design and construction. Earth for the pottery, buckwheat grains for soba: both are kneaded with water, shaped and heat is applied. An unexpected point in common between pottery and food.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3333202534	Gare aux Goûts	26 bis rue Louis-Blanqui	France	Lorient		https://www.gareauxgouts.fr	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	f	f	Chef Vincent Seviller has come up trumps in this establishment near the railway station. He invites diners on a bistronomic journey in a tasteful, modern setting. An experienced and talented craftsman, each dish is artfully presented, flavoursome and balanced. The lunchtime menu is chalked up on a slate, but more elaborate in the evening.	farinellifarah	\N	\N
3337524003	Le Tire Bouchon	45 rue Jules-le-Grand	France	Lorient		https://restaurantalorient.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Pay little attention to the unremarkable façade of this restaurant, as the main focus is on the pretty dining room with its exposed beams and open fire. Refined traditional cuisine that follows the seasons is served. Friendly service with a smile.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3335707279	Sosakumenkobo NAKIRYU	2-34-4 Minamiotsuka	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted	https://www12.plala.or.jp/nakiryu/	Nessun premio	Ramen	5.0	¥	f	t	Soy-sauce ramen, salt ramen and tsukemen are Japanese-style ramens^ dandan noodles and hot-and-sour noodles are Chinese. The combination of both styles in a single bowl is the appeal here. Chef Kazumasa Saito applies his background in Chinese cuisine to full advantage. Dandan noodles with sesame paste and chilli oil is a perennial favourite. If you have room, try the boiled gyoza dumplings and steamed chicken with spicy sauce. In early morning, numbered tickets are distributed for the day.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3339519484	Agastache	134 rue Duguesclin	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://agastache-restaurant-lyon.fr/	Nessun premio	Creative	4.0	€€	t	f	This unfussy, up-to-date bistro sets the scene for instinctive, well-crafted food in the zeitgeist. Fine seasonal produce and a distinct fondness for vegetables result in dishes that combine formal elegance with flavoursome coherence. Now add lashings of generosity and a friendly vibe and you will find yourself in one of the best establishments on the Left Bank of Lyon.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3337189935	M Restaurant	47 avenue Maréchal-Foch	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.mrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€€	t	f	A cocktail of vitamins! Julien Gautier’s cheerful establishment adds a whiff of exuberance to Lyon’s well-heeled, tree-lined Avenue Foch. The smart interior sports a muted blue and flashy orange colour scheme, felt grey designer armchairs, linen tablecloths, a bar and a wine cellar encircled by a conservatory… The similarly charismatic service is as smooth as a silky béarnaise sauce. In the kitchen, the veteran and talented chef, formerly of Léon of Lyon, rustles up an appetising, market-sourced menu, combining flawless technique and know-how in a bid to pamper our tastebuds with delicate flavours tailored to modern appetites. The honey-flavoured madeleines served with a fromage blanc sorbet are awesome!	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3330886230	Veronatuti	122 rue Montesquieu	France	Lyon		https://veronatuti.com	Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	€€	f	t	Start with a salad of fennel and orange segments of Sicilian inspiration, followed by a main course from Emilia-Romagna (stracotto of braised beef in red wine, carrots and onions) and a dessert of Lombardy and Piedmont heritage (homemade ice cream made from toasted corn flour (farina bòna) served with a crumble of sbrisolona and a wafer-thin layer of chocolate). The duo who runs this authentic trattoria embarks diners on a whirlwind gourmet tour of Italy. Everything is made from scratch - even the coffee comes from a local artisan roaster. Delicious food without killer prices.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3339420722	Bergamote	123 rue de Gerland	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurant-bergamote.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This bistronomic bijou is tucked away in the heart of a district in the throes of renovation. In a cosy, nature-inspired interior, youthful Maxime Pujol rolls out his technical skills as he conjures up seasonal dishes, rich in crisp flavours and beautifully presented – all of which at eater friendly prices at lunchtime. More ambitious score in the evening with a surprise menu.	kralrosa	\N	\N
3335553544	Le Jean Moulin	45 rue de Sèze	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://lejeanmoulin-lyon.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Tables are set up on either side of this elongated dining space divided by a glazed wine cellar. The industrial loft-inspired designer decor is the perfect foil to Grégoire Baratier's contemporary cuisine. The menu changes regularly, but here are two examples to give you an idea of the market-fresh cooking served here: a delicate, crispy tartlet with Burgundy snails, creamy mushrooms and parsley pesto^ and a moist cake made from Ardèche chestnuts, with a few meringues, candied clementine and a pear and cardamom sorbet. Fresh, well-crafted cuisine, with the occasional nod to Lyon's culinary heritage.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3330789677	Le Kitchen	34 rue Chevreul	France	Lyon	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lekitchenlyon.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€	f	f	In the student district of the Louis Lumière and Jean Moulin Universities, this Kitchen is thriving. The interior, a delightful blend of Art deco and Scandinavian (as is the owner), holds only eight small square tables. The pastry display case (to eat in or take away), the work of the owner’s pastry chef companion, sets our tastebuds drooling and the kitchen is open for breakfast and teatime, as well as lunch (but is closed in the evenings). Organic local produce, vegetables mainly, take pride of place on the table.	serafinidmitri	\N	\N
3339471124	Le Tiroir	20 grande rue de Vaise	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurant-letiroir.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This establishment in the working-class district of Vaise, appointed in a characteristic trendy bistro vibe, is irresistibly endearing! The work of a youthful team, the food slaloms between iced tomato soup served with a mousse of white balsamic vinegar and a more patriotic Gallic line-up (tartare of beef, foie gras) – the menus and carte are regularly renewed. Excellent value for money and pleasure, including in the evenings.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3336175780	Le Zeste Gourmand	93 rue Bossuet	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://lezestegourmand.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Benjamin Bouvard earned his stripes at Bocuse and La Pyramide before opening this establishment. Expect a minimalist interior that is in tune with the zeitgeist, and food to match. The top-notch produce is well crafted to create variations in texture in dishes such as beef cheek confit cromesqui with a reduced jus, creamy parsley root and pickles. The Dombes chicken with a Thai marinade is a creative and artfully plated dish. Finally, when it comes to dessert, the chocolate and pine feuille-à-feuille pastry shows a mastery of ingredients and a desire to deliver meticulous presentations. Front of house, the service is well-paced and cordial.	pingliu	\N	\N
3336244704	PY Restaurant	16 cours Vitton	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://pyrestaurant.fr/fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	In this dinky brasserie in a smart neighbourhood, Pierre (in the kitchen) and Yuko (front of house) make the magic happen. In this contemporary decor, diners sample generous, well-crafted dishes. The à la carte menu in the evening is enriched with premium dishes such as hare pâté en croûte.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3332570443	Saku Restaurant	27 rue Rachais	France	Lyon	Air conditioning	https://www.sakurestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Saku is the nickname of the chef of this establishment tucked away behind a nondescript façade. He and his wife, both of whom are Japanese, prepare jubilant Gallic cuisine in keeping with today’s tastebuds. The produce is fresh, the dishes are meticulously prepared, at common-sense prices, and the service is friendly^ an enjoyable experience.	vitaleraffaele	\N	\N
3330732466	Siprès	2 place du Prado	France	Lyon	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.sipresrestaurant.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	A pair of chefs (both called Alexis) have opened this friendly restaurant on the Place du Prado and, in a space with exposed stone and tiled walls, one is in charge of savoury, the other of sweet. A perfect partnership, right from the (delicious) starter that they create in tandem: house-made pâté en croûte, enveloped in a crispy golden pastry – courtesy of the pastry chef – with a tasty, well-seasoned stuffing made by the chef. This is followed by a kefta of pollack, chickpeas, garlic confit and harissa tomato sauce, an interesting reinterpretation of this dish, in a fragrant and cosmopolitan version. The lunch set menu, devised for those on the go, changes every week^ for dinner, the menu-carte is more ambitious and evolves with the seasons and the market stalls.	paganialex	\N	\N
3337582682	L'Oustalet Maïanen	16 avenue Lamartine	France	Maillane	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.restaurant-saint-remy-de-provence.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This discreet and pleasant restaurant is located opposite the former home of Frédéric Mistral, a well-known local lad. Enjoy the sun-drenched fare of Thomas Yvan as he shines the spotlight on produce from the Alpilles and Camargue: cod brandade, crushed tomatoes and pistou^ Mediterranean gilt-head bream, velvety mashed green peas, parsnips and Noilly-Prat sauce^ raspberry mousse and sorbet and pistachio almond cakes. A sunshiny banquet served beneath the Virginia creeper arbour or on the patio.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3330352880	Le Bistrot 270	270 chemin de Malombre	France	Malataverne	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.domaine-colombier.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Le Domaine du Colombier's second restaurant serves well-structured bistro fare inspired by top-quality ingredients. Chef Anthony Monteremal's simple, enticing recipes play on bold flavours and follow the seasons, paying homage to the classics. In winter, the tables set up in the contemporary interior afford views of the striking glassed-in cellar. In fine weather, the terrace overlooking the countryside is the place to be for a moment of indulgence and relaxation!	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3334707926	Oxalis	Place de la Fontaine	France	Marcolès	Car park,Terrace	https://www.aubergedela-tour.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This bistro is the more casual sibling of the star Auberge de la Tour, helmed by chef Renaud Darmanin, which is even more reason to stay overnight in the medieval village of Marcolès deep in the Cantal countryside. The dining room takes up the most part of the hotel’s ground-floor and is extended by a terrace overlooking the street. Regional produce takes the limelight in well-crafted recipes, including veg from the cottage garden and other local ingredients such as volcano trout, poultry from the next-door farm, Auvergne cheeses. Examples of dishes: trout, vegetables, garden leaves and a knockout stock of fishbones or the melt-in-the-mouth vanilla and apricot millefeuille.	paganialex	\N	\N
3336032503	Rēpu	944 avenue de la République	France	Marcq-en-Barœul	Air conditioning	http://www.repu.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Chef Abdeldaker Belfatmi wants his guests to leave satisfied and with a full stomach. His organic soft-boiled egg with peas, his pollack with smooth, buttery courgette cream and lemon hazelnut, and his crunchy crumble with pistachio cream and apricot sorbet certainly do the job! This modern brasserie cuisine shows, if proof were needed, that the chef of the former Michelin-starred restaurant Le Marcq has lost none of his flair in the kitchen.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3339203273	La Safranière	52 rue du Lavoir	France	Mende	Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-la-safraniere.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€	t	f	This fine dining establishment stands on the site of an old saffron farm, tucked away in a secluded hamlet of the Gévaudan foothills. Enjoy seasonal cuisine crafted by a veteran chef in a fresh, colourful dining room. He strives to nurture and pamper our tastebuds with a concise, regularly renewed, regional menu: tomato and cantal cheese tartlet, gazpacho and mesclun leaves^ grilled Frézal trout with a genevoise sauce^ shortbread with apricots and rosemary and dark chocolate ice cream. Spot on every time!	bellandigiorgio	\N	\N
3335712567	Le Confidentiel	24 route des Moulins	France	Menthon-Saint-Bernard		https://www.restaurant-leconfidentiel.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	This restaurant – one of many (including some real juggernauts!) surrounding the lake – proves that good things come in small packages. In a compact dining area, you can enjoy dish after dish that is absolutely on point with its bold flavours, such as low-temperature egg, celery and pear, or hake, vegetable noodles and ginger-lemongrass broth. The atmosphere is friendly and relaxed. It really is love at first bite... Now that you're in on the secret, you know what to do!	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3337621577	L'Itinérance	24 esplanade du Général-Leclerc	France	Mers-les-Bains	Wheelchair access	https://litinerance.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Creative	5.0	€€€	f	f	On the shorefront, overlooking the quaint beach cabins and the sea, this restaurant done up in blues and greens bears the tasteful hallmark of interior decorator Caroline Tissier. The gourmet score features flawlessly fresh, consummately crafted and spot-on seasoned produce: mackerel flambé, aubergine caviar and salted anchovies^ pork chop, braised lettuce and seasonal veggies. After roaming the coast, it’s time to put our feet up!	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3337765766	Le Bistrot de La Cueillette	18 rue de Cîteaux	France	Meursault	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	http://www.lacueillette.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Comfortably seated in the vaulted space that once housed the château kitchens, you can expect traditional cuisine, meticulously prepared using carefully selected ingredients: Burgundy snails, Bresse poultry, Charolais beef... Laid-back vibe.	de lucaenrico	\N	\N
3336476085	La Terrasse	Place de l'Église	France	Meyronne	Garden or park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.hotel-la-terrasse.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The terrace under the vine-shaded pergola is the perfect spot in fine weather, while in winter you can take refuge inside, beneath the medieval vaults of this former 11C stronghold, done out with contemporary furnishings. On the menu: dishes with bold flavours, featuring regional producers: lamb from the Lot, farm-reared pork, and poultry from Mayrac etc. View of the cliffs and the Dordogne.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3332987386	La Capitelle	1 rue du Boulanger	France	Mirmande	Terrace	https://www.lacapitelle.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In the heart of this charming medieval village in the Drôme Provençale, La Capitelle – the lovely, lilting name denotes a dry stone shelter used by shepherds and winegrowers – serves a small à la carte menu, plus a daily menu that is changed up regularly with the seasons. Traditional recipes are given a contemporary spin, and dishes are served in a pretty vaulted room with an imposing fireplace. In fine weather, the terrace commands views over the valley. They have a handful of guestrooms for overnight stays.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3331027190	La Beaugravière	214 avenue du Pont-Neuf (N7)	France	Mondragon	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.beaugraviere.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	t	After a long and rewarding career, chef Guy Jullien continues to craft a culinary score that is unabashedly devoted to uplifting, traditional nosh with proper French overtones: foie gras flan and cream of truffle soup, fattened Bresse hen with truffles, roast rack of lamb in thyme, vanilla-raspberry ice cream vacherin… without forgetting a lineup of head-spinning truffle menus. As Gallic as La Marseillaise, the flavours are gutsy and big boned, to be savoured on the peaceful terrace in the shade of the trees in fine weather. The wine cellar is a treasure trove of regional gems. Authenticity and a love of good food set the scene in this family-run inn.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3330824326	Villa Mirasol - Bistrot 1912	2 boulevard Ferdinand-de-Candau	France	Mont-de-Marsan	Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.villamirasol.fr/fr/restaurant-bistronomique	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Villa Mirasol has entrusted the fate of its 100-year-old restaurant to Philippe Lagraula, a chef from Landes (Troisgros and Bras), who rustles up a market-fresh, generous, flavoursome score. He is famous for his unconventional flair, plating and balanced flavours that he rolls out in a modern, no-holds barred score. Examples include a crispy egg in herbs and grilled txistora or Geloux trout, coloured beetroot and verbena-flavoured beurre blanc. Sampling the house dessert, a decadent île flottante (egg whites floating on custard) on the riverside terrace in fine weather is a treat not to be missed!	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3336142620	L'Assiette au Jardin	9 rue du Robinet	France	Noirmoutier-en-l'Île	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://lassietteaujardin.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Imagine a small cheerful bistro-style dining room whose shelves are laden with fine deli produce, a pretty conservatory and a small terrace. The scene is set to sample tasty food in which tradition is cleverly paired with wayfaring influences: Asian and North-African notes flank the Fujiyama oyster (house specialty), the catch of the day and a seasonal vegetable tajine, or “A night in Essaouira” dessert based on dates, fresh dairy ice cream and honey. Delightful.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3330999702	L'Auberge du Pont des Pierres	754 rue Lieutenant Paul-de-Vanssay	France	Montanges	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.pontdespierres.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This restaurant on the road to Monts Jura is invariably busy! Chef Romain Blanc, who hails from the region, has no shortage of talent or ideas when it comes to cooking seasonal local produce: fish from Lake Geneva or nearby fish farms, pork and poultry from the surrounding area, local market gardeners and a herb garden. He also demonstrates a flair for preparing jus and a mastery of cooking processes, and makes a lot from scratch (including ice cream and bread). Bargain prices and service with a smile from Chloé, who will guide you through the nice selection of wines from independent winegrowers.	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3337191275	Le Montcenis	2  place du Champ-de-Foire	France	Montcenis	Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://restaurant-lemontcenis.fr/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Both the decor (vaulted cellar, exposed stone and beams) and the food are full of character. Laurent Dufour draws on fine produce to create generous and authentic dishes, such as guinea fowl breast with spinach leaves and carrots, and green cabbage cannelloni with smoked bacon. The menu changes regularly and, in winter, features truffles, of which the chef is a big fan! A cordial welcome.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3334211622	L'Auberge du Laminak	Route de Nouzonville	France	Montcy-Notre-Dame	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://auberge-du-laminak.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	In this charming inn on the edge of the forest, the Basque country – where the chef is from – meets fine produce from the Ardennes. The result is tasty and skilfully made dishes, such as the slow-cooked egg with piperade and Basque ham.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3335175735	Restaurant Anne & Matthieu Omont - Hôtel de France	1 rue Marx-Dormoy	France	Montmarault	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://hoteldefrance-montmarault.com/fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€€	f	t	Treat yourself to a gourmet interlude in this establishment on the village high street. Chef, Matthieu Omont crafts masterful, boldly creative cuisine, to be enjoyed in a spruce modern setting. A champion of Bourbonnais produce, he also works with top-drawer seafood: fillet of whiting in a crust of cèpes, langoustine cream and risotto of Vernusse pleurote mushrooms, followed by a rum-flavoured raisin pannacotta, finely diced granny smith apples, a pear sorbet and a Piattelli-flavoured emulsion. Comfortable rooms, ideal for an overnight stay.	beloveva	\N	\N
3338210935	L'Artichaut	15 bis rue Saint-Firmin	France	Montpellier		https://www.artichaut-restaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Headed by a chef whose enthusiasm is contagious, this place is an ode to the seasons. Dishes are crafted from market-fresh ingredients and the menu changes regularly: wafer-thin tart of rock crab meat, avocado and green apple^ roast duckling with stuffed thighs and mushroom and shallot duxelles. Fresh ingredients, recipes made from scratch, regional wines: a restaurant that cannot fail but win you over.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3332016318	Le 21ème Commis	23 rue du Mur	France	Morlaix		https://www.le-21-eme-commis-restaurant-morlaix.fr/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	f	Located in the centre of Morlaix and surrounded by gorgeous half-timbered buildings, this recently opened restaurant is run by a chef with experience in MICHELIN-starred establishments. His original cuisine combines Breton ingredients and more exotic influences (particularly Asian). Flavour combinations that delight the taste buds and generous portions, as in his indulgent pear and wine dessert.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3331775690	Le Bistrot de Guillaume	13 rue de Pont	France	Moulins	Terrace		Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Right in the centre of Moulins, the small dining area is light and intimate, already setting the tone, and we don't need to be asked twice to be shown to our table. But the best is yet to come: in his little kitchen, the chef-owner composes dishes that are delicate and intelligent to the joy of our tastebuds, such as his textbook perfect Provençal aioli.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3334387151	Perle des Vosges	22 route Gaschney	France	Muhlbach-sur-Munster	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.perledesvosges.net/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	In this family-run hotel-restaurant, the first thing you notice is the wonderfully traditional interior (chandeliers and silverware). The dishes range from the classic (marengo chicken supreme) to the regional (veal kidneys with mustard seeds, marrow quenelles and spaetzle), to the occasional more contemporary offering (lobster tempura). The cheese platter from the valley is a real highlight.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3336005932	L'Olivier	2 rue Saint-Grégoire	France	Munster	Air conditioning	https://lolivier-munster.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Chef Olivier Lamard, former second-in-command to Michelin-starred Julien Binz, now has his own restaurant. He proposes modern cuisine that draws on the terroir of Alsace: soft cheese mousse, potato salad and home-smoked trout, pork from Goettelmann’s farm, and for dessert, pear with sesame. Nicely prepared dishes made from fine ingredients, some of which come from the chef's grandfather's garden. A charming place.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3334183252	Les Grands Arbres - Verte Vallée	10 rue Alfred-Hartmann	France	Munster	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.vertevallee.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This smart, contemporary interior is the stronghold of chef Thony Billon, who stylishly adds a new spin to regional ingredients. His flawless modern score is paired with a fine list of Alsace wines. It makes the heart sing!	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3332904699	there is ramen	3-10-16 Amanuma	Japan	Tokyo	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Ramen	3.0	¥	f	t	This shop’s message is “Life is well lived that appreciates a nice bowl of ramen”. As a young man, the chef learned these words from his grandfather, and they still reverberate in his heart. Like many from the Mogami region of Yamagata Prefecture, he uses light soy sauce. He seeks a natural flavour for his ramen by using dried sardines and the umami of meat to good effect. Ramen here reminds customers of their hometowns. A photo of his grandfather, smiling kindly, watches over the room.	enacheisabella	\N	\N
3336770378	Cabane	8 rue du Docteur-Foucault	France	Nanterre	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.cabanerestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Chef Jean-François Bury, who boasts stints at the George V and the Shangri-La, is masterfully regaling Nanterre with modern, bistronomic nosh. Well-crafted recipes, generous helpings and wholesome flavours, such as confit of finely sliced veal belly in oregano, smoked apple puree, sucrine lettuce, or the exquisitely crafted and fiendishly tempting lemon and raspberry showpiece.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3331832051	La Mandale	32 rue Léon-Jamin	France	Nantes	Terrace	https://lamandalerestaurant.com/	Nessun premio	Farm to table	5.0	€	t	f	Picture a Klein blue frontage and a trendy bistro furnished with assorted antiques and numerous knick-knacks that is packed to the seams with smiling diners. It seems that Léo Huet, like other chefs of his generation, has hit upon the recipe for success: intriguing, tangy dishes rich in fresh premium produce, such as smoked mussels, kaffir, Thai basil and pistachio or steak with Gorilla pepper, kimchi, shiso and cherries, all with contrasting flavours that surprise and titillate the tastebuds. At dinner, the food becomes distinctly high flying as diners prepare to take their time to do justice to the excellent dishes recommended and explained by Maximilien, the chef’s associate, in a pleasantly unstuffy, relaxed vibe.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3339524960	Meraki	2 rue Menou	France	Nantes		http://www.meraki-nantes.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	In Greek, Meraki means made with love, passion and creativity, which perfectly echoes the ethos of this warm, friendly bistro. Maxime Bocquier in the kitchen and Clément Richard in the front of house (even if he also trained as a chef) have chosen to focus on vegetables and seafood. All their produce is organic and local, including the burrata cheese from a local dairy. The single set menu changes monthly. Examples: stock of grey shrimp poured over barbecued cucumber and smoked eel, which explodes as your tastebuds are titillated by exciting, unexpected flavours. Mainly organic, sometimes natural Loire wines play the leading roles, without forgetting guest star appearances from other wine-growing regions.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3337358727	L'Océanide	2 rue Paul-Bellamy	France	Nantes		https://restaurant-oceanide.fr/	Nessun premio	Seafood, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Roasted scallops with cabbage and crunchy buckwheat, red mullet in a shellfish jus... L'Océanide certainly maintains close ties to the sea, although the menu also features duck foie gras simply ‘cuit au naturel’ and veal kidneys sautéed with shallots. Chef David Garrec sources his produce from the famous Talensac Market next-door, hence the unmistakable freshness of the fish! The authentic 1950s vintage interior oozes old-fashioned charm by the bucket load.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3337622735	Cave à Vin & à Manger - Maison Saint-Crescent	Rond-point de la Liberté	France	Narbonne	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://maison.saintcrescent.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	La Cave à Manger by Lionel Giraud proposes bistro cuisine made with top-notch ingredients from Occitanie. The food is rugged, flavoursome and spot-on – special mention for the chuck beef slowly simmered in its juices and the velvety purée of carrots. La Cave à Vin, located under the same roof, boasts 2,500 wines^ pick a bottle to drink with your meal for a corkage fee. A real winner.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3331421563	Auberge Metzger	55 rue Principale	France	Natzwiller	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.hotel-aubergemetzger.com	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Successive generations have been at the helm here since 1885, each leaving its own distinctive signature on this historic establishment in the heart of the forest. A spacious, contemporary dining room provides the perfect foil to sample regional specialities: calf’s head and tongue, choucroute with all the trimmings, fillet of zander in riesling, while a slate menu offers a selection of seasonal dishes. Start your meal with one of their signature dishes, aniseed-flavoured snails à l’alsacienne, before continuing with a risotto of perfectly seared scallops. A cheerful, family-run vibe depicts the front-of-house team.	ferraroedoardo	\N	\N
3331434421	La Table de Nernier	11 place du Musée	France	Nernier	Terrace	https://la-table-de-nernier-restaurant.eatbu.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	In the medieval village of Nernier on the banks of Lake Geneva between Yvoire and Messery, this charming country inn is warm and hospitable. Rustic (rafters, terracotta tiles) and contemporary features (pendant lights, designer chairs) rub shoulders in a match made in heaven. The market-fresh menu errs towards the traditional, whilst demonstrating the utmost reverence for the seasons. The smiling and attentive service is courtesy of the chef's partner, while the paved terrace is everything one expects of rural villagey France.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3339669978	L'Alchimie	14 rue Maccarani	France	Nice		http://www.lalchimie-restaurant.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	f	Picture an infectiously buzzy neighbourhood hangout, underscored by the vibrant colour scheme of a refurbished bistro. A concise menu, succulent dishes, prices that make sense and the talent of a master chef: such is the secret of this establishment’s success, which is often fully booked. Velvety butternut, chestnut and bacon soup^ tandoori-flavoured roast turkey with black rice and vegetables: high-flying culinary technique by a gourmet alchemist.	melnikovstella	\N	\N
3334424607	La Merenda	4 rue Raoul-Bosio	France	Nice	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted	http://www.lamerenda.net	Nessun premio	Provençal	3.0	€€	t	f	A charmingly simple, old-fashioned little restaurant, where Dominique Le Stanc prepares delicious local dishes (pissaladière, tripe à la niçoise, stockfish, chard pie, lemon tart etc) to be enjoyed at tightly packed tables. N.B. no telephone – drop in to book a table.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3333723861	Chez Davia	11 bis rue Grimaldi	France	Nice	Terrace	http://www.chezdavia.com	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This likeable establishment, run by the same family since 1953, was founded by grandma Davia and taken over in 1985 by mum, Alda, now retired. Since 2016, Pierre Altobelli, whose impressive CV features star establishments in France and Asia, concocts tempting recipes rich in the aromas of Nice. Every detail is perfect, and the ingredients are meticulously sourced. Served in a welcoming vintage bistro décor steeped in authenticity. Heavenly!	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3339475763	Olive & Artichaut	6 rue Sainte-Réparate	France	Nice	Air conditioning	https://www.oliveartichaut.com/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Originally from Nice, the chef moved back to the region with his Breton wife after several stints abroad. He showcases local ingredients in knockout recipes, inspired by the sea and the mountains: pissaladière-style wafer-thin tart with roast black pudding, braised chuck veal with creamy chickpeas and a chocolate and hazelnut praline pie to finish.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3334815043	Bistrot d'Antoine	27 rue de la Préfecture	France	Nice	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	The lilting accent of the South of France can be detected in this bistro, where a really convivial atmosphere reigns. Things hot up in the kitchen, with dishes such as old-fashioned pork casserole or knife-cut beef tartare – only the best makes the cut here. Crowded? Well, yes: Antoine has a huge (and well-deserved) success on his hands.	salluis	\N	\N
3332848891	C'la Vie	12 avenue du Jasset	France	Orsan	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://restaurant-clavie.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	From a long line of bakers, chef Richard Durand has made C'la Vie a real mecca for food lovers. The food is good and life is good! The daily menu features terrific ingredients (most of them local), the flavours are distinctive, and the focus is firmly on dining pleasure. Enjoy your meal in the pared-back dining area inside, or on the terrace in the shade of a hundred-year-old plane tree. A fine selection of wines that celebrates the Rhône Valley and Languedoc, and rightfully so.	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3337250280	Ô en Couleur	9 rue de Beaugency	France	Oucques	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.o-en-couleur-oucques.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	In the colourful, contemporary interior with its large glass façade, or on the terrace in the leafy garden, tuck into the chef's well-crafted dishes concocted with the finest ingredients. Gribiche-style head cheese, pan-fried beef and crumbled offal, small pot of cream and a madeleine… Appealing to the palate, it's also easy on the wallet. Comfortable and colourful guestrooms are available, should you wish to prolong your stay.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3330417707	La Table d'Hôtes	10 avenue du Général-Leclerc	France	Ouistreham	Wheelchair access	https://latabledhotes-caen.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Not far from the seaside resort, this family restaurant is the stomping ground of a couple who have experience working in some fine establishments. Yoann Lavalley has bought the stove which he used during his apprenticeship and uses it to create seasonal cuisine that is both flavourful and indulgent. The sommelier, his wife, has curated a nice wine list that represents excellent value for money. Fish of the day, local meat, Normandy cheeses… A pleasant place.	popafarah	\N	\N
