3334574051	L'Orangerie	9 rue de la Prépoise	France	Pornic	Terrace	http://www.restaurant-orangerie.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Trained by some of the best (Alain Dutournier, Jean-Michel Lorrain, Alain Ducasse), chef Julien Lainé crafts enticing food that surfs between tradition (leek vinaigrette^ veal vol-au-vent^ chocolate fondant cake and cocoa sorbet) and modernity (carpaccio of croaker and blood orange dressing^ pan-seared line-caught seabass with a haddock emulsion). In a seaside resort such as Pornic, this eatery with two colourful little dining areas and an open kitchen is most welcome.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3337203579	L'Auberge du Pas de Vent	281 avenue Pas-de-Vent	France	Pouillon	Car park,Terrace	http://www.auberge-dupasdevent.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Authenticity is the name of the game in this Landes inn that specialises in hearty, wholesome nosh, light years from fads and fashions. The menu pays tribute to the terroir: Chalosse beef, free-range fattened duck, veal from calves fed on their mother’s milk, pure sheep milk cheese from a village shepherd and home-made sourdough bread (without additives). Examples of the nostalgic score include celery and fennel rémoulade, cream of split peas and crispy slivers of coppa or Jurançon calf’s sweetbread served in a skillet. Warm welcome and attentive, slick service. What’s not to like?	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3334342411	Bellavista	Place du Foiral	France	Prats-de-Mollo-la-Preste	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.hotel-le-bellevue.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Catalan	4.0	€€	f	t	It is always a pleasure to return to this eatery at the foot of the ramparts of a fortified citadel, no less! The menu positively smacks of the terroir, which is not surprising as the chef uses local produce delivered by the farmers in person. Slow-roasted Catalan lamb in fresh herbs with seasonal veggies, without forgetting cheese from the Pyrenees... Cosy rooms for overnight stays.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3330118596	L'Émotion	13 place Cadelade	France	Puy-en-Velay	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-lemotion.fr/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	From one year to the next and from one location to another, local chef-owner Michaël Ruat has been regaling the lucky diners of Puy-en-Velay. The interior sports natural materials and designer details (glazed wine cellar). The food forges a culinary course between regional Haute Loire ingredients (green lentils, Fin Gras du Mézenc beef) and a very modern repertoire of dishes (bluefin tuna, grilled watermelon and feta, sauce vierge and chorizo Bellota).	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3338223312	Éclosion	3 rue Laennec	France	Quimper	Wheelchair access	httpss://eclosion-restaurant.fr	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	This colourful, musical eatery in the heart of Quimper hatches modern, inventive bistronomic nosh, crafted by two seasoned chefs who’ve both knocked around a bit. The food reflects their experience and know-how: pink roast duck flanked by mashed, kernels and biscuits of corn, a few gooseberries and roquette leaves^ confit of monkfish is paired with courgettes, chard and figs, while the decadent dessert stars fresh strawberries with raspberry sorbet and a roquette sponge cake. Generous, balanced dishes and cheerful service.	sannamateo	\N	\N
