3333001341	L'AO - L'Aigle d'Or	5 rue Principale	France	Rimbach-près-Guebwiller	Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://hotelaigledor.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	A young generation has brought a zest of modernity by way of more contemporary plating techniques and recipes (octopus with miso broth, or braised breast of pork with bbq-style jus and chimichurri…) all the while continuing to celebrate regional traditions (brawn, frogs’ legs, game etc). Practical rooms for overnight stays.	ozmax	\N	\N
3334058067	Maison Devaux	70 rue du Commerce	France	Rion-des-Landes	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://maisondevaux.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	Housed in a half-timbered building that is typical of this part of France, this restaurant is the domain of Mathis Devaux. The son, grandson and nephew of chefs, you could say he was born into the profession. Expect a decor of terracotta floor tiles and exposed beams, with crockery and tables designed and made by local craftspeople. The chef concocts modern bistro cuisine, drawing on local produce (including black Gascon pork) in dishes such as poached monkfish, fondant leeks with aioli and zest of black lemon, or chocolate and fleur de sel Genoise sponge, vanilla mascarpone cream and a cherry gelée.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3332508159	Maison Cachée	9 rue Haute-Candre	France	Rochefort-en-Terre			Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	After stints in leading star establishments (Alain Ducasse, Maison Pic, Crillon), Alban Chartron (savoury) and his partner Sarah Alba (sweet dishes) have set up shop in Rochefort-sur-Terre, a drop-dead historic village, rife in quaint cobbled lanes and half-timbered granite houses. The duo of chefs knows the business inside out as their spot-on cooking (such as the cod of the day), spicy flavours (illustrated by oxtail with kimchi or a curry/peanut stock on fish) and play on textures (think carrot cake with a light, frothy yoghurt mousse) illustrate. Bistronomic cooking at prices that make sense flanked by a buzzy, homespun vibe and a quirky mismatched interior.	predapriamo	\N	\N
3339465846	Au Lion d'Or - Chez Théo	5 rue Village-Neuf	France	Rosenau	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.auliondor-rosenau.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	A pleasant and elegant inn, run by the same family since 1928. The chef brilliantly weaves flavours of today into the wealth of local specialities, without excluding the specialities of other parts of France! The selection of wines by the glass is short but well put together. Make the most of the beautiful terrace in summer.	nerielijah	\N	\N
