3332125860	Trusty Congee King (Wan Chai)	7 Heard Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.taihing.com/?route=brands-detail&id=3	Nessun premio	Noodles and Congee	3.0	$	t	t	As suggested by its name, you can really trust the quality of the food served in this long-standing congee shop. The menu has become more versatile in recent years with congee, noodles and snack sets available. All congee is cooked in fish broth that gives an extra dimension of flavour. Many rave about the pork liver and scallop congee, sticky rice dumpling with salted egg yolk and pork, and poached grass carp skin.	marinescumario	\N	\N
3336564025	Pharaoh	54 Solomou	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.pharaoh.gr/	Nessun premio	Greek	3.0	€€	f	f	This restaurant boasts a concept that takes guests back in time thanks to its focus on the flavours of bygone days. At Pharaoh you won’t find modern cookers as every dish here is cooked using wood or charcoal as in olden days, endowing everything with a sense of simplicity and authenticity. The decor is a show in itself, with its combination of modern and industrial styles, open-view kitchen, plus a spacious balcony on which to enjoy your meal. Chef Manolis Papoutsakis’ cooking revisits Greece’s culinary traditions, but with a contemporary touch, as witnessed in dishes such as Tarama, Dolmadakia, Papoutsakia and Galaktoboureko. In the evening, a DJ adds to the atmosphere with music played on vinyl discs, so if you don’t want to miss out make sure you book in advance.	sannamateo	\N	\N
3334260062	Akra	12 Aminta	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace		Nessun premio	Greek, Contemporary	3.0	€	t	t	A unique and special experience in which the chef does the cooking next to your table or at the wood-fired grill in front of you while you are seated at the counter. In addition, there’s also a bakery at the front of the establishment offering delicacies baked in ovens distributed around the room, that dispense their enticing aromas to add to the sensorial experience. Renowned chefs Giannis Loukakis and Spiros Pediaditakis run this small space in the charming Pangrati district of the city, where the young and relaxed vibe provides the backdrop for uncomplicated cuisine that is nevertheless full of personality and prepared with fresh, seasonal ingredients. The menu is refreshed every day, with dishes superbly cooked in the wood-fired oven taking centre stage.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3333579938	Jerár	55 Agias Varvaras Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://jerar.gr/	Nessun premio	International	4.0	€€	f	f	Although located away from the tourist heart of the city, Jerár is winning new fans thanks to the cuisine on offer here. In this spacious and informal restaurant with a kitchen that opens out on to the dining room, chef Charis Nikolouzos showcases internationally inspired cooking that combines Greek roots (thanks to his connections with small-scale producers who supply him with his fresh ingredients) and French and Italian culinary detail. On the à la carte, featuring abundant dishes made for sharing, we particularly liked the Cacio e Pepe with “Mikrolimano Shrimp”.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3333101221	Cerdo Negro 1985	5 Vitonos Street	Greece	Athens	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.cerdonegro1985.com	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Fusion	3.0	€€	f	f	This small taverna with a casual ambience, close to the Kerameikos archaeological site, is run in a relaxed fashion by two brothers who have combined their Greek heritage with a passion for Spanish cuisine. In this single-storey property with an attractive covered patio, they complement their varied à la carte of contemporary Mediterranean cooking (most dishes are cooked over a wood fire), with a six-course Taste of Cerdo Negro menu. Make sure you try the homemade bread and the “Welcome to Cerdo Negro” starter.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3334791415	Itsutsu	28 Murasakino Unrinincho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.wakuden.jp/	Nessun premio	Soba	4.0	¥	f	t	As a Wakuden establishment, Itsutsu embraces their 'soba and cuisine' motto while specializing in seasonal dishes. Soba is made into thin noodles, using only the smallest amount of binder and well water from Daitoku-ji Temple. The chef doesn’t brace the noodles with cold water, so the flavour jumps to the fore. Similarly, soba dipping sauce is mild, based on its salt flavour. At lunchtime, the three-item set with soba is recommended. Mackerel sushi is a popular à la carte item. Reservations are required for the prix fixe Buddhist vegetarian cuisine, which includes soba.	friedrichteresa	\N	\N
3334226326	Glorious Cuisine	31-33 Shek Kip Mei Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	Picking out live critters from the tank is part of the fun – Hokkaido scallops, Thai marble goby, and even Hanasaki crab if you’re lucky. As well as the signature braised chicken stuffed with abalone and sea cucumber, do try dishes made with chicken offal, such as stock-poached leafy greens with chicken liver. Double-boiled chicken soup with conpoy and Yunnan ham is available in limited quantities, so consider pre-ordering certain items.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3336787788	Ju Xing Home	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted	https://juxinghome.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	f	t	This hole-in-the-wall is always jam-packed and that's down to chef-owner Ng's cooking, not the decor or service. Cantonese stir-fries prevail, alongside a few spicy options. The must-try salt-baked Wenchang chicken is succulent, flavoursome… and tends to run out early. Live seafood is also big on the menu, eg pan-fried prawn in soy sauce or steamed eel in black bean sauce. Reservations are recommended and it's worth pre-ordering the chicken to avoid missing out.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3330115913	Kwan Kee Clay Pot Rice (Queen's Road West)	Shop 1	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$	f	t	Its red sign, basic interior and traditional stir-fries all point to an authentic Hong Kong food experience. Claypot rice is only served at night and takes time to prepare, so order it first as soon as you’re seated. The three-rice blend results in a chewy texture and appealing fragrance^ the bottom crust is always perfectly scorched. The white eel variety is especially popular^ pair it with claypot dishes with excellent wok hei.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3332381545	Sang Kee	3-4F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.sangkee.com.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	f	t	An iconic landmark of Wan Chai since 1976, Sang Kee has moved shop. The room is brighter, more spacious and offers more seating. But rest assured: the menu hasn’t changed and the food is as good as ever. Despite the lack of fancy plating and luxury ingredients, you’ll find yourself craving their salt-baked chicken, pork liver and wolfberry leaves blanched in stock, and baked fish intestine with egg long after you’ve gone home.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3330786796	Chiuchow Delicacies	Shop 4	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Chiu Chow	4.0	$	t	f	This shop isn’t particularly spacious, but that doesn’t stop customers from coming here for their authentic Chiu Chow cooking at wallet-friendly prices. Sliced goose steeped in signature spiced marinade is velvety without being greasy – refer to the mural for the spices used. The variety of chilled steamed fish on offer is quite a spectacle, all oily and delicious. Some dishes need pre-ordering and expect to share a table with strangers when it’s busy.	vogelbeatrice	\N	\N
3335332702	Café Hunan (Western District)	420-424 Queen's Road West	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Hunanese	4.0	$$	t	t	The kitchen team of Hunanese natives boasts solid skills, especially in quick-fried dishes that sport exceptional wok hei. Ingredients such as chillies and smoked pork are sourced directly from farmers in Hunan. The speciality braised pork elbow involves four complicated cooking steps spanning over 10 hours to develop layered flavours and the right texture. Stir-fried pork with Youxian beancurd and spicy organic cauliflower are also worth trying.	donatidiego	\N	\N
3337253717	Saya	Shop G701	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	$$	f	t	A turquoise colour scheme, rattan furniture and wall coverings impart a retro tropical vibe. The menu is dominated by Isan cuisine from Northeast Thailand, mindfully prepared by a Thai kitchen team. Khao Soy bursts with aromas from the coconut milk curry and chargrilled chicken. Pla Phao, salt-crusted grilled fish seasoned with lemongrass and pandan, is served with lettuce, rice vermicelli and a tangy sauce. Lunch menu offers great value.	longoethan	\N	\N
3336671364	Megan's Kitchen	5F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking	https://meganskitchen.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	t	f	The menu offers many Cantonese dishes, but steamed minced beef patty with dried mandarin peel, and Yu Xiang eggplant in claypot stand out in particular. Better still, all mains come with complimentary rice, soup and dessert. Their famous hot pots spoil diners with an array of soup bases and good quality ingredients. Those who prefer a little privacy will appreciate the booth seating with sliding screens as dividers.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3339284276	Juu-go	71-6 Jodoji Kamiminamidacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Soba	4.0	¥	f	f	Akiya Ishibashi tills the field, harvests the grain, kneads the buckwheat. The chef’s passion for soba permeates a menu consisting purely of soba and soba mash. ‘Think of it as cereal’, he says of his dishes rich in rustic goodness. Soba is deliciously fragrant, thick-cut and al dente. Soba mash, served with roasted buckwheat grains, is delightfully pungent. To enjoy the pure flavour of Ishibashi’s soba, try it first on its own, without seasoning.	grafpaola	\N	\N
3337583352	She Wong Leung	Shop A	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	t	t	In business for over 20 years, this shop is famous for its snake soup. While most people consume snake soup only in winter, the owner formulates a different herbal base for every season to make it a healthy tonic all year round. Set menus comprising of snake soup and home-style dishes offer exceptional value and cater for all tastes. Go for glutinous rice or lamb stew in winter. Double-boiled soups are popular but require pre-ordering.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3331970640	Ship Kee	6F	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	f	Ship Kee opened its doors in 2021 and prides itself on Cantonese classics from the old days. The barbecue chef honed his skills in some prestigious kitchens for over 40 years^ his Master Woo’s honey glazed BBQ pork is seasoned perfectly, tender but springy. The dim sum chef has 30+ years of experience^ his steamed rice rolls with shrimps and Chinese chives look like gems under a velvety, translucent skin. Call ahead to pre-order certain dishes.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3331410526	Yue Kee	9 Sham Hong Road	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	https://yuekee.com.hk	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	f	f	From humble beginnings as a tiny countryside joint in 1958, this second-generation family business has gone big, but without losing its flair. Owning a farm that breeds Qingyuan black brown geese ensures quality and a steady supply. Chargrilled according to the owner’s family recipe and served after 11:45am, their goose is known for its distinctive smokiness, crispy skin and juicy meat. The menu also includes seafood and stir-fries.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3332126454	Po Kee	425P Queen's Road West	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Cantonese Roast Meats	5.0	$	f	t	How far would you go for a bowl of Lai Fan noodles with roast duck leg? Every morning loyal fans line up at the door before this shop opens – that’s how good it is. A fixture in the neighbourhood for over 40 years, Po Kee is hugely popular among locals for its roast meats freshly grilled in the factory behind the shop. Time your visit as roast pork tends to run out before 2 pm and the goose before 4 pm^ or you can pre-order to avoid disappointment.	kovacscarla	\N	\N
3333676879	Tin Hung	Shop D	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Cantonese Roast Meats	4.0	$$	t	f	Popular with locals since 2001, this shop sells its signature roast goose in specific cuts, halves or whole. Geese are shipped from Foshan daily, marinated, roasted to perfection, and served piping hot. Other standouts include honey-glazed char siu, roast duck and drunken chicken. Those looking to pair the meats with a local drink should try their herbal tea. Given the reasonable prices and limited seats, it makes sense to arrive early.	monticristian	\N	\N
3339863013	Tak Kee	Shop G	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Chiu Chow	3.0	$$	t	t	It started out as a street-side hawker stall in the 1990s and still retains the casual, vibrant vibe. The second-generation hands-on owner shops for groceries every day and sometimes helps the experienced chefs with kitchen chores. Pork tripe and peppercorn soup is a culinary highlight, using peppers from Malaysia and Indonesia. Regulars also come for its spiced marinated goose liver, crispy chitterlings stuffed with glutinous rice and oyster omelette.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3333327988	Tim Ho Wan (Sham Shui Po)	9-11 Fuk Wing Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.timhowan.com.hk	Nessun premio	Dim Sum	4.0	$	t	t	The second branch of this famous dim sum chain is roomier than the original, but don’t be surprised to still find a queue of expectant diners at the entrance. Over 20 different dim sum are on offer, all skilfully made and reasonably priced. Some items rotate every two to three months to keep the menu fresh. Don’t miss their shrimp dumplings, baked buns with barbecue pork filling and steamed beef balls.	hatajfiorello	\N	\N
3332027302	Lucky Indonesia	46 Tung Ming Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.instagram.com/luckyindonesian/	Nessun premio	Indonesian	5.0	$	f	f	For over 30 years, this tiny gem has been famous in the neighbourhood for its authentic Central Javanese cooking. The room feels cosy and youthful after a facelift and the food is as tasty as always. For chargrilled satay exuding an addictive smoky aroma, choose from lamb, pork and chicken varieties. Lontong capgome is sticky rice balls with several side dishes such as beef rendang, opor ayam and pindang egg. Pair with an iced longan drink.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3338422966	Takeya	Shop 1	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	$$	f	f	This intimate 15-seater yakitori shop is the brainchild of a Japanese engineer, now the chef, and his wife, now the maître d'. For over a decade, they’ve been feeding hungry diners in the neighbourhood with quality grilled food, with some ingredients flown in from Japan. Rare cuts such as chicken heart and hatsumoto (artery) are definitely worth a try. Pair them with their selection of sake or home-brewed umeshu. Reservations are recommended.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3333812405	La Trattoria	Via Maistra 215	Switzerland	Pontresina	Car park,Terrace	https://www.trattoria-walther.ch/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	f	f	In the charming Hotel Walther, one of Pontresina's most emblematic hotels, this lovely Trattoria has an authentic, lively atmosphere and a stylish rustic feel. The appetising menu embraces all regions of Italy, with delicious pasta as the centrepiece and the focus firmly on flavour and freshness. Friendly Italian service and a good selection of wines.	moltenirene	\N	\N
3330681484	Hao Tang Hao Mian (Tai Wai)	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	$$	f	f	An owner-chef with over 20 years of experience in French cooking opened this 20-seater specialising in just 12 noodle soup items, each with a specific soup base and topping. The signature flat noodles in beef soup with Sichuanese beef cheek and French-style braised oxtail takes two days to make, involving eclectic techniques. The dessert menu is equally impressive – try the all-natural sorbets made in-house with fresh fruits.	gallofilippo	\N	\N
3339919872	Ho To Tai	67 Fau Tsoi Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	f	f	Traditional shops that make their own noodles from scratch are hard to come by. Founded in 1946, this household name is among the remaining few. Though the nostalgic two-storey shop draws a crowd with its signature wonton soup, zhajiang noodles and beef brisket noodle soup are also popular. Try braised white radish with shrimp roe for the deep umami and briny-sweetness. The owner also runs a dried noodle factory with retail outlets all over town.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3330298113	Kwan Kee Bamboo Noodles	Shop E	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	3.0	$	f	t	It’s inside a local market but easy to spot, thanks to the big yellow sign. Watch the kitchen at work through the glass wall as noodles are made the traditional way – with the chef seesawing on a bamboo pole to painstakingly knead the egg-rich dough for that stringy texture. Secret techniques are deployed to remove the soapy taste of lye and accentuate the eggy flavour. Don’t miss the signature noodles tossed in shrimp roe and oyster sauce.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3330084339	Lau Sum Kee (Fuk Wing Street)	82 Fuk Wing Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	f	f	Since 1956, this branch (and the original shop around the corner) has been packed with customers buzzing in and out. The third-generation family business still kneads noodle dough with a bamboo pole, like it used to be done, for that springy texture. Wontons are made on the spot with whole prawns and pork^ even the crunchy radish pickles are homemade. Wonton noodles are a must^ you can choose one or two more toppings if you like.	munteanuclaudia	\N	\N
3331419811	Mak Man Kee	51 Parkes Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only	https://www.mmk.hk	Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	t	f	No one is here for the no-frills interior, typical of any noodle shop in Hong Kong. This 60-year-old establishment is all about Cantonese wonton soup noodles – firm and bouncy prawns, visible through the paper-thin translucent skin, with springy duck egg noodles swimming in a flavourful broth. The noodles taste equally great when simply tossed in oyster sauce or shrimp roe, the latter also available as a pre-packaged condiment to go.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3337963305	Sister Wah	Shop A1	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	t	t	The legendary Sister Wah is no longer at the helm but her sons are running the shop just like she used to. The signature beef brisket in clear soup uses fresh local beef which is braised in a stock with over 10 different herbs. Popular items on the brief menu include homemade pork and cabbage dumplings, drunken chicken, Dan Dan noodles, and braised white radish in beef juices. With only six tables, it fills up as soon as it opens.	galbanielena	\N	\N
3330749504	Tsim Chai Kee (Wellington Street)	98 Wellington Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	t	t	The long lunchtime queue happens for a reason – the noodles here are bouncy and the broth is flavoursome. Only three toppings are offered – springy dace balls, wontons generously filled with pork and shrimps, and sliced beef with a robust meaty flavour and tender texture. You can even choose a combination of any two or all three toppings. Expect to share a table with strangers when it’s busy or eat outside of peak times to beat the crowd.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3334327192	Tasty (Central)	Shop 3016-3018	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access	http://www.tasty.com.hk	Nessun premio	Noodles and Congee	4.0	$$	f	t	Be prepared to queue and share a table because over 1,000 customers a day, many of whom work in IFC, crowd into this Tasty. They mostly come for the trademark shrimp wonton or the much-loved beef and rice noodle stir fry^ congee with prawns and dim sum are also recommended from the vast choice on offer. The last redecoration left the interior looking a lot more contemporary.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3339802844	Shugetsu Ramen (Central)	5 Gough Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining	http://www.shugetsu.com.hk	Nessun premio	Ramen	4.0	$$	t	f	The queues form early for the ramen here, with many of the customers coming for the Tsukemen ramen, as well as the Abura and special soup ramen. The shop makes its own noodles – which you can have thick or thin – but it is the sauce at the base of the slow-cooked soup that really makes the difference: it’s fermented for 18 months in a 100-year-old wooden basket and adds richness and depth.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3331616936	Dragon Inn	Miles 19	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.dragoninn1939.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	$$	f	t	This restaurant is known by almost everyone in the neighbourhood and was revamped in 2017 to include more private rooms alongside the main dining hall. Most guests pick their seafood from the nearby wet market for the chefs here to cook up^ others choose from the catch of the day without looking at the menu. Baked baby lobster with cheese and baked oysters with port are not to be missed. It also serves dim sum during the day.	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3336323813	Din Tai Fung (Tsim Sha Tsui)	Shop 306	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.dintaifung.com.hk	Nessun premio	Shanghainese	4.0	$$	t	f	From the late Mr Yang’s first shop in Taiwan in 1958 grew a multinational chain with branches all over the world. It’s famous for good service, competitive prices and listening to its customer’s feedback, but mostly for its xiao long bao made on the spot. Even the vinegar, free of artificial colours and preservatives, is shipped from Taiwan. Seating accommodates different party sizes, from solo diners to parties of 12. Expect long queues at peak hours.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3333762265	Wing Lai Yuen	Shop 102-105	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Shanghainese, Sichuan	5.0	$$	f	f	Originally a run-down shop in a squatter village, it moved to this airy and bright location in 2000. But one thing never changed – the food is as delicious and affordably priced as ever. The signature Dan Dan noodles come in two versions: a meat one with ground pork and a traditional one without, plus a spicy or mild broth to choose from. Shuizhu mandarin fish packs numbing heat and the portion size is big enough for a few to share.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3339415258	Yi Jia	Shop G04	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Shanghainese, Sichuan	4.0	$$	f	t	A stark contrast of colours, neon lights and retro patterns make the room unorthodox but welcoming. On the menu, you can find Shanghainese and Sichuanese classics like Qili Zhuang drunken chicken in wine lees, and Sichuan boiled fish. But novelty creations such as deep-fried soufflé meringue with mango custard filling are also worth trying. The creator’s sense of humour comes through in the cheeky drinks menu. Set menus are especially well priced.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3333851635	Fung Shing (North Point)	62-68 Java Road	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Shun Tak	4.0	$$	t	t	This long-standing champion of Shun Tak cuisine sports traditional fixtures and fittings. Locals and tourists come for dim sum in the morning, while painstakingly prepared Cantonese favourites and Shun Tak specialities are served at lunch and dinner. Besides signatures like crispy fried chicken and Daliang-style scrambled egg white with milk, don’t miss their sugar egg puff doughnuts available at weekend lunchtime only. Hearty portions to share.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3332901029	Cheung Hing Kee (Tsim Sha Tsui)	GF	Hong Kong	Hong Kong		https://www.chkspb.com	Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	t	f	Besides the typical sheng jian bao with soupy pork filling, this shop serves varieties such as shrimp, mala pork, truffle, crabmeat and roe. The buns are springy, brimming with filling, and crispy on the bottom.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3331585118	Fisholic (North Point)	Shop 14	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.fisholic.hk/	Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	$	t	t	Famous for snacks and noodles made with fish, this stall sells playful items like deep-fried minced fish in the guise of French fries, or fish skin nachos. Fishotto, where minced fish is shaped like rice grains, is also good.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3339682890	Kai Kai (Jordan)	29 Ning Po Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	$	f	f	Traditional Chinese sweet soups like tofu skin soup with ginkgo and Job’s tears, or black sesame soup boast rich flavours. Top it with glutinous rice balls or a hard-boiled egg for extra texture.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
3331408123	Kung Wo Beancurd Factory	118 Pei Ho Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	t	f	This much-loved shop makes its own tofu that boasts a deep, rich soy aroma. As well as the renowned tofu pudding, it also carries other soy products like soy milk, fried stuffed tofu, tofu puffs and golden fish tofu.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3336027168	Sang Kee Foods (Western District)	Shop 4	Hong Kong	Hong Kong			Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	$	t	t	Come to this place with a nose-to-tail concept for Chiuchow-style marinated goose. Made with grain-fed goose from Chiuchow, it boasts a firm texture and meaty flavour. Try the goose blood curd, web, wing, liver, intestine and gizzard, too.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3337871819	Yuan is Here (Western District)	31 North Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Taiwanese	3.0	$	t	t	Decorated with memorabilia and buzzing with night market vibes, this street food shop is the brainchild of its Taiwan-born owner. Some ingredients are imported direct from his hometown to ensure that every bite is as authentic as possible. The signature minced braised pork rice boasts depth and a melty texture, while the traditionally-made double egg oyster omelette is both chewy and eggy at the same time. Round off with taro ball sweet soup.	ferrettivladislav	\N	\N
3333834770	Samsen (Sheung Wan)	23 Jervois Street	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.samsen-hk.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	$$	f	t	Readers may recognize the name it shares with a noodle shop in Wan Chai – yes, this is a spinoff by the same owner-chef, Adam Cliff. While it shares almost the same menu as the Wan Chai branch, certain exclusive dishes stand out. For instance, its signature 11-spice Northern Thai curry takes up to eight hours to make and is the perfect companion to egg noodles. Desserts like young coconut ice cream or mango and sticky rice are also pluses.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
3335104730	Samsen (Wan Chai)	68 Stone Nullah Lane	Hong Kong	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.samsen-hk.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	$$	t	f	This casual Thai noodle shop next to the historic Blue House is aptly named after an area in Bangkok where the Chinese traded with the Thais. Rattan blinds, bare concrete walls and distressed wood furniture give off a street-stall vibe. The signature boat noodles are not to be missed – the flavoursome broth alone takes 6 hours to make. Those with a sweet tooth can round things off with young coconut ice cream. Come early to beat the crowd.	florescufrancesca	\N	\N
3331976893	Sing Kee	2F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.singkeedining.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	5.0	$$	t	t	Sing Kee is a bright, tidy spot serving traditional, no-frills Cantonese food – something that’s increasingly hard to find in Central. Standouts include pan-seared salted chicken, and grilled tiger prawns in Malaysian curry sauce with crispy rice crackers. Specialities like double-boiled fish maw and pork lung in almond milk need pre-ordering. Come at lunch to take advantage of some reasonable prices.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3339511303	Tai Wai Dining Room (Tai Wai)	98 Chik Fuk Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Valet parking	http://www.taiwaidining.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	t	f	The red lanterns at the entrance are a prelude to the nostalgic, Chinese-style interior. The experienced kitchen team shows respect to Cantonese traditions, but with a subtle sense of cheeky humour. Dim sum dominates the menu at lunch, and all-time favourites like duo sausage rolls and pan-fried chicken sticky rice dumplings particularly stand out. Portion sizes are generous, service is thoughtful – and the food is consistently good.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
3330766170	Tai Wing Wah	2F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	f	This bright, fresh and long-standing Cantonese restaurant serves dim sum and ‘Walled Village’ cuisine, alongside assorted Cantonese classics. Walled village-style five-flavour chicken boasts flavoursome, velvety meat. Other specialities include roast duck with bean paste and coriander^ claypot rice with lard, premium soy sauce, steamed mullet with salted lemon^ and, above all, the steamed sponge cake. Also check out the seasonal menu.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3338683043	Din Tai Fung (Causeway Bay)	Shop G3-G11	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://www.dintaifung.com.hk	Nessun premio	Shanghainese	3.0	$$	f	f	The xiao long bao are good enough to justify the long queues – so worry not. Alongside the traditional soupy pork filling, they also come in novelty versions such as black truffle and angled luffa with shrimps. Ingredients are sourced from the same suppliers as its Taiwan flagship and the same kitchen team here delivers food in consistently high quality. Other standouts include double-boiled chicken soup and braised beef brisket noodle soup.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3334229978	Eton	1-2F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Shun Tak	5.0	$$	f	t	In 2019, the long-standing household name Fung Shing closed its doors as the owner-chef retired. A regular customer and the staff then got together to re-open it as Eton in 2020. The room was renovated and about 80% of the kitchen and service teams returned. The menu is largely the same^ dim sum, crispy fried chicken, deep-fried shrimp toast, scrambled egg white with milk in Daliang style, and Shun Tak fish tripe thick soup are still recommended.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3335321013	Ancient Moon	Shop A	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	Singaporean and Malaysian	3.0	$	f	f	On a trip to Singapore and Malaysia, owners Fanni and Lico fell in love with their street food which inspired them to open their fun little spot. The small menu lists about 20 items, but you won’t find typical national dishes here. Instead, it’s among the few places that offer Malaysian chilli pan mee (a flavoursome noodle dish with dried fish and chilli sauce) and free refill of Singaporean bak kut teh, a MSG-free, peppery pork rib soup.	bergmannalexandru	\N	\N
3336942691	Ăn Chơi	15-17 Mercer Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.anchoi.hk	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	4.0	$$	f	t	Run by a binational Chinese-Vietnamese couple, the colourful Ăn Chơi captures the liveliness of Vietnamese street stalls. Their bánh mì sandwiches come in an array of fillings^ varying versions of phở are made according to different regional traditions. Lã Vọng grilled fish uses halibut instead of river fish^ the house-fermented fish sauce is loaded in full-bodied unique flavours. For drinks, try egg coffee or Vietnamese beer.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3335489788	Ba Yi	43 Water Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Xinjiang	5.0	$$	f	f	Despite being somewhat out of the way, lamb-lovers gather here in numbers for items such as stewed lamb and mutton skewers, prepared by the Xinjiangese kitchen team. The signature roasted lamb leg is big enough to share between two and needs pre-ordering. Besides lamb, it’s also worth trying the chicken stew with potato and chilli, as well as the Ketik yoghurt drink. The dining room still features the map of the Silk Road on a stretched canvas.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3334818886	Shek Kee Kitchen	15-17 Ngan Mok Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Cantonese	3.0	$$	f	t	During the day, this cosy joint in the heart of the city serves light meals and fried noodles. At night, the menu specialises in home-style Cantonese dishes. The owner-chef Mr Shek sources the freshest ingredients from wet markets daily and regulars also call him directly to pre-order certain dishes, such as fried chicken with toasted garlic which needs a day’s notice. The pan-fried hand-minced cuttlefish patties are springy and flavourful.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3339193870	Tai Woo	9F	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Wheelchair access	https://taiwoorestaurant.com	Nessun premio	Cantonese	4.0	$$	f	f	One of the district’s most famous names, Tai Woo opened its door in the 80s and moved to this address in 2011 and, while the restaurant may be smaller than before, business is better than ever, with over 1,000 customers served every day. What hasn’t changed is the quality of the cooking – along with a menu of wallet friendly Cantonese seafood dishes, such as fish fried rice with ginger, are favourites like sesame chicken baked in salt.	valentinicolas	\N	\N
3337414201	Ah Chun Shandong Dumpling	60 Lai Chi Kok Road	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Dumplings	4.0	$	t	t	The shop has a traditional feel to it. Green wooden window frames on the wall are reminiscent of old-time Hong Kong. Dumplings are handmade daily and only the freshest ingredients are used in the fillings. Try their most-ordered item lamb and Peking scallion dumplings. Or surprise yourself with the specialty, such as mackerel dumplings and cuttlefish dumplings. Shandong roast lamb and meat pie are also recommended.	salajakub	\N	\N
3333498438	Wang Fu	168 Wellington Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Dumplings	4.0	$	t	t	Wang Fu is famous for its Pekingese dumplings – among the great variety of handmade dumplings on the menu, the green onion mutton one stands out most. Apart from dumpling soups, it also serves fried dumplings with light charred crispy skin and juicy fillings. Try also the tomato and egg dumpling, only available after 2 pm. If you fancy more variety, check out their noodles and cold appetisers as well, or ask about the daily special.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3333089034	Putien (Causeway Bay)	Shop A	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.putien.com	Nessun premio	Fujian	4.0	$$	f	t	The original restaurant was founded in Singapore in 2000 and named after a coastal city in Fujian province – the owner’s hometown. This branch comes with an easy-going atmosphere and its Fujian cuisine is respectful of tradition, with a focus on natural flavours. New items are added to the menu from time to time. Don’t miss their themed offerings that feature a particular seasonal seafood, such as razor clams or oysters.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3339984676	Little Napoli	GF	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning	https://www.littlenapolihk.com	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	$$	f	f	True to the chef’s hometown traditions, classic Neapolitan pizzas and street foods like ripieno fritto and panuozzo are made with only ingredients from Naples. Pizzas such as Margherita or Vesuviana are made to order, baked in an Italian stone oven at 400°C, and served whole, not sliced, boasting a puffy, nicely charred crust and gooey centre. It’s basically a grab-and-go pizzeria with a few seats, so come early if you want to dine in.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3335000444	Eng Kee Noodle Shop	GF	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	$	f	f	This family-run shop is always jam-packed with hungry locals craving Cantonese noodle soup. No matter for dine-in or take-out, expect a reasonable wait. It prides itself on its signature beef brisket – braised one night ahead and steeped in a spiced marinade overnight for silky tenderness and deep flavours. Their oven-grilled char siu is made with pork shoulder and pork neck and has a juicy, springy texture thanks to the fine marbling.	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3331566305	Kau Kee	21 Gough Street	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	$	t	t	Kau Kee has been trading since the 1930s and has consequently built up such a huge following that you’ll probably have to line up in the street first to eat here. It’s all very basic and you’ll have to share your table but the food is delicious. Beef noodles are the speciality^ different cuts of meat with a variety of noodles in a tasty broth or spicy sauce. Try the milk tea too.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3332839053	Sai Kwan Lo Jo	Shop B	Hong Kong SAR China	Hong Kong		http://www.saikwanlojo.com	Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	$	f	t	This takeout-only shop carries both traditional and novelty snacks. Try hand-made lai fun noodles in Sai Kwan style, deep-fried sticky rice dumpling with Iberico pork, or stir-fried turnip cake with XO chilli sauce.	grimaldimorko	\N	\N
3336779466	Sparhelt	Szent István tér 7	Hungary	Balatonfüred	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://sparheltbistro.hu/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Head away from the lakeside to seek out this honest all-day bistro with a smart modern interior and a popular terrace. Dishes have a Hungarian heart and perfectly reflect the seasons, with the likes of chilled fruit soups in summer and hearty, warming dishes in winter. Meat-lovers should order the mangalitsa Wellington if they see it on the menu, while fish fanatics should come on Fridays for the special seafood menu. They offer wines from around the world, but don't pass up the opportunity to try some of the superb local Lake Balaton options.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3338426898	Kistücsök	Bajcsy-Zsilinszky utca 25	Hungary	Balatonszemes	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace	https://kistucsok.hu/	Nessun premio	Hungarian	5.0	€€	t	t	A short walk from the southern shores of Lake Balaton, Kistücsök is part of a small hotel which comes complete with its own swimming pool. Well-regarded locally, the restaurant is known for its consistently good interpretations of classic Hungarian dishes, which have been modernised both in their composition and their look. Flavours are fresh, with the occasional global influence, and prices are reasonable. The ‘Taste of the Region’ menu with wine pairings is always a great choice, and the floating island dessert has become something of a speciality.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3338077574	Casa Christa	Izabella utca 1	Hungary	Balatonszőlős	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.casachrista.hu/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	Roads fringed by almond trees and terraced vines lead to this stunning hillside spot with far-reaching views over Lake Balaton. It’s a restful place and comes with seven restored wine press houses which now play host to designer bedrooms with private saunas. Within the grounds sits this beautiful whitewashed restaurant with a simple bistro-cum-farmhouse style and a lovely terrace affording stunning views out over the vines towards Lake Balaton in the distance. The generous cooking has an equally Mediterranean feel, with bright colours and bold, contrasting flavours.	santoronicola	\N	\N
3335312141	Goli	Arany János Utca 32	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.goli.hu	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	5.0	€€	t	t	Set within the former Goldberger textile factory, Goli refers to the nickname the locals gave to this historic building. It’s a small place with a simple terrace and a colourful, cramped interior, but it’s gloriously friendly and positive vibes simply pour out of the kitchen. Sit at the counter to talk with the chefs, who are eager to guide you through the menu of fresh, tasty Middle Eastern favourites, from warm pita, vibrant salads, and green beans with chilli and lemon, to charred entrecôte with tahini. Deliciously fruity soft drinks and cocktails complete your meal.	mancinialberto	\N	\N
3335989090	N28 Wine and Kitchen	Nagymező utca 28	Hungary	Budapest	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://n28.hu/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	You’ll be greeted as if you’re a regular diner here, even on your first visit, which immediately sets a cheerful tone. The welcoming team come, in part, from the Bock Bistzró stable – and they know how to look after their guests. The surroundings might be modern, but there’s a traditional element to the menu, which looks to the Hungarian larder for its base. Expect seasonally changing dishes such as a tasty vichyssoise soup, followed by juicy wild boar and then a delicious poppy seed cake. 95% of the wines are Hungarian, and everything comes at a great price.	naldinadia	\N	\N
3337493909	Macok	Tinódi Sebestyén tér 4	Hungary	Eger	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.imolaudvarhaz.hu/macok-bisztro-borbar.html	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Set on a cobbled street in the Old Town, alongside the castle walls, this bright, colourful bistro is known by food-lovers across the country – and it certainly deserves its reputation. It’s family-owned and professionally run by a friendly team, and the menu is an appealing mix of colourful Hungarian and Mediterranean dishes. While classic flavours are in abundance, presentation is decidedly modern^ the wild boar soup is not to be missed, as is the beef cheek goulash. As well as a wine shop, they also have bedrooms, and in summer you can sit in the courtyard beside the working water wheel.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3338112202	Anyukám Mondta	Petőfi utca 57	Hungary	Encs	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.anyukammondta.hu/	Nessun premio	Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Anyukám Mondta is everything a good neighbourhood restaurant should be. It offers something to appeal to everyone, while prices cover a wide range to suit all occasions. Excellent produce is prepared with care, resulting in hearty, flavoursome dishes, and service is smooth, well-paced and comes with plenty of personality. Choose from homemade pizzas, refined modern Italian dishes and tempting daily specials – where you might find some Middle Eastern flavours too. The focaccia cooked in the wood-fired oven is a must.	amicowilliam	\N	\N
3336431032	Iszkor	Lillafüredi u. 245/5	Hungary	Mályinka	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://www.iszkor.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	A heartening success story, Iszkor sits in the small village of Mályinka in the Bükk Mountains. A former pub, it’s now a neighbourhood restaurant run by Adam and Luca, and is located in Adam’s home village. It couldn’t be a bigger part of the community: the locals grow produce for them^ they host live music and cinema nights^ and they even have their own ice cream parlour. The generously proportioned, country-style dishes change with the seasons and use every part of the ingredient. In summer, sit on the decked terrace^ in winter, cosy up beside the fire.	ferrettivladislav	\N	\N
3338898392	Morzsa	Király utca 42	Hungary	Pécs	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://thisismorzsa.hu/	Nessun premio	Contemporary, Hungarian	3.0	€	t	t	‘Crumbs’ is a new wave bakery-cum-bistro with a relaxed urban style, owned by a charismatic and exuberant designer. Sit inside to watch the making of the delicious loaves and pastries or head out to the terrace for some people-watching in the part-pedestrianised lane. Modern, flavour-packed small plates are served throughout the day and can be accompanied by something from the biodynamic wine list. Of course, a pastry is a must to finish – the lemon meringue cruffin is a hit.	nerielijah	\N	\N
3337792445	Újváros Bisztró	Arborétum utca 2.	Hungary	Szarvas	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace	https://ujvaros-bisztro.hu/	Nessun premio	Hungarian	5.0	€€	t	t	If you’re in eastern Hungary, it’s worth heading over to this ultra-modern restaurant on the banks of the Holt-Körös River. It occupies a space on the ground floor of a modern office building and is accessed via steps that lead to the river path, where you’ll also find the charming terrace with views of Bolza Castle. The menu showcases refined Hungarian dishes presented in a modern style, with catfish a feature, as well as steaks from Hungary, Uruguay and Australia (Wagyu). The interesting selection of Hungarian wines is arranged by region.	bassioleg	\N	\N
3337263275	Platán Bisztró	Kastély Tér 6	Hungary	Tata	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://platanbisztro.hu/	Nessun premio	Hungarian	5.0	€€	t	f	Part of the Platán complex – which also includes a hotel and spa – this charming bistro sits within the same historic castle outbuilding as Two Michelin Starred Platán Gourmet. It has a pleasingly relaxed, contemporary style, and in the corner is a small shop selling desserts and ice cream. In summer you can dine beneath the branches of a 230-year-old plane tree on a charming stepped terrace which borders the lake. The concise menu sees robust Hungarian dishes given a refined bistro-style makeover while still staying true to their roots. Service is fittingly warm and chatty.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3331694564	Thyme	Custume Place	Ireland	Athlone	Air conditioning	https://www.thymerestaurant.ie	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The chef-owner here is one who’s constantly reinvesting in his beloved restaurant and is always on the search for great new local suppliers – whether that’s fresh vegetables or free-range pork – and the pride he has in his establishment is palpable. The two menus showcase the locality well, with dishes that are satisfying and flavoursome. Do try the cheeses, which are accompanied by homemade crackers made using grains from the brewery next door.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3336866764	Cush	by the Pier	Ireland	Ballycotton	Great view,Wheelchair access	https://cush.ie	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Seafood	5.0	€€	f	t	Family owned and run, Cush is a cosy, traditional pub with a smart, modern restaurant, comfy bedrooms and views out over the rooftops to the fishing boats in the harbour. Local produce features in hearty dishes, with seafood naturally to the fore, and guests are well looked after by the friendly team. A set menu is available in the pub area, with an à la carte and tasting menu on offer in the restaurant.	basileryan	\N	\N
3331555800	Courthouse	1 Monaghan Street	Ireland	Carrickmacross	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://www.courthouserestaurant.ie/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	Relaxed, rustic restaurant featuring wooden floors, exposed ceiling rafters and bare brick^ ask for table 20, by the window. Great value menus offer carefully prepared, flavourful dishes which are a lesson in self-restraint – their simplicity being a key part of their appeal. Friendly, efficient service.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3331385418	Sha-Roe Bistro	Main Street	Ireland	Clonegall		https://sha-roe.ie/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	A welcoming 17C former coaching inn set in a picturesque village^ it’s a simple place with a relaxed, intimate feel and candlelit tables in the evenings. Menus offer carefully presented, unfussy dishes with clear flavours and a classical base. Sourcing of local and farmers’ market ingredients is paramount.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3333701065	Ichigo Ichie Bistro & Natural Wine	5 Fenns Quay	Ireland	Cork	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://ichigoichie.ie	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	€€	t	t	Don’t be fooled by the unassuming, mirror-glazed façade^ once you enter this popular Japanese bistro, you’ll be greeted by the almighty buzz of many contented diners. A relaxed, lively reimagining of the former Ichigo Ichie, the emphasis here is on fairly priced, unfussy dishes that use quality produce. You mustn’t leave without trying the matcha panna cotta with lychee ice cream, or sampling one of their carefully sourced natural wines. The friendly, well-orchestrated service team enhance the experience.	ozmax	\N	\N
3331279310	Goldie	128 Oliver Plunkett Street	Ireland	Cork	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://goldie.ie/	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	t	f	A lively, on-trend seafood bistro with an open kitchen and a stripped-back feel^ the tight-knit team offer friendly service and the feel is relaxed and informal. The daily menu offers well-priced, modern dishes which use a ‘gill-to-fin’ approach, making use of the whole catch from the smaller day boats.	sorrentinosantiago	\N	\N
3336999060	Solas	Unit 1	Ireland	Dingle		https://www.solastapas.com/	Nessun premio	Spanish	5.0	€€	t	t	Located in a charming seaside village, Solas is the home of a harmonious marriage between Irish produce and Spanish cooking. Larger-than-life Chef-Owner Nicky Foley’s travels in Spain inform the menu, which offers a range of dishes true to the Spanish originals whilst incorporating local ingredients and adding a few subtle twists. There’s a pleasing simplicity here, to both the good value food and the rustic décor, which combine well with the friendly, welcoming service.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3336314928	Pichet	14-15 Trinity Street	Ireland	Dublin City	Air conditioning	https://pichet.ie/	Nessun premio	French	4.0	€€	t	f	You can’t miss the neon red signs and striped canopies of this buzzy brasserie – and its checkerboard flooring makes the inside equally striking. Sit in one of two rooms, soaking up the buzz of either the bar or the kitchen as you enjoy a menu rooted in French classics. The likes of tartare, pithivier and tarte Tatin might well appear, despite the odd foray further afield and a commitment to Irish produce throughout. The wine list stretches well beyond France’s borders, with many wines available to order by the glass or, more appropriately, by the pichet.	beloveva	\N	\N
3332727783	Uno Mas	6 Aungier Street	Ireland	Dublin City	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://www.unomas.ie/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	The best seats in the house are at the counter in this buzzing, good value restaurant run by enthusiastic, personable staff. Start with some Spanish-inspired nibbles from the ‘para picar’ section before choosing one of the well-executed, unfussy main dishes which come with many layers of flavour and texture. A dedicated sherry list and a vermouth-based cocktail selection offer appealing additions to your visit.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3338192772	Lottie's	7-9 Rathgar Road	Ireland	Dublin City	Counter dining	https://lotties.ie	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	There’s a terrific buzz in the air at this stylish brasserie-style restaurant, where the unfussy cooking is a fine accompaniment to the lively surroundings. Irish produce is the bedrock of the menu, in hearty, flavour-packed dishes like Andarl Farm pork chop with cabbage & violet mustard, parsnip and a cider jus. The early evening menu is a steal and an extensive choice of cocktails are on hand to kick things off.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3334871929	Richmond	43 Richmond Street South	Ireland	Dublin City		https://richmondrestaurant.ie/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	The owner and his team bend over backwards to make sure you have a great time at this welcomingly worn, rustic shop conversion just outside the city centre. Skilfully prepared, traditionally based dishes are robust yet refined and allow each core seasonal ingredient to shine.	baranovrachel	\N	\N
3332637836	Bistro Cerisier	1-3 Tanaka Shimoyanagicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://bistrocerisier.studio.site/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥	f	t	French ballads warble through a retro interior, recalling the good old days. Regional cuisines such as quenelles from Lyon and cassoulet from Languedoc spill across the menu. Old-school recipes, like white asparagus with Hollandaise sauce in spring and salmis of roast mallard, bring comfort to the soul. Respect for sauces testifies to the commitment to the essence of French cooking.	popafarah	\N	\N
3335619789	Amy Austin	Unit 1	Ireland	Dublin City	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://amyaustin.ie	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences	4.0	€€	t	t	There is a palpable buzz to the atmosphere as soon as you set foot in this quirky restaurant in a lively area of the city. It’s not just the wine on tap that makes this such a popular spot – although it must help – but the superior small plates that offer detailed, precise cooking for a reasonable price tag. Grab a stool at one of the high-top tables, or perhaps in front of the open kitchen, to enjoy globally influenced dishes like scallop crudo and Moroccan-style lamb rump. Friendly service and signature cocktails help to keep the good vibes flowing.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3337486597	La Gordita	6 Montague Street	Ireland	Dublin City	Counter dining	https://lagordita.ie	Nessun premio	Spanish	3.0	€€	t	t	There’s a simple, cosy quality to La Gordita thanks to its narrow dining room with a wooden floor, brown leather upholstery and soft lighting. It’s got a lively atmosphere too, a great accompaniment to the authentic Spanish sharing plates that pack in plenty of flavour – the terrific anchoas de Santoña is a real stand-out dish. Friendly service enhances the experience, and the extensive menu lets you sample as much as possible thanks to the sensible pricing.	de santistobias	\N	\N
3337597767	Spitalfields	25 The Coombe	Ireland	Dublin City	Counter dining,Wheelchair access	https://www.spitalfields.ie	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Set in a historic area of this city is this fittingly traditional-looking Irish pub, where the charming staff offer a warm and friendly welcome. It’s deservedly busy – drinkers are welcome but most are here for the food. Enticing dishes are fresh, flavoursome and great value, with the likes of oxtail and bone marrow Parker House rolls.	bianchiandrea	\N	\N
3336823373	Aldridge Lodge	Aldridge Lodge	Ireland	Duncannon	Car park,Garden or park,Terrace	https://www.aldridgelodge.com	Nessun premio	Country cooking	3.0	€€	t	t	It's no wonder this place is so popular: it's in a beautiful rural location^ the cooking offers great value for money^ and the cheery owners run their restaurant with an infectious bonhomie. Situated inside an attractive house down a little country lane, there are surrounding gardens which provide vegetables for many of the dishes, while the chef's father fishes off Hook Head and provides much of the produce for the seafood-leaning menu – crab and lobster are a particular feature. Homely bedrooms come with hot water bottles and home-baked cookies.	montanarijack	\N	\N
3339308883	Table Forty One	41 Main Street	Ireland	Gorey		https://www.tablefortyone.ie/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	Having worked in various hotels and restaurants around the world, Gorey native Andrew Duncan returned home to open this friendly restaurant situated in the busy town centre. Diners are spread across two rooms, both boasting a wonderfully cosy vibe and welcoming atmosphere. There’s a generosity to the cooking, both in portion size and price, with good produce from County Wexford underpinning the menu – desserts are a strength of the kitchen too.	schulzchiara	\N	\N
3339207189	Saint Francis Provisions	Short Quay	Ireland	Kinsale	Counter dining,Terrace	https://saintfrancisprovisions.squarespace.com/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	f	This endearing, laid-back restaurant holds just 13 seats inside, with a heated terrace out front. The concise, daily changing menu offers a range of Mediterranean-inspired small plates created from the best local ingredients. Dishes are delivered from the open kitchen as and when they are ready, and offer punchy flavours and an appealing simplicity. An all natural wine list completes the picture.	testagabriel	\N	\N
3338134145	Everett's	22 High Street	Ireland	Waterford	Air conditioning	https://www.everetts.ie/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	This proudly run, welcoming bistro is set in the heart of the city and dates from the 15C^ sit on the ground floor with its barrel-fronted bar or in the intimate vaulted brick cellar. Modern menus showcase the best of the Irish larder and generously-sized dishes are assured, refined and full of flavour.	bianconathan	\N	\N
3330499126	Akihana	27 Ichijoji Hinokuchicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch		Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	¥¥	f	t	To revisit the basics after studying creative Chinese cooking, the chef adds polish to a selection of Chinese regional cuisines. Sichuan items dominate, including steamed chicken with spicy sauce, twice-cooked pork and shrimp in chili sauce. The signature mapo tofu is a true original, made with wagyu beef sinew instead of ground meat. Faithful to his Shizuoka roots, he prepares his XO sauce fried rice with stardust shrimps and dried fish fry to create a mutual understanding between the cuisines of Kyoto and the Suruga region.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3334384709	Canton Shunsai Ikki	17-5 Tsukimicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥¥	f	t	The restaurant holds its own niche in Chinese cuisine. The talents of the Guangdong-trained chef are on full display. Guangdong is blessed with the bounty of sea, mountain and river, as is Kyoto, and the light flavour of its cuisine, which draws out the flavour of the ingredients, work well with the food culture of the ancient capital. Shrimp wontons are dressed with Hong Kong soy sauce, Cantonese fried rice is accented with lettuce and roast pork.	calincolin	\N	\N
3330062381	Taiho	149 Nishinokyo Hoshigaikecho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Chinese	5.0	¥	f	f	This Chinese restaurant is run by a family, who all support each other. The father’s offerings, which have pleased the locals for generations, sit side-by-side with authentic Szechuan cuisine from the son’s gastronomic studies. One dish for which Taiho has been renowned since its opening is the ‘Teridon Kinshi’. This quintessentially Kyoto dish consists of rice topped with pork and kinshi tamago (ribbons of omelette). Also recommended is the ‘Yodaredori’, steamed chicken with a spicy sauce.	hofmannelena	\N	\N
3336791776	YI PAN CAI TANAKA	26 Tanaka Satonochicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining	https://yipan-cai-tanaka.x0.com/	Nessun premio	Chinese	3.0	¥¥	t	f	‘Yi Pan Cai’ is Mandarin Chinese for ‘à la carte’. The name reflects the restaurant’s desire for patrons to enjoy dishes they love with a light-hearted spirit. The ‘Dragon’s-Hair Rolls’ are minced shrimp and hamo rolled up in kadaif noodles and deep-fried. Dishes such as pig’s feet marinated in Tsingtao beer and deep-fried^ and shumai steamed dumplings made variously of pork, beef, fish or shellfish, are creatively prepared and served as an assortment. Each dish is delightfully inventive.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3337038647	Asperge Blanche	313-2 Yokosuwancho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://www.aspergeblanche.com/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥	t	f	White is the keynote colour of the antiques-accented interior. The restaurant is decorated with sundries collected at flea markets, while a pendant light wreathes the establishment in its warm glow. The chef prepares traditional cuisine, arrangements stripped to the essentials so the flavours of the ingredients themselves shine clearly. Enamoured of Bincho charcoal, the chef even bakes his bread with it. The name of the restaurant means ‘white asparagus’—no need to ask what their spring speciality is…	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3335287847	DEUX FILLES	199-2 Ayazaimokucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥	f	t	Owner-chef Daisuke Iwata bills his fare as ‘modern French’. His purpose in using generous portions of vegetables is to showcase the bounty of Kyoto. The salad with 30 kinds of vegetables is a perennial favourite. Selecting a white plate as a canvas, he colours it in with vegetables he buys himself in places such as Kameoka and Kamigamo. His skill in déclinaison – taking a single ingredient and turning it into sauté, sauce and powder, then serving it as a single dish – is unique.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3331057940	HUNTER	533-2 Tsuboyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	French	4.0	¥¥	f	t	Chef Imai is as obsessed with meat as a hunter stalking his game. Putting his experience with French cuisine to work, he grills his meat-centric menu on a charcoal grill. In addition to duck, pork and beef, in autumn and winter Imai serves game meats such as boar and deer. Charcuterie such as pâté and rillettes are arranged on plates that look like stumps for a natural look. If you sit at the counter, you’ll have the pleasure of chatting with this personable chef.	carlinikita	\N	\N
3330897754	La pleine lune	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining,Interesting wine list	https://la-pleine-lune.com/	Nessun premio	French	5.0	¥¥	t	f	Chef Naoaki Nishii brings ingredients to life using traditional cuisine. One example is the thick-cut smoked salmon, paired with chestnuts in autumn and turnips in winter to emphasise the seasonal feeling. Meat dishes are garnished with kuro shichimi (‘seven black spices’) to add a Kyoto touch. In homage to classic French cooking, he does not spare the sauce, taking care to impart a modern flavouring. Butter and cream are used sparingly for a lighter taste.	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3338835943	BOCCA del VINO	138-9 Saitocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	¥¥	t	f	The quirky name, ‘mouth of wine’, reflects the chef’s fond memories of Italy, where jugs of wine graced every dinner table. The chef studied in the southern Italy, so recipes are simple, prepared with lashings of tomatoes and olive oil. Seafood features prominently in appetisers, meat and poultry in main dishes, based on the chef’s experiences. Pasta is dressed with the familiar oil, tomatoes and ragu. Comfort food that brings to mind daily life in Italy.	gavrilovnora	\N	\N
3332085151	Lapintaika	499 Kitamonzencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Italian	5.0	¥¥	f	f	The menu is broad, reflecting the wide range of local Italian cooking styles the chef has studied. Each plate feeds two, so sharing is the order of the day. The assorted appetiser, generous in both portion and variety, is a perennial favourite. A full complement of pasta dishes is on offer—the list of spaghettis alone is extensive. The restaurant’s name means ‘coming back’, and indeed the satisfying weekend lunch draws plenty of repeat visitors.	caputostefan	\N	\N
3337154295	Berangkat	334 Maruyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	5.0	¥¥	f	t	Berangkat means ‘beginnings’ in Indonesian, apt for a restaurant serving creative interpretations of cuisine the owner-chef studied in Southeast Asia. Consider, for example, shiraae dressed with coriander, pidan and Szechuan pickles, drizzled with homemade chilli oil. The grilled meat in cinnamon soy sauce borrows from the fare of the street stalls of Vietnam. The Okinawa cuisine, from the owner-chef’s experiences on Ishigakijima Island, is another of the restaurant’s fortes.	haascamilla	\N	\N
3339957194	Eitaroya	448 Tatsunoikecho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	4.0	¥¥	f	f	Seafood rushed straight from the fisheries and vegetables grown by local farmers are what sell this izakaya. The white-smocked chef stands at the counter, showing confidence in his daily-changing menu. Choose how you want your seafood prepared: stewed, salt-grilled, deep-fried as tempura, and more. The sashimi plate is popular for its variety and generous portions. Sashimi is served atop a big bowl of ice, keeping the fish cool in summer and firm in winter.	vecchiatomichael	\N	\N
3331035336	Muromachi Kaji	185 Nakanonocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥	t	f	This kappo izakaya heaves with customers night after night. Sashimi combinations are arranged as for kaiseki traditional multi-course meals. The inclusion of chub mackerel sushi is gratifying. Potatoes are paired with delicacies to conjure a potato salad for grownups that goes well with sake. Plovers emblazoned on the shop curtain and towels are for good luck, representing the overcoming of rough seas. The staff work as a tight-knit crew to surmount the waves of orders the shop’s popularity brings them.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3333870611	Saketosakana DNA	559-1 Torocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.saketosakanadna.com/	Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥	t	t	‘DNA’ was appended to the name to evoke the richness of Japanese cuisine and the spirit of Japan as defining features of the restaurant. There’s a reason why the soup using kombu kelp and bonito dashi stock takes pride of place. Fish is shipped directly from Obama, Fukui Prefecture, so there’s a good selection of sake from Fukui, too. Foodstuffs and sake from the same locale tend to get on well together—there’s that DNA again. The warmth of the three family members is a genetic inheritance from father to son and daughter.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3335421188	Sambongi Shoten	478 Shincho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list		Nessun premio	Izakaya	3.0	¥¥	f	f	Char-grilled meats are the signature fare here. Sambongi Shoten bills itself as an izakaya, but the atmosphere is more like a char-grill bar. The focus is on wine being organic, sake being warm. The menu is remarkably varied, with many creations borrowing ideas from Japanese, Western and Chinese influences. Meats include beef, pork, mutton and duck, as well as game^ the Miyama venison is a crowd-pleaser. The trained eye of a butcher and the flame control of a master of French cooking are on display here.	k�nigsara	\N	\N
3331063822	Choshoku Kishin	555 Komatsucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.kishin.world/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥	t	f	Breakfast is the only meal served here^ rice dishes with soup. Rice is served from the first plume of steam, before it is fully cooked. Choshoku Kishin weaves together the format of tea ceremony cuisine. Guests choose a rice bowl, then select from an assortment of soups. Rice is doled out little by little, so you can experience the change in flavour as steaming progresses. Accompaniments include whole dried round herring and pickled veg. This is the spot for a delightful breakfast with gracious service. Reservations required.	habiliragip	\N	\N
3334079939	KOBUSHI Ramen	1-16 Sujaku Shokaicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Ramen	4.0	¥	t	t	The owner-chef created his menu by trial and error, driven by the search for ingredients that are quintessentially Kyoto. Turning his eye to locally raised duck, he conceived his renowned ‘Kyoto Duck and Dried Nodoguro Soba’. The soup is prepared with dashi of duck bones and tai heads and enriched with dashi of venison bones^ the garnish of Kujo green onions is a consummate Kyoto touch. Those who lean toward lighter flavours should try the ‘Rausu kombu Kake Soba’.	valentimatteo	\N	\N
3330042597	Ichihana	264-1 Nijo Aburanokojicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://nijo-ichihana.com/	Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥	t	t	A typical lunch offering is sashimi and items served in small bowls, while the evening lineup boasts a full complement of sashimi and items served in rice and cooked individually for each guest. Ten ingredients are always available, with gomoku (‘five ingredients’) and wild plants being perennial favourites. To express the seasons through kamameshi, Ichihana offers flavours like bamboo shoots, sweetfish, mushrooms and oysters. While the rice is cooking, enjoy Kyoto flavours such as steamed wheat gluten with sweet miso sauce and steamed tilefish.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3334584795	Ikkon Uehara	232-9 Kamigoryokamiecho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥	t	t	At lunchtime, only omakase set menus are offered^ in the evening, à la carte dishes are also served. Ikkon Uehara aims to cater to a regular clientele, so the menu is comprehensive and the cuisine lovingly prepared. An assorted platter loaded with appetisers show that the old ways are not forgotten. A wooden bowl of fishcake steeped in a clear broth is classic comfort food. The counter is a horigotatsu^ behind the counter, the couple in charge deliver cheerful and gracious service. Tip a cup or two of sake and feel the seasons change.	leonoscar	\N	\N
3338753184	Kikunoi Mugesambo	524 Washiocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://kikunoi.jp/kikunoiweb/Top/index	Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥	f	f	The menu of tea ceremony food conveys the flavours of Kikunoi with the culture of bento. Starting with appetisers, stewed bowls are served ryotei-style. Serving-ware—baskets, lacquer, glasses—changes with the passing seasons, laden with a colourful variety of grilled items and simmered vegetables. The house speciality, Shiguremeshi, is topped with sea bream sashimi smothered in sesame sauce. As you dine, cast your gaze over the stillness of the moss-covered garden.	serrakevin	\N	\N
3331462785	Shichiku Kiko	16 Shichiku Shimotakedonocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	4.0	¥¥	f	t	The tiled-roof row house on Gen’i-dori makes an immediate impression. The owner-chef, wearing a bow tie, rushes about, unable to rest unless he does everything himself. With his wealth of experience, he takes familiar ingredients and raises them to new levels, creating graceful Kyoto cuisine – and it’s good value for money. Appetiser platters are served with rice at lunchtime and in the evening with drinks. The gentle demeanour of the proprietress makes you feel at home.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3330683828	Tan	106-13 Gokencho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://tan.kyoto.jp/	Nessun premio	Japanese	5.0	¥¥	t	f	‘Tan’ comes from the city of Kyotango in Kyoto Prefecture. Naturally, the food hails from the Tango region too: rice grown by employees where the restaurant was founded^ vegetables from the region’s farmers. Service begins with breakfast loaded with vegetables^ lunch consists of bowls of rice with toppings and noodle dishes^ evening fare is à la carte. Each dish is simple yet prepared and plated creatively. The view of the willows along the Shirakawa River seen from the modern interior is wonderfully elegant.	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3332119457	Washoku Haru	230-2 Shimmeicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥	t	t	The blackboard menu is inscribed with familiar Japanese comfort foods such as braised and seasoned burdock root, sukiyaki and fried minced meat cake. Potato salad is not mashed but entwined with cream^ steamed wheat-gluten, wrapped in seaweed and fried, is pleasingly buttery^ and mackerel sushi is served rolled and wrapped in seaweed. The owner-chef fine-tunes his dishes, making every dish fascinating. Oden stew is a fun treat in winter, thanks to his experience in the art of simmering. Stir-fried noodles and ramen are tempting choices as well.	havelisabella	\N	\N
3338849939	Kushi Tanaka	310-10 Uradeyamacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Kushiage	5.0	¥¥	t	t	A tight C-shaped counter surrounds the owner-chef. Imaginatively prepared skewers appear in rapid succession and the variety is extraordinary: mushrooms with soy butter, steamed wheat gluten with yuzu miso, bread filled with cream cheese. The prix fixe offering is called ‘Ippo Tsuko’, meaning ‘one way’, as skewers are placed in front of guests with no consultation. The owner-chef never forgets to show modesty and humour.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3332886689	Oryori Menami	96 Nakajimacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.menami.jp/	Nessun premio	Obanzai	4.0	¥¥	t	t	This restaurant began as a place serving obanzai and yakitori, and the sauce that the chicken and green onion skewer is grilled in goes all the way back to then. Kyoto culinary delights line the counter, such as a stew of deep-fried tofu and leafy vegetables, Kujo leek dressed in vinegar miso and boiled nama-yuba. Here you can linger and relax to the gracious hospitality of the tunic-clad proprietress, who keeps her grandmother’s name alive in the name of the restaurant.	venturaroman	\N	\N
3338544305	Fuyacho 103	225 Owaricho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Oden	5.0	¥¥	t	t	The name is simply the address of this restaurant hidden in a mixed-use complex. Cross the threshold and the interior is filled with the warmth of wood panelling, the coffered ceiling reminiscent of the partitions in an oden pot. The menu ranges from standard fare such as daikon radish and deep-fried tofu to more exotic choices only a former Italian cuisine chef could conjure, such as caciocavallo cheese. Taking a hint from bistecca, the steak is paired with oden dashi soup stock.	ivanovsophia	\N	\N
3332361416	Oito	253 Giommachi Kitagawa	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Oden	4.0	¥¥	f	f	The building, in the style of a townhouse, stands on Kiritoshi Alley in Gion. Portraits of maiko adorn the walls, reinforcing the geisha-district ambience. ‘Lunch Oden’ is the only item on the menu. The owner-chef is mindful of retaining familiar and comforting flavours. Lunch consists of five items of the diner’s choice, accompanied by takikomi-gohan. The choice of oden is up to the customer, but if you choose the popular beef tendon, we recommend pairing it with the tofu or konnyaku.	barbierisalvatore	\N	\N
3332005029	Chinese Noodles ROKU	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Ramen	5.0	¥	t	f	Ramen, soup and other Chinese foods are the soul of this ramen shop by Velrosier. The chef draws soup stock from bones of duck, chicken, venison and pork. Clear soup owes its depth to umami from a medley of dried foods^ dried longan fruit, a Chinese medicinal herb, is a touch only a gourmet of Chinese cuisine would think of. The manifold layers of flavour derive from Roku’s ‘add-on’ approach to seasoning.	paganialex	\N	\N
3337788104	Mendokoro Janomeya	2F	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Ramen	4.0	¥	t	f	This ramen shop focuses on making soup using locally raised chickens. Its three signature flavours are soy sauce, salt and white broth. Be sure to try the chicken ramen. To make the signature soup, dashi is drawn from chicken bones and whole chickens. Following a time-honoured recipe, flavours are enhanced with soy sauce matured in large wooden barrels. The fragrance of the wheat is drawn out by using thin noodles. The ambience is reminiscent of the aristocratic culture of old Kyoto.	tudoroh	\N	\N
3338591590	Menya Inoichi	542 Ebisunocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://inoichi.stores.jp/	Nessun premio	Ramen	3.0	¥	t	f	From the front of the restaurant comes the tempting aroma of dashi, inviting the diner in. True to their Kyoto roots, they pursue a ramen richly suffused with the flavour of dashi. The broth is from Rausu kombu, a type of kelp rich in umami, and several types of dried seafood. The feature dish is ‘Dashi Soba’. The ramen is served in two varieties: the lightly seasoned ‘white’ and the full-bodied ‘black.’ Freshly shaved katsuo-bushi brings out the umami still further.	mazziandrei	\N	\N
3335424878	Muginoyoake	12-5 Nishishichijo Kakegoshicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Ramen	3.0	¥	f	f	The chef has been researching the deliciousness of ramen since he was a schoolboy. In search of a unique flavour, he made ‘Scallop and Japanese Pepper Ramen’ his signature dish. Soup of dashi drawn from chicken, pork and seafood is multilayered and satisfying. The finished Japanese pepper oil imparts a refreshing feeling, and the generous topping of scallop is pure luxury. A carefully calibrated bowl of goodness that is the gift of repeated independent study.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3339524171	Teuchisoba Kanei	11-1 Murasakino Higashifujinomoricho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Soba	5.0	¥	f	t	The owner-chef fell in love with soba, so taught himself how to make it. Using a stone mill, he grinds his “Rough-ground Soba” by hand to create wonderfully rustic juwari, or 100% buckwheat noodles. A shark skin grater and stick of wasabi are provided, so you can start grating your wasabi while you wait for your soba. Pre-soba snacks created with drinks in mind are on offer, including broiled miso, itawasa and dashimaki tamago. The ambience of the traditional wooden townhouse looking out on the verandah of an inner garden sets the mood.	calincolin	\N	\N
3335634325	Izugen	391 Takeyacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Sushi	4.0	¥	t	f	A Kyoto eatery to drop in often and casually. Izugen is a much-loved tradition from the old days, jealously guarded by its third-generation chef. Rice, the essential base of sushi, is cooked with kombu and bonito. Order the Kyoto sushi mixed platter and savour three styles of sushi: bo sushi with mackerel, hako sushi and maki sushi. Sushi is not hand-formed, so there’s no counter, in true Kyoto style. A picture of a maiko hangs on the wall because, the current chef says, he fell in love with it at first sight^ he believes it is auspicious, as the maiko invites customers to ‘maikomu’, or ‘come in’.	sommerlaura	\N	\N
3331011028	Izuu	367 Kiyomotocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://www.izuu.jp/	Nessun premio	Sushi	5.0	¥	t	f	Founded in 1781, Izuu takes its name from its founder, Izumiya Uhee, from a time when lightly salted mackerel from Wakasa was becoming popular in Kyoto, and the custom of eating sabazushi at festivals and ceremonies became common. Seeing an opportunity, Uhee began delivering these treats to the city’s geisha districts. The business passed from generation to generation, and the current, eighth generation owner-chef preserves the tradition of whole-mackerel sushi to this day.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3338314914	KASHIWAI	3-3 Koyama Shimochikawaracho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	Sushi	4.0	¥	t	t	Founded as an antique store, the shop is still decorated with old pottery. ‘Temarizushi’, little sushi balls served in thin cardboard boxes, are as cute as wagashi confections. Seafood and vegetables for sushi are crafted with great care as well. Sea bream is marinated in kombu, shiitake mushrooms are simmered slowly in dashi. Kyoto food culture is woven into the entire menu, as shown by simmered bamboo shoots served in spring and pickled sliced radishes called ‘senmaizuke’ offered in winter. The restaurant is open from morning onwards^ for dinner seating, reservations are required.	huberflorin	\N	\N
3336915466	Sushizen	41-2 Koromonotanacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Sushi	3.0	¥	t	t	Standing in the kitchen is the second-generation chef and his son. Protecting the reputation of their restaurant as a family, father and son carry the torch for future generations. Guests’ eyes are drawn to the chirashizushi heaped with lashings of seafood. Sushi pieces brushed with sweet eel sauce are smothered in thin omelette cut into strips^ this arrangement is both beautiful and practical, as it prevents the fish from drying. Oshizushi of pike conger and conger eel, futomaki stuffed with dried gourd strips and parsley are standard fare. Here the good things never change.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3330278362	Jukuseibuta Kawamura	57-1 Takehana Nishinoguchicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Tonkatsu	3.0	¥	t	t	The nation’s finest pork brands cascade across the menu, so you can choose the type and grade of pork that suits you best. The best is the ‘jukusei-buta’ aged pork that gives the shop its name. Sourced from a butcher in Fushimi, the pork this restaurant handles is rested to enhance its flavour. The plaque on the wall says, ‘Timing is everything’^ the pork is deep-fried twice in low-temperature oil, the cooking time expertly judged. Pork katsu curry, seasoned with ginger and spices, is also tempting.	calincolin	\N	\N
3336849414	Gion Yorozuya	555-1 Komatsucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Udon	5.0	¥	t	f	When Gion Yorozuya was founded, its focus was on meal deliveries to teahouses and playhouses. The restaurant thrived thanks to a favourable reception from geisha and maiko, and today guests queue up at the door well before opening time. The dish of renown is the onion udon. Eager to use Kyoto foodstuffs, the chef smothers his plates in Kujo spring onion. The three pillars of the cuisine that keeps customers coming back are tender noodles, dashi and onions. “Mari”, a dish larded with pickled plums, and “Tsunoda”, enhanced with chicken meat, are named for the celebrities who favour these ingredients.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3337904475	Kanesho	155-2 Tokiwacho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Unagi / Freshwater Eel	4.0	¥	t	f	The shop was founded at the end of the Edo period as a wholesaler of river fish. Situated at the end of an alley as long and narrow as an eel’s bed, Kanesho is recognisable by the leaping eel emblazoned on its noren. ‘Kinshi-don’, the brainchild of the fourth-generation chef, is renowned. This popular dish incorporates ‘kinshitamago’, omelette cut into thin strips, an essential component of Kyoto favourites such as chirashizushi and steamed sushi. ‘Ochazuke Eel’ is eel simmered in dipping sauce and drenched in green tea, a refreshing flavour. A place where one hopes to gain the vitality of the leaping eel.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3331537926	Kyogoku Kaneyo	456 Matsugaecho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning	https://kyogoku-kaneyo.co.jp/	Nessun premio	Unagi / Freshwater Eel	5.0	¥	f	t	This eel restaurant has been in business for seven generations, dating back to the Meiji period. Every day finds the shop crowded with customers, many seeking its signature dish of ‘Kinshi Don’: rice covered in dipping sauce and topped with Edo-style eel and a large Kyoto-style omelette. What makes this east-west marriage of flavours work so well is the dipping sauce, a staple since the restaurant’s inception. The Kanto-style kabayaki, which involves steaming eel before grilling and dipping it in sauce, is a technique from a cook recruited from Tokyo during the founder’s generation. In both looks and taste, Kyogoku Kaneyo bears traces of Japan’s east and west.	vitolajose	\N	\N
3332000297	Hiiragitei	306-6 Ishibashicho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Counter dining	https://www.hiiragitei.com/	Nessun premio	Yakitori	5.0	¥¥	t	t	It’s a family affair at this restaurant specialising in locally raised chicken and obanzai: the father prepares the à la carte dishes, the son the yakitori, and the mother attends to customers’ needs. Every morning the son visits a poultry farm in Shiga Prefecture to purchase and dress whole chickens by himself. The speciality of the house is the white liver, a rare part of the chicken, and back liver complemented with the bitter flavour of cacao nibs.	caprinivaleria	\N	\N
3338067824	Sumiyakisosaitoriya Hitomi	96 Okikucho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Yakitori	4.0	¥	t	f	Sumiyakisosaitoriya Hitomi is full night after night and the delicious grilled chicken is only one reason for this success. The other is the character of the owner-chef. He stays in guests’ line of sight at all times as he assiduously works the Kishu-binchotan charcoal. He guides his service staff of students with fatherly kindness and makes guests feel like family. The restaurant offers baby chicken, local chicken and brand-name chicken, for their differences in taste and texture. Enjoy devotion and passion in every skewer.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3333223272	KORISU	101 Rokurocho	Japan	Kyoto	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Yoshoku	5.0	¥¥	t	t	A mother and two daughters, in their pure-white smocks, make guests feel at home with their family hospitality. French and other Western dishes are served with generous portions, bringing satisfaction that keeps the restaurant’s reputation strong. Hamburger steak and fried shrimp are flavours from the good old days. Escargot and lamb pair well with wine. With only three tables, and the phone often unanswered, getting a reservation can be a bit of a scramble.	romanosimone	\N	\N
3336199971	Shunsai Chuka Bar Mitsukan	4-4-5 Naizencho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Chinese	4.0	¥	t	f	This Chinese bar appeals with its casual izakaya-like atmosphere and authentic cuisine. The aim is to be a place where people can come to drink, so they are very particular about the local Nara sake and shochu. The chef being an expert in Sichuan cuisine, the specialities are spicy chicken and mapo tofu. He also incorporates local ingredients and culture, such as using brand name pork from Gojo to make steamed dumplings, and using ‘Kasa-soba’, from the Kasa area of Sakurai.	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3330818632	A VOTRE SANTE	6-26 Shinasahigaoka	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	French	3.0	¥¥	f	f	Chef Yaoki Tsujimura says that he wants to communicate the sights he saw in France. He recalls memories from training in southern France in the 1990s. Everything from gougère to bread and small confectionery is freshly baked. Dishes made using a generous amount of butter and garnished with sauce have a nostalgic French aroma to them. When you hear the word ‘santé, it means a fun time is about to begin.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3332389405	le content	1-3-8 Ayameike Minami	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	French	4.0	¥¥	t	f	The restaurant’s name is a play on the French adjective ‘content’, meaning ‘happy’ or ‘satisfied’. It is also a term that the chef’s mentor complimented him with during his apprenticeship. At lunchtime, simple prix fixe are offered, but in the evening diners get à la carte items focused squarely on flavour. Offerings such as pâté de campagne, beef cheek simmered in red wine and tarte Tatin showcase traditional French cooking. Cassoulet de Toulouse captures a flavour that etched itself on the chef’s memory.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3339624809	Simple comme Bonjour	68-3 Kawaharajocho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	French	5.0	¥¥	t	t	Kotaro Kawaguchi chose the path of French cuisine, following in the footsteps of his father, who was a cook on a cruise ship. He says that training at Pierre Gagnaire in Paris, a restaurant he had long admired, boosted his morale as a chef. There, he learned the techniques to create harmony between ingredients. There are no standard offerings here, as he is always inspired to offer new creations.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3335617372	Masala an TAKUMI	2281 Nakamachi	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	¥¥	t	t	As a veteran of the Indian culinary world, Chef Takumi Sakanaka is a master spice artisan. His ‘eclectic Japanese, Western and Indian’ fare is born from his Japanese sensibility and experience with French cuisine. The Masala Hassun appetizer is inspired by traditional kaiseki multi-course meals. Pâté de campagne infused with dry curry and handmade Miwa pasta are true to Nara. As the phrase on the shop curtain says, this is ‘nouvelle cuisine of India’.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3330170117	toi Inshokuten	30-3 Hanashibacho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Indian	5.0	¥	t	t	The ‘toi’ in the name of the restaurant is an acronym for ‘trip of imagination’. The destination is India, and the mission is to provide traditional Indian dishes. There are meat, fish and vegetable curries. They do things Thali teishoku-style and serve several kinds of curry of your choice on a large plate. You can also add individual items like pakora, an Indian-style tempura.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3331933922	Shikinoaji Enzu	6-5-14 Omiyacho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed		Nessun premio	Japanese	3.0	¥¥	t	f	The cheerful hospitality of the owner-chef at this kappo will put you at ease. He offers a wide selection of dishes, including tsukuri, tempura and grilled items. He serves several appetisers so you can snack on them while choosing your main dishes. Regular offerings include deep-fried mugwort fu and eggplant with dengaku miso. Although not on the menu, sushi can be prepared if you place an order. The spirit of service he shows makes this a great place to dine.	contimatteo	\N	\N
3334066867	Kushizukushi	31 Yanagimachi	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Kushiage	4.0	¥	t	f	The creative skewers here feature seasonal ingredients and rare ingredients, such as Japanese glass shrimp in the spring, ayu with roe in the autumn and oysters in winter. Items like vegetables pickled in sake lees and goma-dofu give you the full Nara experience. To end comes nyumen that goes down well or dashi chazuke made with rice grown by the owner-chef’s brother. Each item on the set menu is given an extra touch for texture and flavour, making it a truly appealing set meal.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3339942061	Sosakukushinomise Rindo	224-1 Tsujimachi	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Kushiage	5.0	¥¥	f	f	Chef Ueda came up with creative skewers to make use of his experience in both Japanese and Western cuisine. The honekiri-treated hamo requiring very precise cuts is where his Japanese culinary skills shine. The croque monsieur is a French recipe. The menu starts with Western appetisers and incorporates surinagashi, gazpacho and other soups. The free-wheeling culinary ideas on display in the menu have you looking forward to what’s coming.	svobodagreta	\N	\N
3333769823	Pizzeria Luna Nuova	2-1-35 Omiyacho	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Pizza	3.0	¥	f	f	What drew chef Kenji Akai to pizza was its simplicity, being a complete meal in a single dish. He’s passionate about Neapolitan pizza baked in a firewood oven and uses Italian wheat for lightness and fragrance in the crust. The popular item on the menu is the D.O.C. Pizza of buffalo mozzarella, dried cherry tomato and basil. His experience in Italian cuisine is also evident in the home-style Italian sausage and chargrilled dishes.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3337618259	PIZZERIA TRATTORIA MAGAZZINO	172-1 Kamada	Japan	Nara	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only - lunch	https://magazzino.co.jp/	Nessun premio	Pizza	4.0	¥	f	f	The pizza here is prepared true to how it’s done in Naples, with chef Hironori Noda reproducing those authentic flavours. What Naples has that Nara doesn’t is an ocean so, in response, he came up with the idea of a restaurant that’s all about the fields. He grows the vegetables himself and makes them the main ingredients. The garden is his mother’s, and he harvests the vegetables himself, meaning that the bounty of Kashiba proffered here truly springs from ‘Mother Earth’.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3333087879	YAMAOKA PIZZA	455 Onitoricho	Japan	Nara	Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view		Nessun premio	Pizza	5.0	¥	t	f	This restaurant on Mt. Ikomayama overlooks the city. The Italy-trained chef bakes pizzas with his own original take. The key to the taste is Ikoma spring water – the water’s sweetness and softness give the pizza real character. Made using less salt compared to the Italian recipe, the crust has a uniquely fluffy texture. The standard offering is margherita pizza made with vegetables from a local farm. Have your fill of Ikoma pizza you won’t find in Naples or Rome. It’s closed for the month of February.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
