3337900121	Brasserij Kok Verhoeven	NS Plein 32	Netherlands	Tilburg	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	https://www.kokverhoeven.nl/	Nessun premio	Seafood	5.0	€€	f	t	Take the left-hand door to a fashionable, cosmopolitan restaurant offering delicious fish and shellfish. Or, the right-hand door to the more relaxed brasserie with an extensive menu (again largely fish), which will win guests over with its quality and powerful flavours.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3337787000	Restaurant Blauw	Springweg 64	Netherlands	Utrecht	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantblauw.nl	Nessun premio	Indonesian	4.0	€€	f	f	Tradition, a street food influence, authenticity and purity are the words that best sum up this popular restaurant, which showcases the full array of Indonesian cuisine. The rijsttafel (a medley of dishes with rice – also available in a vegan version) provides an excellent opportunity to discover the chef's talent for seasoning and balancing intense flavours. From the succulence of the lamb, the distinctly nutty flavour of the peanut sauce and the delicate spiciness of the gado gado, you can see that this is a chef who knows how to combine generosity with subtlety. Be sure to try the roast goat meat as well!	basileryan	\N	\N
3337602070	Héron	Schalkwijkstraat 26	Netherlands	Utrecht	Counter dining	https://www.heronrestaurant.nl/	Nessun premio	Organic, Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	t	Pure and honest. These two words encapsulate this vibrant place, though they hardly do it justice. Joyce and Victor's deep respect for the seasons and Dutch produce is truly inspiring. They work closely with their suppliers and encourage chef Josephien Blom to be creative within the framework of their sustainable values. The pig's trotters with a tangy remoulade sauce is a classic of the house, but she also gives potatoes a surprising twist with a seaweed sauce and crispy serrated wrack. Prepare to be amazed!	rossettijonas	\N	\N
3339066036	De Watermolen	H. Avelinghstraat 154	Netherlands	Velp	Terrace	https://www.de-watermolen.nl/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This watermill, which is over 600 years old, is without a doubt the star attraction of this charming restaurant. Both the warm and welcoming interior and the secluded terrace are popular. Ramon Klaassen takes great pride in his work, which you cannot fail to notice during his interactions with diners. His unique take on classic dishes never disappoints. For example he rolls up soft-boiled duck ham and fills it with a rich poultry mousse. Playful garnishes such as an onion chutney with nuts and reduced balsamic vinegar add that little something extra. The set menu (with options) is a hit – even for those who do not eat meat or fish.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3339385222	LEV by Mike	Badweg 4	Netherlands	Winterswijk	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.levbymike.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	LEV now occupies the first floor of a historical bathhouse, from where diners can enjoy panoramic views of a natural pond and the cosy charm of a modern brasserie. Mike Vrijdag's culinary concept is a hit: the menu features an extensive selection of small plates ranging from comfort food to cutting-edge creations. This chef's technical skills and playful spirit ensure a dining experience that is always engaging. Take, for instance, his freshly caught sea bass tartare combined with tangy pickled cucumber, soy gel, and a wasabi sorbet providing subtly sweet and spicy kick. A symphony of flavours awaits!	sokolovabigail	\N	\N
3333865176	Frances Vinbar	Henrik Ibsens gate 48	Norway	Oslo	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://www.frances.no	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	One of three restaurants housed in the former US Embassy building, this ground-floor spot occupies a space previously used for the rather less exciting purpose of issuing visas. It’s now been transformed into a café, wine bar and restaurant, serving a selection of Middle Eastern and Mediterranean-inspired sharing plates. The generous dishes catch the eye with their vibrant appearance, then satisfy the palate with their fabulous flavours^ confit cauliflower with the colourful trio of tomato coulis, cashew cream and coriander oil is a prime example.	rossettijonas	\N	\N
