3334043654	Le Braci	ul. Górnośląska 24	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://lebraci.pl/	Nessun premio	Italian	4.0	€	f	t	There's a clubby feel to this intimate Italian restaurant thanks to its zinc-topped bar, high ceiling and dark green colour scheme. The appealing Italian menu covers all regions, with dishes proving to be authentic and full of flavour – especially the impressively precise homemade pasta. A superb range of wines includes those from small Italian producers and lesser-seen regions. Charming service helps to create a welcoming atmosphere.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3332226567	Koneser Grill	ul. Ząbkowska 29	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://konesergrillwarszawa.pl	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills	4.0	€€	f	f	Its location is one of this restaurant’s many strengths, forming part of Centrum Praskie Koneser, an old vodka distillery that now has the feel of a mini walled village^ apartments, shops, art venues and a museum all now sit within the former factory. From the owners of Butchery & Wine, this grill-centric eatery offers a range of quality steaks aged in-house – but everything from the salad to the Basque cheesecake dessert is just as enjoyable. Sharing is the way to go for the best value experience.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3333417814	kontakt	Sandomierska 13	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	https://kontakt.wine/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€	t	f	Just outside of the hustle and bustle of the city centre, you'll find this trendy spot with a wine bar on its lower level and a rustic bistro upstairs. The cooking has a Mediterranean heart, with croquetas and cavatelli likely to appear on a great value menu that’s perfect for sharing. The wine list plays a starring role, providing an extensive choice that largely focuses on natural and bio-dynamic wines from lesser-known producers – and the team have an excellent knowledge of their selection.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3331869413	Kieliszki na Próżnej	ul. Próżna 12	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://kieliszkinaproznej.pl/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	A huge, gravity-defying rack of wine glasses is the first thing you notice when you arrive at this friendly wine bar and bistro. Next, it’s the striking black and white wildlife mural filling one wall. The appealing menus represent good value, especially at lunchtime, and include hearty dishes that are bursting with bold and punchy flavours. An extensive wine list offers plenty of great quality choices to fill all those glasses with, but ‘bring your own’ is welcome too.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3339535324	Ceviche Bar	Twarda 2-4	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://new.cevichebar.pl/	Nessun premio	South American	4.0	€€	f	f	Bringing South American flavours to Warsaw, you’ll quickly find that this bright, airy restaurant is much more than a bar and serves far more than just ceviche. The famous Peruvian dish does feature – with sea bass, tuna and oyster among the varieties – but so do empanadas, grilled steaks and picarones. Argentinian Chef-Owner Martin Gimenez Castro imbues them all with freshness and vitality. In the evening, the music grows louder and the pisco sours start emerging from the bar at increasing speed.	landirobert	\N	\N
3331266620	alewino	ul. Mokotowska 48	Poland	Warsaw	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.alewino.pl/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Spread across various rooms, this starkly decorated bistro started life as a wine shop. There’s still a range of bottles for sale, along with a wine list that offers plenty of younger and lesser-known producers. The well-priced menu allows guests to order a few plates to share, be that classics like beef tartare or dishes that show off seasonal vegetables such as asparagus and morel mushrooms. Look out for the signpost by the gates when arriving, as the entrance is tucked away off the main street.	vitalimercuzio	\N	\N
3330288541	Casa Chef Victor Felisberto	Rua Francisco Ferreira da Mata 99	Portugal	Abrantes	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://casachefvictorfelisberto.pt/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	Discover the special vision of regional cooking showcased by Victor Felisberto, a Portuguese chef with an impressive track record who trained in Paris and gained experience in restaurants in France as well as others in London, Barcelona and Andorra. His speciality is meat cooked over a wood fire, in particular Iberian pork and veal, with the unique feature of using very slow cooking techniques to ensure sublime textures and much more intense flavours. He favours traditionally inspired dishes, home-made desserts of a high quality and bread made with his own recipe.	winternoemi	\N	\N
3330261554	O Típico	Rua Doutor Manuel Alegre 42	Portugal	Águeda	Air conditioning	http://restauranteotipico.pt	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€	f	t	If you’re looking for a typical and authentic dining experience, head for this restaurant in the upper part of town run by a charming married couple. The overall feel is unpretentious with a simple façade and tables set very close together^ however, the single dining room boasts a typical regional charm high on detail that includes antique decorative objects and a few farming implements. Here you’ll find a local clientele, 100% Portuguese cooking that is abundant and full of genuine flavours, and delicious home-made desserts. Make sure you try the octopus “à lagareiro” and the cod gratin with “smashed” potatoes!	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3331609629	Inato Bistrô	Praça do Município 7	Portugal	Braga	Air conditioning	http://www.inatobistro.pt	Nessun premio	Creative, Contemporary	3.0	€	f	t	The name of this restaurant stems from In“ATO”, which in Portuguese means something that is active or in movement, a theme continued on the menu where dishes are served in different acts (I, II, III and IV). Young chefs Miguel Rodrigues and Tiago Costa have joined forces to showcase their creative cuisine, which makes full use of the best-quality local ingredients. Located opposite the elegant setting of the municipal square in the heart of Braga, Inato reminds us that it is possible to prepare amazing dishes from the simplest of ingredients.	dinusauru	\N	\N
3331510037	O Javali	Quinta do Reconco 6	Portugal	Bragança	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.ojavali.pt/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	t	A restaurant that is well run by a couple who are highly passionate about their work, with the husband running the front of house and his wife in charge in the kitchen. Easy to find given its location by the main road, it features a reasonably spacious car park, a public bar and two rustically themed dining rooms, both boasting stone walls and a hunting-inspired decor. Its menu showcases the traditional dishes of the Trás-os-Montes region (including game), all of which are copious and based around the freshest ingredients. Make sure you try the wild boar stew with chestnuts, the rice with hare, and the Bragança-style lamb.	calincolin	\N	\N
3334691457	Vila do Peixe	Rua Doutor João Abel de Freitas 30-A	Portugal	Câmara de Lobos	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	t	f	An ideal lunch or dinner option for visitors given its location in the upper section of the old town (opposite the municipal market) and its huge windows boasting superb views of both the bay and the ocean. If you’re looking for authentic maritime-inspired cooking and fresh fish caught the same day you won’t find a better option, as guests can choose the piece of fish they want to eat as if they were in the market^ the fish is then weighed in front of you and cooked immediately on the grill. Typical dishes well worth sampling, if available, are the popular limpets and sea snails.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3338590951	Marquês de Marialva	Largo do Romal 16	Portugal	Cantanhede	Car park	https://www.marquesdemarialva.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€	t	f	The name pays a small homage to this Portuguese nobleman who played a decisive part in several battles during the Restoration War. The restaurant enjoys a certain prestige as well as a good location in an old house that has been restored. It boasts three intimate dining rooms combining classic and rustic decorative detail, one with an open fire, plus a large function room upstairs. Dishes with a distinct traditional flavour can be found on the à la carte, alongside several tasting menus. Make sure you try the “lagareiro”-style baked cod and the exquisite roast kid!	donatidiego	\N	\N
3335308703	Carvalho	Alameda do Tabolado	Portugal	Chaves	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus	https://restaurante-carvalho.com/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	Located opposite the Tabolado garden and close to the river, in an area with easy parking. Behind the impeccable façade you’ll find a reasonably comfortable and welcoming interior with the main dining room by the entrance and a second space, which is also home to the wine cellar, in the basement. The female owner is at the helm in the kitchen, offering high-quality home-inspired cooking on a menu that changes daily and always includes fresh fish and other typical specialities such as “alheira”, a smoked sausage made with pork and chicken. Superb, friendly service from the front-of-house team completes the picture!	fischerbogdan	\N	\N
3332353422	Bar Agrikultur	Skånegatan 79	Sweden	Stockholm		https://baragrikultur.com	Nessun premio	Swedish, Small eats	5.0	€€	f	t	A warmly run, intimate and cosy wine bar that is a perfect fit for Södermalm. The freshly prepared and delicious small plates are designed for sharing and showcase classic Swedish flavours. The three stainless steel tanks contain home-distilled gin – flavours are changed regularly using various herbs, oils or fruits.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3336410809	Solar do Bacalhau	Rua da Sota 10	Portugal	Coimbra	Air conditioning	http://www.restaurantesolardobacalhau.pt	Nessun premio	Portuguese	5.0	€	t	f	A good location in the Baixa de Coimbra, the section of the old town occupied by merchants and artisans in the Middle Ages. If you’re keen to try the famous Portuguese bacalao you won’t find a better place, as this restaurant impresses with its attractive interior design on two floors, stone walls, a glass-enclosed inner patio and lots of natural light. À la carte and set menu options feature a variety of regional specialities, superb cod dishes cooked in different ways, and a good selection of meats. The display cabinets at the entrance provide a welcoming taster of what’s to come!	ciobanuciprian	\N	\N
3331570343	Dóri	Rua das Companhas	Portugal	Costa Nova do Prado	Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	f	t	Situated between the Aveiro estuary and the Atlantic, on the first floor of a contemporary glass-fronted building offering splendid views, particularly from the terrace. The bar features an enticing display cabinet, while the two dining rooms are bright and functional-contemporary in feel. Although the menu includes delicious meats and a few savoury rice dishes, the speciality here is the wild fish, cooked on the open grill, and the seafood. Don’t leave without trying the fried fish (“fritada de pescado”) or the delicious “ensopado” of turbot.	paganialex	\N	\N
3335064330	Olaias	Rua Abade Pedro 2 - Centro de Artes e Espectáculos	Portugal	Figueira da Foz	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://olaias.figdafoz.com/	Nessun premio	Portuguese	3.0	€€	f	f	This is a restaurant that provides you with an excuse to return at any time of year… and why not! The house speciality, the savoury Carolino rice (with rice grown in the Mondego valley), changes constantly with the seasons, and is cooked in a clay oven, which brings added flavour. We recommend starting with the mouthwatering and smooth Rissol da Tia Fernanda, which is absolutely delicious. Next, it has to be rice, of course (with any accompaniment – duck, fish or oxtail – all are excellent choices) and, to finish, the moist “pão de ló” cake with sea salt, which is truly heavenly. The restaurant is located in the Centro de Artes e Espectáculos and has a meticulous yet unpretentious decor, featuring floor to ceiling windows and fantastic views!	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3336731742	Avista	Estrada Monumental 145	Portugal	Funchal	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.portobay.com/pt/restaurantes/restaurantes-madeira/avista/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	Part of the fabulous The Cliff Bay hotel, Avista is run by the prestigious chef Benoît Sinthon (Il Gallo d'Oro, two Michelin Stars) and, like its older “brother”, boasts truly spectacular views, with the coast, the vast Atlantic Ocean and nearby islands as a backdrop. Here, the cuisine Mediterranean highlights the restaurant’s philosophy of informality in which the idea of sharing plates to enable guests to try more dishes is key, along with a focus on fresh ingredients of the very highest quality.	veselyolivia	\N	\N
3336936099	Casal da Penha	Rua Penha de França - Beco do Ataíde n.1	Portugal	Funchal	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://casaldapenha.com/	Nessun premio	Portuguese	3.0	€€	f	t	A family-run restaurant that extols the virtues of all that is simple yet authentic with a menu which lets the ingredients do the talking. Located in the centre of Funchal, surrounded by large hotels, its modest yet neat and tidy dining room is enhanced by the superb terrace upstairs. The father is in charge of the kitchen, where he prepares dishes with a traditional flavour including lots of regional specialities, delicious fish of the day options, an extensive choice of meats, and tasty rice dishes, including a variety of paellas. Make sure you order the clams “à Bulhão Pato” if available – they are truly delicious!	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3338688635	Norma	Rua Doutor José Sampaio 35	Portugal	Guimaraes	Terrace	https://www.foodbynorma.com/	Nessun premio	Creative, Portuguese	4.0	€€	f	f	Norma occupies an old building that almost passes by unnoticed, yet boasts delightful views, especially from its terrace, from where the vista encompasses São Gualter church, the iconic symbol of the city. The head chef here is Hugo Alves who, having worked in leading restaurants around Portugal, decided to return to his native Guimarães. His cooking is centred on a tasting menu and an à la carte that change every season. Dishes that are a must include the profiterole made with crab, tomato, sweet basil and cream cheese, and the mouthwatering “bràs”. For vegetarians, we recommended the delicious “feijoada” of celery, sesame, tsukudani and orange.	kozakjennifer	\N	\N
3330400989	Zunzum Gastrobar	Avenida Infante D. Henrique. Doca do Jardim do Tabaco	Portugal	Lisbon	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.zunzum.pt	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€€	t	f	This elegant, completely glass-fronted gastro-bar, occupying a modern building close to the city’s cruise ship terminal (and opposite the unusual Museu do Lactário or Milk Station Museum), favours high-quality contemporary cuisine that is based around traditional Portuguese recipes, but without closing the door on inspiration, dishes or techniques from further afield. The bright, designer-inspired interior, with its predominant red and white colour scheme, and the terrace boasting pleasant views of the Tagus come as a pleasant surprise.	novakmonica	\N	\N
3332121617	Carnal	Rua da Misericordia 78	Portugal	Lisbon	Air conditioning	http://www.carnal.pt	Nessun premio	Mexican	4.0	€€	f	f	This lively, centrally located restaurant has quickly become fashionable given that it is owned by famous chef Ljubomir Stanisic (head of the 100 Maneiras group). Carnal describes itself as a Mexican gastro-bar, and is one of those places that immediately appeals to the senses. In its informal, modern design setting featuring subtle details relating to Mexican culture, enjoy harmonious, well-thought-out cooking with a perfect balance between flavour and spiciness in every one of its superb dishes. Don’t miss the delicious pork tacos or the tacos with fried cauliflower.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3339317858	PODA	Rua Sacadura Cabral 25	Portugal	Montemor-o-Novo	Air conditioning	https://restaurantepoda.pt/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	PODA occupies an old agricultural warehouse that has been completely remodelled and decorated in rustic style with a plethora of wood. Chef João Narigueta and his long-term friend Miguel Dominguinhos have joined together to open this dining space in which the traditional cooking of the Alentejo has undergone a renaissance. One of the classic dishes on the menu is the typical “migas gatas” with cod, which is simply presented but with surprising flavour. Another typical regional dish is “enxovalhada”, a sponge cake filled with walnuts and honey and sprinkled with cinnamon. The wine list mainly features local producers.	parisibenjamin	\N	\N
3339205488	O Frade	Calçada da Ajuda 14	Portugal	Lisbon	Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace	http://httpss//fraderestaurante.com	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	A small corner restaurant named after the family that owns it. Its interior is evocative of a traditional Alentejo “tasca”, with simple decorative details that highlight the production of the famous “vinho da talha”, a wine with a long historical footprint that, in keeping with Roman tradition, is made in large earthenware amphorae and is a highly renowned wine in the Alentejo. Welcoming service, plus an attractive U-shaped bar popular for dining, where guests can savour a variety of “petiscos”, rice dishes and traditional Alentejo recipes with a contemporary touch – all accompanied by an extensive choice of wines.	reinhardtgabriela	\N	\N
3330373796	Machado	Rua Doutor António José de Almeida 467	Portugal	Nogueira	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€	f	t	Quality and quantity are both guaranteed at this restaurant occupying an old house in a small village close to Maia. Several separate dining rooms, all with a similar rustic decor, simple table settings and lots of typical decorative details hanging from the walls. Here, it is impossible to leave hungry given the copious portions on the traditional home-cooked menu which teems with local flavours. Make sure you try Machado’s house speciality, the Lafões-style roast veal.	iordachelilly	\N	\N
3330123578	O Pastus	Avenida Marquês De Pombal 5	Portugal	Paço de Arcos	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.opastus.pt	Nessun premio	Portuguese, Contemporary	3.0	€€	t	t	This modest yet charming restaurant opposite the Paço de Arcos gardens is characterised by great enthusiasm, painstaking service and the hard work of young Annakaren Fuentes, who is on top of everything. The cooking here can be defined as modern Portuguese, based around respect for traditional ingredients and flavours, showcased in one tasting menu, entitled Cabal (7 courses). Individual dishes can also be ordered à la carte.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3337552539	Solar do Forcado	Rua Candido dos Reis 14	Portugal	Portalegre	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€	f	t	Located along a narrow, cobbled street in the town’s old quarter, reasonably close to the castle. The modest façade leads to a small but welcoming dining room with a rustic feel and a decor that revolves around the world of bullfighting. Here, the traditional cuisine is focused on meat, with the occasional dish dedicated to bulls in the ring, in homage to the team of “forcados”, a typical aspect of Portuguese bullfights in which both the owner and his father were once involved. Make sure you try the exquisite skewers of bull’s meat, not forgetting the “cozido à portuguesa” stew served every Thursday!	calincolin	\N	\N
3337655898	Gruta	Rua De Santa Catarina 447	Portugal	Porto	Air conditioning,Terrace	http://www.grutaporto.com	Nessun premio	International	5.0	€€	t	t	Gruta’s is one of those of places where you can eat well at a reasonable price. To a backdrop of stylish yet informal decor and a setting in an alleyway just off a shopping street, focuses on a concise menu on which fish and seafood (mainly from the north of the country) take centre stage. Its dishes are high on presentation and flavour, combining Brazilian and Portuguese influences and a contemporary style of cooking.	grasomarkus	\N	\N
3338239162	In Diferente	Rua do Doutor Sousa Rosa 23	Portugal	Porto		http://indiferente.pt	Nessun premio	International	3.0	€€€	t	t	Despite not being in the centre of town or on any of the main tourist routes, it is well worth heading to this peaceful, welcoming and contemporary-style restaurant. Here, Angélica Salvador, the young chef of Brazilian origin, interprets her personal vision of traditional Portuguese and international cooking through dishes that are elaborate and very well presented. Her aim is to create dishes that are different, personal and showcase innovative detail, extracting maximum benefit from the superb fish delivered to the nearby auctions in Matosinhos and Aveiro, as well as from the region’s outstanding meats.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3333074552	Pátio 44	Passeio De São Lázaro	Portugal	Porto	Air conditioning,Terrace		Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	At Patio 44, you’ll be pleasantly surprised by the quality of ingredients used as well as the discreet and simple façade. This project was created by three friends, with chefs Simão Soares and Alfonso Ramos in charge of the kitchen – a partnership that developed from experience working together in a previous restaurant. Their cuisine is centred around traditional Portuguese cuisine enhanced by modern techniques and unique flavours. Standout dishes include the cod “punheta” with crunchy rice, followed by a vegetarian option (tofu and mushrooms with a mouthwatering demi-glace) and an impressive fresh cod prepared with a smooth chickpea purée. To finish, we highly recommend the spectacular “pão de ló” sponge cake fresh out of the oven, served with goat’s cheese ice-cream. The reasonable prices here are another pleasant surprise!	virgolinifrancesco	\N	\N
3332946125	Xtoria	Rua Guilherme Gomes Fernandes 17	Portugal	Setúbal	Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access	https://www.xtoria.pt/	Nessun premio	Contemporary	5.0	€	t	f	You may not be aware that fried cuttlefish is one of Setúbal’s most typical dishes. So, it’s not by chance that this restaurant is barely 200 metres from the statue of the “Fried Cuttlefish”, where you’ll also find a mural featuring fish found in the waters around the city. Understandably, cuttlefish features strongly on the menu at Xtoria, where it is prepared in a unique way and with a hint of modernity. Affordably priced dishes that you won’t want to miss include the cuttlefish with ponzu, black potato, sriracha mayonnaise and lumpfish caviar^ the Mertolenga beef loin with tuna sabayon and Eringy mushrooms in port wine^ and, to round things off, the cardamom cream with a ginger cookie and mango chutney.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3338040276	3 Pipos	Rua de Santo Amaro 966	Portugal	Tonda	Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	http://www.3pipos.pt	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	4.0	€	f	t	The emblem of this restaurant, which is now into its fourth decade and is spoken of very highly by everyone, is three barrels – a reference to its close connection with the wine sector. It features an entrance hall and several dining rooms with a classic-rustic feel and wine-focused decor, in which the menu showcases the cuisine of the Beira Alta region. The simple, copious dishes on offer include pork rice in a garlic and wine sauce, octopus “à lagareiro”, and the loin of confit cod with spinach and pork sausage. The spacious garden and its wine club that sells direct to the public at affordable prices add to its appeal.	bernasconikarl	\N	\N
3331778128	Camelo	Rua de Santa Marta 119	Portugal	Viana do Castelo	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://camelorestaurantes.com/camelo/	Nessun premio	Regional Cuisine	3.0	€	t	f	This family-run restaurant is always full despite its location in a part of town most people generally pass through without stopping. Its facilities include a bar, which leads to several pleasantly arranged dining rooms, a large marquee-style space for private functions, plus a huge garden patio for outdoor gatherings. The high-quality and varied cuisine on offer here is typical of the Minho, featuring fish and seafood from its own live tank, with a predilection for lamprey, plus an extensive selection of meat dishes and even a vegetarian menu. When in season, the lamprey dishes are a must!	guerravictor	\N	\N
3339332345	Tasquinha da Linda	Rua dos Mareantes A-10	Portugal	Viana do Castelo	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.tasquinhadalinda.com	Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	€€	f	f	One of the best dining options in this attractive town on the Costa Verde, this contemporary restaurant located next to the Castelo de Santiago da Barra occupies a docks warehouse in which the large attractive fish and seafood tanks take pride of place. Its owners are fish wholesalers, hence the top-quality fish and seafood that is on offer here, normally sold by weight and at prices that are highly competitive. You won’t find a single meat dish on the menu here! Make sure you save space for desserts made by the owners’ daughter!	zimmermannanna	\N	\N
3338162142	Rio by Paulo André	Praça da República 8	Portugal	Vila do Conde	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://rio.eatbu.com	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	f	A young and informal eatery with an open-view kitchen located at one end of Praça da República, one of Vila do Conde’s most beautiful squares thanks to its setting on the banks of the Ave river. In a nod to the name of his restaurant, chef Paulo André’s professional career is as surprising and unexpected as the meanders in a river! His cisHisontemporary-style cooking will definitely leave its mark given his passion, technical skill and a strong desire to please, plus a continual focus on using locally sourced vegetables (vegetarian dishes feature on the menu), fish and meat. If the weather’s fine, make sure you eat on the terrace.	pingliu	\N	\N
3339631815	Jiwan	4th Floor	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.jiwan.qa/	Nessun premio	Middle Eastern	4.0	﷼﷼	f	f	Its name translates as 'perfect pearl' and the location of this restaurant might indeed be perfect. Sitting on the fourth floor of Qatar’s National Museum, a stunning building modelled on the desert rose, it provides far-reaching views of the port and the Corniche promenade. Traditional Middle Eastern dishes are re-invented in a modern style, as with the cumin madroba, which comes with subtle spicing and enticing textural contrasts. Flavour combinations are nicely balanced, while the set menu is a veritable feast that represents very good value.	pellegriniloren	\N	\N
3336678619	Chai Chuan Tou Yang Rou Tang	115 Bukit Merah View Market & Hawker Centre	Singapore	Singapore			Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	$	t	f	The mutton soup here can be paired with tripe, meatballs, tendon or even brain. The mutton boasts the right mix of fatty and lean meat, without tasting gamey. The broth has a mildly herbal flavour. Come early as they tend to sell out.	schneidermihai	\N	\N
3337381018	Argan	Al Jasra Street	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access	https://www.tivolihotels.com/en/souq-waqif-doha/restaurants/argan	Nessun premio	Moroccan	4.0	﷼	f	t	You’ll find this great value restaurant on a pedestrianised street on the fringes of the Souq Waqif marketplace, a tourist hotspot that’s home to a range of local retailers and eateries. The appealing menu features authentic Moroccan dishes that are packed with flavour and enhanced by careful spicing^ tagine and couscous are their speciality. Desserts such as jawhara are great too, as are the refreshing mocktails – and a mint tea in the plush lounge of the Al Jasra Boutique Hotel, in which the restaurant sits, is a lovely way to end your visit.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3333431908	Hoppers	Barahat Musheireb Street	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking	https://hoppers.dmenus.com/	Nessun premio	Sri Lankan, South Indian	5.0	﷼﷼	t	t	Sri Lankan and South Indian food is the draw here at this outpost of the popular London original. Spread over two floors, the restaurant is in the smart, redeveloped downtown area and is run by a polite and well-organised team. Order a few snacks and mocktails, then a biryani or a finely judged curry accompanied by dosas and, of course, some of the signature hoppers. Before long, you’ll have a veritable feast to enjoy with friends – and one that won’t break the bank either, so feel free to do some over-eager ordering.	riccidaniele	\N	\N
3336758970	Isaan	West Bay Lagoon Street	Qatar	Doha	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.hyattrestaurants.com/en/doha/restaurant/isaan-doha	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	﷼﷼	t	f	Sitting in a corner of the Grand Hyatt Hotel’s cavernous ground floor, this large open-plan restaurant boasts three on-view kitchens all producing authentic Thai cooking. Thailand’s influence extends to the décor too, with teak parquet floors and a Thai boat. Dishes are vibrant and flavoursome, with all regions of Thailand covered and ingredients flown in specially. If you’re not sure of your spicing level, ask the warm and friendly service team for recommendations.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3335557576	Iva New Balkan Cuisine	Kneginje Ljubice 11	Serbia	Belgrade	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://newbalkancuisine.com/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine	5.0	€	t	f	A welcoming bistro with colourful, contemporary-style furnishings and an attractive outdoor space for summer dining. The menu is extensive and based mainly on traditional recipes that have been given a subtle lighter touch while still remaining faithful to their original style and flavour, largely thanks to the use of local ingredients. We particularly recommend the oxtail with caramelized onions, homemade gnocchi with veal brain and bone reduction.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3338689383	Istok	Gospodar Jevremova 50	Serbia	Belgrade	Terrace	https://istokrestoran.com/	Nessun premio	Vietnamese	5.0	€	f	t	Situated just a stone’s throw from the lively town centre, this elegant restaurant with a South Asian ambience serves modern Asian comfort food in generously portioned dishes, some of which are available in half-portions allowing guests to sample different specialities. We particularly enjoyed the Miang Kham, a typical Thai appetiser that is not often served in Western countries. Every dish is served with colourful dips to make them even more appetising.	pingliu	\N	\N
3338691866	Fool	21 Boon Tat Street	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list	http://foolwine.com.sg	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	4.0	$$	f	t	This lively wine bar concept is another brainchild of the chef-owner behind Cloudstreet and Kotuwa. The décor is on trend with a retro 1970s look. The wine list is extensive and well-choreographed, with a slight bias towards older vintages. Pair your wine with snacks and small plates hallmarked by precise execution, beguiling presentations and pronounced flavours. In particular, the chicken liver éclair with date and Madeira is not to be missed.	costasergio	\N	\N
3330428485	Anglo Indian (Shenton Way)	#01-08	Singapore	Singapore	Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.angloindian.com.sg/	Nessun premio	Indian	3.0	$$	t	f	If there’s one dish that customers should expect to find in a restaurant called Anglo Indian it’s chicken tikka masala – and sure enough it’s a firm favourite of many here at this simply decorated spot in the heart of the CBD. The dining room may seat only 20, but there’s a large outdoor terrace where everyone congregates for the well-priced cooking. Other popular choices include butter chicken and mutton dum biryani.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
