3337348290	Collonge Café	Chemin du Château-de-Bellerive 3	Switzerland	Collonge-Bellerive	Terrace	https://www.collonge-cafe.ch/	Nessun premio	Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	t	f	This modern restaurant boasts a great location next to the historical town hall and has a charming terrace laid out in the garden. The seasonally inspired menu successfully brings together modern Italian and French cuisine, while keeping an open mind when it comes to international influences. Cordial and competent service. Tip: the competitively priced lunch menu.	rossiyuri	\N	\N
3335972237	Le Lab by Adel & Niko	Route de la Crottaz 5	Switzerland	Corseaux	Terrace	https://restaurant-lelab.com	Nessun premio	International	3.0	€€	t	f	This establishment is located just past the boundary between Vevey and Corseaux. The ground floor dispenses cookery lessons (for enthusiastic individuals and groups), while the basement houses the restaurant proper. The latter sports a modern vibe depicted by warm colours (a striking crimson-claret wall), an understated wine display and a designer-inspired long counter. The owners, charming Adel and jovial Niko, play a key role in their establishment’s buzzy character. A set menu with a choice of courses at lunchtime and creative, tapas-style dishes to share in the evenings. Pleasant dinky terrace.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3330496091	Edo	Route Sierre-Montana 43	Switzerland	Crans-Montana	Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://edo-tokyo.ch/	Nessun premio	Japanese, Sushi	4.0	€€	t	t	You can be in the Swiss mountains and still enjoy authentic Japanese cuisine, including dishes such as Japanese fondue, grilled chicken with Teriyaki sauce, and delicious gyozas and sushi (takeaway dishes are also available). Here, legendary specialities from Japan are prepared in front of you with high-quality ingredients and meticulous care. Terrace with views of the surrounding peaks.	rizzogabriele	\N	\N
3333452385	Golden Dragon	Talstrasse 3	Switzerland	Davos Platz	Car park,Wheelchair access	https://hotelgrischa.ch/	Nessun premio	Chinese, Sichuan	5.0	€€	f	t	Davos's restaurant scene is not only about regional food – the Chinese restaurant at the Grischa hotel serves Cantonese and Szechuan-style cuisine. Tip: Some dishes are designed for sharing. If you fancy the Peking duck for two, be sure to pre-order (at least 48hr in advance). You can also combine many of the ingredients yourself according to your preferences. The upscale design features wood, stone, leather and a palette of elegant dark shades for a lovely ambience.	piraspeter	\N	\N
3330559794	Gasthaus Schupfen	Steinerstrasse 501	Switzerland	Diessenhofen	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://schupfen.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	f	t	With a history dating back to 1455, this lovely half-timbered house is really something special. In an inviting atmosphere, food is served in three charming rooms and on the idyllic terrace overlooking the Rhine. The menu features classics, including Kalbsgeschnetzeltes Zürcher Art (veal ragout), and seasonal dishes such as Kundelfinger trout with boiled potatoes and spinach. If you are looking for a good location for a wedding or event, the premises can also be rented out.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3339365195	Sonne	Dorf 2	Switzerland	Ebersecken	Car park,Terrace	https://www.sonne-ebersecken.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Swiss	5.0	€€	f	t	At the Häfliger family's lovely 100-year-old restaurant, diners can look forward to fresh, flavoursome food and attentive service provided by experienced staff. Classic Swiss cuisine is served in the form of a seasonal or surprise set menu. Alternatively, you can order à la carte. This place even has its own excellent spring water! Pleasant terrace to the rear of the building. Tip: Delicious cheese is sold in the cheesery next door.	weberdragos	\N	\N
3336545603	Moosegg	Moosegg 231A	Switzerland	Emmenmatt	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.moosegg.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Modern Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	Up here, at an altitude of around 1 000m, there is much to get excited about: the phenomenal view of the Emmental and the Alps – either from the modern, elegant restaurant with its large window front or the magnificent terrace – is complemented by good food with a regional and seasonal focus. For a cheaper but equally indulgent alternative, head to Beiz. The terrific wine selection boasts around 800 different options. Chic guestrooms are available in the adjoining boutique hotel.	brunojulian	\N	\N
3335707794	Zum Pflugstein	Pflugsteinstrasse 71	Switzerland	Erlenbach	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.pflugstein.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	Considered the largest erratic boulder in the canton of Zurich, the Pﬂugstein is located close to this distinguished vineyard farmhouse and lends its name to its fabulous restaurant. The interior comprises an attractive wood-panelled space and a room with a fireplace, while outside there is a truly idyllic terrace. The service team overseen by the charming Jeannine Meili also deserves a mention. Tip: Try the tender boiled beef!	marinescumario	\N	\N
3335866370	Gommerstuba	Ernerstrasse 53	Switzerland	Ernen	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.gommerstuba.com/	Nessun premio	International	3.0	€€	f	t	The friendly hosts here serve contemporary cuisine, which can be ordered à carte or as a set menu – there is also a vegetarian set menu. Many regional wines are featured. A restaurant decor blending wood and stone makes for a pleasant atmosphere. The lovely terrace is also inviting!	popafarah	\N	\N
3337382337	Linde	Niederrohrdorferstrasse 1	Switzerland	Fislisbach	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.linde-fislisbach.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Farm to table	5.0	€€	f	t	The secret of Linde's success is a formula of classic Swiss cuisine made from good ingredients coupled with reasonable prices. A lively atmosphere reigns in this attractive, well-run place with its various dining spaces, large bar area and glassed-in kitchen. Steak tartare and Zürcher Geschnetzeltes (veal) are among the permanent fixtures on the menu. For lunch, the offer is somewhat reduced. The wonderful terrace comes into its own in summer, and there are well-kept guestrooms too.	pesciroberto	\N	\N
3339713027	PINOT	Steigstrasse 12	Switzerland	Fläsch	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-pinot.ch/	Nessun premio	International, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	The location in the side wing of the modern Klinik Gut private hospital may be a little unusual, but the food here is excellent… thanks to Roland Schmid, who has made a name for himself in the region over the years. The decor is trendy and minimalist in style, with an open kitchen^ the view of the mountains and the surrounding area is fabulous – tables on the terrace are understandably coveted. Tip: the tasting menu on Thursday evenings.	galassiniccolo	\N	\N
3330860021	Gasthof zum goldenen Kreuz	Zürcherstrasse 134	Switzerland	Frauenfeld	Terrace	https://www.goldeneskreuz.ch/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This restaurant is steeped in tradition, and much sought after for its excellent seasonal cuisine. At lunchtime, you can order à la carte or opt for one of four three-course set menus. In the evening, there is a tasting menu in addition to an à la carte selection. Attentive service comes courtesy of a friendly and well-organised front-of-house team. Goethe himself was a guest here – the pretty Goethe-Stübli is named after him – and the well-preserved, painted panelling from the 17C adds rustic charm. The terrace is a delightful spot, secluded from the street by abundant greenery. Modern, functional guestrooms are available for overnight stays. Tip for motorists: public car park behind the building.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3334893231	Wirtshus zum Wyberg	Oberteufenerstrasse 1	Switzerland	Freienstein-Teufen	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://wyberg.ch/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The restaurant on the first floor is a little more elegant and comfortable than the bar. The large menu ranges from a delicious veal schnitzel in morel sauce to the classic saddle of venison grand veneur, not to mention a popular lobster menu which includes home-made ravioli.	popafarah	\N	\N
3333449985	Casa Caminada	Obergass 68	Switzerland	Fürstenau	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.casacaminada.com/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This restaurant enjoys a lovely quiet location in the castle grounds. Inside the bright, high-ceilinged space, modern design meets warm wood^ outside, there is a delightful terrace. A charming team provides competent service. They serve regional cuisine, in which seasonal ingredients sourced from select local producers go into extremely flavoursome dishes – the produce steals the show! Andreas Caminada's take on Grisons classics can also be found on the menu. Be sure to try his quark bizochels, for example. Tip: You can buy bread baked in the on-site bakery and other goods in their shop next door.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3337813299	Natürlich	Rue de la Coulouvrenière 38	Switzerland	Geneva	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.naturlich.ch/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Piedmontese	4.0	€€	f	f	Just a few metres from the River Rhône and the BFM theatre, this popular restaurant appeals with its trendy and relaxed bistro-style atmosphere. It serves seasonal modern cuisine based on quality regional ingredients, in dishes such as roast cuttlefish, purple potatoes and cime di rapa. The food is accompanied by a terrific wine list including organic options. And for an even more convivial experience, plates are designed for sharing! Friendly service, too.	martinifederico	\N	\N
3331111827	Bistrot Dumas	Avenue Dumas 7	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning	https://www.lebistrotdumas.ch/	Nessun premio	French	3.0	€€	t	t	This buzzy bistro located in the Champel neighbourhood is often fully booked. The interior is done out simply and tastefully – it is the Art Nouveau stained-glass ceiling panels, as well as the columns, that draw the eye. Their classic take on traditional French cuisine is flavoursome and aromatic, plus everything is made in-house. The service is efficient and attentive.	carlinikita	\N	\N
3335503163	Osteria della Bottega	Grand Rue 3	Switzerland	Geneva	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.osteriadellabottega.com/	Nessun premio	Italian, Seasonal Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	This lively restaurant is located on a steep little street in Geneva's old town. Against a chic industrial-style backdrop with an open kitchen, diners are treated to modern, seasonally inspired Italian cuisine and fine wines, plus attentive and friendly service. It's best to book, as Osteria is very popular! Across the street there is a lovely terrace.	montesialessandro	\N	\N
3330757644	Chez Philippe	Rue du Rhône 8	Switzerland	Geneva	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.chezphilippe.ch/	Nessun premio	Meats and Grills, International	3.0	€€	t	f	Philippe Chevrier from the Domaine de Châteauvieux is the brains behind this huge restaurant inspired by New York-style steakhouses. Relaxed atmosphere, meats sourced from the renowned Boucherie du Molard, fish caught by small-scale fishermen, dishes cooked over a wood fire, a truly authentic cheesecake and an expansive wine list. A real favourite!	galbanielena	\N	\N
3331300105	L'Agape	Rue Caroline 11	Switzerland	Geneva	Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.lagape.ch	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary	4.0	€€	t	t	This lovely old-school bistro ticks all the boxes when it comes to good vibes. It has been tastefully refurbished to showcase features such as its original tiling, wooden banquette seating, mirrors on the walls, a large chandelier fashioned out of old copper pans and a small service counter. As for the food, chef Clément Thellier has designed a short, savvy menu that makes your mouth water with its well-crafted and beautifully presented dishes: sweetbreads en barigoule, bacon crisps, split peas with bacon^ beef tenderloin, toasted bread, pan-fried foie gras, mini vegetables and potato emulsion^ poached and glazed pineapple, toasted pain d'épices and rum ice cream. A lovely dining experience at a reasonable price – not to be sniffed at in Geneva!	caldarolacagilio	\N	\N
