3336244400	Restaurant Schlüssel - Schlüsselstube	Oberdorfstrasse 5	Switzerland	Mels	Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.schluesselmels.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking	5.0	€€	f	f	Schlüsselstube is a bistro where they also serve outstanding food – and it represents really great value for money. Classics such as braised veal cheeks are delicious, and the desserts are extremely hard to resist! When it comes to wine, this cosy place also hits all the right notes. The service provided by waitresses in traditional dress could not be more charming!	venturaroman	\N	\N
3337992846	Le Bistro by Décotterd	Route de Glion 111	Switzerland	Montreux	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access	https://maisondecotterd.com/le-bistro/	Nessun premio	French Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	t	Like its fine dining counterpart, Le Bistro also promises diners a stunning view! In this worthy alternative with a modern interior, the food is simpler, but absolutely the equal in terms of taste and culinary know-how. Be sure to try the pâté en croûte or tarte au chocolat!	vasilievamelia	\N	\N
3330138598	Kaiserstock	Dörfli 2	Switzerland	Riemenstalden	Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace	https://www.kaiserstock.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, International	4.0	€€	t	t	This charming establishment perched in a small mountain village is your reward after the narrow, steep drive up! The fact that the restaurant has many regular customers is of course mainly down to its tasty traditional cuisine. The dishes are prepared with flair from good, fresh produce from the region. Popular options include stews and ravioli. A four- to seven-course set menu is also available if you pre-book (two days in advance). Seasonal specialities such as venison and chamois or Metzgete (pork platter) are also worth considering. Tip: Soups, sausages, jams and other delicacies can be purchased to take home. There are pleasant rustic-style guestrooms for overnight stays. N.B. Cash only!	krausmartina	\N	\N
3336468480	Café de Riex	Route de la Corniche 24	Switzerland	Riex		https://www.cafe-de-riex.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Artisanal seasonal cuisine that showcases small-scale producers and local artisans, featuring hearty meat dishes (pork belly, kidneys, sweetbreads), sauces with real flavour, and delicious home-made ice creams flavoured with herbs from the garden (savory, sage, rosemary). Guests are in for a real treat in this café in the Vaud! The wine list is just as tempting, and features wines produced here in Riex.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3332105612	Le Café Valrose	Place de la Gare 2	Switzerland	Rougemont	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.valrose.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine, Swiss	3.0	€€	f	t	Part of the same establishment as La Table de Valrose, this bistro has a comfortable rustic-style Alpine atmosphere, both outside, on the terrace shaded by chestnut trees, surrounded by mountains, and inside, by the fireplace, in the wood-panelled space. Relax in the lounge bar with a coffee or cocktail in hand. The menu features tasty seasonal fare in the form of simple dishes, while classics such as Valrose fondue (champagne version available), malakoffs and Valrose burgers (meat or veggie) are permanent fixtures on the menu. The dessert trolley is available all afternoon, for teatime.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3331999752	16 ART-BAR-RESTAURANT	Mittelgässli 16	Switzerland	Saanen	Terrace	https://www.16eme.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, International	3.0	€€	f	f	Diners will feel right at home in this charming and inviting restaurant. Set in a former bell foundry, the atmosphere is welcoming and delightfully down to earth. The blend of rustic and modern styles is interesting, and the art on the walls is sure to draw the eye. You can look forward to very friendly and attentive service, as well as pared-down and exceedingly flavourful dishes prepared by owner Nik Buchs. Popular choices here include true classics such as entrecôte or veal cutlet. The extensive wine list also includes organic and biodynamic wines.	popescumaya	\N	\N
3332512120	Zer Schlucht	Blomattenweg 2	Switzerland	Saas-Fee	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.lagorge.ch/restaurant-zer-schlucht.html	Nessun premio	Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	This place boasts a fantastic location right next to the rugged and dramatic Saas-Fee gorge, through which the Feeru Vispa glacial stream flows. Hotel La Gorge offers comfortable, modern accommodation and a delightful dining experience at its restaurant, Zer Schlucht, serving regional and seasonal cuisine in a charming Alpine setting. The mouthwatering options on the menu include classics such as ossobuco, specialties such as Thurgau apple-pomace fed pork with apricot, chanterelles, rosemary and spaetzle, as well as vegan dishes such as gnocchi, mushrooms, chard and pine nuts. Request a table by the floor-to-ceiling windows for stunning views of the gorge and forest. Shorter menu available at lunchtime.	lehmannlucian	\N	\N
3333441513	Dal Mulin	Plazza dal Mulin 4	Switzerland	Saint Moritz	Interesting wine list	https://www.dalmulin.ch/de/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Modern Cuisine	3.0	€€€	t	t	This restaurant in the heart of St Moritz makes diners feel very much at home with its wonderfully stylish and modern take on rustic decor and its charming and attentive front-of-house team. As for the food, it is pleasingly uncomplicated, yet carefully considered and subtle. The wine selection is outstanding – and they even have their own wine shop.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3339199862	Candela	Sonnenstrasse 5	Switzerland	Sankt Gallen	Air conditioning,Terrace	https://restaurantcandela.ch/	Nessun premio	International	3.0	€€	f	t	This pleasantly lively place is located right in the city centre. With high ceilings, dark wood panelling, exposed brickwork and large windows, the restaurant is really atmospheric. As well as Swiss classics, the menu includes Mediterranean fare. There is also a decent selection of vegetarian and vegan dishes. Tip: Take the time to peruse the digestif list.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3337702874	Netts Schützengarten	Sankt Jakob Strasse 35	Switzerland	Sankt Gallen	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.netts.ch/	Nessun premio	International, Country cooking	5.0	€€	t	f	Housed in the Schützengarten Brewery building, this trendy restaurant is popular, not least among the locals! The decor here is lovely – rather rustic at the front, more elegant in the area to the rear. The terrace and beer garden are delightfully secluded – the brewing happens next door, so you're often greeted by pleasant malty aroma. Along with Swiss classics such as Züricher Geschnetzeltes (sliced veal served in a cream and mushroom sauce) or beef Stroganoff, the menu includes Asian-inspired dishes and vegetarian options. Tip: In the courtyard, the brewery has a small bottle museum – well worth a short detour.	marianiadrian	\N	\N
3333517496	Alpenblick	Melchtalerstrasse 40	Switzerland	Sankt Niklausen	Car park,Great view,Terrace	https://www.restaurantalpenblick.ch	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	f	The Anderhalden family have remodelled this inn set in a rather remote location. Diners now take their seats in the restaurant-cum-parlour – the lounge area with its fireplace is ideal for an aperitif – or in the cosy Stübli with its beautiful wooden floor and elegant table settings. The chef-patron cooks up flavourful seasonal dishes^ service comes courtesy of the attentive lady of the house, who is always on hand.	gentilenoah	\N	\N
3334684671	Café de Peney	Route d'Aïre-La-Ville 130	Switzerland	Satigny	Terrace	https://www.cafe-de-peney.ch/	Nessun premio	French, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	Located on an arm of the River Rhône, this popular, bustling eatery, decked out in a profusion of nostalgic paraphernalia, calls to mind a vintage picture postcard and also boasts a wisteria-covered terrace. Fine ingredients are consummately and delicately crafted into delicious dishes, examples of which are the flawlessly cooked Black Angus steak or raspberry tartlet with a refreshing raspberry sorbet.	gattimauro	\N	\N
3332731372	Alpenblick - Swiss Bistro	Oberdorfstrasse 3	Switzerland	Wilderswil	Car park,Terrace	https://www.hotel-alpenblick.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, Swiss	5.0	€€	t	t	Bistro makes for a pleasant alternative to Gourmetstübli in the Alpenblick hotel. Diners soak up the cosy atmosphere as they tuck into the excellent food served here. On the menu: delicious regional and seasonal dishes as well as classics such as Kalbfleisch-Geschnetzeltes (slices of Simmental veal in a creamy sauce) and cheese fondue. And be sure to try the rösti! On Tuesday evenings the restaurant hosts a meat fondue buffet.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3338671153	D'Chuchi	Brunnengasse 3	Switzerland	Schaffhausen		https://www.dchuchi.ch/de/	Nessun premio	Modern Cuisine, Farm to table	4.0	€€	t	f	This small restaurant in a side street in the old town has a charming, down-to-earth and almost intimate atmosphere. It also serves really good food, which owner Jan Schmidlin creates by drawing almost exclusively on regional produce. Shining examples of his delicious modern seasonal fare include veal – saddle, Bäggli, Schupfnudeln (potato dumplings), lettuce, tarragon. There is a four-course set menu and an à la carte selection of dishes. You can also look forward to extremely pleasant, cordial hospitality.	lebedevhazel	\N	\N
3339070950	Schüpbärg-Beizli	Schüpberg 134	Switzerland	Schüpfen	Car park,Terrace	https://www.beizli.ch/	Nessun premio	Swiss, Regional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	This restaurant is quite out of the way, but it's worth the journey here to this remote location, where a cosy, rustic-style interior awaits diners, as well as a lovely terrace, which is very popular in summer! But let's not forget the cooking of owner Christoph Hunziker: he prepares home-style Swiss dishes with a modern twist, stamped with his own ideas. In addition to this, you can expect charming service – sometimes the chefs, too, come to the tables.	egorovzoe	\N	\N
3330136324	Pensiun Aldier	Plaz 154	Switzerland	Sent	Car park,Terrace	https://www.aldier.ch	Nessun premio	Swiss	3.0	€€	f	f	If you like your food straightforward and pared down to the essentials without compromising on taste, then you'll love the excellent Engadine cuisine here. In the pleasingly unpretentious restaurant of the charming little hotel of the same name, the dishes forgo any frills and instead focus on select, fresh local produce. Good wines at fair prices. Shorter menu at lunchtime.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3331298874	SALZHAUS	Landhausquai 15a	Switzerland	Solothurn	Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.restaurant-salzhaus.ch/	Nessun premio	Contemporary, International	3.0	€€	t	t	An attractive blend of urban cool and historical ambiance is the backdrop here and the exposed old brickwork certainly adds to the effect! On regular evenings, the kitchen serves up regionally inspired dishes with an international twist, either as a set menu or à la carte. The chicken cordon bleu with ham, Gruyère, Schupfnudeln (finger-shaped potato dumplings) and spring vegetables is an especially delicious example. Thursday evenings are dedicated to Japanese fusion cuisine. More limited options at lunchtime. Attentive, charming and adept service. Thanks to the beautiful old town location right by the Aare River, tables on the waterfront terrace are coveted in summer.	schmittelisa	\N	\N
3336683516	Zum Alten Stephan	Friedhofplatz 10	Switzerland	Solothurn	Interesting wine list,Terrace	https://www.alterstephan.ch/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	t	This restaurant in the middle of the old town is not only steeped in history, it is also a treat for epicureans. Top-notch, down-to-earth cooking, staff who go the extra mile and a buzzing atmosphere make for a perfect dining experience. While Tamara Bader heads up the service team with effortless charm, her husband Stefan whips us delectable dishes rooted in classic tradition. Think pan-fried sweetbreads with mashed potato, spring vegetables and a morel sauce. House classics such as the cordon bleu are also in high demand. The impressive wine list is dedicated to Swiss, French and Italian labels. Delightful terrace in front of the building.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3330906582	Gasthof zur Sonne	Seestrasse 37	Switzerland	Stäfa	Terrace	https://www.sonnestaefa.ch/	Nessun premio	Swiss, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	t	This 500-year-old heritage-protected inn is run by Patricia and Cäsar Meyer, who represent the second generation of their family here. He has a penchant for fish caught in Lake Zurich, just a stone's throw away – you can't get any fresher or more regional than that! The menu includes some truly rare specialities such as fried livers of fish from Lake Zurich. This attachment to regional produce is, not least, indicative of a commitment to sustainability. The cosy, very well-kept dining rooms are on the first floor, along with the gorgeous balcony terrace, which affords an unobstructed view of the lake. The staff are very attentive and cordial – you're sure to want to come back! Comfortable guestrooms.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3338914908	Panorama - Bistro	Hartlisbergstrasse 39	Switzerland	Steffisburg	Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.panorama-hartlisberg.ch/	Nessun premio	Traditional Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	t	This attractive alternative to the Cayenne offers excellent cuisine at a very reasonable price. Although the dishes are simpler in style, they are prepared with equal sophistication using quality regional produce, always with a certain modern twist. Attentive service, plus the same wine list as in the Cayenne. Wonderful views!	tudoroh	\N	\N
3335822750	Alla Cantina	Piazza Gottardo Zurini 3	Switzerland	Tegna	Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	http://www.ristoranteallacantina.com	Nessun premio	Sicilian, Classic Cuisine	3.0	€€	t	f	Although all the staff at this beautiful historic restaurant on the village square hail from Sicily, they have been working in Switzerland for years. Here, authentic Sicilian cuisine is served in a rustic and welcoming setting that also provides the backdrop for regular music events: the only concessions to Ticino are the polenta-based dishes. Our inspector particularly recommends the sarde in “Beccafico”(stuffed sardine roulade with breadcrumbs, sultanas, pine nuts and orange peel). There’s also a pleasantly cool and tranquil outdoor space for summer dining, plus four attractive and inviting guestrooms on the top floor.	alfieriigor	\N	\N
3334465670	Anker	Dorf 10	Switzerland	Teufen	Air conditioning,Car park	https://anker-teufen.ch/	Nessun premio	International, Traditional Cuisine	3.0	€€	f	t	On the first floor, wood panelling and low ceilings provide a cosy setting in which to choose the appealing mix of traditional and international dishes on the menu. The calves’ liver with sage, onions and rösti, for example, is delicious. A significant amount of the restaurant’s meat comes from its own butchery.	molnarbianca	\N	\N
3332449009	Blume	Freudwilerstrasse 6	Switzerland	Uster	Car park,Terrace	https://www.blumefreudwil.ch/	Nessun premio	Swiss, Farm to table	3.0	€€	f	f	At this pleasant restaurant, heart and skill go into rustling up regional cuisine made with top-notch ingredients. Risotto is one of the chef's specialties, but they also serve offal, such as tripe or liver. The spit-roast skewers flambéed at your table and the Chateaubriand have to be ordered in advance and are served to the whole table. The rustic downstairs space is an appealing backdrop for your meal^ the upstairs room is a little more elegant. With her friendly, outgoing manner, the owner adds a personal touch to the service. The beautiful quiet location is rural yet still close to Zurich.	wagnerpaul	\N	\N
3339917922	Shanghai Food (Nantun)	537	Taiwan	Taichung	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Dim Sum	5.0	$	f	f	A Chinese herbalist by training, the owner hails from Shanghai and was spoilt by his grandpa who made him all sorts of treats. After he moved to Taiwan, he spent three years trying to recreate the most authentic pan-fried buns from memory and opened this shop in 2009. The pork buns boast soupy filling with the perfect ratio of fatty and lean meat. The veggie buns are light and flavourful, filled with bok choy, dried tofu and mushrooms.	tarasovangela	\N	\N
3337794477	Landgasthof Ochsen	Dorfplatz 56	Switzerland	Wölflinswil	Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://ochsen-woelflinswil.ch/wp/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine	5.0	€€	t	f	The food is terrific in this inn dating back to 1288 – the skilful chef clearly pours a lot of love into his cooking. As well as regional dishes and classics, Asian and Mediterranean influences also make their way onto the menu. A meal in their Gaststube is a somewhat simpler affair. There is a lovely terrace overlooking the pond, plus a charming smoking lounge. Pleasant and handy guestrooms.	schr�derfedericha	\N	\N
3336716137	Bazaar	Riedweg 156	Switzerland	Zermatt	Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://cervo.swiss/de/restaurants-bars/bazaar	Nessun premio	International, Asian	4.0	€€	f	f	At this restaurant in the chic Alpine CERVO Mountain Resort – which commands a great panoramic view – you are whisked away to an exotic and predominantly vegetarian world of flavours, ranging from Arabic to Chinese specialities, from Lebanese flatbread (manakish) and pistachio baklava to dim sum and much more. In keeping with its name, this place has a lively and friendly atmosphere, to which original and highly disparate decorative details also contribute.	locatelliflorian	\N	\N
3339967233	Zum Kaiser Franz	Vorstadt 8	Switzerland	Zug	Terrace	https://www.kaiser-franz.ch/	Nessun premio	Austrian, Seasonal Cuisine	5.0	€€	f	t	Here, you won't want to miss out on the Austrian specialities such as Backhenderl (breaded fried chicken), Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) or Topfenknödel (curd dumplings)! Available in a large or small portion, the Wiener schnitzel is a real highlight. Be sure to ask about the fish of the day, freshly caught from the adjacent Lake Zug. As well as the good food, diners can look forward to professional and attentive service in a cosy and stylish setting – the Austrian charm of the decor is the perfect match for the cuisine. The lakeside location provides a lovely backdrop. The nearby multi-storey car park is handy.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3334617891	Rathauskeller Bistro	Ober-Altstadt 1	Switzerland	Zug	Terrace	https://www.rathauskeller.ch/	Nessun premio	Classic Cuisine	4.0	€€	f	f	The friendly service and relaxed atmosphere here are popular with locals and tourists alike. Diners can choose from the selection of classics such as cordon bleu, Lammhacktätschli (lamb patties) and beef roulades, and there is also a seasonal menu. The tables on the gorgeous terrace in front of the building in the cobbled pedestrian zone are coveted. Tip: Just a stone's throw away, the lakeside is perfect for a stroll.	shirocky	\N	\N
3336129151	Bauernschänke	Rindermarkt 24	Switzerland	Zurich	Terrace	https://www.bauernschaenke.ch/	Nessun premio	Country cooking, International	5.0	€€	f	f	This gem of a restaurant is somewhat tucked away in a narrow alley in the city centre. In a historical setting with a cosy, rustic feel, diners tuck into international dishes such as king mackerel with radicchio tardivo, coconut and calamansi, as well as regional specialities such as pork belly gröstel (a traditional Tyrolean potato-based fry-up) with cucumber and butterhead lettuce. Order dishes to share à la carte or take a punt on the five-course surprise menu. The staff will be happy to provide wine recommendations. The well-curated selection is international and includes a decent range of natural wines (unfiltered and sulfite-free). Options are somewhat reduced at lunchtime.	de angelislucas	\N	\N
3338343067	Josef	Gasometerstrasse 24	Switzerland	Zurich	Interesting wine list,Terrace	http://www.josef.ch	Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	€€	f	f	This trendy, urban restaurant and bar is located in the middle of a residential area in Kreis 5 (Zürich's fifth district). The atmosphere is lively and bustling, and in light of their interesting concept, it comes as no surprise that the place is well frequented: they serve tasty modern European cuisine with dishes in starter-sized portions (four is a good number to order). Mouthwatering options include the likes of veal shank ragout with mashed potatoes, confit garlic and Trevisano. Alternatively, there is a five-course set menu – available in omnivore and vegetarian versions. Good wine list and cocktail selection.	monticristian	\N	\N
3334167123	Didi's Frieden	Stampfenbachstrasse 32	Switzerland	Zurich	Terrace	https://www.didisfrieden.ch/	Nessun premio	Farm to table, Classic Cuisine	5.0	€€€	f	f	A fun dining experience is guaranteed at this delightful restaurant with its inviting decor – the wine glass chandeliers are certainly original! In the evening, there is a set menu comprising three, four or five courses. For each course, you have delicious options such as sea bass fillet on spaghetti alla chitarra with summer vegetables and octopus in a saffron sauce. There is a daily set menu at lunchtime, plus a nicely curated wine list. In summer, the gorgeous spacious terrace beckons.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
3333077218	La Bottega di Mario	Nüschelerstrasse 6	Switzerland	Zurich	Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access	https://www.labottegadimario.ch/	Nessun premio	Italian	3.0	€€	f	t	Housed in a historical building (1913), La Bottega is a wonderfully inviting and lively ristorante and salumeria under one roof. Guests are spoilt for choice between the tasty dishes, clearly influenced by Ticino tradition, and the superb selection of salami and ham at the counter – here, the friendly mastri salumieri serve up the cold cuts. Tip: Try the house wine, Merlot di Ticino, poured from a six-litre bottle!	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3338166149	Barranco	Sihlfeldstrasse 141	Switzerland	Zurich	Terrace	https://www.barranco.ch/	Nessun premio	Peruvian	3.0	€€	f	f	Eat, drink, make merry, meet friends… the Kreis 4 district is to Zurich what the Barranco district is to Lima. Nestled among a host of other restaurants and bars, the Peruvian neighbourhood's namesake serves modern Peruvian cuisine that is bursting with flavour, zing and spices. The dishes are designed to be shared and tasted together. The atmosphere is pleasingly unpretentious in this inviting space with a trendy decor featuring Peruvian murals – the relaxed yet efficient service is the icing on the cake. Great cocktail selection. There is a terrace in front of the building, separated from the pavement by plants.	bertinimilan	\N	\N
3338745736	Apis Grill	80 Baoyang East Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Barbecue	4.0	$$	f	f	Tucked away down an alley with no visible signage apart from a triangle, diners are greeted by the awe-inspiring sight of a giant longan wood-fired kiln and rows of charcoal grills behind the counter. The veteran head chef is keen on straight-forward, back-to-basics cooking, in which meat, fish and veggies are grilled over a wood fire. The menu changes every few weeks, but New Zealand venison is a firm fixture. Order the abalone if available.	smirnovjessica	\N	\N
3337963669	Yang Bao Bao (Chaoming Road)	106 Chaoming Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only	http://yangbaobaotw.com	Nessun premio	Dumplings	5.0	$	f	f	In 1993, this dumpling shop began life as a street stall in a local market. Now it has become a household name throughout south Taiwan. Apart from steamed pork and beef dumplings, the variety filled with assorted vegetables also stands out – its plump, full skin enrobes a filling of shredded wood ear fungus, green bok choy, glass noodles and dried tofu. Pancake rolls that are crispy and nicely browned are also popular.	balazsaurora	\N	\N
3336612112	Bei Gang Tsai Rice Tube (Yancheng)	166 Hesi Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	t	f	This third-generation family business dates back to 1956 and many Kaohsiungese grew up with its ‘tube’ sticky rice, which is actually steamed with braised ground pork in a metal tub, turned out on a plate and topped with gravy. Do order a soy-marinated ‘iron egg’ on the side to go with the rice. There are also several soups on the menu, including steamed egg custard soup – the sponge-like custard sucks up the flavourful stock nicely.	horvathmaria	\N	\N
3333792814	Caizong Li	159 Chenggong 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	t	t	The shop may have little ambiance to speak of, but it’s brightly lit and always spotless. Since its founding over 60 years ago, it has focused on two items only – peanut zongzi and kelp miso soup. The kitchen team at the back is always busy wrapping the signature sticky rice dumplings in bamboo leaves, to be steamed and topped with sauces and ground peanuts before served. Consider taking home some frozen zongzi, especially around Dragon Boat Festival.	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3338022983	Cheng Tsung Duck Rice	245 Yucheng Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	$	f	t	This simple shop is always jam-packed with customers. Its signature is undoubtedly the eponymous duck rice – smoked duck pieces on steamed rice drizzled with a secret sauce. Another speciality, hand-sliced duck leg rice, is available in limited quantity, boasting smoky and juicy flesh. And of course, the duck also goes well with the array of noodles on offer. Try assorted duck offal soup, and side dishes made with bean sprouts.	nagyemma	\N	\N
3335874744	Chun Lan Gua Bao	5 Fusing 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	$	f	t	Since 2000, this shop has been famous for its oversize steamed bun sandwiches packed with tasty fillings. The must-try is definitely the assorted gua bao stuffed with crisp pickled cabbage, half-fatty soy-braised pork, ground peanut sugar, and the secret red chilli sauce, all working miraculously together. There is even a plant-based version for vegan customers. Healthy drinks such as Job's Tears milk or almond soy milk are also on hand to quench your thirst.	demurtasarianna	\N	\N
3331240438	Cianjin Braised Pork Rice	26 Datong Street 2nd Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	$	t	t	This third-generation family business dates back to 1959 and its signature braised pork rice has been the favourite breakfast for generations of Kaohsiungese. Only the back cut is used, with pork skin and a layer of fat that give the dish a complex depth. Feel free to order shredded pork, dried fish floss, marinated tofu, or even a soft-boiled duck egg to go with the rice. It’s always busy and may close early when all food has sold out.	pisanipiso	\N	\N
3334288335	Ciao Zai Tou Huang's Braised Pork Rice (Ciaotou)	106 Ciaonan Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	f	f	Ciaotou was the centre of Taiwan’s sugar production and this 6-decade-old joint fascinates its fans with terrific braised pork rice boasting a savoury-sweet taste. Pork shoulder and belly in a specific ratio are hand-diced and braised till melting before being drizzled over steamed rice. Pork thick soup, and assorted pork offal make perfect companions with the signature rice. Expect to queue any time of the day. It closes on major holidays.	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3332452859	Hou Chi Duck Rice	201 Zihciang 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	$	t	f	For over 40 years, Hou Chi has been attracting a loyal following with its tasty duck dishes. Its famously nourishing dang gui duck soup exudes deep herbal aromas^ order it with noodles to make a complete meal. The signature duck rice comes with thickly sliced duck and pickled radish. Order an extra platter of smoked or braised duck if you fancy more protein. You can even specify which cuts you prefer.	serafinidmitri	\N	\N
3332344633	Hsiu Ming	41 Yongping Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	f	t	Installed next to Cishan Old Street since 1986, this neat little shop has stood the test of time. Pork offal can be paired with egg noodles, glass noodles or steamed rice. The fleshy and springy pork tongue is the popular dish – best enjoyed with a dab of grated garlic for a kick. Braised ground pork rice topped with a sunny-side-up egg is also a must: pierce the yolk so it runs down over the rice for a mouthful of tasty goodness.	morettipaolo	\N	\N
3332111947	Hung Chi Rice Shop	96 Liwun Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	$	t	f	As opposed to typical braised pork rice shops that can sometimes feel a little dated, this one boasts a bright, simple interior with full-length windows. The cartoon pig logo also makes it appealing to a younger audience. Despite its fresh look, the menu focusses on good old Taiwanese favourites. Braised pork rice is a must, and you have the option to top it with an over-easy egg. Do also order sides like braised cabbage, and pork tendon.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3330117239	Lao Ye Mei Shi Guan (Fengshan)	54-56 Haiyang 1st Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	$	f	f	The restaurant has been a landmark of Fengshan’s culinary scene for almost two decades. Its speciality, smoked duck glazed in cane sugar, is a masterclass of flavour and is particularly juicy and tender thanks to the duck breed from China. Pan-fried pork belly with lemongrass is another hit, featuring freshly slaughtered local pork and sustainably grown lemongrass from the owner’s farm, without forgetting the fish soup that cooks for four hours.	casiniivan	\N	\N
3336319010	Liang Chia Pig Knuckle	229 Yangming Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only	https://restaurant-1127845.business.site/?utm_source=gmb&utm_medium=referral	Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	$	f	f	For 20+ years, locals have been swooning over the pork knuckle rice here – ham hock braised in a marinade with spices and Chinese herbs, served with a glistening amber sauce^ the peppery aftertaste is spellbinding. Steamed rice from Hualian and a julienne of crispy bamboo shoots cut through the richness. Marine fish cooked to order are also a firm favourite. Noodle lovers can't get enough of the umami-laden pork bone broth lifted by veggie sweetness.	rossigiovanni	\N	\N
3337623785	Liao Chi Migao	119 Ciaonan Road	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	t	t	This no-frills shop near the train station has been famous for their migao, or rice cake, since 1955. Glutinous rice mixed with dried shrimps and shallot is steamed in ceramic ramekins as opposed to bamboo tubes. The rice cake is then turned out onto a serving plate, drizzled with braised pork sauce, topped with pork floss and pickled cucumber. Pair it with the herbal soup known as si shen tang, or pork intestine vermicelli soup as accompaniment.	zaitsevvictoria	\N	\N
3331920938	Tang Jai Yang (Bang Kho Laem)	171 Chan Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿	t	f	Tang Jai Yang’s chef started cooking char siu, or Cantonese-style barbecue pork, for family and friends before selling it online. There, it went viral, so he opened this understated place. Since almost every dish on the menu contains the succulent pork, you can’t really go wrong.	lazarmaya	\N	\N
3335671230	Mi Yuan Tzu Steamed Glutinous Rice	30 Nanhai Street	Taiwan	Kaohsiung	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	$	f	t	After selling sticky rice in a market for 10-plus years, the owner couple opened this shop in 2021. Tables are set on a plant-adorned porch with tiled floor and walls^ the cartoon duck and handwritten logo create a strong visual identity. The signature boneless duck sticky rice entices with its sesame oil and ginger aromas, while taro pork rib soup boasts starchy tuber infused with meaty flavours. Honey black tea from Taitung makes the perfect pairing.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
