3330777810	Baannai	102/13 Soi Kamphaeng Phet 5	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace,Valet parking	https://www.baannaihotel.com/dining	Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Baan Nai, or ‘inner house’ in Thai, is so called because the owner’s great grandfather built it on the innermost part of his land. The house, and recipes cooked by its occupants, have passed down through the family to the present day where, as a boutique hotel and homely restaurant, it serves delicious time-tested dishes like Taengmo Pla Haeng (watermelon with dried fish flakes) and Khanom Phra Phai (sweet mung bean dumplings). Group booking is required.	brandtclara	\N	\N
3336996213	Burapa	26 Soi Sukhumvit 11	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	This Orient Express-themed restaurant aims to take diners on a journey from east to north-east Thailand via flavoursome cooking that joins culinary elements from Isan and the province of Trat. The ground floor is designed to look like a luxury train bar – perfect for enjoying one of their many signature cocktails –  then the 1st and 2nd floors resemble the business and first-class carriages respectively. The well-priced dishes use recipes from the owner’s mother. Booking is essential.	ionescuamy	\N	\N
3338828533	Jeh O	113 Soi Charat Mueang	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	Jeh O might be known for her Mama Noodles Tom Yum, but her menu contains numerous other top-notch dishes. Many, including her delicious fried tofu with crispy garlic, boiled rice with duck, and signature crispy pork, are popular Thai favourites. Though the staff only speaks Thai, there’s an English picture menu for non-Thai speakers. Outside the shop, an eager crowd waits up to two hours for tables^ to get in faster, arrive just before opening or near closing.	fabbrijuan	\N	\N
3331548789	Krua Apsorn (Dusit)	503-505 Sam Sen Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	This family-run stall is inevitably a hit with anyone who eats here, including patrons such as the Thai royal family. The simplicity of the exterior belies the gem of a Thai kitchen hidden inside. Some dishes are unique and feature the family's secret recipes. The stir-fried pork with bird's-eye chilli is tender and bursting with herbal aromas. The signature yellow curry with large prawns and crispy lotus root strikes the perfect blend of sour, spicy and sweet.	cartasilvia	\N	\N
3331416355	Plu	3 Soi Phra Phinit	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	The Water Library’s Plu offers outstanding food, a cosy ambience, and great service in an Art Deco-adorned colonial house. Among the beautifully presented authentic pan-Thailand dishes is the signature braised pork belly and soft-boiled eggs in five-spiced soup^ the pork belly is tender and juicy, the deep-fried tofu absorbs the aromatic broth, and the soft-boiled eggs only enhance the flavour and texture. Start with one of the restaurant’s signature cocktails.	battagliadaniela	\N	\N
3335747355	Prik-Yuak	108 Pradiphat Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Prik-Yuak has flourished for 30 years, starting in the bustling Chatuchak markets and now stationed in a spacious, inviting location. The restaurant maintains its beloved approach to home-style Thai cooking. Signature dishes like the Southern Thai pork belly and egg stew showcase tender meat, boiled eggs, and tofu. The venue charms with light, earth-toned decor, a serene garden, and includes a café and boutique shop to enhance the dining experience.	sch�fervalentina	\N	\N
3339873311	Samlor	1076 Charoen Krung Road	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	t	Samlor means ‘tricycle’ in Thai and a traditional one hangs outside this cosy restaurant. Inside the loft-style space, chef Napol creates flavoursome, well-presented elevated Thai cuisine inspired by local street food with specially selected ingredients. They also have an à la carte menu, which includes a cut and catch of the day. Guests need to check with the chef what is available.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
3338279307	Thai Niyom	Mahatun Plaza	Thailand	Bangkok	Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Hidden in the shadow of skyscrapers is this gem of a restaurant, which got its start serving family recipes, but now offers an array of Thai cuisine from Chiang Mai to Hat Yai. It is a great place to sample delicious Thai cooking from every region on the same table. Quality ingredients are sourced locally and turned into dishes like the recommended Phuket stir-fried pork belly with shrimp paste and the Chiang Mai Combo, a Northern Thai-style appetiser plate.	kellercosmin	\N	\N
