3338680561	Khao Soi Mae Sai	29/1 Ratchaphruek Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	f	f	This shop serves the famous Khao Soi, featuring rich and slightly spicy curry notes. You can choose your preferred meat toppings, and the portions are so delicate that you might find yourself wanting another round!	rivaalexei	\N	\N
3332692338	Busarin Cuisine	133 Rattanakosin Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Cash only		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	Busarin, the new sister restaurant of Magnolia Café, has high ceilings, a collection of chinaware and leather green sofa booths that contrast with the light pink walls. When you dine here, it’s like being welcomed into Chef Noi’s home. They serve northern-Thai based on family recipes with noodles and roti instead of rice. The standout is a streaky pork that’s braised in a hung lay curry for two days and emits a powerful aroma of ginger and spices.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3336773798	Huan Soontaree	208 Pa Tan Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	t	Soontaree Vechanont doesn’t just own “Soontaree’s House” – the singer also performs here nightly. Set on the Ping River in an open-air, Lanna-style building with more tables outside, this charming restaurant can accommodate up to 350 guests. Among the Northern Thai cooking they serve is their signature boneless murrel fish stuffed with pork. It’s a creative dish, with the well-seasoned sausage proving suitably fragrant and spicy.	vecchimirko	\N	\N
3338900843	Huen Muan Jai	24 Ratchaphruek Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park	https://www.huenmuanjai2554.com	Nessun premio	Northern Thai	4.0	฿	t	f	Headed up by former TV chef Charan Thipeung, this restaurant – whose name means ‘happy home’ – has been serving authentic Northern Thai food since 2011. Set in a Lanna house with a tree-lined garden, it’s a popular, wallet-friendly destination that offers hard-to-find traditional dishes alongside classic favourites. The uniquely flavoured spicy minced fish salad is highly recommended and if you’re unfamiliar with the cuisine, start with the excellent Northern appetiser sampler.	berninialex	\N	\N
3331249543	Krua Lawng Khao	18 Mu 2	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park		Nessun premio	Northern Thai	3.0	฿	t	f	Food and atmosphere are well-matched at this chill Northern Thai restaurant in Mae Rim. It’s in a two-storey wooden pavilion with regular tables downstairs and cushioned floor seating upstairs^ both options offer relaxing rice field views and refreshing breezes. The food here is equally fresh, as well as flavourful and easy on the wallet^ the Northern Thai spicy pork salad and the Northern Thai hot and spicy soup with fish and morning glory are recommended.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3333828232	Dan Chicken Rice (San Sai)	45 Mu 3	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	฿	f	f	For over 20 years this local favourite has been serving tasty, wallet-friendly chicken rice, first in Sam-Yaek Market in San Sai and now at this larger branch on Old San Sai Road. Show up early, both to beat the crowds and because the food invariably runs out before closing time.	fiorentinolukas	\N	\N
3337674662	Go Neng (Wichayanon)	77 Wichayanon Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	f	f	Go Neng has been serving deep-fried dough sticks for almost four decades. No matter what shape they take – crocodile, dinosaur, dragon or elephant – each one boasts the same puffy perfection and crispy texture. Other bites, such as the deep-fried bun and fried whole-wheat dough are also great.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3334469789	Lung Khajohn Wat Ket	Opposite to Wat Ket Karam	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	f	t	For decades, this place has been serving distinctive Khao Kriab Pak Moh, or steamed rice skin dumplings, opposite Wat Ket Karam. These contain a tasty salty-sweet filling wrapped in a coconut-infused rice flour sheet and a side of coconut cream. Tapioca balls with sweet pork are also offered.	siliprandipiergiorgiofranco	\N	\N
3335500479	Roti Pa Day	In front of Wat Mahawan	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	฿	f	f	First-timers should order the plain crispy roti with condensed milk to start. The roti dough here is uniquely made without eggs, but slowly cooked to a crispy-chewy perfection in coconut oil. Choose from 20 toppings.	kuznetsovella	\N	\N
3336262578	Sanpakoi Kanomjeen	Thongkam Market	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	t	t	Established in 1977 and a local favourite at Thongkam Market, this spot offers tasty and affordable Kanomjeen (fresh rice vermicelli) with various curries. Try the Nam-Lo, a mix of spicy pork and chicken curry sauces. If noodles aren’t your thing, swap them for rice. Not only are the street food dishes here delicious, but they’re great value too – especially when you consider that side vegetables are unlimited.	stannaomi	\N	\N
3335886802	Ekachan	95 Chang Khlan	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	This new restaurant in the heart of old Chiang Mai is run by a local chef who embraces the slow food concept, using ingredients from around the country. The fried rice with sweet shrimp is nicely cooked with sweet shrimp paste and tasty condiments, including fresh chilli, shallots and mango. The spicy beef turmeric curry is a standout, with an intense mix of herbs and spices. If you’re looking for the spice bomb, they can add fresh Thai chillies.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3337626018	Magnolia Café	131/70	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	With just four large communal tables, Magnolia is a simple, cosy spot enlivened by bold colours, vintage décor, and chandeliers. Their à la carte menu offers tasty, well presented fare from across Thailand. Dishes are distinguished by vivid, gutsy flavours^ fried sun-dried squid with peanut sauce and fresh watermelon with desiccated salmon are exemplars. In lieu of a dessert menu, they serve lovely complimentary pandan pudding. Do visit their wine shop next door.	colombostefano	\N	\N
3333578417	Meena	13/5 Mu 2	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Don’t be alarmed when you pass through a rice field driving here, as this hidden gem is worth it. As its name suggests, this alfresco restaurant specialises in rice, alongside new spins on Thai classics. Most are garnished with fruits and edible flowers, giving them bursts of colour. Along with the five-colour rice balls, northern-style spicy minced fish salad is a delight. Vegans will enjoy their many options, including the spicy stir-fried eryngii mushrooms.	ozmax	\N	\N
3330870145	Na Chantra	Chantra Khiri Hotel	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace	https://www.chantrakhirichalet.com	Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	Set up in the hills inside the Chantra Khiri Hotel, Na Chantra offers gorgeous views of the national park and a menu that features central and northern Thai dishes. Vegetables and herbs come from their next-door farm and everything else – like the savoury northern sausage with chilli paste – is made from scratch. Don’t miss their signature minced pork with fresh veg and spicy sauce, or the piquant yellow curry soup with sea bass. Start your evening outside, with a seat by the infinity pool.	fabbromikhail	\N	\N
3330658046	Saiyut and Doctor Sai Kitchen	32 Chotana Road Soi 12	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	t	Since 2004, Doctor Sai has been serving pan-Thai dishes, including royal fare, following recipes from her mother, Saiyud, a former cooking instructor, in a setting reminiscent of dining at home. Start with an elegant appetiser like fried prawns and peanuts in an egg net, flower dumplings, or deep-fried pork wrapped in egg noodles. By dessert – try the sweet potato in syrup – you’ll guess this home, with its warm service, belongs to a royal from a bygone era.	bauergiulia	\N	\N
3339575552	Sanae	64/1 Wangsingkham Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿	t	f	This halal kitchen next to the Ping River is one for beef fans. With indoor and outdoor dining, the big outdoor kitchen cooks a creative à la carte menu with balanced flavours. The beef fat rice topped with egg yolk has a smoky flavour. The spicy Thai soup with beef shank is packed with spice aroma.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3335709919	Tune In Garden	139 Mu 3	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	This restaurant is owned by the late National Artist of Thailand and his wife. She cooks delicious homestyle fare drawn from a cookbook she wrote based on her mother-in-law’s recipes. First-timers are served a fixed-price menu^ returners can order from the cookbook. Roasted pork ribs with cabbage and fermented pork with fermented bean curd relish stand out. Booking is required.	petrovmelissa	\N	\N
3337438818	Rasik Local Kitchen	44/3 Sridonchai Road	Thailand	Chiang Mai	Air conditioning		Nessun premio	Thai contemporary	5.0	฿฿	f	f	This chef's table experience showcases seasonal flavours and beloved Thai classics. The talented chef interacts with guests from the open kitchen and uses traditional cooking methods, such as a charcoal stove, to add depth to the dishes. The mild red curry with grilled pork and damask rose looks simple but the authentic taste of homemade Thai curry paste hides inside. The sliced pork is tender and the curry texture is smooth with a rich but balanced flavour.	volkovnatalie	\N	\N
3338620766	La Voi	324/61 Chaiyaphruek Road	Thailand	Chon Buri			Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	฿	t	f	The owner uses premium beef to prepare the broth and toppings. The clear and amber soup, which is cooked with beef for hours, is their secret sauce. For newcomers, it is highly recommended to start with the mixed beef soup, which comes with a variety of beef toppings, including meatballs, different cuts of beef, and beef organs, allowing diners to enjoy all the textures and flavours of beef.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3330188947	Khao Lam Mae Khai Toon Klao	357 Sukhumvit Road	Thailand	Chon Buri	Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	f	f	For over 60 years, this dessert stall has served classic sweetened sticky rice in the traditional way – cooked in bamboo with fresh coconut milk. Choose from original white or aromatic black sticky rice, garnished with taro, black beans, or ginkgo nuts^ available in three portion sizes.	marinescumario	\N	\N
3338604409	Krua Laew Tae R-Rom	17/62 Mu 6	Thailand	Chon Buri	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿	t	t	With a limited menu, the kitchen excels in seafood, Thai food and home-made curries with bold, rich flavours. The crab, shrimp, clams and fish are served ultra-fresh at reasonable prices, with rare catches often appearing on the menu. The restaurant doesn't open if the line-catch on that day is not successful. Booking a week in advance is necessary.	szabosofia	\N	\N
3331851688	Lung Shall Kitchen	50 Mu 7	Thailand	Chon Buri	Credit cards not accepted		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿	t	t	Simplicity and quality go hand in hand at this hidden gem with an intimate atmosphere. Experience food in its most authentic form thanks to skilfully prepared fresh ingredients. The bold yet nuanced stir-fried black squid ink delivers an intense, textured exploration of the sea's flavours.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3336204378	Pladids	60/57 Mu 4	Thailand	Chon Buri	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	t	This shop serves a Thai samrap (set menu) including jasmine rice cooked with Thai wild almond. The menu has a home-style, local quality, and interesting seasonal options. Each dish boasts complex yet balanced flavours.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3335756907	Kai Yang Rabeab (Khao Suan Kwang)	99 Mittraphap Road	Thailand	Khon Kaen	Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	5.0	฿	t	f	Throw a stick in Khon Kaen and you’ll likely hit a street food place serving grilled chicken and Isan dishes. You’d be lucky if you landed on this one. Its secret is tender, juicy chicken from three local breeds. A second downtown branch offers the same menu minus grilled offal.	m�llercristian	\N	\N
