3333899347	Krua Suwimol	1229 9 Mittraphap Road	Thailand	Nakhon Ratchasima	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿	f	f	This simple, open-air restaurant serves Thai-Chinese fare. The food is distinctive for its simply cooking techniques yet quality dishes with extra-fresh ingredients and intense flavours. They offer a fantastic range, including several seafood and made-to-order options. Deep-fried chicken thigh with fish sauce and stir-fried spicy seafood are recommended.	puglieseadam	\N	\N
3332780620	Chai	4 Soi Samakkhi 38	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Fuss-free food, live seafood in tanks cooked to order and a speedy service have earned Chai Phochana its loyal following. The stir-fried squid comes with a rich, creamy salted egg yolk and spring onions. The spicy sour soup with giant catfish roes and vegetables is also tasty. Open till late, for night owls with a hunger pang, this is the place for you.	tohnjohn	\N	\N
3334514246	Chang-Wang-Imm	44 Mu 4	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Down by the banks of the Chao Phraya, enjoy affordable yet tasty Thai cuisine with relaxing river views from a charming 1950s house. Everything here is vintage, from the old-fashioned décor to the classic cooking techniques and flavours. The traditional Thai curry with pork, shrimp paste and basil is highly recommended. Book table #52 for remarkable private views from the upper deck. Live music adds to the ambience at the weekend.	pierimarco	\N	\N
3339964124	Kaeng Pa Loong Sa-Nga	285/162-3 Soi Ngam Wong Wan 23 Lane 11	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Run by the same family for over 20 years, this restaurant is something of a hidden gem for spice-lovers. Their signature dish, jungle curry soup with hand-minced fish, provides suitably lip-smacking flavours using ingredients like red chilli, fingerroot and turkey berry. An outdoor area embraces nature, with curved tree trunk tables and an arboretum. Herbs and spices from the forest are used as seasoning, often with game meats – the succulent stir-fried deer with cumin leaves is a must.	ttuyungim	\N	\N
3331112919	Hong Seng	280 Mu 2	Thailand	Nonthaburi	Cash only,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿฿	f	t	On the Chao Praya by the Rama IV Bridge, this renowned Thai-Chinese spot has been known for reasonably priced flavoursome fare since 1957. Its open-air dining room and wooden terrace set the stage for relaxed meals featuring highlights like grilled giant river prawns with spicy sauce and mini deep-fried crab meat wrapped in tofu skin. Open for lunch, the place extends its hours on weekends. Reach it by boat, or if driving, park in the public space under the bridge.	vargalucia	\N	\N
3336038090	Khao Mun Gai Nha Jone	119/239 Soi 17	Thailand	Pathum Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	฿	t	t	There's a real buzz about this perpetually busy shop that is worth the drive from Bangkok. The delicious chicken is tender and juicy, served simply with sauces that add a real kick. Opening times are limited as they often sell out within a few hours – a testament to the quality.	landirobert	\N	\N
3333650882	Krua Luang Ten	160 Mu 2	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿	f	t	Krua Luang Ten makes for an unusual setting with its tables arranged on sand-covered floors. Check the whiteboard for the specials, which often feature the catch of the day and seasonal ingredients. The dishes masterfully balance robust Southern Thai flavours for authentic spiciness, and the complimentary vegetables come with tai pla sauce. N.B. The restaurant is closed on the 10th, 20th, and 30th of the month.	cervigaia	\N	\N
3339031186	Mon	46/11-12 Mu 1	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿	t	f	Established for over 35 years, the restaurant has fostered a close connection with local fishermen, ensuring the delivery of a diverse selection of fresh seafood. The open-air main dining area exudes the charm of an old Thai-Chinese eatery. Popular among divers returning from Mu Ko Similan, the intense flavours authentically represent local cuisine, with generously sized dishes. Standouts include the stir-fried crab with lime and the southern curry featuring river snails and wild betel leaves.	palombasauro	\N	\N
3330909166	Roe Dang	55/15 Mu 1	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿	f	t	Basic furnishings and modest dish presentations belie the skill behind their precisely cooked recipes, which are made to order. Specialising in authentic Southern Thai seafood, they source the day's catch for dishes such as red grouper with bitter melon, and simple stir-fried melinjo leaves with fresh prawns. Their home-made curries use local Phang-nga ingredients. The wall of celebrity photos attests to its popularity.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3336650856	Tonfon Bistro	Krabi 1002 Rural Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Since opening its doors in 1995, the chef-owner has consistently cooked flavoursome, well presented southern fare with an emphasis on locally sourced ingredients and authentic recipes. Daily deliveries of fresh seafood and organic produce come from nearby farms. Savour dishes like stir-fried pork with shrimp paste and bitter bean or curry with crab legs and betel leaves. While the menu may be concise, each dish reflects the chef's passion. Indoor and outdoor seating is available.	benedettifilip	\N	\N
3338565851	Khok Kloi Tom Yam Noodles with Eggs	6/10 Phet Kasem Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	฿	t	t	Their fresh tom yum noodles are accompanied by piquant spicy and sour flavours^ dry or in an intense broth. They’re known for impressively sized portions at reasonable prices. The soft minced pork and healthy liver have a beautiful scent of fresh lime juice and chilli in a sweet broth.	neagufilippo	\N	\N
3336785557	Hok Kee Lao	19 Senarat Road	Thailand	Phang-Nga	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese	5.0	฿฿	f	f	For over 40 years, this heritage restaurant has been serving up delicious Thai, Chinese, and Southern flavours. It's an ideal spot for family gatherings, offering a warm and inviting atmosphere. The menu includes Chinese favourites such as nicely moist chicken pae sa flavoured with seasoned soy sauce and paired with morning glory. If you are lucky, try the fried tofu with minced pork and shrimp.	baroneandres	\N	\N
3334599631	Pa Lek Boat Noodles	Bang Lan Road (opposite to Maha That temple)	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	f	t	This third-generation family-run street food joint has been offering tasty boat noodles for over five decades. Their experience shines through in the delicious broth, well-balanced in flavours. Try their pork or beef boat noodles for great value, or consider the recommended dry tom yum-style egg noodles with pork. The friendly owners' hospitality attracts a bustling lunch crowd.	novotnycecilia	\N	\N
3338823519	Pranom Shredded Chicken Noodles (Tha Wasukri)	47/9 Mu 4	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	4.0	฿	f	f	On Ayutthaya-Ang Thong Road, near Wat Phanom Yong, the shredded chicken noodle soup needs no extra seasoning. The tom yum broth is perfectly balanced^ chicken is tender, while slow-cooked chicken feet are an option. Available for breakfast and lunch only.	romaniriccardo	\N	\N
3337912251	Here Klae Pork Satay	Pamaprao Road	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	3.0	฿	t	f	Now run by the third-generation grill master, this humble shophouse boasts a history spanning over nine decades and remains one of Ayutthaya’s most cherished spots for charcoal-grilled pork satay. The skewered meat is meticulously marinated, offering an aromatic blend of nine spices. Don't miss the pork offal – it pairs perfectly with the accompanying peanut sauce. Please note: takeaways only, and cash is the accepted payment method.	guerravictor	\N	\N
3331588490	Roti Sai Mai Abeedeen-Pranom Sangaroon	32/1 Mu 4	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	t	f	Over 70 years have passed, but this renowned spot opposite Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya Hospital still serves the same perfect rotis with candy floss, made by the same family. Their specialty, the green pandan roti, is known for its delightful gooeyness. As popular as ever, be prepared to queue.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3334093373	Baan Pu Karn	15 Mu 5	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿	f	f	This simple eatery is set in the chef-owner's house. The mouthwatering Thai dishes are made from local ingredients and fresh seafood that’s hard to find in this province. This is good cooking and well-seasoned recipes with lovely herbal aromas and the natural umami of shrimps and crab meat. The kitchen sometimes closes early if dishes sell out, so it’s best to call ahead or arrive early. And booking a table at the weekend is a necessity.	d'angelonino	\N	\N
3332608082	Baan Ta Ko Rai	112/941 Mu 3	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	Here at this blue-roofed local favourite they prove there’s more to Ayutthaya than grilled river prawns. Ingredients are carefully selected from produce grown within the community and it uses fish from nearby rivers as the catch of the day. The herb-scented fish cakes are delectable, while stir-fried Chinese kale with deep fried salted fish is equally impressive. Portion sizes are generous, so check before ordering.	costantinitomas	\N	\N
3334165116	Kin Lookdeaw	35 Mu 9	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	t	The name of the restaurant encourages guests to ‘focus on eating’ at this quaint house with an open-air pavilion overlooking a serene pond. The chefs, veterans in the kitchen, prepare simple Thai dishes and make their own chilli paste from scratch. The regular pounding of the pestle in the mortar reverberates through nature’s own soundtrack. Try the stir-fried crispy fish with aromatic ginger and salted eggs.	palmieridaniel	\N	\N
3336945974	Ruan Thai Kung Pao	1/2 Mu 4	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Car park,Terrace		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	t	This riverside restaurant is a great place to stop for lunch after paying respects at Wat Choeng Len. Diners gather here for some of the finest fresh produce from the river, including grilled prawns and deep-fried sheatfish. The aromatic green curry with clown featherback fish balls is another highlight. Advance ordering of the huge river prawns – expertly cooked over charcoal – is highly recommended, as they are both popular and in limited supply.	stracciaantonio	\N	\N
3331348202	U-Khao	99 Mu 2	Thailand	Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	U-Khao, or ‘land of plenty’, has 2 dining areas smartly decorated in white and blue. The menu serves up the nostalgic flavours of the owner’s childhood, as it’s based on her mother’s Thai recipes. They use traditional cooking methods presented with a modern aesthetic. The old-school style egg stew with pork belly is a flavoursome, intense stew with juicy meat. The grilled shrimp relish with vegetables is also highly recommended for its spicy relish and smoky aroma.	farinalucas	\N	\N
3338028735	Go Benz	163 Krabi Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Asian	4.0	฿	t	t	The constantly busy Go Benz has been serving popular dishes, including their speciality pork with peppery broth and rolled rice noodles, for over 20 years – and it’s easy to see why it’s quite such a popular spot. Many of the dishes often sell out, like the fragrant dry boiled rice with crispy pork and tender pork offal. Also well worth ordering is the crispy pork with sweet soy sauce, which is seasoned wonderfully and has a lovely charcoal-grilled crust.	dvorakgiorgia	\N	\N
3337433116	Surf & Turf by Soul Kitchen	115 Phangnga Road	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus		Nessun premio	European Contemporary	3.0	฿฿	t	t	The menu changes every month in this intriguing restaurant. Regular options range from home-made pastas to a signature seafood dish, plus specials that are cleverly curated to showcase Chef Tom's latest culinary creations. The chef artfully prepares his dishes, blending quality ingredients to tantalise the taste buds. And thanks to the ever-changing selection of handpicked wines, there's always something different to sip with your meal.	rusnakhannah	\N	\N
3335360743	Niyom Salt Grilled Duck	5/19 Mu 3	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Grills	4.0	฿	t	f	This unassuming gem serves around 30-40 juicy, tender charcoal-roasted ducks every day. Order a half or whole bird and savour the wholesome flavour and crispy skin fresh off the stove with either spicy-sour or tamarind sauce for dipping. Grilled chicken is sometimes an option, too.	medvedevkatie	\N	\N
3339792183	Khao Tom Thanon Di Buk	185/11 Phang-Nga Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles and Congee	4.0	฿	f	t	This family-run gem serves comforting classics, from aromatic Khao Tom porridge to a secret-recipe Chinese brown soup with various toppings. Weekend specials include braised pork ribs and chicken with fermented soybeans. Adding a twist, they serve sandwiches filled with distinctly flavoured kaya. The perfect balance of casual dining and unique culinary delights is complemented by charming local Thai-Chinese decor.	benettisergey	\N	\N
3335332557	Roti Chaofa	44 Chaofa Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	5.0	฿	f	t	For over 35 years, the locals have flocked to Roti Chaofa for Thai-Muslim breakfasts, curries and Thai-style chicken biryani. The crisp, golden-brown rotis with a fluffy inner, are nicely salted and enjoyed with sweets or savouries. The tangy, juicy Beef Massaman curry is delightful.	ferrijacopo	\N	\N
3335974887	Roti Thaew Nam	6 Thep Krasattri Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	฿	f	f	Soft, crispy, non-oily roti emerge from a huge charcoal pan. At this 70-year-old Halal breakfast spot, they're shaped, fried and served in the blink of an eye and served with tender beef or chicken curry. The sweeter roti with banana and egg has no added sugar.	raduionela	\N	\N
3330237024	Kin-Kub-Ei	81/9 Mu 7	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Cash only,Terrace		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	With its shaded garden, recently renovated Kin-Kub-Ei retains its inviting charm, while debuting a casual yet warm new dining area. Chef Tipsuda 'Tubtim' Khanchaijatuwit and Ei prepare southern Thai specialties passed down through the generations, nicely balancing flavours and prioritising quality. The menu ensures affordability without sacrificing taste. The crispy golden-brown local fish with tangy curry paste epitomises their commitment to flavour and tradition.	lombardiemanuele	\N	\N
3330241879	Krua Baan Platong	167/1 Mu 5	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿	f	t	Popular with Thai celebrities and prominent politicians, this eatery tucked away in a tiny alley in Thalang deserves its excellent reputation. The chefs source quality local ingredients to produce intensely flavoured dishes that encapsulate the essence of Phuket. Highlights include stir-fried banana stalk with plump shrimps and shrimp paste, and melt-in-your-mouth steamed pork belly with their signature southern Thai budu dipping sauce. Booking and ordering in advance are a must.	fontanagiuseppe	\N	\N
3338785928	Krua Kao Kuk	47/4 Phatthana Road	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	t	The legacy of the original roadside stall lives on, thanks to the owner's granddaughter. Famous for its boiled rice with fish, this humble restaurant also serves a variety of other home-style dishes that are worth trying. The quality is clear in these bold-flavoured plates. The deep-fried meatballs, made to a family recipe, are a great start to the meal and go well with the fresh fish menu, which is cooked in a traditional Phuket style.	fioreerik	\N	\N
3336867149	Krua Praya	216/19 Mu 3	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Wheelchair access		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	f	Krua Praya showcases Southern Thai, especially Phuket, cuisine. Its traditional décor and captivating rooftop charm visitors. The menu features skilfully prepared dishes with bold flavours and enticing aromas. The standout pork belly dishes include the signature fried pork belly with curry paste and young coconut shoots, delivering a crispy, spicy delight. Alternatively, the Phuket-style stew offers a rich non-spicy option, served in a satisfying gravy.	popafarah	\N	\N
3331696801	Mor Mu Dong	9/4 Mu 3 Soi Pa Lai	Thailand	Phuket	Car park		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	Mor Mu Dong takes its name from its owner, Mor, and the Mu Dong Canal, where it is located. Nestled in a mangrove forest, it is housed in a set of rustic pavilions where diners can enjoy seafood and take in the views that change with the tide. In the open kitchen, tanks of live seafood affirm the freshness of the food. Order 3–4 vibrant dishes to share and enjoy the Southern Thai flavours bursting from them.	antonovrebecca	\N	\N
3335988510	Naam Yoi	63/250 Ruam Phattana Road	Thailand	Phuket	Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Going from steam-table hole-in-the-wall to a small cook-to-order eatery to a casual, tree-lined, open-air restaurant, Naam Yoi has cemented its identity as a solid family restaurant with a canon of tried-and-true dishes. Ingredients are obtained daily from local markets by the auntie of the family who is the head chef. Homestyle classics like river snail curry, spicy stir-fry of split gill mushrooms, and braised pork rule the roost here.	novotarskymariia	\N	\N
3335892191	The Charm Dining Gallery	93 Dibuk Road	Thailand	Phuket			Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	f	Having grown up working in his family's food business, Chef Buriphat always wanted to do something special with their recipes. Over the last few years, he has realised that vision, impressing diners with his honest interpretation of traditional Southern Thai-Peranakan cuisine. Check out the delicious stir-fried pork belly with herbs and sweet dark soy sauce, and be sure to try the pork rib soup with tofu and salted fish.	cellericelina	\N	\N
3337595214	Ton Mayom	23/1 Mu 6	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	5.0	฿	t	t	The Mayom (star gooseberry) is a local tree located at the front of this outlet that offers a shady setting. They serve fried local fish with an aromatic curry and Southern Thai sour curry soup with seabass and young coconut shoots. The signatures are delicious and a must-try.	costanzomaurizio	\N	\N
3335857282	A Pong Mae Sunee	99 Soi Soon Uthit	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	5.0	฿	t	f	For over five years, Sunee’s street food stall has been renowned for its Khanom A Pong—delicious coconut crepes. Cooked in mini woks over charcoal, the crepes are unique for their light, crispy shell and soft centre—a perfect balance of sweetness and creamy coconut. Be sure to arrive early at this beloved stall to experience these irresistible snacks.	venturialessia	\N	\N
3338680498	Pathongko Mae Pranee	57 Wirat Hong Yok 3 Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Street Food	4.0	฿	t	f	Customers with a sweet tooth and fans of deep-fried goodness line up here from 6am to get their daily fix. The deep-fried Patongko (dough sticks) and salapao are freshly prepared^ the crunchy fries are golden-brown. It’s all very tasty^ even without the dipping sauces.	beckerradu	\N	\N
3337977175	Chuan Chim	37/3 Montri Road	Thailand	Phuket	Cash only		Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	f	One of the oldest food shops in Phuket, now run by the second generation, offers the freshest seafood, all prepared à la minute. The chef's impressive wok skills shine through in every dish, with highlights like the aromatic Tom Yam seafood soup and deep-fried squid with garlic and pepper.	fiorellifiorello	\N	\N
3330744880	Toh Daeng	GF	Thailand	Phuket	Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access	https://www.baanarjor.com	Nessun premio	Thai	5.0	฿฿	f	t	‘Toh-daeng’ translates as ‘red dining table’ – and you will find one here, running the length of the kitchen wing at this renovated manor house which serves as a window into Phuket’s past. The restaurant is surrounded by farmland, where they grow ingredients including mulberry and coconut. Well-balanced dishes allow the natural flavours of the produce to shine^ rambutan red curry with grilled pork neck is a highlight, with the rambutan adding a natural sweetness.	urbanalessia	\N	\N
3334300406	Ruean Panya	1300/600 Soi Ekkachai 13	Thailand	Samut Sakhon	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai	3.0	฿฿	f	f	Open since 1995, this family-run restaurant – which blends food and art – is a hidden gem. Spread across four houses, it has a relaxed vibe that gives the impression of dining at a friend's, while painting-filled interiors add a gallery feel. Owner Prunhnee does all the cooking herself^ her attention to detail and the complexity of flavours make her dishes memorable. Local seafood is a feature, and their signature mud crab coconut dip or ‘Lhon Pu’ is a must-have.	frolovjulia	\N	\N
3337595186	Yok Kheng	5/2 Tonpo Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Noodles	5.0	฿	f	f	Consummately crafted regional specialties are the highlight here, particularly long tong, a Surat Thani delicacy. It features succulent dry noodles in a pink sweet and sour sauce with tender portions of pig’s blood, skin and meat. Leave room for the delectable mango with sticky rice.	silvestritommy	\N	\N
3334406005	Pa Ting	1/8 Mu 5	Thailand	Surat Thani	Car park,Great view		Nessun premio	Seafood	3.0	฿฿	t	t	Established in 1967, Pa Ting is run by the founder’s daughter. The restaurant is a basic, open-air building overlooking Don Sak River, serving seafood cooked according to local recipes. The spicy salad with salted Kulao fish bursts with flavoursome Thai herbs. The crab curry with seablite leaves enjoys the natural umami of freshly caught seafood, enhanced with spicy in-house curry paste. Plenty of parking at the front.	bigazzimattia	\N	\N
3333258974	Keo Pla	560/4 Na Mueang Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	3.0	฿	f	t	This locally renowned noodle shop first opened in 1959. The homemade fish dumplings with celery and fish balls packed with umami invariably attract long queues. The soup strikes just the right balance of sweet and savoury with a herbal aroma. Hearty, generous portions.	bellinicarlos	\N	\N
3338697121	Khao Phra Ram Long Song Lao Ohw	22 2 Witeetad Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	฿	t	f	With a legacy spanning 6 decades, locals flock here for the exquisite satay pork and renowned phra ram long song, an ancient Siamese delicacy. It features tender sliced pork in a curry sauce that masterfully balances rich gutsy paste with creamy coconut milk.	pirijiri	\N	\N
3330698357	Lian Tai	70 Chonkasem Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Cash only		Nessun premio	Small eats	4.0	฿	f	f	Lian Tai specialises in deep-fried doughnuts. The family uses the original fermented dough recipe concocted by their father more than 5 decades ago. Cooked to a crisp, outer golden-brown with a soft, puffy inside, the Patongo is irresistible when dipped in rich sweet pandan custard.	giordanopietro	\N	\N
3337397834	Phunisa	11/1 Mu 1	Thailand	Surat Thani	Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	f	f	Standing atop a picturesque hill, the restaurant commands splendid views of the Tapi River winding through a green landscape of palm tree plantations and mountains. They serve tasty Southern Thai fare, including salted duck egg and local river prawns. A spicy seafood sauce and chargrill aroma add depth and complexity to the natural umami of prawns, while a spicy Southern Thai curry soup with pork cartilage features intense peppery and spicy flavours.	orlovclaire	\N	\N
3331270834	Sum Gradang Nga	31/57-59 Soi Donnok 8/1	Thailand	Surat Thani	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Southern Thai	3.0	฿฿	t	t	Set in a charming house surrounded by ylang-ylang plants, Sum Gradang Nga is a hit with the locals for its Southern Thai cuisine bursting with gutsy flavours. Take the spicy pork cartilage with piquant seasoning, for example. Alternatively, the crab curry, which exudes umami, is served with vermicelli, fresh vegetables and a sweet-sour cucumber salad. Two dining areas: an alfresco space shaded by trees and a cool interior with a pastel pink décor.	rizzimartin	\N	\N
3337387334	Lucky	1 Thathong Road	Thailand	Surat Thani	Air conditioning,Car park		Nessun premio	Thai-Chinese, Southern Thai	4.0	฿฿	t	t	Lucky is a 2-storey restaurant with a simple, vintage vibe. The chef-owner has upheld the legacy of previous generations in this family-run eatery. She visits the market every day to select the freshest ingredients and oversees every dish that leaves the kitchen – a selection of Thai-Chinese, southern Thai and seafood cuisine. Don't miss the allure of wok-fried shrimp with chilli and salt, where the enticing blend of salt, chilli, garlic, and pepper creates an aromatic delight.	karpovlucy	\N	\N
3336578466	Som Tum Jinda	63/1-2 Phichit Rangsan Road	Thailand	Ubon Ratchathani	Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only		Nessun premio	Isan	5.0	฿฿	t	t	Chef-owner Jinda is a specialist in somtum dishes. She first plied her trade back in 1974 in the local university before moving downtown. The Isan-style spicy fish maw with bamboo shoot salad has a nice balance of herbs and its powerful aroma is punctuated by the intensity of the Tiliacora juice. The signature, somtum with crispy catfish, dispenses an impressive tang. Somtum Jinda is also famous over the border in Lao where they have another branch.	brunettibruno	\N	\N
